en demonstrators were arrested in a day of protests held at the offices of several presidential candidates in Iowa on Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — “How many people had fun today?” said David Goodner, a 30-year-old community organizer, to a bus full of Occupy the Caucus protesters on their way from Newt Gingrich’s local campaign headquarters to President Obama’s. The question was met with cheers, as the group considered the 18 arrests, including those of two local teenagers, that made today a sign of success.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For ‘Occupy the Caucus’ Protesters, a Successful Day of Arrests', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T04:34:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Will Storey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Will', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/512b46a4-bee3-5f94-81fb-85646746449b', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/512b46a4-bee3-5f94-81fb-85646746449b'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for Dec. 31, 2011, for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for Dec. 31, 2011, for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dec. 31, 2011', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York T