ter it opened in a Lincoln Park townhouse and quickly became a national destination, The Chicago Sun-Times reported on Sunday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charlie Trotter’s Closing in Chicago', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trotter, Charlie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Charlie Trotter's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T13:59:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9db316b2-5e99-5b41-a8cd-f79ed66780a5', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9db316b2-5e99-5b41-a8cd-f79ed66780a5'}, {'abstract': 'If the Giants lose against Dallas, the story will change very quickly: Many fans will want to show Tom Coughlin the door.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/coughlin-a-keeper-win-or-lose/', 'snippet': 'If the Giants lose against Dallas, the story will change very quickly: Many fans will want to show Tom Coughlin the door.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Giants Coach Tom Coughlin is poised for a triumphant night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coughlin a Keeper, Win or Lose?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T14:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c221792-e140-5564-9c4a-54a9ca27ac21', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c221792-e140-5564-9c4a-54a9ca27ac21'}, {'abstract': 'Now that the gluttony of the holiday season is over, we can all be on our best behavior. That includes travel companies, several of which are turning over a new leaf for the New Year.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/new-years-resolutions-from-the-travel-industry/', 'snippet': 'Now that the gluttony of the holiday season is over, we can all be on our best behavior. That includes travel companies, several of which are turning over a new leaf for the New Year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the gluttony of the holiday season is over, we can all be on our best behavior. That includes travel companies, several of which are turning over a new leaf for the New Year. Among their resolutions for the coming year:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Year’s Resolutions From the Travel Industry', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colonial Williamsburg', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glo