neighborhood known as Little Syria is about to disappear from Lower Manhattan. But several young advocates are determined to save what they can.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1891, Yusuf Sadallah arrived in Lower Manhattan from the town of Baskinta, in the part of the Ottoman Empire that is now Lebanon. Going by the name of Joseph Sadallah, he set up a trading shop on Washington Street, where other immigrants from the Levant — Syrians, Lebanese and Palestinians — had created a vibrant Arab quarter known as Little Syria.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Little Syria (Now Tiny Syria) Finds New Advocates', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARAB-AMERICANS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Landmarks Preservation Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Financial District (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T17:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06d2211e-e12a-5edf-aa15-5efa1ee22b47', 'word_count': 1073, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06d2211e-e12a-5edf-aa15-5efa1ee22b47'}, {'abstract': 'Perhaps no candidate has more on the line on Tuesday than  Gov. Rick Perry of Texas.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/in-iowa-rick-perry-is-stuck-in-the-second-tier/', 'snippet': 'Perhaps no candidate has more on the line on Tuesday than  Gov. Rick Perry of Texas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every candidate has a lot on the line