firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84ff12b1-4a49-58d1-b2e8-8ff506f5d6a2', 'word_count': 1391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84ff12b1-4a49-58d1-b2e8-8ff506f5d6a2'}, {'abstract': 'Last week, I climbed a rocky hill south of San Francisco at sunset and spent 10 minutes trying to compose the perfect shot on my iPhone. I was watching a magnificent sunset through a tiny four-inch screen. In the new year, I resolve to take a break from technology and let my brain do a little wandering on its own.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/resolved-in-2012-to-enjoy-the-view-without-help-from-an-iphone/', 'snippet': 'Last week, I climbed a rocky hill south of San Francisco at sunset and spent 10 minutes trying to compose the perfect shot on my iPhone. I was watching a magnificent sunset through a tiny four-inch screen. In the new year, I resolve to take a brea...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, I drove to Pacifica, a beach community just south of San Francisco, where I climbed a large rocky hill as the sun descended on the horizon. It painted a typically astounding California sunset across the Pacific Ocean. What did I do next?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/technology/bits-disruptionsview/bits-disruptionsview-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/technology/bits-disruptionsview/bits-disruptionsview-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/technology/bits-disruptionsview/bits-disruptionsview-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disruptions: Resolved in 2012: To Enjoy the View Without Help From an iPhone', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lehrer, Jonah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Ocean', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T18:42:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ece747df-54e0-5fc2-8898-003e66a0b6cb', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ece747df-54e0-5fc2-8898-003e66a0b6cb'}, {'abstract': 'ABC had its best end-of-the-year prime-time numbers since 2000 with coverage of the ball dropping in Times Square, according to preliminary results.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/new-years-rockin-eve-draws-strong-ratings/', 'snippet': 'ABC had its best end-of-the-year prime-time numbers since 2000 with coverage of the ball dropping in Times Square, according to preliminary results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC extended “Dick Clark’s New Year’s Rockin’ Eve” on Saturday night, and it appeared to pay off, giving the network its best end-of-the-year prime-time ratings since 2000. The two new hours of New Year’s Eve merriment, from 8 to 10 p.m., drew about 8.3 million viewers, an unusually high number for a Saturday night. Repeats on the other networks drew between 1.5 million and 3 million viewers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘New Year’s Rockin’ Eve’ Draws Strong Ratings', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Dick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seacrest, Ryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T18:48:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de888baf-6cbd-5f01-abce-ba044183a308', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de888baf-6cbd-5f01-abce-ba044183a308'}, {'abstract': 'An adaptive trait in a complicated century: the ability to fall forward without falling down.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/falling-forward-without-falling-down/', 'snippet': 'An adaptive trait in a complicated century: the ability to fall forward without falling down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a Twittter post for a new year in a century in which the things we don’t know are easily as important as those we do. In such an environment, what qualities can help individuals and communities avoid big missteps? I’d start with literacy, connectedness, empathy, engagement, enterprise and anthropophilia. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Falling Forward (Without Falling Down)', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Revkin, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T19:17:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ffe86fb-10d4-556e-87bf-4b255e4cde29', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ffe86fb-10d4-556e-87bf-4b255e4cde29'}, {'abstract': 'Palestinian and Israeli negotiators will meet in Jordan on Tuesday in an effort to revive moribund peace talks, although none of the sides involved suggested any reason to view the meeting as a sign of significant progress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/world/middleeast/palestinians-and-israelis-will-talk-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Palestinian and Israeli negotiators will meet in Jordan on Tuesday in an effort to revive moribund peace talks, although none of the sides involved suggested any reason to view the meeting as a sign of significant progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Palestinian and Israeli negotiators plan to meet for the first time in more than a year in Jordan on Tuesday, in an effort to revive moribund peace talks, although none of the sides involved suggested any reason to view the meeting as a sign of significant progress.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinians and Israelis Will Talk This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Palestinians and Israelis to Hold First Talks in Over a Year in Jordan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T19:22:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56560737-1804-5857-91f4-eda26949bf78', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56560737-1804-5857-91f4-eda26949bf78'}, {'abstract': 'By your enemies shall they know ye.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/sad-things-wonkish-and-trivial/', 'snippet': 'By your enemies shall they know ye.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I see that some people out there don’t like me. A couple of odds and ends:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sad Things (Wonkish and Trivial)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T19:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcb9a107-4a22-5d86-9bc9-4f357f060637', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcb9a107-4a22-5d86-9bc9-4f357f060637'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Michele Bachmann took the pulpit at the Jubilee Family Church Sunday and preached a message of redemption and winning.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/bachmann-makes-final-pitch-to-iowa-faithful/', 'snippet': 'Representative Michele Bachmann took the pulpit at the Jubilee Family Church Sunday and preached a message of redemption and winning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OSKALOOSA, Iowa – Representative Michele Bachmann took the pulpit at the Jubilee Family Church here during the morning worship service on Sunday and preached from Scripture, weaving her personal story with biblical parables about redemption — a message that seemed tailored to reassure undecided voters about the viability of her embattled campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann Makes Final Pitch to Iowa Faithful', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T19:35:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Saulny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saulny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a2c3d12-b46d-5c7b-ba6c-9ebdabfd4ca5', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a2c3d12-b46d-5c7b-ba6c-9ebdabfd4ca5'}, {'abstract': 'Nebraska used to win in numbing, overwhelming fashion, but even the most spoiled fans are getting used to the current reality under Coach Bo Pelini.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/a-nebraska-fan-faces-the-new-reality/', 'snippet': 'Nebraska used to win in numbing, overwhelming fashion, but even the most spoiled fans are getting used to the current reality under Coach Bo Pelini.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was walking through the office when a colleague stopped me. “Did I hear you say something about Nebraska football?” he asked, innocently, cheerfully, not realizing the twisted synapses that were about to fire in my brain. I frowned and shook my head over the idea of writing about the team. “My comments would be too blue,” I assured him glibly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Nebraska Fan Faces the New Reality', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Callahan, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martinez, Taylor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelini, Bo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suh, Ndamukong', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Michigan State University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T19:45:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Woods', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woods', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b07f06d7-7458-504f-8034-3b898de401a3', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b07f06d7-7458-504f-8034-3b898de401a3'}, {'abstract': 'Police in Nassau County are trying to determine how John Capano, an off-duty agent with the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives, died after intervening in a robbery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/nyregion/a-routine-errand-to-drugstore-turns-deadly.html', 'snippet': 'Police in Nassau County are trying to determine how John Capano, an off-duty agent with the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives, died after intervening in a robbery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday morning, James J. Capano stopped in front of the pharmacy where his son, an off-duty federal agent, had lost his life less than 24 hours earlier. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/nyregion/jp-SHOT-1325452640515/jp-SHOT-1325452640515-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/02/nyregion/jp-SHOT-1325452640515/jp-SHOT-1325452640515-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/nyregion/jp-SHOT-1325452640515/jp-SHOT-1325452640515-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/nyregion/jp-SHOT-1325452640515/jp-SHOT-1325452640515-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/02/nyregion/jp-SHOT-1325452640515/jp-SHOT-1325452640515-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As U.S. Agent Is Mourned, Officials Try to Figure Out Who Shot Him', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As U.S. Agent Is Mourned, Officials Try to Figure Out Who Shot Him', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugstores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T19:59:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein and Tim Stelloh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelloh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e7a6f0e-8c1d-5d11-8ba3-6ad7542f9bc4', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e7a6f0e-8c1d-5d11-8ba3-6ad7542f9bc4'}, {'abstract': 'In conducting the New York Philharmonic on New Year’s Eve, Alan Gilbert made a point about works with a distinctly American style.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/arts/music/new-york-philharmonic-at-avery-fisher-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'In conducting the New York Philharmonic on New Year’s Eve, Alan Gilbert made a point about works with a distinctly American style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alan Gilbert had an elegantly straightforward idea for the New York Philharmonic’s New Year’s Eve concert at Avery Fisher Hall (and on televisions everywhere, thanks to PBS). He set aside the orchestra’s long tradition of following the Central European model of offering either bubbly programs of Viennese waltzes or grandly serious works like Beethoven’s Ninth Symphony as well as recent alternatives, like presenting a pops concert featuring a Broadway singer or light classics that would not otherwise be heard in a Philharmonic program. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/new-1/new-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/new-1/new-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/new-1/new-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 931, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/new-1/new-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/new-1/new-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G