provision in the Massachusetts health care program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Newt Gingrich said on Sunday that he intended to campaign in New Hampshire, where polls show him running third, rather than move directly to South Carolina, where he is leading.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich to Take Aim at Romney in New Hampshire', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T22:14:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6527332d-4d31-5eb6-93fd-c050d5258c91', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6527332d-4d31-5eb6-93fd-c050d5258c91'}, {'abstract': 'The author George R. R. Martin, the executive producer of the HBO series “Game of Thrones,” has given his fans a late Christmas gift in the form of a sample chapter from his forthcoming “Winds of Winter.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/arts/television/game-of-thrones-treat.html', 'snippet': 'The author George R. R. Martin, the executive producer of the HBO series “Game of Thrones,” has given his fans a late Christmas gift in the form of a sample chapter from his forthcoming “Winds of Winter.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The author George R. R. Martin has given his fans a late Christmas gift in the form of a sample chapter from his forthcoming “Winds of Winter,” the sixth book in “A Song of Ice and Fire,” his popular fantasy series. Mr. Martin, who is also the executive producer of the HBO series “Game of Thrones,” which is adapted from his novels, posted a preview of his latest work on his Web site, georgerrmartin.com, last week. No publication date has been announced. The series’s fifth book, “A Dance With Dragons,” was published in July after a six-year wait; it sold more than 170,000 print copies on its first day. Mr. Martin also announced that the book’s paperback edition, to be released in July, would contain a different sample chapter from “Winds.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Game of Thrones’ Treat', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Game of Thrones’ Treat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, George R R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T22:23:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfe5863c-7c72-557e-bec9-bf0b823ec7ef', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfe5863c-7c72-557e-bec9-bf0b823ec7ef'}, {'abstract': 'The annual celebration of all things Scottish will be held in the spring at 59E59 Theaters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/theater/schedule-announced-for-scotland-week.html', 'snippet': 'The annual celebration of all things Scottish will be held in the spring at 59E59 Theaters.', 'lead_paragraph': '59E59 Theaters has announced that it will present the United States premiere of “A Slow Air,” a new play written and directed by David Harrower, beginning April 4 as part of Scotland Week, the annual celebration of all things Scottish. “A Slow Air” explores the impact of the 2007 terrorist attack on the Glasgow Airport from the perspective of a family in a nearby village. It had its premiere at the Traverse Theater during the 2011 Edinburgh Festival Fringe. “Blackbird,” a previous play from Mr. Harrower, had a well-received run at Manhattan Theater Club in 2007 and won the 2007 Olivier Award in London for best new play. 59E59 is also set to present the United States premiere of “Federer Versus Murray,” a dark comedy written and directed by Gerda Stevenson, on April 4.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Schedule Announced for Scotland Week', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Schedule Announced For Scotland Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '59E59 THEATERS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrower, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T22:25:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/708d89ea-5a6e-588b-a0c4-578185ead3f3', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/708d89ea-5a6e-588b-a0c4-578185ead3f3'}, {'abstract': 'The comedian Russell Brand has filed for divorce from the pop star Katy Perry; after being hospitalized for shortness of breath, the singer Etta James is now breathing on her own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/arts/music/footnotes.html', 'snippet': 'The comedian Russell Brand has filed for divorce from the pop star Katy Perry; after being hospitalized for shortness of breath, the singer Etta James is now breathing on her own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After 14 months of marriage, the comedian Russell Brand has filed for divorce from the pop star Katy Perry, citing “irreconcilable differences,” The Associated Press reported. The couple, above, met in 2009 at the MTV Video Music Awards, of which Mr. Brand was the host. They were married in October 2010. ... After being hospitalized on Dec. 21 for shortness of breath, the R&B singer Etta James — who has terminal leukemia — is now breathing on her own and has been taken off a respirator, The Associated Press reported on Saturday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Footnotes', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Footnotes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Etta', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Katy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brand, Russell', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T22:27:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c3f3e74-cd8e-51bb-b52d-2dcf8995443d', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c3f3e74-cd8e-51bb-b52d-2dcf8995443d'}, {'abstract': 'A question of whether his sudden gains in the polls will hold.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/santorum-on-the-rise-pushes-his-supporters-for-help/', 'snippet': 'A question of whether his sudden gains in the polls will hold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SIOUX CITY, Iowa – Emboldened by a late and unexpected rise in the polls, Rick Santorum came to this conservative corner of rural Iowa on Sunday and urged his supporters to redouble their efforts to help ensure a win in the state’s caucuses on Tuesday night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Santorum Pushes Supporters to Keep His Surge Alive', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T22:31:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0807d9b8-1422-596c-bcd9-950cf4f25b8a', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0807d9b8-1422-596c-bcd9-950cf4f25b8a'}, {'abstract': '“The Enchanted Island,” a pastiche incorporating elements from Shakespeare and Baroque works by Handel, Vivaldi and others, had its premiere Saturday at the Metropolitan Opera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/arts/music/the-enchanted-island-at-the-metropolitan-opera-review.html', 'snippet': '“The Enchanted Island,” a pastiche incorporating elements from Shakespeare and Baroque works by Handel, Vivaldi and others, had its premiere Saturday at the Metropolitan Opera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forget “Auld Lang Syne.” The best music to ring in a new year is “Now a bright new day is dawning,” the joyous chorus that ends “The Enchanted Island,” the inventive concoction that had its premiere on Saturday night at the Metropolitan Opera. The music for this finale is lifted from the “Hallelujah” chorus that concludes Handel’s oratorio “Judas Maccabaeus.” The new words are by the librettist Jeremy Sams, who devised the story and assembled this fanciful, clever and touching pastiche by selecting arias, ensembles, choruses and dances from works by Handel, Vivaldi, Rameau and lesser-known Baroque composers. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/02ISLAND/02ISLAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/02ISLAND/02ISLAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/02ISLAND/02ISLAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/02ISLAND/02ISLAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/02ISLAND/02ISLAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shiny Bibelot From Shakespeare, Handel & Co.', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shiny Bibelot From Shakespeare, Handel & Co.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Domingo, Placido', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T22:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/41999daa-80fa-5c47-81c5-eab95cb55c4d', 'word_count': 1105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41999daa-80fa-5c47-81c5-eab95cb55c4d'}, {'abstract': 'WebOS, the TouchPad tablet’s core software, was developed by Palm in about nine months, and former employees said the software was deeply flawed because of the way it was built.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/technology/hewlett-packards-touchpad-was-built-on-flawed-software-some-say.html', 'snippet': 'WebOS, the TouchPad tablet’s core software, was developed by Palm in about nine months, and former employees said the software was deeply flawed because of the way it was built.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The TouchPad tablet from Hewlett-Packard was one of the most closely watched new gadgets of 2011 — and quickly turned out to be the year’s biggest flop. The TouchPad, which was supposed to be a rival to Apple’s iPad, lasted just seven weeks on the market before H.P. killed it, citing weak sales.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/business/02jpPalm/02jpPalm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/business/02jpPalm/02jpPalm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/02/business/02jpPalm/02jpPalm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Flop of H.P. TouchPad, an Object Lesson for the Tech Sector', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Flop of H.P. TouchPad, an Object Lesson for the Tech Sector', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Apotheker, Leo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitman, Margaret C', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palm Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hewlett-Packard Company', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T22:37:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d7b3fcc-d73e-5ede-9d09-8fd4d144747a', 'word_count': 1596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d7b3fcc-d73e-5ede-9d09-8fd4d144747a'}, {'abstract': '“The Enchanted Island” at Metropolitan Opera borrows from the Baroque era when taking music from one opera and fitting it with new words was commonplace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/100000001256282/metropolitan-pastiche.html', 'snippet': '“The Enchanted Island” at Metropolitan Opera borrows from the Baroque era when taking music from one opera and fitting it with new words was commonplace.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Enchanted Island” at Metropolitan Opera borrows from the Baroque era when taking music from one opera and fitting it with new words was commonplace.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/video-ab-enchantedisland/video-ab-enchantedisland-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/video-ab-enchantedisland/video-ab-enchantedisland-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/video-ab-enchantedisland/video-ab-enchantedisland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/01/arts/video-ab-enchantedisland/video-ab-enchantedisland-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Metropolitan Pastiche', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print