4, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/business/sub02TLC2/sub02TLC2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/02/business/sub02TLC2/sub02TLC2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Speaking for TLC, the Least Said Is Best', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Speaking for TLC, The Least Said Is Best', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TLC (TV Network)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-01T23:16:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0d98ef1-2ced-5142-81ee-ff6d9366a233', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0d98ef1-2ced-5142-81ee-ff6d9366a233'}, {'abstract': 'Alexei Ratmansky’s “Nutcracker,” which just finished a run at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, occurs in a child’s world, and its best fare comes in the dancing of the children, the corps and supporting players.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/arts/dance/ratmanskys-nutcracker-occurs-in-a-childs-world.html', 'snippet': 'Alexei Ratmansky’s “Nutcracker,” which just finished a run at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, occurs in a child’s world, and its best fare comes in the dancing of the children, the corps and supporting players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We live in a golden age of children’s fiction, and in the most memorable moments of his staging of “The Nutcracker,” Alexei Ratmansky takes his place among the most imaginative children’s authors. The snow scene that ends Act I, with aspects of seduction, terror and vengefulness unlike in any other “Nutcracker,” has a dramatic urgency that recalls some of the classic works of Hans Christian Andersen. The time-traveling scenes whereby a pas de deux in each act shows us a Princess and Prince who are the adult alter egos of Clara and the Nutcracker Boy recall some of the finest parts of the “Harry Potter” and “His Dark Materials” series. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/abt-2/abt-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/abt-2/abt-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/abt-2/abt-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/abt-2/abt-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/02/arts/abt-2/abt-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fairy Tale Stoked by Childhood Dreams', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline':