aret Singer, Dies at 82', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'NIGHTCLUBS AND CABARETS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lea, Barbara', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T00:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bbebd94-1702-5b89-b168-9e726c9d04e5', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bbebd94-1702-5b89-b168-9e726c9d04e5'}, {'abstract': 'Extremists on both sides of the drug-policy issue have taken over the conversation. We must give centrists a voice, or America’s drug problem will only get worse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/opinion/drug-policy-needs-centrists.html', 'snippet': 'Extremists on both sides of the drug-policy issue have taken over the conversation. We must give centrists a voice, or America’s drug problem will only get worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ACCORDING to a recent study by the Centers for Disease Control, drug overdoses have increased almost six-fold in the last 30 years. They now represent the leading cause of accidental death in the United States, having overtaken motor vehicle accidents for the first time on record. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Overdosing on Extremism', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Overdosing on Extremism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T00:09:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin A. Sabet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Sabet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/98251695-492f-5428-ad5b-82904540a9f6', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98251695-492f-5428-ad5b-82904540a9f6'}, {'abstract': 'Slap Shot will provide live analysis of the Winter Classic between the Rangers and the Flyers, beginning at 3 p.m. Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/live-coverage-of-winter-classic-on-monday/', 'snippet': 'Slap Shot will provide live analysis of the Winter Classic between the Rangers and the Flyers, beginning at 3 p.m. Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Slap Shot will provide live analysis of the Winter Classic game between the Rangers and the Flyers, beginning at 3 p.m. Monday. On Sunday, the N.H.L. moved the game’s start time from 1 to 3 p.m. in the hope of improving ice conditions. NBC’s coverage will still start at 1 p.m., the same time the gates open at Citizens Bank Park.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Coverage of Winter Classic on Monday', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Flyers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T00:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57048057-a901-54a5-a36b-7d8aeb09d5c5', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57048057-a901-54a5-a36b-7d8aeb09d5c5'}, {'abstract': 'The minor bowl games may not have an effect on a college tournament that the N.C.A.A. should institute, but they have value in ways that have nothing to do with football.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/sports/ncaafootball/football-playoff-is-a-necessity-but-bowl-games-have-their-place.html', 'snippet': 'The minor bowl games may not have an effect on a college tournament that the N.C.A.A. should institute, but they have value in ways that have nothing to do with football.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By the time we arrived in Queens at the Comus Club’s 89th annual Christmas Ball, I’d already begun to reconsider my position that the minor bowl games that dot the college football landscape were irrelevant.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/sports/YRHODEN/YRHODEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/02/sports/YRHODEN/YRHODEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/sports/YRHODEN/YRHODEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/sports/YRHODEN/YRHODEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/02/sports/YRHODEN/YRHODEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bring on a Playoff, but Save the Bowl System', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bring on a Playoff, but Save the Bowl System', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bowl Championship Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bowl Games', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T00:30:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By William C. Rhoden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Rhoden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8200386f-3c64-5f45-8c90-08b414bd787f', 'word_count': 1334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8200386f-3c64-5f45-8c90-08b414bd787f'}, {'abstract': 'Antipiracy legislation before both chambers of Congress has bipartisan support, but online content providers are concerned it goes too far. They are right to be alarmed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/business/media/the-danger-of-an-attack-on-piracy-online.html', 'snippet': 'Antipiracy legislation before both chambers of Congress has bipartisan support, but online content providers are concerned it goes too far. They are right to be alarmed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By invoking the acronym SOPA right at the get-go, I may be daring many of you to check the next column over for something a little less chewy. After all, SOPA, which stands for Stop Online Piracy Act, sounds like a piece of arcane Internet government regulation — legislation that entertainment companies desperately care about and that leaves Web nation and free-speech crusaders frothing at the mouth. The rest of us? What were we talking about again?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/12/business/media/carr-50/carr-50-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/12/business/media/carr-50/carr-50-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Danger of an Attack on Piracy Online', 'kicker': 'The Media Equation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Danger Of an Attack On Piracy Online', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T00:43:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6f1346a-cd47-52b6-97cd-edce6a9908a6', 'word_count': 1350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6f1346a-cd47-52b6-97cd-edce6a9908a6'}, {'abstract': 'The Rangers and the Flyers play in the first-and fourth-largest TV markets in the country and also have a venomous history that is hard to equal.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/01/rangers-and-flyers-bring-bare-knuckle-history-to-a-showcase/', 'snippet': 'The Rangers and the Flyers play in the first-and fourth-largest TV markets in the country and also have a venomous history that is hard to equal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — When the N.H.L. and NBC originally plotted the Winter Classic, the idea was to present two traditional rivals. It does not hurt that this year’s matchup — the Rangers and the Flyers — play in the first- and fourth-largest television markets in the country, but these clubs also have a venomous history that is hard to equal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rangers and Flyers Bring Bare-Knuckle History to a Showcase', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Flyers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T00:45:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein and Stu Hackel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hackel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': 