res_cnd/02fires_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/02/us/02fires_cnd/02fires_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Los Angeles Police Arrest Suspect in Car Arsons', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Fourth Night of Car Fires in Los Angeles, an Arrest Is Made', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARSON', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T13:32:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/285d9b54-3d19-5259-9d5a-0f10d41c9876', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/285d9b54-3d19-5259-9d5a-0f10d41c9876'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s City Kitchen features a recipe for an Italian-style rabbit stew.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/for-the-coming-cold-braised-rabbit/', 'snippet': 'This week’s City Kitchen features a recipe for an Italian-style rabbit stew.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a cold weather meal, a braised rabbit is a fine choice. The recipe in this week’s City Kitchen is for an oven-baked version of the classic hunter-style rabbit alla cacciatore. A touch of tomato, some crimini mushrooms and some dried porcini, garlic and rosemary are all you need, plus a splash of wine and chicken stock. The proportions are forgiving, so measurements need not be exact. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Braised Rabbit, a Warming Winter Meal', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T13:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2ae17c2-40e2-5222-a3ef-03abda7087c3', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2ae17c2-40e2-5222-a3ef-03abda7087c3'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Tebow played poorly and his numbers reflected it. Tony Romo’s statistics looked fine, but looks can be deceiving.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/statistical-lows-for-romo-and-tebow/', 'snippet': 'Tim Tebow played poorly and his numbers reflected it. Tony Romo’s statistics looked fine, but looks can be deceiving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone could see that Tim Tebow was having a bad day Sunday, and the numbers backed that up. He was 6 for 22 for 60 passing yards in a loss against Kansas City, and his rushing wasn’t anything special (six carries for 16 yards).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Statistical Lows for Romo and Tebow', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romo, Tony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T14:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2895196f-a645-5b29-b752-91af5cb9bf9d', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2895196f-a645-5b29-b752-91af5cb9bf9d'}, {'abstract': 'Fat camp for adults, a shortage of A.D.H.D. drugs, Charlie Trotter plans to hang up the apron and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/monday-reading-a-week-at-a-fat-camp-for-grownups/', 'snippet': 'Fat camp for adults, a shortage of A.D.H.D. drugs, Charlie Trotter plans to hang up the apron and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: A Week at a Fat Camp for Grown-Ups', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T14:58:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9bd3b3b-690a-508f-bcbb-bee1775925c2', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9bd3b3b-690a-508f-bcbb-bee1775925c2'}, {'abstract': 'A Hungary update, from Kim Lane Scheppele.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/the-unconstitutional-constitution/', 'snippet': 'A Hungary update, from Kim Lane Scheppele.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest on Hungary from my Princeton colleague Kim Lane Scheppele, below the fold.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Unconstitutional Constitution', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T15:04:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ed6d88e-c2c7-56a4-ab59-51012fd2859b', 'word_count': 2461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ed6d88e-c2c7-56a4-ab59-51012fd2859b'}, {'abstract': 'What Chicago means by “nobody”.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/hermetic-economic-cults-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'What Chicago means by “nobody”.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad DeLong points to repeated quotes from Chicago economists asserting that any economist proposing fiscal stimulus – Christy, Larry, me – must be corrupt. And then they get all huffy about the way I insult them!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hermetic Economic Cults (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T15:11:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33c5929d-9d65-5b80-ab1e-f7ab5ab0bd9e', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33c5929d-9d65-5b80-ab1e-f7ab5ab0bd9e'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Michele Bachmann reappears on television in Iowa with a 30-second ad that comes just in time for Tuesday’s caucuses.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/bachmann-returns-to-iowa-airwaves/', 'snippet': 'Representative Michele Bachmann reappears on television in Iowa with a 30-second ad that comes just in time for Tuesday’s caucuses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — Representative Michele Bachmann hasn’t been on the air in Iowa with a television commercial since August when she surprised the country by placing first in the state’s straw poll. But she reappeared on Monday with a 30-second spot that comes just in time for the caucuses on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann Returns to Iowa Airwaves', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T15:22:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4181fd5d-5ca6-5534-9852-7bd39716a459', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4181fd5d-5ca6-5534-9852-7bd39716a459'}, {'abstract': 'A new service called Gym-Pact tries to motivate users to get to the gym, and fines people who don’t. Gym-goers collect cash if they meet their commitments.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/gym-pact-fines-you-for-not-exercising/', 'snippet': 'A new service called Gym-Pact tries to motivate users to get to the gym, and fines people who don’t. Gym-goers collect cash if they meet their commitments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the start of a new year, many people resolve to shed their holiday paunch by hitting the gym more frequently. It’s easy to stay motivated for a few weeks, but then other things seem to take precedence — late nights at work, happy hour or the couch. \xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gym-Pact Fines You for Not Exercising', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Clubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T15:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a12606a-6a17-519b-93fb-936881aa4d6f', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a12606a-6a17-519b-93fb-936881aa4d6f'}, {'abstract': 'An interview with the mathematician and geneticist behind the Human Genome Project and the Broad Institute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/science/100000001255558/eric-lander.html', 'snippet': 'An interview with the mathematician and geneticist behind the Human Genome Project and the Broad Institute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An interview with the mathematician and geneticist behind the Human Genome Project and the Broad Institute.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/video-lander/video-lander-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/03/science/video-lander/video-lander-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/video-lander/video-lander-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/science/video-lander/video-lander-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eric Lander', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Genome Project', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T15:58:53+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'Thomas Lin and Tony Cenicola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cenicola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/1b64d814-b2c8-57cc-9ca2-f9cfb312c44e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/1b64d814-b2c8-57cc-9ca2-f9cfb312c44e'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Lander, the head of the Broad Institute, went from the most solitary of sciences (math) to forging collaborations on the leading edge of biology, a field he never formally studied.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/science/broad-institute-director-finds-power-in-numbers.html', 'snippet': 'Eric Lander, the head of the Broad Institute, went from the most solitary of sciences (math) to forging collaborations on the leading edge of biology, a field he never formally studied.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAMBRIDGE, Mass. — His Ph.D. is in pure mathematics, in a subfield so esoteric and specialized that even if someone gets a great result, it can be appreciated by only a few dozen people in the entire world. But he left that world behind and, with no formal training, entered another: the world of molecular biology, medicine and genomics. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03JPLAND1_SPAN/03JPLAND1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03JPLAND1_SPAN/03JPLAND1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03JPLAND1_SPAN/03JPLAND1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Power in Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Power in Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biology and Biochemistry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitehead Institute for Biomedical Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lander, Eric S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Broad Institute', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T16:12:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28273158-8b01-574c-87d4-6ac348787030', 'word_count': 2308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28273158-8b01-574c-87d4-6ac348787030'}, {'abstract': 'My parenting resolutions for this 2012: clean it, own it and enjoy it.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/new-years-resolutions-to-parent-by/', 'snippet': 'My parenting resolutions for this 2012: clean it, own it and enjoy it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Either you’re the kind of person who makes New Year’s resolutions or you’re not. I most emphatically am and a few of my resolutions are very specific to me as a parent. I’ve made the whole idea of “the parent we want to be” versus the “parent we actually are” something of a meme for Motherlode in part because for me, there’s often such a huge gap between the two.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Year’s Resolutions to Parent By', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', '