-01-02T19:35:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec1540f8-3d6c-5fb0-9575-a2be65c37a23', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec1540f8-3d6c-5fb0-9575-a2be65c37a23'}, {'abstract': 'The demonstration — a day after the country’s new “majoritarian” Constitution took effect — marked the first time that opposition forces joined together to rally against a new constitution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/world/europe/rare-opposition-protests-in-hungary.html', 'snippet': 'The demonstration — a day after the country’s new “majoritarian” Constitution took effect — marked the first time that opposition forces joined together to rally against a new constitution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUDAPEST — As the governing party celebrated its achievements inside, tens of thousands of Hungarians rallied outside the nation’s 19th-century opera house on Monday in a rare opposition protest of what critics see as a campaign by Prime Minister Viktor Orban to undermine democracy and consolidate his power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/HUNGARY-1/HUNGARY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/03/world/HUNGARY-1/HUNGARY-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/HUNGARY-1/HUNGARY-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Opposition Protests Constitution in Hungary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Opposition Protests Constitution In Hungary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hungary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orban, Viktor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T19:35:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Palko Karasz and Melissa Eddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Palko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Karasz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea25bfa9-e70e-59e0-87b6-6def6be3b718', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea25bfa9-e70e-59e0-87b6-6def6be3b718'}, {'abstract': 'While security forces said there had been no attack, Finance Minister Rafe al-Essawi said a car bomb rocked his convoy as it returned to Baghdad from a funeral.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/world/middleeast/conflicting-reports-of-attack-on-iraqs-finance-minister-rafe-al-essawi.html', 'snippet': 'While security forces said there had been no attack, Finance Minister Rafe al-Essawi said a car bomb rocked his convoy as it returned to Baghdad from a funeral.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — As reports of violence in Iraq go, this one seemed straightforward, almost routine: A convoy carrying a leading Sunni politician was said to be hit by a roadside bomb north of Baghdad on Sunday night, wounding two bodyguards but leaving the official unscathed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reports Differ of Attack on an Iraqi Minister', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reports Differ of Attack on an Iraqi Minister', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shiite Muslims', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunni Muslims', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T19:39:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88601ddd-db7d-5381-a1a2-d14a9a7da18f', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88601ddd-db7d-5381-a1a2-d14a9a7da18f'}, {'abstract': 'Nigel Lythgoe, the executive producer of “So You Think You Can Dance,” revealed in a Twitter message that the network had canceled the results show for the season scheduled to start in May.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/new-reality-on-fox-hurry-up-and-dance/', 'snippet': 'Nigel Lythgoe, the executive producer of “So You Think You Can Dance,” revealed in a Twitter message that the network had canceled the results show for the season scheduled to start in May.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The reality show “So You Think You Can Dance” is getting shorter. Weeks or maybe months before Fox would have announced the change, the program’s executive producer, Nigel Lythgoe, disclosed in a Twitter message on Sunday that the network had canceled the results show for the season scheduled to start in May. “I will have to change the format,” he added. Fox previously split the show into two nights, revealing the weekly results a day after the competitions. The eighth season, last year, lost ground to another summer competition, “America’s Got Talent” on NBC, but it remains an important piece of Fox’s schedule. A Fox scheduling executive said on Twitter on Monday that the reasons for the shortening would be explained “in due time.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Reality on Fox: Hurry Up and Dance', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lythgoe, Nigel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T19:42:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7ba6af9-1d08-54a4-b5f9-451ec060842e', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7ba6af9-1d08-54a4-b5f9-451ec060842e'}, {'abstract': 'Welcome to our coverage of the 2012 Winter Classic between the Rangers and the Flyers.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/welcome-to-the-winter-classic/', 'snippet': 'Welcome to our coverage of the 2012 Winter Classic between the Rangers and the Flyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brad Richards, the Rangers’ prized off-season acquisition, scored early in the third period to lift the Rangers to a 3-2 victory against the Flyers in the Winter Classic at Citizens Bank Park on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Analysis: Rangers Win Winter Classic', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens Bank Park (Philadelphia, Pa)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bobrovsky, Sergei', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryzgalov, Ilya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staal, Marc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Flyers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T19:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98af3a3f-4b11-5d76-94ae-11ddd544bede', 'word_count': 3150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98af3a3f-4b11-5d76-94ae-11ddd544bede'}, {'abstract': 'New year, new Academy Awards poster, but the celebrity-industrial complex chugs on.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/were-baa-ack-and-the-academy-is-too/', 'snippet': 'New year, new Academy Awards poster, but the celebrity-industrial complex chugs on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bagger may have taken last week off, but the celebrity-industrial complex never rests. Meryl Streep earned kudos from the Kennedy Center and will receive an honorary Golden Bear from the Berlin Film Festival next month. The Palm Springs International Film Festival also announced yet more honorees – Charlize Theron, Jessica Chastain and Howard Shore join most of the season’s other lauded performers. And the Academy signaled once again that it is not trying to shake things up this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We’re Baa-ack, and the Academy Is, Too', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chastain, Jessica', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crystal, Billy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plummer, Christopher', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sherak, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shore, Howard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Meryl', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Theron, Charlize', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T19:45:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63872864-eee2-5590-a3a3-caaabbbd725b', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63872864-eee2-5590-a3a3-caaabbbd725b'}, {'abstract': 'My mistakes, and those of Heritage.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/mistakes-and-how-to-deal-with-them/', 'snippet': 'My mistakes, and those of Heritage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So Alex Tabarrok thinks he has a great gotcha in my warnings about deficits and interest rates from 2003. Except, I’ve already acknowledged that mistake:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mistakes and How To Deal With Them', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T19:51:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebd725d1-25ef-5b2b-912d-ec9b578ecf84', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebd725d1-25ef-5b2b-912d-ec9b578ecf84'}, {'abstract': 'Sonoma State University has announced details about the opening of its new music hall, including a partnership with the San Francisco Symphony.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/lang-lang-to-play-at-sonoma-state-opening/', 'snippet': 'Sonoma State University has announced details about the opening of its new music hall, including a partnership with the San Francisco Symphony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the financier Sanford I. Weill wanted a sense of what the music hall being built at Sonoma State University would sound like, he asked a friend, the pianist Lang Lang, to stop by to play. Mr. Weill liked what he heard, so he and his wife, Joan, went on to donate $12 million toward the project’s $130 million cost. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lang Lang to Play at Sonoma State Opening', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lang Lang', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weill, Sanford I', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Symphony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T19:51:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad6eed9d-5ff7-5549-adc6-8e88f8118086', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad6eed9d-5ff7-5549-adc6-8e88f8118086'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Lander laid the groundwork for a joint venture between two fierce rivals: Harvard and M.I.T.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/science/broad-institute-collaboration-began-with-a-disastrous-lunch.html', 'snippet': 'Eric Lander laid the groundwork for a joint venture between two fierce rivals: Harvard and M.I.T.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the annals of academic rivalries, perhaps none is fiercer than the crosstown one between Harvard and the Massachusetts Institute of Technology. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03BROA/03BROA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03BROA/03BROA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03BROA/03BROA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 