 only 5 spots for best picture, when 10 can be nominated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Oscar nomination ballots were mailed out last week – they are due back on Jan. 13 – and the new voting rules are already causing problems. It’s not quite a debacle on the order of hanging chads, but as Scott Feinberg writes at The Hollywood Reporter, some voters are perplexed about why the ballot only has five spaces for best picture, when there can be up to 10 nominees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oscar Ballot Doesn’t Add Up for Some Voters', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Condon, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T20:15:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ef6a1ae-e5a8-5e9a-a670-b1e8adc3fff5', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ef6a1ae-e5a8-5e9a-a670-b1e8adc3fff5'}, {'abstract': 'In a study of 30,000 men and women, those whose rates increased over a decade were almost twice as likely to die of heart disease.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/health/research/rise-in-resting-heart-rate-linked-to-coronary-artery-disease.html', 'snippet': 'In a study of 30,000 men and women, those whose rates increased over a decade were almost twice as likely to die of heart disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A large study has found that a rise in resting heart rate over a decade may indicate an increased risk of death from coronary artery disease.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Risks: Resting Hear