ority — and food is medicine. But doctors mete out meals with caution, providing fewer calories than needed at first because the patients may be so frail that major swings in diet can be life-threatening. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03ANOR/03ANOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03ANOR/03ANOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03ANOR/03ANOR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Protocol to Treat Anorexia Is Faulted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protocol To Treat Anorexia Is Faulted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eating Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANOREXIA NERVOSA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T21:16:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b63826c-3de9-57c5-bc3a-14799d584262', 'word_count': 1085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b63826c-3de9-57c5-bc3a-14799d584262'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney is using a well-worn joke about his wife falling on “da butt in Dubuque.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/romney-sounds-increasingly-confident-in-iowa/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney is using a well-worn joke about his wife falling on “da butt in Dubuque.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBUQUE, Iowa — Ann Romney fell on her bottom in Dubuque four years ago, and her husband can’t stop talking about it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Sounds Increasingly Confident in Iowa', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T21:18:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3d215cd-5d93-523a-b5d6-eb9fd6a4c1a6', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3d215cd-5d93-523a-b5d6-eb9fd6a4c1a6'}, {'abstract': 'In “Pity the Billionaire” Thomas Frank gives his take on how the right has turned the country’s economic woes to its benefit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/books/thomas-franks-pity-the-billionaire-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Pity the Billionaire” Thomas Frank gives his take on how the right has turned the country’s economic woes to its benefit.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Pity the Billionaire,” by Thomas Frank, is a showcase example of the problems that can be created by the long lead time (six to nine months or more if a project has not been fast-tracked) involved in publishing a topical book in an age when news is instantaneous, and there is 24/7, wall-to-wall coverage of hot-button issues. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/arts/jp-book/jp-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 762, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/arts/jp-book/jp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/arts/jp-book/jp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Conservatives Spin the Nation’s Predicament', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Liberal Does His Spin On Conservatives’ Spin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frank, Thomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T21:22:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bba510b-c514-5db9-895c-1b2e860181a3', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bba510b-c514-5db9-895c-1b2e860181a3'}, {'abstract': 'What started as a nauseating task to behead a chicken ends as a date in court for a Brooklyn man.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/out-of-the-kitchen-and-into-a-bit-of-trouble/', 'snippet': 'What started as a nauseating task to behead a chicken ends as a date in court for a Brooklyn man.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blame it on the chicken. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out of the Kitchen and Into a Bit of Trouble', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bedford-Stuyvesant (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T21:24:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noah Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61f2e85b-49e0-5f1a-95fa-610f826e406f', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61f2e85b-49e0-5f1a-95fa-610f826e406f'}, {'abstract': 'Laurie Garrett of the Council on Foreign Relations talks about bioterrorism and the public policy implications of a deadly bird flu threat.', 'web_url': 'https://consults.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/a-public-policy-expert-looks-at-the-bird-flu-threat/', 'snippet': 'Laurie Garrett of the Council on Foreign Relations talks about bioterrorism and the public policy implications of a deadly bird flu threat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Responding to experiments in the Netherlands and the United States in which scientists created a highly transmissible form of the potentially deadly H5N1 bird flu virus, the National Science Advisory Board for Biosecurity urged scientific journals not to publish details of the work out of fear that the information could be used by terrorists. Laurie Garrett, senior fellow for global health at the Council on Foreign Relations and a recipient of a 1996 Pulitzer Prize for her coverage of an Ebola epidemic, responds to questions about the public policy implications of bird flu and bioterrorism. Her latest book, “I Heard the Sirens Scream,” offers a detailed account of the 2001 anthrax attacks and the bioterrorism policy actions that resulted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Public Policy Expert Looks at the Bird Flu Threat', 'kicker': 'Consults', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viruses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T21:28:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91b23bff-2360-5c48-8c89-10e3aa11f7c8', 'word_count': 1112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91b23bff-2360-5c48-8c89-10e3aa11f7c8'}, {'abstract': 'Contagion depends on a complex interplay between a virus and its victim, including where it enters the body, the types of cells in which it can reproduce and whether it can then escape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/health/an-explanation-of-how-avian-flu-spreads.html', 'snippet': 'Contagion depends on a complex interplay between a virus and its victim, including where it enters the body, the types of cells in which it can reproduce and whether it can then escape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recent reports that two teams of scientists had genetically altered a deadly flu virus to make it more contagious have provoked fear, even outrage, in some quarters.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03FLU/03FLU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03FLU/03FLU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03FLU/03FLU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Hard Would It Be for Avian Flu to Spread?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Hard Would It Be For Avian Flu To Spread?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viruses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T21:28:59+0000',