 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e183707-eb6e-5670-8fb7-219f1eea20a7', 'word_count': 893, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e183707-eb6e-5670-8fb7-219f1eea20a7'}, {'abstract': 'In her latest blog post, Laura Klein writes: In the past, I dreamed of plucking my students from their miserable homes and finding solutions to their problems. I felt powerful and capable, as though I would be able to offer them something better. Now I know that the best I might do is to just be there when they return from their holiday break, offering them something steady and certain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/02/sometimes-you-have-to-settle-for-just-being-there/', 'snippet': 'In her latest blog post, Laura Klein writes: In the past, I dreamed of plucking my students from their miserable homes and finding solutions to their problems. I felt powerful and capable, as though I would be able to offer them something better. ...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sometimes You Have to Settle for Just Being There', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T21:40:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By LAURA KLEIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KLEIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39e6d5bf-842e-529c-bf40-6b73f8754ab0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39e6d5bf-842e-529c-bf40-6b73f8754ab0'}, {'abstract': 'Blindfolded experts who listened to violins made by old masters and high-quality modern instruments couldn’t tell the difference between them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/science/in-play-off-between-old-and-new-violins-stradivarius-lags.html', 'snippet': 'Blindfolded experts who listened to violins made by old masters and high-quality modern instruments couldn’t tell the difference between them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What gives a violin made by Stradivari or Guarneri del Gesù its remarkable sound? Researchers have examined the wood preservatives, varnish, even the effects of the Little Ice Age on the density of wood, for anything that might explain the instruments’ almost magical properties. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03VIOL/03VIOL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 488, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03VIOL/03VIOL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03VIOL/03VIOL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Classic vs. Modern Violins, Beauty Is in Ear of the Beholder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Classic vs. Modern Violins, Beauty Is in Ear of the Beholder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Violins', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T22:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Wade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0279cd45-bab9-5bf3-8bb6-fcb4641b9778', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0279cd45-bab9-5bf3-8bb6-fcb4641b9778'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers have found that prolonged droughts and soil overuse may have led to the decline of the ancient city of Angkor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/science/angkor-seat-of-the-khmer-empire-wilted-when-water-ran-low.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers have found that prolonged droughts and soil overuse may have led to the decline of the ancient city of Angkor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Angkor, the ancient city in Cambodia that was the seat of the Khmer empire, flourished from the 9th to the 15th century. Today, tourists still appreciate the remnants of its architecture and sophisticated hydro-engineering systems, composed of canals, moats and large reservoirs known as barays.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03OBWATER3/03OBOX3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03OBWATER3/03OBWATER3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/science/03OBWATER3/03OBW