ne, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40e2ed4e-5efa-5a40-9ee7-3826c5b3731f', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40e2ed4e-5efa-5a40-9ee7-3826c5b3731f'}, {'abstract': 'She announced on New Year’s Eve that the concert was her last at the Bowery Ballroom.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/patti-smith-ends-bowery-residency/', 'snippet': 'She announced on New Year’s Eve that the concert was her last at the Bowery Ballroom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As 2011 recedes in the rear-view mirror and the weekend’s confetti is swept away, we note as well the passing of another tradition. On New Year’s Eve, Patti Smith announced from the stage at the Bowery Ballroom that the concert was her last — at the Bowery Ballroom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Patti Smith Ends Bowery Residency', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Patti', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bowery Ballroom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bowery (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T22:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel M. Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37e597b5-d677-529d-92a4-eb413ebe3b6a', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37e597b5-d677-529d-92a4-eb413ebe3b6a'}, {'abstract': 'The Dolphins’ Taylor, who is retiring, said: “I don’t deserve it. You know Don Shula deserves to be carried off this field, Dan Marino does, Zach Thomas deserved to be carried off this field.”', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/jason-taylor-on-being-carried-off-the-field/', 'snippet': 'The Dolphins’ Taylor, who is retiring, said: “I don’t deserve it. You know Don Shula deserves to be carried off this field, Dan Marino does, Zach Thomas deserved to be carried off this field.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter your rooting interest, it was nice to see teams that were already eliminated compete so fiercely in Week 17. The Dolphins, the Chargers and the Chiefs fought the good fight, and won. The league is smart to schedule divisional games on the final weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jason Taylor on Being Carried Off the Field', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-02T22:17:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/408114c1-624e-579b-a343-5334d91d65c9', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/408114c1-624e-579b-a343-5334d91d65c9'}, {'abstract': 'In the Democratic Republic of Congo, the French term délestage is used to describe power cutoffs, but when applied to food shortages, it illustrates a stark reality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/world/africa/in-congolese-capital-power-cut-applies-to-food.html', 'snippet': 'In the Democratic Republic of Congo, the French term délestage is used to describe power cutoffs, but when applied to food shortages, it illustrates a stark reality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KINSHASA, Democratic Republic of Congo — Today, the big children will eat, Cynthia, 15, and Guellor, 13. Tomorrow, it will be the turn of the little ones, Bénédicte, Josiane and Manassé, 3, 6, and 9. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/JP-KINSHASA/JP-KINSHASA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/03/world/JP-KINSHASA/JP-KINSHASA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/JP-KINSHASA/JP-KINSHASA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/JP-KINSHASA/JP-KINSHASA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/world/JP-KINSHASA/JP-KINSHASA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Congo Children, Food Today Means None Tomorrow', 'kicker': 'Kinshasa Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Congo Children, Food Today Means None Tomorrow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rationing and Allocation of Resources', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malnutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Congo, Democratic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Famine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subjec