 'nyt://article/695b9311-eb3a-538a-909e-0fdf54b58009'}, {'abstract': 'Occupy protesters go after the Democratic Party, showing that they are equal opportunity agitators.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/democrats-become-target-of-occupy-protests/', 'snippet': 'Occupy protesters go after the Democratic Party, showing that they are equal opportunity agitators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In what Occupy the Caucus members called a symbolic “die-in,” 12 protesters lay motionless on the lobby floor of the Renaissance Des Moines Savory Hotel Monday afternoon before getting arrested. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Become Target of Occupy Protests', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schultz, Debbie Wasserman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic National Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:09:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad1046b8-1d74-572e-8bd5-046869804e04', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad1046b8-1d74-572e-8bd5-046869804e04'}, {'abstract': 'In “Jane by Design,” a new drama on ABC Family, a teenage girl who stumbles into a job in the fashion world is emotionally manipulated, professionally undermined and romanced by louses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/arts/television/jane-by-design-on-abc-family-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Jane by Design,” a new drama on ABC Family, a teenage girl who stumbles into a job in the fashion world is emotionally manipulated, professionally undermined and romanced by louses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1980s the most dangerous place for a teenage American girl to be was in a horror movie. The wider the eyes and the rosier the cheeks, the more certain it was that she would meet a grisly fate.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/arts/jane/jane-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 234, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/arts/jane/jane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/arts/jane/jane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A High School Naïf Doubles as a Competent Career Gal', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A High School Naïf Doubles As a Competent Career Gal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC Family', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacDowell, Andie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:21:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/43a979a9-ed45-5ee7-bbfc-1e4ebf035062', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43a979a9-ed45-5ee7-bbfc-1e4ebf035062'}, {'abstract': 'The notion that any European Union nation can block a law is giving way to a new approach in which a group of countries can adopt laws among themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/world/europe/future-in-mind-europeans-plan-for-less-unanimity.html', 'snippet': 'The notion that any European Union nation can block a law is giving way to a new approach in which a group of countries can adopt laws among themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — For decades, any European Union nation could block proposed laws in the most delicate policy areas, like taxation, consigning them to the scrap heap if they encroached too much on its power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/BRUSSELS/BRUSSELS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/BRUSSELS/BRUSSELS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/world/BRUSSELS/BRUSSELS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europeans Planning for Less Unanimity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europeans Planning for Less Unanimity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'valu