'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:37:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc5ca299-8a19-5154-acc9-431fd55fca8c', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc5ca299-8a19-5154-acc9-431fd55fca8c'}, {'abstract': 'The Walnut Street Theater in Philadelphia will present the American premiere of “Love Story, The Musical” in September.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/theater/love-story-the-musical-heading-to-philadelphia.html', 'snippet': 'The Walnut Street Theater in Philadelphia will present the American premiere of “Love Story, The Musical” in September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Walnut Street Theater in Philadelphia will present the American premiere of “Love Story, The Musical” in September. Based on Erich Segal’s novel and movie, the musical has a book and lyrics by Stephen Clark and music and additional lyrics by Howard Goodall. After a sold-out season at the Chichester Festival Theater in England, the show transferred in December 2010 to London’s West End, where it was nominated for three Olivier Awards.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Love Story, the Musical’ Heading to Philadelphia', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Love Story, The Musical’ Heading to Philadelphia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Street Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:38:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb3fa891-7c94-54b3-b828-0a06b2c49660', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb3fa891-7c94-54b3-b828-0a06b2c49660'}, {'abstract': 'In a case that has gripped Scandinavia, “lost fragments” of work by Henrik Ibsen are suspected to have been forged.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/theater/ibsen-fragments-under-scrutiny.html', 'snippet': 'In a case that has gripped Scandinavia, “lost fragments” of work by Henrik Ibsen are suspected to have been forged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a case that has gripped Scandinavia, “lost fragments” of work by Henrik Ibsen, above, are suspected to have been forged. An economic crimes unit in Norway is looking for possessions and letters that supposedly relate to Ibsen, and to Knut Hamsun, a Nobel-winning novelist and Nazi sympathizer, The Observer of London has reported. Geir Ove Kvalheim, a Norwegian scriptwriter and actor, has been charged with forging more than a dozen documents and is scheduled for trial in April. The case began when Mr. Kvalheim said he had found fragments of a previously unknown Ibsen play, “The Sun God,” a discovery that would have changed literary history. News reports say that Mr. Kvalheim, who could face up to six years in prison if convicted of the offense, has refused to comment on the charges.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ibsen ‘Fragments’ Under Scrutiny', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ibsen ‘Fragments’ Under Scrutiny', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibsen, Henrik', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forgery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1711eed-866b-5b55-b3b7-534a69e7dfe7', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1711eed-866b-5b55-b3b7-534a69e7dfe7'}, {'abstract': 'Eric G. Pryor has been named the new executive director of the Center for Arts Education.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/arts/arts-education-center-names-new-executive.html', 'snippet': 'Eric G. Pryor has been named the new executive director of the Center for Arts Education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric G. Pryor has been named the new executive director of the Center for Arts Education, the organization’s board announced on Monday. The center provides programs, professional development and advocacy for New York City’s public schools. Mr. Pryor previously served as executive director of the New Jersey State Museum and as president of the Visual Arts Center of New Jersey. He succeeds Richard Kessler, who became the dean of Mannes College the New School for Music in August.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arts Education Center Names New Executive', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arts Education Center Names New Executive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Arts Education', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:39:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccb6b076-77d9-58d2-9bfc-6987a9535283', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccb6b076-77d9-58d2-9bfc-6987a9535283'}, {'abstract': 'American premieres of the Philip Glass opera “Kepler” and of John Cage’s 1991 orchestral trilogy, “Twenty-six, Twenty-eight and Twenty-nine,” will be featured at the Spoleto Festival USA.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/arts/music/a-packed-schedule-for-spoleto-festival.html', 'snippet': 'American premieres of the Philip Glass opera “Kepler” and of John Cage’s 1991 orchestral trilogy, “Twenty-six, Twenty-eight and Twenty-nine,” will be featured at the Spoleto Festival USA.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American premieres of the Philip Glass opera “Kepler” and of John Cage’s 1991 orchestral trilogy, “Twenty-six, Twenty-eight and Twenty-nine,” will be featured at the Spoleto Festival USA, which runs from May 25 through June 10 in Charleston, S.C. The festival’s schedule will also include Mike Daisey’s solo shows “The Agony and the Ecstasy of Steve Jobs” and “Teching in India”; Les 7 Doigts de la Main’s “Traces”; a production of Noël Coward’s “Hay Fever” by the Gate Theater of Dublin; and “Making Up the Truth” by Jack Hitt. In addition to Mr. Glass’s opera, directed by Sam Helfrich, Spoleto will offer the American premiere of “Feng Yi Ting,” a contemporary Chinese opera by the composer Guo Wenjing and directed by Atom Egoyan. Additional concerts will be given by K. D. Lang and Mavis Staples, and dance performances will include works from Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Packed Schedule For Spoleto Festival', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Packed Schedule For Spoleto Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spoleto Festival USA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:40:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/06721431-1071-5957-8cf6-5d7ff63042a8', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06721431-1071-5957-8cf6-5d7ff63042a8'}, {'abstract': 'Two companies plan to use novel solar storage technology to power households on summer nights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/business/energy-environment/building-storehouses-for-the-suns-energy-for-use-after-dark.html', 'snippet': 'Two companies plan to use novel solar storage technology to power households on summer nights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If solar energy is eventually going to matter — that is, generate a significant portion of the nation’s electricity — the industry must overcome a major stumbling block, experts say: finding a way to store it for use when the sun isn’t shining.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/business/STORAGE/STORAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/03/business/STORAGE/STORAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/business/STORAGE/STORAGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 583, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/business/STORAGE/STORAGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/business/STORAGE/STORAGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Storehouses for Solar Energy Can Step In When the Sun Goes Down', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Storehouses for Solar Energy Can Step In When the Sun Goes Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BrightSource Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:41:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0188b036-c982-50d2-b891-93054fb01fa5', 'word_count': 1255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0188b036-c982-50d2-b891-93054fb01fa5'}, {'abstract': 'Speaking to a crowd of several hundred Mitt Romney urged voters to come out on caucus night, proclaiming he was going to “win this thing.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/romney-confident-winning-iowa/', 'snippet': 'Speaking to a crowd of several hundred Mitt Romney urged voters to come out on caucus night, proclaiming he was going to “win this thing.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'MARION, Iowa — Mitt Romney told a Cedar Rapids crowd Monday that President Obama is great — at some things. “I watch a president who’s become the great divider, the great complainer, the great excuse-giver, the great blamer,” Mr. Romney said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Confident of Winning — Something', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:42:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f7c9ad1-eca8-5db2-8f01-a38eafe54c1e', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f7c9ad1-eca8-5db2-8f01-a38eafe54c1e'}, {'abstract': 'An eastern Iowa city known for its moderate politics draws three presidential candidates in one day.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/davenport-becomes-a-magnet-for-candidates/', 'snippet': 'An eastern Iowa city known for its moderate politics draws three presidential candidates in one day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVENPORT, Iowa – It took Carolyn Barry nearly until the caucuses to make up her mind. But her flirtations with a series of other candidates seemed a thing of the past as she enthusiastically shook Mitt Romney’s hand while wearing a campaign button that spoke to suddenly solid support. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Davenport Becomes a Magnet for Candidates', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Des Moines (IA)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:44:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. G. Sulzberger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Sulzberger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07144dab-ea64-57c5-b466-fe62db80decc', 'word_count': 862, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07144dab-ea64-57c5-b466-fe62db80decc'}, {'abstract': 'Designating Boko Haram as a foreign terrorist group will only inflame anti-Americanism among Nigerian Muslims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/opinion/in-nigeria-boko-haram-is-not-the-problem.html', 'snippet': 'Designating Boko Haram as a foreign terrorist group will only inflame anti-Americanism among Nigerian Muslims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GOVERNMENTS and newspapers around the world attributed the horrific Christmas Day bombings of churches in Nigeria to “Boko Haram” — a shadowy group that is routinely described as an extremist Islamist organization based in the northeast corner of Nigeria. Indeed, since the May inauguration of President Goodluck Jonathan, a Christian from the Niger Delta in the country’s south, Boko Haram has been blamed for virtually every outbreak of violence in Nigeria.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Nigeria, Boko Haram Is Not the Problem', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Nigeria, Boko Haram Is Not the Problem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boko Haram', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jonathan, Goodluck', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:49:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jean Herskovits', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herskovits', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec49bfff-1349-5bf7-8036-1cdfc5fe3b67', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec49bfff-1349-5bf7-8036-1cdfc5fe3b67'}, {'abstract': 'A lockout in a contract dispute affects about 465 workers at an Electro-Motive locomotive factory in London, Ontario, that Caterpillar acquired in 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/business/workers-locked-out-at-caterpillar-locomotive-plant-in-canada.html', 'snippet': 'A lockout in a contract dispute affects about 465 workers at an Electro-Motive locomotive factory in London, Ontario, that Caterpillar acquired in 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA — A lockout late Sunday of about 465 workers at a Canadian locomotive factory owned by a Caterpillar unit has renewed debate in Canada about the labor impact of foreign ownership.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caterpillar Locks Out Workers in Canada', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Caterpillar Locks Out Workers In Canada', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Canadian Auto Workers Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Caterpillar Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:51:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/457cdcb0-6008-5174-aaac-0c42c6515f2b', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/457cdcb0-6008-5174-aaac-0c42c6515f2b'}, {'abstract': 'Teva Pharmaceutical Industries of Israel named Jeremy Levin of Bristol-Myers Squibb as its next chief executive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/business/teva-names-a-new-chief-executive.html', 'snippet': 'Teva Pharmaceutical Industries of Israel named Jeremy Levin of Bristol-Myers Squibb as its next chief executive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Teva Pharmaceutical Industries of Israel named Jeremy Levin of Bristol-Myers Squibb as its next chief executive, replacing Shlomo Yanai. Mr. Levin, 58, a doctor educated at the University of Cambridge, worked at Bristol-Myers as senior vice president for strategy, alliances and transactions. He will take over as president and chief in May, Teva said in a statement, after Mr. Yanai, 59, retires. Teva’s shares plunged last year amid mounting competition for its No. 1 drug, a branded multiple sclerosis medicine called Copaxone. Mr. Yanai, a former Israeli army general with no previous pharmaceutical experience, spent $6.5 billion last year to buy the American biotechnology company Cephalon, then told investors in December that Teva might not able to meet its long-term target of $31 billion in sales by 2015. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teva Names a New Chief Executive', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Company News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Teva Names a New Chief Executive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:55:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0807c1f2-1f6c-5ff0-bec5-ba559319e8bc', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0807c1f2-1f6c-5ff0-bec5-ba559319e8bc'}, {'abstract': 'The fires, believed to have begun in Torres del Paine National Park last week, have also affected two other regions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/world/americas/sebastian-pinera-defends-response-to-chile-wildfires.html', 'snippet': 'The fires, believed to have begun in Torres del Paine National Park last week, have also affected two other regions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO DE JANEIRO — Wildfires swept through unseasonably hot, dry parts of southern Chile on Monday, as firefighters struggled to extinguish the blazes and as the government of Sebastián Piñera, Chile’s beleaguered billionaire president, defended its response. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/CHILE/CHILE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/03/world/CHILE/CHILE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/CHILE/CHILE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/CHILE/CHILE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/world/CHILE/CHILE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chile’s President Defends His Response to Wildfires', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chile’s President Defends His Response to Wildfires', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinera, Sebastian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forest and Brush Fires', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Torres del Paine National Park (Patagonia, Chile)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:56:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero and Pascale Bonnefoy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Pascale', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bonnefoy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0580e28e-3822-5ef8-97a9-ef84d55f161a', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0580e28e-3822-5ef8-97a9-ef84d55f161a'}, {'abstract': 'The 62 Queens Library branches, like other libraries serving large immigrant populations, have increased their collections in foreign languages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/nyregion/queens-libraries-serve-59-languages.html', 'snippet': 'The 62 Queens Library branches, like other libraries serving large immigrant populations, have increased their collections in foreign languages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best-selling biography of Steve Jobs is flying off the shelves at libraries in Queens, which is not surprising. But in many of the borough’s 62 branches, the copies being borrowed are in Korean, Chinese or Spanish.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/nyregion/LIBRARY1/LIBRARY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/03/nyregion/LIBRARY1/LIBRARY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/nyregion/LIBRARY1/LIBRARY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/nyregion/LIBRARY1/LIBRARY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/nyregion/LIBRARY1/LIBRARY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Queens Libraries Speak the Mother Tongue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Libraries Speak the Mother Tongue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Queens Borough Public Library', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T00:56:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1df1a6c3-71c4-5186-bcb6-1bafd2daeba9', 'word_count': 1221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1df1a6c3-71c4-5186-bcb6-1bafd2daeba9'}, {'abstract': 'New and unlimited reserves of cash from so-called independent groups are bankrolling a constant stream of negative political ads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/opinion/the-slush-funds-of-iowa.html', 'snippet': 'New and unlimited reserves of cash from so-called independent groups are bankrolling a constant stream of negative political ads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Turning on the television in Iowa recently has meant getting hit by an unrelenting arctic blast of campaign ads stunning in volume and ferocity. Residents here say they have never seen anything like the constant negativity in decades of witnessing the quadrennial combat of the state presidential caucuses. The ads have transformed the Republican race for a simple reason: a new landscape of unlimited contributions to “independent” groups that was created by the Supreme Court.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Slush Funds of Iowa', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Slush Funds of Iowa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T01:03:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/325fa9fc-91db-57f5-bbe5-e445a154ecfe', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/325fa9fc-91db-57f5-bbe5-e445a154ecfe'}, {'abstract': 'Pawnshops and gold dealers are thriving as cash-strapped Greeks give up valuables to make ends meet. But authorities say many of the shops are concealing a rapidly expanding illicit trade in gold.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/world/europe/as-greece-struggles-pawnbrokers-prosper.html', 'snippet': 'Pawnshops and gold dealers are thriving as cash-strapped Greeks give up valuables to make ends meet. But authorities say many of the shops are concealing a rapidly expanding illicit trade in gold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — With all the contraction in the Greek economy, with employees laid off en masse and one in four small businesses forced to close, it might seem odd that new shops are springing up like mushrooms in Athens and other cities.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Greece’s Sour Economy, Some Shops Are Thriving', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Greece’s Sour Economy, Some Shops Are Thriving', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pawnbroking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}