t all to lead the team to the N.F.C. East title.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/sports/football/giants-coach-tom-coughlin-set-in-ways-because-they-work.html', 'snippet': 'The Giants’ second-half swoons under Tom Coughlin have been well chronicled. Still, the coach weathered it all to lead the team to the N.F.C. East title.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — The notion that coaches in the N.F.L. have job security has always been something of a misconception. Positions are few. Expectations are high. Careers are short. And, generally, one can expect the current prevailing sentiment about a coach’s performance — whatever that sentiment might be — to have all the staying power of rent money.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/sports/JPGIANTS/JPGIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/03/sports/JPGIANTS/JPGIANTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/sports/JPGIANTS/JPGIANTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/sports/JPGIANTS/JPGIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/sports/JPGIANTS/JPGIANTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Coughlin Is Set in His Ways, Because They Work', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coach Set In Ways, Because They Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rolle, Antrel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T01:20:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/08c5067e-57e4-551c-961d-4eb9ecc45528', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08c5067e-57e4-551c-961d-4eb9ecc45528'}, {'abstract': 'A scandal in Germany flared anew when the country’s biggest newspaper confirmed that President Christian Wulff had made a menacing telephone call to its editor in an effort to snuff out a damaging story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/world/europe/german-presidents-call-to-paper-reignites-scandal-over-loan.html', 'snippet': 'A scandal in Germany flared anew when the country’s biggest newspaper confirmed that President Christian Wulff had made a menacing telephone call to its editor in an effort to snuff out a damaging story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A smoldering political scandal that could harm Chancellor Angela Merkel flared anew on Monday when Germany’s biggest newspaper confirmed that the president, Christian Wulff, had made a menacing telephone call to its editor in an unsuccessful effort to snuff out a damaging news story.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'German President’s Call to Paper Reignites Scandal Over Loan', 'kicker': None, 'c