’s suspect nuclear program, are creating new hurdles ahead of parliamentary elections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/world/middleeast/boycott-by-reformers-could-undermine-elections-in-iran.html', 'snippet': 'A likely boycott by harshly silenced reformists, combined with economic problems arising from Iran’s suspect nuclear program, are creating new hurdles ahead of parliamentary elections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iran’s conservative Islamic hierarchy has been seeking to portray the coming parliamentary elections as an enviable model of Middle East democracy and an inspiration for the Arab Spring revolts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/IRAN-1/IRAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/03/world/IRAN-1/IRAN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/IRAN-1/IRAN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/IRAN-1/IRAN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/world/IRAN-1/IRAN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Election Fears and Economic Woes Pose New Challenges for Iran’s Leaders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Election Fears and Economic Woes Pose New Challenges for Iran’s Leaders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T01:53:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f91d91b-6a69-5842-b039-5079728446ea', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f91d91b-6a69-5842-b039-5079728446ea'}, {'abstract': 'Reporting and policing can be a high adrenaline business. But the decade-long trajectory in New York is toward expanded police power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/nyregion/at-wall-street-protests-clash-of-reporting-and-policing.html', 'snippet': 'Reporting and policing can be a high adrenaline business. But the decade-long trajectory in New York is toward expanded police power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In late November, the police commissioner, Raymond W. Kelly, ordered every precinct in his domain to read a statement. Officers, the commissioner said, must “respect the public’s right to know about these events and the media’s right of access to report.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/nyregion/GOTHAM/GOTHAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rules on News Coverage Are Clear, but the Police Keep Pushing', 'kicker': 'Go