 Briere bore down on him on a penalty shot with 19.6 seconds remaining to seal the Rangers’ victory in the Winter Classic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — A boyhood fantasy came to life under an evening sky burnished by a chilly wind. More than 46,000 fans stood roaring at Citizens Bank Park in 38-degree temperatures as a national television audience sat in warm homes holding its breath. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/sports/CLASSIC2/CLASSIC2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/sports/CLASSIC2/CLASSIC2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/sports/CLASSIC2/CLASSIC2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Rangers’ Win at Ballpark, Lundqvist Gets the Save', 'kicker': 'Winter Classic: Rangers 3, Flyers 2', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Rangers’ Win at Ballpark, Lundqvist Gets the Save', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staal, Marc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Briere, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lundqvist, Henrik', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Flyers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T02:26:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/108c2754-fa9c-5ada-8c66-972511b3e9d5', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/108c2754-fa9c-5ada-8c66-972511b3e9d5'}, {'abstract': 'A officer’s wedding offers insight into Civil War Army politics.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/sam-oliver-gets-married/', 'snippet': 'A officer’s wedding offers insight into Civil War Army politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sam Oliver was going to be married. The recently widowed lieutenant colonel, 35 years old, had proposed to a young lady back home in Massachusetts and she accepted. Now he just needed to get time off from his duties along the Virginia section of the Washington defenses. On New Year’s Day 1862, he applied by letter for a three-week furlough. He submitted it to his commanding colonel, William Greene, who was pleased to comply — not because he wanted Oliver’s happiness, but because he wanted to get rid of him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sam Oliver Gets Married', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T02:30:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42358ff0-71ce-51a2-91d5-aab318f792c1', 'word_count': 1616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42358ff0-71ce-51a2-91d5-aab318f792c1'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of patients, including illegal immigrants, who are well enough to be discharged have languished in city hospitals for months or years because there is nowhere to send them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/nyregion/nowhere-to-go-patients-linger-in-hospitals-at-a-high-cost.html', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of patients, including illegal immigrants, who are well enough to be discharged have languished in city hospitals for months or years because there is nowhere to send them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hundreds of patients have been languishing for months or even years in New York City hospitals, despite being well enough to be sent home or to nursing centers for less-expensive care, because they are illegal immigrants or lack sufficient insurance or appropriate housing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/nyregion/jp-PATIENTS/jp-PATIENTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/nyregion/jp-PATIENTS/jp-PATIENTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/nyregion/jp-PATIENTS/jp-PATIENTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nowhere to Go, Patients Linger in Hospitals, at a High Cost', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nowhere to Go, Patients Linger In Hospitals, At a High Cost', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T02:32:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd6c3ed4-e867-5829-93b2-010611b99725', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd6c3ed4-e867-5829-93b2-010611b99725'}, {'abstract': 'The interim leaders took a step toward setting up a permanent government for the post-Qaddafi era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/world/africa/libya-sets-plan-for-assembly-on-constitution.html', 'snippet': 'The interim leaders took a step toward setting up a permanent government for the post-Qaddafi era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Libya’s interim government posted on its Web site a draft law laying out procedures for electing a planned constitutional assembly, taking a first step toward the establishment of a new government after the overthrow of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Libya Begins Plan to Elect Assembly', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Libya Begins Plan To Elect Assembly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T02:33:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fff6fd7-83e7-5dc3-b877-5559063b9796', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fff6fd7-83e7-5dc3-b877-5559063b9796'}, {'abstract': 'In one of Rhode Island’s poorer cities, a reading experiment flourishes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/opinion/nocera-the-central-falls-success.html', 'snippet': 'In one of Rhode Island’s poorer cities, a reading experiment flourishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Central Falls, R.I., is a speck of a city, one square mile of triple-decker houses and tired storefronts a few miles up the road from the state capital, Providence. It is the poorest city in Rhode Island, with 27 percent of its residents below the poverty line, according to the Census Bureau. Earlier this year, it started bankruptcy proceedings. Its mayor, who is the subject of a state police investigation, has been pushed aside in favor of a receiver, who has taken control of the city’s finances.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subTyp