 England in the Olympics and went on to help create some of Hollywood’s greatest sword fights, choreographing bladework and coaching actors from Errol Flynn to Antonio Banderas, and who appeared on-screen himself as Darth Vader, crossing lightsabers with Mark Hamill (as Luke Skywalker) in the original “Star Wars” trilogy, died on Sunday in West Sussex, England. He was 89.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/arts/ANDERSON-obit/ANDERSON-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 614, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/arts/ANDERSON-obit/ANDERSON-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/arts/ANDERSON-obit/ANDERSON-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bob Anderson, Sword Master, Dies at 89', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bob Anderson, Sword Master, Dies at 89', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fencing (Sport)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stunts and Stuntmen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swords', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, BOB', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T02:43:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'fir