ng along.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/sports/football/jets-rex-ryan-says-he-missed-signs-of-dissension.html', 'snippet': 'After a disappointing season that ended in three straight losses, Jets Coach Rex Ryan blamed himself for not realizing that players were not getting along.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — On the first morning of the Jets’ off-season, Darrelle Revis refused to speak with reporters, barking, “Leave me alone,” as he left the locker room. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/sports/JPJETS/JPJETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 976, 'width': 781, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Jets, Anger and Issues Linger', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Jets, Anger and Issues Linger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, Santonio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tannenbaum, Mike', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T02:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/06099462-e46d-5759-bbda-69bf9c2628de', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06099462-e46d-5759-bbda-69bf9c2628de'}, {'abstract': 'Though Ms. Yarkoni became famous for entertaining the troops during Israel’s wars, she later criticized the military and tried to forge a legacy as an advocate for peace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/arts/music/yaffa-yarkoni-86-who-sang-for-israeli-wartime-troops-is-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Though Ms. Yarkoni became famous for entertaining the troops during Israel’s wars, she later criticized the military and tried to forge a legacy as an advocate for peace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Yaffa Yarkoni, an Israeli singer who became famous for entertaining the troops during Israel’s wars but later criticized the military and tried to forge a legacy as an advocate for peace, died Sunday in Tel Aviv. She was 86. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/YARKONI-obit/YARKONI-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/world/YARKONI-obit/YARKONI-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/world/YARKONI-obit/YARKONI-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yaffa Yarkoni, Who Sang for Israeli Soldiers, Dies at 86', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yaffa Yarkoni, 86; Sang for Israeli Soldiers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T02:52:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a4af4df-acbd-520f-a4b3-957d9349bde9', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a4af4df-acbd-520f-a4b3-957d9349bde9'}, {'abstract': 'A few states raised their minimum wages on New Year’s Day. At a time of increasing inequality, the federal minimum needs a boost, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/opinion/falling-behind.html', 'snippet': 'A few states raised their minimum wages on New Year’s Day. At a time of increasing inequality, the federal minimum needs a boost, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, Washington became the first state to have a minimum wage above $9 an hour, $9.04 to be exact. Seven other states also had increases on New Year’s Day because they, too, adjust their minimum wages to keep pace with rising costs. In Oregon, the hourly minimum rose to $8.80; in Colorado to $7.64, with the wages in Arizona, Florida, Montana, Ohio and Vermont in between. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Falling Behind', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Falling Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T02:53:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f71669c4-9831-5a0b-a873-716fb103c0b5', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f71669c4-9831-5a0b-a873-716fb103c0b5'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine Poetry is experiencing a bit of success ahead of its 100th birthday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/opinion/keeping-the-muse-in-business.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine Poetry is experiencing a bit of success ahead of its 100th birthday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s nearly a century since the magazine Poetry was founded on uncertain prospects and an “open door” promise: “May the great poet we are looking for never find it shut.” Across the decades, the slim, challenging magazine has survived, publishing all manner of startling new poets, including T.S. Eliot, Langston Hughes, Wallace Stevens, Gwendolyn Brooks, Ezra Pound and Marianne Moore. Robert Frost happily celebrated its first decade in a subscription blurb urging readers to try Poetry as the “best boost” ever for struggling versifiers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping the Muse in Business', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keeping the Muse in Business', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Poetry (Magazine)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiman, Christian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lilly, Ruth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T02:58:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/daf68db0-6739-5fed-9bb3-35eb72d0d0eb', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daf68db0-6739-5fed-9bb3-35eb72d0d0eb'}, {'abstract': 'Allan E. Parrish gets mixed up.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/female/', 'snippet': 'Allan E. Parrish gets mixed up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — Happy Blogiversary! One year ago, my first Wordplay post went live, and life as I knew it has not been the same since. I went into detail about my start here the other day so I won’t bore you with it again, but I would like to thank you all once again for being such an important part of the New York Times crossword world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday: Male and Female', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T03:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46fe5db5-7d64-5d4e-8024-510071754097', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46fe5db5-7d64-5d4e-8024-510071754097'}, {'abstract': 'Competing histories across the Strait of Gibraltar contribute to its peculiar arrangement of exclaves.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/02/fighting-over-parsley/', 'snippet': 'Competing histories across the Strait of Gibraltar contribute to its peculiar arrangement of exclaves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On July 11, 2002, six Moroccan gendarmes occupied Isla de Perejil [1], or Parsley Island, an uninhabited, Spanish-administered rock of about 37 acres, just 220 yards off the Moroccan coast. If the standoff had lasted longer than a few days, and if blood had actually been spilled, we might now know it as the Parsley War. But on July 18, they were overwhelmed and forcibly ejected by Equipo 31, a crack team of Spanish special forces soldiers. No shots were fired. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Over Parsley', 'kicker': 'Borderlines', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parsley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gibraltar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Morocco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T03:01:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c78fff49-f68e-5859-8874-564446a6dc88', 'word_count': 1889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c78fff49-f68e-5859-8874-564446a6dc88'}, {'abstract': 'Rex Ryan’s most glaring deficiency: How can he claim to have a firm command of his team if he too often doesn’t have control of himself?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/sports/football/rex-r