tion was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the Modern Love essay “A Once-Upon-a-Time Romance.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Jan. 3, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T09:29:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68f08aae-9e2f-5ea9-9eb9-415995c7feba', 'word_count': 44, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68f08aae-9e2f-5ea9-9eb9-415995c7feba'}, {'abstract': '6 Q’s About the News | What is the significance of the Iowa primary election?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/all-eyes-on-iowa/', 'snippet': '6 Q’s About the News | What is the significance of the Iowa primary election?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHERE are Republican voters making their “final inspection” of presidential hopefuls?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'All Eyes on Iowa', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T09:59:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eb54ac0-bf43-540d-82c9-e4904bc09b62', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eb54ac0-bf43-540d-82c9-e4904bc09b62'}, {'abstract': 'Josh Haner has spent the last few weeks covering the Republication presidential campaign in Iowa. At first, he played it safe. But when he got bored, the creativity blossomed.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/on-the-campain-trail-in-iowa/', 'snippet': 'Josh Haner has spent the last few weeks covering the Republication presidential campaign in Iowa. At first, he played it safe. But when he got bored, the creativity blossomed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Josh Haner, a staff photographer for The New York Times, has been covering the Republican presidential campaign in Iowa since Dec. 11. This is the first time Mr. Haner, one of the Lens blog’s co-editors, has covered a presidential campaign. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Campaign Trail in Iowa', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T10:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8246a22-cddb-55a1-9062-b65c18b1d248', 'word_count': 1134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8246a22-cddb-55a1-9062-b65c18b1d248'}, {'abstract': 'Tuesday’s Lens blog features a conversation with Mr. Haner, one of the Lens blog’s co-editors, about the task of making a good picture in spite of the theatricality. Sometimes that means embracing it.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/on-lens-in-iowa-with-times-photographer-josh-haner/', 'snippet': 'Tuesday’s Lens blog features a conversation with Mr. Haner, one of the Lens blog’s co-editors, about the task of making a good picture in spite of the theatricality. Sometimes that means embracing it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Josh Haner, a staff photographer for The New York Times, has been trekking through ice cream factories and coffee shops throughout Iowa on a politics assignment since mid-December. This is the first time Mr. Haner has tackled a presidential campaign, and he’s learning as he goes. Whether in Algona or in Urbandale, it turns out, there’s more to a picture than a podium.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Lens: In Iowa With Times Photographer Josh Haner', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T10:01:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da2096aa-cc2c-523e-a104-aeacaa8f73e0', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da2096aa-cc2c-523e-a104-aeacaa8f73e0'}, {'abstract': 'Student Opinion | Do you think it’s possible to change your life through New Year’s resolutions? Did you make any this year?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/do-you-make-new-years-resolutions/', 'snippet': 'Student Opinion | Do you think it’s possible to change your life through New Year’s resolutions? Did you make any this year?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Happy New Year! Do you see the start of 2012 as an opportunity to improve your life? Have you made any changes or resolutions? Do you want to? If not, why not?  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Make New Year’s Resolutions?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T10:03:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstnam