ws', '_id': 'nyt://article/12dbd7e7-aa78-56ad-937e-5e6c3a67bb43', 'word_count': 1468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12dbd7e7-aa78-56ad-937e-5e6c3a67bb43'}, {'abstract': 'Artbanka Museum of Young Art, a recently opened space, showcases the work of graduate students and professors at Czech art academies.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/in-prague-a-showcase-for-art-students-and-professors/', 'snippet': 'Artbanka Museum of Young Art, a recently opened space, showcases the work of graduate students and professors at Czech art academies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Murdered garden gnomes in a Baroque palace in Prague? No, that’s not the premise of some bizarre television show. It is one of the 350 works on view at the\xa0 Artbanka Museum of Young Art (www.artbanka.cz), whose exhibition space showcases the work of graduate students and professors at Czech art academies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Prague, a Showcase for Art Students and Professors', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T11:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacy Meyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8de4b60-2b3e-5d58-ab0c-9e429264e3bb', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8de4b60-2b3e-5d58-ab0c-9e429264e3bb'}, {'abstract': 'The overall debts of the federal government are five times as large as the much discussed “national debt,” and can be addressed only through a very long-term approach, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/the-true-federal-debt/', 'snippet': 'The overall debts of the federal government are five times as large as the much discussed “national debt,” and can be addressed only through a very long-term approach, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. He is the author of the coming book “The Benefit and the Burden: Tax Reform – Why We Need It and What It Will Take.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The True Federal Debt', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T11:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3df7057-be7e-52f0-8d72-1f4832643f92', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3df7057-be7e-52f0-8d72-1f4832643f92'}, {'abstract': 'In an essay published this week in a Communist Party magazine, President Hu Jintao said the West is trying to dominate China by spreading its culture and ideology.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/world/asia/chinas-president-pushes-back-against-western-culture.html', 'snippet': 'In an essay published this week in a Communist Party magazine, President Hu Jintao said the West is trying to dominate China by spreading its culture and ideology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — President Hu Jintao has said China must strengthen its cultural production to defend against the West’s assault on the country’s culture and ideology, according to an essay in a Communist Party policy magazine published this week. The publication of Mr. Hu’s words signaled that a new major policy initiative announced in October would continue well into 2012.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/world/CHINA-1/CHINA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/04/world/CHINA-1/CHINA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/world/CHINA-1/CHINA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/world/CHINA-1/CHINA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/04/world/CHINA-1/CHINA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s President Lashes Out at Western Culture', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China’s President Lashes Out at Western Culture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T11:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4789515-bc95-5b27-8a51-1e4767694701', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4789515-bc95-5b27-8a51-1e4767694701'}, {'abstract': 'It’s remarkable that our system essentially puts a special tax on my company for offering people long-term employment — by charging more to insure older workers.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/further-thoughts-on-why-our-health-rates-fell/', 'snippet': 'It’s remarkable that our system essentially puts a special tax on my company for offering people long-term employment — by charging more to insure older workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First, thanks to everyone who encouraged me to keep writing (see my last post). The encouragement was, well, encouraging. I’ll do my best to keep it real, with numbers when appropriate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Further Thoughts on Why Our Health Rates Fell', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T12:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9b4f0da-e2ee-5653-a21d-3dbb5f4765f2', 'word_count': 1543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9b4f0da-e2ee-5653-a21d-3dbb5f4765f2'}, {'abstract': 'Winter in New Delhi.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/image-of-the-day-january-3/', 'snippet': 'Winter in New Delhi.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: January 3', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T12:14:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44c880b0-a970-58bc-9e11-d2e6665536f7', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44c880b0-a970-58bc-9e11-d2e6665536f7'}, {'abstract': 'Perhaps hoping to prevent a repeat of the summer of 2010, chief minister moves swiftly.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/quick-action-in-kashmir-after-shooting/', 'snippet': 'Perhaps hoping to prevent a repeat of the summer of 2010, chief minister moves swiftly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The government of Jammu and Kashmir took swift action after security forces killed an 18-year-old male Monday, arresting five men in connection with the shooting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quick Action in Kashmir After Shooting', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T12:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/057910af-044c-58c5-b47a-d5d75394b739', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/057910af-044c-58c5-b47a-d5d75394b739'}, {'abstract': 'DaVinci Furniture says China Central Television distorted and fabricated evidence that the company had passed off cheap goods from southern China as luxury imports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/business/global/chinese-retailer-casts-doubt-on-tv-investigation.html', 'snippet': 'DaVinci Furniture says China Central Television distorted and fabricated evidence that the company had passed off cheap goods from southern China as luxury imports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — Last July, China’s biggest state-run television broadcaster accused a luxury retailer named DaVinci Furniture of passing off low-quality goods from a factory in southern China as premium imports from Italy and other foreign lands. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/business/FURNITURE/FURNITURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/04/business/FURNITURE/FURNITURE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/business/FURNITURE/FURNITURE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 102