drew Luck for a year or two?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the biggest news of Black Monday. Bill Polian was out. He and Bill Belichick, brilliant and difficult men, had matched personnel wits for over a decade, and Colts-Patriots meetings had turned into signature games of an era. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Polians Fired; What Should Colts Do Next?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polian, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T12:50:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4a23670-7e60-589c-a7e9-38c18b5f1c35', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4a23670-7e60-589c-a7e9-38c18b5f1c35'}, {'abstract': 'American chefs and gourmet food trucks are captivating Parisian palates.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/eurofile-the-new-american-tastemakers-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'American chefs and gourmet food trucks are captivating Parisian palates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans have been eagerly crossing the Atlantic just to gorge themselves in Paris for centuries, but their gastronomic passion has never been even remotely reciprocated, until now. Three of the city’s best new modern bistro chefs are American, and Paris’s first gourmet food truck, Le Camion qui Fume, selling blue-cheese burgers, caramelized onions, frites and more, was recently outfitted by Kristin Frederick, a Californian.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eurofile | The New American Tastemakers in Paris', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T13:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Lobrano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobrano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b80a70e-d2e1-50d9-8d6f-aac9b4010e1e', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b80a70e-d2e1-50d9-8d6f-aac9b4010e1e'}, {'abstract': 'You could probably argue that the regular-season outcomes of the two New York area football teams had nothing to do with the University of Massachusetts or everything to do with it.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/giants-jets-tannenbaum-and-umass/', 'snippet': 'You could probably argue that the regular-season outcomes of the two New York area football teams had nothing to do with the University of Massachusetts or everything to do with it.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We talk to the staff up there, they do a good job. I like to think we get good information as well. I try to help them out when I can with favors.” Jets General Manager Mike Tannenbaum on his connections at UMass, in a Star-Ledger article last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants, Jets, Tannenbaum and UMass', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Victor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ducasse, Vladimir', 'rank': 3