t $2.2 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deal-making in the shale gas sector, one of the hottest last year, is off to a strong start in 2012, with two foreign companies buying big stakes in operations in the United States. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sinopec and Total Continue Shale Gas Buying Spree', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BHP Billiton PLC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chesapeake Energy Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T13:11:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35c52e4d-88b6-56ab-86a4-df41aea9d0a7', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35c52e4d-88b6-56ab-86a4-df41aea9d0a7'}, {'abstract': 'Residents of a village in northwestern China where hundreds of Muslims tried to defend a mosque against demolition have said that many civilians were injured when police attacked.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/world/asia/violent-clashes-reported-in-china-over-mosque-demolition.html', 'snippet': 'Residents of a village in northwestern China where hundreds of Muslims tried to defend a mosque against demolition have said that many civilians were injured when police attacked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Residents of a village in northwestern China where hundreds of Muslims tried to defend a mosque against demolition by the authorities have said that many civilians were injured when police attacked and that at least two might have been killed, according to news agency reports on Tuesday. ', 'print_secti