lifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8f81b98-35ef-57b6-bd0c-e279a2ea5bbc', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8f81b98-35ef-57b6-bd0c-e279a2ea5bbc'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s wealthiest are not nearly as skilled as Iowans when it comes to using their strength to local advantage.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/the-power-of-the-purse-and-elections/', 'snippet': 'New York’s wealthiest are not nearly as skilled as Iowans when it comes to using their strength to local advantage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For excellent reasons, the main one being common sense, New York will be far from the thoughts of Iowa Republicans in their caucuses on Tuesday night. But the city’s mayor has surprisingly been an issue. At least, he has been for one candidate, Newt Gingrich, the former House speaker. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Using the Power of the Purse to Steer Politics', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethanol', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republi