': 'nyt://article/6e8cb524-7d89-5896-a9b2-cd6f0c7ffec2', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e8cb524-7d89-5896-a9b2-cd6f0c7ffec2'}, {'abstract': '3M, the maker of Post-it notes and Scotch Tape, has agreed to buy the office and consumer products business of the Avery Dennison Corporation for $550 million in cash.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/3m-to-buy-avery-dennison-unit/', 'snippet': '3M, the maker of Post-it notes and Scotch Tape, has agreed to buy the office and consumer products business of the Avery Dennison Corporation for $550 million in cash.', 'lead_paragraph': '3M, the maker of Post-it notes and Scotch Tape, has agreed to buy the office and consumer products business of the Avery Dennison Corporation for $550 million in cash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3M to Acquire a Unit of Avery Dennison', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '3M Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Avery Dennison Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Latham & Watkins', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T14:52:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6dfc7ee-86d6-5a45-92fb-61cbbd4be55c', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6dfc7ee-86d6-5a45-92fb-61cbbd4be55c'}, {'abstract': 'Some companies are betting that the increased use of solar panels will open the way for solar thermal, a kind of energy storage that compensates for the vagaries of photovoltaic generation.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/the-convoluted-economics-of-storing-energy/', 'snippet': 'Some companies are betting that the increased use of solar panels will open the way for solar thermal, a kind of energy storage that compensates for the vagaries of photovoltaic generation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I reported in Tuesday’s paper, some companies think that one form of renewable energy is going to open a window for another — that solar photovoltaic panels, which convert sunlight directly into electricity, are going to increase the grid’s need for a type of solar energy that can be stored. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Convoluted Economics of Storing Energy', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Renewable Energy Laboratory', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T15:17:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dbf7b87-2ffd-55c8-827f-9b969d5c9b34', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dbf7b87-2ffd-55c8-827f-9b969d5c9b34'}, {'abstract': 'After a 2-14 season without Peyton Manning, Indianapolis fires two executives (but not the coach — at least not yet).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/sports/the-colts-cant-win-for-losing.html', 'snippet': 'After a 2-14 season without Peyton Manning, Indianapolis fires two executives (but not the coach — at least not yet).', 'lead_paragraph': 'You have to hand it to the Indianapolis Colts because whatever they do, they do it big, all the way back to their moving-vans-rolling-out-of-Baltimore days. Now, after turning the platform of their almost-dynasty into a quadruple flip with three twists in the pike position (from 10-6 in 2010 to 2-14 in 2011, degree of difficulty: 8.9), they followed with the equally big response of canning the architect of the Peyton Manning Dynasty, Bill Polian, and his handpicked successor/offspring, Chris.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/sports/04leading1/04leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/04/sports/04leading1/04leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/sports/04leading1/04leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/sports/04leading1/04leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/04/sports/04leading1/04leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Colts Can’t Win for Losing', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Colts Can’t Win for Losing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luck, Andrew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T15:39:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62eb6566-f727-55be-a630-a68c932c8f08', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62eb6566-f727-55be-a630-a68c932c8f08'}, {'abstract': 'Fletcher Cox, a third-year junior, is projected to be selected in the first two rounds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/sports/ncaafootball/mississippi-states-fletcher-cox-declares-for-nfl-draft.html', 'snippet': 'Fletcher Cox, a third-year junior, is projected to be selected in the first two rounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mississippi State defensive tackle Fletcher Cox is skipping his senior season and declaring for the N.F.L. draft. Cox is considered one of the country’s best defensive line prospects and is projected by N.F.L. evaluators as a second-round pick, though some analysts believe he could be selected late in the first round. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/sports/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 815, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/sports/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/04/sports/BRIEFS/BRIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mississippi State Defensive Tackle Declares for N.F.L. Draft', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mississippi State’s Cox Declares for N.F.L. Draft', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mississippi State University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T15:46:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ac23b72-8611-5bda-b0c9-c18d5a4affc9', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ac23b72-8611-5bda-b0c9-c18d5a4affc9'}, {'abstract': 'Besides consecutive losses in the Rose Bowl, Wisconsin will cope with losses to its roster and coaching staff in the off-season.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/wisconsin-has-more-than-rose-bowl-loss-to-worry-about/', 'snippet': 'Besides consecutive losses in the Rose Bowl, Wisconsin will cope with losses to its roster and coaching staff in the off-season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PASADENA, Calif. — Wisconsin lost for the third time this season Monday evening. As painful as it was, it was equally fitting for a team that has now lost two consecutive Rose Bowls by a combined 9 points.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisconsin Has More Than Bowl Loss to Worry About', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rose Bowl (Football Game)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ball, Montee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bielema, Bret', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Russell', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Wisconsin-Madison', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T15:52:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Fiammetta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fiammetta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3445dc9-2938-5ef7-95cf-a33ccdebd4e1', 'word_count': 659, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3445dc9-2938-5ef7-95cf-a33ccdebd4e1'}, {'abstract': 'Rupert Murdoch starts tweeting, and deleting, over the weekend; a new ambassador for young people’s literature; returning to the question of the police and Occupy Wall Street protests.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/the-breakfast-meeting-jan-3/', 'snippet': 'Rupert Murdoch starts tweeting, and deleting, over the weekend; a new ambassador for young people’s literature; returning to the question of the police and Occupy Wall Street protests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twitter users could experience Rupert Murdoch unfiltered this New Year’s weekend, as he joined the service and immediately began sharing his thoughts large and small. One post indicated support for Rick Santorum on the eve the Iowa caucuses, saying he was “Only candidate with genuine big vision for country.” In the past, Brian Stelter writes on The Caucus blog, Mr. Santorum has criticized Fox News as part of his broader complaint that the news media has ignored his candidacy, saying, “You know, Bill O’Reilly has refused to put me on his program.” On Monday night, Mr. O’Reilly acknowledged Mr. Santorum’s recent rise in the polls and said, “We have invited Rick Santorum to appear on Wednesday.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting, Jan. 3', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MYERS, WALTER DEAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T15:52:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4fd0477-a68e-58e7-81c0-85f34310d762', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4fd0477-a68e-58e7-81c0-85f34310d762'}, {'abstract': 'With votes not yet cast in Iowa, Mitt Romney has been buying up air time in Florida.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/feet-in-iowa-eye-on-florida/', 'snippet': 'With votes not yet cast in Iowa, Mitt Romney has been buying up air time in Florida.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:12 p.m. | Updated  DES MOINES\xa0— With the political world’s attention focused on Iowa, Mitt Romney’s campaign is looking several steps ahead and turning to Florida, where it is buying up time on broadcast television in that voter-rich primary state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feet in Iowa, Eye on Florida', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T15:59:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c474b378-8af3-50f9-9bfa-d2ce69f2283e', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c474b378-8af3-50f9-9bfa-d2ce69f2283e'}, {'abstract': 'Expect the Falcons to do what the Cowboys should have done Sunday night: control the tempo with no-huddle and mitigate the Giants’ pass rush with quick-hitting plays.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/wild-card-games-what-the-film-says/', 'snippet': 'Expect the Falcons to do what the Cowboys should have done Sunday night: control the tempo with no-huddle and mitigate the Giants’ pass rush with quick-hitting plays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Benoit, who has been contributing weekly film reviews this season, trains his eye on the wild-card matchups:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wild-Card Games: What the Film Says', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T16:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dc6c846-8c0c-5946-b21d-141a51a705a6', 'word_count': 1587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dc6c846-8c0c-5946-b21d-141a51a705a6'}, {'abstract': 'Seeing a chiropractor or engaging in light exercise relieves neck pain more effectively than relying on pain medication, new research shows.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/for-neck-pain-chiropractic-and-exercise-are-better-than-drugs/', 'snippet': 'Seeing a chiropractor or engaging in light exercise relieves neck pain more effectively than relying on pain medication, new research shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seeing a chiropractor or engaging in light exercise relieves neck pain more effectively than relying on pain medication, new research shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Neck Pain, Chiropractic and Exercise Are Better Than Drugs', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chiropractors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Neck', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain-Relieving Drugs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T16:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c40f37d-13e7-5f13-b7c7-e91a854c1e2c', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c40f37d-13e7-5f13-b7c7-e91a854c1e2c'}, {'abstract': 'Recent quakes in Youngstown, Ohio, were the 10th and 11th to occur near a 9,200-foot-deep disposal well used in the hydraulic fracturing process.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/on-our-radar-quakes-and-fracking/', 'snippet': 'Recent quakes in Youngstown, Ohio, were the 10th and 11th to occur near a 9,200-foot-deep disposal well used in the hydraulic fracturing process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 4.0 magnitude earthquake that struck Youngstown on Saturday occurred at a site that was almost identical to one hit a week earlier, a seismologist says — close to the bottom of a 9,200-foot-deep disposal well where liquid waste from natural-gas wells had been injected under pressure. The finding provides further evidence that the waste from the fracking process may have migrated from the well into deeper rock formations. [The New York Times]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Quakes and Fracking', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T16:25:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50f42360-792c-5d6e-82ba-3448e2f48d89', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50f42360-792c-5d6e-82ba-3448e2f48d89'}, {'abstract': 'Two men were found guilty of the murder of a black teenager, Stephen Lawrence, in April 1993, a case that prompted an examination of racism in London’s police force.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/world/europe/guilty-verdicts-in-1993-racial-murder-of-stephen-lawrence-in-britain.html', 'snippet': 'Two men were found guilty of the murder of a black teenager, Stephen Lawrence, in April 1993, a case that prompted an examination of racism in London’s police force.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — More than 18 years late by the reckoning of the victim’s family and many others across Britain, a jury at the Old Bailey on Tuesday found two white men guilty of the racially motivated stabbing and murder of a black youth named Stephen Lawrence on a south London street in April 1993. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/world/BRITAIN-1/BRITAIN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/world/BRITAIN-1/BRITAIN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/04/world/BRITAIN-1/BRITAIN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guilty Verdicts in 1993 Racial Murder Case That Changed Justice in Britain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guilty Verdicts in 1993 Racial Murder Case That Changed Justice in Britain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawrence, Stephen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T16:51:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36b97c42-05c5-59a0-99c7-42c27e666541', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36b97c42-05c5-59a0-99c7-42c27e666541'}, {'abstract': 'The City of Baltimore has terminated its contract with the company that organized the inaugural Baltimore Grand Prix, which was run over Labor Day weekend last year.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/wheelies-the-finish-line-edition/', 'snippet': 'The City of Baltimore has terminated its contract with the company that organized the inaugural Baltimore Grand Prix, which was run over Labor Day weekend last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The Finish Line Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bentley Motors Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fisker Automotive', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baltimore (Md)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T16:56:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c306496-80a4-5cd1-8cf2-5ae21fd70cf6', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c306496-80a4-5cd1-8cf2-5ae21fd70cf6'}, {'abstract': 'With his candidacy battered by negative campaign ads, Newt Gingrich is adjusting his strategy to rescue his ailing campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/us/politics/iowa-caucus-votes.html', 'snippet': 'With his candidacy battered by negative campaign ads, Newt Gingrich is adjusting his strategy to rescue his ailing campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BURLINGTON, Iowa — With his candidacy battered by negative campaign ads and a disappointing showing in the Iowa caucuses, Newt Gingrich is adjusting his strategy to rescue his ailing campaign, aggressively swatting back at Mitt Romney, whose supporters have painted him into the box of a Washington influence-peddler. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/us/CAMPAIGN-1/CAMPAIGN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/04/us/CAMPAIGN-1/CAMPAIGN-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/us/CAMPAIGN-1/CAMPAIGN-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/us/CAMPAIGN-1/CAMPAIGN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/04/us/CAMPAIGN-1/CAMPAIGN-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Frustrated Gingrich Looks Past Iowa and Lashes Back at Romney', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Frustrated Gingrich Lashes Back at Romney and Awaits the Next Round', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f48d760-a9e4-5b4d-bab0-61f6c13349df', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f48d760-a9e4-5b4d-bab0-61f6c13349df'}, {'abstract': 'Is he really a weaker not-Romney alternative than Rick Perry or Newt Gingrich?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/the-strengths-of-rick-santorum/', 'snippet': 'Is he really a weaker not-Romney alternative than Rick Perry or Newt Gingrich?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The conventional wisdom holds that Rick Santorum’s last-minute bid to consolidate the not-Mitt Romney vote in Iowa is, like so many other developments in this election season, nothing but good news for Romney — because Santorum’s rise is preventing Rick Perry or Newt Gingrich from gaining ground instead, and in a drawn-out campaign Romney would ultimately “be more threatened by Gingrich or Perry” (as HotAir’s Ed Morrissey puts it) than by the former Pennsylvania senator. “On record, on economic conservative credibility, on ties to big donors,” Dave Weigel writes, “Santorum’s not the opponent Romney feared most.” “If Perry or Gingrich are in the top three, we have a real race headed into South Carolina,” Erick Erickson suggests. But if Santorum wins Iowa, “we might as well sit back and declare Mitt Romney the nominee.” (Judging by these quotes, the Romney camp seems to agree.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Strengths of Rick Santorum', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:01:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f4dd120-a329-559a-9efa-7afedb41030b', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f4dd120-a329-559a-9efa-7afedb41030b'}, {'abstract': 'The director of “Newsies,” Jeff Calhoun recently told BroadwayWorld.com that “it’ll be fun to be with Jeremy again,” which was apparently an inadvertent slip on his part, since a moment later Mr. Calhoun lamented that he might get “in trouble” for saying that.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/jeremy-jordan-on-verge-of-joining-broadway-move-of-disneys-newsies/', 'snippet': 'The director of “Newsies,” Jeff Calhoun recently told BroadwayWorld.com that “it’ll be fun to be with Jeremy again,” which was apparently an inadvertent slip on his part, since a moment later Mr. Calhoun lamented that he might get “in trouble” for...', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the major casting questions pending on Broadway is whether “Newsies,” this spring’s new Disney musical, will star Jeremy Jordan, whose performance as the newsboy Jack Kelly drew critical acclaim in the show’s premiere in New Jersey last year and helped persuade Disney Theatrical Productions to transfer it to New York. Now that Mr. Jordan is free from the Broadway musical “Bonnie & Clyde,” which closed on Friday, it’s a good bet that he’ll be hawking “papes” as Jack on Broadway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeremy Jordan On Verge of Joining Broadway Move of Disney’s ‘Newsies’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calhoun, Jeff', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jordan, Jeremy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:04:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dcf9689-cbe5-53a3-bb51-53a6bf3bef1c', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dcf9689-cbe5-53a3-bb51-53a6bf3bef1c'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Shear, Times political reporter and chief correspondent for The Caucus, has been on the ground in Iowa all week, following the candidates, watching the polls and talking to voters. He hosted a Facebook chat on Tuesday afternoon.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/iowa-caucus-facebook-chat/', 'snippet': 'Michael Shear, Times political reporter and chief correspondent for The Caucus, has been on the ground in Iowa all week, following the candidates, watching the polls and talking to voters. He hosted a Facebook chat on Tuesday afternoon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 4:12 p.m. As Iowans and voters around the country awaited the beginning of the 2012 Republican nomination contests on Tuesday night, Michael Shear, a Times political reporter and chief correspondent for The Caucus blog, hosted a live — and lively — discussion about the caucuses on The Times’s Facebook page. Below, a transcript of highlights from the chat. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iowa Caucuses Q. & A.', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:09:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dc7ed1a-343f-5327-9c5c-0c9e4aaaf04c', 'word_count': 74, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dc7ed1a-343f-5327-9c5c-0c9e4aaaf04c'}, {'abstract': 'I don’t exactly regret my initial enthusiasm for Lego Friends. But I do regret my willingness to overlook the doggedness of marketers.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/should-lego-be-gender-free-or-just-less-complicated/', 'snippet': 'I don’t exactly regret my initial enthusiasm for Lego Friends. But I do regret my willingness to overlook the doggedness of marketers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I just saw my first commercial for those Lego Friends for girls I wrote about here before the holiday, and after my first glimpse of Heartlake City, the new Lego world, I wondered if I’d spoken too soon about my willingness to place my order now. As the new Ladyfig characters in their brightly colored cafe morphed, on screen, into animated creations that looked far more Polly Pocket than Lego Hermione Granger, I cringed a little. Then I took a closer look at the building, with its ice-cream cups, flowers and railings. And it occurred to me that maybe the real problem with Lego, for girls and boys, isn’t the gender specificity of the various building sets. It’s that there are so many sets for building so many specific things.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should Lego Be Gender-Free — or Just Less Complicated?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Toys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:14:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c61b154d-82e0-52e5-8583-a9da2a00d7b1', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c61b154d-82e0-52e5-8583-a9da2a00d7b1'}, {'abstract': 'Ron Paul gives the sense that he is the leader of a movement more than of a political campaign, and he believes the consistency of his message will win over voters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/us/politics/ron-pauls-stump-speech.html', 'snippet': 'Ron Paul gives the sense that he is the 