e Bulls are among those who have endured criticism for bad behavior during games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Santonio Holmes of the Jets appeared to quit on the team in a loss to the Dolphins Sunday, a number of teammates went public with their criticism. But it wasn’t the first time in recent sports history that a player was in the spotlight for not being a team-first guy. Jorge Posada of the Yankees took himself out of the lineup in May when Manager Joe Girardi tried to bat him ninth in the lineup against the Red Sox. And in 1994 Scottie Pippen of the Bulls refused to play when Coach Phil Jackson designed a scoring play for his teammate Toni Kukoc.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Pippen to Holmes: Is There a Penalty for Quitting on a Team?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, Santonio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pippen, Scottie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posada, Jorge', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:26:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3601159-e66d-5e57-9fd8-10674be23f73', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3601159-e66d-5e57-9fd8-10674be23f73'}, {'abstract': 'Supporters said Rick Santorum has enjoyed a surge in the polls because he addresses Iowa’s unique economic challenges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/us/politics/rick-santorum-on-the-stump.html', 'snippet': 'Supporters said Rick Santorum has enjoyed a surge in the polls because he addresses Iowa’s unique economic challenges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CEDAR RAPIDS, Iowa — Rick Santorum’s surge in the polls took many political watchers by surprise. But it shouldn’t have shocked anyone who has watched him preside over one of his nearly 400 town hall meetings in Iowa over the last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Hours Later, the Audience Is Won Over', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Hours Later, the Audience Is Won Over', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:27:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72246778-a170-50d0-9ff9-2324bae7588d', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72246778-a170-50d0-9ff9-2324bae7588d'}, {'abstract': 'The Producers Guild, recently, a strong predictor of the Oscar for best picture, chose 10 films to compete for its top honor of the year.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/producers-guild-releases-its-nominations/', 'snippet': 'The Producers Guild, recently, a strong predictor of the Oscar for best picture, chose 10 films to compete for its top honor of the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Producers Guild just released its nominations, and the top film contenders are:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Producers Guild Announces Its Nominations', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:32:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f85af6e-3c88-5a94-bdec-e15e0bd5ff25', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f85af6e-3c88-5a94-bdec-e15e0bd5ff25'}, {'abstract': 'A Russian peacekeeper fatally shot a young Moldovan man as he sped through a checkpoint early on New Year’s Day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/world/europe/shooting-raises-tensions-between-moldova-and-russia.html', 'snippet': 'A Russian peacekeeper fatally shot a young Moldovan man as he sped through a checkpoint early on New Year’s Day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Tension rose between Russia and Moldova, a former Soviet republic that recently celebrated 20 years of independence, after a Russian peacekeeper fatally shot a young Moldovan man as he sped through a checkpoint early on New Year’s Day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shooting at Checkpoint Raises Tensions in a Disputed Region Claimed by Moldova', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shooting at Checkpoint Raises Tensions in a Disputed Region Claimed by Moldova', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moldova', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:36:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ce7bcea-137f-5c27-b3af-5c8f44141133', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ce7bcea-137f-5c27-b3af-5c8f44141133'}, {'abstract': 'Van Halen has invited music writers to a small show at Cafe Wha?, the latest enigmatic hint to the band’s plans for a 2012 tour.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/van-halen-stalwart-arena-rock-band-to-play-intimate-set-at-small-club/', 'snippet': 'Van Halen has invited music writers to a small show at Cafe Wha?, the latest enigmatic hint to the band’s plans for a 2012 tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Van Halen has invited music writers and critics to an intimate concert at Cafe Wha? in Greenwich Village on Thursday night as a prelude to a tour with the band’s classic lineup later this year. Nothing official has been released, but journalists have been told the group will play a short set. The one-night performance in that 250-seat club on MacDougal Street in Manhattan marks the latest enigmatic hint that the band has sent about its plans for the year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Van Halen, Stalwart Arena-Rock Band, to Play Intimate Set at Small Club', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, David Lee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Van Halen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:39:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3358fc8-65ff-51bd-8630-8a99382f458d', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3358fc8-65ff-51bd-8630-8a99382f458d'}, {'abstract': 'A man suspected of hurling Molotov cocktails at locations in Queens and Nassau County was being questioned on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/man-being-questioned-in-firebombings-in-queens/', 'snippet': 'A man suspected of hurling Molotov cocktails at locations in Queens and Nassau County was being questioned on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Updated 1:33 p.m. | The police are questioning a man who investigators believe may be responsible for four firebomb attacks in Queens over the weekend, the city’s police commissioner said on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Being Questioned in Firebombings', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jamaica (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nassau County (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:42:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74bec463-5039-5b4c-8b41-455954e52695', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74bec463-5039-5b4c-8b41-455954e52695'}, {'abstract': 'The Math for America program, which attracts and trains math teachers, is shifting its focus away from new recruits to teachers who are already in the classroom, and plans to more than double its presence in New York City in the next several years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/03/training-program-for-math-teachers-will-shift-its-focus/', 'snippet': 'The Math for America program, which attracts and trains math teachers, is shifting its focus away from new recruits to teachers who are already in the classroom, and plans to more than double its presence in New York City in the next several years...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Training Program for Math Teachers Will Shift Its Focus ', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:50:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANNA M. PHILLIPS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68331b74-a360-5474-b146-5b4cd783d052', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68331b74-a360-5474-b146-5b4cd783d052'}, {'abstract': 'The designer’s first capsule collection with a mass retailer goes on sale next month.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/bulls-eye-jason-wu-for-target/', 'snippet': 'The designer’s first capsule collection with a mass retailer goes on sale next month.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I can finally afford Jason Wu!” squealed a fan upon hearing about the forthcoming Jason Wu for Target collection, in stores Feb. 5. The capsule, Wu’s first in collaboration with a mass retailer, possesses a lot of the label’s familiar, feminine spirit but takes more direct inspiration from French New Wave films and the actress Jean Seberg. Pleated frocks with sailor-striped hemlines, dainty silk blouses with neck ties and collars, and sportier knits and tennis skirts stand out as some of the line’s most wearable pieces. “My goal was not to duplicate anything from my main collection,” Wu says. “Instead I designed completely new clothes and accessories that reflect my taste and have a voice of their own.” Friendly reminders of Wu’s work (like the touch of lace on a trench coat or T-shirt) are matched with a delightful dose of animal humor. (Meet Milu, a mischievous kitty and the collection’s mascot, who makes appearances as a print on a scarf and tee.) Here, a Riviera cotton striped A-line dress and canvas satchel explain why Wu calls the whole gamut “gamine chic.” It seems, as they say, les jeux sont faits.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bull’s-Eye | Jason Wu for Target', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wu, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Target Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:51:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb6ee8dd-f0e5-5888-86d4-3ab7c0d31f8e', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb6ee8dd-f0e5-5888-86d4-3ab7c0d31f8e'}, {'abstract': 'The president of the French club Paris-St.Germain says that David Beckham will remain with the M.L.S. team in Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/beckham-appears-likely-to-stay-with-galaxy/', 'snippet': 'The president of the French club Paris-St.Germain says that David Beckham will remain with the M.L.S. team in Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Beckham’s days in Major League Soccer are apparently not over after all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beckham Appears Likely to Stay With Galaxy', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckham, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADIDAS AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:51:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83b1567c-1de7-5c28-84a6-a9a1dfe9ebfd', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83b1567c-1de7-5c28-84a6-a9a1dfe9ebfd'}, {'abstract': 'The vote count remained too close to call into early Wednesday morning, when Mitt Romney was finally declared the winner by just eight votes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/03/us/politics/20110104_IOWA_600.html', 'snippet': 'The vote count remained too close to call into early Wednesday morning, when Mitt Romney was finally declared the winner by just eight votes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The vote count remained too close to call into early Wednesday morning, when Mitt Romney was finally declared the winner by just eight votes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/us/politics/20110104_IOWA_600-slide-BB64/20110104_IOWA_600-slide-BB64-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/03/us/politics/20110104_IOWA_600-slide-BB64/20110104_IOWA_600-slide-BB64-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/us/politics/20110104_IOWA_600-slide-BB64/20110104_IOWA_600-slide-BB64-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/us/politics/20110104_IOWA_600-slide-BB64/20110104_IOWA_600-slide-BB64-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/03/us/politics/20110104_IOWA_600-slide-BB64/20110104_IOWA_600-slide-BB64-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Iowa Caucuses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:53:58+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/2bdbb113-d561-5263-8f67-aaeaefb5aaf2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/2bdbb113-d561-5263-8f67-aaeaefb5aaf2'}, {'abstract': "Carla Smits-Nusteling, KPN's chief financial officer, disagreed with a decision to quadruple the top management board to 12 members from three, the company said.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/business/global/04iht-kpn04.html', 'snippet': "Carla Smits-Nusteling, KPN's chief financial officer, disagreed with a decision to quadruple the top management board to 12 members from three, the company said.", 'lead_paragraph': 'A business executive who became the first woman to be appointed chief financial officer of a large Dutch company resigned on Tuesday, citing a dispute over a management reorganization at her employer, the phone operator KPN.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dutch Firm’s Finance Officer Quits After Reorganization', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dutch Firm’s Finance Officer Quits After Reorganization', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:56:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By KEVIN J. O&rsquo;BRIEN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Orsquo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf7a8be1-2400-5ac0-96e6-3c1b93202a11', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf7a8be1-2400-5ac0-96e6-3c1b93202a11'}, {'abstract': 'The lable Lika Mimika creates espadrilles in unisex styles, in soft lamb, goat and calfskin, are hand-stitched in Spain and come in a range of neutrals and pop colors.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/great-for-hopping-about/', 'snippet': 'The lable Lika Mimika creates espadrilles in unisex styles, in soft lamb, goat and calfskin, are hand-stitched in Spain and come in a range of neutrals and pop colors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MARIJANA CONDIC and Lisa Leipziger, friends in Frankfurt, had a modest mission: to make espadrilles that were sturdier than the Spanish styles they love to wear. “I came back from holiday in Spain and told Marijana we have to do something special with espadrilles so they don’t fall apart after a month,” Ms. Leipziger said. Their label, Lika Mimika, is the happy result. The unisex styles, in soft lamb, goat and calfskin, are hand-stitched in Spain and come in a range of neutrals and Pop colors. Two new styles, lined with rabbit fur or curly lamb shearling, are a clever travel shoe: cozy for the flight and vacation-ready upon landing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Great for Hopping About', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T17:56:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Blumenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blumenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7e7868b-82b8-5669-95cf-bc64429e9b5a', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7e7868b-82b8-5669-95cf-bc64429e9b5a'}, {'abstract': 'Infomercials have earned a cheesy reputation, but at least one owner believes that, done right, they can yield great results — which is why TerraCycle is trying again.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/why-were-trying-another-informercial/', 'snippet': 'Infomercials have earned a cheesy reputation, but at least one owner believes that, done right, they can yield great results — which is why TerraCycle is trying again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are about to take another shot at something that ended in failure five years ago. Yes, we are making another infomercial, but this time I think I know what I’m doing.\xa0Actually, that may be an exaggeration. This time, I at least have the experience of having gone through the process once before.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why We’re Trying Another Infomercial', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TerraCycle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T18:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ae5d0cd-98ac-5560-9d8f-be6639acedea', 'word_count': 999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ae5d0cd-98ac-5560-9d8f-be6639acedea'}, {'abstract': '“Bridesmaids” and “The Ides of March” get a boost in the Oscar derby with nominations from the Producers Guild.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/bridesmaids-ides-of-march-get-a-little-help-from-producers-guild/', 'snippet': '“Bridesmaids” and “The Ides of March” get a boost in the Oscar derby with nominations from the Producers Guild.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Order another corsage for “Bridesmaids” because it’s going to the party. The Producers Guild chose the comedy as one of its 10 best films of the year, possibly advancing its standing with the Academy on the road to Oscar. “The Ides of March,” George Clooney’s political thriller, also got a nod, another boost following several Golden Globe nominations. “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo,” which so far has been a longer shot according to most Academy Awards watchers, made the list, too. The other films the Producers Guild chose are the expected bunch: “The Artist,” “The Descendants,” “The Help,” “Moneyball,” “Midnight in Paris,” “Hugo” and “War Horse.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Bridesmaids,’ ‘Ides of March’ Get a Little Help From Producers Guild', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clooney, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gosling, Ryan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T18:02:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89af08cb-9ff2-56cd-b95f-f29c11f54f1f', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89af08cb-9ff2-56cd-b95f-f29c11f54f1f'}, {'abstract': 'Why “America the Beautiful” is the wrong song for Mitt Romney to be quoting.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/mitt-romney-and-america-the-beautiful-when-reach-exceeds-grasp/', 'snippet': 'Why “America the Beautiful” is the wrong song for Mitt Romney to be quoting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES – It is jarring, in an age of irony and nuance, to hear Mitt Romney conclude his stump speeches with a riff on the hymn, “America the Beautiful.” At an early-morning rally today, a few hours before the Iowa caucuses begin, he discussed his love for the patriotic song — probably the most beloved in the canon – and recited several of the song’s verses, strongly suggesting that its vision of the country differed from President Obama’s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Romney’s Reach Exceeds His Grasp', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T18:04:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f93f24b3-9235-5143-a7e2-36dff7b80ea1', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f93f24b3-9235-5143-a7e2-36dff7b80ea1'}, {'abstract': 'A strong stump speech is one of the most important components of a presidential campaign. Times reporters following the candidates have deconstructed and annotated four candidates’ stump speeches, providing context and checking facts.', 'web_url