cting about $260,000 of his lobbying fees to shell companies linked to State Senator Carl Kruger, was expected to plead guilty Wednesday in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/nyregion/guilty-plea-by-richard-lipsky-lobbyist-is-expected-in-bribery-case.html', 'snippet': 'Richard J. Lipsky, who was accused of directing about $260,000 of his lobbying fees to shell companies linked to State Senator Carl Kruger, was expected to plead guilty Wednesday in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard J. Lipsky, a prominent New York lobbyist who was charged in the bribery conspiracy case that also ensnared State Senator Carl Kruger, is expected to plead guilty on Wednesday in Federal District Court in Manhattan, a person briefed on the matter said Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lobbyist Is Expected to Plead Guilty in Corruption Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lobbyist Is Expected to Plead Guilty in Corruption Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lipsky, Richard J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kruger, Carl', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T19:35:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f4305ce-b66a-52a9-9263-d4078747f7c9', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f4305ce-b66a-52a9-9263-d4078747f7c9'}, {'abstract': 'In response to an essay advocating taking time off between high school and college, readers raised financial concerns, to which the author, the former admissions dean at Middlebury, has responded.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/gap-year/', 'snippet': 'In response to an essay advocating taking time off between high school and college, readers raised financial concerns, to which the author, the former admissions dean at Middlebury, has responded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the holidays, readers flooded The Choice’s mailbox with thoughtful comments and observations, including on the initial student postings to our first-person “Envelope, Please” series.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From the Mail Bag: On Taking a Gap Year', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T19:35:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca R. Ruiz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Ruiz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/853c270e-7958-5e57-913d-5dd15d6c932e', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/853c270e-7958-5e57-913d-5dd15d6c932e'}, {'abstract': 'Rupert Murdoch went out of his way to praise the show that replaced Glenn Beck at 5 P.M. And though the channel and its former star were supposed to work together in the future, so far they haven’t.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/murdoch-tweet-hints-at-chill-between-fox-news-and-glenn-beck/', 'snippet': 'Rupert Murdoch went out of his way to praise the show that replaced Glenn Beck at 5 P.M. And though the channel and its former star were supposed to work together in the future, so far they haven’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Twitter message from Rupert Murdoch about the Fox News talk show “The Five” drew notice on Monday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Murdoch Tweet Hints at Chill Between Fox News and Glenn Beck', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AILES, ROGER E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Glenn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GBTV', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T19:42:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6aca7ec2-9f73-509e-8970-aa89c934bb97', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6aca7ec2-9f73-509e-8970-aa89c934bb97'}, {'abstract': 'Liverpool has decided not to appeal the suspension of Luis Suarez, and continues to defend him, in racism case.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/liverpool-wont-appeal-suspension-of-suarez/', 'snippet': 'Liverpool has decided not to appeal the suspension of Luis Suarez, and continues to defend him, in racism case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Liverpool has decided not to appeal the eight-game suspension given to striker Luis Suárez, who was found to have used racial insults against Manchester United defender Patrice Evra in December. But the club took a few parting shots at the findings of the commission that handed down the ban before announcing its decision not to appeal it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liverpool Won’t Appeal Suspension of Suárez', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suarez, Luis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Football Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liverpool (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester United (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T19:42:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ef058f7-ee46-5a6e-9364-ac11947e5ec1', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ef058f7-ee46-5a6e-9364-ac11947e5ec1'}, {'abstract': 'Michele Bachmann makes her last campaign stop about repealing President Obama’s health care law.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/bachmann-looks-to-an-election-night-miracle/', 'snippet': 'Michele Bachmann makes her last campaign stop about repealing President Obama’s health care law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEST DES MOINES, Iowa — Representative Michele Bachmann made her longstanding pledge to repeal President Obama’s health care law the central focus of her last campaign stop in the Des Moines area before tonight’s caucuses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann Looks to an Election Night ‘Miracle’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T19:42:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Saulny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saulny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1cccfc9-f0d5-5a19-8957-7c01f94f0d6e', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1cccfc9-f0d5-5a19-8957-7c01f94f0d6e'}, {'abstract': 'By arresting five Indian security officers, the authorities moved swiftly to keep the killing of a teenager from provoking more violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/world/asia/quick-action-in-kashmir-after-protesters-death.html', 'snippet': 'By arresting five Indian security officers, the authorities moved swiftly to keep the killing of a teenager from provoking more violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — A day after security forces shot and killed a teenager during protests over electricity shortages in Indian-administered Kashmir, regional authorities moved swiftly on Tuesday to keep the killing from setting off new rounds of demonstrations during what has been an unusually peaceful period in the region.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quick Action in Kashmir After Death of Protester', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quick Action In Kashmir After Death Of Protester', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T19:46:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1220ae89-1683-517c-b0d2-936c85dcc6fb', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1220ae89-1683-517c-b0d2-936c85dcc6fb'}, {'abstract': 'Simon Doonan’s tongue-in-cheek book says straight food is heavy and gay food is lighter and more decorative. Mix the two, he advises, to stay slim.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/dining/simon-doonans-eating-guide-for-gay-and-straight.html', 'snippet': 'Simon Doonan’s tongue-in-cheek book says straight food is heavy and gay food is lighter and more decorative. Mix the two, he advises, to stay slim.', 'lead_paragraph': '“HERE’S a good example of what we’re talking about,” Simon Doonan said. My Cuban sandwich had just arrived, pressed flat and bulging with cheese. He was giving it a withering once-over. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/dining/04GAY_SPAN/04GAY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType