eadline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AILEY, ALVIN, AMERICAN DANCE THEATER', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T20:26:26+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8d94691e-c9b7-501e-b54c-232b1aaf2650', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8d94691e-c9b7-501e-b54c-232b1aaf2650'}, {'abstract': 'Comedy shows lifted CBS in the ratings on Monday night, but the powers of a reality dating show on ABC appear to be fading.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/fewer-viewers-check-out-the-bachelor-on-abc/', 'snippet': 'Comedy shows lifted CBS in the ratings on Monday night, but the powers of a reality dating show on ABC appear to be fading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Could the television broadcast audience be growing less susceptible to the charms of “The Bachelor” on ABC? The season premiere of the series averaged 7.7 million total viewers over a two-hour period on Monday night, according to Nielsen data, down from the 9 million viewers who watched the 15th-season premiere last January. There was also a 17 percent drop in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic when compared with last year. This placed ABC a distant second in the overall ratings among the broadcast networks, behind the CBS Monday comedy block. CBS finished No. 1 in all ratings categories in every prime-time half-hour.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fewer Viewers Check Out ‘The Bachelor’ on ABC', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T20:29:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ccf65f4-bec1-5372-8c1c-211ccd0007f0', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ccf65f4-bec1-5372-8c1c-211ccd0007f0'}, {'abstract': 'A resolution to convert paper savings bonds to electronic bonds requires a data-entry commitment.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/resolution-convert-paper-bonds-to-electronic-versions/', 'snippet': 'A resolution to convert paper savings bonds to electronic bonds requires a data-entry commitment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a New Year’s financial resolution, I’ve decided to take care of a financial skeleton in my closet. Well, it’s actually a shoebox, not a skeleton — but it is literally sitting in a closet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Resolution: Convert Paper Bonds to Electronic Versions', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T20:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75c0d729-32d1-5e46-be1c-c56d99107e8e', 'word