e New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mendacity of Dopes', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T23:13:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47518bb8-88f7-5975-a52d-cfc3d672564f', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47518bb8-88f7-5975-a52d-cfc3d672564f'}, {'abstract': 'From the Trinity Choir and Trinity Baroque Orchestra, energetic performances of the midsection of the “Christmas Oratorio.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/arts/music/trinity-choir-and-baroque-orchestras-bach-at-one-review.html', 'snippet': 'From the Trinity Choir and Trinity Baroque Orchestra, energetic performances of the midsection of the “Christmas Oratorio.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The presentations could hardly have been more disparate in scale, spirit and spectacle, or lack of it. Still, fresh memories of “The Enchanted Island,” the remarkable Baroque confection unveiled by the Metropolitan Opera on New Year’s Eve, crowded in on the experience of two Bach cantatas performed by the Trinity Choir and Trinity Baroque Orchestra on Monday afternoon as part of the Bach at One series at the intimate St. Paul’s Chapel in Lower Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bach Cantatas Adapted for One Baby’s Early Days', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bach Cantatas Adapted for One Baby’s Early Days', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trinity Baroque Orchestra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T23:20:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3825cf0-3450-57d0-be45-e3bf2845259f', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3825cf0-3450-57d0-be45-e3bf2845259f'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama is hoping to strike the same emotional chord with Iowa supporters that he did in 2008 — and break Republicans’ monopoly on attention in the state.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/obama-looks-for-a-share-of-the-iowa-spotlight/', 'snippet': 'President Obama is hoping to strike the same emotional chord with Iowa supporters that he did in 2008 — and break Republicans’ monopoly on attention in the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican caucus is clearly the big story Tuesday night, but that hasn’t stopped President Obama from trying to grab some of the spotlight in Iowa. The president is hosting a live video conference for Democrats attending precinct caucuses across Iowa, where he will try to get himself in shape to repeat his 2008 win in the state, while at the same time landing a punch or two against the Republicans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Looks for a Share of the Iowa Spotlight', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T23:21:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', '