 the Financial Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Association Fannie Mae', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T23:53:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c15bd8d-cf85-57f3-b77c-ef6c8ec90d0d', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c15bd8d-cf85-57f3-b77c-ef6c8ec90d0d'}, {'abstract': '“Once Upon a Time in Anatolia,” an award winner at Cannes, directed by the Turkish filmmaker Nuri Bilge Ceylan, is both police procedural and existential meditation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/movies/once-upon-a-time-in-anatolia-directed-by-nuri-bilge-ceylan-review.html', 'snippet': '“Once Upon a Time in Anatolia,” an award winner at Cannes, directed by the Turkish filmmaker Nuri Bilge Ceylan, is both police procedural and existential meditation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A metaphysical road movie about life, death and the limits of knowledge, “Once Upon a Time in Anatolia” has arrived just in time to cure the adult filmgoer blues. It was directed by the Turkish filmmaker Nuri Bilge Ceylan, whose earlier movies include “Distant” and “Three Monkeys” and who in recent years has emerged as one of the consistently most exciting directors on the international scene. His latest, which shared the grand prize at the 2011 Cannes Film Festival, takes the unassuming form of a police investigation that, as miles and words mount, evolves into a plangent, visually stunning meditation on what it is to be human.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/arts/04once/04once-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/04/arts/04once/04once-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/arts/04once/04once-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 589, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/arts/04once/04once-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/04/arts/04once/04once-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Search for a Body, Another for Meaning', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Once Upon a Time in Anatolia'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Search for a Body, Another for Meaning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ceylan, Nuri Bilge', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T23:54:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4498acfc-d4c0-5be1-a38c-0d74a9bc5f23', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4498acfc-d4c0-5be1-a38c-0d74a9bc5f23'}, {'abstract': 'The Malaysian government, the largest shareholder in Proton Holdings, the parent of the niche British sports-car manufacturer, may divest itself of its stake in Proton, according to reports.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/with-ownership-of-corporate-parent-reportedly-in-flux-lotus-cars-awaits-a-resolution/', 'snippet': 'The Malaysian government, the largest shareholder in Proton Holdings, the parent of the niche British sports-car manufacturer, may divest itself of its stake in Proton, according to reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ambitions of Lotus Cars, which showed six concepts just over a year ago at the Paris auto show, are again the subject of rumors and speculation. The Malaysian government may follow the advice once given by Colin Chapman, the founder of Lotus, to “simplify and add lightness” by divesting itself of Proton Holdings, the corporate parent of the boutique British sports-car manufacturer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Ownership of Corporate Parent Reportedly in Flux, Lotus Cars Awaits a Resolution', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ferrari SpA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lotus Cars Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proton', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malaysia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T23:54:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rory Carroll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carroll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb4d401d-d827-52d1-be09-5cfd8659053d', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb4d401d-d827-52d1-be09-5cfd8659053d'}, {'abstract': '“If you want to be president, man up and be president,” Rick Santorum said.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/santorum-delivers-harsh-critique-of-obama-and-his-values/', 'snippet': '“If you want to be president, man up and be president,” Rick Santorum said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'URBANDALE, Iowa – The students at Des Moines Christian Assembly found out Tuesday morning that class was being dismissed early so they could get a special civics lesson from a visiting former United States senator, Rick Santorum.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Santorum Delivers Harsh Critique of Obama and His Values', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-03T23:59:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4b50ee5-2003-5e60-9f0c-e54f7a77d44c', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4b50ee5-2003-5e60-9f0c-e54f7a77d44c'}, {'abstract': 'The psychiatrist and author Robert Jay Lifton disagrees with Steven Pinker’s new book arguing that humans have become less violent. Readers are invited to respond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/opinion/invitation-to-a-dialogue-are-we-less-violent.html', 'snippet': 'The psychiatrist and author Robert Jay Lifton disagrees with Steven Pinker’s new book arguing that humans have become less violent. Readers are invited to respond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'