n neighboring Lebanon are getting a very different picture of events in Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While supporters of the Syrian uprising have done a remarkable job of documenting the Arab League observer mission \x97 filling YouTube channels with video of outraged citizens describing the violent crackdown on dissent by the Syrian government \x97 viewers of one television station in neighboring Lebanon are getting a very different picture of events in Syria.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Hezbollah TV, Syrians Who Support Assad Claim to Be the Victims', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T00:10:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36fef4fc-6e04-592b-9c36-9398547aa41f', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36fef4fc-6e04-592b-9c36-9398547aa41f'}, {'abstract': 'After saturation coverage of the campaigning in Iowa, news media outlets, at last, report on the results.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/decoding-the-iowa-caucus-coverage/', 'snippet': 'After saturation coverage of the campaigning in Iowa, news media outlets, at last, report on the results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2012 Iowa caucuses on Tuesday night offer a first judgement on the Republican presidential candidates. But with its changing cast of frontrunners, Web-paced reports of scandal and intrigue, and saturation TV coverage of rural campaign stops, the Iowa campaigning has provided enough spectacle to exhaust entire teams of reporters. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Decoding the Iowa Caucus Coverage', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T00:10:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b96a6a8f-5d95-5ee2-bbb6-ec20f2ffc7c5', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b96a6a8f-5d95-5ee2-bbb6-ec20f2ffc7c5'}, {'abstract': 'Why the first wave of entrance poll data is too unreliable to be released by The Times.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/explaining-tonights-polls/', 'snippet': 'Why the first wave of entrance poll data is too unreliable to be released by The Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Within an hour or so, we’ll be getting results about Iowa voters’ preferences from interviews that are known as “entrance polls” — similar to the exit polls conducted for primaries in other states. Edison Research of Somerville, N.J. stations interviewers at a random number of caucus sites, and they ask voters before they head inside to fill out questionnaires about their choices for a presidential candidate, and their positions on other issues.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Explaining Tonight’s Polls', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T00:17:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Phillips', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Phillips', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/289d9652-6b3a-5d05-a4b3-54ec98381478', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/289d9652-6b3a-5d05-a4b3-54ec98381478'}, {'abstract': 'The Iowa offensive tackle Riley Reiff told coach Kirk Ferentz today that he will skipping his senior year to declare for the N.F.L. Draft.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/sports/ncaafootball/iowa-tackle-reiff-will-enter-draft.html', 'snippet': 'The Iowa offensive tackle Riley Reiff told coach Kirk Ferentz today that he will skipping his senior year to declare for the N.F.L. Draft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Iowa offensive tackle Riley Reiff told coach Kirk Ferentz today that he will skipping his senior year to declare for the N.F.L. Draft. Reiff is considered one of the top tackle prospects in the N.F.L. Draft; ESPN projects him as a Top 10 pick. Reiff is planning on leaving this weekend to train. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iowa Tackle Will Enter Draft', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iowa Tackle Will Enter Draft', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T00:22:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79bb4840-c926-5947-b09e-3cc4eee99a13', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79bb4840-c926-5947-b09e-3cc4eee99a13'}, {'abstract': 'The offense has stagnated in the absence of Amar’e Stoudemire and Iman Shumpert. Both seem likely to return Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/sports/basketball/knicks-feel-effects-of-missing-players.html', 'snippet': 'The offense has stagnated in the absence of Amar’e Stoudemire and Iman Shumpert. Both seem likely to return Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENBURGH, N.Y. — The most compelling action on the Knicks’ practice court Tuesday came 30 minutes after practice ended. There, in a spirited game of 3-on-3, Amar’e Stoudemire and Iman Shumpert traded passes and slick drives.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/04/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks Hope to Get Boost From Return of Rookie', 'kicker': None, 'content_k