'snippet': 'Residents of the medieval villages of the Cinque Terre in Italy are working to restore the Unesco World Heritage site after a devastating October storm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VERNAZZA, Italy — When Unesco added the Cinque Terre, five medieval coastal towns perched along the Ligurian Coast, to its World Heritage List in 1997, it cited “the harmonious interaction between people and nature to produce a landscape of exceptional scenic quality.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/world/LIGURIA-1/LIGURIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/04/world/LIGURIA-1/LIGURIA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/world/LIGURIA-1/LIGURIA-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/world/LIGURIA-1/LIGURIA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/04/world/LIGURIA-1/LIGURIA-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Liguria’s Coastal Hills, a Storm’s Fury Brings a Struggle for Restoration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Liguria’s Coastal Hills, A Storm’s Fury Brings A Struggle for Restoration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'v