he likely did not commit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/opinion/a-very-likely-miscarriage-of-justice.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Jerry Brown of California should commute the life sentence Shirley Ree Smith received for a crime she likely did not commit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The power to pardon is an essential means of justice, allowing a governor to right what the law got wrong. Gov. Jerry Brown of California has been asked to commute to time served the sentence of Shirley Ree Smith, who was convicted in 1997 of killing her grandson and has already served 10 years of a 15-years-to-life sentence. We urge the governor to commute her sentence so she does not now have to return to prison as a result of a misguided Supreme Court ruling. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘A Very Likely Miscarriage of Justice’', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '&#8216;A Very Likely Miscarriage of Justice&#8217;', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shaken Baby Syndrome', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T02:32:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/849d508a-9c8e-5d4d-9c38-c38133da1470', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/849d508a-9c8e-5d4d-9c38-c38133da1470'}, {'abstract': 'A new evaluation system can help improve a crucial program for children from poor families.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/opinion/raising-standards-for-head-start.html', 'snippet': 'A new evaluation system can help improve a crucial program for children from poor families.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Head Start program, which prepares disadvantaged 3- and 4-year-olds for school, has served nearly 30 million children since it was created in 1965. While there is little doubt that the federal program is critically important for these children and their parents, quality varies widely among programs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raising Standards for Head Start', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Raising Standards for Head Start', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Pre-School)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Head Start Program', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T02:36:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6cb8d07-f9f6-50bb-a36d-04c95a6725cb', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6cb8d07-f9f6-50bb-a36d-04c95a6725cb'}, {'abstract': 'The Rams’ nonconference victory ended a 54-game losing streak against ranked opponents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/sports/ncaabasketball/no-22-harvard-loses-to-fordham.html', 'snippet': 'The Rams’