ists say hundreds or thousands are needed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Syrian activists reported that at least two people were killed on Tuesday in the restive city of Hama in central Syria, despite the presence of Arab League observers there. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria Killings Continue; Group to Add Observers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria Killings Continue; Group to Add Observers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T04:07:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2958ca7-5594-57f6-8ed6-8648594d901b', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2958ca7-5594-57f6-8ed6-8648594d901b'}, {'abstract': 'Youssou N’Dour, although extremely popular in his country, must overcome a lack of political experience in his campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/world/africa/youssou-ndour-senegal-singer-runs-for-president.html', 'snippet': 'Youssou N’Dour, although extremely popular in his country, must overcome a lack of political experience in his campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Putting his lucrative recording and touring career on hold in response to what he called a “supreme patriotic duty,” the Senegalese singer-songwriter Youssou N’Dour announced late Monday that he was running for president of his country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/world/SENEGAL/SENEGAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/04/world/SENEGAL/SENEGAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/world/SENEGAL/SENEGAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/04/world/SENEGAL/SENEGAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/04/world/SENEGAL/SENEGAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Singer Responds to ‘Patriotic Duty’ to Enter Senegal’s Presidential Race', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Singer Responds to ‘Supreme Patriotic Duty’ to Enter Senegal’s Presidential Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Senegal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "N'Dour, Youssou", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wade, Abdoulaye', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T04:13:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_