 {'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Sulzberger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48555015-34a5-5d8b-ba53-2af744eec2a6', 'word_count': 1394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48555015-34a5-5d8b-ba53-2af744eec2a6'}, {'abstract': 'The energy at Rick Santorum’s post-caucus party in Johnston, Iowa, was palpable.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/lovin-it-at-the-santorum-ballroom/', 'snippet': 'The energy at Rick Santorum’s post-caucus party in Johnston, Iowa, was palpable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHNSTON, Iowa — “I’m lovin’ it!” shouted Lynn Rodgers as she stood in front of a television tuned to Fox News.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Lovin’ It’ at the Santorum Ballroom', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T04:25:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf929a90-ff97-5e5a-8f07-5050ff5a3b40', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf929a90-ff97-5e5a-8f07-5050ff5a3b40'}, {'abstract': 'Conceding that he had not placed in the top three in Iowa, Mr. Gingrich nevertheless vowed to continue on and blasted the process of negative campaigning.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/gingrich-promises-great-debate-in-n-h/', 'snippet': 'Conceding that he had not placed in the top three in Iowa, Mr. Gingrich nevertheless vowed to continue on and blasted the process of negative campaigning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — Newt Gingrich promised that a “great debate” in the Republican party will begin tomorrow in New Hampshire as he lashed out at Mitt Romney as a “Massachusetts moderate” who would not fundamentally fix the country’s problems.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Promises ‘Great Debate’ in N.H.', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T04:39:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5113578b-ed82-5caa-a2ef-4fb650a33d36', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5113578b-ed82-5caa-a2ef-4fb650a33d36'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’s political unit is on the ground in the Hawkeye State — with the candidates and at the caucus sites — to provide live updates and analysis as the 2012 nominating contests begin.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/iowa-caucus-live-coverage/', 'snippet': 'The Times’s political unit is on the ground in the Hawkeye State — with the candidates and at the caucus sites — to provide live updates and analysis as the 2012 nominating contests begin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Caucusgoers all over Iowa are gathering in their communities Tuesday night to pick a Republican nominee for president. The Times’s political unit is on the ground in the Hawkeye State — with the candidates and at the caucus sites — to provide live updates and analysis of the 2012 nominating contests. Follow along on the live dashboard and on Twitter (@thecaucus), get real-time results and dig deeper into the numbers with FiveThirtyEight. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iowa Caucus Live Blog', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T04:45:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84a0c2c4-3911-5960-a1e6-efaf728f1ba4', 'word_count': 11073, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84a0c2c4-3911-5960-a1e6-efaf728f1ba4'}, {'abstract': 'A bill to increase female representation in Parliament is on hold, again.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/a-long-wait-for-equality-in-parliament/', 'snippet': 'A bill to increase female representation in Parliament is on hold, again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Indian Parliament will “remain a male bastion for the near future,” Nilanjana S. Roy writes in the International Herald Tribune. The lower house, “almost 90 percent male in its composition, had ensured that a bill intended to increase the number of female members would not be passed for at least another year,” she writes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Long Wait for Equality in Parliament', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T04:50:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ca2f4ca-71c6-568d-b722-1bc873996c0d', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ca2f4ca-71c6-568d-b722-1bc873996c0d'}, {'abstract': 'Representative Michele Bachmann of Minnesota declined to drop out of the Republican presidential contest despite having come in last in the Iowa caucus.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/bachmann-stays-in-the-race/', 'snippet': 'Representative Michele Bachmann of Minnesota declined to drop out of the Republican presidential contest despite having come in last in the Iowa caucus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — Michele Bachmann declined to drop out of the Republican presidential contest despite having come in last in the Iowa caucus, receiving only about 5 percent of the vote.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann Stays in the Race', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T04:50:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a129459d-de23-5c92-9f1f-8818a45756ac', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a129459d-de23-5c92-9f1f-8818a45756ac'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/03/news-quiz-jan-4-2012/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Jan. 4, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T04:52:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffa66390-15b0-5f9f-86bd-a30a6a5ba7b0', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffa66390-15b0-5f9f-86bd-a30a6a5ba7b0'}, {'abstract': 'About 150 people associated with the Occupy Wall Street movement demonstrated in Midtown Manhattan against a military spending bill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/nyregion/3-arrested-as-occupy-protestors-march-in-midtown.html', 'snippet': 'About 150 people associated with the Occupy Wall Street movement demonstrated in Midtown Manhattan against a military spending bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 150 people associated with the Occupy Wall Street movement demonstrated on Tuesday at several Midtown locations, including Grand Central Terminal, where three people were arrested, the authorities said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3 Arrested as Occupy Protesters March in Midtown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grand Central Terminal (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T04:58:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ad5baa5-48bb-5db5-982e-934e04c05d4f', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ad5baa5-48bb-5db5-982e-934e04c05d4f'}, {'abstract': 'For sore muscles, ice is not always the panacea that most of us believe it to be, and in some instances, it can be counterproductive.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/why-ice-may-be-bad-for-sore-muscles/', 'snippet': 'For sore muscles, ice is not always the panacea that most of us believe it to be, and in some instances, it can be counterproductive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Already, the benches in gym locker rooms and beside basketball courts are filling with 2012’s early casualties, those of us who, goaded by New Year’s resolutions, are exercising a bit too enthusiastically and developing sore muscles. Many of us will then drape ice packs over our aching muscles. But a new review article published this month in the journal Sports Medicine suggests that for sore muscles, ice is not always the panacea that most of us believe it to be and that, in some instances, it can be counterproductive. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Ice May Be Bad for Sore Muscles', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Phys Ed: Why Ice May Not Be Good for Sore Muscles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muscles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T05:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2755e147-aa9b-5ac4-b07f-bfd124984a3f', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2755e147-aa9b-5ac4-b07f-bfd124984a3f'}, {'abstract': 'Reports from the city’s major brokerage firms blame dwindling condominium inventory for a 12 percent decline in the fourth quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/realestate/manhattan-real-estate-prices-are-steady-but-sales-drop.html', 'snippet': 'Reports from the city’s major brokerage firms blame dwindling condominium inventory for a 12 percent decline in the fourth quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Manhattan real estate market closed out 2011 with prices relatively flat, but sales volume for the fourth quarter was down by more than 12 percent from the previous year largely because of shrinking condominium inventory as fewer new developments came to market, according to reports that will be released by the city’s major brokerage firms on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Real Estate Prices Are Steady in Manhattan, but Sales Fall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Real Estate Prices Are Steady In Manhattan, but Sales Fall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condominiums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T05:04:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian S. Toy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Toy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67d230d4-36a7-57ff-9566-dfd7b9f05064', 'word_count': 850, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67d230d4-36a7-57ff-9566-dfd7b9f05064'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 197 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/word-of-the-day-regal/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 197 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'regal •\\ˈre-gəl\\• adjective', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | regal', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T05:05:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_materi