{'abstract': 'Republican caucus-goers took a weak field and made it stronger.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/in-praise-of-iowa/', 'snippet': 'Republican caucus-goers took a weak field and made it stronger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s easy to complain about the Iowa caucuses – easy and completely justifiable. Iowa’s caucus-goers have given us the presidency of Jimmy Carter, lent credibility to Pat Robertson’s political ambitions and created a permanent constituency for ethanol subsidies among Democrats and Republicans alike. As friendly and civic-minded as Iowans may be, there’s no reason why a low-turnout contest in a small, rural state should play such an outsize role in every presidential nominating process.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Praise of Iowa', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T05:58:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd883913-671e-5b88-b8d4-c7aa534b1628', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd883913-671e-5b88-b8d4-c7aa534b1628'}, {'abstract': 'Landon Donovan, starting his second off-season loan in England in two years, made his first appearance for Everton on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/landon-donovan-could-return-for-everton-today/', 'snippet': 'Landon Donovan, starting his second off-season loan in England in two years, made his first appearance for Everton on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:35 p.m. | Updated Landon Donovan provided some wonderful highlights during his two-month, 13-game loan to Everton in 2010. Though credited with only two goals during his brief time with the Toffees, Donovan played extremely well: he injected speed on the wing, served up assists, took corner kicks and helped the squad earn victories over the likes of Manchester City, Manchester United and Chelsea. Named the club’s player of the month for January, he made a lasting impression with fans, teammates and Everton Manager David Moyes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donovan Returns for Everton', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donovan, Landon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Everton (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T06:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Godfrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Godfrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c695d909-a930-5846-9248-fa6865b6