asic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlasic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd7da7ed-4dcd-5325-ac1e-69bfb569d317', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd7da7ed-4dcd-5325-ac1e-69bfb569d317'}, {'abstract': 'DeRozan, George, and Iguodala have all improved from beyond the arc this season.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/three-new-stars-in-three-point-land/', 'snippet': 'DeRozan, George, and Iguodala have all improved from beyond the arc this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The addition of a consistent 3-point shot is one of the great off-season glamor moves in the world of N.B.A. player development, akin to adding “15 pounds of muscle,” or a non-point guard claiming to have put in work on his ball-handling. But there’s good reason for teams and players to value the extension of range back to the 3-point arc; although the long ball is certainly chic, it’s also an incredibly efficient shot and a facilitator for an established halfcourt offense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Three New Stars in 3-Point Land', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'George, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Granger, Danny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hibbert, Roy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iguodala, Andre', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indiana Pacers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'n