ing that she would not continue her campaign for the Republican presidential nomination.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:12 p.m. | Updated WEST DES MOINES, Iowa — On the morning before Iowa’s first-in-the-nation caucuses, Representative Michele Bachmann of Minnesota said she was counting on a “miracle” to resurrect her faltering campaign. On the morning after, she acknowledged that it was beyond saving.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann Says She Will Not Continue in the Race', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T16:31:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a215f1b-491a-583c-b4cd-0d7783647d66', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a215f1b-491a-583c-b4cd-0d7783647d66'}, {'abstract': 'By naming Scott Thompson as its new chief, the struggling Internet company sent a signal that it intended to try to fix its problems in the public domain, rather than taking itself private.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/with-new-ceo-yahoo-charts-independent-course/', 'snippet': 'By naming Scott Thompson as its new chief, the struggling Internet company sent a signal that it intended to try to fix its problems in the public domain, rather than taking itself private.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the announcement of its new chief executive on Wednesday, Yahoo appears determined to chart its own course, rather than selling out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With New C.E.O., Yahoo Charts Independent Course', 'kicker': 'DealBoo