ountability for the state’s public school system. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Cuomo’s State of the State Address', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the State Message (NYS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T18:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ba25f69-3c20-5926-b457-484a19f48796', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ba25f69-3c20-5926-b457-484a19f48796'}, {'abstract': 'With his endorsement of Mitt Romney, John McCain chose the man he clashed with four years ago over Rick Santorum, whom he clashed with only last year.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/for-mccain-a-choice-between-old-enemies/', 'snippet': 'With his endorsement of Mitt Romney, John McCain chose the man he clashed with four years ago over Rick Santorum, whom he clashed with only last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Senator John McCain, the last Republican presidential nominee, choosing between former Gov. Mitt Romney of Massachusetts or Rick Santorum, a former Senate colleague, was a pick between old enemies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For McCain, a Choice Between Old Enemies', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T18:34:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a69dbe2-8cfa-528d-a9b6-c5fa7bdce051', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a69dbe2-8cfa-528d-a9b6-c5fa7bdce051'}, {'abstract': 'A newspaper in Collingswood, N.J., says that a marker honoring the actor, who grew up there, was brought to its offices after it was found in a dump. Jim Maley, the mayor of Collingswood, said the plaque was removed during the cleanup of a park where it hung and was going to be returned.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/plaque-honoring-michael-landon-is-on-a-highway-to-huh/', 'snippet': 'A newspaper in Collingswood, N.J., says that a marker honoring the actor, who grew up there, was brought to its offices after it was found in a dump. Jim Maley, the mayor of Collingswood, said the plaque was removed during the cleanup of a park wh...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though it may lack the drama of a saloon fistfight or shootout on the Ponderosa ranch, the saga of a marker honoring the “Bonanza” star Michael Landon that was posted in Collingswood, N.J., has yielded differing accounts of what happened to it before it reached the office of a weekly newspaper there and, if nothing else, has revealed how strong sentiment for the actor still runs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Plaque Honoring Michael Landon Is on a Highway to Huh?', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playgrounds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landon, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T18:35:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbdce1ef-5946-5048-8ffe-c1619ed14354', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbdce1ef-5946-5048-8ffe-c1619ed14354'}, {'abstract': 'The scene at the caucuses brings to mind a scene from a movie.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/apocalypse-iowa/', 'snippet': 'The scene at the caucuses brings to mind a scene from a movie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Brooks: Gail, anybody can be a pundit when there’s some decisive thing to talk about, but when you’ve got a tie, that’s when we separate the pros from the amateurs. If a tie in a football or a baseball game is like kissing your sister, then a tie in an Iowa caucus would be like kissing Rick Santorum’s sister.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apocalypse Iowa', 'kicker': 'Opinionator', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlson, Tucker', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 