 '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/4a1c0063-403a-5a0b-9ad1-2a9b587cdef0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/4a1c0063-403a-5a0b-9ad1-2a9b587cdef0'}, {'abstract': 'Learning about how one scientist is using bioluminescence to draw attention to water pollution, holding a class forum on the issue and then finding ways to take action.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/making-the-invisible-visible-exploring-and-addressing-water-pollution/', 'snippet': 'Learning about how one scientist is using bioluminescence to draw attention to water pollution, holding a class forum on the issue and then finding ways to take action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | What is bioluminescence, and what function does it play in living organisms? How have researchers harnessed bioluminescence in studies of toxicity and pollution? In this lesson, students explore deep-sea bioluminescence, learn how scientists use this property to identify contaminants in water and participate in a forum on water pollution. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making the Invisible Visible: Exploring and Addressing Water Pollution', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T20:11:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Cutraro and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cutraro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d177c992-6eaf-5ceb-bca2-16c740b2a366', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d177c992-6eaf-5ceb-bca2-16c740b2a366'}, {'abstract': 'A report, commissioned in response to the phone-hacking scandal and released Wednesday, offered a window into the relationship between the news media and the Metropolitan Police Service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/world/europe/report-tells-of-cozy-relationship-between-british-news-media-and-london-police-surrounding-phone-hacking-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'A report, commissioned in response to the phone-hacking scandal and released Wednesday, offered a window into the relationship between the news media and the Metropolitan Police Service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Do not indulge in “late-night carousing” with journalists. Do not flirt with them, either. And above all, advised a report released here on Wednesday, if you are a police officer, do not let a member of the news media ply you with alcohol in an effort to get you to “drop your defenses” and start saying things you should keep to yourself. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip for London Police Officers: Booze and Secrets Don’t Mix', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tip for London Police Officers: Booze and Secrets Don’t Mix', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scotland Yard (Metropolitan Police Service)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stephenson, Paul Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'g