for the producers said that they expected to recoup their full investment by the time the show closes; the producers declined to provide that dollar amount.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Relatively Speaking’ to Close at the End of the Month', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T20:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By PATRICK HEALY', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'HEALY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3494fb8-d8b5-58f1-ab78-27a3dffc95ee', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3494fb8-d8b5-58f1-ab78-27a3dffc95ee'}, {'abstract': 'A slightly smaller field shifted its attention to New Hampshire and South Carolina, the next chances for someone not named Romney to challenge the perceived front-runner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/us/politics/bachmann-and-perry-withdrawals-would-shift-race.html', 'snippet': 'A slightly smaller field shifted its attention to New Hampshire and South Carolina, the next chances for someone not named Romney to challenge the perceived front-runner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — After a weeks-long battle over the allegiance of Iowa caucusgoers, the race for the Republican nomination broke open into a wider contest on Wednesday, as the remaining candidates moved to exploit a still-unsettled electorate and expanded playing field in New Hampshire and South Carolina.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Race Moves Beyond Iowa', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republican Race Moves Beyond Iowa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T20:30:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b0bdd20-be48-5553-afc9-e23d71e6cb0d', 'word_count': 1164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b0bdd20-be48-5553-afc9-e23d71e6cb0d'}, {'abstract': 'Friends and colleagues remember Dummett, one of the 20th century’s most influential philosophers, who died last week.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/remembering-michael-dummett/', 'snippet': 'Friends and colleagues remember Dummett, one of the 20th century’s most influential philosophers, who died last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sir Michael Dummett, one of the most influential philosophers of the 20th century, died last week in Oxford, England. He held the position of Wykeham Professor of Logic at Oxford University from 1979 until his retirement in 1992. Below is a gathering of reminiscences from fellow philosophers, including Hilary Putnam, Timothy Williamson, Dorothy Edgington, Daniel Isaacson, and several others who knew Dummett, worked with him or were influenced by his life and work. We invite readers to offer their own contributions in the comments section.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Michael Dummett', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T20:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dc34d64-e0dc-5d7a-9e74-c45942adfc08', 'word_count': 7724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dc34d64-e0dc-5d7a-9e74-c45942adfc08'}, {'abstract': "Jimi Sitko is a competitive vegan bodybuilder that has forged a distinctive, small subculture of anti-beefcake beefcakes who hope to change more of their competitors' eating habits.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000001232617/the-competitive-vegan-bodybuilder.html', 'snippet': "Jimi Sitko is a competitive vegan bodybuilder that has forged a distinctive, small subculture of anti-beefcake beefcakes who hope to change more of their competitors' eating habits.", 'lead_paragraph': "Jimi Sitko is a competitive vegan bodybuilder that has forged a distinctive, small subculture of anti-beefcake beefcakes who hope to change more of their competitors' eating habits.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/17/multimedia/video-veganbodybuilders/video-veganbodybuilders-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legac