.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/knitty-gritty/', 'snippet': 'A room at the Hotel Pelirocco, in Brighton, England, is entirely knitted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chunky, cabled, cropped — wool is popping up in everyone’s wardrobes this season. (Chalk it up to all those knitting clubs and yarn-bombers.) But who would expect to check into a hotel room and find the sheets, the bedside lamp and even the morning breakfast knitted?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knitty Gritty', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T21:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lena de Casparis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Casparis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b878393-a2f1-527b-8885-a7648f5988b9', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b878393-a2f1-527b-8885-a7648f5988b9'}, {'abstract': 'The City Council speaker has been criticized for allowing the indicted councilman access to his discretionary money.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/quinn-stands-behind-decision-on-seabrook-funds/', 'snippet': 'The City Council speaker has been criticized for allowing the indicted councilman access to his discretionary money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 5:23 p.m. | A slightly testy City Council Speaker Christine C. Quinn on Wednesday defended her decision not to strip Councilman Larry Seabrook of control over more than $350,000 in discretionary funds in the coming budget cycle, even as he awaits a second trial on corruption charges related to his use of such funds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quinn Stands Behind Decision on Seabrook Funds', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quinn, Christine C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seabrook, Larry B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T21:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11ffaeef-77a8-51fa-ac08-3c6ab06c6983', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11ffaeef-77a8-51fa-ac08-3c6ab06c6983'}, {'abstract': 'Neighbors of a new business on Lenox Avenue complained that its look was too garish, and recalled an earlier, uglier time.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/a-new-sign-and-a-liquor-store-becomes-a-wine-shop/', 'snippet': 'Neighbors of a new business on Lenox Avenue complained that its look was too garish, and recalled an earlier, uglier time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sign is now of the times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Sign, and a Liquor Store Becomes a Wine Shop', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gentrification', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Signs and Signage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wine and Spirits', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'HARLEM (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T21:01:54+0000', 'document_type': 'art