ract': 'The inland market in southwestern France is more reasonably priced than the nearby Mediterranean and Atlantic coastal regions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/greathomesanddestinations/real-estate-in-southwestern-france.html', 'snippet': 'The inland market in southwestern France is more reasonably priced than the nearby Mediterranean and Atlantic coastal regions.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A RESTORED MEDIEVAL HOUSE WITH SIX BEDROOMS IN SOUTHERN FRANCE', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/greathomesanddestinations/20120108ihhfrance-slide-JKKD/20120108ihhfrance-slide-JKKD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/03/greathomesanddestinations/20120108ihhfrance-slide-JKKD/20120108ihhfrance-slide-JKKD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/03/greathomesanddestinations/20120108ihhfrance-slide-JKKD/20120108ihhfrance-slide-JKKD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'House Hunting in ... Southwestern France', 'kicker': 'International Real Estate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'House Hunting in ... Southwestern France', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T21:22:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Great Homes & Destinations', 'byline': {'original': 'By Virginia C. McGuire', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Virginia', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McGuire', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e31de68a-b3c4-5f8c-a244-a8dcde347439', 'word_count': 1088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e31de68a-b3c4-5f8c-a244-a8dcde347439'}, {'abstract': 'Univision flexed its popularity muscles last week, scoring an impressive weekly win over every English-language broadcast network among viewers between the ages of 18 and 34.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/for-univision-the-holidays-bring-viewers/', 'snippet': 'Univision flexed its popularity muscles last week, scoring an impressive weekly win over every English-language broadcast network among viewers between the ages of 18 and 34.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What happens when the broadcast networks decide to scale down their programming for a week because of the holidays? They lose viewers to Univision.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Univision, the Holidays Bring Viewers', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Univision', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T21:23:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09294a4d-6e5d-538d-bad3-808219df396a', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09294a4d-6e5d-538d-bad3-808219df396a'}, {'abstract': 'The current quarterback Greg McElroy and the former quarterback Boomer Esiason were scathing in their criticism of the Jets.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/team-draws-criticism-from-past-and-present-jets/', 'snippet': 'The current quarterback Greg McElroy and the former quarterback Boomer Esiason were scathing in their criticism of the Jets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In separate radio interviews Wednesday, Jets quarterbacks past and present unloaded on the team for fostering a culture of dysfunction and selfishness. And neither of them was Joe Namath.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Team Draws Criticism From Past and Present Jets', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T21:23:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dd82f78-7cb9-592b-bcef-808851ca4cf6', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dd82f78-7cb9-592b-bcef-808851ca4cf6'}, {'abstract': '“NCIS” draws more than 20 million viewers, but the premiere of ABC’s “Work It” does not fair nearly as well.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/new-programming-same-old-results-as-cbs-reigns/', 'snippet': '“NCIS” draws more than 20 million viewers, but the premiere of ABC’s “Work It” does not fair nearly as well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the return of new programming CBS resumed its usual Tuesday-night perch as the No. 1 network in total viewers and in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic. “NCIS” led the way as it broke the 20-million total viewer barrier while “NCIS: Los Angeles” had its largest audience of the season with 17 million. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Programming, Same Old Results as CBS Reigns', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T21:25:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e0c5c3d-e01c-58fd-a955-9a3e4416f811', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e0c5c3d-e01c-58fd-a955-9a3e4416f811'}, {'abstract': 'In his debut novel, Ayad Akhtar describes the coming of age of a young Pakistani-American in Milwaukee in the 1980s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/books/american-dervish-by-ayad-akhtar-review.html', 'snippet': 'In his debut novel, Ayad Akhtar describes the coming of age of a young Pakistani-American in Milwaukee in the 1980s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What a pleasure to encounter a first novel as self-assured and effortlessly told as Ayad Akhtar’s “American Dervish.” Mr. Akhtar, a first-generation Pakistani-American, has written an immensely entertaining coming-of-age story set during the early 1980s among the Pakistanis in the author’s hometown, Milwaukee.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/arts/05book/05book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/arts/05book/05book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/05/arts/05book/05book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stumbling Through an American Muslim Maze', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stumbling Through an American Muslim Maze', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T21:33:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Langer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Langer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/79d37fff-4e0f-5ed9-b4eb-dfa0423e6377', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79d37fff-4e0f-5ed9-b4eb-dfa0423e6377'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s decision to make four recess appointments could face a legal challenge over executive prerogative and the Senate’s power to declare when it is in recess.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/obama-tempts-fight-over-recess-appointments/', 'snippet': 'The president’s decision to make four recess appointments could face a legal challenge over executive prerogative and the Senate’s power to declare when it is in recess.', 'lead_paragraph': ' 5:41 p.m. | Updated  President Obama’s decision on Wednesday to grant recess appointments to four officials — even though the Senate contends that it is not in recess — was an unprecedented legal step that brought into sharper focus a recent bipartisan struggle over presidential power.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Tempts Fight Over Recess Appointments', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T21:34:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbae2d02-0976-5e3a-a907-1d1310a1d27e', 'word_count': 1293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbae2d02-0976-5e3a-a907-1d1310a1d27e'}, {'abstract': 'To raise a child who enjoys good food, you have to cook good food yourself.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/teaching-children-to-love-healthy-food/', 'snippet': 'To raise a child who enjoys good food, you have to cook good food yourself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chicken fingers. No one — no chef and no parent — wants to raise a child who eats only chicken fingers. Or only white bread, or pasta-with-butter-and-nothing-else. The question of how to raise that highly desirable child who eats everything is one many first-time parents grapple with, and Fanae Aaron, an author and art director, was one such parent. Unlike most of us, though, who approach the process through trial and error, asking around the playground and either embracing or completely rejecting the foods we grew up with, Ms. Aaron set out to ask chefs how they fed their kids (who, she rightly presumed, mostly ate more than just white food).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teaching Children to Love Healthy Food', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker-Pope, Tara', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T21:35:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c10c463e-f7be-513c-b25c-8a07e6574411', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c10c463e-f7be-513c-b25c-8a07e6574411'}, {'abstract': 'If it’s good, I did it, if it’s bad, I had nothing to do with it.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/romney-on-jobs/', 'snippet': 'If it’s good, I did it, if it’s bad, I had nothing to do with it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greg Sargent has been demanding that Mitt Romney be held accountable for two claims that he makes about jobs: (1) That Obama has been a job-destroyer (2) that he, Romney, created 100,000 jobs at Bain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney on Jobs', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T21:42:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eef6feff-5977-500b-8655-6f5d88470082', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eef6feff-5977-500b-8655-6f5d88470082'}, {'abstract': 'European countries agreed in principle to impose an embargo on Iran’s oil, diplomats said, their most aggressive move yet in the tense standoff with Iran over its nuclear program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/world/europe/europe-moves-toward-ban-on-iran-oil.html', 'snippet': 'European countries agreed in principle to impose an embargo on Iran’s oil, diplomats said, their most aggressive move yet in the tense standoff with Iran over its nuclear program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Iran on Thursday sought to downplay the importance of intensified economic sanctions against it, even as European Union countries moved closer to agreement on an embargo on Iranian oil, their boldest step so far in the increasingly tense standoff with Iran over its nuclear program. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/world/europe/europe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Takes Bold Step Toward a Ban on Iranian Oil', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Bold Step, Europe Nears Embargo on Iran Oil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3,