an Melville.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long ago, The Onion ran the mock-headline: “Book Given As Gift Actually Read.” More recently, the Tumblr site The Books They Gave Me has collected autobiographical reminiscences that illustrate the sometimes perilous task of finding the right book for the right reader. But what about book-giving as a theme in literature itself? The Times ran a feature last month itemizing the books “authors love to give and receive,” but the examples below suggest that some writers have taken a dim view of book-giving in their own work:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Perilous Art of Giving Books', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AMIS, MARTIN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melville, Herman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T21:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34f19bb1-7da6-5564-b06d-3dca585cebbc', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34f19bb1-7da6-5564-b06d-3dca585cebbc'}, {'abstract': 'A bevy of young actresses is contending for the unofficial title of most fashionable and memorable performance on a red carpet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/fashion/golden-globes-alert-seeking-the-next-young-actress-to-reign-in-red-carpet-fashions.html', 'snippet': 'A bevy of young actresses is contending for the unofficial title of most fashionable and memorable performance on a red carpet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT last year’s Golden Gl