'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d2fb122-895e-5f63-8519-857e32bdfd05', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d2fb122-895e-5f63-8519-857e32bdfd05'}, {'abstract': 'Coverage of the caucuses Tuesday night gave CNN an unusual second-place finish, but its 1.3 million viewer total was well below the 2.2 million total of four years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/fox-news-leads-in-iowa-ratings-cnn-in-second-has-big-falloff/', 'snippet': 'Coverage of the caucuses Tuesday night gave CNN an unusual second-place finish, but its 1.3 million viewer total was well below the 2.2 million total of four years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The cable news networks finished in slightly scrambled positions in the ratings for coverage of the Iowa caucuses Tuesday night, with the perennial leader, Fox News, in first, CNN in second, and MSNBC in third. Typically, MSNBC is second and CNN is third.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fox News Leads in Iowa Ratings; CNN, in Second, Has Big Falloff', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSNBC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T22:56:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'ori