eople will eventually\xa0wear glasses and contact lenses with built-in screens, delivering content we can use. It will be like having smartphones in our eyes, but much smarter ones.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Wearable Computers Help You Sleep, Not Tweet', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute for the Future', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-04T23:18:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1273128a-d428-539e-a260-1604ed37eeaf', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1273128a-d428-539e-a260-1604ed37eeaf'}, {'abstract': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission named Pamela A. Gibbs to head its recently created Office of Minority and Women Inclusion, fulfilling a mandate of the Dodd-Frank Act.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/a-new-diversity-monitor-for-the-s-e-c/', 'snippet': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission named Pamela A. Gibbs to head its recently created Office of Minority and Women Inclusion, fulfilling a mandate of the Dodd-Frank Act.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:52 a.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Diversity Monitor for the S.E.C.', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keyword