egacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/05/arts/VIDEOGAMES/VIDEOGAMES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Real Connections in Game Land', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Real Connections In Game Land', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T00:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Video Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Schiesel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schiesel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3885f9fc-9d41-522b-85b7-9feaf624d33f', 'word_count': 1218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3885f9fc-9d41-522b-85b7-9feaf624d33f'}, {'abstract': 'The Green Mountain Project performed Monteverdi’s Vespers of the Blessed Virgin at the Church of St. Jean Baptiste.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/arts/music/vespers-of-1640-at-church-of-st-jean-baptiste-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Green Mountain Project performed Monteverdi’s Vespers of the Blessed Virgin at the Church of St. Jean Baptiste.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The soprano Jolle Greenleaf and the violinist Scott Metcalfe may not have fully realized that they were on to something big when they started the Green Mountain Project, an outgrowth of Ms. Greenleaf’s superb vocal ensemble, Tenet. The idea was to assemble the proper forces for Monteverdi’s Vespers of the Blessed Virgin — a collection of sacred works published in 1610 — and to ring in 2010 with a performance celebrating the 400th anniversary of the work. The concert proved a resounding success, and Ms. Greenleaf (the group’s artistic director) and Mr. Metcalfe (its music director) reconvened their forces at the start of 2011 and attracted a huge audience. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/arts/VESPERS1/VESPERS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 686, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Presenting Sacred Works in a Style From the 1600s', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Presenting Sacred Works in a Style From the 1600s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monteverdi, Claudio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Mountain Project', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T00:03:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/933d313c-d82b-5106-b129-e94837597494', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/933d313c-d82b-5106-b129-e94837597494'}, {'abstract': 'Minnesota’s Sixth Congressional District, which Michele Bachmann has represented since 2007, could be redrawn to her disadvantage.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/bachmanns-next-decision-whether-to-run-for-re-election/', 'snippet': 'Minnesota’s Sixth Congressional District, which Michele Bachmann has represented since 2007, could be redrawn to her disadvantage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEST DES MOINES, Iowa — Having only decided not to continue her presidential bid on Wednesday morning, Representative Michele Bachmann of Minnesota has yet to decide whether to run for re-election to Congress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bachmann’s Next Decision: Whether to Run for Re-election', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bachmann, Michele M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T00:04:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ebe18c3-7259-56b3-b830-944fc39d3a55', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ebe18c3-7259-56b3-b830-944fc39d3a55'}, {'abstract': 'The enterprising art-world duo Suzanne Oxenaar and Otto Nan opened Hotel The Exchange on the Dramrak last month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/garden/rooms-at-hotel-the-exchange-in-amsterdam-fashion-checks-in.html', 'snippet': 'The enterprising art-world duo Suzanne Oxenaar and Otto Nan opened Hotel The Exchange on the Dramrak last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States has Alex Calderwood, the risk-taking owner of the Ace Hotel chain with its street art aesthetic, but the Netherlands has Suzanne Oxenaar and Otto Nan. The enterprising art-world duo opened their first hotel, The Lloyd, in Amsterdam in 2004, and it quickly became the go-to place for artists, musicians and designers. In 2010, they opened the pop-up Llove Hotel in Tokyo, a tongue-in-cheek twist on that city’s pay-by-the-hour hotels.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/garden/05ROOMS1_SPAN/05CURRENTS6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/05/garden/05ROOMS1_SPAN/05CURRENTS6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/garden/05ROOMS1_SPAN/05CURRENTS6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/garden/05ROOMS1_SPAN/05CURRENTS6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/05/garden/05ROOMS1_SPAN/05CURRENTS6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Hotel The Exchange in Amsterdam, Fashion Checks In', 'kicker': 'Currents | Rooms', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Amsterdam, Fashion Checks In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMSTERDAM (NETHERLANDS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T00:08:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Wagner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wagner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46347a54-1b5e-591c-95ad-710cb4683b56', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46347a54-1b5e-591c-95ad-710cb4683b56'}, {'abstract': 'With convenience comes the job of keeping the vent clean, a chore that might be a good candidate for that 2012 to-do list.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/garden/services-cleaning-that-dryer-vent.html', 'snippet': 'With convenience comes the job of keeping the vent clean, a chore that might be a good candidate for that 2012 to-do list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s the holy grail of New York apartment living: your own washer-dryer. But along with the convenience comes the job of keeping the dryer vent clean, a chore that, for apartment and single-home dwellers, might be a good candidate for that 2012 to-do list. \xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/garden/05SERVICES/05CURRENTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/05/garden/05SERVICES/05CURRENTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/garden/05SERVICES/05SERVICES-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/garden/05SERVICES/05CURRENTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/05/garden/05SERVICES/05CURRENTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}