r-powered .177-caliber pellet gun. The eighth grader, Jaime Gonzalez, had brandished the weapon in the hallway at Cummings Middle School, after most students were already in their classrooms. The student pointed the gun at Brownsville police officers who came to the scene, and he ignored numerous commands to drop it, police officials said. Two officers fired their weapons, and the student was shot twice. Police officials said he had assaulted a student before the officers arrived and told witnesses that he was going to confront the officers with the weapon. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas: Student With Pellet Gun Is Killed by Police', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas: Student With Pellet Gun Is Killed By Police', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T01:06:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manny Fernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2bfc48e-ee18-5f6d-af61-568c9839cd58', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2bfc48e-ee18-5f6d-af61-568c9839cd58'}, {'abstract': 'A reader says it is unwise to pile up student debt in the hope of better job prospects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/opinion/back-to-school-and-debt.html', 'snipp