Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Bishop Who Fathered 2 Children Resigns', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Bishop Who Fathered 2 Children Resigns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clergy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T01:10:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad3a2706-cf02-5eb5-9468-165fb789eae1', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad3a2706-cf02-5eb5-9468-165fb789eae1'}, {'abstract': 'An advisory panel had recommended more research into implantable mesh used to treat urinary incontinence because of reports of serious injuries linked to the devices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/health/research/fda-orders-more-study-on-surgical-mesh-risks.html', 'snippet': 'An advisory panel had recommended more research into implantable mesh used to treat urinary incontinence because of reports of serious injuries linked to the devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration issued an order on Wednesday requiring makers of implantable surgical mesh used to treat urinary incontinence in women to study its risks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Orders Surgical Mesh Makers to Study Risks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.D.A. Orders Surgical Mesh Makers to Study Risks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Implants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Devices', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgery and Surgeons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Incontinence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T01:12:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Meier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/348afe2d-174e-514f-8bc8-36c0b3fad8bb', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/348afe2d-174e-514f-8bc8-36c0b3fad8bb'}, {'abstract': 'Despite having had four consecutive winning seasons, the Falcons, who will play the Giants on Sunday, have not won a single playoff game during that period.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/sports/football/falcons-shoot-for-a-rarity-a-playoff-win.html', 'snippet': 'Despite having had four consecutive winning seasons, the Falcons, who will play the Giants on Sunday, have not won a single playoff game during that period.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLOWERY BRANCH, Ga. — The Atlanta Falcons are caught between floors, between smooth and wrinkled, between coming or going. They are considered solid, often better than that, but no one is going to give the Falcons their due until solid turns into something substantial, like a playoff win or two.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/sports/Y-FALCONS/Y-FALCONS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/sports/Y-FALCONS/Y-FALCONS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/05/sports/Y-FALCONS/Y-FALCONS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Falcons Still Pursuing Elusive Playoff Victory', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Falcons Still Pursuing Elusive Playoff Victory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Matt (1985- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, Roddy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Mike (1959- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Julio (1989- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Falcons', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T01:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Glier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7a5f5b5-09f3-55e1-99ec-a2a46f3cebab', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7a5f5b5-09f3-55e1-99ec-a2a46f3cebab'}, {'abstract': 'Kenneth R. Feinberg, administrator of the $20 billion fund created to pay damages from the 2010 Gulf of Mexico oil spill, has reopened the cash window.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/business/energy-environment/louisiana-payments-for-gulf-spill-resume.html', 'snippet': 'Kenneth R. Feinberg, administrator of the $20 billion fund created to pay damages from the 2010 Gulf of Mexico oil spill, has reopened the cash window.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Kenneth R. Feinberg, administrator of the $20 billion fund created to pay damages from the 2010 Gulf of Mexico oil spill, has reopened the cash window. Mr. Feinberg halted payments on Tuesday while seeking clarification from the federal judge overseeing litigation related to the disaster. Judge Carl J. Barbier recently ruled that 6 percent of settlements after Nov. 7 be put in escrow for certain plaintiff litigation expenses. On Wednesday, he issued a ruling stating that the payment only applies to new settlements, and that the 6 percent will be calculated from the net amount of the settlement after withholding for liens and other obligations, not from the gross amount. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Louisiana: Payments for Gulf Spill Resume', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Louisiana: Payments For Gulf Spill Resume', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barbier, Carl J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico Oil Spill (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinberg, Kenneth R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T01:14:03+0000'