ning, Mary Anderson helps out at an equine therapy program for children with disabilities like impaired mobility, autism and blindness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/nyregion/overcoming-her-own-pain-to-help-disabled-children-ride-and-walk-tall.html', 'snippet': 'Every Saturday morning, Mary Anderson helps out at an equine therapy program for children with disabilities like impaired mobility, autism and blindness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mary Anderson tugged on the strap of Kiarra Boodram’s helmet, making sure it was secure, then pushed Kiarra’s wheelchair up to Hot Diggity, a white pony three and a half feet tall with gray and black patches. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/05/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/05/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Retired, but Overcoming Her Pain to Help Disabled Children Ride, and Walk, Tall', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Retired, but Overcoming Her Pain to Help Disabled Children Ride, and Walk, Tall', 'name'