fter beating the Jets and the Cowboys, the Giants open the playoffs against the Falcons and their star quarterback.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/giants-go-from-facing-rex-ryan-to-rob-ryan-to-matt-ryan/', 'snippet': 'After beating the Jets and the Cowboys, the Giants open the playoffs against the Falcons and their star quarterback.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — By the end of the day Sunday, the Giants will have faced a number of notable opponents on their quest for a Super Bowl: the New England Patriots, the San Francisco 49ers, the New Orleans Saints, the Green Bay Packers and three guys named Ryan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Go From Facing Rex Ryan to Rob Ryan to Matt Ryan', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Matt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Falcons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Cowboys', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T02:36:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4517851b-8201-53eb-b57e-7ae110d6fa01', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4517851b-8201-53eb-b57e-7ae110d6fa01'}, {'abstract': 'The thing that I’ve learned from my own personal experience of working at a struggling Baghdad trauma center is that you should cherish every single victory that you take part in making and enjoy it to the extreme, because those proud moments never last.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/04/night-in-a-baghdad-e-r/', 'snippet': 'The thing that I’ve learned from my own personal experience of working at a struggling Baghdad trauma center is that you should cherish every single victory that you take part in making and enjoy it to the extreme, because those proud moments neve...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the United States military has left Iraq, the long-term legacy of two decades of war and sanctions will become clearer over the coming months and years. Not only through violence, but also in the emergence – or otherwise – of civil institutions and their ability to provide basic services. Here, one Iraqi doctor writes about how her hospital is coping.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Night in a Baghdad E.R.', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T02:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lubna Naji', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lubna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Naji', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c96050bf-67a2-54f7-a656-4d34e1792216', 'word_count': 1242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c96050bf-67a2-54f7-a656-4d34e1792216'}, {'abstract': 'Monitors designed to gauge physical activity and subsequent calories burned might become a silver bullet for weight loss and for sticking to 