er, Sheik Hamad bin Jassim al-Thani, consulted on Wednesday with Ban Ki-moon, the United Nations secretary general, about enhancing the performance of the Arab League monitors in Syria. “The monitors have tried their best,” Sheik Hamad said, but they lack any previous experience, so could benefit from United Nations technical help. The protocol that Syria signed with the Arab League demands that the government, not the monitors, halt the violence, the minister said, so forging a regional solution and avoiding a referral to the Security Council requires that Syria respect that agreement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Role of Monitors in Syria Comes Under Scrutiny', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Role of Monitors in Syria Comes Under Scrutiny', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thani, Hamad bin Jassim al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T02:52:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3727405-3868-50f1-91f6-adaa4f19dbce', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3727405-3868-50f1-91f6-adaa4f19dbce'}, {'abstract': 'The appointment of Richard Cordray means the agency will have a strong pro-consumer leader and can now exercise its full powers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/opinion/the-consumer-financial-protection-bureau-gets-a-chief.html', 'snippet': 'The appointment of Richard Cordray means the agency will have a strong pro-consumer leader and can now exercise its full powers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly six months after it opened its doors, the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau finally has a director, after President Obama’s recess appointment of Richard Cordray, a former attorney general of Ohio who served as the bureau’s chief of enforcement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Consumer Bureau Gets a Chief', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Consumer Bureau Gets a Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cordray, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Labor Relations Board', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T02:52:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1adf1d9-ac33-523a-b0cd-683c918ca3ac', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1adf1d9-ac33-523a-b0cd-683c918ca3ac'}, {'abstract': 'Frank DiMattina, who is said to be an associate of the Genovese crime family, is accused of shaking down a man who bought Ariana’s Catering Hall from him in March.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/nyregion/frank-dimattina-accused-of-threatening-a-catering-rival.html', 'snippet': 'Frank DiMattina, who is said to be an associate of the Genovese crime family, is accused of shaking down a man who bought Ariana’s Catering Hall from him in March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The alleged Genovese crime associate was the owner of one of Staten Island’s most popular catering halls, and he came to believe that his life had the makings of a reality television drama. He produced slick promotional videos for the show that he conceived and hoped to star in, “Banquet Boyz,” and posted them on YouTube. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/nyregion/BANQUET/BANQUET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 569, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/nyregion/BANQUET/BANQUET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/05/nyregion/BANQUET/BANQUET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Dreams of Reality-Show Stardom to Accusations of Tough-Guy Extortion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Dreams of Reality-Show Stardom to Accusations of Tough-Guy Extortion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Genovese Crime Family', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 