he song would surprise Katharine Lee Bates, who wrote the words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney has done a swell job memorizing the words to “America the Beautiful.” Especially since that awkward afternoon in 2008 when he had trouble reminding a houseful of Iowans about “our beautiful land and our mountains and … and … and our waving, or, uh, what is it, let’s see, waving filled … no, how does it … and uh … \xa0amber waves of grain!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Covering ‘America the Beautiful’', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T03:06:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Sherr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sherr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac997822-e313-563c-b5d8-462eb0389e6d', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac997822-e313-563c-b5d8-462eb0389e6d'}, {'abstract': 'The appointment of Richard Cordray as director of the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau finally gives the agency the legal standing to supervise payday lenders, money transfer agencies, credit bureaus and debt collectors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/us/politics/cordrays-appointment-clears-way-for-consumer-financial-agency.html', 'snippet': 'The appointment of Richard Cordray as director of the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau finally gives the agency the legal standing to supervise payday lenders, money transfer agencies, credit bureaus and debt collectors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Payday lenders, money transfer agencies, credit bureaus and debt collectors, take notice: the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau is coming after you, and quickly.', 'print