l', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9e06ecd-3fea-52cd-b587-1ecb31a0ccd4', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9e06ecd-3fea-52cd-b587-1ecb31a0ccd4'}, {'abstract': 'On Jan. 5, 1914, Henry Ford, head of the Ford Motor Company, introduced a minimum wage scale of $5 per day, more than doubling the wages for most employees.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/jan-5-1914-henry-ford-implements-5-a-day-wage/', 'snippet': 'On Jan. 5, 1914, Henry Ford, head of the Ford Motor Company, introduced a minimum wage scale of $5 per day, more than doubling the wages for most employees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Jan. 5, 1914, Henry Ford, head of the Ford Motor Company, introduced a minimum wage scale of $5 per day, more than doubling the wages for most employees. He also offered profit sharing to employees who lived a clean lifestyle, reduced the daily worker’s shift to eight hours from nine and declared that no employee would “be discharged except for proved unfaithfulness or irremediable inefficiency.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jan. 5, 1914 | Henry Ford Implements the $5-a-Day Wage', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T09:28:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22389c1c-263b-5e67-80c4-f444c78f1f66', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22389c1c-263b-5e67-80c4-f444c78f1f66'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the sentence that is free of grammatical error?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/test-your