'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4ffe7dc-2c10-5923-b13e-1b4e73928eb8', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4ffe7dc-2c10-5923-b13e-1b4e73928eb8'}, {'abstract': 'Two tastes that go beautifully together.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/magazine/pork-and-apples.html', 'snippet': 'Two tastes that go beautifully together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a classic — really killer — combination, but one most people don’t play around with much. Once I started to think about it, though, the possibilities for pork and apples seemed myriad: obviously, you can cook chops and chunks in a cast-iron skillet, maybe with a little bacon and onions . . . an easy vision. Bacon-wrapped apples, skewered and roasted or broiled (or grilled, for you warm-climate people) is another. A B.C.A. — bacon, cheese (soft, mild, brie-ish cheese, especially) and apple — is a fine sandwich, especially when cooked as you would a grilled cheese.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/magazine/08eat1_span/08eat1_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/magazine/08eat1_span/08eat1_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/magazine/08eat1_span/08eat1_span-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/magazine/08eat1_span/08eat1_span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/magazine/08eat1_span/08eat1_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/magazine/08eat1_span/08eat1_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/magazine/08eat1_span/08eat1_span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pork and Apples', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sweet, Savory, Simple', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pork', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPLES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T12:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/288fef83-dcd7-50ae-9ffe-fe8e6edc219e', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/288fef83-dcd7-50ae-9ffe-fe8e6edc219e'}, {'abstract': 'The actor Timothy Olyphant has found a good fit in the modern-day western series “Justified” on FX, based on stories by Elmore Leonard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/arts/television/timothy-olyphant-in-elmore-leonards-justified-on-fx.html', 'snippet': 'The actor Timothy Olyphant has found a good fit in the modern-day western series “Justified” on FX, based on stories by Elmore Leonard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the premiere of the new season of “Justified,” beginning Jan. 17, a dashing psychopath makes a casual reference to this Kentucky crime drama’s signature prop, the Stetson worn by the protagonist, United States Marshal Raylan Givens.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08OLYPHANT_SPAN/08OLYPHANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08OLYPHANT_SPAN/08OLYPHANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08OLYPHANT_SPAN/08OLYPHANY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08OLYPHANT_SPAN/08OLYPHANY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08OLYPHANT_SPAN/08OLYPHANY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Defined by a Smile and a Drawl', 'kicker': 'Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defined by a Smile and a Drawl', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX (TV Network)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olyphant, Timothy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T12:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Egner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa4f1d6d-c75c-5ad1-a58f-b3692b316e38', 'word_count': 1865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa4f1d6d-c75c-5ad1-a58f-b3692b316e38'}, {'abstract': 'Involving people in the product-development process can create a network of evangelists.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/turning-facebook-followers-into-online-focus-groups/', 'snippet': 'Involving people in the product-development process can create a network of evangelists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aaron Schwartz founded his three-person watch company last year with an unusual slogan: “We’re not craftsmen, we’re just good listeners” — listeners to customers, that is.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turning Facebook Followers Into Online Focus Groups', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdsourcing (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T12:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By David H. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93b19fe6-033f-5030-b16f-254493d98563', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93b19fe6-033f-5030-b16f-254493d98563'}, {'abstract': 'A published report says that Research in Motion’s board will relieve the company’s two co-chief executives of their additional titles and duties as co-chairmen. But that may not solve RIM’s problem, which is an inability to create a new generation of competitive products in a timely way. One analyst said the problem was that the two men “don’t want bosses.”', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/would-rim-get-fixed-with-a-new-chairman/', 'snippet': 'A published report says that Research in Motion’s board will relieve the company’s two co-chief executives of their additional titles and duties as co-chairmen. But that may not solve RIM’s problem, which is an inability to create a new generation...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, Research in Motion, maker of the BlackBerry,\xa0avoided a showdown with a Canadian mutual fund operator at its annual meeting by agreeing to study the relationship between its management and its directors. Like other investors, Northwest and Ethical Investments  was concerned that James L. Balsillie and Mike Lazaridis, RIM’s co-chief executives, also serve as co-chairmen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/blogs/bitpix-rim-hq1/bitpix-rim-hq1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/blogs/bitpix-rim-hq1/bitpix-rim-hq1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/10/blogs/bitpix-rim-hq1/bitpix-rim-hq1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Would a New Chairman Fix RIM?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Balsillie, James L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lazaridis, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Research In Motion Ltd', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T12:11:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65bc0eb7-4b7f-52ff-99a3-5248b1ae5429', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65bc0eb7-4b7f-52ff-99a3-5248b1ae5429'}, {'abstract': 'The state’s new guidelines aim to keep parolees from returning to prison for minor infractions, but for one Harlem man, the changes came too late.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/rating-a-parolees-risk-before-a-return-to-prison/', 'snippet': 'The state’s new guidelines aim to keep parolees from returning to prison for minor infractions, but for one Harlem man, the changes came too late.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brendan Cochrane had been, by and large, a model parolee. After serving 10 years for attempted murder, he started a video production business, moved into an apartment in Manhattan, got engaged and abstained from drugs and alcohol.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rules May Help Parolees Avoid Jail for Small Errors', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Probation and Parole', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T12:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Walker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3636672-299d-543d-8aba-218cd1c7dd0e', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3636672-299d-543d-8aba-218cd1c7dd0e'}, {'abstract': 'Société Générale of France has announced an agreement to achieve about 880 “voluntary departures” in its domestic investment banking business, joining other banks that are planning job reductions in response to Europe’s debt crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/european-banks-prepare-for-more-layoffs/', 'snippet': 'Société Générale of France has announced an agreement to achieve about 880 “voluntary departures” in its domestic investment banking business, joining other banks that are planning job reductions in response to Europe’s debt crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Less than a week into the new year, European banks are already planning new job cuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'European Banks Prepare More Job Cuts', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T12:20:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe4a728f-a17e-51c6-b95f-4dc5dd9c96b1', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe4a728f-a17e-51c6-b95f-4dc5dd9c96b1'}, {'abstract': 'Economists behaving badly, early 2009.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/how-this-started/', 'snippet': 'Economists behaving badly, early 2009.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reading some of the comments on the ongoing dispute over manners in economics, I see many people claiming that the freshwater guys have not been as extreme as I say, that they never declared that Keynesian economics is completely invalid. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How This Started', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T12:21:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e1643ea-74e2-56bc-bb01-946baa525d6c', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e1643ea-74e2-56bc-bb01-946baa525d6c'}, {'abstract': 'India’s super-cheap tablet will get upgrades, manufacturer says, which will delay deliveries.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/aakash-update-oversold-underperforming/', 'snippet': 'India’s super-cheap tablet will get upgrades, manufacturer says, which will delay deliveries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Within days of going on sale online, the 2,500 rupee (about $47) Aakash computer appears to be sold out, according to the tablet’s official Web site.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aakash Update: Oversold, Underperforming', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T12:23:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamposh Raina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamposh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Raina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c80c1aa-3d07-590a-96a3-cc1c0a845424', 'word_count': 913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c80c1aa-3d07-590a-96a3-cc1c0a845424'}, {'abstract': 'Fewer ice drifts and an earlier arrival of spring imperil many harp seal pups.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/a-short-childhood-for-seal-pups-on-thin-ice/', 'snippet': 'Fewer ice drifts and an earlier arrival of spring imperil many harp seal pups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a mother harp seal, timing is everything. Pups are born and nursed on seasonal sea ice during a brief window before the spring sun melts the ephemeral nursery. After only 12 days, the mother weans her pups and the family slides into the ocean together.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Seal Pups on Thin Ice, a Short Childhood', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drownings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'valu