and commodities dropped.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Shares Rally and Recover, but the Euro Falls Again', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Shares Rally and Recover, but the Euro Falls Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADP Employer Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labor Department (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T13:35:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cedd9d5-1204-56b9-8930-a6357404b7c0', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cedd9d5-1204-56b9-8930-a6357404b7c0'}, {'abstract': 'Carey Mulligan explains why being naked on camera felt liberating in “Shame.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/transforming-a-body-and-a-performance/', 'snippet': 'Carey Mulligan explains why being naked on camera felt liberating in “Shame.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'What does it take to make an Oscar-worthy performance for an actress? From Nicole Kidman’s nose to Charlize Theron’s pounds, a physical transformation is often key. The Bagger took a close look at the hopefuls in this season’s race, who endured piercings and shavings (Rooney Mara in “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo”), gained weight (Michelle Williams, who wanted it for her curves in “My Week With Marilyn”) and added British teeth (Meryl Streep in “The Iron Lady”). In “Albert Nobbs,” Glenn Close and Janet McTeer even changed gender, a process that Ms. McTeer said quickly gave her a window into her character.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Transforming a Body — and a Performance', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fassbender, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQueen, Steve', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mulligan, Carey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Refn, Nicolas Winding', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T13:41:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/201f9ae7-55cd-5a14-b3b3-f02f9107c7f6', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/201f9ae7-55cd-5a14-b3b3-f02f9107c7f6'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/morning-take-out-396/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook Aside, Market for I.P.O.’s Stays Cool \xa0|\xa0 It will take more than Facebook to heat up the tepid market for initial public offerings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T13:46:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66a840b2-4520-58c1-92de-49df4c6c475b', 'word_count': 2267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66a840b2-4520-58c1-92de-49df4c6c475b'}, {'abstract': 'The Argentine public’s excessive reaction to the news that President Cristina Fernández de Kirchner has cancer is an alarming reminder that she has personalized power far too much.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/the-cult-of-kirchner/', 'snippet': 'The Argentine public’s excessive reaction to the news that President Cristina Fernández de Kirchner has cancer is an alarming reminder that she has personalized power far too much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — Argentinians breathed a sigh of relief on Wednesday when President Cristina Fernández de Kirchner’s spokesman announced that the operation to remove her cancerous thyroid gland had gone off without a hitch. Supporters gathered outside the hospital since Tuesday night cheered in jubilation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cult of Kirchner', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirchner, Cristina Fernandez de', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirchner, Nestor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Buenos Aires (Argentina)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T13:48:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', '