 face, or whatever body part to which you want to impart a glowing, healthy look.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/vain-glorious-spray-your-vitamins/', 'snippet': 'A new treatment allows you to spray vitamins onto your face, or whatever body part to which you want to impart a glowing, healthy look.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With 2012 under way and New Year’s resolutions established (eat fewer frites, exercise more, drink less), why not add a less challenging one — take more vitamins.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Spray Your Vitamins', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T14:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Earle-Levine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Earle-Levine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2539b5e-376d-53b4-88af-25f4a046dca9', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2539b5e-376d-53b4-88af-25f4a046dca9'}, {'abstract': 'Some call the move to soon close 10 percent of public libraries in Britain an austerity measure, others a transformation project. Really it’s a crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/the-demise-of-the-public-library/', 'snippet': 'Some call the move to soon close 10 percent of public libraries in Britain an austerity measure, others a transformation project. Really it’s a crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A couple of years ago, after a reading in Karachi, I told off a young man who was asking me to sign a pirated copy of one of my books. Piracy is destroying publishing in Pakistan, I told him. He said he understood but added that because pirated books are cheaper he could buy more of them. It’s not as if Karachi is filled with public libraries, he said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Demise of the Public Library', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T14:17:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kamila Shamsie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kamila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shamsie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/809bdea9-e168-5e80-838e-ddf0b343d10a', 'word_count': 648, 'uri': 'nyt://article/809bdea9-e168-5e80-838e-ddf0b343d10a'}, {'abstract': 'In expressing support for full-fledged casinos in New York, Mr. Cuomo is perhaps facing reality, but also pushing a notion that typically makes money off gamblers who don’t have much to begin with.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/cuomos-push-for-casinos-not-good-news-for-all-gamblers/', 'snippet': 'In expressing support for full-fledged casinos in New York, Mr. Cuomo is perhaps facing reality, but also pushing a notion that typically makes money off gamblers who don’t have much to begin with.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At about the same time that Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo began his “State of the State” speech on Wednesday, \xa0a middle-aged woman walked away from a slot machine called Great Wall in the new gambling hall adjoining Aqueduct racetrack. That machine had taken enough of her money for one day, said the woman, who preferred to keep her name to herself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo’s Push for Casinos Not Good News for All Gamblers', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Mario M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Sheldon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aqueduct Racetrack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Resorts World Casino New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlantic City (NJ)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T14:17:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edb60596-5858-5804-8821-04b08fbf79b1', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edb60596-5858-5804-8821-04b08fbf79b1'}, {'abstract': 'The Nook has sold well and drawn critical praise, but its maker acknowledged that it has not been profitable, leaving investors anxious about future costs.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/barnes-noble-considers-spinning-off-its-nook-unit/', 'snippet': 'The Nook has sold well and drawn critical praise, but its maker acknowledged that it has not been profitable, leaving investors anxious about future costs.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:13 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barnes & Noble Considers Spinning Off Its Nook Unit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Barnes & Noble Nook', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barnes & Noble Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T14:32:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman and Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4242da39-ba5e-5841-a103-f0503255568b', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4242da39-ba5e-5841-a103-f0503255568b'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cumberbatch, who offers a contemporary portrayal of Sir Arthur Conan Doyle’s consulting detective, will play a major role in the sequel to J. J. Abrams’ “Star Trek” movie — but just what role is a mystery all its own.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/sherlock-star-benedict-cumberbatch-is-clued-in-to-star-trek-role/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cumberbatch, who offers a contemporary portrayal of Sir Arthur Conan Doyle’s consulting detective, will play a major role in the sequel to J. J. Abrams’ “Star Trek” movie — but just what role is a mystery all its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The case of the vacant “Star Trek” role appears to be solved — or has it? The “Sherlock” star Benedict Cumberbatch, who offers a contemporary portrayal of Sir Arthur Conan Doyle’s consulting detective, Sherlock Holmes, on that BBC and PBS series, has been cast in a major role in a sequel to “Star Trek,” the cinematic reimagining of James T. Kirk’s outer-space adventures from J. J. Abrams and his crew. But just what role Mr. Cumberbatch will play in the new movie is a mystery all its own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Sherlock’ Star Benedict Cumberbatch Is Clued In to ‘Star Trek’ Role', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T14:33:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By DAVE ITZKOFF', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ITZKOFF', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4a90884-3d9d-5379-85b1-3683bc432163', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4a90884-3d9d-5379-85b1-3683bc432163'}, {'abstract': 'Rick Santorum on Thursday criticized the president for making a recess appointment to the consumer protection bureau and also took a swipe at Mitt Romney, his main rival in New Hampshire.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/santorum-criticizes-obama-for-recess-appointments/', 'snippet': 'Rick Santorum on Thursday criticized the president for making a recess appointment to the consumer protection bureau and also took a swipe at Mitt Romney, his main rival in New Hampshire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Rick Santorum on Thursday assailed President Obama for the recess appointments he made a day earlier, accusing the president of thinking he is “above the law” and urging the Senate to “go to the ramparts on this one.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mul