the thousands, and that’s the way she likes it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The designer Angela Scott’s lovingly offbeat boots and heels don’t sell by the thousands and can’t be found in more than a handful of stores — Jeffrey in New York and Tomorrowland in Japan are two of them — but that’s exactly how the Texas-based designer likes it. “I think there’s something unique about a product that isn’t overproduced,” says Scott about her shoes, all of which are bench-made in small-batch factories by cobblers who hand-stitch and mold the vegetable-tanned leather and eco-friendly cork soles that characterize Scott’s collection. “I’d love to just be in one shop, the best shop, in cities around the world. That would be a lovely place for me to sit,” she says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cobbled Together | The Office of Angela Scott', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T15:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Scire', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scire', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdba7ccb-700d-5cb5-bb21-8497f8c0f49c', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdba7ccb-700d-5cb5-bb21-8497f8c0f49c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Khan has had to cancel upcoming performances—as well as a run of “Sacred Monsters,” with Sylvie Guillem, in France this week—due to an injured Achilles tendon.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/akram-khan-cancels-show-due-to-injury/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Khan has had to cancel upcoming performances—as well as a run of “Sacred Monsters,” with Sylvie Guillem, in France this week—due to an injured Achilles tendon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Akram Khan’s first full-length solo work, “Desh” received rapturous critical notices and attracted capacity audiences when it had its premiere at Sadler’s Wells this past October. So much so that the theater, unusually, decided to present “Desh” — a work in which Mr. Khan explores the confluence of his Bangladeshi origins with his British upbringing — again this season, in February. But Mr. Khan has had to cancel these coming performances, as well as a run of “Sacred Monsters,” with Sylvie Guillem, in France this week, because of an injured Achilles tendon, which is likely to keep him offstage for several months. Sadler’s Wells plans to schedule a replacement run of “Desh” in October.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Akram Khan Cancels Show Due to Injury', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Akram', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sadler's Wells", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T15:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roslyn Sulcas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roslyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sulcas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2677f69e-e3f8-5f1e-a205-2f904283015f', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2677f69e-e3f8-5f1e-a205-2f904283015f'}, {'abstract': 'New polls show some movement in the field in New Hampshire.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/a-shift-in-the-numbers/', 'snippet': 'New polls show some movement in the field in New Hampshire.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:55 a.m. | Updated  MANCHESTER — Results from New Hampshire tracking polls over the last 