h': 'A bronze disk recently discovered in the mud near the Putney Bridge in London seemed innocent enough, but on close inspection it has turned out to be one of the oldest pieces of British pornographic art, according to the Guardian. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ancient Pornographic Artifact Discovered by the Thames', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pornography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of London', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T18:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/699cda96-e9a6-5fea-a395-28d197d1df1a', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/699cda96-e9a6-5fea-a395-28d197d1df1a'}, {'abstract': 'The Italian company Motus brings its latest show, an interdisciplinary look at financial and social turmoil in Greece, to the Under the Radar festival.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/under-the-radar-5-questions-about-alexis-a-greek-tragedy/', 'snippet': 'The Italian company Motus brings its latest show, an interdisciplinary look at financial and social turmoil in Greece, to the Under the Radar festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In December 2008, weeks of rioting erupted in Athens after a police officer shot and killed a 15-year-old boy named Alexandros Grigoropoulos. Two years later the officer was convicted of murder and sentenced to life in prison.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under the Radar: 5 Questions About ‘Alexis: A Greek Tragedy’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Under the Radar Festival', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grigoropoulos, Alexandros', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T18:31:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8e8fd4d-43f2-51ed-9fc7-8f1326759e3a', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8e8fd4d-43f2-51ed-9fc7-8f1326759e3a'}, {'abstract': 'A push to repeat the bipartisanship of last year’s State of the Union address.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/another-try-for-bipartisanship/', 'snippet': 'A push to repeat the bipartisanship of last year’s State of the Union address.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago, as Washington grappled with the shooting rampage that nearly took the life of Representative Gabrielle Giffords, the centrist group Third Way made a modest suggestion to members of Congress: Mingle with lawmakers from the opposite party at the\xa0State of the Union address.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Try for Bipartisanship', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle'