'nyt://article/e3eb0d16-a834-55ed-ae04-4b4de5a9d06e'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney may have won the Iowa caucuses, but Rick Santorum appears to be seeing the largest improvement in the polls.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/first-post-iowa-polls-show-bounce-for-santorum/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney may have won the Iowa caucuses, but Rick Santorum appears to be seeing the largest improvement in the polls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bounce that candidates receive in the polls after a primary or caucus is typically as much a function of exceeding expectations as their actual performance. Although Mitt Romney won the Iowa caucuses by eight votes, it looks as though Rick Santorum will see the largest improvement in his poll numbers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Post-Iowa Polls Show Bounce for Santorum', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T18:52:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/850b90cc-2c4c-5602-964f-0d4c7afa14a7', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/850b90cc-2c4c-5602-964f-0d4c7afa14a7'}, {'abstract': 'If the G.O.P. is so crazy, why is it poised to nominate Mitt Romney?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/a-party-of-extremists/', 'snippet': 'If the G.O.P. is so crazy, why is it poised to nominate Mitt Romney?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unlike the liberal writers quoted in my last post, Jacob Weisberg’s column on Mitt Romney’s inevitability doesn’t indulge in wishful thinking about how the primary campaign is rendering Romney unelectable in the fall. But his desire to insist on the G.O.P.’s extremism to leads him into this seemingly-contradictory analysis:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Party of Extremists?', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T18:54:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80b22a6a-365a-59f4-86b5-613a48d3c266', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80b22a6a-365a-59f4-86b5-613a48d3c266'}, {'abstract': 'Melena Ryzik has a drink with the actor Corey Stoll, who plays Ernest Hemingway in Woody Allen’s “Midnight in Paris.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/awardsseason/100000001249088/the-importance-of-being-ernest-hemingway.html', 'snippet': 'Melena Ryzik has a drink with the actor Corey Stoll, who plays Ernest Hemingway in Woody Allen’s “Midnight in Paris.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Melena Ryzik has a drink with the actor Corey Stoll, who plays Ernest Hemingway in Woody Allen’s “Midnight in Paris.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/video-ab-carpetbaggerparis/video-ab-carpetbaggerparis-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/video-ab-carpetbaggerparis/video-ab-carpetbaggerparis-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20