ce': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Words of Wisdom for Applicants from India', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T18:57:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23b8385a-2dea-5aab-84ef-61b9f7775241', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23b8385a-2dea-5aab-84ef-61b9f7775241'}, {'abstract': 'The recent Northeast chill requires serious outerwear — the kind that’s stuffed with down, lined with fleece and trimmed with fur.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/winter-wonders-lovers-of-puffers/', 'snippet': 'The recent Northeast chill requires serious outerwear — the kind that’s stuffed with down, lined with fleece and trimmed with fur.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The recent Northeast chill requires serious outerwear\xa0— the kind that’s stuffed with down, lined with fleece and trimmed with fur. Here, the television personality Alexa Chung dials down her metallic Marc Jacobs dress and Mary Janes with a furry and more utilitarian parka; the actress Julianne Moore makes an anorak look elegant by pairing it with chic black and brown accessories; and the actress Naomi Watts bundles up in dusty red denim and motorcycle boots.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winter Wonders | Lovers of Puffers', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T19:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd79d189-3b9a-5e2d-9d64-0cded5ef258e', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd79d189-3b9a-5e2d-9d64-0cded5ef258e'}, {'abstract': 'A survey of the top articles of 2011 from The New York Times Travel section.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/the-top-10-travel-articles-of-2011/', 'snippet': 'A survey of the top articles of 2011 from The New York Times Travel section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Life on a giant cruise ship, dealing with canceled flights, an alternate route to Machu Picchu — these are all subjects that attracted Web readers in 2011. As with last year’s version, this year’s list is topped by our annual Where to Go roundup. Other popular articles included spring weekend getaways, a different way to look at Paris and an essay on why we travel in unsettling times. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Top 10 Travel Articles of 2011', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T19:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/251c54ff-76e1-5dba-a22a-7ada6b1a1ac0', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/251c54ff-76e1-5dba-a22a-7ada6b1a1ac0'}, {'abstract': 'Dirk Diggler, porn star; Marky Mark makes the most of a sizable part.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/five-ku-