talks hockey with Jim Devellano, the senior vice president of the Red Wings and the former assistant general manager of the Islanders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Slap Shot contributor Christopher Botta talks hockey with Jim Devellano, the senior vice president of the Red Wings and the former assistant general manager of the Islanders. Also, Brian Compton of NHL.com and Adam Rotter of SNYRangersBlog join in. Topics include Rangers Coach John Tortorella, the Islanders’ John Tavares, Bruins-Devils and the N.H.L. draft. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Listen: SNY.tv Metro Hockey Podcast', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Red Wings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T19:18:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db7e243b-7a66-5bbf-81c8-04c5be399e1e', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db7e243b-7a66-5bbf-81c8-04c5be399e1e'}, {'abstract': 'Illegal hits drew long suspensions from the N.H.L. for repeat offenders Dan Carcillo of Chicago and Rene Bourque of Calgary.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/n-h-l-hands-down-two-big-suspensions/', 'snippet': 'Illegal hits drew long suspensions from the N.H.L. for repeat offenders Dan Carcillo of Chicago and Rene Bourque of Calgary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Calgary Flames forward Rene Bourque and Chicago Blackhawks wing Dan Carcillo may now be wishing that they had not again incurred the wrath of the N.H.L.’s disciplinary department. The two players received significant suspensions — five games for Bourque and seven for Carcillo — in response to their actions in recent games.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.H.L Hands Down Two Suspensions', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carcillo, Dan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shanahan, Brendan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calgary Flames', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Blackhawks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T19:26:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2c406ea-1aa6-59a9-85e0-dbca9698f955', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2c406ea-1aa6-59a9-85e0-dbca9698f955'}, {'abstract': 'Travel offered freedom and meant never having to commit to just one thing, or to one person.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/fashion/a-place-to-lay-my-heart-modern-love.html', 'snippet': 'Travel offered freedom and meant never having to commit to just one thing, or to one person.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN I met Joe, he told me he was trying to decide where to live. At the time, he lived in — well, that was hard to say. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', '