r’s race, which will route participants around the Great Lakes region in a four-state, one-province loop, begins in Traverse City, Mich. on June 23 and will conclude, at least for those whose old iron withstands the ordeal, in Dearborn, Mich., on July 1.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Racing Against Time Around the Great Lakes', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hemmings Motor News', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Lakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T19:35:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44e1d8e9-6914-5895-810e-6340b4059c7c', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44e1d8e9-6914-5895-810e-6340b4059c7c'}, {'abstract': 'The European Commission said airlines that refused to participate in its carbon trading system could be banned from European airports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/business/global/eu-toughens-stance-in-airline-carbon-dispute.html', 'snippet': 'The European Commission said airlines that refused to participate in its carbon trading system could be banned from European airports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — The European Commission said on Thursday that airlines that did not follow a new European law requiring them to account for their emissions of greenhouse gases could face being banned from European airports.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Stands Firm on Airline Emissions, Raising Fears of a Trade Conflict', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe Stands Firm on Airline Emissions, Raising Fears of a Trade Conflict', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T19:37:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Kanter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d0845e1-8409-5fde-bfe5-3b6835074c3b', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d0845e1-8409-5fde-bfe5-3b6835074c3b'}, {'abstract': 'The columnist Bill Conlin’s prominent portrait in the Baseball Hall of Fame’s Scribes and Mikemen exhibit preceded accusations against him of child molesting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/sports/baseball/sportswriters-tribute-seems-out-of-place-to-some-hall-of-fame-visitors.html', 'snippet': 'The columnist Bill Conlin’s prominent portrait in the Baseball Hall of Fame’s Scribes and Mikemen exhibit preceded accusations against him of child molesting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COOPERSTOWN, N.Y. — In a quiet, sun-splashed corridor, beyond the storied gallery of bronze plaques, a seemingly ordinary exhibit has created a singularly awkward situation for the Baseball Hall of Fame. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/sports/06cooperstown1/06cooperstown1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/06/sports/06cooperstown1/06cooperstown1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/sports/06cooperstown1/06cooperstown1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/sports/06cooperstown1/06cooperstown1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/06/sports/06cooperstown1/06cooperstown1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sportswriter’s Hall of Fame Tribute Is Out of Place to Some', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sportswriter’s Tribute At Hall of Fame Upsets Some Visitors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Inquirer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Hall of Fame', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conlin, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baseball Writers Assn of America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Phillies', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T19:38:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a460e59-ed4a-5f9d-a095-abc6e0f6d66b', 'word_count': 1246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a460e59-ed4a-5f9d-a095-abc6e0f6d66b'}, {'abstract': 'The first of the Carpetbagger’s looks at the season’s Scene Stealers is the actor who played Hemingway in “Midnight in Paris.” Watch the video with Corey Stoll.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/a-role-that-was-good-and-true-and-stole-the-scene/', 'snippet': 'The first of the Carpetbagger’s looks at the season’s Scene Stealers is the actor who played Hemingway in “Midnight in Paris.” Watch the video with Corey Stoll.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Corey Stoll was just a little-known actor who happened to be appearing opposite Scarlett Johansson in “A View From the Bridge” on Broadway when Woody Allen – who cast Ms. Johansson in his film “Match Point” — came to see the show. Not long after, Mr. Stoll, best known from his role as the bald detective on the short-lived “Law & Order: Los Angeles,” was called in to see Mr. Allen about a part in “Midnight in Paris.” He was duly petrified but wound up with the role of Hemingway. He donned a wig and a mustache, and on screen he was one of the most memorable stars in a cast that included Owen Wilson and Marion Cotillard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Role That Was Good and True and Stole the Scene', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, WOODY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotillard, Marion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johansson, Scarlett', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Owen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T19:43:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a34c01d4-d8a2-530d-9ce8-c4f0fe45b599', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a34c01d4-d8a2-530d-9ce8-c4f0fe45b599'}, {'abstract': 'A woman discovers the answer to the question: Why do many men, after a breakup or a divorce, find it so difficult to be alone, while most women in the same situation seem just fine?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/fashion/why-men-cant-stand-to-be-alone-after-a-breakup-or-a-divorce.html', 'snippet': 'A woman discovers the answer to the question: Why do many men, after a breakup or a divorce, find it so difficult to be alone, while most women in the same situation seem just fine?', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONE cold, misty autumn morning, I slipped and fell. I was on my way out to do errands, the mossy wooden deck on the north side of my house was slick with dew, I was in a hurry, I skidded, and both feet flew out from under me. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/fashion/SUB08FIRSTPERSON/SUB08FIRSTPERSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 