ttps://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/a-gadget-is-more-than-the-sum-of-its-parts/', 'snippet': 'If you think Amazon’s real cost to make that Kindle Fire is $201, then by all means go to China and cobble one together yourself. The components are only part of the cost of any gadget.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a teenager growing up in the Cleveland suburbs, my first real job was at a Chick-fil-A restaurant in a local mall. I did everything: manned the cash register, made sandwiches and cleaned up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Gadget Is More Than the Sum of Its Parts', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amazon Kindle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chick-fil-A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T20:36:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c12f4f45-4861-5a90-a5b6-4aab0c65a07f', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c12f4f45-4861-5a90-a5b6-4aab0c65a07f'}, {'abstract': 'The day in sports included heavy snowfall at the biathlon World Cup in Oberhof, Germany, and an upset in the quarterfinals of the Brisbane tennis tournament in Australia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/05/sports/20120105photoreplay.html', 'snippet': 'The day in sports included heavy snowfall at the biathlon World Cup in Oberhof, Germany, and an upset in the quarterfinals of the Brisbane tennis tournament in Australia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The day in sports included heavy snowfall at the biathlon World Cup in Oberhof, Germany, and an upset in the quarterfinals of the Brisbane tennis tournament in Australia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/sports/20120105photoreplay-slide-EYHW/20120105photoreplay-slide-EYHW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/sports/20120105photoreplay-slide-EYHW/20120105photoreplay-slide-EYHW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/05/sports/20120105photoreplay-slide-EYHW/20120105photoreplay-slide-EYHW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Photo Replay: Jan. 5', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biathlon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nordic Combined (Winter Sport Event)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T20:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8a74d127-88d4-5deb-8c0e-01e023ce2a37', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8a74d127-88d4-5deb-8c0e-01e023ce2a37'}, {'abstract': 'The New York auction house Guernsey’s explained on Thursday that all bidders in its planned winner-take-all auction of more than 5,500 artifacts salvaged from the wreckage of the Titanic must agree to abide by 19 pages’ worth of court-ordered covenants and commitments governing the collection.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/responsible-bidders-sought-for-titanic-auction/', 'snippet': 'The New York auction house Guernsey’s explained on Thursday that all bidders in its planned winner-take-all auction of more than 5,500 artifacts salvaged from the wreckage of the Titanic must agree to abide by 19 pages’ worth of court-ordered cove...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York auction house Guernsey’s explained on Thursday that all bidders in its planned winner-take-all auction of more than 5,500 artifacts salvaged from the wreckage of the Titanic must agree to abide by 19 pages’ worth of court-ordered covenants and commitments governing the collection. “The court has final approval and the right to make sure the buyer has the capability and the desire,” said Arlan Ettinger, president of Guernsey’s. “It’s like getting a puppy,” he added. “It takes a great deal of care.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Responsible Bidders Sought for Titanic Auction', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Titanic (Ship)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ettinger, Arlan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Guernsey's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Premier Exhibitions Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T20:40:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93d23786-6e9a-5b32-b64d-81ed80a54e29', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93d23786-6e9a-5b32-b64d-81ed80a54e29'}, {'abstract': 'The French equivalent of the Golden Globes makes special mention of Uggie, the canine star of “The Artist.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/writers-art-directors-and-now-uggie/', 'snippet': 'The French equivalent of the Golden Globes makes special mention of Uggie, the canine star of “The Artist.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until someone or Kanye West  tells us otherwise, the Bagger will take this as evidence that blog campaigns and wild Twitter sprees work: The fine folks at Movieline, who started the “Consider Uggie” campaign on behalf of the little dog in “The Artist,” point us to a prize that the Jack Russell terrier has already won. It’s from the French, bien sûr. Last month he earned a special mention in the Prix Lumière Awards, France’s equivalent of the Golden Globes, with “The Artist” picking up four other nominations – best film, best director, best actor and best actress – over all. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Writers, Art Directors and Now Uggie', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Kanye', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Movieline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T20:40:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8df3af95-bcd7-50c2-817e-e79a9ba6ad4b', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8df3af95-bcd7-50c2-817e-e79a9ba6ad4b'}, {'abstract': 'The move comes after two contractors working for the private company, GardaWorld, were detained on suspicion of gun smuggling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/world/asia/afghanistan-shuts-down-gardaworld-a-canadian-security-firm.html', 'snippet': 'The move comes after two contractors working for the private company, GardaWorld, were detained on suspicion of gun smuggling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The Afghan government said Thursday that it was shutting down the operations of one of the largest foreign security companies operating in the country after detaining two of its contractors on suspicion of gun smuggling.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghanistan Closes Firm Providing Security', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghanistan Closes Firm Providing Security', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mercenaries and Private Military Contractors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense Contracts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T20:53:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/623366e0-9375-5dbb-ba18-216474238c43', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/623366e0-9375-5dbb-ba18-216474238c43'}, {'abstract': 'The popular digital music service has only been able to reach a deal with EMI — the others are suing for copyright infringement. But now EMI is suing, too, accusing Grooveshark’s parent company of breach of contract.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/new-lawsuit-means-all-major-labels-are-suing-grooveshark/', 'snippet': 'The popular digital music service has only been able to reach a deal with EMI — the others are suing for copyright infringement. But now EMI is suing, too, accusing Grooveshark’s parent company of breach of contract.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Grooveshark, a popular digital music service that is being sued for copyright infringement by three of the four major record companies, now has problems with the one big label that it has a licensing deal with.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Lawsuit Means All Major Labels Are Suing Grooveshark', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EMI Group PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grooveshark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T20:54:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73caf2e3-d969-510d-b403-7b43416f0f74', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73caf2e3-d969-510d-b403-7b43416f0f74'}, {'abstract': 'A judge rules that the Bloomberg administration is siding with Hasidic Jews in a development plan that would discriminate against blacks and Latinos.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/judge-halts-plans-for-a-development-in-brooklyn/', 'snippet': 'A judge rules that the Bloomberg administration is siding with Hasidic Jews in a development plan that would discriminate against blacks and Latinos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The blighted border of Williamsburg, Bedford-Stuyvesant and Bushwick has been more like the Bermuda Triangle than the Broadway Triangle for developers over the last two decades.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Cites Bias in Halting Brooklyn Development Plan', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Vito J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Broadway Triangle Community Coalition', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ridgewood-Bushwick Senior Citizens Council', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Jewish Organizations of Williamsburg', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bedford-Stuyvesant (NYC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (NYC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T21:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/689df8c6-0fe3-5392-b1ed-0952f272014f', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/689df8c6-0fe3-5392-b1ed-0952f272014f'}, {'abstract': 'A Central Saint Martins graduate teams up with a master craftsman in Jaipur, India, to make candy-colored jewels.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/the-get-alice-cicolini-ring/', 'snippet': 'A Central Saint Martins graduate teams up with a master craftsman in Jaipur, India, to make candy-colored jewels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alice Cicolini, a London-based Central Saint Martins graduate, works with Kamal Meenakar, a master craftsman in Jaipur, India, on her candy-colored jewels. The pieces get their distinct finishes through champlevé, an intricate enameling process (called meenakari in India). “I’m drawn to enamel because it’s like painting on precious metal,” said Cicolini, whose latest creations incorporate exotic shapes and motifs associated with religious architecture found along the ancient Silk Road.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Alice Cicolini Ring', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T21:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/975790e6-cfe8-5eb8-824c-c8f3ad6b6ad5', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/975790e6-cfe8-5eb8-824c-c8f3ad6b6ad5'}, {'abstract': 'In Zakes Mda’s new memoir, his life and hard times are mostly played for wistful comedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/books/sometimes-there-is-a-void-by-zakes-mda-review.html', 'snippet': 'In Zakes Mda’s new memoir, his life and hard times are mostly played for wistful comedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The South African novelist, poet and playwright Zakes Mda has a formidable political lineage. His father, A. P. Mda, was a guiding light in the 1959 founding of the Pan Africanist Congress. He was a lawyer and by all accounts a stern, serious man. Zakes Mda (pronounced EM-dah) is a serious man of a different sort: one who refuses to be somber. In “Sometimes There Is a Void,” his new memoir, his life and hard times are mostly played for wistful comedy.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/arts/06ARTSBOOK/06ARTSBOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/arts/06ARTSBOOK/06ARTSBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/06/arts/06ARTSBOOK/06ARTSBOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Of Women, Politics and Laughs', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Of Women, Politics and Laughs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mda, Zakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T21:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5df7c4cd-c606-5963-bc4b-926d8bd2c559', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5df7c4cd-c606-5963-bc4b-926d8bd2c559'}, {'abstract': "Rick Santorum takes the fight for the nomination to one of Mitt Romney's strongholds, New Hampshire.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000001266313/the-caucus--santorums-in-new-hampshire.html', 'snippet': "Rick Santorum takes the fight for the nomination to one of Mitt Romney's strongholds, New Hampshire.", 'lead_paragraph': "Rick Santorum takes the fight for the nomination to one of Mitt Romney's strongholds, New Hampshire.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/multimedia/video-caucus-120105-zeleny/video-caucus-120105-zeleny-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/05/multimedia/video-caucus-120105-zeleny/video-caucus-120105-zeleny-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/05/multimedia/video-caucus-120105-zeleny/video-caucus-120105-zeleny-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/05/multimedia/video-caucus-120105-zeleny/video-caucus-120105-zeleny-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caucus | Santorum in New Hampshire', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', '