 with travel and all, quite possibly no posting for some time. At the meetings all my stuff will be on Saturday: a joint presentation of my work with Gauti Eggertsson at 8 AM, a meet-and-greet at the Worth booth from 3:30-5, and a presentation of my 33-year-old paper on interstellar trade (kept fresh by time dilation) at Yoram Bauman’s humor in economics session at 8 PM. What will I do with all my free time?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economisting', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T21:13:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e8b47df-f572-55a9-94ce-6a5b686ce07f', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e8b47df-f572-55a9-94ce-6a5b686ce07f'}, {'abstract': 'Ozzie Guillen and Carlos Zambrano have been friends. Now, they’re part of the same team.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/miami-nice-zambrano-joins-guillen/', 'snippet': 'Ozzie Guillen and Carlos Zambrano have been friends. Now, they’re part of the same team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Carlos Zambrano’s lowest moments in the major leagues, Ozzie Guillen has been there. In June 2010, after a dugout fight with a teammate during a game against the White Sox, Zambrano had dinner with Guillen. Last August, after Zambrano packed his belongings and left the Cubs during a game in Atlanta, Guillen’s wife spoke with him and Guillen publicly called Zambrano his friend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Miami Nice: Zambrano Joins Guillen', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_