s', 'value': 'Welch, Florence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cunningham, Merce, Dance Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florence and the Machine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T21:41:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3baaf11-4623-5425-a236-18f4f738827d', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3baaf11-4623-5425-a236-18f4f738827d'}, {'abstract': 'At the Twenty Sided Store in Brooklyn, players dive into role-playing games like Dungeons & Dragons or card games like Magic: The Gathering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/nyregion/at-the-twenty-sided-store-gamers-unleash-their-alter-egos.html', 'snippet': 'At the Twenty Sided Store in Brooklyn, players dive into role-playing games like Dungeons & Dragons or card games like Magic: The Gathering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON a moonless winter night you journey across a perilous landscape of snaking subway trains, howling traffic and steam-hissing sewers. The rattling dice in your pocket guide you like an oracle toward the object of your quest. At last you spy it: the blue-painted crystal glowing in the window of the Twenty Sided Store. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08SUB2JOINT2/08SUB2JOINT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08SUB2JOINT2/0