al': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdd85cf8-2971-56d8-88e7-815690be7d1c', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdd85cf8-2971-56d8-88e7-815690be7d1c'}, {'abstract': 'The Manhattan Chamber Orchestra celebrated its 25th anniversary with a program of duos, trios and quartets at Symphony Space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/arts/music/manhattan-chamber-orchestra-at-symphony-space-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Manhattan Chamber Orchestra celebrated its 25th anniversary with a program of duos, trios and quartets at Symphony Space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Manhattan Chamber Orchestra, when it comes down to it, is really just one musician, the composer, conductor, violinist and violist Richard Auldon Clark, along with however many players he can bring together for the project at hand. In prosperous times it was an actual orchestra, assembled from New York’s rich freelance pool. When finances are tighter — now, for example — it is a chamber group. So if it seemed odd that the orchestra’s 25th-anniversary celebration, at the Leonard Nimoy Thalia at Symphony Space on Wednesday evening, was a program of duos, trios and quartets, think of that as a measure of Mr. Clark’s flexibility. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/arts/06CHAMBERS_SPAN/06CHAMBERS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/06/arts/06CHAMBERS_SPAN/06CHAMBERS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/arts/06CHAMBERS_SPAN/CHAMBERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':