1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ebfcced-161d-5e04-85c3-1adcb5bd7ea0'}, {'abstract': 'When a guest calls and says that the sitter canceled and can she bring her toddler to your adults-only party, what do you say? Almost all commenters agreed on this one.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/05/parental-quandary-considered-should-you-bring-a-child-to-an-adult-party/', 'snippet': 'When a guest calls and says that the sitter canceled and can she bring her toddler to your adults-only party, what do you say? Almost all commenters agreed on this one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every week, the Motherlode Parental Quandary team of experienced, expert parents (that’s all of us — own it!) weighs in\xa0 on a dilemma of an ethical, social or moral nature that could only happen to a fellow parent. We offer fantastic advice, and this week’s advice was unusually universal. Nearly all of us were agreed on what last week’s\xa0 parent should have done — but caught off guard on the phone isn’t the best time to call to mind even the clearest of solutions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parental Quandary Considered: Should You Bring a Child to an Adult Party?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-05T22:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', 