s threatened by encroaching urban development wage a campaign of trickery at construction sites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/movies/pom-poko-directed-by-isao-takahata.html', 'snippet': 'In “Pom Poko” an enclave of raccoonlike creatures threatened by encroaching urban development wage a campaign of trickery at construction sites.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Pom Poko” — one of the final offerings in the welcome Studio Ghibli retrospective at the IFC Center — wasn’t directed by the studio’s master animator, Hayao Miyazaki, but certainly bears his influence. Directed by Mr. Miyazaki’s frequent collaborator Isao Takahata, the film, from 1994, credits Mr. Miyazaki with “planning,” and it’s easy to see: its ecological concerns, nuance and occasional lyricism place it squarely within the Ghibli oeuvre but not among its masterpieces.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/arts/06RDPPOM_SPAN/06RDPPOM_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/06/arts/06RDPPOM_SPAN/06RDPPOM_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/arts/06RDPPOM_SPAN/FILM-ROUNDUP3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 582, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/arts/06RDPPOM_SPAN/06RDPPOM_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/06/arts/06RDPPOM_SPAN/06RDPPOM_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Angry Critters Spearhead an Ecological Battle', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Pom Poko'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Takahata, Isao', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T00:14:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f674aad1-7c4e-569f-9b32-c931c39c8b36', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f674aad1-7c4e-569f-9b32-c931c39c8b36'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Bernard Sanders, the Vermont independent, responds to a news article, “Factory Jobs Gain, but Wages Retreat.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/opinion/from-senator-bernard-sanders-free-trade-vs-jobs.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Bernard Sanders, the Vermont independent, responds to a news article, “Factory Jobs Gain, but Wages Retreat.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Free Trade vs. Jobs', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Free Trade vs. Jobs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}