 House floor, Democrats prevented the start of a scheduled lawmaking session for a second day in a row on Thursday, as pressure over “right to work” legislation mounted in Indianapolis. Republicans say a law prohibiting union contracts at private-sector workplaces from requiring workers to pay union dues or other fees would attract businesses to the state, while Democrats say the measure would weaken unions and harm benefits for workers. Scores of labor union members and supporters chanted “Kill the bill!” outside the State House chamber as Republican leaders twice on Thursday tried to call lawmakers to order only to find that too few Democrats were present; at least seven of them needed to appear to meet a quorum requirement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indiana: Absent Democrats Hold Up House Session', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indiana: Absent Democrats Hold Up House Session', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T01:34:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brie