nia would be forced to impose severe cuts in public schools that could reduce the school year by three weeks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Californians Are Asked for $6.9 Billion in New Taxes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Californians Asked for $6.9 Billion in New Taxes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T01:48:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fe508e2-f31b-5706-b856-469a744a0ab4', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fe508e2-f31b-5706-b856-469a744a0ab4'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s suggestion that he draws inspiration from the country’s founders while President Obama seeks a “European-style welfare state,” among other things, carries risks from Democrats and Republicans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/us/politics/romney-facing-risks-left-and-right.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s suggestion that he draws inspiration from the country’s founders while President Obama seeks a “European-style welfare state,” among other things, carries risks from Democrats and Republicans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — On the campaign trail, Mitt Romney casts himself as the guardian of American opportunity, who would stop President Obama’s attempt “to replace our merit-based society with an entitlement society.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Facing Risks Left and Right', 'kicker': 'Political Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney Facing Risks Left and Right', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T01:49:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0327653a-f836-5be7-90c6-95fcba8c8d46', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0327653a-f836-5be7-90c6-95fcba8c8d46'}, {'abstract': 'The second session of Congress will likely include a lawsuit over recent appointments by President Obama, as well as Senate Republicans turning minor procedures into major headaches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/us/politics/recent-fights-in-congress-could-be-just-warm-ups.html', 'snippet': 'The second session of Congress will likely include a lawsuit over recent appointments by President Obama, as well as Senate Republicans turning minor procedures into major headaches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Remember the first session of the 112th Congress, how things were rancorous, partisan and at times somewhat apocalyptic? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recent Fights in Congress Could Be Just Warm-Ups', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recent Fights in Congress Could Be Just Warm-Ups', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T01:50:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e99c2a4-9ad7-5d0f-a937-da48b4654cd0', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e99c2a4-9ad7-5d0f-a937-da48b4654cd0'}, {'abstract': 'As technology has enlarged the size of video boards in stadiums, players have learned to use them as a rearview mirror to locate their opponents on the field.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/sports/football/stadium-video-screens-offer.html', 'snippet': 'As technology has enlarged the size of video boards in stadiums, players have learned to use them as a rearview mirror to locate their opponents on the field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has been constant advancement in football equipment over the years, from lighter shoulder pads to safer helmets. Shoes can be custom-designed to fit a player’s cleat preference. Undergarments wick away sweat while still keeping the player warm. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/sports/giants/giants-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/06/sports/giants/giants-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/sports/giants/giants-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/sports/giants/giants-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/06/sports/giants/giants-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stadium Video Screens Offer Football Players a Live Advantage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Wait To Watch the Replay?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Victor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MetLife Stadium (NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T01:51:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fee6a00-2593-56cb-8aa6-b410ec9c768d', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fee6a00-2593-56cb-8aa6-b410ec9c768d'}, {'abstract': 'In Mexico and Latin America, old migratory patterns are changing as migrants move to a wider range of cities and countries, creating regional challenges and opportunities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/world/americas/migrants-new-paths-reshaping-latin-america.html', 'snippet': 'In Mexico and Latin America, old migratory patterns are changing as migrants move to a wider range of cities and countries, creating regional challenges and opportunities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTA MARÍA ATZOMPA, Mexico — When the old-timers here look around their town, all they see are new arrivals: young Mexican men working construction and driving down wages; the children of laborers flooding crowded schools; even new businesses — stores, restaurants and strip clubs — springing up on roads that used to be dark and quiet.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/world/Mexico/Mexico-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'i