child to attend to. So she was in a hurry. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holding a Spot for Stigma in the City’s Food Stamp Lines', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Holding a Spot for Stigma In the City’s Food Stamp Lines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Identification Devices', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fingerprinting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T02:33:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd368277-07f9-5dbf-98ad-006245877df7', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd368277-07f9-5dbf-98ad-006245877df7'}, {'abstract': 'On the remote Makah reservation, visitors can experience an area’s stormy euphoria and gloom — and still catch the ferry home for dinner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/us/washington-outpost-draws-those-seeking-slap-of-sea-spray.html', 'snippet': 'On the remote Makah reservation, visitors can experience an area’s stormy euphoria and gloom — and still catch the ferry home for dinner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MAKAH INDIAN RESERVATION, Wash. — There are more remote outposts in America than this one. There are places where the wind can be more brutal, the rain more relentless and the sea, maybe, mightie