 and the lapse of nearly two decades in bringing any of the white teenagers involved to justice, caused outrage across Britain. Judge Colman Treacey, who sentenced the two men on Wednesday to 15 and 14 years in prison, said that he was barred from imposing harsher sentences because the killers were juveniles at the time of the attack, and because tougher sentencing guidelines for racially aggravated crimes were introduced after the killing. The attorney general, Dominic Grieve, said he would consider whether the terms were “too lenient” and whether to appeal them.\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: Government Will Review Murder Sentences', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawrence, Stephen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T05:22:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6736e692-0009-5a84-86f2-599878435499', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6736e692-0009-5a84-86f2-599878435499'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Duell’s understated comic flare enlivened Broadway shows (“A Funny Thing Happened on the Way to the Forum”), television series (“Police Squad!) and Hollywood films (One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/theater/william-duell-puckish-character-actor-dies-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Duell’s understated comic flare enlivened Broadway shows (“A Funny Thing Happened on the Way to the Forum”), television series (“Police Squad!) and Hollywood films (One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest).', 'lead_paragraph': 'William Duell, a diminutive character actor whose puckishness and understated comic flair enlivened Broadway shows, television series and Hollywood films, died at his home in Manhattan on Dec. 22. He was 88.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/arts/DUELL-obit/DUELL-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/arts/DUELL-obit/DUELL-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/arts/DUELL-obit/DUELL-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'William Duell, Puckish Character Actor, Dies at 88', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'William Duell, 88, an Actor Who Played Quirky Roles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T05:27:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_mate