football master who made people miserable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A links roundup this morning in which people don’t have much nice to say:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Criticism of Mark Sanchez and Bill Polian', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polian, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T11:25:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a662c926-bcb0-5211-bd9f-b7b0af28beca', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a662c926-bcb0-5211-bd9f-b7b0af28beca'}, {'abstract': 'A report of a possible miscount in one precinct during the Iowa caucuses has underscored the close race, and that anomalies are common during vote counting.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/winner-of-iowa-caucus-still-in-doubt/', 'snippet': 'A report of a possible miscount in one precinct during the Iowa caucuses has underscored the close race, and that anomalies are common during vote counting.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:46 p.m. | Updated At just before 2 a.m. on Wednesday, Matt Strawn, the Iowa Republican Party chairman, addressed reporters who had spent the night following the historically close Republican caucus race between Mitt Romney and Rick Santorum. The margin separating the candidates was small — eight votes — but he was prepared to declare a victor. “Congratulations to Governor Mitt Romney, the winner of the 2012 Iowa caucuses,” Mr. Strawn said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iowan Casts Doubt on Winner of Caucus', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T11:37:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/884dd2e9-e3d3-584e-8d69-f462c8a6822d', 'word_count': 1445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/884dd2e9-e3d3-584e-8d69-f462c8a6822d'}, {'abstract': 'An attack killed 26 people and underlined the confusion and complexity growing amid Syria’s protests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/world/middleeast/bomb-attack-in-syrian-capital-kills-25.html', 'snippet': 'An attack killed 26 people and underlined the confusion and complexity growing amid Syria’s protests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — A bomb tore through a crowded neighborhood in Damascus on Friday, killing 26 people and wounding dozens more, unleashing scenes of chaos and underlining the growing confusion and complexity of the Syrian uprising, officials and residents said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/world/07syria2-span/07syria2-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/07/world/07syria2-span/07syria2-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/world/07syria2-span/07syria2-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/world/07syria2-span/07syria2-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/world/07syria2-span/07syria2-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bomb Kills Dozens in Damascus, Stoking Suspicions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bomb Kills 26 in Damascus, and Each Side in Uprising Has a Theory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Damascus (Syria)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T11:43:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Shadid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shadid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/381db039-ff39-5455-aa80-cb8fbb9afdc8', 'word_count': 1256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/381db039-ff39-5455-aa80-cb8fbb9af