r': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T13:38:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shaila Dewan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shaila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dewan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69aa6fe1-39eb-52c9-ada8-4f76e7c5d37e', 'word_count': 1305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69aa6fe1-39eb-52c9-ada8-4f76e7c5d37e'}, {'abstract': 'Good teachers have a lasting impact beyond classroom, G.M. to reinforce Volt batteries, the new consumer chief promises a strong agenda and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/friday-reading-good-teachers-have-big-impact-beyond-classroom/', 'snippet': 'Good teachers have a lasting impact beyond classroom, G.M. to reinforce Volt batteries, the new consumer chief promises a strong agenda and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Friday Reading: Good Teachers Have Big Impact Beyond Classroom', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T13:39:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81849868-dfc8-5952-99d0-fd73a5d36b6c', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81849868-dfc8-5952-99d0-fd73a5d36b6c'}, {'abstract': 'Fill in the blanks in several paragraphs frm this article from the Science section, “Booking a Flight to Space, With Travel Insurance.” Use your own words and phrases, or schoose from a scrambled list of the words or phrases that were removed.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/fill-in-space-tourism/', 'snippet': 'Fill in the blanks in several paragraphs frm this article from the Science section, “Booking a Flight to Space, With Travel Insurance.” Use your own words and phrases, or schoose from a scrambled list of the words or phrases that were removed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Directions: Fill in the blanks in several paragraphs in this article from the Science section, “Booking a Flight to Space, With Travel Insurance.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fill-In | Space Tourism', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T13:49:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a60eb531-f6ea-5af0-ba47-8e2c61020deb', 'word_count': 693, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a60eb531-f6ea-5af0-ba47-8e2c61020deb'}, {'abstract': 'Also, do more attractive members of Congress get more press attention? And are there attractive members of Congress?', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/the-breakfast-meeting-spin-off-the-nook-to-save-it-abfab-and-van-halen-return/', 'snippet': 'Also, do more attractive members of Congress get more press attention? And are there attractive members of Congress?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Nook, the Barnes & Noble e-reader, has sold well and drawn praise from reviewers, but has yet to make a profit. It is a tricky situation, with investors anxious about the future costs tied to the product and the company convinced that investments of as much $200 million to $250 million a year will pay dividends, DealBook reports. The company is considering a way out by spinning off the Nook division.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Spin Off the Nook to Save It? Ab/Fab and Van Halen Return', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, David Lee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barnes & Noble Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Book Search', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Van Halen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'xkcd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T13:56:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/375d2ad6-6bf8-536e-9a98-b25e9f7a8322', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/375d2ad6-6bf8-536e-9a98-b25e9f7a8322'}, {'abstract': 'The star of “A Gifted Man” talks about his skin-care regimen, why he shaves at night, and how much makeup he likes his actress wife to wear.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/face-time-patrick-wilson/', 'snippet': 'The star of “A Gifted Man” talks about his skin-care regimen, why he shaves at night, and how much makeup he likes his actress wife to wear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I reached Patrick Wilson by phone as he was on his way to the set of his CBS series “A Gifted Man,” in which he appears as Dr. Michael Holt. Wilson is on camera a great deal, with a lot of close-ups, and of course the series is filmed in high definition\xa0— so he and his makeup artist, Anita Gibson, pay close attention to his skincare regimen (especially since he has to shave daily). I got the whole grooming scoop for you gentlemen. And ladies, I think you’ll find something of interest here, too!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Face Time | Patrick Wilson', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T14:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Turnbow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c3b91cf-a4a3-5618-8441-b870ccf4ffb3', 'word_count': 1146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c3b91cf-a4a3-5618-8441-b870ccf4ffb3'}, {'abstract': 'The anti-corruption crusader at a crossroads.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/anna-hazares-team-seeks-your-advice/', 'snippet': 'The anti-corruption crusader at a crossroads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the dust fades after Parliament’s heated debate over the anti-corruption Lokpal Bill many are examining what, exactly, the anti-corruption activist Anna Hazare contributed to India’s political landscape. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anna Hazare’s Team Seeks Your Advice', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'conte