t atmospheric aerosols over the eastern United States would increase ground temperatures.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/rethinking-the-effects-of-aerosols/', 'snippet': 'A study projects that the elimination of direct atmospheric aerosols over the eastern United States would increase ground temperatures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you hear the word aerosol, a can of hairspray, spray paint or whipped cream may come to mind. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rethinking the Effects of Aerosols', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T14:45:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna M. Foster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58f176ac-4beb-5921-9cd7-a36a56d3e4dd', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58f176ac-4beb-5921-9cd7-a36a56d3e4dd'}, {'abstract': 'Timothy M. Dolan, the ebullient leader of the archdiocese of New York, has a high goal: restoring the scandal-ravaged image of the Roman Catholic Church in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/nyregion/timothy-dolan-new-yorks-next-cardinal.html', 'snippet': 'Timothy M. Dolan, the ebullient leader of the archdiocese of New York, has a high goal: restoring the scandal-ravaged image of the Roman Catholic Church in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT is not a good time for the Roman Catholic Church in America, but Archbishop Timothy M. Dolan, the cardinal-designate of New York, has made it his mission to remind people that there is more to the church than scandal. Taping his weekly radio show last month, he praised the beauty of a recent church service in Yonkers and recounted an emotional visit to the solitary confinement wing at Rikers Island.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08SUBDOLAN1/08SUBDOLAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08SUBDOLAN1/08SUBDOLAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08SUBDOLAN1/08SUBDOLAN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 789, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08SUBDOLAN1/08SUBDOLAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08SUBDOLAN1/08SUBDOLAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Next Cardinal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s Next Cardinal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cardinals (Roman Catholic Prelates)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolan, Timothy M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T14:47:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a9dc77a-3cec-5341-b870-ca90160e883a', 'word_count': 1714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a9dc77a-3cec-5341-b870-ca90160e883a'}, {'abstract': 'C. S. Lewis nominated Tolkien, the “Hobbit” and “Lord of the Rings” author, in 1961, but the jury said of his work that “the result has not in any way measured up to storytelling of the highest quality,” according to papers in the Nobel archive in Stockholm.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/tolkien-snubbed-by-nobel-prize-jury-papers-reveal/', 'snippet': 'C. S. Lewis nominated Tolkien, the “Hobbit” and “Lord of the Rings” author, in 1961, but the jury said of his work that “the result has not in any way measured up to storytelling of the highest quality,” according to papers in the Nobel archive in...', 'lead_paragraph': 'J. R. R. Tolkien may have been the creator of one of the most popular fantasy series of the modern era, but nearly 40 years after his death the author of “The Hobbit” and “The Lord of the Rings” is still receiving some of the toughest reviews of his career. Tolkien’s latest detractor, according to a report in a Swedish newspaper, is the jury for the 1961 Nobel Prize in literature, which dismissed him as a candidate for the honor, saying Tolkien wasn’t up to snuff. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tolkien Snubbed by Nobel Prize Jury, Papers Reveal', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '