n the Strait of Hormuz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Under growing pressure from the United States, some of Asia’s largest economies are reluctantly looking for options to reduce the amount of oil they buy from Iran, a move that would further tighten the economic vise on an increasingly defiant nation that announced plans for a new round of naval drills in the Strait of Hormuz.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pressed by U.S., Asian Countries Look for Ways to Reduce Purchases of Iranian Oil', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pressed by U.S., Asian Countries Look for Ways to Reduce Purchases of Iranian Oil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Strait of Hormuz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T15:23:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher and Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03ce0c5b-3bb5-56d4-8557-627895e7e161', 'word_count': 1333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03ce0c5b-3bb5-56d4-8557-627895e7e161'}, {'abstract': 'The blood-covered girl, with puncture wounds to her neck and face, was found cradled in her babbling mother’s arms in an apartment in Bedford-Stuyvesant before dawn on Friday. The girl’s mother is in custody.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/brooklyn-girl-3-found-fatally-wounded-in-apartment/', 'snippet': 'The blood-covered girl, with puncture wounds to her neck and face, was found cradled in her babbling mother’s arms in an apartment in Bedford-Stuyvesant before dawn on Friday. The girl’s mother is in custody.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:21 p.m. | Updated  Officers responding early Friday to a call of a jumper on the roof of a four-story building in Brooklyn found a blood trail leading down to Apartment 4A. The door was ajar, and when they walked in, the police said, the picture got even worse: A young mother was sitting on a couch in the living room, babbling and cradling her fatally wounded 2-year-old girl.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mother in Custody After Death of Girl, 2, in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bedford-Stuyvesant (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T15:24:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker and Tim Stelloh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 