, 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d1b0bbd-a48a-5116-8037-06c2242264b9', 'word_count': 1193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d1b0bbd-a48a-5116-8037-06c2242264b9'}, {'abstract': 'What happens when a factory shuts down. A documentary play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/magazine/end-of-the-line.html', 'snippet': 'What happens when a factory shuts down. A documentary play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2008, General Motors announced the closing of its metal-stamping plant in Wyoming, Mich., and 1,500 workers lost their jobs. Austin Bunn, a playwright and professor, chronicled the experience and what came after in a nonfiction play. Bunn, in collaboration with the Working Group Theater, spent two years trying to understand exactly what happened to the people and the town that relied on the factory. He recorded hundreds of hours of conversations with dozens of workers, managers, historians, bartenders, city consultants and others. Their words (edited and condensed for dramatic purposes) became the documentary play “Rust,” adapted here. (Some characters have had their names changed; one is a composite.) “Rust” had its premiere in Grand Rapids, Mich., in September.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/magazine/08gm_chameleon-slide-YBC1/08gm_chameleon-slide-YBC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 476, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/magazine/08gm_chameleon-slide-YBC1/08gm_chameleon-slide-YBC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 476}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/magazine/08gm_chameleon-slide-YBC1/08gm_chameleon-slide-YBC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 813, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/magazine/08gm_chameleon-slide-YBC1/08gm_chameleon-slide-YBC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/magazine/08gm_chameleon-slide-YBC1/08gm_chameleon-slide-YBC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'End of the Line', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'End of the Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T16:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Bunn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bunn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ce8fb54-a5f6-552e-a7a3-d8602fa8c09f', 'word_count': 3030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ce8fb54-a5f6-552e-a7a3-d8602fa8c09f'}, {'abstract': 'An Asian-American veteran warns about the dangers of hazing in the armed services.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/an-asian-american-veteran-reflects-on-when-discipline-becomes-hazing/', 'snippet': 'An Asian-American veteran warns about the dangers of hazing in the armed services.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The deaths of Army Private Danny Chen and Marine Lance Corporal Harry Lew have sent shock waves through Asian-American communities. Eight U.S. Army service members have been charged with hazing-related crimes against Private Chen, a Chinese-American soldier and, like me, the son of Chinese immigrants. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Asian-American Veteran Reflects on When Discipline Becomes Hazing', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, Danny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shinseki, Eric K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T16:03:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Hsia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hsia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2bb21cf-e673-56f1-994f-50377f2d6a26', 'word_count': 1061, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2bb21cf-e673-56f1-994f-50377f2d6a26'}, {'abstract': 'A branch of an Australian coffee roaster and retailer, Toby’s Estate, will open on Monday in Williamsburg, Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/tobys-estate-bringing-more-coffee-to-williamsburg/', 'snippet': 'A branch of an Australian coffee roaster and retailer, Toby’s Estate, will open on Monday in Williamsburg, Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the last few years, the coffee scene in New York City has been something of a land rush, with some notable out-of-town companies setting up shop and teaching us a thing or two about how to roast, brew and correctly steam milk for a cappuccino. Some of them opened coffee shops (La Colombe Torrefaction, of Philadelphia; Gimme! Coffee, of Ithaca, N.Y.). Some opened training labs (Counter Culture Coffee, of Durham, N.C.; Intelligentsia Coffee and Tea, of Chicago), and some opened roasting facilities and coffee bars (Blue Bottle Coffee, of San Francisco and Oakland, Calif.; Stumptown Coffee Roasters, of Portland, Ore.). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toby’s Estate Bringing More Coffee to Williamsburg', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffeehouses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T16:10:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Strand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3018a856-4b0a-57e7-8a42-fbede8fe4c21', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3018a856-4b0a-57e7-8a42-fbede8fe4c21'}, {'abstract': 'The Red Bulls and Arsenal on Friday completed details on a loan deal in which Thierry Henry will return to the north London club through mid-February.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/arsenal-and-red-bulls-complete-henry-loan-deal/', 'snippet': 'The Red Bulls and Arsenal on Friday completed details on a loan deal in which Thierry Henry will return to the north London club through mid-February.', 'le