di Division of Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bug Labs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler Group LLC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mercedes-Benz', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Porsche AG', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T16:20:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/713509b7-046c-58cc-ac7c-800ac4c5c1e4', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/713509b7-046c-58cc-ac7c-800ac4c5c1e4'}, {'abstract': 'The Vatican’s formation of an ordinariate for Episcopal priests who want to move to Catholicism will add to the small number of married priests in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/us/married-roman-catholic-priests-are-testing-a-tradition.html', 'snippet': 'The Vatican’s formation of an ordinariate for Episcopal priests who want to move to Catholicism will add to the small number of married priests in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On New Year’s Day, the Vatican announced the formation of a nationwide ordinariate — kind of a diocese without borders — for Episcopal priests and their congregations who want to move together into Roman Catholicism. The big news is not that some Episcopalians will have a zippier express lane into Catholicism, but that there will soon be even more married Catholic priests in America. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/nyregion/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/07/nyregion/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/nyregion/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/nyregion/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/nyregion/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cohort of Married Roman Catholic Priests, and More Are on the Way', 'kicker': 'Beliefs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cohort of Married Roman Catholic Priests, and More Are on the Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celibacy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Episcopal Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T16:22:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Oppenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oppenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97225135-da85-59ed-be0c-ec5c0116c43b', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97225135-da85-59ed-be0c-ec5c0116c43b'}, {'abstract': 'Mia, age 7, wears only boys’ clothes, but Grandma sends pink, frills and fluff.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/parental-quandary-grandma-gives-girly-gifts-to-a-tomboy/', 'snippet': 'Mia, age 7, wears only boys’ clothes, but Grandma sends pink, frills and fluff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Grandparents, and in particular the grandparents on the “in-law” side, can provide a nearly endless series of quandaries for some parents. The lucky ones among us have two charming sets who support us in all things parental and offer our children the best grandparenting going. Most of us (among those fortunate enough to have our parents around at all) would name at least one or two areas where we’re not quite sure how to navigate all these familial relationships. Gretchen (her name, and her daughter’s, have been changed) falls into that category.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parental Quandary: Grandma Gives Girly Gifts to a Tomboy', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T16:25:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7bc75a0-23e2-56ba-b1ff-22a69a9efb68', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7bc75a0-23e2-56ba-b1ff-22a69a9efb68'}, {'abstract': 'A new book catalogs L.L. Bean’s influential output, including duck boots, chamois shirts, field coats and Wicked Good Slippers.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/bookshelf-100-years-of-l-l-bean/', 'snippet': 'A new book catalogs L.L. Bean’s influential output, including duck boots, chamois shirts, field coats and Wicked Good Slippers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bookshelf | 100 Years of L.L. Bean', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T16:35:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3deb57fa-6b91-510f-8b71-ffc22497eb66', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3deb57fa-6b91-510f-8b71-ffc22497eb66'}, {'abstract': 'People in Australia and New Zealand consume more marijuana and amphetamines than anyone else in the world, research in The Lancet has concluded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/world/asia/marijuana-use-most-rampant-in-australia-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'People in Australia and New Zealand consume more marijuana and amphetamines than anyone else in the world, research in The Lancet has concluded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SYDNEY — A study published Friday in a British medical journal may have finally uncovered the secret behind Australia’s laid-back lifestyle, and it turns out to be more than just sun and surf: The denizens Down Under, it turns out, consume more marijuana than any other people on the planet.', 'sour