e': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10e856b9-01ca-5941-9e75-5bb866ab775a', 'word_count': 1150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10e856b9-01ca-5941-9e75-5bb866ab775a'}, {'abstract': 'In a video that had been posted to YouTube, Charles Barkley called his new gig as a spokesperson for Weight Watchers a scam, and had some harsh words for the Hawks.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/charles-barkley-live-and-uncensored-sort-of/', 'snippet': 'In a video that had been posted to YouTube, Charles Barkley called his new gig as a spokesperson for Weight Watchers a scam, and had some harsh words for the Hawks.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:58 p.m. | Updated Ah, Charles Barkley. In a video posted to YouTube that captured him chatting with the other TNT announcers during a commercial break of Thursday’s game between the Miami Heat and the Atlanta Hawks, Barkley called his new gig as a spokesperson for Weight Watchers a scam, and had some harsh words for the Hawks. It is definitely worth a watch. (Or, it was worth a watch until the video was pulled down due to a copyright claim by the N.B.A. )', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charles Barkley: Live and Uncensored, Sort of', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barkley, Charles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Hawks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T17:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Brustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f043a9e2-5707-54c5-b61d-9c82749db21c', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f043a9e2-5707-54c5-b61d-9c82749db21c'}, {'abstract': 'London, Havana, Lhasa and, yes, even the final frontier. A year’s worth of reasons to pack your bags and take off.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/travel/45-places-to-go-in-2012.html', 'snippet': 'London, Havana, Lhasa and, yes, even the final frontier. A year’s worth of reasons to pack your bags and take off.', 'lead_paragraph': '1. PanamaGo for the canal. Stay for everything else. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08COVER_SPAN/08COVER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08COVER_SPAN/08COVER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08COVER_SPAN/Cover-Big-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08COVER_SPAN/08COVER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08COVER_SPAN/08COVER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The 45 Places to Go in 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The 45 Places to Go in 2012', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T17:03:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By NEW YORK TIMES', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b693902a-c3d8-5404-9327-7dc9d8bb1d8d', 'word_count': 8675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b693902a-c3d8-5404-9327-7dc9d8bb1d8d'}, {'abstract': 'Start with China and India — and not just the cities — writes The New York Times columnist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/travel/where-to-go-to-understand-the-world-in-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Start with China and India — and not just the cities — writes The New York Times columnist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you want to understand the world, you need to understand Asia. That, in turn, means setting foot in China and India.Together, those two countries account for one-third of humanity and much of the world’s recent economic growth. They reflect two of our richest civilizations, two broad religious traditions and a vast share of the world’s artistic heritage — and its future.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS3_SPAN/Spread-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS3_SPAN/Spread-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS3_SPAN/Spread-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS3_SPAN/Spread-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS3_SPAN/Spread-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where to Go to Understand the World in 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Let Passions Lead The Way: ... Understand the World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T17:03:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f90d81a7-b51f-56c7-9e2b-126f49b58fab', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f90d81a7-b51f-56c7-9e2b-126f49b58fab'}, {'abstract': 'The curator of the Harlem Studio Museum has high hopes for biennials from Dakar to Morocco.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/travel/where-to-go-to-see-art-in-2012.html', 'snippet': 'The curator of the Harlem Studio Museum has high hopes for biennials from Dakar to Morocco.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I find that art is a great starting point for exploring the world. Of course, my own travel is often determined by art exhibitions and projects. I love L.A., and I’ve been thrilled by the international attention to “ Pacific Standard Time,”  a huge, multi-institution exhibition showing art of California in the most inspiring and groundbreaking way. From the L.A. County Museum of Art to the Hammer Museum to the California African American Museum and many, many more, “Pacific Standard Time” is a whole new way to experience a vast range of significant art and artists and a great moment for the city.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS1_SPAN/Spread-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS1_SPAN/Spread-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS1_SPAN/Spread-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS1_SPAN/Spread-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS1_SPAN/Spread-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where to Go to See Art in 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Let Passions Lead The Way: ... See Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Studio Museum in Harlem', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T17:03:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thelma Golden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thelma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Golden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/118cba56-146b-5b43-abe8-33542eacd1b5', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/118cba56-146b-5b43-abe8-33542eacd1b5'}, {'abstract': 'Saris in India, sweaters in Peru and vintage in Los Angeles. The designer shares her shopping secrets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/travel/where-to-go-to-shop-in-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Saris in India, sweaters in Peru and vintage in Los Angeles. The designer shares her shopping secrets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have been buying vintage clothing for textiles and inspiration since I was 10 years old, so anywhere I go I try to find a thrift shop or vintage shop. I just love it. I remember filming a movie as the costume designer in 1995 in Pennsylvania and drove from Pittsburgh to Niagara Falls just to find vintage trinkets!', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS7-SPAN/08PASSIONS7-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS7-SPAN/08PASSIONS7-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS7-SPAN/Spread-4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS7-SPAN/08PASSIONS7-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS7-SPAN/08PASSIONS7-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where to Go to Shop in 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Let Passions Lead The Way: ...Hunt for Treasure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T17:04:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': "By L'Wren Scott", 'person': [{'firstname': "L'wren", 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b71f7fc-d07c-5ee0-9343-b549e0787ebc', 'word_count': 414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b71f7fc-d07c-5ee0-9343-b549e0787ebc'}, {'abstract': 'The chief executive of RCA Records suggests stops in Brooklyn, Paris, London and Jamaica.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/travel/where-to-go-to-hear-music-in-2012.html', 'snippet': 'The chief executive of RCA Records suggests stops in Brooklyn, Paris, London and Jamaica.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve traveled all over the world — Europe, Africa, South America, Asia — and music is everywhere. People are full of music in Cairo, and music is on every street corner and temple in India.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS9_SPAN/08PASSIONS9_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS9_SPAN/08PASSIONS9_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS9_SPAN/Spread-5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS9_SPAN/08PASSIONS9_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS9_SPAN/08PASSIONS9_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where to Go to Hear Music in 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Let Passions Lead The Way: ...Hear Music', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T17:04:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Edge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d84dbd0-1de3-5cfd-9a0b-eae1f0c0beaf', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d84dbd0-1de3-5cfd-9a0b-eae1f0c0beaf'}, {'abstract': 'Best sushi? Japan. Favorite Manhattan restaurant? Head to the East Village, writes the owner and chef of the Momofuku Restaurant Group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/travel/where-to-go-to-eat-in-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Best sushi? Japan. Favorite Manhattan restaurant? Head to the East Village, writes the owner and chef of the Momofuku Restaurant Group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve eaten sushi around the world, and the best in Tokyo is at Sushi Sawada. In the kitchen, it’s just the chef, Koji Sawada, and his wife. And there’s nothing there except charcoal and a box of rice. As old-school as you can get. I found it to be a breath of fresh air.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS5_SPAN/08PASSION5_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS5_SPAN/08PASSION5_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS5_SPAN/Spread-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS5_SPAN/08PASSION5_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/travel/08PASSIONS5_SPAN/08PASSION5_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where to Go to Eat in 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Let Passions Lead The Way: ... Eat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T17:04:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f458c583-ab05-5af8-8e6d-f895a69fc32a', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f458c583-ab05-5af8-8e6d-f895a69fc32a'}, {'abstract': 'Henry Alford explains how — and why — to behave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/books/review/would-it-kill-you-to-stop-doing-that-a-modern-guide-to-manners-by-henry-alford-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'Henry Alford explains how — and why — to behave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Henry Alford’s breezy guide to manners begins promisingly with a fact-finding trip to Japan, “the Fort Knox of the World Manners Reserve.” He hires a Japanese etiquette coach and learns that it’s rude to point with your fingers or sneeze in public. Alford wisely wastes no time trying to see the logic of Japanese dos and don’ts, which often make no more sense than our own. We don’t have to know why it’s rude not to slurp your noodles in Tokyo. Why is beside the point. Wherever we’re strangers, even if it’s in Morocco in Cell Block 6, all we need are the rules — the etiquette manual. “Manners,” Alford explains, “are principles, and etiquette is the specific acts of these principles.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/books/review/08WILLET/08WILLET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/books/review/08WILLET/08WILLET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/books/review/08WILLET/08WILLET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Henry Alford on How to Behave', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Manners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alford, Henry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T17:04:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jincy Willett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jincy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b82e25f-cbcd-50e2-9dc6-b956bd0edf42', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b82e25f-cbcd-50e2-9dc6-b956bd0edf42'}, {'abstract': 'Hackers have stolen some of the programming code for two of Symantec’s antivirus products for businesses, but the company said the products involved — which were Symantec Endpoint Protection 11.0 and Symantec Antivirus 10.2 — were four and five years old.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/symantec-confirms-segment-of-source-code-stolen/', 'snippet': 'Hackers have stolen some of the programming code for two of Symantec’s antivirus products for businesses, but the company said the products involved — which were Symantec Endpoint Protection 11.0 and Symantec Antivirus 10.2 — were four and five ye...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hackers have stolen some of the programming code for two of Symantec’s antivirus products for businesses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/blogs/bitpix-symantec-monitors1/bitpix-symantec-monitors1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1022, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/11/blogs/bitpix-symantec-monitors1/bitpix-syman