-s-military-rescues-iranians-captured-by-pirates/', 'snippet': 'Thirteen Iranians whose fishing vessel had been seized by pirates in November were rescued by the United States Navy in the North Arabian Sea, the Pentagon announced on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 6:33 p.m. In the middle of a tense standoff between Iran and the United States, the crew of an American destroyer patrolling the North Arabian Sea rescued 13 Iranian fishermen who had been taken hostage by Somali pirates more than a month ago, the Pentagon announced on Friday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Navy Rescues Iranians Held by Pirates', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARABIAN SEA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Persian Gulf', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Strait of Hormuz', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey and J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb48e309-6658-5704-ae11-8a001e8d47f0', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb48e309-6658-5704-ae11-8a001e8d47f0'}, {'abstract': 'Microsoft Word is full of keyboard shortcuts to help speed things along as you work. Although the Web has plenty of pages listing the shortcuts, you can also generate your own chart right from the Word program itself.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/tip-of-the-week-make-your-own-shortcuts-in-word/', 'snippet': 'Microsoft Word is full of keyboard shortcuts to help speed things along as you work. Although the Web has plenty of pages listing the shortcuts, you can also generate your own chart right from the Word program itself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Microsoft Word, for both Windows and Mac OS X systems, is full of keyboard shortcuts to help speed things along as you work. Although the Web has plenty of pages listing the shortcuts (like Microsoft’s own collection for Word 2010), you can also generate your own chart right from the Word program itself — which can be handy if you want to print it or edit the list to add your own custom key commands. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Make Your Own Shortcuts in Word', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:02:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e9cb85a-13c6-5124-982c-8db7d39f5f94', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e9cb85a-13c6-5124-982c-8db7d39f5f94'}, {'abstract': 'Compendiums of “The Walking Dead” continue their strong performance on the graphic books best-seller lists.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/graphic-books-best-sellers-zombies-continue-their-reign/', 'snippet': 'Compendiums of “The Walking Dead” continue their strong performance on the graphic books best-seller lists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has become old hat to see “The Walking Dead,” the series about human survivors in a world overrun by zombies, on our best-seller lists. This week, two more collected editions join the lists. On the hardcover list, the second omnibus of the series, which reprints issues 24 through 48 of the series, written by Robert Kirkman and illustrated by Charlie Adlard, arrives at No. 4. On the paperback list, vol. 15, which reprints issues 85 through 90, lands at the top spot. It’s in good company, with a compendium edition including the first 48 issues at No. 2, and vol. 1, which contains the first six issues, at No. 9.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: Zombies Continue Their Reign', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graphic Novels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirkman, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:02:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e80f0894-705e-5cb3-83c5-7cf7c4b3d2b2', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e80f0894-705e-5cb3-83c5-7cf7c4b3d2b2'}, {'abstract': 'In this past week’s Ethicist column, a reader explained her decision to boycott a production of “The Nutcracker” because of her political differences with one of its sponsors, David Koch.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/baffling-reader-correspondence-of-the-week/', 'snippet': 'In this past week’s Ethicist column, a reader explained her decision to boycott a production of “The Nutcracker” because of her political differences with one of its sponsors, David Koch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this past week’s Ethicist column, Edith Palmer of Brooklyn explained why her political differences with David Koch kept her from taking her granddaughter, Rachel, to see a production of “The Nutcracker” that he sponsored. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baffling Reader Correspondence of the Week', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:05:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5640506-b4b5-58db-b065-fa033d0b76c5', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5640506-b4b5-58db-b065-fa033d0b76c5'}, {'abstract': 'A bomb kills at least 25 people in a Damascus neighborhood | The United States adds 200,000 new jobs in December.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000001268226/timescast--january-6-2012.html', 'snippet': 'A bomb kills at least 25 people in a Damascus neighborhood | The United States adds 200,000 new jobs in December.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A bomb kills at least 25 people in a Damascus neighborhood | The United States adds 200,000 new jobs in December.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/multimedia/video-tc-120106/video-tc-120106-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/06/multimedia/video-tc-120106/video-tc-120106-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/multimedia/video-tc-120106/video-tc-120106-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/06/multimedia/video-tc-120106/video-tc-120106-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | January 6, 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat and Shayla Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Shayla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/893d96a5-0dad-54ce-b016-dc9e3827c245', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/893d96a5-0dad-54ce-b016-dc9e3827c245'}, {'abstract': 'On a cold day, with little room to cook, vegetable risotto is easy, bright and satisfying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/dining/versatile-risotto-made-with-winter-vegetables-city-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'On a cold day, with little room to cook, vegetable risotto is easy, bright and satisfying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A RECENT ski trip with friends allowed me to transport the City Kitchen philosophy to the slopes. Our little group gets together annually to enjoy the invigorating and rejuvenating process of speeding downhill on fresh powder. We also spend a lot of time eating, drinking, making merry — and cooking.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/dining/11KITCH5/11KITCH5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/dining/11KITCH5/11KITCH5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 740}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/dining/11KITCH5/11KITCH5-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1008, 'width': 817, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/dining/11KITCH5/11KITCH5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1008, 'width': 817, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/dining/11KITCH5/11KITCH5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/dining/11KITCH5/11KITCH5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/dining/11KITCH5/11KITCH5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Winter’s Chill, Vegetable Risotto Adapts', 'kicker': 'City Kitchen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Winter’s Chill, Vegetable Risotto Adapts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Risotto', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:07:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c51ec96-5b22-5721-9b0a-79d520fb9cb8', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c51ec96-5b22-5721-9b0a-79d520fb9cb8'}, {'abstract': 'The Academy’s promo for the Oscars telecast pokes fun at the dust-up over ouster of Brett Ratner and Eddie Murphy and pays tribute, sort of, to “Transformers.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/megan-fox-and-josh-duhamel-but-no-optimus-prime/', 'snippet': 'The Academy’s promo for the Oscars telecast pokes fun at the dust-up over ouster of Brett Ratner and Eddie Murphy and pays tribute, sort of, to “Transformers.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Academy’s tagline for this year’s Oscars is “Celebrate the movies in all of us,” and with its first promo for the Feb. 26 show, to be broadcast on ABC, the movie they would most like to celebrate is … “Transformers.” Megan Fox and Josh Duhamel star in the spot, which pokes gentle fun at the dust-up over the ouster of Brett Ratner and Eddie Murphy as producer and host, and features cameos from William Fichtner (correctly cast as a version of the telecast’s new producer, spiky-haired Brian Grazer), Robin Williams and others. To be fair, the promo, made with the imprimatur of FunnyOrDie, also has shades of “Mission: Impossible” and “The Princess Bride,” at least in Mr. Crystal’s hair and makeup (although he looks more like Carol Kane). If it’s a sign of the kind of telecast we’ll see next month, we can bet on highly referential, high-production-value montages and familiar humor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Megan Fox and Josh Duhamel, but No Optimus Prime', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duhamel, Josh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fox, Megan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grazer, Brian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Eddie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratner, Brett', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:15:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afd5791e-af0b-56be-899d-d3a217fa3636', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afd5791e-af0b-56be-899d-d3a217fa3636'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of feeling sorry for Japan, the United States should look to it as a model for economic recovery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/opinion/sunday/the-true-story-of-japans-economic-success.html', 'snippet': 'Instead of feeling sorry for Japan, the United States should look to it as a model for economic recovery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tokyo', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/opinion/07japan-img/07japan-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/opinion/07japan-img/07japan-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Myth of Japan’s Failure', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Myth of Japan’s Failure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AKAMAI TECHNOLOGIES INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:19:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By EAMONN FINGLETON', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eamonn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'FINGLETON', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/72d3eb43-a643-5295-97d3-725c2dd72b71', 'word_count': 2119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72d3eb43-a643-5295-97d3-725c2dd72b71'}, {'abstract': 'Turnips are often overlooked by food shoppers, but they can be a surprisingly flavorful addition to your table.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/giving-turnips-a-second-look/', 'snippet': 'Turnips are often overlooked by food shoppers, but they can be a surprisingly flavorful addition to your table.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last fall, I was speaking with the Meatball Shop chef, Daniel Holzman, and the conversation turned to one of his favorite side dishes: Smashed Turnips With Fresh Horseradish.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giving Turnips a Second Look', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:20:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/257b3f5c-2887-540a-a9c9-01f89c48d25f', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/257b3f5c-2887-540a-a9c9-01f89c48d25f'}, {'abstract': 'A frequent guest on the news channel, Ms. Cheney will “offer commentary across all Fox News platforms” and fill in for some Fox News hosts.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/fox-news-hires-liz-cheney-as-analyst-and-substitute-host/', 'snippet': 'A frequent guest on the news channel, Ms. Cheney will “offer commentary across all Fox News platforms” and fill in for some Fox News hosts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Liz Cheney, the daughter of former Vice President Dick Cheney, is joining Fox News Channel as a paid contributor and substitute host, the channel confirmed Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fox News Hires Liz Cheney as Analyst and Substitute Host', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheney, Liz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:21:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbeec5ad-258d-580c-a196-5de9ad577f76', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbeec5ad-258d-580c-a196-5de9ad577f76'}, {'abstract': 'The trick with risotto is learning how to cook it right, which takes a certain amount of repetition.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/a-risotto-in-winter/', 'snippet': 'The trick with risotto is learning how to cook it right, which takes a certain amount of repetition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trick with risotto is learning how to cook it right, which takes a certain amount of repetition. A proper risotto is made by adding hot broth, in increments, to a particular kind of short-grained Italian rice (arborio or carnaroli) and cooking it, uncovered, over a brisk flame. Ideally it’s best to learn at the elbow of someone who knows how, because the process can be a bit difficult to describe. Risotto is not so much about a recipe as it is a technique. Once mastered, it is a joy to make.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Risotto in Winter', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Risotto', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:27:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/669261aa-2613-5f25-88f8-be2fbaa78bc1', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/669261aa-2613-5f25-88f8-be2fbaa78bc1'}, {'abstract': 'Checking in on the second season of “Portlandia” on IFC.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/channel-surfing-portlandia/', 'snippet': 'Checking in on the second season of “Portlandia” on IFC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The second season of Carrie Brownstein and Fred Armisen’s rigorously lo-fi comedy “Portlandia” arrives on IFC on Friday night riding a relentless wave of hype. Not many shows this small-bore — six half-hour episodes in the first season, expanded to 10 for Season 2 — get this kind of attention, with late-night guest spots, a red-carpet New York premiere (for the second season!) and a tour, which comes to Brooklyn and Manhattan on Jan. 20 and 21.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Channel Surfing: ‘Portlandia’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Armisen, Fred', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brownstein, Carrie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/312ba72e-8d62-503d-b43c-73b3e5ca8010', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/312ba72e-8d62-503d-b43c-73b3e5ca8010'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmaker Joe Berlinger, who, with a directing partner, Bruce Sinofsky, has chronicled the saga of the West Memphis Three, did so as advocate and journalist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/movies/filmmakers-as-advocates-in-paradise-lost-series.html', 'snippet': 'The filmmaker Joe Berlinger, who, with a directing partner, Bruce Sinofsky, has chronicled the saga of the West Memphis Three, did so as advocate and journalist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN the Arkansas men known as the West Memphis Three were released from prison this summer, it was a momentous occasion not only for those convicts, who had each spent nearly 20 years behind bars for murders they say they did not commit, but also for the people who had followed their case and become convinced of their innocence.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08BERLINGER2_SPAN/08BERLINGER2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08BERLINGER2_SPAN/08BERLINGER2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08BERLINGER2_SPAN/08BERLINGER2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08BERLINGER2_SPAN/08BERLINGER2_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08BERLINGER2_SPAN/08BERLINGER2_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Filmmakers Take Dual Roles in Quest for Truth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Filmmakers Take Dual Roles In Quest for Truth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, Jason', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlinger, Joe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sinofsky, Bruce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Misskelley, Jessie Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Echols, Damien', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ebbc23f-7b54-5842-8c32-ee9cffefa7b6', 'word_count': 1696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ebbc23f-7b54-5842-8c32-ee9cffefa7b6'}, {'abstract': 'A Time/CNN ORC International survey also shows that nearly half of Republicans likely to vote in the primary could change their minds in the next two weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/romney-santorum-see-a-bounce-in-south-carolina-poll/', 'snippet': 'A Time/CNN ORC International survey also shows that nearly half of Republicans likely to vote in the primary could change their minds in the next two weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that Iowa’s caucus is over, the candidates’ standings are rolling in from the next set of states in the primary lineup. And more poll results are expected before the day is over. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney and Santorum See Bounce in South Carolina Poll', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:32:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marjorie Connelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marjorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Connelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b033d743-e4c9-5739-ad0d-88d5dfc1c146', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b033d743-e4c9-5739-ad0d-88d5dfc1c146'}, {'abstract': 'New polls in South Carolina give Mitt Romney a comfortable lead, with Rick Santorum and Newt Gingrich in a battle for second.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/romney-leads-south-carolina-polls/', 'snippet': 'New polls in South Carolina give Mitt Romney a comfortable lead, with Rick Santorum and Newt Gingrich in a battle for second.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — The first South Carolina polls in more than two weeks are out, and they show a lead for Mitt Romney but with Rick Santorum and Newt Gingrich in a competitive position. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Leads South Carolina Polls', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:33:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/512deef3-c044-5a6a-a6fc-22677a5756fe', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/512deef3-c044-5a6a-a6fc-22677a5756fe'}, {'abstract': 'In what appears to be a recurring 15-year cycle, the compound annual return of the S.& P. stock index peaks at more than 15 percent, then plunges. It’s plunge time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/business/economy/a-historical-cycle-bodes-ill-for-the-markets.html', 'snippet': 'In what appears to be a recurring 15-year cycle, the compound annual return of the S.& P. stock index peaks at more than 15 percent, then plunges. It’s plunge time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT the turn of the last century, it was widely accepted that American stocks were virtually certain to be good long-term investments. Now, far fewer people are confident of that.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Historical Cycle Bodes Ill for the Markets', 'kicker': 'Off the Charts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Historical Cycle Bodes Ill For the Markets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Standard & Poor's 500-Stock Index", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:39:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db5e36a4-504a-5a4a-9950-eb5d36674d39', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db5e36a4-504a-5a4a-9950-eb5d36674d39'}, {'abstract': 'After almost 35 years, this specialty-food chain is making its own bread, with the baker, Louis Volle, offering choices like pain de mie and dark chestnut bread.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/dining/for-dean-deluca-a-big-leap-baking-its-own-bread-food-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'After almost 35 years, this specialty-food chain is making its own bread, with the baker, Louis Volle, offering choices like pain de mie and dark chestnut bread.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly 35 years after Dean & DeLuca opened its first shop, on Prince Street in SoHo, this specialty-food chain has made another big leap. It has started baking its own bread, in a kitchen on West 28th Street, instead of selling only a collection of breads from companies like Sullivan Street Bakery and Amy’s Bread. The baker is Louis Volle, above, a 28-year-old New Yorker who grew up in France and worked at Fauchon before returning to bake bread at Per Se and Bouchon Bakery. He has introduced a basic baguette and a fine round sourdough at Dean & DeLuca, as well as some less-common standouts. In Mr. Volle’s hands, pain de mie, a dense French white bread meant for slicing, has a beautifully fluted crust and is delicious as a substitute for brioche, with a slab of pâté. His dark chestnut bread has a deep earthiness. Several other loaves are studded with fruits and nuts.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dean & DeLuca Baking Its Own Breads', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dean & DeLuca Baking Its Own Breads', 'name': 