'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:48:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARQUAVIUS BURNETT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marquavius', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BURNETT', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/119fe569-3b31-5677-b757-7cccb909072d', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/119fe569-3b31-5677-b757-7cccb909072d'}, {'abstract': 'Companies can no longer say they “neither admit nor deny” civil charges by the Securities and Exchange Commission in cases where criminal guilt has already been established.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/business/sec-to-change-policy-on-companies-admission-of-guilt.html', 'snippet': 'Companies can no longer say they “neither admit nor deny” civil charges by the Securities and Exchange Commission in cases where criminal guilt has already been established.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Securities and Exchange Commission, in a fundamental policy shift, said Friday that it would no longer allow defendants to say they neither admit nor deny civil fraud or insider trading charges when, at the same time, they admit to or have been convicted of criminal violations.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/business/SEC/SEC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 721, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/business/SEC/SEC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/business/SEC/SEC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Changes Policy on Firms’ Admission of Guilt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'S.E.C. Changes Policy on Firms’ Admissions of Guilt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:50:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e322bd4-9cd1-570c-9d9c-7047b2eac49e', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e322bd4-9cd1-570c-9d9c-7047b2eac49e'}, {'abstract': 'Nearly a century after it was conceived, this suburban community in the Bronx retains its dash of country, as well as its easy access to city life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/realestate/fieldston-the-bronx-living-in-in-the-city-but-not-of-it.html', 'snippet': 'Nearly a century after it was conceived, this suburban community in the Bronx retains its dash of country, as well as its easy access to city life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE grand houses of Fieldston — about 260, all single-family — are mostly generations old, devoid of the uniformity in other parts of the city and in suburban subdivisions. Nearly a century after it was conceived, this flowing suburban community in the northwest corner of the Bronx retains its dash of country, as well as its easy access to city life, having kept faith with its developers’ original vision. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/realestate/08LIVING_SPAN/08LIVING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/realestate/08LIVING_SPAN/08LIVING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/realestate/08LIVING_SPAN/living-in-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/realestate/08LIVING_SPAN/08LIVING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/realestate/08LIVING_SPAN/08LIVING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the City, but Not of It', 'kicker': 'Living In | Fieldston, the Bronx', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the City, but Not of It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T18:53:18+0000', '