', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/movies/devil-span/devil-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/06/movies/devil-span/devil-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/movies/devil-span/devil-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/06/movies/devil-span/devil-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/06/movies/devil-span/devil-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Rome, Bending Joints but Limiting the Budget', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Devil Inside'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Rome, Bending Joints But Limiting the Budget', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Occult Sciences', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T20:25:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/22a5e00d-22fa-583b-9201-7bba0e37475e', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22a5e00d-22fa-583b-9201-7bba0e37475e'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Greenblatt told reporters about his thinking as he faces hard choices on what shows to extend on the network. The fall, he said, was “worse than I hoped for, but about what I expected.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/nbc-entertainment-head-weighs-in-on-community-30-rock-and-house/', 'snippet': 'Robert Greenblatt told reporters about his thinking as he faces hard choices on what shows to extend on the network. The fall, he said, was “worse than I hoped for, but about what I expected.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'PASADENA, Calif. — Robert Greenblatt, who runs entertainment for NBC, acknowledged here that the fall had been brutally difficult for his network’s prime time schedule, “worse than I hoped for, but about what I expected.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC Entertainment Head Weighs In on ‘Community,’ ’30 Rock’ and ‘House’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seasons and Months', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fey, Tina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenblatt, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laurie, Hugh', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seacrest, Ryan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, Howard', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Universal', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T20:26:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddc80b60-c095-5df9-9035-2e577d28e325', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddc80b60-c095-5df9-9035-2e577d28e325'}, {'abstract': 'The White House will propose a 0.5 percent pay raise for civilian federal employees in the 2013 budget, an administration official said on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/white-house-to-propose-pay-raise-for-federal-workers/', 'snippet': 'The White House will propose a 0.5 percent pay raise for civilian federal employees in the 2013 budget, an administration official said on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The White House will propose a 0.5 percent pay raise for civilian federal employees in the 2013 budget, an administration official said on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'White House to Propose Pay Raise for Federal Workers', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T20:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efc4fc9d-8e6a-5056-9ab6-09fee23ca463', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efc4fc9d-8e6a-5056-9ab6-09fee23ca463'}, {'abstract': 'During a New Year’s Eve party at the Rangers’ hotel in Philadelphia, Brandon Dubinsky’s grandfather offers a simple toast: Drink up. And drink up we did, from the buildup caught on HBO’s cameras to the game itself to the subsequent jubilation and heartache.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/247-episode-4-a-final-salute/', 'snippet': 'During a New Year’s Eve party at the Rangers’ hotel in Philadelphia, Brandon Dubinsky’s grandfather offers a simple toast: Drink up. And drink up we did, from the buildup caught on HBO’s cameras to the game itself to the subsequent jubilation and ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were so many story lines woven into the Winter Classic between the Flyers and the Rangers, you had to wonder how HBO could possibly do it justice. Sean Avery was waived. Ilya Bryzgalov was benched (and went straight to the news media). Marc Staal was cleared to play. Questionable calls were followed by questionable reactions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘24/7’ Episode 4: A Final Salute', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Avery, Sean', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryzgalov, Ilya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giroux, Claude', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laviolette, Peter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Brad', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rupp, Mike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Staal, Marc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tortorella, John', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Flyers', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T20:31:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c69b681-cdc7-531d-ac08-73650be6db5b', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c69b681-cdc7-531d-ac08-73650be6db5b'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’s restaurant critic, Pete Wells, referees a championship bout between two all-duck meals offered by Asian restaurants in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/duck-versus-duck-pitting-ssam-bars-duck-lunch-against-wongs-duckavore-dinner/', 'snippet': 'The Times’s restaurant critic, Pete Wells, referees a championship bout between two all-duck meals offered by Asian restaurants in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': '“DUCK really is the other pork, isn’t it?” a friend observed last week. And of course, she’s right. The two animals meander around the barnyard, grazing and grunting and generally acting like hungry teenagers. But all the while they are building up a formidable cushion of sweet fat that has the miraculous quality of improving just about any food it touches.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Duck Versus Duck: Pitting Ssam Bar’s Duck Lunch Against Wong’s Duckavore Dinner', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T20:32:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87f9259c-f9a7-5e45-9eba-fccd3b1d33ec', 'word_count': 1702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87f9259c-f9a7-5e45-9eba-fccd3b1d33ec'}, {'abstract': 'Minnesota officials will check for the presence of zebra mussels and other invaders in boats being hauled along the state’s roads.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/on-our-radar-road-checks-for-invasive-species/', 'snippet': 'Minnesota officials will check for the presence of zebra mussels and other invaders in boats being hauled along the state’s roads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time, state officers in Minnesota will conduct random road checks this year for invasive species that could be hitchhiking on trailers, boats and other vehicles. [Duluth News Tribune]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Road Checks for Invasive Species', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T20:36:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16add57f-7c53-56bc-8f49-0ce88e1c5e4d', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16add57f-7c53-56bc-8f49-0ce88e1c5e4d'}, {'abstract': 'Giants receiver (and salsa guy) Victor Cruz turns down an opportunity to compete on “Dancing With the Stars.”', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/victor-cruz-decides-not-to-go-dancing/', 'snippet': 'Giants receiver (and salsa guy) Victor Cruz turns down an opportunity to compete on “Dancing With the Stars.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. – Part of the reason Giants receiver Victor Cruz’s popularity has exploded this season – beyond his franchise-record 1,536 receiving yards – is his trademark salsa dance, which he has done after most of his 9 touchdowns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Victor Cruz Decides Not to Go ‘Dancing’', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salsa Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Victor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T20:38:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c734312-130b-58cf-bb28-b8731278b74d', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c734312-130b-58cf-bb28-b8731278b74d'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographer Meg Stuart, who lives in Berlin, returns to New York with “Blessed,” an acclaimed experimental piece from 2007.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/arts/dance/meg-stuart-choreographs-blessed-at-new-york-live-arts.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographer Meg Stuart, who lives in Berlin, returns to New York with “Blessed,” an acclaimed experimental piece from 2007.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN Meg Stuart’s “Blessed” a white-clad man in sandals — picture a Brazilian hippie passing a lazy day at the beach — traverses a stage that resembles a storybook island. His flattened movement gives him the two-dimensional air of Nijinsky on holiday. But there’s something not quite right about this strange scene: the set, which features a palm tree, a hut with a chair and an enormous swan, is made entirely of cardboard. Soon enough it begins to rain. There’s trouble ahead. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08STUART2_SPAN/08STUART2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08STUART2_SPAN/08STUART2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08STUART2_SPAN/08STUART2_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08STUART2_SPAN/08STUART2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08STUART2_SPAN/08STUART2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Perseverance in a Collapsing World', 'kicker': 'Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perseverance in a Collapsing World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stuart, Meg', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T20:40:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News',