 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b45a45de-4701-5a3b-a075-03a2a113b1f6', 'word_count': 1451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b45a45de-4701-5a3b-a075-03a2a113b1f6'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Capano had been inside the pharmacy when a man armed with what turned out to be a pellet gun stole hundreds of painkillers and cash, law enforcement officials have said.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/remembering-an-a-t-f-officer-killed-while-trying-to-stop-a-robber/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Capano had been inside the pharmacy when a man armed with what turned out to be a pellet gun stole hundreds of painkillers and cash, law enforcement officials have said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A funeral service was held Friday in Seaford, N.Y., for John Capano, a federal agent, who was shot by a retired Nassau County police officer during a confused situation last Saturday while trying to detain a man who had robbed a pharmacy, according to law enforcement officials.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering an A.T.F. Officer Killed While Trying to Stop a Robber', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Capano, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nassau County (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T20:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ac55caf-937b-509f-8d1d-4ace591884e5', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ac55caf-937b-509f-8d1d-4ace591884e5'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats mocked Republicans on the floor of the House for not returning to work on legislation aimed at creating jobs. Republicans dismissed the complaints as theater.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/house-democrats-ask-where-are-the-republicans/', 'snippet': 'Democrats mocked Republicans on the floor of the House for not returning to work on legislation aimed at creating jobs. Republicans dismissed the complaints as theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Democrats took to the floor of an empty House chamber on Friday to mock Republicans who they said were taking a vacation rather than buckling down to work on legislation to create jobs, cut taxes and extend unemployment benefits for millions of Americans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Democrats Ask, ‘Where Are the Republicans?’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T20:47:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Pear', 'person':