ker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T21:21:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98895ac4-d2d7-53a9-b984-b4fd9420e960', 'word_count': 1400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98895ac4-d2d7-53a9-b984-b4fd9420e960'}, {'abstract': 'Rick Santorum is joining the crowd in South Carolina for a couple of events on Sunday, even as the New Hampshire primary to heat up.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/santorum-heads-to-south-carolina-on-sunday/', 'snippet': 'Rick Santorum is joining the crowd in South Carolina for a couple of events on Sunday, even as the New Hampshire primary to heat up.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:03 p.m. | Updated DUBLIN, N.H. — Rick Santorum and Gov. Rick Perry of Texas are joining the crowd and heading to South Carolina even as the New Hampshire primary heats up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perry and Santorum Head to South Carolina on Sunday', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T21:24:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bde1f24-7b04-5157-bdd9-1c57d469ad90', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bde1f24-7b04-5157-bdd9-1c57d469ad90'}, {'abstract': 'A stimulus measure by the new prime minister, Mario Monti, allows shopkeepers to set their own hours, but while some praise the move, others say it will harm mom-and-pop stores.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/business/global/more-time-to-buy-in-italy-but-is-that-a-good-thing.html', 'snippet': 'A stimulus measure by the new prime minister, Mario Monti, allows shopkeepers to set their own hours, but while some praise the move, others say it will harm mom-and-pop stores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — The first days of the new year have heralded a subtle revolution in Italy: the deregulation of operating hours for commercial venues like shops, bars and restaurants. And as revolutions tend to go, the measure has aroused praise in some corners and howls of protest in others. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/business/global/07hours-pic/07hours-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/07/business/global/07hours-pic/07hours-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/business/global/07hours-pic/07hours-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 884, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/business/global/07hours-pic/07hours-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/business/global/07hours-pic/07hours-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Time to Buy in Italy, but Is That a Good Thing?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Italy, Mom-and-Pop StoresWorry That Longer Hours May Hurt Business', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monti, Mario', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T21:29:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bdf80a3-1621-5c5d-87b4-1711ffde1690', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bdf80a3-1621-5c5d-87b4-1711ffde1690'}, {'abstract': 'Bjork said she would perform her “Biophilia” show, an elaborate stage performance of her recent compositions about nature, for 10 nights in New York in February.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/bjork-bringing-biophilia-to-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Bjork said she would perform her “Biophilia” show, an elaborate stage performance of her recent compositions about nature, for 10 nights in New York in February.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bjork said on Friday that she would perform her “Biophilia” show for 10 nights in New York in February. The residency will mark the first time the Icelandic singer and songwriter has brought the elaborate stage performance of her recent compositions about nature to North America. Six performances will take place at the New York Hall of Science in Queens, starting on Feb. 3, and four shows will be staged at Roseland Ballroom in Manhattan, beginning on Feb. 22. No other performances have been scheduled in the United States. The show had its premiere at the Manchester International Festival in England and has received ecstatic reviews from critics. Performed in the round, it features a 24-woman choir, a giant Tesla coil and several large custom-built instruments that Bjork and her collaborators invented: a portable pipe organ, four 10-foot pendulums that play harp notes as they swing, a gramophone-like contraption called a “Sharpsichord” and another piece called a “gameleste,” which is a fusion of a celesta and a gamelan. The songs are eerie and convoluted, with unusual melodies and fluctuating meters, meant to capture the patterns in natural phenomena like those of gravity, lunar cycles, DNA and crystals. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bjork Bringing ‘Biophilia’ to New York', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bjork', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Hall of Science', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roseland Ballroom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T21:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3da0cad7-f6a4-5008-9636-92a22b772b29', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3da0cad7-f6a4-5008-9636-92a22b772b29'}, {'abstract': 'Many older unemployed people — nearly two million over age 55 — must make tough decisions about how to make up for lost income.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/your-money/laid-off-with-retirement-almost-in-sight.html', 'snippet': 'Many older unemployed people — nearly two million over age 55 — must make tough decisions about how to make up for lost income.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Achieving financial security in retirement is hard enough for most working Americans. But for those who lost their jobs just as the finish line was within sight, the whole notion may now seem out of reach.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/your-money/07money/07money-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/07/your-money/07money/07money-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/your-money/07money/07money-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/your-money/07money/07money-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/your-money/07money/07money-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Laid Off, With Retirement Almost in Sight', 'kicker': 'Your Money', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laid Off, With Retirement Almost in Sight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T21:33:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/675fc274-3050-5694-88d1-955e068cb14c', 'word_count': 1523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/675fc274-3050-5694-88d1-955e068cb14c'}, {'abstract': 'Alber Elbaz reveals a prefall collection full of texture, shine and stunning proportions.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/just-one-look-lanvin/', 'snippet': 'Alber Elbaz reveals a prefall collection full of texture, shine and stunning proportions.', 'lead_paragraph': '“This collection is about fabric, technology and volume,” Alber Elbaz said at the start of his prefall presentation earlier today. Citing innovations in fabric\xa0—\xa0first, with the incorporation of metals into knits and wovens, and now with things that have been bonded, plastified and waxed\xa0—\xa0as his muse, Elbaz went on to show a collection full of texture (felted wool and fox), shine (sequins and coated cotton so glossy it looks wet) and stunning proportions (fly-away jackets and exaggerated, egg-shaped shoulders). Here, a romantic all-emerald look that illustrates all three of Elbaz’s points is anchored by a giant cameo pendant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Lanvin', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T21:34:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/193f4a7e-54b1-530b-9718-9e18696d01e2', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/193f4a7e-54b1-530b-9718-9e18696d01e2'}, {'abstract': 'While automakers typically do business with many suppliers, the design and construction of combustion engines have largely been the responsibility of the carmaker. But that is changing with e-mobility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/automobiles/at-risk-the-core-of-a-cars-identity.html', 'snippet': 'While automakers typically do business with many suppliers, the design and construction of combustion engines have largely been the responsibility of the carmaker. But that is changing with e-mobility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Berlin', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/automobiles/08MOTO/08MOTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/automobiles/08MOTO/08MOTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': '