one, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9921439-0afc-5a3e-8da3-a0c1c727e3af', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9921439-0afc-5a3e-8da3-a0c1c727e3af'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s Your Money column looks at the various tricks that older unemployed Americans may use until they find a new job or manage to eke their way to retirement.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/some-tips-for-unemployed-older-americans/', 'snippet': 'This week’s Your Money column looks at the various tricks that older unemployed Americans may use until they find a new job or manage to eke their way to retirement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the latest jobs report provided some reason for tempered optimism, older Americans who find themselves unemployed are typically out of work much longer than their younger peers. And that can make the road to retirement much more challenging.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Tips for Unemployed Older Americans', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T21:34:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/321b0a21-ddde-556f-a39a-3c805393787c', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/321b0a21-ddde-556f-a39a-3c805393787c'}, {'abstract': 'The current spate of silent-film tributes recall some comedies that demonstrate that Hollywood’s nostalgia for its early days is nothing new.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/movies/awardsseason/silent-movie-era-tributes-from-the-past.html', 'snippet': 'The current spate of silent-film tributes recall some comedies that demonstrate that Hollywood’s nostalgia for its early days is nothing new.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOLLYWOOD’S collective fascination with the silent-film era is hitting a peak with “Hugo” and “The Artist,” each a homage to a bygone time. The tributes continue with Film Forum’s series of MGM silent features, complete with live piano accompaniment (through Feb. 6); an exhibition at the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts (through Feb. 25); and a new DVD release of the recent restoration of the only known color copy of the 1902 Georges Méliès masterpiece “A Trip to the Moon,” which is featured in “Hugo.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08SILENTS1_SPAN/08SILENTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08SILENTS1_SPAN/08SILENTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08SILENTS1_SPAN/08SILENTS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 718, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08SILENTS1_SPAN/08SILENTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/arts/08SILENTS1_SPAN/08SILENTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tributes That Leave 