ecoming the most disliked player in the N.B.A.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:38 p.m. | Updated As much as the Knicks’ early season struggles have put fans into fits of hand-wringing, at least one can take solace in the fact that one of the most disliked players in the league doesn’t suit up for New York. He’s so unpopular that he’s being soundly booed in arenas across the country if he dare sets foot on the court. In Toronto the other night, fans mocked him by waving large posters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Humphries, the Boo-Birds’ New King', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Humphries, Kris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kardashian, Kim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Nets', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T21:49:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Silverman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silverman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/205d9a51-c581-5fe0-8c66-b8d194c7d737', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/205d9a51-c581-5fe0-8c66-b8d194c7d737'}, {'abstract': 'Even with Atlanta’s addition of the rookie Julio Jones at receiver, Michael Turner carried the ball 301 times this season, second among N.F.L. running backs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/sports/football/falcons-running-back-michael-turner-still-shoulders-the-load.html', 'snippet': 'Even with Atlanta’s addition of the rookie Julio Jones at receiver, Michael Turner carried the ball 301 times this season, second among N.F.L. running backs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLOWERY BRANCH, Ga. — The Atlanta Falcons, who play their home games in the living-room comfort of a domed stadium, began practice outdoors here Wednesday morning in a 38-degree chill, but without topcoats. A national radio sports talk host labeled the Falcons a finesse team that will capitulate in the kind of chilly, sloppy weather the Giants occasionally play in, which made Falcons running back Michael Turner laugh. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/sports/07falcons1/07falcons1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/sports/07falcons1/07falcons1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/sports/07falcons1/07falcons1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Team Called Soft, Falcons Run With Ferocity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Team Called Soft, Falcons Run With Ferocity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Julio (1989- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Falcons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T21:52:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ray Glier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d035fc4-88fd-54f9-b9a5-4f8be439dad4', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d035fc4-88fd-54f9-b9a5-4f8be439dad4'}, {'abstract': 'The government said there was still not enough evidence to recommend routine removal, but allowed free replacement for some women who received the implants under the National Health Service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/world/europe/british-clarification-on-implant-scandal-leaves-women-more-confused-than-ever.html', 'snippet': 'The government said there was still not enough evidence to recommend routine removal, but allowed free replacement for some women who received the implants under the National Health Service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The British government said on Friday that there was still not enough evidence to recommend routine removal of breast implants made by a now-defunct French company using silicone of dubious quality. But it also said that it would allow about 3,000 women who received the implants under the National Health Service to have them taken out and replaced free of charge if they and their doctors decided it was “right to do so.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source