t_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/us/politics/MICHELLE/MICHELLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/07/us/politics/MICHELLE/MICHELLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/us/politics/MICHELLE/MICHELLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/us/politics/MICHELLE/MICHELLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/us/politics/MICHELLE/MICHELLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Michelle Obama and the Evolution of a First Lady', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Lady’s Fraught White House Journey to Greater Fulfillment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'First Ladies (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T22:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jodi Kantor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jodi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kantor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2530bb66-1cd0-548a-9b7f-331eb0c3d9b1', 'word_count': 3284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2530bb66-1cd0-548a-9b7f-331eb0c3d9b1'}, {'abstract': 'After the disappointment that greeted the F.D.A.’s decision not to regulate antibiotics in animal agriculture, the agency delivered a token gesture by announcing a ban on extra-label uses of the cephalosporin, an antibiotic that’s been on its way out for years.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/the-f-d-a-s-token-gesture/', 'snippet': 'After the disappointment that greeted the F.D.A.’s decision not to regulate antibiotics in animal agriculture, the agency delivered a token gesture by announcing a ban on extra-label uses of the cephalosporin, an antibiotic that’s been on its way ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'My column last week described how the Food and Drug Administration is declining to regulate the use of antibiotics in animal agriculture. After withdrawing its own 34-year-old request/promise to restrict the routine use of penicillin and tetracyclines in farm animal feed, the F.D.A. made it crystal clear that, despite the increasingly common threat of antibiotic-resistant bacteria in supermarket meat, it would leave the regulating up to industry itself. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The F.D.A.’s Token Gesture', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factory Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Philpott, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T22:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d1abb3f-c092-5720-b2ac-70fc333ffedd', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d1abb3f-c092-5720-b2ac-70fc333ffedd'}, {'abstract': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural events from this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/the-week-in-culture-pictures-jan-8-2/', 'snippet': 'A slide show of photographs of cultural events from this week.', 'lead_paragraph': ' More Photographs', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Culture Pictures, Jan. 8', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T22:30:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88eb75b1-d6e3-5077-a341-06313b8644b2', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88eb75b1-d6e3-5077-a341-06313b8644b2'}, {'abstract': 'Celebrating Joan of Arc, the cross-dressing, teenage virgin-warrior-martyr-saint, on her 600th birthday.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/lumiere-the-koan-of-joan/', 'snippet': 'Celebrating Joan of Arc, the cross-dressing, teenage virgin-warrior-martyr-saint, on her 600th birthday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today is the 600th anniversary of the birth of Joan of Arc, the cross-dressing, teenage virgin-warrior-martyr-saint. So what better way for President Nicolas Sarkozy — three months away from an election and mired in Europe’s economic crisis — to feel good about France than to make a pilgrimage to her birthplace? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lumière | The Koan of Joan', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T22:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Sciolino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciolino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ee84501-285b-5b82-88af-1b6fc65d2aff', 'word_count': 1217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ee84501-285b-5b82-88af-1b6fc65d2aff'}, {'abstract': '“Bunny Lake Is Missing,” adapted from a 1957 mystery, portrays a woman desperately searching for her 3-year-old daughter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/theater/reviews/bunny-lake-is-missing-at-the-brick-theater-review.html', 'snippet': '“Bunny Lake Is Missing,” adapted from a 1957 mystery, portrays a woman desperately searching for her 3-year-old daughter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s something perhaps inadvertently timely about “Bunny Lake Is Missing,” now at the Brick in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. This stage noir, about a single mother’s desperate search for her 3-year-old daughter after she disappears from nursery school, speaks to parental anxiety in an age when child abuse seems rife. The play — based on Evelyn Piper’s 1957 pulp mystery (the source for Otto Preminger’s 1965 screen adaptation) — derives tension from its resonant, inescapable subtext. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/arts/BUNNY/BUNNY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/07/arts/BUNNY/BUNNY-articleLar