a'}, {'abstract': 'A fond farewell to Filene’s Basement, where I scored a dress that took me through my first years working in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/fashion/farewell-to-filenes-basement.html', 'snippet': 'A fond farewell to Filene’s Basement, where I scored a dress that took me through my first years working in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WERE it not for Filene’s Basement, I would have gone to my proms in a potato sack. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/fashion/08FILENES2_SPAN/08FILENES2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/fashion/08FILENES2_SPAN/08FILENES2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/fashion/08FILENES2_SPAN/08FILENES2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/fashion/08FILENES2_SPAN/08FILENES2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/fashion/08FILENES2_SPAN/08FILENES2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering the Fever, and Fun, of the Basement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Remembering the Fever, and Fun, of the Basement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Filene's Basement Corporation", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basements and Cellars', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T22:54:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Weinman Lear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Weinman', 'lastname': 'Lear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fcad428-fcd4-51cc-b47b-96e2f7f721ea', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fcad428-fcd4-51cc-b47b-96e2f7f721ea'}, {'abstract': 'After performing the New York premiere of Thomas Adès’s “Polaris: Voyage for Orchestra,” the New York Philharmonic, conducted by Alan Gilbert, offered a moving account of Mahler’s Ninth Symphony.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/arts/music/new-york-philharmonic-performs-mahler-and-thomas-ades-review.html', 'snippet': 'After performing the New York premiere of Thomas Adès’s “Polaris: Voyage for Orchestra,” the New York Philharmonic, conducted by Alan Gilbert, offered a moving account of Mahler’s Ninth Symphony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mahler’s 80-minute Ninth Symphony is presented as the only work on an orchestra program, most people in the audience feel they have gotten their money’s worth. Especially if the performance of this turbulent and, by the end, sublimely moving symphony is as well played and resolute as the one Alan Gilbert conducted with the New York Philharmonic on Thursday night at Avery Fisher Hall.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/arts/SUB-PHIL/SUB-PHIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 753, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/arts/SUB-PHIL/SUB-PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/arts/SUB-PHIL/SUB-PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sailing a Sea Teeming With Sonic Treasures', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sailing a Sea Teeming With Sonic Treasures', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mahler, Gustav', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ades, Thomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T22:57:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/72dd3b22-b1bd-5ba8-9f36-d917cf62cbdc', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72dd3b22-b1bd-5ba8-9f36-d917cf62cbdc'}, {'abstract': 'This triptych of short plays, part of the Under the Radar festival, is written and directed in hypnotic style by Toshiki Okada.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/theater/reviews/toshiki-okadas-under-the-radar-entry-at-japan-society-review.html', 'snippet': 'This triptych of short plays, part of the Under the Radar festival, is written and directed in hypnotic style by Toshiki Okada.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everybody dances to his or her own drummer in the plays of Toshiki Okada, and it’s a lonely, spastic beat each of them hears. The characters who appear in “Hot Pepper, Air Conditioner, and the Farewell Speech” — a triptych of short plays at Japan Society, directed in hypnotic style by Mr. Okada — may be the most gracefully graceless people in town.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Temp Workers Too Twitchy to Engage in Office Politics', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Hot Pepper, Air Conditioner, and the Farewell Speech'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Temp Workers Too Twitchy To Engage in Office Politics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Under the Radar Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Okada, Toshiki', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Japan Society', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T23:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad31d712-32d5-5786-8552-fa045cddbb9f', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad31d712-32d5-5786-8552-fa045cddbb9f'}, {'abstract': 'A New York man has won a lawsuit against a woman who was accused of registering Web domains incorporating his name and demanding $1 million in exchange for ownership of the addresses.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/new-york-cyber-squatter/', 'snippet': 'A New York man has won a lawsuit against a woman who was accused of registering Web domains incorporating his name and demanding $1 million in exchange for ownership of the addresses.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A New York man on Friday won a lawsuit against a woman whom he accused of registering Web addresses incorporating his name and demanding $1 million for each of them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Wins Web Squatting Suit Involving His Name', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-06T23:04:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddc6d7a0-d946-5a40-a5b8-f111dcd0dc80', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddc6d7a0-d946-5a40-a5b8-f111dcd0dc80'}, {'abstract': 'Frank DiMattina, former owner of the popular Staten Island catering hall Ariana’s, forced a rival to withdraw a bid on a lucrative contract for school lunches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/nyregion/caterer-linked-to-organized-crime-is-convicted-of-extortion.html', 'snippet': 'Frank DiMattina, former owner of the popular Staten Island catering hall Ariana’s, forced a rival to withdraw a bid on a lucrative contract for school lunches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank DiMattina, a suspected Genovese family associate who had dreams of reality television stardom, was convicted Friday of extortion and a related firearms charge.', 'p