Mirror', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demolition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florence (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Restoration Hardware', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Napa (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Williams-Sonoma Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bathrooms and Toilets', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T00:18:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Colman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Colman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3636f6ff-1850-5110-9875-27d727b8465e', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3636f6ff-1850-5110-9875-27d727b8465e'}, {'abstract': 'The Quiet Man Public House in Peekskill offers Smithwick’s and Harp, many potato dishes and other tastes of the old sod.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/nyregion/quiet-man-public-house-a-real-irish-pub-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Quiet Man Public House in Peekskill offers Smithwick’s and Harp, many potato dishes and other tastes of the old sod.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I STILL remember the first time I had a Guinness properly poured and at the optimal (not too cool) temperature. It was in a small pub in a small town in Ireland, and it was like nothing I’d ever tasted — thick and rich and full of flavor. I wanted to drink it slowly, almost eat it with a spoon. I had dinner that night, too, but I couldn’t tell you what I had: The experience was all about the beer.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08DINEWE3/08DINEWE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08DINEWE3/08DINEWE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08DINEWE3/08DINEWE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where You Can Pull Your Own Guinness', 'kicker': 'Westchester Dining | Peekskill', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where You Can Pull Your Own Guinness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peekskill (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T00:20:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily DeNitto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeNitto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e308976-b3fd-5b3f-9f88-d97933aa3064', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e308976-b3fd-5b3f-9f88-d97933aa3064'}, {'abstract': 'Timehop, like a diary, lets you “capture a moment in time” so you can look back on it later.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/fashion/timehop-a-new-online-service-tells-you-what-you-were-doing-a-year-ago.html', 'snippet': 'Timehop, like a diary, lets you “capture a moment in time” so you can look back on it later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIKE many 29-year-old Web designers from Brooklyn, Kelsey Rahn spent part of New Year’s Day hung over, poring over a list of resolutions. “Make more time for myself.” “Make soup in my Crock-Pot twice a month.” “Join the gym by Friday.” ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/fashion/08NOTICED/08NOTICED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/fashion/08NOTICED/08NOTICED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/fashion/08NOTICED/08NOTICED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Back Pages: Digital Diary Traces Memories', 'kicker': 'Noticed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Back Pages: Digital Diary Traces Memories', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T00:28:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Considine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Considine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/099f09f5-b92f-5cde-b9d1-0fc88f160b78', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/099f09f5-b92f-5cde-b9d1-0fc88f160b78'}, {'abstract': 'Red Lulu Cocina in South Norwalk, whose appearance is more outré than sombrero, puts a cosmopolitan spin on south-of-the-border cuisine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/nyregion/red-lulu-cocina-in-south-norwalk-review.html', 'snippet': 'Red Lulu Cocina in South Norwalk, whose appearance is more outré than sombrero, puts a cosmopolitan spin on south-of-the-border cuisine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNLIKE most Mexican restaurants, Red Lulu Cocina and Tequila Bar, in South Norwalk, favors clubby gothic over cactus and sombrero. Its ornate chandeliers, some adorned with black birds, are set to a dim luminescence. Capacious booths, with privacy draperies, surround a cruciform communal table decked out with a super-elongated candelabrum. There is a surfeit of red throughout — from the velour curtains by the entrance to the lights strung along the railing of the upstairs balcony. And films projected onto one of two brick walls add to the sense of hyperactivity.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08DINECT1/08DINECT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08DINECT1/08DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08DINECT1/08DINECT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ambience Is Gothic, but Flavor Is Mexican', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | South Norwalk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ambience Is Gothic, But Flavor Is Mexican', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reyes, Juan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T00:31:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/34eff840-29f2-52f7-8ff5-15adc85fd4ec', 'word_count': 1127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34eff840-29f2-52f7-8ff5-15adc85fd4ec'}, {'abstract': 'Davis Freeman’s “Too shy to stare,” an installation performance in which audience members participate in unexpected ways, is part of Performance Space 122’s Coil Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/arts/dance/too-shy-to-stare-a-davis-freeman-installation-performance-review.html', 'snippet': 'Davis Freeman’s “Too shy to stare,” an installation performance in which audience members participate in unexpected ways, is part of Performance Space 122’s Coil Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Outside the curtained door are two lights, one green and one red. When the green light comes on, you pass one of your allotted cards between the curtains and into an unseen hand. When the red light comes on, you enter. Inside you meet yourself. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/arts/STARE/STARE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop