ates that the Obama campaign considers battlegrounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama dined for the second time with four winners of the quarterly “Dinner With Barack” contest, and for the second time, all four winners were from states that the Obama campaign considers battlegrounds that could help determine whether Mr. Obama is re-elected.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Has Lunch With Contest Winners — From Swing States', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T00:36:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/facf77cf-9f22-5c41-b730-ce7f0b972440', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/facf77cf-9f22-5c41-b730-ce7f0b972440'}, {'abstract': 'Mark V. Hurd was fired by the board at Hewlett-Packard, but the veracity of a racy lawsuit raises some questions about his ouster at a time when the company was thriving.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/business/in-hps-ouster-of-hurd-a-question-of-truth-or-titillation-common-sense.html', 'snippet': 'Mark V. Hurd was fired by the board at Hewlett-Packard, but the veracity of a racy lawsuit raises some questions about his ouster at a time when the company was thriving.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Ms. Fisher was scared. She was a nervous wreck but attempted to appear relaxed. She sat down on one of two love seats in the sitting room. She was worried when you came over and sat directly next to her and put your arm on the back of the love seat. As you did so, your hand brushed across her breast. ... It happened a second time and Ms. Fisher said ‘you know that you are touching my breast, right?’ You said, ‘Oh, sorry, sorry’ and then laughed it off.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/business/07stewart-pic/07stewart-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/07/business/07stewart-pic/07stewart-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/business/07stewart-pic/07stewart-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In H.P. Tale, a Question of Truth or Titillation', 'kicker': 'Common Sense', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In H.P. Tale, A Question Of Truth Or Titillation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hurd, Mark V', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Jodie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allred, Gloria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hewlett-Packard Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T00:40:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By James B. Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cee73ca3-3698-5def-ba6a-ca631032261f', 'word_count': 1669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cee73ca3-3698-5def-ba6a-ca631032261f'}, {'abstract': 'Mint, a Garden City branch of an Indian restaurant in Manhattan, has a sleek exterior and upscale décor, but the food is uneven.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/nyregion/mint-in-garden-city-has-a-glossy-finish-review.html', 'snippet': 'Mint, a Garden City branch of an Indian restaurant in Manhattan, has a sleek exterior and upscale décor, but the food is uneven.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINT makes a good first impression. The restaurant, a seven-month-old Garden City branch of an Indian restaurant in Manhattan, is a beauty.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08DINELI1/08DINELI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08DINELI1/08DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08DINELI1/08DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Cuisine With a Glossy Finish', 'kicker': 'Long Island Dining | Garden City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indian Cuisine With a Glossy Fi