ns', 'value': 'Zynga Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T01:07:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c23ab58-b012-5977-9fda-f38c63637e7d', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c23ab58-b012-5977-9fda-f38c63637e7d'}, {'abstract': 'Yahoo’s new chief executive, Scott Thompson, is receiving a hefty pay package to join the Internet company, including stock grants worth about $22.5 million and a base annual salary of $1 million.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/big-pay-day-for-yahoos-new-c-e-o/', 'snippet': 'Yahoo’s new chief executive, Scott Thompson, is receiving a hefty pay package to join the Internet company, including stock grants worth about $22.5 million and a base annual salary of $1 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scott Thompson is getting a very friendly welcome to Yahoo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Payday for Yahoo’s New Chief', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Scott', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PayPal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T01:09:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1e88bda-dcfa-5f00-a913-5dd673a16760', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1e88bda-dcfa-5f00-a913-5dd673a16760'}, {'abstract': 'A man who has been convicted three times in the 1992 murder of an 11-year-old baby sitter in suburban Chicago was released from prison on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/us/illinois-inmate-cleared-by-dna-is-freed.html', 'snippet': 'A man who has been convicted three times in the 1992 murder of an 11-year-old baby sitter in suburban Chicago was released from prison on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man who has been convicted three times in the 1992 murder of an 11-year-old baby sitter in suburban Chicago was released from prison on Friday after a local prosecutor decided not to challenge an appellate court’s ruling that reversed the last conviction. The man, Juan Rivera, 39, had been incarcerated at the Stateville Correctional Center in the far southwest suburbs of Chicago. The Lake County state’s attorney, Michael Waller, in a statement defended his office’s prosecution of Mr. Rivera, whose case was featured in an article in The New York Times Magazine. “I am mindful that for Mr. Rivera and some others, this decision will be viewed as too late in coming,” Mr. Waller said. Though there was no physical evidence linking Mr. Rivera to the crime, he was convicted of raping and murdering the baby sitter, Holly Staker, based largely on his confession. In 2005, DNA testing determined that Mr. Rivera was not the source of semen found inside Holly, and he was awarded a new trial, his third. Mr. Rivera was convicted again. In its reversal order last month, the appellate court suggested that Mr. Rivera’s confession was coerced. The investigation into Holly’s murder has been reopened. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: Inmate Cleared by DNA Is Freed', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: Inmate Cleared By DNA Is Freed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivera, Juan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T01:10:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/418ec817-6eb7-50cb-a8e2-e99db22cd69a', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/418ec817-6eb7-50cb-a8e2-e99db22cd69a'}, {'abstract': 'Harry Thomas Jr. pleaded guilty on Friday to charges that he stole from programs receiving federal money and filed a false tax return.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/us/council-member-resigns-and-pleads-guilty.html', 'snippet': 'Harry Thomas Jr. pleaded guilty on Friday to charges that he stole from programs receiving federal money and filed a false tax return.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harry Thomas Jr. pleaded guilty on Friday to charges that he stole from programs receiving federal money and filed a false tax return. Mr. Thomas resigned from the Council of the District of Columbia on Thursday night. Judge John D. Bates of Federal District Court said that Mr. Thomas could spend up to 47 months in prison and that the sentence would determined at a hearing on May 3. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Council Member Resigns and Pleads Guilty ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'District Council Member Resigns and Pleads Guilty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T01:12:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Siddons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siddons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/86175475-4696-50eb-87c9-b866a8399c6f', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86175475-4696-50eb-87c9-b866a8399c6f'}, {'abstract': 'In a high-seas operation mixing diplomacy, drama and Middle Eastern politics, American sailors boarded the mother ship of Somali pirates and freed 13 Iranian hostages who had been captive since November.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/world/middleeast/for-iranians-held-by-pirates-us-to-the-rescue.html', 'snippet': 'In a high-seas operation mixing diplomacy, drama and Middle Eastern politics, American sailors boarded the mother ship of Somali pirates and freed 13 Iranian hostages who had been captive since November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABOARD THE FISHING VESSEL AL MULAHI, in the Gulf of Oman — Senior Iranian military officials this week bluntly warned an American aircraft carrier that it would confront the “full force” of the Iranian military if it tried to re-enter the Persian 