ial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89984add-86f0-56c1-a46e-090947f45787', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89984add-86f0-56c1-a46e-090947f45787'}, {'abstract': 'Fresh from a victory in Iowa and enjoying a lead in the polls, Mitt Romney is nevertheless facing history that suggests New Hampshire is not a done deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/us/politics/front-runner-role-could-thwart-romney-in-new-hampshire.html', 'snippet': 'Fresh from a victory in Iowa and enjoying a lead in the polls, Mitt Romney is nevertheless facing history that suggests New Hampshire is not a done deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TILTON, N.H. — The advantages for Mitt Romney are abundant in the Republican presidential primary here, but there is one obstacle that stands far taller than Rick Santorum, Newt Gingrich or any rival: The inclination of New Hampshire to knock a front-runner down to size.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/us/07romney2-span/07romney2-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/07/us/07romney2-span/07romney2-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/us/07romney2-span/07romney2-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/us/07romney2-span/07romney2-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/us/07romney2-span/07romney2-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Advantages Could Prove Disadvantageous', 'kicker': 'Political Memo', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney Advantages Could Prove Disadvantageous', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T02:51:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e860cd3-c20b-5e1f-9c5d-df56c1513e0c', 'word_count': 1037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e860cd3-c20b-5e1f-9c5d-df56c1513e0c'}, {'abstract': 'Carmelo Anthony had 37 points, including the 3-pointer that gave the Knicks, who blew an 8-point lead down the stretch, the lead for good against Washington with 15.5 seconds left.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/sports/basketball/knicks-avoid-upset-by-winless-wizards.html', 'snippet': 'Carmelo Anthony had 37 points, including the 3-pointer that gave the Knicks, who blew an 8-point lead down the stretch, the lead for good against Washington with 15.5 seconds left.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The desperation was spelled out on the scoreboard, across the Knicks’ bench and finally in their lineup. They were teetering on the edge of disaster before finding momentary salvation from sources both obvious and unexpected.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/sports/jp-knicks/jp-knicks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 660, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/sports/jp-knicks/jp-knicks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/sports/jp-knicks/jp-knicks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shaky Knicks Rally to Keep Wizards Winless', 'kicker': 'Knicks 99, Wizards 96', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shaky Knicks Rally to Keep Wizards Winless', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "Stoudemire, Amar'e", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Wizards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "D'Antoni, Mike", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shumpert, Iman', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wall, John', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T02:52:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2beb7685-190c-510d-9cc8-56d8fc79826e', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2beb7685-190c-510d-9cc8-56d8fc79826e'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of Impressionist works can be seen in “Divided Light and Color: American Impressionist Landscapes” at the Bruce Museum in Greenwich, Conn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/nyregion/american-impressionists-finding-beauty-in-land-review.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of Impressionist works can be seen in “Divided Light and Color: American Impressionist Landscapes” at the Bruce Museum in Greenwich, Conn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans were not in the forefront of advanced art in the 19th century, but they did have one thing going for them: an interest in the novel and innovative. And so they embraced Impressionism — a radical, anti-academic movement at that time, though today it has come to seem like a tasteful and slightly saccharine idiom (think of Thomas Kinkade, the mass-market painter who has trademarked himself as a neo-Impressionist “Painter of Light”). ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08ARTSCT1_SPAN/08ARTSCT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08ARTSCT1_SPAN/08ARTSCT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08ARTSCT1_SPAN/08ARTSCT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 628, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08ARTSCT1_SPAN/08ARTSCT1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08ARTSCT1_SPAN/08ARTSCT1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Beauty in Land', 'kicker': 'Arts | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding Beauty In Land', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bruce Museum of Arts and Science', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T02:53:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7842ede8-174b-5d5c-82d7-70ebba78df29', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7842ede8-174b-5d5c-82d7-70ebba78df29'}, {'abstract': 'Sitting improperly on a subway seat is perhaps the most minor crime for which New Yorkers are routinely arrested.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/nyregion/minor-offense-on-ny-subway-can-bring-ticket-or-handcuffs.html', 'snippet': 'Sitting improperly on a subway seat is perhaps the most minor crime for which New Yorkers are routinely arrested.', 'lead_paragraph': 'William D. Peppers recalled how empty the subway car was. It was not yet 4 a.m. on a Friday, so most of New York was still asleep, but he was already late for his job at a Bronx bakery. As his train passed through Midtown Manhattan, Mr. Peppers stretched out, closed his eyes and nodded off.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/nyregion/SEAT/SEAT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/07/nyregion/SEAT/SEAT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/nyregion/SEAT/SEAT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Relax, if You Want, but Don’t Put Your Feet Up', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bad Manners Then, Cause for Arrest Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T02:57:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein and Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7d3b895-3ec1-5830-9650-036050dd4197', 'word_count': 1387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7d3b895-3ec1-5830-9650-036050dd4197'}, {'abstract': 'One Iraqi, returning to Baghdad after five years, finds his country’s new normal–violence, political crises and uncertainty.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/living-amid-the-violence-in-iraq/', 'snippet': 'One Iraqi, returning to Baghdad after five years, finds his country’s new normal–violence, political crises and uncertainty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The boom and shudder of numerous explosions woke me. It was my first morning in Baghdad in nearly five years, and, coincidentally, only days after the withdrawal of the American troops from Iraq. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Living Amid the Violence in Iraq', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T03:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Razzaq al-Saiedi', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a14c281-350d-5b62-857c-1a486d6109be', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a14c281-350d-5b62-857c-1a486d6109be'}, {'abstract': 'Joe Krozel builds a log cabin with four double-stacked 15-letter entries.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/06/turned/', 'snippet': 'Joe Krozel builds a log cabin with four double-stacked 15-letter entries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY’S PUZZLE — Now that’s a fairly wide open grid, isn’t it? Joe Krozel has used that grid before (Across Lite, Solution, blog), and he’s back today with another 64-word puzzle that builds what looks to me like the beginnings of a log cabin: we have those double stacks of 15’s crossing each other near the edges of the grid. And they are some pretty nifty 15’s, I must say.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saturday: One Whose Head Is Turned', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content