ect', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T03:08:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bc23936-920d-53bf-bd29-e0e32abd96df', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bc23936-920d-53bf-bd29-e0e32abd96df'}, {'abstract': 'After a week in Washington, Representative Michael G. Grimm returns to Staten Island to go to church, work out at the gym and head over to Queens for some of his mother’s pasta.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/nyregion/rep-michael-grimm-recharges-body-and-soul-on-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'After a week in Washington, Representative Michael G. Grimm returns to Staten Island to go to church, work out at the gym and head over to Queens for some of his mother’s pasta.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael G. Grimm, a freshman United States congressman representing Staten Island, has been a Marine, an undercover F.B.I. agent and the owner of a health food restaurant in Manhattan called Healthalicious. After a week in Washington, Mr. Grimm, 41, a Republican, spends his Sundays in the Heartland Village neighborhood of Staten Island, where he lives on the top floor of a multifamily house with his puppy, Sebastian, a Yorkshire terrier. The dog is a regular presence in his office in the Capitol.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE_SPAN/08ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE_SPAN/08ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE_SPAN/08ROUTINE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE_SPAN/08ROUTINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08ROUTINE_SPAN/08ROUTINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recharging Body and Soul', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recharging Body and Soul', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grimm, Michael G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T03:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f98180f9-adf4-5c7e-ad42-59ac87b918d5', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f98180f9-adf4-5c7e-ad42-59ac87b918d5'}, {'abstract': 'Residents were angry about the severity of fine-particle pollution in the capital and the government’s lack of transparency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/world/asia/china-to-release-more-data-on-air-pollution-in-beijing.html', 'snippet': 'Residents were angry about the severity of fine-particle pollution in the capital and the government’s lack of transparency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — China said on Friday that it would begin to publish more detailed air quality data on Beijing later this month, following a public outcry over official government readings that critics said underestimated the severity of the air pollution problem in the smog-filled capital.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China to Release More Data on Air Pollution in Beijing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China to Release More Data On Air Pollution in Beijing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T03:21:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f10e8188-8484-5b99-bd28-f7def92e17f2', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f10e8188-8484-5b99-bd28-f7def92e17f2'}, {'abstract': 'The restaurant Candle 79 was where the psychologist Kelly McGonigal and associates celebrated the publication of “The Willpower Instinct,” her study of self-control.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/nyregion/at-candle-79-an-organic-vegan-book-party.html', 'snippet': 'The restaurant Candle 79 was where the psychologist Kelly McGonigal and associates celebrated the publication of “The Willpower Instinct,” her study of self-control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The urge to eat virtuously is one of those things that come around each January — like cold weather and the Rose Bowl — only, for most people, inevitably to pass. At Candle 79, however, a fine-dining organic vegan restaurant on 79th Street and Lexington Avenue, diners can preserve their culinary purity the year round, with dishes like the seitan piccata with creamed spinach or spaghetti and wheat balls, and drinks from the eco-friendly bar. (Who knew the Maker’s Mark distillery had a low-carbon footprint?) While there were no self-announcing resolution-makers in the crowd the other night, there was — by coincidence — a Stanford University psychologist,  Kelly McGonigal, celebrating the publication of “The Willpower Instinct,” her scientific study on the nature of self-control.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08TABLE_SPAN/08TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08TABLE_SPAN/08TABLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08TABLE_SPAN/08TABLE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08TABLE_SPAN/08TABLE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/nyregion/08TABLE_SPAN/08TABLE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You Say You Made a Resolution', 'kicker': 'At the Table | Candle 79', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You Say You Made a Resolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T03:23:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e176232b-6d2b-5ad1-8730-b11e4f491282', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e176232b-6d2b-5ad1-8730-b11e4f491282'}, {'abstract': 'Big surprise. Some of the Republican presidential candidates are once again using race to pander to the right.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/opinion/blow-the-gops-black-people-platform.html', 'snippet': 'Big surprise. Some of the Republican presidential candidates are once again using race to pander to the right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That didn’t take long.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth':