', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruz, Victor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salsa Dancing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T03:51:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b1d381d-7350-5011-a08a-07057737474b', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b1d381d-7350-5011-a08a-07057737474b'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans in the State Senate moved a “right to work” measure out of committee, and it is expected to pass next week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/us/indiana-right-to-work-measure-expected-to-pass.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans in the State Senate moved a “right to work” measure out of committee, and it is expected to pass next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS — House Democrats brought state lawmaking to a halt in Indiana for much of this week, refusing for a third straight day on Friday to come out to their chamber floor in a procedural effort to stop “right to work” legislation at the center of a mounting battle over unions here. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/us/INDIANA-1/INDIANA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/07/us/INDIANA-1/INDIANA-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargehe