s in New Hampshire since leaving Iowa on Wednesday, fighting for a respectable finish in the top three.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican candidates have, combined, attended dozens of campaign events in New Hampshire since leaving Iowa on Wednesday, fighting for a respectable finish in the top three.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/us/politics/07campaign-slide-6EJ0/07campaign-slide-6EJ0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/07/us/politics/07campaign-slide-6EJ0/07campaign-slide-6EJ0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/us/politics/07campaign-slide-6EJ0/07campaign-slide-6EJ0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/07/us/politics/07campaign-slide-6EJ0/07campaign-slide-6EJ0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/07/us/politics/07campaign-slide-6EJ0/07campaign-slide-6EJ0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Gear Up for New Hampshire Primary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T05:58:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/243dc1dc-f827-5da8-849a-9912d573904f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/243dc1dc-f827-5da8-849a-9912d573904f'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Dickinson, 20, accepted a plea bargain Friday in Vancouver Provincial Court and will be sentenced Feb. 7. His charges include participating in the June 15 riot after the Canucks lost Game 7 of the Stanley Cup finals and breach of recognizance.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/a-conviction-after-vancouver-riot/', 'snippet': 'Ryan Dickinson, 20, accepted a plea bargain Friday in Vancouver Provincial Court and will be sentenced Feb. 7. His charges include participating in the June 15 riot after the Canucks lost Game 7 of the Stanley Cup finals and breach of recognizance...', 'lead_paragraph': 'VANCOUVER, British Columbia — Ryan Dickinson, a 20-year-old from suburban Coquitlam, accepted a plea bargain Friday in Vancouver Provincial Court and will be sentenced Feb. 7. His charges include participating in the June 15 riot after the Canucks lost Game 7 of the Stanley Cup finals and breach of recognizance. He has been in jail since his arrest last month for violating a court-ordered curfew connected with a previous assault charge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conviction After Vancouver Riot', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Canucks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T06:04:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Mackin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41b6e5cf-0841-5744-9457-a9fc89ef0bfb', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41b6e5cf-0841-5744-9457-a9fc89ef0bfb'}, {'abstract': 'Japan said that it will set more stringent age limits on nuclear reactors and require operators to prepare for severe accidents as part of legal changes in the wake of the Fukushima crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/world/asia/japan-new-limits-on-reactors.html', 'snippet': 'Japan said that it will set more stringent age limits on nuclear reactors and require operators to prepare for severe accidents as part of legal changes in the wake of the Fukushima crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Japan said Friday that it will set more stringent age limits on nuclear reactors and require operators to prepare for severe accidents as part of legal changes in the wake of the nuclear crisis at Fukushima. The age limit could also be a step toward fulfilling a government promise to eventually phase out nuclear power in the quake-prone nation. Japan already requires utilities to conduct safety checks on reactors at 30 years, and again at 40 years, to stay in operation. Fresh legislation will set the legal lifespan of reactors at 40 years, though the government will still approve extensions on a case-by-case basis. Excluding the six damaged reactors at the Fukushima Daiichi plant, 13 others in Japan will hit the 40-year limit in the next decade, according to the Ministry of Trade. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan: New Limits on Reactors', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan: New Limits on Reactors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T06:26:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/56849e9b-e296-54f8-af9a-3657a017bdf4', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56849e9b-e296-54f8-af9a-3657a017bdf4'}, {'abstract': 'Lifting a state of martial law in place since 2009 sets the stage for a return to democratic elections in Fiji, but the country’s current leader announced new restrictions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/world/asia/fiji-lifts-martial-law-but-installs-new-regulations.html', 'snippet': 'Lifting a state of martial law in place since 2009 sets the stage for a return to democratic elections in Fiji, but the country’s current leader announced new restrictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SYDNEY, Australia — Fiji’s military rulers on Saturday officially lifted a state of martial law that has been in place since 2009, setting the stage for public deliberations on a new constitution and a promised return to democratic elections within the next two years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_