orden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68532200-b879-54f0-ac97-689b4fa5ad35', 'word_count': 1102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68532200-b879-54f0-ac97-689b4fa5ad35'}, {'abstract': 'The noble idea of limiting the Baseball Hall of Fame to the truly elite is a fantasy as the writers who vote for players continue to wrestle with the residue of the game’s steroids era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/sports/baseball/at-the-hall-of-fame-forgetting-history-and-perhaps-repeating-it.html', 'snippet': 'The noble idea of limiting the Baseball Hall of Fame to the truly elite is a fantasy as the writers who vote for players continue to wrestle with the residue of the game’s steroids era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The noble idea of limiting the Baseball Hall of Fame to the truly elite is a fantasy. Babe Ruth and Willie Mays have plaques in Cooperstown, but so do Rick Ferrell and Jesse Haines. There are no distinctions between members inducted on the first writers’ ballot and those who wait decades for the veterans’ committee. Officially, all are equal.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/sports/YKEPNER/YKEPNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/sports/YKEPNER/YKEPNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/sports/YKEPNER/YKEPNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Hall, Forgetting History and Perhaps Repeating It', 'kicker': 'On Baseball', 'content_kicke