SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Engineered Doomsday', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Engineered Doomsday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Erasmus Medical Center', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T20:18:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2315608-807a-520c-b508-04517e2cd695', 'word_count': 787, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2315608-807a-520c-b508-04517e2cd695'}, {'abstract': 'The American Academy of Pediatrics is warning that a harsh early environment can lay the groundwork for lifelong achievement gaps, health problems and poverty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/opinion/sunday/kristof-a-poverty-solution-that-starts-with-a-hug.html', 'snippet': 'The American Academy of Pediatrics is warning that a harsh early environment can lay the groundwork for lifelong achievement gaps, health problems and poverty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PERHAPS the most widespread peril children face isn’t guns, swimming pools or speeding cars. Rather, scientists are suggesting that it may be “toxic stress” early in life, or even before birth.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/