b5a55699'}, {'abstract': 'Rick Santorum warns that Mitt Romney  was the candidate of the “establishment” and would only perpetuate “the status quo.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/santorum-escalates-attacks-on-romney/', 'snippet': 'Rick Santorum warns that Mitt Romney  was the candidate of the “establishment” and would only perpetuate “the status quo.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' AMHERST, N.H. — In what may have been a preview of Saturday night’s debate, Rick Santorum took several swipes at Mitt Romney by name Saturday, departing from his usual practice of referring to the front-runner only obliquely. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Santorum Escalates Attacks on Romney', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T22:23:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bda4863-c0b9-5a0a-b3bb-641ed19383f9', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bda4863-c0b9-5a0a-b3bb-641ed19383f9'}, {'abstract': 'A Franco-American regiment celebrates the New Year with the president.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/lincolns-french-toast/', 'snippet': 'A Franco-American regiment celebrates the New Year with the president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By January 1862, fighting had quieted down in the East. The troops were in winter quarters, and the new Union commander, Gen. George McClellan, was sick with typhoid fever. Only President Lincoln seemed to be champing at the bit for action. The day after Christmas he had ordered Gen. Ambrose Burnside “to be off at once.” Exactly where Burnside was to go, Lincoln didn’t say, so everyone stayed put.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln’s French Toast', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T22:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By James H. Johnston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Johnston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8123903c-10b8-53fe-a04d-198da8c01a08', 'word_count': 1324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8123903c-10b8-53fe-a04d-198da8c01a08'}, {'abstract': 'The stock market went on a roller-coaster ride in 2011, plunging in the third quarter and surging in the fourth, to end about where it started. For mutual fund investors, the volatility may not end.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/business/mutfund/for-mutual-fund-investors-a-bright-end-to-a-murky-year.html', 'snippet': 'The stock market went on a roller-coaster ride in 2011, plunging in the third quarter and surging in the fourth, to end about where it started. For mutual fund investors, the volatility may not end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO said making money was supposed to be fun?', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/business/08-MFQ-Lede-Cover/08-MFQ-Lede-Cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 891, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/business/08-MFQ-Lede-Cover/08-MFQ-Lede-Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/business/08-MFQ-Lede-Cover/08-MFQ-Lede-Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'That Bright Light May Be Deceiving', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That Bright Light May Be Deceiving', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T22:38:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Mutual Funds', 'byline': {'original': 'By Conrad De Aenlle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Conrad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'De Aenlle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7da253d-7811-519a-b7ac-70a152134440', 'word_count': 1248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7da253d-7811-519a-b7ac-70a152134440'}, {'abstract': 'After their ship was taken hostage at gunpoint, Iranian fishermen survived six weeks by relying on calm nerves, prayer, camaraderie and, in the end, duplicity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/world/middleeast/iranians-tell-of-six-weeks-of-fear-with-somali-pirates.html', 'snippet': 'After their ship was taken hostage at gunpoint, Iranian fishermen survived six weeks by relying on calm nerves, prayer, camaraderie and, in the end, duplicity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABOARD THE FISHING VESSEL AL MULAHI, in the Gulf of Oman — Late on Thursday afternoon, as the American destroyer Kidd loomed alongside this hijacked Iranian dhow, the warship’s loudspeaker issued a command in Urdu to the dhow’s frightened Urdu-speaking crew. American sailors stood ready, weapons in hand. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/world/08pirate-span/08pirate-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/world/08pirate-span/08pirate-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/world/08pirate-span/pirate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/world/08pirate-span/08pirate-span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/world/08pirate-span/08pirate-span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bold Lie Turns Run-In at Sea Into Dramatic Rescue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bold Lie Turns High-Seas Run-In Into Dramatic Rescue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Oman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Piracy at Sea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T22:42:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08ee35bb-ddf4-5416-bca6-f71abbb650b7', 'word_count': 1933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08ee35bb-ddf4-5416-bca6-f71abbb650b7'}, {'abstract': 'Regulators and mutual fund executives differ on the stability of money market funds since the financial crisis. The S.E.C. is expected to soon propose more changes in the industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/business/mutfund/money-market-funds-may-soon-face-more-changes.html', 'snippet': 'Regulators and mutual fund executives differ on the stability of money market funds since the financial crisis. The S.E.C. is expected to soon propose more changes in the industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS Europe was lurching from crisis to crisis in late October, a Norwegian lender — a $40 billion bank with a strong credit rating, four blue-chip owners and a 50-year track record — abruptly stumbled.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/0