pportunity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/business/mutfund/as-asia-slows-down-investors-may-still-want-to-dive-in.html', 'snippet': 'After Asian stocks underperformed other markets late last year, some investment advisers see a buying opportunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE European credit crisis has dominated the headlines, but the biggest reaction to shaky global economic and financial conditions has been in Asia. Stock markets there — and funds investing in them — trailed other major regions during the fourth quarter of 2011. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/business/08-MFQ-EMERGE1/08-MFQ-EMERGE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/business/08-MFQ-EMERGE1/08-MFQ-EMERGE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/business/08-MFQ-EMERGE1/08-MFQ-EMERGE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Slower Growth in Asia May Yield Bargains', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slower Growth in Asia May Yield Bargains', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T23:12:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Mutual Funds', 'byline': {'original': 'By Conrad De Aenlle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Conrad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'De Aenlle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92c1d07a-7615-5299-a45a-ab001d959910', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92c1d07a-7615-5299-a45a-ab001d959910'}, {'abstract': 'Managers of three of the fourth quarter’s better-performing mutual funds found winners in a variety of places.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/business/mutfund/three-mutual-funds-at-the-front-of-a-late-2011-rally.html', 'snippet': 'Managers of three of the fourth quarter’s better-performing mutual funds found winners in a variety of places.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Standard & Poor’s 500-stock index returned nothing in 2011, but a lost year overshadowed a late rally. Managers of three of the fourth quarter’s better-performing mutual funds found winners in such varied places as small-capitalization stocks, auto parts retailers and aerospace companies. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/business/08-MFQ-TOP3/08-MFQ-TOP3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/08/business/08-MFQ-TOP3/08-MFQ-TOP3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/business/08-MFQ-TOP3/08-MFQ-TOP3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Three Funds, a Front-Row Seat on a Rally', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Three Funds, a Front-Row Seat to a Fourth-Quarter Rally', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutua