m/2012/01/07/dempsey-scores-hat-trick-in-fulhams-f-a-cup-win/', 'snippet': 'Fulham’s Clint Dempsey scored a hat trick, Aston Villa’s Brad Guzan saved a penalty kick and Everton’s Landon Donovan had an assist in a big day for American players in England.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fulham’s Clint Dempsey scored a hat trick, Aston Villa’s Brad Guzan saved a penalty kick in injury time and Landon Donovan had an assist on Everton’s opening goal in a memorable day for American players in England. All three were playing matches in the F.A. Cup, as the Premier League — and the rest of England — took a break from league play for a weekend of matches in the world’s oldest domestic cup competition. For more, read our soccer roundup here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dempsey Scores Hat Trick in Fulham’s F.A. Cup Win', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Clint', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T23:47:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa416b1c-332e-55ef-aa48-10f74f1440c0', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa416b1c-332e-55ef-aa48-10f74f1440c0'}, {'abstract': 'In the Legislature’s annual two-month session, opening this week, the Senate is to take up a bill asking voters to decide on gambling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/us/politics/in-florida-lawmakers-consider-gambling-bill.html', 'snippet': 'In the Legislature’s annual two-month session, opening this week, the Senate is to take up a bill asking voters to decide on gambling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — As the Florida Legislature sprints into action on Tuesday for its annual two-month session, lawmakers will face the politically volatile task of redrawing the electoral map (sure to attract a court challenge) and devising new ways to plug a $2 billion deficit in the state budget.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/us/SUB-FLORIDA/SUB-FLORIDA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Florida, Lawmakers Consider Gambling Bill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Florida, Lawmakers Consider Gambling Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rich, Nan H', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T23:51:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fccf7911-7f5e-516d-9744-263aa79abe82', 'word_count': 1232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fccf7911-7f5e-516d-9744-263aa79abe82'}, {'abstract': 'Charles Haley was frequently described as talented but troubled. Specific instances of his bizarre behavior have been well established. On the field, however, Haley was a Hall of Famer.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/07/a-vote-for-charles-haley-pick-your-hall-of-famers/', 'snippet': 'Charles Haley was frequently described as talented but troubled. Specific instances of his bizarre behavior have been well established. On the field, however, Haley was a Hall of Famer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pro Football Hall of Fame selection committee has narrowed the list of 26 semifinalists to the group of 15 modern-era finalists who will be considered for the class of 2012. The list is at the bottom of this post. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vote for Charles Haley; Pick Your Hall of Famers', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Halls of Fame', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haley, Charles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-07T23:52:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Barall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/130f4e28-c6cd-54b5-969e-e05f92986aad', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/130f4e28-c6cd-54b5-969e-e05f92986aad'}, {'abstract': 'To many Republicans and some scholars, President Obama’s decision to sidestep Senate confirmation for several appointees risked ending the Senate’s right to give advice and consent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/us/politics/experts-say-obamas-recess-appointments-could-signify-end-to-a-senate-role.html', 'snippet': 'To many Republicans and some scholars, President Obama’s decision to sidestep Senate confirmation for several appointees risked ending the Senate’s right to give advice and consent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — To many Republicans and some constitutional scholars, President Obama’s decision last week to ignore a sitting Senate and sidestep the confirmation process for several appointees risked nothing short of an end to the Senate’s role of providing advice and consent on presidential appointments.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/business/CONFIRM/CONFIRM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Appointments Challenge Senate Role, Experts Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Appointments Challenge Senate Role, Experts Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T00:07:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ac62a72-0819-5f6c-b3d5-d521818ef478', 'word_count': 1236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ac62a72-0819-5f6c-b3d5-d521818ef478'}, {'abstract': 'Iraq’s security forces have been parading detainees before television cameras and airing their confessions to show they are cracking down on terrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/world/middleeast/iraq-turns-justice-into-a-show-and-terror-confessions-a-script.html', 'snippet': 'Iraq’s security forces have been parading detainees before television cameras and airing their confessions to show they are cracking down on terrorism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — The cameras were rolling and the reporters were ready inside the auditorium, so the Iraqi police officer gave the signal: Bring in the prisoners. In they shuffled, 21 men accused of terrorism and murder, hands shackled, eyes tracing the floor. This was no day in court. Today, they were lined up to meet the press. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/world/jp-iraq/jp-iraq-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/world/jp-iraq/jp-iraq-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/world/jp-iraq/jp-iraq-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq Turns Justice Into a Show, and Terror Confessions a Script', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq Turns Justice Into a S