om/2012/01/08/us/mel-and-gary-panter-have-a-father-and-son-art-exhibition-in-sulphur-springs.html', 'snippet': 'Mel Panter is an artist who paints noble cowboys. Gary Panter, his son, is the guy who created the look for “Pee-wee’s Playhouse.” And now they have a two-man hometown exhibition in Sulphur Springs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SULPHUR SPRINGS — It was a perfect family moment for Gary Panter — the punk visionary, underground comics master and “Pee-wee’s Playhouse” set designer — and his father, Mel. The son’s culture-bending Day-Glo artwork was displayed in a small-town gallery in Northeast Texas alongside his father’s oils of iconic Texana.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/us/08TTCULTURE/08TTCULTURE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/us/08TTCULTURE/08TTCULTURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/us/08TTCULTURE/08TTCULTURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Day-Glo Meets Cowboys in Father-Son Art Show', 'kicker': 'Texas Monthly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Day-Glo Meets Cowboys in Father-Son Art Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panter, Gary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T00:45:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lee Hancock', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lee', 'middlename':