 They are comrades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/business/global/germany-resists-europes-pleas-to-spend-more.html', 'snippet': 'In Berlin, there is a deep consensus among policy makers and economists — bordering on orthodoxy — that austerity and growth are not enemies. They are comrades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — Spain, Italy and Greece are taking a knife to public spending because they have no choice. But Germany is still healthy enough that it could do its troubled trading partners a favor and focus more on promoting demand and less on cutting debt.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/world/europe/08hawks/08hawks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/world/europe/08hawks/08hawks-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/world/europe/08hawks/08hawks-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': "Germany Resists Europe's Pleas to Spend More", 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Europe’s Pleas, Germany Resists Spending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weidmann, Jens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bundesbank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}