f Susan Sontag’s journals and stars in “Sontag: Reborn,” a Builders Association production at the Public Theater, part of the Under the Radar festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Susan Sontag of the skunk-striped hair and the illustrious reputation as a public figure looks back on another Susan Sontag, a precocious but insecure young woman hungering for experience, in “Sontag: Reborn,” a touching, exquisitely rendered portrait of the artist (and thinker) in the process of self-creation at the Public Theater as part of the Under the Radar festival.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/sontag/sontag-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/sontag/sontag-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/sontag/sontag-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/sontag/sontag-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/sontag/sontag-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Life, Mediated in a Journal, by a Writer Busy Being Born', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Sontag: Reborn'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Life, Mediated in a Journal, By a Writer Busy Being Born', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sontag, Susan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weems, Marianne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Under the Radar Festival', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T21:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2028ad35-f444-5312-a9cf-bea83a4d2c7a', 'word_count': 1102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2028ad35-f444-5312-a9cf-bea83a4d2c7a'}, {'abstract': 'If not for a luxury cruise ship that failed to reach her destination on her maiden voyage in 1912, many New Yorkers would be remembering the epic and icy conflagration that engulfed and encased a tower in Lower Manhattan earlier that same year.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/consumed-in-fire-cloaked-in-ice-equitables-headquarters-fell-100-years-ago/', 'snippet': 'If not for a luxury cruise ship that failed to reach her destination on her maiden voyage in 1912, many New Yorkers would be remembering the epic and icy conflagration that engulfed and encased a tower in Lower Manhattan earlier that same year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If that enormous White Star liner had made port on her maiden voyage that year, 1912 would probably have been known by generations of New Yorkers as the year of the great Equitable disaster.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Consumed in Fire, Cloaked in Ice, Equitable’s Headquarters Fell 100 Years Ago', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 's