s', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e1b8141-ac3e-5edc-a042-db64f3c0c029', 'word_count': 1032, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e1b8141-ac3e-5edc-a042-db64f3c0c029'}, {'abstract': 'Clients of NMA, also known as Norm Marshall & Associates, include General Motors, Heineken, Puma and the Xbox unit of Microsoft.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/business/media/corbis-to-acquire-nma-group.html', 'snippet': 'Clients of NMA, also known as Norm Marshall & Associates, include General Motors, Heineken, Puma and the Xbox unit of Microsoft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Corbis, the digital media company owned by Bill Gates that licenses the intellectual property rights to photographs, music and public personalities, is expanding again by acquiring the NMA Group in Los Angeles, a pioneer in the realm of branded entertainment, which helps marketers weave products into the plots of movies and television shows.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09SUBproduct/09SUBproduct-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 736, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09SUBproduct/09SUBproduct-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09SUBproduct/09SUBproduct-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Corbis to Acquire NMA Group', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_he