r overcome her industry inexperience, and the company is now said to be seeking her replacement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — About a year ago, a team of Disney movie executives traveled to rural Britain to visit Steven Spielberg’s “War Horse” set. Mud and manure greeted them. But knowing that film sets are usually filthy and suspecting this one might be particularly so, the group arrived in grungy clothes and work boots.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09jpcarney/09jpcarney-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09jpcarney/09jpcarney-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09jpcarney/09jpcarney-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09jpcarney/09jpcarney-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09jpcarney/09jpcarney-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Hollywood’s Clubby Culture, a Disney Marketer’s Rapid Downfall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Disney Marketer’s Downfall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DreamWorks Studios', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pixar Animation Studios', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T22:47:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3336d6f3-7d28-5de8-bdb1-84b9c8c9f70b', 'word_count': 1361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3336d6f3-7d28-5de8-bdb1-84b9c8c9f70b'}, {'abstract': 'Just resting.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/not-dead-yet/', 'snippet': 'Just resting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I did warn readers of a likely gap in blogging; it got longer than I expected as stuff fell in on me. On my way home from Chicago, and normal blogging should resume tomorrow.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Dead Yet', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T22:52:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bde483e-465d-5da4-a1fa-b6a2a8639099', 'word_count': 41, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bde483e-465d-5da4-a1fa-b6a2a8639099'}, {'abstract': 'The Round Robin Teams top bracket played on Dec. 30, the last day of the Edgar Kaplan Winter Regional in Manhattan, was won by two married couples.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/crosswords/bridge/round-robin-teams-at-edgar-kaplan-winter-regional-bridge.html', 'snippet': 'The Round Robin Teams top bracket played on Dec. 30, the last day of the Edgar Kaplan Winter Regional in Manhattan, was won by two married couples.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Round Robin Teams top bracket played on Dec. 30, the last day of the Edgar Kaplan Winter Regional in Manhattan, was won by two married couples: Steve and Rona Levine of New York City, and Ralph and Gloria Tamlyn of Larchmont, N.Y.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keen Evaluation Ends in Slam', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keen Evaluation Ends in Slam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T22:52:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f663f10-8d6e-5475-8b8f-b6dfe28d69a1', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f663f10-8d6e-5475-8b8f-b6dfe28d69a1'}, {'abstract': 'Glen Campbell, who has Alzheimer’s disease, performed at Town Hall as part of his “Goodbye Tour.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/arts/music/glen-campbells-goodbye-tour-at-town-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'Glen Campbell, who has Alzheimer’s disease, performed at Town Hall as part of his “Goodbye Tour.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last June, Glen Campbell announced that he had Alzheimer’s disease, and on Saturday night he came to Town Hall as part of what was billed as the “Goodbye Tour.” Everyone in the room understood. The faithful, reverent crowd appeared not to mind that for much of the show Mr. Campbell was reading lyrics from prompters that had been set between the monitors at the foot of the stage. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/campbell/campbell-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 806, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/campbell/campbell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/campbell/campbell-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Campbell Says Goodbye With Sparkle and Guitar', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Campbell Says Goodbye With Sparkle and Guitar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, Glen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T22:56:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/35dbf76d-128d-59ae-b942-752c8739ef1c', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35dbf76d-128d-59ae-b942-752c8739ef1c'}, {'abstract': 'In “Takes” the choreographer Nichole Canuso and the multimedia artist Lars Jan combine dance and cinema in a piece where the action occurs within a transparent cube.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/arts/dance/nichole-canuso-dance-company-in-takes-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Takes” the choreographer Nichole Canuso and the multimedia artist Lars Jan combine dance and cinema in a piece where the action occurs within a transparent cube.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many couples, the two people in Nichole Canuso’s “Takes” seem trapped together, trapped by each other and the past. In their case the enclosure is literal: a cube the size of a small room. Its walls are made of a fabric gauzy enough to see through but substantial enough to serve as screens for live video of the dancers inside. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/take/take-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1017, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/take/take-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/take/take-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Couple’s Intimate Rotations While Surrounded on All Sides', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Couple’s Intimate Rotations While Surrounded on All Sides', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Canuso, Nichole', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T22:58:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/504a407e-d7ed-505e-9e9e-5e76b63c70ed', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/504a407e-d7ed-505e-9e9e-5e76b63c70ed'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Dewey makes an avian-able debut.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/better/', 'snippet': 'Michael Dewey makes an avian-able debut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — Interesting. You would think a simple, clean theme like this had been done before, but in this debut by Michael Dewey, it seems as if the theme entries are appearing for the first time in The New York Times. It’s possible that similar, avian-themed grids have appeared in other newspapers, but not here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday: Better-Than-You Type', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T23:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9f0445b-5854-59dd-8a76-ced2b2567ee4', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9f0445b-5854-59dd-8a76-ced2b2567ee4'}, {'abstract': 'The ATS will be offered with three powertrain choices, two transmissions and an optional Borg Warner all-wheel-drive system.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/cadillac-spells-its-bmw-3-series-fighter-a-t-s-2/', 'snippet': 'The ATS will be offered with three powertrain choices, two transmissions and an optional Borg Warner all-wheel-drive system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Introduced on Sunday, Jan. 8: 2013 Cadillac ATS.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cadillac Spells Its BMW 3 Series Fighter ATS', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cadillac Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T23:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48629936-f428-58dd-a54e-e7a15ecc8649', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48629936-f428-58dd-a54e-e7a15ecc8649'}, {'abstract': 'Winter Jazzfest, about 60 performances over Friday and Saturday, did what it has been doing since 2005: pushing new groups and their music into visibility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/arts/music/winter-jazzfest-with-herculaneum-and-erimaj-review.html', 'snippet': 'Winter Jazzfest, about 60 performances over Friday and Saturday, did what it has been doing since 2005: pushing new groups and their music into visibility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At best, Winter Jazzfest is an extraordinary thing. It’s a significant jazz festival, not tied to any cultural institution. And it doesn’t rely on the names that would fill Carnegie Hall or Rose Theater, but on those that make up the music’s daily life, chosen with discernment and advocacy. That’s inspired.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/jazz-1/jazz-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 762, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/jazz-1/jazz-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/jazz-1/jazz-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ear-Openers: New Sounds, No Dogma', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ear-Openers: New Sounds, No Dogma', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Village (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Winter Jazzfest', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T23:02:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6be9aed6-b869-5425-9eb9-11534161f0fa', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6be9aed6-b869-5425-9eb9-11534161f0fa'}, {'abstract': 'A super PAC plans to attack Mitt Romney’s work with the private equity firm Bain Capital, using clips from an anti-Romney film and money from the casino mogul Sheldon Adelson.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/us/politics/pro-gingrich-pac-plans-tv-ads-against-romney.html', 'snippet': 'A super PAC plans to attack Mitt Romney’s work with the private equity firm Bain Capital, using clips from an anti-Romney film and money from the casino mogul Sheldon Adelson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Thanks to a $5 million donation from a wealthy casino owner, a group supporting Newt Gingrich plans to place advertisements in South Carolina this week attacking Mitt Romney as a predatory capitalist who destroyed jobs and communities, a full-scale Republican assault on Mr. Romney’s business background.\xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/us/GINGRICH-1/GINGRICH-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/us/GINGRICH-1/GINGRICH-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/09/us/GINGRICH-1/GINGRICH-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'PAC Ads to Attack Romney as Predatory Capitalist', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'PAC Ads to Hit Romney’s Role At Equity Firm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T23:08:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel and Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e405d93d-e4fa-5db7-8537-d517e82f9d8f', 'word_count': 1252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e405d93d-e4fa-5db7-8537-d517e82f9d8f'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re a Giants fan who is planning to make the trip to Wisconsin this week, or know someone who is, we’d like to talk with you.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/seeking-traveling-giants-fans/', 'snippet': 'If you’re a Giants fan who is planning to make the trip to Wisconsin this week, or know someone who is, we’d like to talk with you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After Sunday’s dismantling of the Falcons, the Giants now head on the road for a meeting with Aaron Rodgers and the defending Super Bowl champion Green Bay Packers. If you’re a Giants fan who is planning to make the trip to Wisconsin this week, or know someone who is, we’d like to talk with you. Reach out to us in the comments field below, and we’ll contact you by e-mail. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking Traveling Giants Fans', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T23:09:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bef58ccd-faad-5516-bd17-a9ea972d9b3c', 'word_count': 71, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bef58ccd-faad-5516-bd17-a9ea972d9b3c'}, {'abstract': 'South Sudan is only a few months old, and two members of its upstart press corps have already been briefly jailed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/business/media/in-south-sudan-a-rough-start-to-press-freedom.html', 'snippet': 'South Sudan is only a few months old, and two members of its upstart press corps have already been briefly jailed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a thatched hut in Juba, the capital of South Sudan, about 10 young men and women sat on lawn chairs made of brown plastic. They loudly typed on the computer keyboards on the tables in front of them. Two fans were blowing heavily. But the loud humming, which turned all speaking in the room into yelling, didn’t come from them. It came from the backyard, and when it suddenly stopped, the young people saved their work. Minutes later their screens turned dark.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09citizen1/09citizen1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09citizen1/09citizen1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09citizen1/09citizen1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09citizen1/09citizen1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/09/business/09citizen1/09citizen1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Fledgling Country, Perils for the Press', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Fledgling Country, Perils for the Press', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sudan People's Liberation Army", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T23:10:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benno Muchler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benno', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Muchler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16e7fa59-9a07-5b3a-af4b-17c2ea9fd215', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16e7fa59-9a07-5b3a-af4b-17c2ea9fd215'}, {'abstract': 'The Preservation Hall Jazz Band celebrated the New Orleans hall’s 50th anniversary at Carnegie Hall on Saturday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/arts/music/preservation-hall-jazz-band-at-carnegie-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Preservation Hall Jazz Band celebrated the New Orleans hall’s 50th anniversary at Carnegie Hall on Saturday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Preservation Hall Jazz Band, a quintessential New Orleans institution, discovered new out-of-town admirers after Hurricane Katrina, and it brought many of them along for a concert on Saturday night at Carnegie Hall to celebrate its 50th anniversary.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/09preservation-web/09preservation-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/09preservation-web/09preservation-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/arts/09preservation-web/09preservation-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Tribute to New Orleans Institution, Baton Is Passed to New Fans', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Tribute to New Orleans Institution, Baton Is Passed to New Fans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Preservation Hall Jazz Band', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T23:13:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/41ee485a-83f5-5751-a3a6-44bfce34a3df', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41ee485a-83f5-5751-a3a6-44bfce34a3df'}, {'abstract': 'The first half of the Denver Broncos’ playoff game against the Pittsburgh Steelers on Sunday was Tim Tebow’s career in a nutshell.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/08/tim-tebow-is-no-good-except-for-when-hes-great/', 'snippet': 'The first half of the Denver Broncos’ playoff game against the Pittsburgh Steelers on Sunday was Tim Tebow’s career in a nutshell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first half of the Denver Broncos’ A.F.C. playoff game against the Pittsburgh Steelers on Sunday was Tim Tebow’s career in a nutshell. In the first quarter, he couldn’t do anything — going three-and-out on two possessions, including one on which Denver actually went backward.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tim Tebow Is No Good. Except for When He’s Great.', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-08T23:23:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f763aa20-271a-5060-926a-dee01dd407ec', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f763aa20-271a-5060-926a-dee01dd407ec'}, {'abstract': 'Influenced by cable and the Internet, the network news divisions of ABC, CBS and NBC have shifted the focus to differentiating their nightly shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/business/media/at-abc-cbs-and-nbc-news-accentuating-the-differences.html', 'snippet': 'Influenced by cable and the Internet, the network news divisions of ABC, CBS and NBC have shifted the focus to differentiating their nightly shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a time when each of the Big Three nightly newscasts on American television tended to open with the same story — the latest campaign speech, a new government study or perhaps a big snowstorm. That time is gone. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/business/media/09networks-1/09networks-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 260, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/08/business/media/09networks-1/09networks-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/08/business/media/09networks-1/09networks-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Three Newscasts Are Changing the State of Play', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Changing the State of Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Brian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenstiel, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelley, Scott', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC News', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS News', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Project for Excellence in Journalism', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC News', 'ran