ec-2fa9a1b18ffd'}, {'abstract': 'The oversight panel of the Basel Committee on Banking Supervision said that the rule did not mean banks would never be allowed to dip below required levels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/business/bank-regulators-to-allow-leeway-on-liquidity-rule.html', 'snippet': 'The oversight panel of the Basel Committee on Banking Supervision said that the rule did not mean banks would never be allowed to dip below required levels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the financial crisis, regulators have been pushing big banks to increase capital and ensure short-term liquidity, a move aimed at avoiding the cash flow troubles that brought the financial system to the brink of disaster in 2008.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bank Regulators to Allow Leeway on Liquidity Rule', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bank Regulators To Allow Leeway On Capital Rule', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Basel Committee on Banking Supervision', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T00:43:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96b6c224-c924-5fa5-bc21-648b1515f88e', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96b6c224-c924-5fa5-bc21-648b1515f88e'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich’s wooing of The New Hampshire Union Leader secured one of the most coveted endorsements of the presidential election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/us/politics/the-union-leader-in-nh-backs-gingrich-tears-down-his-rivals.html', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich’s wooing of The New Hampshire Union Leader secured one of the most coveted endorsements of the presidential election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Newt Gingrich may not have much money to spend on advertising here. But he does have Joseph W. McQuaid, the publisher of New Hampshire’s largest newspaper, The Union Leader. And Mr. McQuaid will happily spill barrel after barrel of ink trying to tear every other candidate down.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/us/LEADER/LEADER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 702, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In New Hampshire Newspaper, Gingrich Gets Coveted and Ferocious Supporter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In New Hampshire Newspaper, Gingrich Gets Coveted and Ferocious Supporter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQuaid, Joseph W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Hampshire Union Leader', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T00:47:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed2cfa3f-8132-53ea-a780-532c6b03ebd8', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed2cfa3f-8132-53ea-a780-532c6b03ebd8'}, {'abstract': 'Keven Joseph Davis, who was brought in by the father of Venus and Serena Williams when they were girls to aid in the development of their careers, died Dec. 23 at 54.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/sports/tennis/keven-davis-helped-venus-and-serena-williams-reach-top.html', 'snippet': 'Keven Joseph Davis, who was brought in by the father of Venus and Serena Williams when they were girls to aid in the development of their careers, died Dec. 23 at 54.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Dec. 21, 2000, Venus Williams stood before a throng of reporters who had come to record another first. Reebok was signing her to the largest endorsement contract signed by a female athlete: five years, $40 million.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/sports/subYRHODEN/subYRHODEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/09/sports/subYRHODEN/subYRHODEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/sports/subYRHODEN/subYRHODEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/sports/subYRHODEN/subYRHODEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subTyp