n. 12 disaster, this is what you see:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haiti’s Slow Recovery', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Haiti’s Slow Recovery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martelly, Michel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interim Haiti Recovery Commission', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T02:38:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a287caa2-1443-5fd9-992a-5f3659c98ab7', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a287caa2-1443-5fd9-992a-5f3659c98ab7'}, {'abstract': 'An Idaho couple’s fight with the Environmental Protection Agency could undermine environmental controls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/opinion/the-sacketts-and-the-clean-water-act.html', 'snippet': 'An Idaho couple’s fight with the Environmental Protection Agency could undermine environmental controls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chantell and Michael Sackett’s case against the Environmental Protection Agency before the Supreme Court on Monday might appear to be David versus Goliath. But those supporting the Sacketts with friend-of-the-court briefs are corporate Goliaths like General Electric and real estate developers eager to weaken the E.P.A.’s ability to protect wetlands and waterways under the federal Clean Water Act. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sacketts and the Clean Water Act', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sacketts and the Clean Water Act', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Water Act', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Idaho', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T02:39:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8030b485-2e85-5e17-989f-f03248f398c6', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8030b485-2e85-5e17-989f-f03248f398c6'}, {'abstract': 'A leader of the Muslim Brotherhood’s political party said it had decided to support keeping the military-appointed cabinet and prime minister in place for six months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/world/middleeast/muslim-brotherhood-backs-egyptian-militarys-transition-date.html', 'snippet': 'A leader of the Muslim Brotherhood’s political party said it had decided to support keeping the military-appointed cabinet and prime minister in place for six months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Poised to dominate the new Parliament here, Egypt’s largest Islamist group is putting off an expected confrontation with Egypt’s military rulers, keeping its distance from more radical Islamist parties and hoping that the United States will continue to support the country financially, a top leader of the group’s political arm said Sunday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Islamists in Egypt Back Timing of Military Handover', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Islamists In Egypt Back Date Of Handover', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T02:39:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddc8b313-d5ed-5d63-8ae4-54661a0e424f', 'word_count': 1170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddc8b313-d5ed-5d63-8ae4-54661a0e424f'}, {'abstract': 'Voters should not be fooled. The assault on women’s reproductive health is a central part of the Republican agenda.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/opinion/republicans-versus-reproductive-rights.html', 'snippet': 'Voters should not be fooled. The assault on women’s reproductive health is a central part of the Republican agenda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Iowa, the Republican presidential contenders tried to outdo one another in attacking reproductive rights as they sought the support of caucusgoers from the religious right. In New Hampshire, where voters are less socially conservative, the candidates have focused more on economic issues. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Versus Reproductive Rights', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Republicans Versus Reproductive Rights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T02:40:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cab1912b-d846-571a-8066-f81df30ac33e', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cab1912b-d846-571a-8066-f81df30ac33e'}, {'abstract': 'This year commuting tax benefits will get better for drivers, while the deal for those who take trains or buses will get worse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/opinion/second-class-commuters.html', 'snippet': 'This year commuting tax benefits will get better for drivers, while the deal for those who take trains or buses will get worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year, more than 2.7 million of the nation’s commuters will have to pay an additional $550 in taxes, thanks