, 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/building-an-archive-from-the-rubble/', 'snippet': 'Larry Racioppo’s bosses didn’t want pretty pictures — they wanted to show how bad the city’s housing stock was. He delivered, documenting how the city’s housing agency rebuilt entire neighborhoods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1989, Larry Racioppo got his first regular job in years: taking pictures showing New York City at its worst. He spent his days stepping through dank basement crack dens and apartments that were as burned-out as their inhabitants. On rooftops, spent shell casings littered the tar like fallen leaves. At street level, entire neighborhoods had been reduced to empty lots.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Building an Archive From the Rubble', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T10:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91d12685-b744-50d4-862e-a25cdd163542', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91d12685-b744-50d4-862e-a25cdd163542'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors investigated an allegation that a former chairman of President Lee Myung-bak’s ruling Grand National Party tried to buy votes in a party leadership race.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/world/asia/south-korea-investigates-vote-buying-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors investigated an allegation that a former chairman of President Lee Myung-bak’s ruling Grand National Party tried to buy votes in a party leadership race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — President Lee Myung-bak’s ruling Grand National Party faced a growing crisis on Monday as prosecutors investigated an allegation from a whistle-blowing lawmaker that one of its former chairmen tried to buy votes in a party leadership race .', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Korea Investigates Vote-Buying Scandal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Korea: Accused of Vote Buying, Lawmaker Is Urged to Resign', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T10:04:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/033b7997-d1d2-5393-9693-cb576fe20a46', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/033b7997-d1d2-5393-9693-cb576fe20a46'}, {'abstract': '6 Q’s About the News | How is a kinetic artist using “useless machines” to capture the imagination of millions of YouTube viewers?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/a-frenetic-burst-of-organized-chaos/', 'snippet': '6 Q’s About the News | How is a kinetic artist using “useless machines” to capture the imagination of millions of YouTube viewers?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO is Joseph Herscher? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘A Frenetic Burst of Organized Chaos’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T10:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c9dd06b-da53-54fd-a2f1-1017d0540e87', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c9dd06b-da53-54fd-a2f1-1017d0540e87'}, {'abstract': 'Cumbersome process makes it hard for India’s 10 million overseas citizens to vote.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/why-nris-are-also-nvis-non-voting-indians/', 'snippet': 'Cumbersome process makes it hard for India’s 10 million overseas citizens to vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, Indian Prime Minister Manmohan Singh reminded his country’s 10 million non-resident citizens that they can vote in elections under a law passed in 2010. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why NRIs Are Also NVIs (Non Voting Indians)', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singh, Manmohan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Times of India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T10:43:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None