ways to make iPhones even more child-friendly,  prostate cancer screenings show no benefit and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Web Sites for 2012 Travel Savings', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T14:31:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b37b03b-e781-5044-b48c-5aa7c33ec611', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b37b03b-e781-5044-b48c-5aa7c33ec611'}, {'abstract': 'The men’s basketball team at Fordham caught a hot hand when a Jewish cantor named Daniel Pincus  began singing “The Star-Spangled Banner” before games.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/at-jesuit-school-a-pregame-assist-from-a-jewish-singer/', 'snippet': 'The men’s basketball team at Fordham caught a hot hand when a Jewish cantor named Daniel Pincus  began singing “The Star-Spangled Banner” before games.', 'lead_paragraph': ' If you’re hoping for a talisman to improve your team’s chances of victory, why not make it a man with a talis? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Jesuit School, a Pregame Assist From a Jewish Singer', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject'