.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/eavesdropping-on-social-quail/', 'snippet': 'Quail are highly social, calling to one another throughout the day — a possible adaptation to living in high-density populations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jennifer Gee, a biologist at the Claremont University Consortium and the University of California, Riverside, writes from the tropical dry forest near Álamos, Mexico, where she and Jennifer Calkins are studying Callipepla quail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eavesdropping on Social Quail', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T14:52:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Gee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca1b96e5-3ea0-5098-8a24-dbea9253eb8c', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca1b96e5-3ea0-5098-8a24-dbea9253eb8c'}, {'abstract': 'Several announcements of a new Google TV are expected at the International Consumer Electronics Show, involving LG Electronics, Sony, Samsung and Vizio.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/google-tv-tries-again/', 'snippet': 'Several announcements of a new Google TV are expected at the International Consumer Electronics Show, involving LG Electronics, Sony, Samsung and Vizio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Manufacturers of televisions have been searching for something — anything! — to reverse a years-long slide in profits.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Google TV Tries Again', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television Sets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LG Electronics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T14:52:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99f75f77-f71d-5216-b72f-c03a16e7c886', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99f75f77-f71d-5216-b72f-c03a16e7c886'}, {'abstract': 'A company harnesses biofuel from landfills to generate electricity with minimal releases of methane, a long-lasting heat-trapping gas.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/biomass-and-electricity-part-one/', 'snippet': 'A company harnesses biofuel from landfills to generate electricity with minimal releases of methane, a long-lasting heat-trapping gas.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Burning natural gas releases less heat-trapping carbon dioxide than burning coal does because it has only about half as much carbon per unit of energy. But it can exacerbate global warming if it escapes unburned into the atmosphere as methane; in a century, a methane molecule will trap as much heat as 21 carbon dioxide molecules would. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biomass and Electricity, Part One', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methane', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Benning (Ga)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T14:56:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8785d71-3e6a-5bf6-ab53-8236099db097', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8785d71-3e6a-5bf6-ab53-8236099db097'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the roster of exhibitors at C.E.S. reveals more than 200 companies that not only hail from the Chinese city Shenzhen, but include the city’s name in their own.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/whats-in-a-name-at-c-e-s-oftentimes-its-shenzhen/', 'snippet': 'A look at the roster of exhibitors at C.E.S. reveals more than 200 companies that not only hail from the Chinese city Shenzhen, but include the city’s name in their own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — This year’s International Consumer Electronics Show, which opens here Tuesday, will include, according to the show’s producer,\xa0 more than 2,700 exhibitors. Many of the usual players will be in attendance, including name brands like Canon, Sony, Samsung, Panasonic, LG.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s in a Name? At C.E.S., Oftentimes, It’s Shenzhen', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shenzhen (China)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T15:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Grobart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grobart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3d62fe3-c0a8-59ad-a189-312df15dab8a', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3d62fe3-c0a8-59ad-a189-312df15dab8a'}, {'abstract': 'Our series on Marfa artists kicks off with the artist collective-cum-band Foundation for Jammable Resources.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/the-real-artists-of-marfa-foundation-for-jammable-resources/', 'snippet': 'Our series on Marfa artists kicks off with the artist collective-cum-band Foundation for Jammable Resources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multim