e net-a-porter.com and farfetch.com. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital Dressing Room', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T16:42:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By ERICA M. BLUMENTHAL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b7f1b3a-ff24-58d3-ac07-4caa3d3569c0', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b7f1b3a-ff24-58d3-ac07-4caa3d3569c0'}, {'abstract': 'The Suffolk University two-day tracking poll shows Ron Paul steady in second place, while Jon M. Huntsman Jr. and Newt Gingrich are basically tied at third.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/romneys-lead-in-new-hampshire-slips-in-poll/', 'snippet': 'The Suffolk University two-day tracking poll shows Ron Paul steady in second place, while Jon M. Huntsman Jr. and Newt Gingrich are basically tied at third.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — While Mitt Romney remains the front-runner among Republican primary voters in New Hampshire, his once formidable lead appears to be slipping. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Lead in New Hampshire Slips in Poll', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and P