he insider trading case against Rajat K. Gupta heads toward trial, the prosecution and the defense are each seeking to gain the upper hand.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/cat-and-mouse-game-in-the-gupta-prosecution/', 'snippet': 'As the insider trading case against Rajat K. Gupta heads toward trial, the prosecution and the defense are each seeking to gain the upper hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We often think of prosecutions as involving a single crime that took place at a particular moment, so that the charges are fixed and the information that will be presented in court fairly clear-cut. In white-collar prosecutions, that is rarely the case, as prosecutors refine their case after filing charges, sometimes finding new violations, while defendants try to pry evidence from the government that can help their defense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cat-and-Mouse Game in the Gupta Prosecution', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Rajat K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T19:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9a61d25-b765-505a-9e7f-3a2a4cdae774', 'word_count': 1212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9a61d25-b765-505a-9e7f-3a2a4cdae774'}, {'abstract': 'A revamped CBS morning show is meant to emphasize hard news — a quick study of the first day shows some differences between it and its competitors.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/cbs-begins-to-redefine-whats-news-in-the-morning/', 'snippet': 'A revamped CBS morning show is meant to emphasize hard news — a quick study of the first day shows some differences between it and its competitors.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:11 p.m. | Updated On Monday, CBS introduced a revamped morning show that is meant to distinguish itself from its more popular competitors — the top-rated “Today” show at NBC and ABC’s “Good Morning America” — by emphasizing hard news. With the help of a TV remote control and TVEyes, here’s a look at how “CBS This Morning” diverged from the others.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'CBS Begins to Redefine What’s News in the Morning', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T19:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10c1f169-71da-578a-ba43-1a815f82b6e1', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10c1f169-71da-578a-ba43-1a815f82b6e1'}, {'abstract': '“Looking for a Missing Employee,” about the troubling disappearance of a Lebanese government official, is the long overdue and too brief American debut of the actor and director Rabih Mroué.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/rabih-mroue-at-coil-festival-making-sense-of-a-mysterious-disappearance-in-lebanon/', 'snippet': '“Looking for a Missing Employee,” about the troubling disappearance of a Lebanese government official, is the long overdue and too brief American debut of the actor and director Rabih Mroué.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So often, political art makes us feel that the cure is as bad as the disease. Didactic, self-righteous and smug, full of easy slogans, this sort of art leaves people just as boxed in as the systems it supposedly critiques.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rabih Mroué at Coil Festival: Making Sense of a Mysterious Disappearance in Lebanon', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mroue, Rabih', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baryshnikov Arts Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T19:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a129598d-a03a-5e4f-9b05-bb9f4ca66b19', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a129598d-a03a-5e4f-9b05-bb9f4ca66b19'}, {'abstract': 'Many of India’s airlines are rife with safety violations, including shortages of pilots and engines, according to an unreleased report by the industry’s top regulator.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/business/global/indian-airlines-suffer-from-safety-issues-regulator-says.html', 'snippet': 'Many of India’s airlines are rife with safety violations, including shortages of pilots and engines, according to an unreleased report by the industry’s top regulator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Many of India’s airlines are rife with safety violations, according to an unreleased report by the industry’s top regulator here.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/business/Indiaair/Indiaair-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 265, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/10/business/Indiaair/Indiaair-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 265}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/business/Indiaair/Indiaair-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/business/Indiaair/Indiaair-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/10/business/Indiaair/Indiaair-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Regulator Cites Safety Violations and Financial Ills of Airlines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indian Regulator Cites Safety Violations and Financial Ills of Airlines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T19:01:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29d065af-e301-5c41-af46-37657fd88a8c', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29d065af-e301-5c41-af46-37657fd88a8c'}, {'abstract': 'The Northwestern football team has not won a bowl game since 1949. Its men’s basketball team has never made the N.C.A.A. tournament–could it be a different story this year?', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/with-one-drought-continuing-northwestern-looks-to-end-another/', 'snippet': 'The Northwestern football team has not won a bowl game since 1949. Its men’s basketball team has never made the N.C.A.A. tournament–could it be a different story this year?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Northwestern fell to Texas A&M, 33-22, in the Meineke Car Care Bowl\xa0of\xa0Texas on New Year’s Eve, the loss extended the N.C.A.A.’s longest bowl losing streak to nine games.\xa0 The only time Evanston’s football faithful have celebrated a postseason win was the 1949 Rose Bowl, a 20-14 victory over California.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With One Drought Continuing, Northwestern Looks to End Another', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bowl Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rose Bowl (Football Game)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carmody, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': '