X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0af3992-a566-5c53-841d-0d043fa48669', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0af3992-a566-5c53-841d-0d043fa48669'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers are looking for opportunities to identify adolescents who have problems and to provide support.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/health/views/seeing-social-media-as-adolescent-portal-more-than-pitfall.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers are looking for opportunities to identify adolescents who have problems and to provide support.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a hundred years ago, when the telephone was introduced, there was some hand-wringing over the social dangers that this new technology posed: increased sexual aggression and damaged human relationships. “It was going to bring down our society,” said Dr. Megan Moreno, a specialist in adolescent medicine at the University of Wisconsin-Madison. “Men would be calling women and making lascivious comments, and women would be so vulnerable, and we’d never have civilized conversations again.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/science/10KLAS/10KLAS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 980, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/science/10KLAS/10KLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/10/science/10KLAS/10KLAS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeing Social Media More as Portal Than as Pitfall', 'kicker': '18 and Under', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeing Social Media More as Portal Than as Pitfall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bullies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T19:19:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Views', 'byline': {'original': 'By Perri Klass, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Perri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klass', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c77fead0-e038-5f63-8f00-35437bb1f794', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c77fead0-e038-5f63-8f00-35437bb1f794'}, {'abstract': 'Without Zach Randolph in the lineup, the Memphis Grizzlies have lost all semblance of order on offense.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/randolphs-injury-costs-grizzlies-offense-order/', 'snippet': 'Without Zach Randolph in the lineup, the Memphis Grizzlies have lost all semblance of order on offense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Memphis Grizzlies are in some considerable trouble, and for at least six or seven more weeks, Zach Randolph won’t be able to right their wrongs on the strength of his mid-post game. A nasty medial collateral ligament tear ensured that much, and though Randolph is fortunate to have dodged a need for surgery, his absence has sent Memphis’ offense into a tailspin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Randolph’s Injury Costs Grizzlies Offense, Order', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T19:20:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By ROB MAHONEY', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MAHONEY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06bf0d81-8dd6-51c3-a4e7-0625d41ac6c2', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06bf0d81-8dd6-51c3-a4e7-0625d41ac6c2'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich delivers on a promise, releasing a Web video called “Taxman,” accusing Mitt Romney of raising $700 million worth of taxes while governor of Massachusetts.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/gingrich-video-criticizes-romney-on-taxes/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich delivers on a promise, releasing a Web video called “Taxman,” accusing Mitt Romney of raising $700 million worth of taxes while governor of Massachusetts.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:03 p.m. | Updated  MANCHESTER, N.H. — Newt Gingrich on Monday delivered on a promise he had made a day earlier, releasing a Web video called “Taxman,” accusingMitt Romney of raising $700 million worth of taxes while governor of Massachusetts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Video Criticizes Romney on Taxes', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T19:21:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fb40f89-4b93-56b1-b280-7b66c28419c4', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fb40f89-4b93-56b1-b280-7b66c28419c4'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich advised a major private equity firm, even though he is faulting Mitt Romney for his ties to that industry.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/gingrichs-own-close-tie-to-buyout-industry/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich advised a major private equity firm, even though he is faulting Mitt Romney for his ties to that industry.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:56 p.m. | Updated Newt Gingrich has ramped up his attacks on Mitt Romney as a heartless leveraged buyout executive for his years at Bain Capital, asking reporters in Manchester on Monday, “Is capitalism really about the ability of a handful of rich people to manipulate the lives of thousands of other people and walk off with the money? Or is that, somehow, a little bit of a flawed system?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich’s Own Close Tie to Buyout Industry', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Forstmann, Theodore J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kravis, Henry R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T19:22:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman and Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dcf645b-0114-5789-97c1-a6c8dc05c5f0', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dcf645b-0114-5789-97c1-a6c8dc05c5f0'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers suggest physical activity increases the flow of blood and oxygen to the brain and may lead to increased levels of norepinephrine and endorphins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/health/research/exercise-yields-dividends-in-the-classroom-studies-suggest.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers suggest physical activity increases the flow of blood and oxygen to the brain and may lead to increased levels of norepinephrine and endorphins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Physical exercise in children improves not only cardiovascular health but also academic performance, an analysis of several studies has found.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Childhood: Exercise Yields Dividends in the Classroom', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Childhood: Exercise Yields Dividends in the Classroom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}