e river that runs through it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Interior Secretary Signs Grand Canyon Mining Ban', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Metals and Minerals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brewer, Jan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salazar, Ken', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Geographic Society', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado River', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Grand Canyon (Ariz)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T20:33:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97c57d62-c589-5df0-a2a2-610ae54ef9bc', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97c57d62-c589-5df0-a2a2-610ae54ef9bc'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court refused to expand its reasoning in the Citizens United case, which relaxed restrictions on corporate and labor political donations, to allow campaign spending by foreigners.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/supreme-court-retains-ban-on-foreign-campaign-donations/', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court refused to expand its reasoning in the Citizens United case, which relaxed restrictions on corporate and labor political donations, to allow campaign spending by foreigners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a terse four words, the Supreme Court on Monday issued an order upholding prohibitions against foreigners making contributions to influence American elections.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Retains Ban on Foreign Campaign Donations', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T20:34:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John H. Cushman Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Cushman', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3727bc06-2194-5235-a286-e54daccf641a', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3727bc06-2194-5235-a286-e54daccf641a'}, {'abstract': 'Tebow mania and the quarterback’s heroics draw a huge crowd for CBS.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/tebow-wins-for-cbs-too/', 'snippet': 'Tebow mania and the quarterback’s heroics draw a huge crowd for CBS.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fueled by Tim Tebow mania and capped by Tebow’s 80-yard game-winning touchdown pass on the first play of overtime, the broadcast of the Denver Broncos’ 29-23 victory over the Pittsburgh Steelers produced huge ratings for CBS on Sunday. According to preliminary overnight Nielsen estimates it was the highest-rated National Football League wild-card playoff game in 24 years and CBS averaged nearly 42 million viewers during the 7 p.m. hour. ', '