ss than a month after it named Ben Smith, a standout writer from Politico, as its editor in chief.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/buzzfeed-raises-15-5-million-in-financing/', 'snippet': 'BuzzFeed announced Monday that it had raised $15.5 million in financing, less than a month after it named Ben Smith, a standout writer from Politico, as its editor in chief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Monday brought surprises from BuzzFeed, the social Web site that is suddenly and rather robustly investing in reporting muscle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BuzzFeed Raises $15.5 Million in Financing', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T22:16:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3e0762e-99a7-5606-98e2-52404b58d7c5', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3e0762e-99a7-5606-98e2-52404b58d7c5'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks so much to all who contributed to our lively – if somewhat technologically challenged – discussion about the scientists who made bird flu take wing.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/deadly-viruses-pro-or-con/', 'snippet': 'Thanks so much to all who contributed to our lively – if somewhat technologically challenged – discussion about the scientists who made bird flu take wing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks so much to all who contributed to our lively — if somewhat technologically challenged — discussion about the scientists who made bird flu take wing. Responses reflected an unusually wide array of ideas, from the conviction that nothing in the world could justify experiments like those in question to the equally impassioned conviction that nothing should get in their way. Similarly, some argued that the data these experiments produced are of only marginal usefulness, while others felt they would prove as invaluable as Galileo’s discovery. But what, as Andrew S asked, is the most appropriate ethical framework for sorting through these claims? For those who might have more to say, we’ll keep the comments open for a while longer. Readers, have at it!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deadly Viruses: Pro or Con?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T22:17:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/634c6e66-64cc-5189-9546-fb260b3e7a6d', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/634c6e66-64cc-5189-9546-fb260b3e7a6d'}, {'abstract': 'Equations add a new twist to the way mathematicians, scientists and architects use their noodle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/science/pasta-inspires-scientists-to-use-their-noodle.html', 'snippet': 'Equations add a new twist to the way mathematicians, scientists and architects use their noodle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most people eating pasta might enjoy the taste or appreciate the texture of noodles cooked al dente.', 'print_sect