cle/a0afdcd0-e947-573b-bf36-1a34d1df4483', 'word_count': 902, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0afdcd0-e947-573b-bf36-1a34d1df4483'}, {'abstract': 'A new vaccine, previously thought to protect uninfected women who have infected partners, has now been found useless against herpes simplex virus-2 in a double-blinded placebo-controlled trial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/health/research/herpes-vaccine-falls-short-in-clinical-trial.html', 'snippet': 'A new vaccine, previously thought to protect uninfected women who have infected partners, has now been found useless against herpes simplex virus-2 in a double-blinded placebo-controlled trial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The search for a vaccine to prevent infection with two types of herpes simplex, or H.S.V., is under way, but success is proving elusive. A new vaccine, previously thought to protect uninfected women who have infected partners, has now been found useless against one form, H.S.V.-2, in a double-blinded placebo-controlled trial.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Herpes Vaccine Falls Short in Clinical Trial', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prevention: Herpes Vaccine Falls Short in Clinical Trial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Journal of Medicine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexually Transmitted Diseases', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Herpes Viruses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T22:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c657f219-0c6d-5a82-8c5b-f9733beba09a', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c657f219-0c6d-5a82-8c5b-f9733beba09a'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Last Holiday: A Memoir,” Gil Scott-Heron, who died last year, describes his life and America in the second half of the 20th century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/books/the-last-holiday-a-memoir-by-gil-scott-heron-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Last Holiday: A Memoir,” Gil Scott-Heron, who died last year, describes his life and America in the second half of the 20th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the poet, novelist, piano player and spoken-word recording artist Gil Scott-Heron died unexpectedly last May, at 62, he left behind a prickly and galvanizing body of work. His best songs — “The Revolution Will Not Be Televised,” “Whitey on the Moon,” “We Almost Lost Detroit” — are rarely heard on classic-rock radio; they’re too eccentric and polemical and might kill a workingman’s lunchtime buzz. But they’ll still stop you in your tracks.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/arts/BOOK/BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 672, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/10/arts/BOOK/BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'His Story: A Writer of