rants from fellow food celebrities like Anthony Bourdain, is going to be a busy woman over the next two years. In 2013 and 2014 she will release three e-books focusing on seasonal entertaining and two new cookbooks, her new publisher said. Ballantine Books, part of Random House, has lured back Ms. Deen after losing her to Simon & Schuster more than a decade ago. (Pamela Cannon, now an executive editor at Random House, discovered Ms. Deen in 1997 while dining at her restaurant, The Lady & Sons, in Savannah, Ga., and edited her first two cookbooks.) Gina Centrello, the president and publisher of the Random House Publishing Group, said in a statement, “As her Random House family, we are especially thrilled to welcome Paula Deen back home where together we will build upon and expand her singular and remarkable brand.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Cookbooks From Paula Deen', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Cookbooks From Paula Deen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deen, Paula', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ballantine Books', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-09T23:30:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/725e98b6-492b-5f3d-aa62-c5e12516d179', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/725e98b6-492b-5f3d-aa62-c5e12516d179'}, {'abstract': 'An M.I.T. physicist’s video ser