b-96eb-7b87ab7369f4'}, {'abstract': 'In parts of Brazil, militias extort money, punish those who cross them and carry out extrajudicial killings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/world/americas/in-parts-of-brazil-militias-operate-outside-the-law.html', 'snippet': 'In parts of Brazil, militias extort money, punish those who cross them and carry out extrajudicial killings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NITERÓI, Brazil — Patrícia Acioli, a judge known for imprisoning corrupt police officers, pulled into the driveway of her home one August night in this city across the bay from Rio de Janeiro. Her pursuers arrived at the same time. Then they did their work, shooting her 21 times until her body lay crumpled in the seat of her car. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/world/BRAZIL-1/BRAZIL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/10/world/BRAZIL-1/BRAZIL-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/world/BRAZIL-1/BRAZIL-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Brazil, Officers of the Law, Outside the Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officers of the Law, Outside the Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T00:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero and Taylor Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Taylor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae464633-1652-5949-bfb8-e868cbf13083', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae464633-1652-5949-bfb8-e868cbf13083'}, {'abstract': 'K. J. Choi, once the only South Korean playing full time on the PGA Tour, will have plenty of company from his homeland this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/sports/golf/south-korean-men-make-their-way-to-pga-tour.html', 'snippet': 'K. J. Choi, once the only South Korean playing full time on the PGA Tour, will have plenty of company from his homeland this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KAPALUA, Hawaii — On Wednesday nights before a tournament, K. J. Choi visits the Korean Baptist church closest to the course he is playing, a practice that dates to when he was the PGA Tour’s first and only full-time player from South Korea. In the familiar hymns, sung in his native tongue, Choi experiences a connection, a communion, that he struggled at first to forge on the tour, where the courses and the language were foreign to him.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 's