 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57b75943-d0af-50f2-a0d6-8daf6881ec4b', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57b75943-d0af-50f2-a0d6-8daf6881ec4b'}, {'abstract': 'Federal authorities say the soldier, Craig B. Baxam, 24, flew to Kenya last month with the goal of joining the militant terrorist group Al Shabab in Somalia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/us/maryland-former-soldier-charged-with-trying-to-aid-terrorism.html', 'snippet': 'Federal authorities say the soldier, Craig B. Baxam, 24, flew to Kenya last month with the goal of joining the militant terrorist group Al Shabab in Somalia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A former soldier from Maryland was charged Monday with trying to provide material support to a terrorist organization in Africa. Federal authorities say the soldier, Craig B. Baxam, 24, flew to Kenya last month with the goal of joining the militant terrorist group Al Shabab in Somalia. He converted to Islam shortly before dropping out of the United States Army in July, after four years of service, including in Iraq, federal authorities said. Mr. Baxam planned to donate money to Al Shabab, a violent militia group that opposes the Somalian government, authorities said. He faces a maximum sentence of 15 years in prison. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maryland: Former Soldier Charged With Trying to Aid Terrorism', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Mid-Atlantic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Maryland: Ex-Soldier Suspected of Aiding Terrorists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T01:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robbie Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robbie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/12d1cafc-c914-5b0f-8be7-37ce9cf5140a', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12d1cafc-c914-5b0f-8be7-37ce9cf5140a'}, {'abstract': 'The founder of Prescreen.com, a former Groupon executive, says the idea for the business came to him at Sundance in 2010, when he noticed that most movies there would never be seen again.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/new-rental-service-focuses-on-indie-film/', 'snippet': 'The founder of Prescreen.com, a former Groupon executive, says the idea for the business came to him at Sundance in 2010, when he noticed that most movies there would never be seen again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you have a new business that involves indie film, this is your moment to hustle — or at least to hire a publicist to hustle on your behalf. Sundance starts next week, and it’s a make-or-break moment for glom-on marketing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Rental Service Focuses on Indie Film', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T01:01:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media