efe1-c101-5c84-8d99-9e4a3b414b93', 'word_count': 1043, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d590efe1-c101-5c84-8d99-9e4a3b414b93'}, {'abstract': 'The encounter between Israeli and Palestinian officials was kept at such a low profile that it was almost as if it had not happened at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/world/middleeast/israelis-and-palestinians-discuss-peace-talks-in-jordan.html', 'snippet': 'The encounter between Israeli and Palestinian officials was kept at such a low profile that it was almost as if it had not happened at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Israeli and Palestinian officials met in the Jordanian capital on Monday, their second session in less than a week, after peace talks had been stalled for more than a year. The encounter was kept at such a low profile, however, that it was almost as if it had not happened at all — attesting to the fragility of the contacts and the apparently minimal expectations each side has for progress.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peace Talks Are Discussed in a Session in Jordan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peace Talks Are Discussed In a Session In Jordan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T02:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10b3df2c-c965-57f5-bf99-33239fcda5ea', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10b3df2c-c965-57f5-bf99-33239fcda5ea'}, {'abstract': 'Coming to terms with what long-form scholarship in the digital age really means.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/09/the-digital-humanities-and-the-transcending-of-mortality/', 'snippet': 'Coming to terms with what long-form scholarship in the digital age really means.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is a blog. There, I’ve said it. I have been resisting saying it — I have always referred to this space as a “column” — not only because “blog” is an ugly word (as are clog, smog and slog), but because blogs are provisional, ephemeral, interactive, communal, available to challenge, interruption and interpolation, and not meant to last; whereas in a professional life now going into its 50th year I have been building arguments that are intended to be decisive, comprehensive, monumental, definitive and, most important, all mine. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Digital Humanities and the Transcending of Mortality', 'kicker': 'Stanley Fish', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T02:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Fish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3abfcf6-a0e4-5099-a27c-a1b7a2c83d4c', 'word_count': 2254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3abfcf6-a0e4-5099-a27c-a1b7a2c83d4c'}, {'abstract': 'The Packers will open the playoffs healthy and at home, but their defense needs work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/sports/football/scoring-points-allows-packers-to-disguis