-points-to-threat-of-cheap-but-potent-weapons/', 'snippet': 'President Obama and his national security team are drawing attention to what they see as a growing threat to the American military: relatively inexpensive weapons to keep American forces at a distance, rather than defeat them outright.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama and his national security team are drawing attention to what they see as a growing threat to the American military. In an article in Tuesday’s issue of The Times, Thom Shanker reports on the administration’s prediction that security challenges in the coming decade will be defined by the use of relatively inexpensive weapons to keep American forces at a distance, rather than defeat them outright.He writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Strategy Points to Threat of Cheap but Potent Weapons', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T02:34:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/253c0df4-b218-5be3-9c5d-a4d7db323b6d', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/253c0df4-b218-5be3-9c5d-a4d7db323b6d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Weissenberg was known for his thundering aggressiveness and rational detachment at the keyboard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/arts/music/alexis-weissenberg-pianist-of-fire-and-ice-dies-at-82.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Weissenberg was known for his thundering aggressiveness and rational detachment at the keyboard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alexis Weissenberg, a charismatic Bulgarian-born pianist known for his thundering aggressiveness and rational detachment at the keyboard, and for his unapologetic defense of those traits in interviews, died on Sunday in Lugano, Switzerland. He was 82.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/arts/music/WEISSENBERG-obit/WEISSENBERG-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/arts/music/WEISSENBERG-obit/WEISSENBERG-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/10/arts/music/WEISSENBERG-obit/WEISSENBERG-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alexis Weissenberg, Pianist of Fire and Ice, Dies at 82', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alexis Weissenberg, Pianist of Fire and Ice, Dies at 82', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bulgaria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weissenberg, Alexis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T02:34:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organiz