ction is a wideranging one that documents the history of tattooing, from the Prehistoric era to the present day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Amsterdam, which claims to have the greatest number of museums per square mile in the world, few topics are left unexplored. There is a museum that delves into sex, another on war (or at least the Dutch resistance), and a museum dedicated, of course, to marijuana. Last fall, a museum opened with a focus on another topic that rarefied institutions generally avoid: tattoos.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tattoos, Through Time: A New Museum for Amsterdam', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T11:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ivan Quintanilla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ivan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quintanilla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a353cd4-abd0-5f87-aaf5-6586ee830488', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a353cd4-abd0-5f87-aaf5-6586ee830488'}, {'abstract': 'The odds say we’ll see two of the top three scoring offenses in the Super Bowl this year, and that could lead to a record-breaking result.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/packers-on-top-in-total-passing-value/', 'snippet': 'The odds say we’ll see two of the top three scoring offenses in the Super Bowl this year, and that could lead to a record-breaking result.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Packers, the Saints and the Patriots have three of the best passing offenses in N.F.L. history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Packers on Top in  Total Passing Value', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Saints', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T11:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chase Stuart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chase', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stuart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61eb74bc-ae87-58d0-b5ab-a07d3dc88aa5', 'word_count': 1587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61eb74bc-ae87-58d0-b5ab-a07d3dc88aa5'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Kantrowitz, an expert on paying for college and the founder of FinAid.org, is answering  questions from readers of The Choice about financial aid applications this week', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/kantrowitz-part-two/', 'snippet': 'Mark Kantrowitz, an expert on paying for college and the founder of FinAid.org, is answering  questions from readers of The Choice about financial aid applications this week', 'lead_paragraph': '10:27 a.m. | Updated We are no longer accepting questions for this feature.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Part 2: Answers on the Fafsa, the Free Application for Federal Student Aid', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T11:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Kantrowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kantrowitz', 'qualifier': None, 