recasts of Amazon’s success with the new Kindle Fire. At the same time they are reducing their forecasts of the overall e-reader market, which suggests that they see the basic Kindles losing popularity.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/will-the-kindle-fire-kill-e-readers/', 'snippet': 'Amazon’s tablet might be so successful it cannibalizes the retailer’s e-readers. Analysts are outdoing themselves with forecasts of Amazon’s success with the new Kindle Fire. At the same time they are reducing their forecasts of the overall e-read...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the holiday season is history, it is clear that the Kindle Fire did substantially better than many forecasts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/09/technology/09gadgetwise-fire/09gadgetwise-fire-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will the Kindle Fire Kill E-Readers?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amazon Kindle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T11:03:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b607fe88-472d-5df1-8662-49554cf0721b', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b607fe88-472d-5df1-8662-49554cf0721b'}, {'abstract': 'A Pentagon language-training contract, a military background, Iranian heritage and some linguistic work may have contributed to Iran’s arrest and conviction of Amir Mirzaei Hekmati.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/world/middleeast/iran-imposes-death-sentence-on-us-man-accused-of-spying.html', 'snippet': 'A Pentagon language-training contract, a military background, Iranian heritage and some linguistic work may have contributed to Iran’s arrest and conviction of Amir Mirzaei Hekmati.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Pentagon language-training contract won in 2009 by Kuma Games, a New York-based company that develops reality-based war games — including one called “Assault on Iran” — lists as a main contact Amir Mirzaei Hekmati, the former Marine from Flint, Mich., now on death row in an Iranian prison, convicted of spying for the C.I.A.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/world/SUB-IRAN/SUB-IRAN-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 567, 'width': 401, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/world/SUB-IRAN/SUB-IRAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 567, 'width': 401, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/world/SUB-IRAN/SUB-IRAN-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/world/SUB-IRAN/SUB-IRAN-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': '