es', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ford C-Max Targets Prius, Volt and Ghosts of Minivans Past', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T13:42:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Ulrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ulrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c0045cf-d85a-52b0-a4d3-6dc99436a234', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c0045cf-d85a-52b0-a4d3-6dc99436a234'}, {'abstract': 'Within a week, Argentinians were told their president had cancer and then that she did not. They deserve an explanation.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/kirchners-false-positive/', 'snippet': 'Within a week, Argentinians were told their president had cancer and then that she did not. They deserve an explanation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUENOS AIRES — Last week, I took a look at President Cristina Fernández de Kirchner’s cancer diagnosis and how she has personalized power far too much. On Saturday, Argentinians were stunned to learn that, after removing the president’s thyroid gland, doctors discovered she didn’t have cancer after all but rather a benign tumor. Following the initial relief, doubts quickly set in: despite assurances that such misdiagnoses can happen, many Kirchner critics cited the episode as another example of why the government’s words can’t be trusted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kirchner’s False Positive', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tumors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirchner, Cristina Fernandez de', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Buenos Aires (Argentina)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T13:44:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Politi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Politi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd4b3f86-830a-5a6c-a2b4-58adab8c12bb', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd4b3f86-830a-5a6c-a2b4-58adab8c12bb'}, {'abstract': 'The grand tourers are offered with 4-liter V-8s sourced from Audi, the British marque’s corporate sibling under Volkswagen Group.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/bentley-continental-v-8s-trace-family-ties-to-germany/', 'snippet': 'The grand tourers are offered with 4-liter V-8s sourced from Audi, the British marque’s corporate sibling under Volkswagen Group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shown Monday, Jan. 9: 2012 Bentley Continental GT V-8 and Continental GTC V-8.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bentley Continental V-8s Trace Family Ties to Germany', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value