'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/d358830e-26cb-53af-96d6-763fbf577ebf', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/d358830e-26cb-53af-96d6-763fbf577ebf'}, {'abstract': 'Critics argue that the attacks on Mitt Romney over his role at Bain Capital are attacks on the free-market system and help the Democrats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/us/politics/new-hampshire-vote-seen-as-gauge-as-rivals-try-to-slow-romney.html', 'snippet': 'Critics argue that the attacks on Mitt Romney over his role at Bain Capital are attacks on the free-market system and help the Democrats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Attacks on Mitt Romney by some of his rivals set off outrage within the Republican Party on Tuesday as voters went to the polls and the candidates turned their attention to South Carolina.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/us/11elect_span2/11elect_span2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/us/11elect_span2/11elect_span2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/us/11elect_span2/11elect_span2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Attacks on Romney Prompt G.O.P. Backlash', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Attacks on Romney Prompt Backlash Within G.O.P.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T16:27:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d368f20a-cc40-5f13-830a-d35544ec9f20', 'word_count': 1358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d368f20a-cc40-5f13-830a-d35544ec9f20'}, {'abstract': 'Paramount said it had acquired the distribution rights to “Cirque du Soleil Worlds Away,” a 3-D movie written and directed by Andrew Adamson (of the “Shrek” and “Narnia” franchises), and whose producers include James Cameron.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/cirque-du-soleil-3d-movie-coming-at-you-this-year/', 'snippet': 'Paramount said it had acquired the distribution rights to “Cirque du Soleil Worlds Away,” a 3-D movie written and directed by Andrew Adamson (of the “Shrek” and “Narnia” franchises), and whose producers include James Cameron.', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to a partial list compiled by Dan Kois for The New York Times Magazine, moviegoers at 3-D films last year had Captain America’s shield, Justin Bieber’s hand and 40 partly chewed bean buns flung at them in stereoscopic illusions. This year, audiences can get ready to guard their laps against Cirque du Soleil acrobats who appear to be flying off the screen: Paramount said on Tuesday that it had acquired the distribution rights for a new 3-D movie about that Montreal-based circus troupe, written and directed by Andrew Adamson (of the “Shrek” and “Narnia” franchises) and produced by, among others, James Cameron (a filmmaker who knows a thing or two about 3-D movies). The film, called “Cirque du Soleil Worlds Away,” will feature performances from various shows presented by the troupe. Rob Moore, the vice chairman of Paramount, said in a statement that it will also include “a timeless original story written especially for this movie.” The studio said “Cirque du Soleil Worlds Away” is planned for worldwide release later this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cirque du Soleil 3-D Movie Coming at You This Year', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACROBATS AND ACROBATICS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ADAMSON, ANDREW', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, James', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cirque du Soleil', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paramount Pictures', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montreal (Quebec)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T16:28:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b04e4bd-7ede-55b7-a2c5-1fd0eeb35dc8', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b04e4bd-7ede-55b7-a2c5-1fd0eeb35dc8'}, {'abstract': 'The government said it would allow foreign retailers who sell just one brand of products to open wholly-owned stores in India, up from a maximum of 51 percent ownership now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/business/global/rule-change-would-allow-some-foreign-owned-stores-in-india.html', 'snippet': 'The government said it would allow foreign retailers who sell just one brand of products to open wholly-owned stores in India, up from a maximum of 51 percent ownership now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUMBAI, India — A month after political opposition led the Indian government to indefinitely delay a decision to allow foreign retailers like Walmart into the country, policy makers on Tuesday changed a rule that would make it easier for predominantly single-brand foreign chains like Ikea and Gap to set up fully owned stores here.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rule Change Would Allow Some Foreign-Owned Stores to Open in India', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rule Change Would Allow Some Foreign-Owned Stores to Open in India', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starbucks Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T16:29:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79d48b54-bd25-5be0-8fe2-107c73f36d42', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79d48b54-bd25-5be0-8fe2-107c73f36d42'}, {'abstract': 'Treasury Secretary Timothy F. Geithner hopes to enlist China in a campaign to use sanctions to pressure Iran and convince Beijing to change its economic policies to American liking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/business/global/a-long-shot-for-geithner-as-he-begins-beijing-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Treasury Secretary Timothy F. Geithner hopes to enlist China in a campaign to use sanctions to pressure Iran and convince Beijing to change its economic policies to American liking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Timothy F. Geithner, the Treasury secretary, came to Beijing on Tuesday hoping to persuade Chinese leaders to toughen their stance toward Iran and to soften their opposition to a stronger renminbi, a move that could help the American economy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/business/GEITHNER/GEITHNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/business/GEITHNER/GEITHNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/business/GEITHNER/GEITHNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/business/GEITHNER/GEITHNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/business/GEITHNER/GEITHNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Talks With the Chinese, Geithner Faces an Uphill Climb', 'kic