acy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/dining/11SCHOHARIE1_SPAN/11SCHOHARIE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/dining/11SCHOHARIE1_SPAN/11SCHOHARIE1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/dining/11SCHOHARIE1_SPAN/11SCHOHARIE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/dining/11SCHOHARIE1_SPAN/11SCHOHARIE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Storm-Ravaged Village Builds a Bond at the Lunch Table', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Storm-Ravaged Village Builds a Bond at Lunch Table', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Schoharie (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Irene (2011)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T16:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca9c2b55-9e85-5d2b-a5e4-4d2a2dd59a3e', 'word_count': 1054, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca9c2b55-9e85-5d2b-a5e4-4d2a2dd59a3e'}, {'abstract': 'How Newt Gingrich and Rick Perry became class warriors.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/return-of-the-repressed/', 'snippet': 'How Newt Gingrich and Rick Perry became class warriors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the course of the 2000s, under a tax-cutting, business-friendly Republican administration, middle class paychecks grew much more slowly than the economy as a whole, upward mobility for the poor continued to lag behind parts of Western Europe, and the combination of unfunded tax cuts and deficit spending worsened the country’s fiscal picture just as the Baby Boomers were poised to retire. Then came the financial crisis, touched off in part by gross recklessness on Wall Street. Then came the Great Recession, which threw millions of Americans out of work, hit downscale workers much harder than it did the college-educated, and sent the deficit spiraling upward to unprecedented heights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Return of the Repressed', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T16:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0b73ba5-bfd7-5a91-bab0-a440954ee90a', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0b73ba5-bfd7-5a91-bab0-a440954ee90a'}, {'abstract': 'Prabal Gurung’s first prefall collection was consistent with the designer’s aesthetic: pretty with an edge.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/just-one-look-prabal-gurung/', 'snippet': 'Prabal Gurung’s first prefall collection was consistent with the designer’s aesthetic: pretty with an edge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prabal Gurung’s first prefall collection was consistent with the designer’s aesthetic: pretty with an edge. The silhouettes ranged from classic sheaths (in emerald green) to prim pleated skirts and fish-tail shirtdresses (with contrast colors on front and back). But what makes Gurung the next generation’s red carpet go-to for the avant-garde (Rooney Mara, Jessica Chastain) is his ability to imprint himself on traditional fabrics and textures.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Prabal Gurung', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gurung, Prabal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T16:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9722294-5c30-55ef-a300-9fe78362ae18', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9722294-5c30-55ef-a300-9fe78362ae18'}, {'abstract': 'The progressive country and western songwriter and singer performed in a club-style setting after a PowerPoint presentation.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/john-hiatt-performs-songs-for-the-road-at-panasonic-press-event/', 'snippet': 'The progressive country and western songwriter and singer performed in a club-style setting after a PowerPoint presentation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — As the first day of press previews came to an end on Monday night, in an antiseptic conference room on the second floor of the Cobo Center, music broke out. The Panasonic Automotive Systems Company of America decided to sweeten the appeal of the company’s press conference by presenting John Hiatt, the progressive country and western songwriter and singer known for songs about cars and the roads. He was also promoting his own product, his latest CD called “Dirty Jeans and Mudslide Hymns.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'John Hiatt Performs Songs for the Road at Panasonic Press Event', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T16:48:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8196b670-d1c2-5499-8564-5cc05a3f0b8a', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8196b670-d1c2-5499-8564-5cc05a3f0b8a'}, {'abstract': 'A  snake found in a heavily logged area of eastern Tanzania is likely to be classified as critically endangered, conservationists say.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/on-our-radar-a-new-snake/', 'snippet': 'A  snake found in a heavily logged area of eastern Tanzania is likely to be classified as critically endangered, conservationists say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Wildlife Conservation Society reports the discovery of a striking snake, the Matilda’s horned viper, in eastern Tanzania. Its habitat, estimated at only a few square miles, is already severely degraded from logging and the manufacture of charcoal, the group says, and the species is likely to be classified as critically endangered.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: A New Snake', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T16:52:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7f6f583-55e6-5007-89c1-31d80443e1ad', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7f6f583-55e6-5007-89c1-31d80443e1ad'}, {'abstract': 'An electrical fire broke out in the door panel of the Lincoln MKZ concept late on Tuesday morning.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/lincoln-on-the-hot-seat-at-cobo-center/', 'snippet': 'An electrical fire broke out in the door panel of the Lincoln MKZ concept late on Tuesday morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — To build drama around the debut of its MKZ concept, Lincoln used no fog machines. The sedan nevertheless created a wisp of ambience later in the morning here with an electrical fire in the driver’s door panel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lincoln, on the Hot Seat at Cobo Center', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Division of Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T17:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/958aa975-8ecb-5539-b719-3c6325224a44', 'word_count': 52, 'uri': 'nyt://article/958aa975-8ecb-5539-b719-3c6325224a44'}, {'abstract': 'The company appoints a new chief financial officer, Andrew Warren, and spreads out the responsibilities of the former chief operating officer who left and will not be replaced.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/after-departures-discovery-reorganizes-its-executive-suite/', 'snippet': 'The company appoints a new chief financial officer, Andrew Warren, and spreads out the responsibilities of the former chief operating officer who left and will not be replaced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Discovery Communications on Monday named a new chief financial officer and spread out the responsibilities of its former chief operating officer, completing a reorganization of the company’s executive suite.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Departures, Discovery Reorganizes Its Executive Suite', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, Bruce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liguori, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Andrew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winfrey, Oprah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Discovery Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Discovery Networks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T17:04:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe98ae53-570a-533c-9c4b-a648aaea2bbe', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe98ae53-570a-533c-9c4b-a648aaea2bbe'}, {'abstract': 'Overview of the car.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/10/automobiles/autoshow/toyota-prius-c.html', 'snippet': 'Overview of the car.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview of the car.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/automobiles/autoshow/toyota-prius-c-slide-1Y2J/toyota-prius-c-slide-1Y2J-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/automobiles/autoshow/toyota-prius-c-slide-1Y2J/toyota-prius-c-slide-1Y2J-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/10/automobiles/autoshow/toyota-prius-c-slide-1Y2J/toyota-prius-c-slide-1Y2J-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Toyota Prius C', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T17:08:09+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6f8022cb-7ed1-59a1-9a64-6c5db4b6ce53', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6f8022cb-7ed1-59a1-9a64-6c5db4b6ce53'}, {'abstract': 'When children head to the New Hampshire polls with their parents, they bring questions along.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/taking-my-children-to-the-new-hampshire-primary/', 'snippet': 'When children head to the New Hampshire polls with their parents, they bring questions along.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because I live in New Hampshire, I got up bright and early this morning, loaded the kids in the car and headed out to vote. My children are 10, 7, 6 and 5, and the two oldest remember coming with me to vote in the last presidential election. But a primary is different, and more confusing. Even though I’d explained it several times in the last few weeks, only my oldest child, Sam, really remembered what the primary meant (and when I asked him to name some of the differences between the Republican and Democratic Parties, he offered that the Democrats were represented by a blue elephant — although he was able to correctly identify his grandfather as a Republican).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking My Children to the New Hampshire Primary', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T17:09:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bad24f72-4777-539a-be1f-d1ef71ade566', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bad24f72-4777-539a-be1f-d1ef71ade566'}, {'abstract': 'Brad Pitt’s funny acceptance speech was among the highlights of the New York Film Critics Circle dinner.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/brad-pitt-denbygate-and-other-scenes-from-the-critics-circle/', 'snippet': 'Brad Pitt’s funny acceptance speech was among the highlights of the New York Film Critics Circle dinner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was higher-than-normal security at the New York Film Critics Circle awards dinner, but it wasn’t for fear of a showdown between David Denby and Scott Rudin. (Not that anyone had forgotten about Denbygate – more on that later.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brad Pitt, Denbygate and Other Scenes From the Critics Circle', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Albert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Denby, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolie, Angelina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitt, Brad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudin, Scott', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorkin, Aaron', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Meryl', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thatcher, Margaret H', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Film Critics Circle', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Village Voice', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T17:10:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08aad224-ec88-5c07-b5d8-622a6c09b149', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08aad224-ec88-5c07-b5d8-622a6c09b149'}, {'abstract': 'As Newt Gingrich dropped by a polling place at a school just a few blocks from downtown Manchester, he was pounced on by scores of journalists Tuesday morning.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/in-an-effort-to-greet-voters-gingrich-finds-mainly-news-media/', 'snippet': 'As Newt Gingrich dropped by a polling place at a school just a few blocks from downtown Manchester, he was pounced on by scores of journalists Tuesday morning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — “This is like being in New Orleans at Mardi Gras!” Newt Gingrich called out from one of his most intense crowds of the week. But it was not a crush of voters. As he dropped by a polling place at a school just a few blocks from downtown Manchester, he was pounced on by scores of journalists Tuesday morning. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In an Effort to Greet Voters, Gingrich Finds Mainly News Media', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manchester (NH)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T17:16:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e2308f1-b997-5cd0-9655-0ceb1c921441', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e2308f1-b997-5cd0-9655-0ceb1c921441'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Reserve said it transferred $76.9 billion in profits to the Treasury Department last year, slightly less than its 2010 transfer but much more than in any other previous year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/business/economy/fed-returns-77-billion-in-profits-to-treasury.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Reserve said it transferred $76.9 billion in profits to the Treasury Department last year, slightly less than its 2010 transfer but much more than in any other previous year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Federal Reserve said on Tuesday that it contributed $76.9 billion in profits to the Treasury Department last year, slightly less than its record 2010 transfer but much more than in any other previous year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fed Turns Over $77 Billion in Profits to the Treasury', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fed Turns Over $77 Billion In Profits to the Treasury', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T17:22:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea9b034c-adac-5b72-8693-9656323eb77a', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea9b034c-adac-5b72-8693-9656323eb77a'}, {'abstract': 'When Republicans pledge to slash federal spending, they ignore that government is necessary for big projects that voters care about.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/romneys-big-government-critique-runs-into-a-new-hampshire-roadblock/', 'snippet': 'When Republicans pledge to slash federal