None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T18:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0313966c-a697-5acb-a78f-35ca27d9670b', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0313966c-a697-5acb-a78f-35ca27d9670b'}, {'abstract': 'The  International Documentary Association responds to the Academy’s new rules governing eligibility for documentaries.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/new-documentary-rules-will-affect-docuweeks-group-says/', 'snippet': 'The  International Documentary Association responds to the Academy’s new rules governing eligibility for documentaries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The International Documentary Association has weighed in on the rule changes that will winnow films qualified for the documentary Oscar by, among other things, requiring a review in either The New York Times or The Los Angeles Times. In a statement on Tuesday, the association for nonfiction film — which sponsors an annual DocuWeeks program that has qualified documentaries as Oscar submissions by putting them in theaters, but often without getting the requisite review — said the new rules “will certainly have an impact” on its screening program. But that impact, it said, wouldn’t be clear until both the Academy and the editorial staffs of the two newspapers provided more information.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Documentary Rules Will Affect DocuWeeks, Group Says', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T18:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f94f614b-ead4-53cd-9301-d270bb357a59', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f94f614b-ead4-53cd-9301-d270bb357a59'}, {'abstract': 'Citibank is offering a new app that lets its ThankYou rewards members pool points using Facebook.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/citibank-lets-loyalty-members-pool-points-on-facebook/', 'snippet': 'Citibank is offering a new app that lets its ThankYou rewards members pool points using Facebook.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Citibank has offered a new Facebook app that lets members of its ThankYou rewards program pool points with friends and family.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Citibank Lets Loyalty Members Pool Points on Facebook', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T18:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c2aa96e-4fce-539d-a02b-93f664535d79', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c2aa96e-4fce-539d-a02b-93f664535d79'}, {'abstract': 'Had history unfolded differently, visitors to Central Park would have seen a statue of Mary Poppins alongside the Alice in Wonderland and Hans Christian Andersen statues.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/when-new-york-snubbed-mary-poppins/', 'snippet': 'Had history unfolded differently, visitors to Central Park would have seen a statue of Mary Poppins alongside the Alice in Wonderland and Hans Christian Andersen statues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If things had turned out differently 45 years ago, Mark Bransdon might have been looking at a life-size statue of Mary Poppins in Central Park, a few steps from the familiar statues of Hans Christian Andersen and Alice, of “Alice in Wonderland.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When New York Snubbed Mary Poppins', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benepe, Adrian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Travers, P L', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Parks and Recreation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bowral (Australia)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T18:03:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/621d980a-d6f0-5105-b6c3-b61f3f7ffe98', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/621d980a-d6f0-5105-b6c3-b61f3f7ffe98'}, {'abstract': 'Why have we let New Hampshire turn its “first in the nation” primary from a fluke into an entitlement?', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/not-set-in-granite/', 'snippet': 'Why have we let New Hampshire turn its “first in the nation” primary from a fluke into an entitlement?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Right now, while we indulge New Hampshire’s childish insistence on its presidential primary being “first in the nation,” Americans should decide to bury this tradition. Nearly a century is enough: the Granite State has somehow turned a fluke into an entitlement. Worse, its obsession with primacy prolongs, complicates and distorts the presidential nominating process. In a democracy, no state should be first forever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Set in Granite', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Elections (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic National Committee', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'g