m once overseen by Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/perry-in-sharp-attack-on-vultures-like-bain/', 'snippet': 'Rick Perry steps up his criticism of the private equity firm once overseen by Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT MILL, S.C. — Corporate takeover firms like Mitt Romney’s Bain Capital are “vultures” that pick struggling companies clean and leave local communities to pick up the pieces, Gov. Rick Perry of Texas said on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perry Attacks ‘Vultures’ Like Bain', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T18:49:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a40aafe-d9db-5aab-8281-577f5da6a2e3', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a40aafe-d9db-5aab-8281-577f5da6a2e3'}, {'abstract': 'The new location, opening Wednesday, is larger and more elaborate than the original No. 7 in Fort Greene, but will have a sandwich menu that’s similar to the one at the No. 7 Sub shop in the Ace Hotel in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/no-7-sub-gets-bigger-in-greenpoint/', 'snippet': 'The new location, opening Wednesday, is larger and more elaborate than the original No. 7 in Fort Greene, but will have a sandwich menu that’s similar to the one at the No. 7 Sub shop in the Ace Hotel in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No. 7 Sub’s new location, opening next Wednesday in Greenpoint, Brooklyn, is larger and more elaborate than the original No. 7 in Fort Greene, but will have an inventive sandwich menu that’s similar to the one at the sub shop that the owners, including the chef, Tyler Kord, have in the Ace Hotel in Manhattan. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No. 7 Sub Gets Bigger in Greenpoint', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T18:57:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c611b2b3-fff7-5dbb-929f-fd0a2c3c63e5', 'word_count': 143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c611b2b3-fff7-5dbb-929f-fd0a2c3c63e5'}, {'abstract': 'With the Encore, Buick goes smaller in hopes of luring younger buyers.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/a-buick-bigger-than-a-breadbox/', 'snippet': 'With the Encore, Buick goes smaller in hopes of luring younger buyers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Introduced on Tuesday, Jan. 10: 2013 Buick Encore.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Buick, Bigger than a Breadbox', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buick Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T18:57:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Ulrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ulrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d78281a-fcc3-5127-a5e5-1404afd44949', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d78281a-fcc3-5127-a5e5-1404afd44949'}, {'abstract': 'Checking in on “Billy the Kid,” the latest installment of PBS’s “American Experience” series.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/channel-surfing-billy-the-kid/', 'snippet': 'Checking in on “Billy the Kid,” the latest installment of PBS’s “American Experience” series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Billy the Kid lived his brief life at precisely the right moment to make him an excellent candidate for an installment of “American Experience” on PBS. It was an era of the kind of enthusiastic newspaper coverage that leads to outsize legends. And it was an era that left a sparse but compelling photographic record, poetic images of hard-living men and prettily posed women who come alive yet remain tantalizingly distant.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Channel Surfing: ‘Billy the Kid’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarty, Henry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T19:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24c57afb-083b-5c04-ad76-e37442de0eff', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24c57afb-083b-5c04-ad76-e37442de0eff'}, {'abstract': 'The month-long odyssey straight north through the ice showed signs of gathering steam this week as images taken by the United States Coast Guard tracked the vessels’ progress.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/images-from-a-russian-tankers-icy-journey-to-alaska/', 'snippet': 'The month-long odyssey straight north through the ice showed signs of gathering steam this week as images taken by the United States Coast Guard tracked the vessels’ progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague William Yardley reports, the coastal town of Nome, Alaska, is anxiously watching its frozen waters for an emergency shipment of fuel being brought by a Russian tanker escorted by an American icebreaker. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Images From a Russian Tanker’s Icy Journey to Alaska', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Icebreakers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Coast Guard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T19:08:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06849d60-e6b9-5535-a87e-120f53f94c23', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06849d60-e6b9-5535-a87e-120f53f94c23'}, {'abstract': 'Jon M. Huntsman Jr. paid a visit to the Webster School polling place on Tuesday, after an earlier stop by Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/a-huntsman-throng-at-a-popular-polling-site/', 'snippet': 'Jon M. Huntsman Jr. paid a visit to the Webster School polling place on Tuesday, after an earlier stop by Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Polling place madness, rinse and repeat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Huntsman Throng at a Popular Polling Site', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T19:11:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Leibovich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leibovich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f825f11-31fe-5c85-b20b-6ec3e390b3b2', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f825f11-31fe-5c85-b20b-6ec3e390b3b2'}, {'abstract': 'The case of Sahar Gul, a teen-ager confined and abused by her husband and his family, has become a test of whether Afghanistan is starting to take women’s rights seriously.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/in-one-girls-story-a-test-of-womens-rights-in-afghanistan/', 'snippet': 'The case of Sahar Gul, a teen-ager confined and abused by her husband and his family, has become a test of whether Afghanistan is starting to take women’s rights seriously.', 'lead_paragraph': ' I went to find Sahar Gul.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In One Girl’s Story, a Test of Women’s Rights in Afghanistan', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domestic Violence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gul, Sahar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T19:14:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93256a2d-6278-50da-a748-564e7e30741d', 'word_count': 1490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93256a2d-6278-50da-a748-564e7e30741d'}, {'abstract': 'A group of students form the Netherlands who are learning about the American election process are making campaign phone calls for a variety of candidates, including Rick Santorum and Ron Paul.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/the-caucus-click-holland-gets-out-the-vote/', 'snippet': 'A group of students form the Netherlands who are learning about the American election process are making campaign phone calls for a variety of candidates, including Rick Santorum and Ron Paul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEDFORD, N.H. — Sake Slootweg, who was photographed outside Rick Santorum’s campaign headquarters here, is part of a group of students from the Netherlands who are learning about the American election process and making campaign phone calls for a variety of candidates, including Mr. Santorum and Ron Paul. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Caucus Click: Dutch Get Out the Vote', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T19:20:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evan McGlinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGlinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bcbc4c6-a8c0-5f0e-92d2-9a2655a71ba6', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bcbc4c6-a8c0-5f0e-92d2-9a2655a71ba6'}, {'abstract': 'Parker Posey will host the Sundance Film Festival Awards, and a jury for the festival is unveiled.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/a-sundance-royal-returns/', 'snippet': 'Parker Posey will host the Sundance Film Festival Awards, and a jury for the festival is unveiled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once an Indie Queen always an Indie Queen? Yes – if you’re Parker Posey, who has been in more than a dozen Sundance films over the years, including “Party Girl” and “The House of Yes.” On Tuesday the festival announced that she will host the 2012 Sundance Film Festival Awards on Jan. 28. Ms. Posey, 43, also stars as a cuckoo from cuckoo-ville boss in “Price Check,” a comic drama that will have its premiere at the festival. Sundance on Tuesday also announced its roster of jurors. The full list, which includes names like the director Justin Lin (“Better Luck Tomorrow,” “Fast Five”) and Charles Ferguson (the director/producer of the Oscar-winning documentary “Inside Job”), can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sundance Royal Returns', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T19:21:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e69f9f2-b8b8-5cd2-8a7d-2b76f009a23a', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e69f9f2-b8b8-5cd2-8a7d-2b76f009a23a'}, {'abstract': 'Showtime is expanding a service to let its subscribers stream hundreds of television episodes and feature films both in and out of the home.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/showtime-extends-its-anytime-service/', 'snippet': 'Showtime is expanding a service to let its subscribers stream hundreds of television episodes and feature films both in and out of the home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following the lead of its larger rival HBO, Showtime is beginning to broaden access to an Internet service that lets its subscribers stream hundreds of television episodes and feature films.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Showtime Extends Its ‘Anytime’ Service', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Showtime', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T19:23:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1072a42c-0114-5a38-bbe8-8e4f426abd9f', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1072a42c-0114-5a38-bbe8-8e4f426abd9f'}, {'abstract': 'Not a good performance, but not as terrible as advertised.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/more-on-japan-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'Not a good performance, but not as terrible as advertised.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Say this for Eamonn Fingleton: he has started a useful blogospheric discussion of just how badly Japan really did. Noah Smith has weighed in on my last post; here’s a further take.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More On Japan (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T19:28:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1e43ce3-bf6c-5ac2-9066-253d09bab562', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1e43ce3-bf6c-5ac2-9066-253d09bab562'}, {'abstract': 'The goods exchanged are unclear in a sexually charged encounter between a dealer and a client in Radoslaw Rychcik’s adaptation of a French play, but the high stakes are not.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/theater/reviews/in-the-solitude-of-cotton-fields-by-radoslaw-rychcik.html', 'snippet': 'The goods exchanged are unclear in a sexually charged encounter between a dealer and a client in Radoslaw Rychcik’s adaptation of a French play, but the high stakes are not.', 'lead_paragraph': '“In the Solitude of Cotton Fields,” a visceral adaptation of a French play by Bernard-Marie Koltés, portrays a high-octane, sexually charged meeting between a dealer and a client, where the goods exchanged are unclear, but the high stakes are not. On another level, this production, staged in Polish with English supertitles by Radoslaw Rychcik, is about a confrontation between theater and rock concert. The rock concert wins. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/theater/10cotton/10cotton-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/10/theater/10cotton/10cotton-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/10/theater/10cotton/10cotton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'c