anization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6d2a83d-44fb-5467-a179-2d54d05479fc', 'word_count': 1310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6d2a83d-44fb-5467-a179-2d54d05479fc'}, {'abstract': 'The season premiere on Sunday drew an average of 4.2 million total viewers — double the average prime-time rating for PBS.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/downton-abbey-delivers-big-audience-for-pbs/', 'snippet': 'The season premiere on Sunday drew an average of 4.2 million total viewers — double the average prime-time rating for PBS.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Season 2 premiere of “Downton Abbey” on PBS on Sunday drew an average of 4.2 million total viewers, a number that would impress even the most cold-hearted dowager. That performance doubled the average prime-time rating for PBS, according to Nielsen data, and the show experienced an 18 percent jump in the 18-to-49-year-old demographic when compared with the typical rating from the first season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Downton Abbey’ Delivers Big Audience for PBS', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T20:21:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/907a4b53-642b-5a7b-9153-4f162806d763', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/907a4b53-642b-5a7b-9153-4f162806d763'}, {'abstract': 'Christmas season was the perfect time to visit the villages of Trás-os-Montes, in the isolated northeast corner of Portugal.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/in-rural-portugal-ancient-villages-homemade-delights-and-the-science-of-mooching/', 'snippet': 'Christmas season was the perfect time to visit the villages of Trás-os-Montes, in the isolated northeast corner of Portugal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three year-old Matilde, dressed in a pink sweatsuit that read “Fashion Beauty Girl,” wanted to take her princess doll to the pig slaughter. Her mom, whom I had met through my hosts in this small Portuguese town, objected. “The piggies are going to make the princess dirty,” she said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Rural Portugal, Ancient Villages and Homemade Delights', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portugal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T20:23:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/beba4ab4-efa2-5ce2-bbfd-61bfc95d3f26', 'word_count': 1660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/beba4ab4-efa2-5ce2-bbfd-61bfc95d3f26'}, {'abstract': 'What should children know about sexuality — and when should they know it?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/should-we-have-national-standards-for-sex-education/', 'snippet': 'What should children know about sexuality — and when should they know it?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group of advocates for sexuality education in schools, including the Sexuality Information and Education Council of the United States, Advocates for Youth and Answer, have joined forces and worked with “40 individuals from the fields of health education, sexuality education, public health, public policy, philanthropy and advocacy” to create what they call “national sexuality education standards (PDF).” The report says that the goal of the proposed standards is to “provide clear, consistent and straightforward guidance on the essential minimum, core content for sexuality education that is developmentally and age-appropriate for students in Grades K–12.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should We Have National Standards for Sex Education?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Abstinence (Sexual)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Education', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T20:24:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ca6565c-375f-59eb-a5d8-8ee287577a6e', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ca6565c-375f-59eb-a5d8-8ee287577a6e'}, {'abstract': 'Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/have-n-f-l-questions-judy-battista-has-answers-8/', 'snippet': 'Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Are the Texans underrated? Where will Andrew Luck land? How many more coaches will lose their jobs before the draft? Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers. Use the comment field below for your questions. Answers will appear Friday on The Fifth Down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Have N.F.L. Questions? Judy Battista Has Answers', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Battista, Judy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Texans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T20:25:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4779ea6-831c-570e-b1e9-9dcae495d975', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4779ea6-831c-570e-b1e9-9dcae495d975'}, {'abstract': 'The two-plus-two hybrid sports coupe immediately rendered Lexus’ $375,000 carbon-fiber supercar dated-looking, if not obsolete.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/with-racy-lf-lc-lexus-risks-the-ire-of-lf-a-buyers/', 'snippet': 'The two-plus-two hybrid sports coupe immediately rendered Lexus’ $375,000 carbon-fiber supercar dated-looking, if not obsolete.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Introduced on Monday, Jan. 9: Lexus LF-LC concept.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Racy LF-LC, Lexus Risks the Ire of LF-A Buyers', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACURA DIVISION OF HONDA MOTOR CO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LEXUS DIVISION OF TOYOTA MOTOR SALES USA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T20:25:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Ulrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ulrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e36720e8-27c6-5b3a-a201-8144ce60faf6', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e36720e8-27c6-5b3a-a201-8144ce60faf6'}, {'abstract': 'If you’re a vegetarian or vegan living in the heartland, share your strategies for getting by.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/vegetarian-eating-in-the-land-of-iceberg-lettuce/', 'snippet': 'If you’re a vegetarian or vegan living in the heartland, share your strategies for getting by.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, A.G. Sulzberger, a national correspondent in the Kansas City bureau, writes about his plight as a vegetarian living in the meat-loving Midwest, where salads are often topped with crumbled bacon and beans are bathed in lard. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vegetarian Eating in the Land of Iceberg Lettuce', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T20:26:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/517b2ff9-fe85-5e76-a9dc-9fe7bf6bda55', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/517b2ff9-fe85-5e76-a9dc-9fe7bf6bda55'}, {'abstract': 'A report from the Department of Health and Human Services says a state agency lacks independence from the governor’s office and has broken several requirements of federal law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/nyregion/federal-government-criticizes-new-york-on-disabled-care.html', 'snippet': 'A report from the Department of Health and Human Services says a state agency lacks independence from the governor’s office and has broken several requirements of federal law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — The federal government sharply criticized New York’s oversight of the developmentally disabled in a new report, saying the state agency charged with oversight lacks independence from the governor’s office, failed to account for how it is spending public money and has broken several requirements of federal law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Report Criticizes New York on Monitoring Care of Developmentally Disabled', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Report Criticizes New York on Monitoring Care of Developmentally Disabled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Abuse of the Disabled', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office for People With Developmental Disabilities (NYS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commission on Quality of Care and Advocacy for Persons With Disabilities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T20:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danny Hakim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a55988c-e52d-5eb4-8920-b4eaa92bff2b', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a55988c-e52d-5eb4-8920-b4eaa92bff2b'}, {'abstract': 'The Packers beat the Giants, 38-35, on Dec. 4, an exciting game that showcased strategies and tendencies that could come into play again on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/sports/football/giants-know-they-can-match-packers-score-for-score.html', 'snippet': 'The Packers beat the Giants, 38-35, on Dec. 4, an exciting game that showcased strategies and tendencies that could come into play again on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Green Bay Packers games are best thought of as basketball games. The Packers are going to score often. Their opponents are going to score often. Defensive play is more appropriately measured in stops and turnovers, not necessarily points allowed. Every forced punt is a success. Keeping the score close gives either team a chance to win in the final seconds.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/sports/JPBREAKDOWN1/JPBREAKDOWN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/sports/JPBREAKDOWN1/JPBREAKDOWN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/sports/JPBREAKDOWN1/JPBREAKDOWN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/sports/JPBREAKDOWN1/JPBREAKDOWN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/sports/JPBREAKDOWN1/JPBREAKDOWN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Know They Can Match the Packers Score for Score', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Instant Replay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ballard, Jake', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicks, Hakeem', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierre-Paul, Jason', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodgers, Aaron', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T20:34:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name':