cting Yet Ugly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T20:37:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c544898f-1b62-5344-a883-d9133a4d432a', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c544898f-1b62-5344-a883-d9133a4d432a'}, {'abstract': 'The crew of the U.S.S. Chung-Hoon gave Billy Hurley, a Naval Academy graduate who served on the ship from 2007 to 2009, an enthusiastic reception in Honolulu ahead of his PGA Tour debut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/sports/golf/naval-officer-embarks-on-pga-tour-career.html', 'snippet': 'The crew of the U.S.S. Chung-Hoon gave Billy Hurley, a Naval Academy graduate who served on the ship from 2007 to 2009, an enthusiastic reception in Honolulu ahead of his PGA Tour debut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONOLULU — Over lunch Monday in the wardroom of the U.S.S. Chung-Hoon, Lt. j.g. Lauren Griebel acknowledged that she met President Obama over the holidays while playing a round of golf with her father on a local course. Smiling broadly, Griebel said, “It wasn’t Billy Hurley, but yeah.” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/sports/YGOLF2/YGOLF2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/sports/YGOLF2/YGOLF2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': 