itle': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/c70a0ce5-4baa-5cd3-b266-04a9bbc3b20b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/c70a0ce5-4baa-5cd3-b266-04a9bbc3b20b'}, {'abstract': 'Five to seven meetings among conference commissioners between now and July 4 will help shape the future of the college football postseason.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/sports/ncaafootball/talks-begin-with-an-open-mind-on-college-football-playoff.html', 'snippet': 'Five to seven meetings among conference commissioners between now and July 4 will help shape the future of the college football postseason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — Street sweepers washed away the celebratory beads and the other remnants from the revelry that followed Monday night’s Bowl Championship Series title game. And as fans poured out of the city, 11 conference commissioners and Notre Dame Athletic Director Jack Swarbrick met Tuesday to begin cleaning up the future of college football’s postseason.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/sports/BCS/BCS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 854, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/sports/BCS/BCS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/sports/BCS/BCS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With an Open Mind on a Playoff, Conference Commissioners Meet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With an Open Mind on a Playoff, Conference Commissioners Meet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'k