to a major report released on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/world/SUB-INDIA/SUB-INDIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/world/SUB-INDIA/SUB-INDIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/world/SUB-INDIA/SUB-INDIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Malnutrition Widespread in Indian Children, Report Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Malnutrition Widespread in Indian Children, Report Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Malnutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T22:08:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47b42fa8-091e-5738-b6b4-72adb4ca5ee1', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47b42fa8-091e-5738-b6b4-72adb4ca5ee1'}, {'abstract': 'More on Lucas, Cochrane, and all that.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/mistakes-and-ideology/', 'snippet': 'More on Lucas, Cochrane, and all that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark Thoma sends us to Simon Wren-Lewis on the controversy over fiscal stimulus and all that; Wren-Lewis, refreshingly, doesn’t try to make excuses for Lucas and Cochrane:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mistakes and Ideology', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T22:10:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/002a4e75-7cb8-5b35-9706-54ab3be5f56d', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/002a4e75-7cb8-5b35-9706-54ab3be5f56d'}, {'abstract': 'In an appointment with election-year ramifications, Cecilia Muñoz will be director of the Domestic Policy Council.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/hispanic-adviser-is-promoted-at-white-house/', 'snippet': 'In an appointment with election-year ramifications, Cecilia Muñoz will be director of the Domestic Policy Council.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The White House said Tuesday that Cecilia Muñoz, who has led its efforts to overhaul immigration laws, had been named director of the Domestic Policy Council, making her one of President Obama’s chief advisers on a broad swath of issues, including education and gay rights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hispanic Adviser Is Promoted at White House', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T22:11:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b5dccfc-1bf9-50aa-a64c-061d69a85139', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b5dccfc-1bf9-50aa-a64c-061d69a85139'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from New Hampshire, Italy, Nigeria and Pakistan.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/pictures-of-the-day-new-hampshire-and-elsewhere-2/', 'snippet': 'Photographs from New Hampshire, Italy, Nigeria and Pakistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from New Hampshire, Italy, Nigeria and Pakistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: New Hampshire and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T22:18:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b12f6ee-6a2d-56f4-98dc-c400902c585e', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b12f6ee-6a2d-56f4-98dc-c400902c585e'}, {'abstract': 'Polls close at 7 p.m. Eastern time in most of the state, although the bulk of results will not be reported until after 8 p.m. In the meantime, there should be some demographic insights available from exit polls as well as a few statistical findings that we have to share with you.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/live-blogging-the-new-hampshire-primary/', 'snippet': 'Polls close at 7 p.m. Eastern time in most of the state, although the bulk of results will not be reported until after 8 p.m. In the meantime, there should be some demographic insights available from exit polls as well as a few statistical finding...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to FiveThirtyEight’s live blog of the New Hampshire primary. Polls have closed, and The New York Times has projected Mitt Romney as the winner, but we will still have plenty of statistical insights into the election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Analysis From the New Hampshire Primary', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T22:20:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcb20a76-d97d-5ab5-bb89-d377b8b85ada', 'word_count': 2682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcb20a76-d97d-5ab5-bb89-d377b8b85ada'}, {'abstract': 'The songs of Walter Donaldson and Gus Kahn open the Lyrics & Lyricists season at the 92nd Street Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/arts/music/makin-whoopee-at-the-92nd-street-y-review.html', 'snippet': 'The songs of Walter Donaldson and Gus Kahn open the Lyrics & Lyricists season at the 92nd Street Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An erupting wellspring of euphoria: that would describe the vintage swing emanating from Vince Giordano and the Nighthawks at the 92nd Street Y during Saturday evening’s season-opening program of Lyrics & Lyricists. It is challenging enough for a band to churn out museum-ready facsimiles of 80-year-old pop tunes outfitted with stylistically accurate period arrangements. But Mr. Giordano’s ensemble, like the Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra playing the blues, preserves old music with such deep affection and idiomatic understanding that the past becomes the present and the term “quaint” simply doesn’t apply. In its lighthearted way, the music swung as intensely as any being created today. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/LYRICS/LYRICS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/LYRICS/LYRICS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/LYRICS/LYRICS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/LYRICS/LYRICS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/LYRICS/LYRICS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jaunty Songs That Reveal a Bleaker Reality', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jaunty Songs That Reveal a Bleaker Reality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donaldson, Walter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ninety-Second Street Y', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'kahn, Gus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T22:22:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/172f825c-7f03-5b88-954e-31e2dc654008', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/172f825c-7f03-5b88-954e-31e2dc654008'}, {'abstract': 'Carven’s Guillaume Henry found inspiration in Diane Arbus photographs from the 1960s for his prefall collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/just-one-look-carven/', 'snippet': 'Carven’s Guillaume Henry found inspiration in Diane Arbus photographs from the 1960s for his prefall collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carven’s Guillaume Henry was looking at Diane Arbus photographs from the 1960s for inspiration for his prefall collection. “Ordinary people looking extraordinary,” said Henry about his muse: a very specific suburban girl who rides the subway in the early morning, is moody, makes her own clothes (or wears her mother’s) and wants to look pretty but can only afford synthetic shoes. Hence, the plastic tortoise kitten heels, the fabrics that make references to shag carpets and couches (her only resources) and the jackets made of a leather that’s washed to look faux (she’s just not that fancy). “She’s sweet looking but not dull,” Henry said. And she has a terrific, intuitive sense of style, one that doesn’t require money. Here, because he likes “calm, strong, happy colors with metallics,” is a yellow shearling jacket and skirt look paired with the coolest metallic pumps and matching camera bag. Anything but dull, indeed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Carven', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywor