37, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a7f21e9-c3c2-5f8a-af78-2ca33e9765d0'}, {'abstract': 'Scott M. Stringer, the Manhattan borough president and a likely candidate for mayor, held a press conference to denounce what he said was a rash of episodes.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/stringer-and-jewish-leaders-condemn-anti-semitic-acts/', 'snippet': 'Scott M. Stringer, the Manhattan borough president and a likely candidate for mayor, held a press conference to denounce what he said was a rash of episodes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scott M. Stringer, the Manhattan borough president and a likely candidate for mayor, held a press conference on Tuesday with a group of Jewish leaders to denounce what he said was a rash of anti-Semitic episodes in the city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stringer and Jewish Leaders Condemn Anti-Semitic Acts', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stringer, Scott M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T22:36:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9245af5-e3b6-5b6d-8f06-f209166aaa3c', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9245af5-e3b6-5b6d-8f06-f209166aaa3c'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists close in on the zone of overlap between Gambel’s and elegant quail species in Mexico.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/two-quail-species-in-the-brush/', 'snippet': 'Scientists close in on the zone of overlap between Gambel’s and elegant quail species in Mexico.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jennifer Gee, a biologist at the Claremont University Consortium and the University of California, Riverside, writes from the tropical dry forest near Álamos, Mexico, where she and Jennifer Calkins are studying Callipepla quail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Quail Species in the Brush', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ranches', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T22:38:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Gee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/294ec590-a27c-5028-beb2-e75a718be263', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/294ec590-a27c-5028-beb2-e75a718be263'}, {'abstract': 'Two Republicans in California’s Congressional delegation say they will step down, as three more mull their options after redistricting.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/with-house-redistricting-looming-2-california-republicans-retire/', 'snippet': 'Two Republicans in California’s Congressional delegation say they will step down, as three more mull their options after redistricting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Days after Representative Elton Gallegly announced his retirement from Congress, another veteran California Republican in the House said he, too, planned to forgo a bid for re-election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With House Redistricting Looming, 2 California Republicans Retire', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T22:39:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d5fac34-3449-5e70-b8d5-0d5e2c5f145c', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d5fac34-3449-5e70-b8d5-0d5e2c5f145c'}, {'abstract': 'The chief curator at Tate Modern in London is to join the Metropolitan to raise its profile in contemporary art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/arts/design/metropolitan-museum-hires-tate-modern-curator-for-contemporary-art.html', 'snippet': 'The chief curator at Tate Modern in London is to join the Metropolitan to raise its profile in contemporary art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sending a signal that it intends to become a serious competitor in the field of contemporary art for the first time in half a century, the Metropolitan Museum of Art has recruited a prominent London curator to oversee a new department devoted to art of the 20th and 21st centuries. She is Sheena Wagstaff, chief curator of Tate Modern since 2001, who has been responsible for programming there and for helping to organize exhibitions devoted to artists like Roy Lichtenstein, Barnett Newman, Jeff Wall and Eva Hesse. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/MET-JP/MET-JP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/MET-JP/MET-JP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/MET-JP/MET-JP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Met Gears Up to Be a Player in Contemporary Art', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Met Gears Up to Be a Major Player in Contemporary Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T22:40:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ba49967-064e-50a9-acab-21046b11ba77', 'word_count': 1153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ba49967-064e-50a9-acab-21046b11ba77'}, {'abstract': 'Makerbot, a Brooklyn-based start-up that builds 3-D printers announced its latest offering on Tuesday, the MakerBot Replicator. The new 3-D printer can make larger objects than the company’s previous 3-D printers.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/makerbot-introduces-new-larger-two-color-3-d-printer/', 'snippet': 'Makerbot, a Brooklyn-based start-up that builds 3-D printers announced its latest offering on Tuesday, the MakerBot Replicator. The new 3-D printer can make larger objects than the company’s previous 3-D printers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three-dimensional printing is getting more sophisticated. Makerbot, a Brooklyn-based start-up that builds 3-D printers for the consumer market, announced its latest offering on Tuesday, the MakerBot Replicator.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Makerbot Introduces Larger, Two-Color 3-D Printer', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MakerBot Industries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T22:58:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0ed241a-5d74-559c-a383-71fa9a0959b7', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0ed241a-5d74-559c-a383-71fa9a0959b7'}, {'abstract': 'The two states with the largest influence on the primary process fail to reflect the demographics of the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/view-of-the-world-from-new-hampshire-and-iowa/', 'snippet': 'The two states with the largest influence on the primary process fail to reflect the demographics of the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. —While traveling around Iowa and New Hampshire, I’ve been surrounded by white people. With few exceptions, the only non-whites I’ve encountered have been journalists who’ve parachuted into these states to cover the Republican campaigns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'View of the World From New Hampshire and Iowa', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T23:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ed0c7b8-8e97-50e1-8ced-f5a8d7b57e4b', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ed0c7b8-8e97-50e1-8ced-f5a8d7b57e4b'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney has won the New Hampshire Republican primary, achieving a sweep of the first two critical contests in the 2012 presidential race and boosting his chances at becoming his party’s nominee this fall.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/new-hampshire-primary-live-blog/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney has won the New Hampshire Republican primary, achieving a sweep of the first two critical contests in the 2012 presidential race and boosting his chances at becoming his party’s nominee this fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Mitt Romney has won the New Hampshire Republican primary, achieving a sweep of the first two critical contests in the 2012 presidential race and boosting his chances at becoming his party’s nominee this fall. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Hampshire Primary Live Blog', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T23:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c98c1fec-edc8-537d-9a33-12cc97e7c6e8', 'word_count': 11622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c98c1fec-edc8-537d-9a33-12cc97e7c6e8'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Kliën’s “Choreography for Blackboards,” created with Steve Valk, had its American premiere at the Invisible Dog Art Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/arts/dance/choreography-for-blackboards-at-invisible-dog-review.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Kliën’s “Choreography for Blackboards,” created with Steve Valk, had its American premiere at the Invisible Dog Art Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The drawing was already under way Sunday afternoon when I arrived a few minutes early at the Invisible Dog Art Center for Michael Kliën’s “Choreography for Blackboards” (created in collaboration with the dramaturge Steve Valk), which had its American premiere as part of Performance Space 122’s Coil festival. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/BOARDS/BOARDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/BOARDS/BOARDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/BOARDS/BOARDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Doodles, Puddles, Responses and Chalk', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Doodles, Puddles, Responses And Chalk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coil Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T23:03:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba758667-3113-59df-9286-f6d5166dcc14', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba758667-3113-59df-9286-f6d5166dcc14'}, {'abstract': 'The New School’s chamber music series featured a performance by the Amphion String Quartet, an impressive ensemble that was started at Yale in 2009.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/arts/music/amphion-string-quartet-in-schneider-concerts-review.html', 'snippet': 'The New School’s chamber music series featured a performance by the Amphion String Quartet, an impressive ensemble that was started at Yale in 2009.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New School’s chamber music series, founded in 1957 and called the Schneider Concerts (in honor of the violinist Alexander Schneider) since 1993, has a dual mission. For young but accomplished ensembles, it is a venerable forum, known for its sterling track record. The pianist Peter Serkin made his New York debut in the series, as did the Guarneri Quartet, and you could have heard early performances by Murray Perahia and Yo-Yo Ma there. For its audiences the Schneider Concerts are an inexpensive way to hear consistently fine performances. (Tickets go for $17; $15 for 65+; and $5 for students.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/amphion/amphion-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/amphion/amphion-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/amphion/amphion-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/amphion/amphion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/amphion/amphion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shining a Bright Light on Stormy Passages', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shining a Bright Light on Stormy Passages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Amphion String Quartet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New School', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-10T23:04:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccca68da-3277-5f9b-911d-a4d7ff6ae956', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccca68da-3277-5f9b-911d-a4d7ff6ae956'}, {'abstract': 'Small plates in the Financial District from the former chef at Vandaag.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/