ts to keep up with the latest developments.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/tvs-that-keep-up-with-evolution/', 'snippet': 'Samsung says it will sell a kit to allow consumers to reboot their TV sets to keep up with the latest developments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — The idea of a smart television is a few years old, but it is evolving so rapidly that Samsung Electronics is worried that consumers may be reluctant to buy a television for fear of missing out on the next big thing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TVs That Keep Up With Evolution', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television Sets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Electronics Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T01:18:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccd052f0-7eb2-54bf-8541-f4f5cbea82df', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccd052f0-7eb2-54bf-8541-f4f5cbea82df'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court should end the Federal Communications Commission’s misguided indecency policy for radio and television broadcasts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/opinion/one-first-amendment.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court should end the Federal Communications Commission’s misguided indecency policy for radio and television broadcasts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Constitution generally prohibits the government from suppressing words and images unless they are obscene. But the Supreme Court upheld a narrow exception to this free speech tenet in 1978, letting the Federal Communications Commission ban “indecent but not obscene” material from radio and television because it said broadcast media were pervasive and accessible to children. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One First Amendment', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One First Amendment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indecency, Obscenity and Profanity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T01:19:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d24b488-0ceb-5864-bd56-cf83287dc8a4', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d24b488-0ceb-5864-bd56-cf83287dc8a4'}, {'abstract': 'The outcome was a measure of strength for Mitt Romney and a test for challengers seeking a strong performance to propel them into the South Carolina primary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/us/politics/mitt-romney-wins-in-new-hampshire-republican-primary.html', 'snippet': 'The outcome was a measure of strength for Mitt Romney and a test for challengers seeking a strong performance to propel them into the South Carolina primary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Mitt Romney swept to victory in the New Hampshire primary on Tuesday, turning back a ferocious assault from rivals who sought to disqualify him in the eyes of conservatives, in a contest that failed to anoint a strong opponent to slow his march to the Republican nomination.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/us/11elect_span3/11elect_span3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/us/11elect_span3/11elect_span3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/us/11elect_span3/11elect_span3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/us/11elect_span3/11elect_span3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/us/11elect_span3/11elect_span3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Wins G.O.P. Primary in New Hampshire', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney Is Winner In New Hampshire Blunting Attacks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T01:19:3