enetics-pioneer-dies-at-95.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Crow was a leading exponent of a subject that aided the understanding of evolutionary change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James F. Crow, a leader in the field of population genetics who helped shape public policy toward atomic radiation damage and the use of DNA in the courtroom, died last Wednesday at his home in Madison, Wis. He was 95.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/us/CROW-obit/CROW-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/us/CROW-obit/CROW-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/us/CROW-obit/CROW-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'James F. Crow, Population Genetics Pioneer, Dies at 95', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'James F. Crow Is Dead at 95; Population Genetics Pioneer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Wisconsin-Madison', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T01:34:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Wade', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wade', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/179441f0-8297-590a-9ebc-1294e05014eb', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/179441f0-8297-590a-9ebc-1294e05014eb'}, {'abstract': 'The private equity industry has come under scrutiny as Mitt Romney’s Republican rivals have attacked his record at the investment firm Bain Capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/business/as-romney-campaign-advances-private-equity-becomes-part-of-the-debate.html', 'snippet': 'The private equity industry has come under scrutiny as Mitt Romney’s Republican rivals have attacked his record at the investment firm Bain Capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The titans of private equity have long feared this moment. As Mitt Romney has established himself as the front-runner for the Republican nomination, not only has his record at Bain Capital come under intense scrutiny and withering attacks — but so has the private equity industry.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/us/PRIVATE/PRIVATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/us/PRIVATE/PRIVATE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/us/PRIVATE/PRIVATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/us/PRIVATE/PRIVATE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/us/PRIVATE/PRIVATE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Romney Advances, Private Equity Becomes Part of the Debate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Romney Campaign Advances, Private Equity Becomes Part of the Debate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T01:45:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman and Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39b4ed41-63a5-5f47-9859-40f67fe799ce', 'word_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39b4ed41-63a5-5f47-9859-40f67fe799ce'}, {'abstract': 'The move to reduce the routine use of antibiotics in livestock, which creates drug-resistant pathogens, is far from sufficient.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/opinion/fda-creeps-forward.html', 'snippet': 'The move to reduce the routine use of antibiotics in livestock, which creates drug-resistant pathogens, is far from sufficient.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, the Food and Drug Administration took a small step toward reducing the routine use of antibiotics in livestock, a practice that creates drug-resistant pathogens and threatens the effectiveness of some antibiotics in human medicine. It restricted the use of a class of antibiotics called cephalosporins. Because they require a prescription, farm veterinarians use them less than other antibiotics, like penicillin.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Creeps Forward', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.D.A. Creeps Forward', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIBIOTICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factory Farming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Livestock', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T01:46:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3ce8a67-ead0-549d-b962-1cda1e193df2', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3ce8a67-ead0-549d-b962-1cda1e193df2'}, {'abstract': 'This week, New York City’s busiest train line is shutting down four nights for repairs, closing off a central artery between Midtown Manhattan and Downtown Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/nyregion/new-york-city-subway-closes-for-overnight-repairs.html', 'snippet': 'This week, New York City’s busiest train line is shutting down four nights for repairs, closing off a central artery between Midtown Manhattan and Downtown Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a fundamental birthright of New Yorkers that their subway never stops for a breather. The city stays up all night, and so its trains must follow suit. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/nyregion/SUBWAY1/SUBWAY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/nyregion/SUBWAY1/SUBWAY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/nyregion/SUBWAY1/SUBWAY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/nyregion/SUBWAY1/SUBWAY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/nyregion/SUBWAY1/SUBWAY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Seismic Shift for the Subway: Closing Lines for Night Repairs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For the Subway That Never Rests, A Seismic Shift In Night Closings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Transit Authority', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T01:49:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e81113b5-4863-5c60-8038-ffd483870d1a', 'word_count': 886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e81113b5-4863-5c60-8038-ffd483870d1a'}, {'abstract': 'Miguel Batista has signed with the Mets for the 2012 season; his role has yet to be determined.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/mets-sign-batista/', 'snippet': 'Miguel Batista has signed with the Mets for the 2012 season; his role has yet to be determined.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Miguel Batista pitched the final game of the 2011 season for the Mets, beating Cincinnati, 3-0, at age 40 to become the oldest pitcher in franchise history to throw a shutout. Now Batista will try to see what he can do for the Mets at 41. Batista has signed with them for the 2012 season; his role has yet to be determined.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Sign Batista', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Batista, Miguel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T01:49:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Schreiber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schreiber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70f3e343-4956-57c2-bb9d-88f7e36b0d1c', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70f3e343-4956-57c2-bb9d-88f7e36b0d1c'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney declared on Tuesday night that his campaign had “made history” in New Hampshire and vowed to continue on to South Carolina as he pursues be his party’s nomination.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/mitt-romney-focuses-on-obama-during-victory-speech/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney declared on Tuesday night that his campaign had “made history” in New Hampshire and vowed to continue on to South Carolina as he pursues be his party’s nomination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Mitt Romney declared on Tuesday night that his campaign had “made history” in New Hampshire and vowed to continue on to South Carolina as he pursues his party’s nomination to take on President Obama in the fall. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Focuses on Obama During Victory Speech', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T01:50:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27c00670-6309-5038-859b-176d82ec9d19', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27c00670-6309-5038-859b-176d82ec9d19'}, {'abstract': 'Full-time online schools may be inappropriate for a majority of students and need to be monitored closely.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/opinion/troubled-online-charter-schools.html', 'snippet': 'Full-time online schools may be inappropriate for a majority of students and need to be monitored closely.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charter schools, which receive public money but are subject to fewer state regulations, are operating in 40 states. A growing body of research shows that charter schools generally perform no better than traditional schools and are often worse as measured by student test data. This is particularly true of online charter schools, which educate more than 200,000 full-time students and are spreading quickly across the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Troubled Online Charter Schools', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Troubled Online Charter Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'K12 Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Charter Schools', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T01:52:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0a9d113-1431-5b32-8905-bf45e9f774f6', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0a9d113-1431-5b32-8905-bf45e9f774f6'}, {'abstract': 'A prevailing sense among New Hampshire primary voters that Mitt Romney is the candidate most likely to defeat President Obama helped lift him to victory.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/10/how-romney-won/', 'snippet': 'A prevailing sense among New Hampshire primary voters that Mitt Romney is the candidate most likely to defeat President Obama helped lift him to victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — A prevailing sense among New Hampshire primary voters that Mitt Romney is the candidate most likely to defeat Barack Obama helped lift him to victory on Tuesday.', 'source': 'T