rapher based in Toronto, was inspired by Eugene Richards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christopher Manson is a British photographer based in Toronto and a recent graduate of Ryerson University. Mr. Manson, 32,\xa0 has spent the last year working on a project about teenagers with Type 1 diabetes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photographing an Invisible Subject', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Eugene', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Getty Images', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T10:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Hamblett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamblett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3e848d8-736f-567a-b84c-be62b2bfcb04', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3e848d8-736f-567a-b84c-be62b2bfcb04'}, {'abstract': 'More than you think. Without it, the 99 percent would be a whole lot poorer, and there definitely wouldn’t be any good goat cheese.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/magazine/what-does-wall-street-do-for-you.html', 'snippet': 'More than you think. Without it, the 99 percent would be a whole lot poorer, and there definitely wouldn’t be any good goat cheese.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hating Wall Street is an American tradition that dates back even to the days when Thomas Jefferson cursed that money lover Alexander Hamilton. And for centuries, the complaints about it have largely stayed the same: It does nothing! It creates chaos! It’s a parasite that sucks hardworking Americans dry! (Or something to that effect.) But these are distortions of a fundamentally beneficial business. The country’s largest investment banks, commercial banks and a few big insurance companies (what we generally refer to as Wall Street) play the crucial role of intermediation — matching borrowers with lenders. Most of the time, the industry does this extremely well (though in the case of matching homeowners’ debt to the global financial system, too enthusiastically). Perhaps the best way to really appreciate what Wall Street does is to imagine life without it.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15economy_span/15economy_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15economy_span/15economy_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15economy_span/15economy_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15economy_span/15economy_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15economy_span/15economy_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Does Wall Street Do for You?', 'kicker': 'It’s the Economy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A World Without Wall Street', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T10:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Davidson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davidson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72e9f575-b20f-5ec6-8090-5acf6a1a5527', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72e9f575-b20f-5ec6-8090-5acf6a1a5527'}, {'abstract': 'Tottenham has quietly moved up to third in the Premier League, and can tie Manchester United for second place by winning a makeup game against Everton on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/tottenham-works-its-way-back-to-the-top/', 'snippet': 'Tottenham has quietly moved up to third in the Premier League, and can tie Manchester United for second place by winning a makeup game against Everton on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rob Hughes writes Tuesday about Tottenham’s quiet rise to third place in the Premier League in a season that began with the riots near its home stadium. The disturbances forced the postponement of Tottenham’s opener against Everton, and its Premier League schedule began instead with consecutive losses to Manchester United and Manchester City.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tottenham Works Its Way Back to the Top', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tottenham Hotspur (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T10:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebc832ff-a925-5256-9145-ab77d2bc4d2a', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebc832ff-a925-5256-9145-ab77d2bc4d2a'}, {'abstract': 'The writer, comedian and Golden Globe host has made a great career of irreverence. But his best trick is being just reverent enough to keep getting invited to the party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/magazine/ricky-gervais-would-like-to-non-apologize.html', 'snippet': 'The writer, comedian and Golden Globe host has made a great career of irreverence. But his best trick is being just reverent enough to keep getting invited to the party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a onetime mess hall on a decommissioned Royal Air Force base outside London, Ricky Gervais was directing the 4-foot-6 star of a low-budget re-enactment of “The Passion of the Christ” on how to play the Crucifixion for more laughs.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15gervais1_span/15gervais1_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15gervais1_span/15gervais1_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 