asia/north-korea-opens-door-to-american-food-aid.html', 'snippet': 'The country accused the United States “politicizing” the assistance, but still indicated that it may be willing to engage Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — North Korea indicated on Wednesday that it was open to further negotiations with the United States, which it said demanded a halt of its uranium-enrichment program in return for food aid before the death of Kim Jong-il last month.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea Open to Talks on Nuclear Program', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korea Suggests That It Is Open to More Nuclear Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Aid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T10:05:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b82a00a8-c5ea-5ae0-a6ec-e1a4d8676794', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b82a00a8-c5ea-5ae0-a6ec-e1a4d8676794'}, {'abstract': 'Student Opinion |  Tell us what game you’d like to see redesigned, whether a board game, a game you play with others online, a classic video game, or even a centuries-old childhood game like hide and seek.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/what-game-would-you-like-to-redesign/', 'snippet': 'Student Opinion |  Tell us what game you’d like to see redesigned, whether a board game, a game you play with others online, a classic video game, or even a centuries-old childhood game like hide and seek.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Have you ever played Dungeons & Dragons, the first commercially published role-playing game? What are your favorite games, online and off? If you were given the chance to redesign a game of any kind, as the hundreds of thousands of passionate “D&D” fans soon will be, what changes or updates would you recommend? Why?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Game Would You Like to Redesign?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T10:07:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f03d1fbf-8a2b-542d-b64a-0ca98e38c47c', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f03d1fbf-8a2b-542d-b64a-0ca98e38c47c'}, {'abstract': 'The government reported that the German economy expanded by 3 percent in 2011, but estimated that it actually contracted in the final quarter of the year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/business/global/data-show-german-economy-stalling.html', 'snippet': 'The government reported that the German economy expanded by 3 percent in 2011, but estimated that it actually contracted in the final quarter of the year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The German economy expanded faster than any other Group of 7 nation last year, official data showed Wednesday, but the stress of the euro crisis and a slowing global economy appear to be already weighing on output.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/business/Euro/Euro-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/12/business/Euro/Euro-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/business/Euro/Euro-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Data Show German Economy Stalling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'German Economy Shows Signs of a Slowdown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T10:59:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cd33b98-b57e-58c3-b182-ed52e278fb33', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cd33b98-b57e-58c3-b182-ed52e278fb33'}, {'abstract': 'Analysis of differing approaches to unemployment insurance and its duration in the United States and Europe has not yet found an optimal length, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/20