d-push-for-more-reform-after-curbing-military-power/', 'snippet': 'Having conquered the bastions of the military establishment, the Turkish ruling party is now reluctant to press for reforms that could limit its own power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — The Turkish military has long regarded it as part of its job description to guard against the governments it serves. There have been three coups in Turkey since the end of World War II. And though the last one occurred more than 30 years ago, the armed forces have not surrendered their prerogative to call politicians to heel. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Game of Turkey', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Basbug, Ilker', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evren, Kenan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kilicdaroglu, Kemal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T11:41:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Finkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4353247-90d5-5861-94e0-2b45653b3929', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4353247-90d5-5861-94e0-2b45653b3929'}, {'abstract': 'Before the program, Johnson Security had no construction-related security business.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/