uncing on Wednesday that he was withdrawing his $1.7 billion bid to take over the metal recycler.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Icahn Drops Bid for Commercial Metals', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T13:51:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fd062c2-de51-5602-a6bc-0c07ea4e128a', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fd062c2-de51-5602-a6bc-0c07ea4e128a'}, {'abstract': 'Or actually the depression.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/feel-the-expansion/', 'snippet': 'Or actually the depression.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The WaPo has a heartrending story on the suffering being imposed on ordinary Greeks. So much for the doctrine of expansionary austerity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feel the Expansion', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T13:54:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/538dcc1b-7df3-5aff-b656-f4b8003e1a5e', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/538dcc1b-7df3-5aff-b656-f4b8003e1a5e'}, {'abstract': 'Aircraft flying over the India-Bangladesh border.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/image-of-the-day-january-11/', 'snippet': 'Aircraft flying over the India-Bangladesh border.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: January 11', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T13:56:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2c0c445-30b7-5f87-b82c-10324339ec48', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2c0c445-30b7-5f87-b82c-10324339ec48'}, {'abstract': 'To celebrate 50 years of the spy-movie franchise Metro-Goldwyn-Maye and 20th Century Fox’s home entertainment division are releasing a collection containing 22 James Bond movies on Blu-ray.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/twenty-two-is-quite-enough-comprehensive-james-bond-boxed-set-is-planned/', 'snippet': 'To celebrate 50 years of the spy-movie franchise Metro-Goldwyn-Maye and 20th Century Fox’s home entertainment division are releasing a collection containing 22 James Bond movies on Blu-ray.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you had to limit yourself to just one James Bond-related purchase for your Q-approved high-end home entertainment system, which would you pick? An early Sean Connery classic like “Goldfinger”? A contemporary Daniel Craig reboot like “Casino Royale”? Or what about a boxed set of nearly every Bond film that’s been released over the last half-century? If you fall into that last category (and, presumably, have the financial backing of Her Majesty’s government) there will soon be a DVD collection to suit your refined tastes. Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer and 20th Century Fox’s home entertainment division announced that they are planning to sell a boxed set called “Bond 50,” celebrating 50 years of the spy-movie franchise and containing Blu-ray versions of the 22 canonical James Bond films that have so far been released, starting with “Dr. No” (1962).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twenty-Two Is Quite Enough: Comprehensive James Bond Boxed Set Is Planned', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blu-Ray Disc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bond, James (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connery, Sean', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Craig, Daniel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twentieth Century Fox', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T13:59:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb6ffc17-1173-5e0e-9298-59fbc4428f4e', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb6ffc17-1173-5e0e-9298-59fbc4428f4e'}, {'abstract': 'Albert Brooks talks about the lengths he went to to understand his violent character in “Drive.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/albert-brooks-finds-a-new-use-for-his-characters-backstory/', 'snippet': 'Albert Brooks talks about the lengths he went to to understand his violent character in “Drive.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the scene-stealers at the New York Film Critics Circle dinner on Monday was the best-supporting-actor winner, Albert Brooks, whose kudos began with an impromptu shout-out from Aaron Sorkin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Albert Brooks Finds a New Use for His Character’s Backstory', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Albert', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gosling, Ryan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Refn, Nicolas Winding', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorkin, Aaron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Film Critics Circle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T14:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5509c846-9526-55f3-a14a-03bc707645ef', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5509c846-9526-55f3-a14a-03bc707645ef'}, {'abstract': 'The actress, who stars alongside Kelsey Grammer in “Boss” on Starz, discusses her beauty regimen.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/face-time-hannah-ware/', 'snippet': 'The actress, who stars alongside Kelsey Grammer in “Boss” on Starz, discusses her beauty regimen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are not yet familiar with the actress Hannah Ware, I highly suggest you read on. Hailing from England, where she modeled for a while, she recently discovered her true calling\xa0—\xa0acting. I met up with her at her Brooklyn apartment while she was on hiatus from shooting “Boss,” a dark drama on the Starz network in which she plays Emma, the estranged daughter of Chicago’s mayor (Kelsey Grammer). The show is up for a Golden Globe this weekend, and Ware is looking forward to joining her castmates on the red carpet. She will no doubt be sporting a stylish ensemble, and her makeup will be fresh and modern, because, as you will see, this lady has great taste!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Face Time | Hannah Ware', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T14:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Turnbow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/187b7e85-8524-580b-af3e-e2114f7b24de', 'word_count': 1253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/187b7e85-8524-580b-af3e-e2114f7b24de'}, {'abstract': 'On not understanding what life is like for most Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/uncompassionate-conservatism/', 'snippet': 'On not understanding what life is like for most Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Atkins, over at Digby’s blog, gets at what I’ve been trying to say about Romney, and more eloquently:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uncompassionate Conservatism', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T14:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58e1811b-d50d-50a0-bdc1-048c69104078', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58e1811b-d50d-50a0-bdc1-048c69104078'}, {'abstract': 'Ydanis Rodriguez, a City Council member from northern Manhattan, has asked for permission to donate a $5,000 stipend to the Occupy Wall Street movement.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/councilman-seeks-to-donate-money-from-speaker-to-occupy-wall-street/', 'snippet': 'Ydanis Rodriguez, a City Council member from northern Manhattan, has asked for permission to donate a $5,000 stipend to the Occupy Wall Street movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several members of the New York City Council have embraced the cause of Occupy Wall Street, praising the movement, joining its marches and, in some cases, getting arrested alongside the demonstrators. Now one councilman wants to lavish something else on it: money.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Councilman Seeks to Donate Stipend to Occupy Wall Street', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'City Councils', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zuccotti Park (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T14:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f0d28d7-5272-5fa9-87b1-572bc3e0485c', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f0d28d7-5272-5fa9-87b1-572bc3e0485c'}, {'abstract': 'The prime minister fired his defense secretary as the government drew closer to a collision with the powerful military.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/world/asia/firing-of-pakistans-defense-secretary-raises-tension-with-army.html', 'snippet': 'The prime minister fired his defense secretary as the government drew closer to a collision with the powerful military.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — Prime Minister Yousaf Raza Gilani fired his defense secretary, a retired general and confidant of Pakistan’s army chief, on Wednesday as the civilian government appeared headed for a collision with the country’s powerful military leadership.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/world/12pakistan/12pakistan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/world/12pakistan/12pakistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/12/world/12pakistan/12pakistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Secretary’s Ouster in Pakistan Adds to Tension With Army', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistani Prime Minister Fires Defense Official, Stoking Tensions With Army', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilani, Yousaf Raza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kayani, Ashfaq Parvez', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T14:05:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8516e31d-9565-5396-ac54-c0d9be549c8d', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8516e31d-9565-5396-ac54-c0d9be549c8d'}, {'abstract': 'BlackRock retracted a notification that it had reduced its stake in the struggling Italian bank UniCredit after a query by Italy’s financial markets regulator.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/blackrock-maintains-stake-in-unicredit/', 'snippet': 'BlackRock retracted a notification that it had reduced its stake in the struggling Italian bank UniCredit after a query by Italy’s financial markets regulator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — BlackRock, the world’s largest asset manager, said on Wednesday that its stake in the struggling Italian bank UniCredit stood at 3.09 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BlackRock Says Its Stake in UniCredit Is Unchanged', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T14:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00f810e2-2e94-5a75-b00c-225490324a3a', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00f810e2-2e94-5a75-b00c-225490324a3a'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s Campaign Stops column.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/the-battle-of-the-also-rans/', 'snippet': 'This week’s Campaign Stops column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s Campaign Stops column looks at how the Republican primary became a battle for second place:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Battle of the Also-Rans', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T14:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df01eb11-7ee1-5514-a3af-be22c8f7c346', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df01eb11-7ee1-5514-a3af-be22c8f7c346'}, {'abstract': 'New York State wraps up the public comment period on regulations it has proposed for policing a controversial gas extraction method.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/a-deadline-for-fracking-comments/', 'snippet': 'New York State wraps up the public comment period on regulations it has proposed for policing a controversial gas extraction method.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As if the recent series of hearings and the invitation for written comments from the public were not enough, contingents from both sides of the fracking issue in New York State organized rallies and press conferences this week in anticipation of the close of the comment period on the state’s proposed gas drilling regulations on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Deadline for Fracking Comments', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shale', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Business Council of New York', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Environmental Conservation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marcellus Shale', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T14:17:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72f81f61-bcee-5463-a15a-5adae82f83b2', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72f81f61-bcee-5463-a15a-5adae82f83b2'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s campaign will announce Wednesday that it raised $24 million in the fourth quarter of 2011 and is going into 2012 with more than $19 million cash on hand.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/romney-raises-24-million-in-fourth-quarter/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s campaign will announce Wednesday that it raised $24 million in the fourth quarter of 2011 and is going into 2012 with more than $19 million cash on hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, N.H. — Mitt Romney‘s campaign will announce Wednesday morning that it raised $24 million for the fourth quarter of 2011 and is going into 2012 with more than $19 million cash on hand, several sources in the campaign confirmed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Raised $24 Million in Last Quarter', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'sub