', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cc6fa2e-0fdf-5b90-b411-659c064bdbf2', 'word_count': 1168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cc6fa2e-0fdf-5b90-b411-659c064bdbf2'}, {'abstract': 'Special needs calculators from Merrill Lynch and others can help families start planning for complex financial situations.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/financial-planning-calculators-for-those-with-special-needs/', 'snippet': 'Special needs calculators from Merrill Lynch and others can help families start planning for complex financial situations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Families with children who have special needs or disabilities face even bigger hurdles than most people when it comes to planning for their financial futures. Merrill Lynch Wealth Management has introduced\xa0 a free online special needs calculator to help parents and guardians get started in evaluating their situation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Financial Planning Calculators for Those with Special Needs', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Calculators', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Longevity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MetLife Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T16:11:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ead760c8-b897-5e9d-aade-ec81a998b50c', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ead760c8-b897-5e9d-aade-ec81a998b50c'}, {'abstract': 'Gervais’s relationship with other celebrities and his own celebrity status has been something of a moving target, the source of much comedy and, occasionally, some authentic discomfort.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/how-ricky-gervais-deals-with-fame-and-the-famous/', 'snippet': 'Gervais’s relationship with other celebrities and his own celebrity status has been something of a moving target, the source of much comedy and, occasionally, some authentic discomfort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since his much discussed performance as host of the 2011 Golden Globe Awards — one that forever put Charlie Sheen, Hugh Hefner and the “Sex and the City 2” poster in their places — Ricky Gervais has had a reputation as a comedian unafraid to tell harsh truths to a room full of famous people. But Gervais, a creator and star of the British version of “The Office,” has been having it both ways: as I write in an article in this weekend’s magazine, his true achievement is being irreverent enough to titillate audiences but reverent enough to his distinguished targets for them to invite him back to zing them yet again. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Ricky Gervais Deals With Fame and the Famous', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'David, Larry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gervais, Ricky', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibson, Mel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hefner, Hugh', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neeson, Liam', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T16:27:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7801d487-9efd-5a64-a87f-f52d73519e54', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7801d487-9efd-5a64-a87f-f52d73519e54'}, {'abstract': 'The trend of improving power efficiency in computing — Koomey’s Law — is, if anything, even more impressive than the long-term, steady advance in computer performance called Moore’s Law. Recognizing the energy-efficiency trendline becomes part of the thinking of engineers and executives, and an assumption in business planning and in imagining future products.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/a-new-law-for-the-mobile-computing-era/', 'snippet': 'The trend of improving power efficiency in computing — Koomey’s Law — is, if anything, even more impressive than the long-term, steady advance in computer performance called Moore’s Law. Recognizing the energy-efficiency trendline becomes part of ...', 'lead_paragraph': ' The new gadgetry at the International Consumer Electronics Show this week owes a lot to the crisp articulation of ever-increasing computer performance known as Moore’s Law. First proclaimed in 1965 by Intel’s co-founder Gordon Moore, it says that the number of transistors that can be put on a microchip doubles about every two years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New ‘Law’ for the Mobile Computing Era', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New u2018Lawu2019 For the Mobile Era', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koomey, Jonathan G', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Gordon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Gordon E', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T16:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e76ef80-ccf7-573d-827c-36e090e3404b', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e76ef80-ccf7-573d-827c-36e090e3404b'}, {'abstract': 'The Row added pops of color to its predominantly neutral palette for prefall.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/just-one-look-the-row-2/', 'snippet': 'The Row added pops of color to its predominantly neutral palette for prefall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Row, known for sticking to a predominantly neutral palette (black, gray, navy; spring 2012 was all white), added pops of two lively new colors — maroon and blush pink — to its repertory for prefall. True to the brand’s ethos, the collection was stocked with exquisitely tailored, wearable separates: leather jackets, T-shirts and skirts; cozy turtleneck sweaters; and crisp button-down shirts. Wow factor arrived in the form of alligator bags (new shapes include a flat shopper and a bucket, shown here), fox fur scarves and graphic fox fur coats, like this one.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | The Row', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T16:34:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4590de25-d8a4-59a2-ae08-d115fec21742', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4590de25-d8a4-59a2-ae08-d115fec21742'}, {'abstract': 'Aryca, a Chinese company, modified a pair of swimming goggles to include a watertight chamber that encloses an iPhone.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/iphone-goggles/', 'snippet': 'Aryca, a Chinese company, modified a pair of swimming goggles to include a watertight chamber that encloses an iPhone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Strap on these goofy goggles and you can videotape your adventures under the sea with your iPhone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goggles That Take Your iPhone Under the Sea', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T16:39:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d60e8c1-549d-54ce-a641-ffd6759140ac', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d60e8c1-549d-54ce-a641-ffd6759140ac'}, {'abstract': 'Called the “Cosmic Opera,” the series will feature performances by actors in burlesque garb, a live string orchestra, opera singers, elaborate stage sets and a complex laser show.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/dance-shows-coming-to-hammerstein-ballroom/', 'snippet': 'Called the “Cosmic Opera,” the series will feature performances by actors in burlesque garb, a live string orchestra, opera singers, elaborate stage sets and a complex laser show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A young entrepreneur from Long Island announced plans on Wednesday to stage a series of dance-music concerts at the Hammerstein Ballroom this year that will feature surreal projections on the walls of the Manhattan Center’s ornate room.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Multimedia Dance Shows Coming to Hammerstein Ballroom', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Timberlake, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cirque du Soleil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hammerstein Ballroom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Swedish House Mafia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T16:39:43+0000', 'document_