 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c493404f-e548-586f-b881-a312c8a25e2e', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c493404f-e548-586f-b881-a312c8a25e2e'}, {'abstract': 'The Dardennes brothers talk about their film “The Kid With a Bike,” which Belgium bypassed in its submission for foreign-language Oscar but which is up for a Golden Globe this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/the-dardennes-have-an-idea-about-the-selection-process/', 'snippet': 'The Dardennes brothers talk about their film “The Kid With a Bike,” which Belgium bypassed in its submission for foreign-language Oscar but which is up for a Golden Globe this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year there is at least one movie whose absence from the competition for the Academy Award for best foreign-language film causes critics and fans to question the selection process. Last year it was France’s critically acclaimed submission, “Of Gods and Men,” which won the Grand Prix at the Cannes Film Festival and many other European awards, but did not get an Oscar nomination or even a spot on the earlier shortlist of nine films.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dardennes Have an Idea About the Selection Process', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dardenne, Jean-Pierre', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dardenne, Luc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belgium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cannes (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T16:46:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c23dcc18-ba3d-519c-821e-77ba8e50195e', 'word_count': 1467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c23dcc18-ba3d-519c-821e-77ba8e50195e'}, {'abstract': 'President Bashar al-Assad addressed a rally in Damascus, thanking his supporters and pledging to defeat what he said were conspiracies against his country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/world/middleeast/president-assad-makes-rare-public-speech-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'President Bashar al-Assad addressed a rally in Damascus, thanking his supporters and pledging to defeat what he said were conspiracies against his country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — President Bashar al-Assad of Syria appeared in public on Wednesday for the first time since the uprising against his rule began 10 months ago, addressing a rally in Umayyad Square in Damascus. He thanked the crowd for its support and pledged to defeat what he said were conspiracies against his country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/world/syria/syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/12/world/syria/syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/world/syria/syria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/world/syria/syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/12/world/syria/syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbn