o be killed in a bomb attack on his car in Tehran on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video From Iran Shows Bombing Aftermath', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T17:02:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c4a2c52-1258-5f8d-9a14-a1f7ed9449a4', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c4a2c52-1258-5f8d-9a14-a1f7ed9449a4'}, {'abstract': 'The former Miami coach Tony Sparano figures to emphasize a power-running game for the Jets’ offense.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/sports/football/jets-sparano-offensive-coordinator.html', 'snippet': 'The former Miami coach Tony Sparano figures to emphasize a power-running game for the Jets’ offense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The University of New Haven’s football team was in Pennsylvania to play a game the next day, and its head coach, Tony Sparano, had just made a disturbing discovery: he had forgotten to pack his pants. Sparano wore the same pair — tan and polyester — for every game, and he was not about to stray from routine. His wife, Jeanette, drove back to Connecticut to collect the pants at the cleaners, then rushed back to Pennsylvania to present them to Sparano. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/sports/JETS/JETS-jumbo.jpg', 'h