 the bind faced by William Burris, the owner of a box-rental franchise in Washington, D.C., who learned that his franchisor had gone bankrupt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Can a Franchisee Do When the Chain Fails?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Franchises', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intellectual Property', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T17:03:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Darren Dahl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Darren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dahl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fb4f959-2ee6-5f99-8cb7-6ab89503efec', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fb4f959-2ee6-5f99-8cb7-6ab89503efec'}, {'abstract': 'Emma Stone, Rooney Mara and Keira Knightley were all inspired to leave calf-skimming coats unbuttoned over their dresses.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/winter-wonders-night-moves/', 'snippet': 'Emma Stone, Rooney Mara and Keira Knightley were all inspired to leave calf-skimming coats unbuttoned over their dresses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week’s freeze out transitioned into a springlike weekend, inspiring women to leave calf-skimming coats unbuttoned over their dresses. Here, the actress Rooney Mara wears a robelike piece in all black; the actress Emma Stone embraces winter white in a double-breasted trench with extra-large lapels; and the actress Keira Knightley chooses a long, ladylike take on the peacoat to pair with lace.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winter Wonders | Night Moves', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T17:08:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bccd61f6-fea0-5930-9151-53365cf5f97a', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bccd61f6-fea0-5930-9151-53365cf5f97a'}, {'abstract': 'Regulators agreed to require brokerage firms to segregate the accounts of swaps customers from company money. But the rule would not have prevented MF Global’s loss of customer money.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/regulator-adopts-new-customer-protection-rules/', 'snippet': 'Regulators agreed to require brokerage firms to segregate the accounts of swaps customers from company money. But the rule would not have prevented MF Global’s loss of customer money.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:16 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Rules on Swaps Will Protect Big Traders', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Futures and Options Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chilton, Bart', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gensler, Gary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sommers, Jill E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations