rds (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fincher, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaminski, Janusz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Society of Cinematographers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T18:51:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13878078-b05f-5757-a3a1-0faa4dc053ec', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13878078-b05f-5757-a3a1-0faa4dc053ec'}, {'abstract': '“Leap of Faith” would be the latest addition to a Broadway season that had a dearth of new original musicals only a few months ago.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/leap-of-faith-hoping-to-head-to-broadway-this-spring/', 'snippet': '“Leap of Faith” would be the latest addition to a Broadway season that had a dearth of new original musicals only a few months ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The producers of the new musical “Leap of Faith” are hoping to bring the show to Broadway this spring, instead of in fall 2012 as previously announced, according to one of the producers, Daryl Roth. In a newsletter sent to friends and colleagues and some journalists on Tuesday night about her current projects, Ms. Roth wrote that there should be news shortly on “Leap of Faith” and that “hopefully” it will open in the spring. The musical, which is expected to star four-time Tony Award nominee Raúl Esparza as an evangelical con man, has been rumored recently as the next tenant for the St. James Theater, given the possibility that its current musical, “On A Clear Day You Can See Forever,” will close soon. “On A Clear Day,” starring Harry Connick Jr., opened in December to mostly negative reviews and has been selling modestly at the box office.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Leap of Faith’ Hopes to  Land  on Broadway This Spring', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Leap of Faith (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Esparza, Raul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Daryl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St James Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T18:52:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ed9e257-9b6b-5095-ac46-64c06afc17dc', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ed9e257-9b6b-5095-ac46-64c06afc17dc'}, {'abstract': 'Less than two months in power, the moderate Islamic party of Prime Minister Abdelilah Benkirane is pushing to relax strict abortion laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/world/africa/new-prime-minister-surprises-moroccans-with-support-for-abortion.html', 'snippet': 'Less than two months in power, the moderate Islamic party of Prime Minister Abdelilah Benkirane is pushing to relax strict abortion laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CASABLANCA — Less than two months after winning power in Morocco’s elections, the moderate Islamic party of Prime Minister Abdelilah Benkirane is surprising opponents by moving to relax the country’s strict abortion laws.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/world/12abortion_337/12abortion_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Prime Minister Surprises Moroccans With Support for Abortion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Moroccan Government Seeks Relaxed Abortion Laws', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Morocco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T18:53:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Jay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f073b662-80fa-5d15-8c87-5d3262307a32', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f073b662-80fa-5d15-8c87-5d3262307a32'}, {'abstract': 'Calling all students ages 13 to 25: we’re facilitating a discussion about violence in hockey (and other sports). Join us!', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/reading-club-violence-in-hockey/', 'snippet': 'Calling all students ages 13 to 25: we’re facilitating a discussion about violence in hockey (and other sports). Join us!', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the third installment of the Learning Network Reading Club, the content is a gripping article in the series “Punched Out,” about the violence that takes place among hockey players serving in the role of enforcer, reported by The Times’s John Branch. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reading Club | Violence in Hockey', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T18:54:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f174879-c1f7-5c64-82e5-575621eaca1f', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f174879-c1f7-5c64-82e5-575621eaca1f'}, {'abstract': 'The discovery, scientists say, suggests there are probably millions of these so-called circumbinary planets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/science/scientists-find-more-planets-orbiting-two-stars.html', 'snippet': 'The discovery, scientists say, suggests there are probably millions of these so-called circumbinary planets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the “Star Wars” movies, Luke Skywalker’s home planet, Tatooine, orbits two suns, giving it two sunsets and two sunrises every day. In September, scientists discovered the first planet in our galaxy that orbits two stars; now they have discovered two more and suggest that there are probably millions of these so-called circumbinary planets in the Milky Way. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kepler Finds More Planets Orbiting Two Stars', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kepler Finds More Planets Orbiting Two Stars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kepler Space Telescope', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stars and Galaxies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', '