t://article/3ab34849-9d18-5ccf-a512-73294e6cf5be', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ab34849-9d18-5ccf-a512-73294e6cf5be'}, {'abstract': 'The Red Hot Chili Peppers’ lead vocalist has a broken foot.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/red-hot-chili-peppers-delay-tour-after-anthony-kiedis-has-surgery/', 'snippet': 'The Red Hot Chili Peppers’ lead vocalist has a broken foot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Red Hot Chili Peppers have postponed the start of their tour this year until late March because Anthony Kiedis, the group’s lead vocalist, has undergone surgery to repair a broken foot, according to the band’s Web site. The cause of the injury has not been made public, but surgeons operated on Mr. Kiedis’s right foot to remove a crushed sesamoid bone – a small bone in the ball of the foot at the base of the big toe — and to reattach a flexor tendon, the statement said. The 49-year-old front man is expected to recover fully.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Hot Chili Peppers Delay Tour After  Kiedis Has Surgery', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Red Hot Chili Peppers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tampa (Fla)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T19:02:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f83cc987-6607-5caa-8dc0-c8845093d4c3', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f83cc987-6607-5caa-8dc0-c8845093d4c3'}, {'abstract': 'Apple is expected to 