blican primary on Tuesday, but the Republican party is just a convenience for Mr. Paul, through which he spreads his other-worldly message. He is not really a member of the party in its current form, and more importantly, neither are many of his supporters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ron Paul’s Victory Speech', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T19:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc21ef65-f336-5959-a60a-c7f881a3fd6e', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc21ef65-f336-5959-a60a-c7f881a3fd6e'}, {'abstract': 'Members of the visual effects team for Terrence Malick’s “Tree of Life,” a family drama that flashes back to the origins of the universe, discuss video clips that showcase the processes they used to create certain effects.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/below-the-line-the-effects-of-the-tree-of-life/', 'snippet': 'Members of the visual effects team for Terrence Malick’s “Tree of Life,” a family drama that flashes back to the origins of the universe, discuss video clips that showcase the processes they used to create certain effects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A family drama usually isn’t the first kind of movie to come to mind when one thinks about visual effects. But “The Tree of Life,” Terrence Malick’s film that incorporates the formation of the universe into the tale of one Texas family, has awards prognosticators taking notice of its nontraditional visual techniques. The film is on the Oscar shortlist for best visual effects and is likely the only film listed there to have used computer-generated imagery, space photography, drops of colored dyes and splashes of half-and-half in tanks of water to generate its effects.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Below the Line: The Effects of ‘The Tree of Life’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dinosaurs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glass, Dan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malick, Terrence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T19:32:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a66aa2db-a84c-5a96-b560-0c2606d0be6f', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a66aa2db-a84c-5a96-b560-0c2606d0be6f'}, {'abstract': 'January 11, 2012 — In South Carolina, campaigns and “super PACs” have already committed to spending more than $5 million on TV ads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000001279195/south-carolina-media-deluge.html', 'snippet': 'January 11, 2012 — In South Carolina, campaigns and “super PACs” have already committed to spending more than $5 million on TV ads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'January 11, 2012 — In South Carolina, campaigns and “super PACs” have 