ame': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/681791fb-ce3e-5792-ab5d-7a70e2df09f2', 'word_count': 1844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/681791fb-ce3e-5792-ab5d-7a70e2df09f2'}, {'abstract': 'Olympia Dukakis will play a female version of the magician Prospero in a production of “The Tempest” this summer at Shakespeare & Company, based in Lenox, Mass.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/olympia-dukakis-to-play-prospero-for-shakespeare-company/', 'snippet': 'Olympia Dukakis will play a female version of the magician Prospero in a production of “The Tempest” this summer at Shakespeare & Company, based in Lenox, Mass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Olympia Dukakis will play a female version of the magician Prospero in a production of “The Tempest” this summer at Shakespeare & Company, based in Lenox, Mass., the theater announced on Tuesday. She will be joined on stage by her brother, Apollo Dukakis, who will play Gonzalo, and Rocco Sisto as Caliban.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Olympia Dukakis to Play Prospero for Shakespeare & Company', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Olympia Dukakis to Play Prospero, With Brother', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dukakis, Olympia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teachout, Terry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T19:45:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0b7a835-9000-5d3c-9f04-dd5c0a79c70e', 'word_count': 504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0b7a835-9000-5d3c-9f04-dd5c0a79c70e'}, {'abstract': 'The Pistons rebuilding process is going slowly and painfully in a 2-8 start.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/pistons-prince-frustrated-by-poor-start/', 'snippet': 'The Pistons rebuilding process is going slowly and painfully in a 2-8 start.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pistons starting small forward Tayshaun Prince has seen just about everything in his nine seasons with the team. He’s been part of a championship team in 2004, one that came so close to repeating in 2005, and has made six trips to the Eastern Conference finals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pistons, Prince Frustrated by Poor Start', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T19:51:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOANNE C. GERSTNER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'GERSTNER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2114060-5b6f-5ddf-9767-b1c58b124b93', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2114060-5b6f-5ddf-9767-b1c58b124b93'}, {'abstract': 'Carey Mulligan discusses how acting differs from theater to films like “Shame.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/carey-mulligan-and-the-play-that-is-shame/', 'snippet': 'Carey Mulligan discusses how acting differs from theater to films like “Shame.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the last year, Carey Mulligan appeared in two much-admired movies, “Drive” and “Shame,” and gave an acclaimed performance in “Through a Glass Darkly,” a stage adaptation of Ingmar Bergman’s 1961 film. But before that run, she hadn’t worked for nearly a year, disatisfied with the scripts she was receiving. “Everything seemed exactly the same as stuff I’d been doing,” she told the Bagger recently.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carey Mulligan and the Play That Is ‘Shame’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T20:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e41a2c5f-2265-5ff4-a16f-03442c653815', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e41a2c5f-2265-5ff4-a16f-03442c653815'}, {'abstract': 'Alan Gilbert, the conductor of the New York Philharmonic, halted the orchestra and made everyone wait when the cellphone belonging to a member of the audience at Tuesday night’s concert began to ring and ring and ring during the final movement of Mahler’s Ninth Symphony.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/new-york-philharmonic-interrupted-by-chimes-mahler-never-intended/', 'snippet': 'Alan Gilbert, the conductor of the New York Philharmonic, halted the orchestra and made everyone wait when the cellphone belonging to a member of the audience at Tuesday night’s concert began to ring and ring and ring during the final movement of ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The end of Mahler’s Ninth Symphony contains some of the most spiritual and peaceful music ever written. So when a cellphone began ringing – and ringing, ringing, ringing without cease – during a performance by the New York Philharmonic on Tuesday evening, Alan Gilbert did something conductors virtually never do. He stopped the performance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Philharmonic Interrupted by Chimes Mahler Never Intended', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Alan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mahler, Gustav', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T20:05:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebc357e4-819d-5c46-bee2-85f532a7263c', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebc357e4-819d-5c46-bee2-85f532a7263c'}, {'abstract': 'Demonstrating a new technology, WaterBlock — a coating applied directly to the insides of gadgets — makes them impervious to water damage.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/how-to-use-an-ipod-under-water/', 'snippet': 'Demonstrating a new technology, WaterBlock — a coating applied directly to the insides of gadgets — makes them impervious to water damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — The most astonishing products here at the International Consumer Electronics Show are often the ones you can’t buy yet, like a process called WaterBlock from the company HzO. In a demonstration, an iPod with the WaterBlock treatment — not enclosed in any kind of case or covering — was dropped in a fish tank while playing, and it played on undisturbed … for hours.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Use an iPod Underwater', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T20:06:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c84d3dbe-e7ce-5de3-b1dc-e41928196b7a', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c84d3dbe-e7ce-5de3-b1dc-e41928196b7a'}, {'abstract': 'Kate Middleton shows how to look good and stay warm with a sweater dress; Motilo.com launches; and cloche hats make a comeback.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/12/fashion/20120112-BROWSING.html', 'snippet': 'Kate Middleton shows how to look good and stay warm with a sweater dress; Motilo.com launches; and cloche hats make a comeback.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kate Middleton shows how to look good and stay warm with a sweater dress; Motilo.com launches; and cloche hats make a comeback.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/fashion/20120112-BROWSING-slide-Z6D7/20120112-BROWSING-slide-Z6D7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 899, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/fashion/20120112-BROWSING-slide-Z6D7/2012