/cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/what-is-the-state-of-your-block/', 'snippet': 'With Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s State of the City Address scheduled for Thursday, City Room is asking readers to provide a local perspective.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thursday at 1 p.m., Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg will give his annual State of the City Address. He can be expected to tout the year’s successes and promote his administration’s policies and plans going forward. City Room will cover it live with a video feed and tweets from our reporters and editors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is the State of Your Block?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the City Message (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T20:34:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d851ecc-2405-50b4-871a-e1a7e5c5abe6', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d851ecc-2405-50b4-871a-e1a7e5c5abe6'}, {'abstract': 'Bad ratings for the Bowl Championship Series bowls are part of the reason the system is being scrutinized, but will one of the limited playoff possibilities turn this trend around?', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/bowl-ratings-dip-or-trend/', 'snippet': 'Bad ratings for the Bowl Championship Series bowls are part of the reason the system is being scrutinized, but will one of the limited playoff possibilities turn this trend around?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is mildly amusing to read the two different takes on the pitifully low television ratings garnered by Monday night’s Bowl Championship Series title game. While the cable industry prefers the headline “ESPN Scores Cable’s Second-Largest Audience Ever,” everyone else has been quick to point out that it drew fewer viewers than any B.C.S. championship game ever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bowl Ratings: Dip or Trend?', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bowl Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sugar Bowl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richardson, Trent', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bowl Championship Series', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clemson University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louisiana State University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T20:36:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab019d8f-0b74-50d7-aa0f-7ada59fb49d0', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab019d8f-0b74-50d7-aa0f-7ada59fb49d0'}, {'abstract': 'That tops the roughly $3.2 million that Senator Scott P. Brown of Massachusetts raised during the same period for what promises to be one of the costliest races in the country.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/warren-raised-5-7-million-for-senate-bid/', 'snippet': 'That tops the roughly $3.2 million that Senator Scott P. Brown of Massachusetts raised during the same period for what promises to be one of the costliest races in the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON – Elizabeth Warren, the Harvard professor seeking the Democratic nomination to challenge Senator Scott P. Brown of Massachusetts in November, announced Wednesday that she had raised $5.7 million in the last three months of 2011.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Warren Raised $5.7 Million for Senate Bid', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Scott P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coakley, Martha M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T20:37:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c74d1c9-5fe7-5974-9a40-4dd6776e8f25', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c74d1c9-5fe7-5974-9a40-4dd6776e8f25'}, {'abstract': 'The economy “expanded at a modest to moderate pace” from late November through the end of December, the Fed said in its beige book business survey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/business/fed-survey-finds-growth-widespread.html', 'snippet': 'The economy “expanded at a modest to moderate pace” from late November through the end of December, the Fed said in its beige book business survey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Economic expansion improved last month across most of the country while hiring was limited and housing remained stagnant, the Federal Reserve said on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Economy Grows, Jobs Are Still Scarce, Fed Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Economy Grows, Jobs Are Still Scarce, Fed Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T20:39:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/339c7585-626f-5e4c-b2d8-f6910f50ab64', 'word_count': 635, 'uri': 'nyt://article/339c7585-626f-5e4c-b2d8-f6910f50ab64'}, {'abstract': "New York's education debate just gained another player, with the arrival of the New York Campaign for Achievement Now. The group wants to make it easier for parents to turn failing schools into charters, but it has been criticized by groups who say it's too closely tied to a charter schools supporter.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/11/another-player-enters-new-yorks-advocacy-arena/', 'snippet': "New York's education debate just gained another player, with the a