 York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/world/12EGYPT2sub/12EGYPT2sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/12/world/12EGYPT2sub/12EGYPT2sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/world/12EGYPT2sub/12EGYPT2sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Carter Says Egypt’s Military Is Likely to Retain Some Political Powers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carter Says Egypt’s Military Is Likely To Hold On to Some Political Powers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Jimmy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tantawi, Mohamed Hussein', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T21:17:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f19046e6-005b-525c-a96e-f8361892d10c', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f19046e6-005b-525c-a96e-f8361892d10c'}, {'abstract': 'Video-game simulators have become important features of automakers’ show displays.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/offstage-simulators-take-up-their-positions-at-detroit-auto-show/', 'snippet': 'Video-game simulators have become important features of automakers’ show displays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — With so many new vehicles vying for attention during press previews at the auto show, it’s no longer sufficient to roll a car onstage through a fog bank. Automakers are turning to side exhibits that incorporate some aspect of virtual reality, usually involving driving simulators, to keep people interested in its products long after the fog machine is switched off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Offstage, Simulators Take Up Their Positions at Detroit Auto Show', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'North American International Auto Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cadillac Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hyundai Motor Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iRacing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kia Motors Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mazda Motor Corp', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T21:20:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Schembari', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schembari', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f96431fe-3a15-5d09-9a39-4b6e389d2d7f', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f96431fe-3a15-5d09-9a39-4b6e389d2d7f'}, {'abstract': 'No.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/are-we-almost-out-of-the-liquidity-trap-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'No.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aha. Greg Mankiw tells us that when you apply the coefficients for his suggested simple Taylor rule (a rule for setting the Fed funds rate), it shows the desired rate closing in on zero from below, suggesting that the end of the liquidity trap may be near.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are We Almost Out of the Liquidity Trap? (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T21:20:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4aa0e360-1ca0-5ac9-9dd2-0801a6149169', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4aa0e360-1ca0-5ac9-9dd2-0801a6149169'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas Quasthoff, announcing his retirement, says his health no longer lets him live up to his high standard.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/thomas-quasthoff-celebrated-bass-baritone-is-retiring-from-performing/', 'snippet': 'Thomas Quasthoff, announcing his retirement, says his health no longer lets him live up to his high standard.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Thomas Quasthoff, 52, the celebrated German bass-baritone renowned for his sensitive, expressive performances and deep artistic intelligence, says he is retiring from the concert stage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multi