the galleries', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many philanthropists donate money to found an institution and then leave it up to officials to worry about the operating costs. Not Dame Jillian Sackler. On Tuesday, officials at the Arthur M. Sackler Gallery and the Freer Gallery of Art in Washington announced that Ms. Sackler had donated $5 million to establish an endowment to fund the director’s post and programs at the galleries that are named, in part, after her husband. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sackler’s Widow Gives Smithsonian Galleries $5 Million Endowment', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T21:40:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/535a0e38-1815-5047-afae-2897e12dbe9c', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/535a0e38-1815-5047-afae-2897e12dbe9c'}, {'abstract': 'Despite recent talk of a bankruptcy filing by Eastman Kodak, the company’s booth was doing brisk business at C.E.S., showing new consumer printers, digital cameras and other products.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/for-kodak-business-as-usual-at-c-e-s/', 'snippet': 'Despite recent talk of a bankruptcy filing by Eastman Kodak, the company’s booth was doing brisk business at C.E.S., showing new consumer printers, digital cameras and other products.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Business was brisk at Eastman Kodak’s expansive booth at the International Consumer Electronics Show in Las Vegas, even as the company was reportedly weighing a bankruptcy filing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': 