and destruction, is the kind of frisky theatrical adventure that would be twice as much fun at about half the length. Presented at the Connelly Theater in the East Village as part of the Coil Festival organized by Performance Space 122, the show is a freewheeling collage critiquing the country’s devouring ambition as seen through the glittering prism of Las Vegas, that great neon mirage that sprang from the Nevada sands to seduce and betray innumerable dreamers of big dreams.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/12mission/12mission-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/12mission/12mission-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/12mission/12mission-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/12mission/12mission-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/12mission/12mission-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Story of America, Founding to Foreclosure (Singing and Dancing, Too)', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Mission Drift'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Story of America, Founding to Foreclosure (Singing and Dancing, Too)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Theater of the Emerging American Moment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coil Festival',