ragraph': 'Anglophiles, historians, intellectuals and aesthetes will embrace the Anthology Film Archives retrospective of the filmmaker Patrick Keiller, running through Wednesday. Since 1981 Mr. Keiller, a leading light of Britain’s art cinema, has been making shorts and film essays with a formal, academic rigor influenced by the French avant-gardist Chris Marker (“La Jetée”). Mr. Keiller is best known for the Robinson Trilogy — “London” (1994), “Robinson in Space” (1997) and “Robinson in Ruins” (2010) — which is the centerpiece of Anthology’s overview.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/FILMROUNDUP1/FILMROUNDUP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/FILMROUNDUP1/FILMROUNDUP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/FILMROUNDUP1/FILMROUNDUP1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 611, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/FILMROUNDUP1/FILMROUNDUP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/FILMROUNDUP1/FILMROUNDUP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Life Triumphs in Rural England', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Robinson in Ruins'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T22:49:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4415bb4d-d62e-500c-9ac5-58372da437f3', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4415bb4d-d62e-500c-9ac5-58372da437f3'}, {'abstract': 'The last day of the Edgar Kaplan Winter Regional in Manhattan was held at the end of last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/crosswords/bridge/edgar-kaplan-winter-regional-in-manhattan-bridge.html', 'snippet': 'The last day of the Edgar Kaplan Winter Regional in Manhattan was held at the end of last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the last day of the Edgar Kaplan Winter Regional in Manhattan, held at the end of last year, the Swiss Teams was won by Sylvia Moss, Migry Zur-Campanile and Pietro Campanile of New York City, and Alex Ornstein of Roslyn Heights, N.Y.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/arts/card/card-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 258, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Last Day of a Tournament Boasts Some Notable Playing', 'kicker': 'Bridge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Last Day of a Tournament Boasts Some Notable Playing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridge (Card Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cards and Card Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T22:51:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Bridge', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Alder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd9b641f-0279-52e9-a919-32b0226ea1e8', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd9b641f-0279-52e9-a919-32b0226ea1e8'}, {'abstract': '“I am fully committed to moving the smart card program forward,”  Joseph J. Lhota, the transportation authority’s new chairman, said.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/at-second-blush-new-m-t-a-chief-likes-smart-cards/', 'snippet': '“I am fully committed to moving the smart card program forward,”  Joseph J. Lhota, the transportation authority’s new chairman, said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a marquee proposal by Jay H. Walder, chairman of the Metropolitan Transportation Authority during the relatively flush times of 2009: Replace the MetroCard with a computer chip-enabled “smart card” that would speed up boarding times and save the agency millions of dollars a year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Upon Reflection, New M.T.A. Chief Says He Likes ‘Smart Cards’ for the Subway', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'MetroCard (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lhota, Joseph J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walder, Jay H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-11T22:52:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/009958b8-e60e-5df9-96c0-31c3afb7c42d', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/009958b8-e60e-5df9-96c0-31c3afb7c42d'}, {'abstract': 'A 35-year-old toll booth attendant in Turkey finds solace in routine away from his father’s lacerating tongue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/movies/toll-booth-directed-by-tolga-karacelik-review.html', 'snippet': 'A 35-year-old toll booth attendant in Turkey finds solace in routine away from his father’s lacerating tongue.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Toll Booth” is a slow burn of a movie — so slow, in fact, that it bravely gambles with our attention. Painstakingly written and directed by Tolga Karacelik, this Turkish character study places us inside the head of Kenan (Serkan Ercan), a simmering 35-year-old toll booth attendant whose meticulous grooming signals a desperate need for control.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/FILMROUNDUP2/FILMROUNDUP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/FILMROUNDUP2/FILMROUNDUP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/FILMROUNDUP2/FILMROUNDUP2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/FILMROUNDUP2/FILMROUNDUP2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/FILMROUNDUP2/FILMROUNDUP2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 7