e House is not focusing on the re-election campaign. His schedule, at least for one day, suggests otherwise.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/obama-practices-the-2012-two-step/', 'snippet': 'The president’s spokesman says the White House is not focusing on the re-election campaign. His schedule, at least for one day, suggests otherwise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since President Obama’s return from Hawaii last week, the White House has labored to dispel any notion that he is plunging into his re-election campaign. Mr. Obama, his press aides say, did not watch the New Hampshire primary returns, nor did he schedule a jobs event at the White House on Wednesday as a riposte to Republican charges that he hasn’t created enough of them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Practices the 2012 Two-Step', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T00:04:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79744764-b152-54bf-8488-637024a10f11', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79744764-b152-54bf-8488-637024a10f11'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Haley Barbour granted 203 full pardons over his two terms, including 17 to convicted murderers. He also granted 19 other criminals lesser degrees of clemency, like conditional suspensions of their sentences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/01/11/us/barbour-pardondocs.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Haley Barbour granted 203 full pardons over his two terms, including 17 to convicted murderers. He also granted 19 other criminals lesser degrees of clemency, like conditional suspensions of their sentences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Haley Barbour granted 203 full pardons over his two terms, including 17 to convicted murderers. He also granted 19 other criminals lesser degrees of clemency, like conditional suspensions of their sentences.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pardons by Haley Barbour', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barbour, Haley', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T00:17:32+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/743bc1be-7abf-53e6-bcc4-3a3e51d8cfc2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/743bc1be-7abf-53e6-bcc4-3a3e51d8cfc2'}, {'abstract': 'Joran van der Sloot, who became notorious as the prime suspect in the disappearance of Natalee Holloway, pleaded guilty to the 2010 murder of a Peruvian woman he met at a casino and could face 30 years in prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/world/americas/peru-suspect-in-holloway-case-pleads-guilty-in-lima-murder.html', 'snippet': 'Joran van der Sloot, who became notorious as the prime suspect in the disappearance of Natalee Holloway, pleaded guilty to the 2010 murder of a Peruvian woman he met at a casino and could face 30 years in prison.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Joran van der Sloot, the Dutchman who became notorious as the prime suspect in the disappearance of an 18-year-old Alabama woman in Aruba in 2005, pleaded guilty in a Lima courtroom on Wednesday to the 2010 murder of a Peruvian woman he met at a casino. The case of the American woman, Natalee Holloway, who vanished during a senior class trip, remains unresolved despite being the subject of several books and television programs, as well as many lurid tabloid headlines over the years. The Peruvian woman, Stephany Flores, 21, was strangled in a Lima hotel room five years to the day after Ms. Holloway’s disappearance. “I am truly sorry for this act,” Mr. van der Sloot told the judges on Wednesday, according to The Associated Press. He bowed his head as his lawyer argued that he had killed Ms. Flores in a state of “extreme psychological trauma” brought on because he was “persecuted” during the Holloway investigation. Prosecutors have asked for a 30-year sentence. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peru: Suspect in Holloway Case Pleads Guilty in Lima Murder', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peru: Suspect in Holloway Case Pleads Guilty in Lima Murder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holloway, Natalee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Peru', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van der Sloot, Joran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T00:28:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'pers