'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/world/middleeast/egypt-anti-mubarak-uprising-to-be-honored-with-holiday.html', 'snippet': 'Egypt’s military rulers declared Jan. 25 an official holiday to celebrate the anniversary of the uprising that ousted President Hosni Mubarak last year and recognize demonstrators killed during the protests.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Egypt’s military rulers on Tuesday declared Jan. 25 an official holiday to celebrate the anniversary of the uprising that ousted President Hosni Mubarak last year. The day will also recognize the roughly 800 demonstrators who were killed during the 18 days of protests. But that date already honors the police, and earlier this week the minister of the interior suggested that it was possible to “integrate” the two occasions, leading political activists to quip that such a dual holiday would celebrate both the “victims” and the “perpetrators.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt: Anti-Mubarak Uprising to Be Honored With Holiday', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt: Anti-Mubarak Uprising To Be Honored With Holiday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T01:05:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mayy El Sheikh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mayy', 'middlename': 'El', 'lastname': 'Sheikh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_ma