 baseman Don Mattingly, to a minor league contract.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/yankees-add-another-mattingly/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees signed outfielder Preston Mattingly, the son of the former Yankees first baseman Don Mattingly, to a minor league contract.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees signed the free-agent minor league outfielder Preston Mattingly, the son of the former Yankees first baseman Don Mattingly, to a minor league contract.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Add Another Mattingly', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mattingly, Don', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T01:32:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1f5c479-550f-5b75-980a-dc99dc32fee5', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1f5c479-550f-5b75-980a-dc99dc32fee5'}, {'abstract': 'Members of a Chatham, N.J., softball team hope to stay friends, keep their jobs and, well, see the Giants win.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/eight-men-in/', 'snippet': 'Members of a Chatham, N.J., softball team hope to stay friends, keep their jobs and, well, see the Giants win.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifty years ago, if the Giants were headed to Green Bay to play the Packers in the playoffs, fans in New York might have considered themselves lucky to catch the game on television. Today, with tickets available online and frequent-flier miles accruing with every credit-card purchase, fans can dare to dream a little more boldly. Six members of a Chatham, N.J., softball team — a mix of lawyers, Wall Streeters and computer software salesmen — are set to travel to Lambeau Field for Sunday’s showdown between the Giants and the Packers. It will be a trip of cheap hotels and high hopes, cramped rental cars and unexpectedly good seats at the game. The men — they will be joined by two pals in Milwaukee — have agreed to create a Titletown travelogue. Their hopes are to stay friends, keep their jobs and, well, see the Giants win.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eight Men In: A Trip to Lambeau', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Road Trips', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T01:34:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doug Chase', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doug', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chase', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64745d28-5359-5d87-8e1d-8de3a86ad9c7', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64745d28-5359-5d87-8e1d-8de3a86ad9c7'}, {'abstract': 'The popularity of all things “Downton Abbey” has American book marketers trying to ride a British aristocracy wave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/business/media/mad-for-downton-publishers-have-a-reading-list.html', 'snippet': 'The popularity of all things “Downton Abbey” has American book marketers trying to ride a British aristocracy wave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British melodrama “Downton Abbey” is already the darling of American public television. Now it has become a marketing tool for booksellers and publishers hoping to tap into the passion of the show’s audience. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/business/media/Downton/Downtown-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/12/business/media/Downton/Downtown-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/business/media/Downton/Downtown-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 911, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/business/media/Downton/Downtown-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/12/business/media/Downton/Downtown-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If You’re Mad for ‘Downton,’ Publishers Have Reading List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If You&#8217;re Mad for &#8216;Downton,&#8217; Publishers Have Reading List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain'