, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T01:44:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08f80da7-f3b8-5e77-860b-ad5b38b7c4d9', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08f80da7-f3b8-5e77-860b-ad5b38b7c4d9'}, {'abstract': 'It’s too early to know whether the trend of slower growth will persist after the economy improves, but controlling spending will require reforms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/opinion/slower-growth-in-health-spending.html', 'snippet': 'It’s too early to know whether the trend of slower growth will persist after the economy improves, but controlling spending will require reforms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Health care spending in the United States increased at the slowest rate in half a century in 2009 and 2010, essentially keeping pace with the growth of the economy, according to the latest federal data. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slower Growth in Health Spending', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slower Growth in Health Spending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T01:45:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf6346f8-338e-586f-a5f5-b39d995413c6', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf6346f8-338e-586f-a5f5-b39d995413c6'}, {'abstract': 'Engineers, archaeologists and historians tried to uncover the World War II escape tunnels to replicate the ingenuity of the Royal Air Force fliers. They were partly successful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/world/europe/at-great-escape-site-tunnel-is-excavated-by-modern-engineers.html', 'snippet': 'Engineers, archaeologists and historians tried to uncover the World War II escape tunnels to replicate the ingenuity of the Royal Air Force fliers. They were partly successful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAMBRIDGE, England — For scale, they were no match for the Great Pyramids of Giza or the Panama Canal. The labor took months rather than years and a work force of barely 100 men. As for materials, there were none, beyond what the captured Royal Air Force fliers who built them could scavenge, scrounge or improvise.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/world/12TUNNEL1/12TUNNEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/12/world/12TUNNEL1/12TUNNEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/world/12TUNNEL1/12TUNNEL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/world/12TUNNEL1/12TUNNEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/12/world/12TUNNEL1/12TUNNEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Latter-Day Dig of ‘Great Escape’ Tunnels Humbles Modern Engineers', 'kicker': 'Memo From Britain', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Latter-Day Dig of ‘Great Escape’ Tunnels Humbles Modern Engineers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engineering and Engineers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T01:45:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b2bc4f3-a7e3-582b-89f9-4e48530d74bb', 'word_count': 1046, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b2bc4f3-a7e3-582b-89f9-4e48530d74bb'}, {'abstract': 'Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac say they will extend their existing programs so that unemployed borrowers can defer part or all of their monthly payments for up to 12 months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/business/unemployed-mortgage-holders-get-payment-extension.html', 'snippet': 'Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac say they will extend their existing programs so that unemployed borrowers can defer part or all of their monthly payments for up to 12 months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although home foreclosure rates appear to be stabilizing and unemployment is slowly coming down, there are still millions of jobless borrowers who are at risk of losing their homes because they cannot afford their monthly payments.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unemployed Mortgage Holders Get Extension on Payments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unemployed Mortgage Holders Get Extension on Payments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Association Fannie Mae', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T01:48:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Motoko Rich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Motoko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e5a8e98-e04f-5e67-8459-9c2b9e07324a', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e5a8e98-e04f-5e67-8459-9c2b9e07324a'}, {'abstract': 'Gregory Wasson, the drugstore chain’s chief, said it would take an earnings loss rather than accept Express Scripts’ proposal to pay below-average rates to the company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/business/walgreen-stands-firm-on-decision-to-end-express-scripts-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Gregory Wasson, the drugstore chain’s chief, said it would take an earnings loss rather than accept Express Scripts’ proposal to pay below-average rates to the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — The chief executive of the Walgreen Company defended the chain’s decision to end its relationship with the prescription benefit manager Express Scripts, even as rivals have stepped up their efforts to attract pharmacy customers covered by Express Scripts plans.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walgreen Is Firm on End of Express Scripts Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Walgreen Is Firm on End Of Express Scripts Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugstores', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Express Scripts Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walgreen Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T01:50:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Japsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Japsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfbd4bf3-800d-59eb-915c-13d83cf64b76', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfbd4bf3-800d-59eb-915c-13d83cf64b76'}, {'abstract': 'In allying himself with the anti-immigrant activist Kris Kobach, Mitt Romney has lurched toward the extremist right.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/opinion/romneys-hard-line-on-immigration.html', 'snippet': 'In allying himself with the anti-immigrant activist Kris Kobach, Mitt Romney has lurched toward the extremist right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney, who used to try to sound like a moderate on immigration, has dropped the pretense. On Wednesday, he proudly accepted the endorsement of the anti-immigrant activist Kris Kobach, architect of the nation’s most radical immigration crackdowns, including the unconstitutional show-your-papers laws in Arizona and Alabama. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Hard Line', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney’s Hard Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kobach, Kris W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Development, Relief, and Education for Alien Minors Act', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T01:53:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/08e8442b-4871-5fe3-9a9c-351b8180a9a9', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08e8442b-4871-5fe3-9a9c-351b8180a9a9'}, {'abstract': 'Demoralized by renovations and eviction attempts, residents at the Chelsea Hotel greeted the news that punk songstress Patti Smith would perform a private show there with deep skepticism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/nyregion/doubts-over-patti-smith-concert-plan-for-chelsea-hotel-tenants.html', 'snippet': 'Demoralized by renovations and eviction attempts, residents at the Chelsea Hotel greeted the news that punk songstress Patti Smith would perform a private show there with deep skepticism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You know that times have changed at the Chelsea Hotel  when a planned private concert by one of its famed former tenants, the punk songstress Patti Smith, evokes grousing and doubts. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/nyregion/CHELSEA2/CHELSEA2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 695, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/nyregion/CHELSEA2/CHELSEA2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/12/nyregion/CHELSEA2/CHELSEA2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Hotel of Artists, Skepticism Over a Show', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Hotel Of Artists, Skepticism Over a Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HOTEL CHELSEA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Patti', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T01:58:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8f3eb3e-bfc4-593d-a700-c28d774330b1', 'word_count': 475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8f3eb3e-bfc4-593d-a700-c28d774330b1'}, {'abstract': 'Feeding logs into a woodstove during a fairly mild January brings to mind other purposes for the fire than to keep warm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/opinion/burning-time.html', 'snippet': 'Feeding logs into a woodstove during a fairly mild January brings to mind other purposes for the fire than to keep warm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In October, 45 degrees feels like a reason to start a fire in the woodstove. Less so in January, when 45 degrees feels unseasonably mild.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Burning Time', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The Rural Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Burning Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Winter (Season)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wood and Wood Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T01:58:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verlyn Klinkenborg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klinkenborg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/816b5e19-d80b-5648-9301-3bb27efc2cf2', 'word_count': 327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/816b5e19-d80b-5648-9301-3bb27efc2cf2'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Avery was a medical researcher who made a single, crucial discovery about newborns’ ability to breathe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/health/research/mary-ellen-avery-premature-babies-savior-dies-at-84.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Avery was a medical researcher who made a single, crucial discovery about newborns’ ability to breathe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Mary Ellen Avery, a medical researcher who helped save hundreds of thousands of premature infants with a single, crucial discovery about their ability to breathe, died on Dec. 4 in West Orange, N.J. She was 84.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/us/AVERY-obity/AVERY-obity-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/us/AVERY-obity/AVERY-obity-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/12/us/AVERY-obity/AVERY-obity-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mary Ellen Avery, Premature Babies’ Savior, Dies at 84', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'M. E. Avery, Premature Babies’ Savior, Dies at 84', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN ASSN FOR THE ADVANCEMENT OF SCIENCE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Premature Babies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T01:59:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/eebfcc28-311d-56f1-b9af-13910011d56e', 'word_count': 929, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eebfcc28-311d-56f1-b9af-13910011d56e'}, {'abstract': 'Fernando Martinez, who was signed to great fanfare in 2005, was put on waiver by the Mets this week and was claimed by Houston.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/once-a-top-prospect-martinez-is-headed-to-houston/', 'snippet': 'Fernando Martinez, who was signed to great fanfare in 2005, was put on waiver by the Mets this week and was claimed by Houston.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Fernando Martinez signed with the Mets on July 11, 2005, there was great excitement surrounding a 16-year-old from the Dominican Republic who was projected to become an elite outfielder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Once a Top Prospect, Martinez Is Headed to Houston', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martinez, Fernando', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T02:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab377169-81c7-5a6a-868a-c8d935b1801e', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab377169-81c7-5a6a-868a-c8d935b1801e'}, {'abstract': 'Progressives who are frustrated with President Obama have something to cheer in the resurrection of the Justice Department’s Civil Rights Division.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/voting-in-plain-sight/', 'snippet': 'Progressives who are frustrated with President Obama have something to cheer in the resurrection of the Justice Department’s Civil Rights Division.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of all the domestic policy differences between the Bush and Obama administrations, just about the sharpest and most telling may be their opposite responses to the drive by Republican-dominated states to require voters to present photo identification at the polls. The Bush administration thought photo ID was a dandy idea. The Obama administration recognizes it for what it is: a cynical effort to insure that fewer young people and members of minority groups (read, likely Democratic voters) are able to cast a ballot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Voting in Plain Sight', 'kicker': 'Linda Greenhouse', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T02:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/018b9287-dee0-567a-b6d6-33dbca8a2cf6', 'word_count': 1317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/018b9287-dee0-567a-b6d6-33dbca8a2cf6'}, {'abstract': 'Offensive material is easily found with apps that come installed on most mobile devices or can be downloaded, but there are ways parents can limit this.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/technology/personaltech/guarding-a-childs-mobile-device-from-pornography.html', 'snippet': 'Offensive material is easily found with apps that come installed on most mobile devices or can be downloaded, but there are ways parents can limit this.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many teenagers recently opened a new iPhone, Android or iPod Touch, immediately downloaded textPlus, a popular free texting app, and headed for their bedrooms.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/business/12-SMART1/12-SMART1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/business/12-SMART1/12-SMART1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/12/business/12-SMART1/12-SMART1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Safeguarding a Child’s Mobile Device From Pornography', 'kicker': 'App Smart', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Safeguarding a Child’s Mobile Device From Pornography', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N