121 yards from scrimmage against the Lions, look no further than the previous two seasons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/sports/football/healthy-pierre-thomas-pushes-forward-carrying-saints-with-him.html', 'snippet': 'For proof that the Saints are a different team depending on Pierre Thomas, who gained 121 yards from scrimmage against the Lions, look no further than the previous two seasons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'METAIRIE, La. — There went Pierre Thomas, on a screen pass in the Superdome late last Saturday. He maneuvered past one Detroit Lions defender, split two others, stumbled, regained his balance with one hand and continued to plow forward. It took three defenders to wrestle him to the turf.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/sports/Y-SAINTS-2/Y-SAINTS-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/sports/Y-SAINTS-2/Y-SAINTS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/12/sports/Y-SAINTS-2/Y-SAINTS-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Healthy Running Back Has Saints Recalling Title Run', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Healthy Running Back Has Saints Recalling Title Run', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brees, Drew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Saints', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T03:55:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b717625a-a37b-5b1f-81f4-dff52240a247', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b717625a-a37b-5b1f-81f4-dff52240a247'}, {'abstract': 'During this slump, women are getting degrees while men settle for so-so jobs. Who will end up ahead?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2012/01/11/will-women-get-ahead-by-going-back-to-school/', 'snippet': 'During this slump, women are getting degrees while men settle for so-so jobs. Who will end up ahead?', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Women Get Ahead by Going Back to School?', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T03:58:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cca535d3-d858-5089-8bde-89637592b02a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cca535d3-d858-5089-8bde-89637592b02a'}, {'abstract': 'The Taliban’s willingness to open a political office in Qatar represents a critical point in the United States’ attempt to negotiate an end to the Afghanistan war.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/at-a-crossroads-for-peace-with-the-taliban/', 'snippet': 'The Taliban’s willingness to open a political office in Qatar represents a critical point in the United States’ attempt to negotiate an end to the Afghanistan war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The road to creating lasting peace in the midst of war is often fraught with setbacks, and success is never guaranteed. Over the last year, Marc Grossman, a low-key diplomat, led a small team of American officials in secret meetings with Mullah Muhammad Omar, a representative of Afghanistan’s Taliban leader, in hopes of starting peace talks. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At a Crossroads for Peace With the Taliban', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Omar, Muhammad (Taliban Leader)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T04:12:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c6fef72-32c9-5441-8428-657cb70b9d91', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c6fef72-32c9-5441-8428-657cb70b9d91'}, {'abstract': 'The price to dine with the president was high. But supporters could hear him speak after a concert for $100.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/11/obama-raises-money-in-chicago/', 'snippet': 'The price to dine with the president was high. But supporters could hear him speak after a concert for $100.', 'lead_paragraph': ' CHICAGO — Telling supporters that change may be hard but remains possible, President Obama received a warm welcome home here on Wednesday, bolstering his 2012 campaign coffers at three fund-raisers attracting an eclectic mix of wealthy donors and spirited college students.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Raises Money in Chicago', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T04:15:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Ann Cullotta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': 'Ann', 'lastname': 'Cullotta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/573a7296-1c79-565d-bb59-cd7253fb2f35', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/573a7296-1c79-565d-bb59-cd7253fb2f35'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. McWhinnie was a rare-book dealer and gallerist known as a champion of words and images on paper in an age of electronic reading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/books/john-mcwhinnie-an-expert-in-rare-books-dies-at-43.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. McWhinnie was a rare-book dealer and gallerist known as a champion of words and images on paper in an age of electronic reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John McWhinnie, a rare-book dealer and gallerist known as a champion of words and images on paper in an age of electronic reading, died on Friday in a snorkeling accident in the British Virgin Islands. He was 43.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/MCWHINNIE-obit/MCWHINNIE-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/arts/MCWHINNIE-obit/MCWHINNIE-obit-th