-b72b-b589205d6cbd', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9902c657-2674-5084-b72b-b589205d6cbd'}, {'abstract': 'Officers accused of mistreating suspected militants in Afghanistan and Pakistan will avoid charges, but allegations in Libya will get scrutiny, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/world/europe/britain-to-investigate-role-in-claim-of-torture-by-libyans.html', 'snippet': 'Officers accused of mistreating suspected militants in Afghanistan and Pakistan will avoid charges, but allegations in Libya will get scrutiny, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — British officials announced on Thursday that they had ordered a criminal investigation into the role played by MI6, the country’s secret intelligence service, in operations that led to two Libyan opponents of Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi being delivered to Libyan jails, where, they said, they were tortured by Colonel Qaddafi’s secret police.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/world/europe/13britain/13britain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/13/world/europe/13britain/13britain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/world/europe/13britain/13britain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/world/europe/13britain/13britain-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/world/europe/13britain/13britain-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain to Investigate Role in Claim of Torture by Libyans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain to Investigate Role in Claim of Torture by Libyans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extraordinary Rendition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scotland Yard (Metropolitan Police Service)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Secret Intelligence Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T13:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns and Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c64fb80-449e-5cca-b2fb-1caf700f141b', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c64fb80-449e-5cca-b2fb-1caf700f141b'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/morning-take-out-159/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For Europe, Few Options in a Vicious Cycle of Debt \xa0|\xa0 As difficult as the last two years have been for Europe, 2012 could be even tougher. Each week, countries will need to sell billions of dollars’ worth of bonds — a staggering $1 trillion in total — to replace existing debt and cover current budget deficits.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T13:37:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e37a9f3-4780-5170-8d6b-468e1e8b714a', 'word_count': 2181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e37a9f3-4780-5170-8d6b-468e1e8b714a'}, {'abstract': 'Also, a French journalist is killed in Syria and fashion bloggers who are completely really secure about their masculinity. Really.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/the-breakfast-meeting-a-billionaires-backing-and-digging-deeper-on-downton/', 'snippet': 'Also, a French journalist is killed in Syria and fashion bloggers who are completely really secure about their masculinity. Really.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Politico profiles the three billionaires who “could drag out” the Republican presidential nomination process by nearly single handedly sustaining the advertising campaigns of Newt Gingrich, Rick Santorum and Jon Huntsman Jr. Their role – writing large checks to PACs that back their candidate – has been aided by recent federal court decisions weakening checks on political spending. They are: Sheldon Adelson, casino magnate and patron to Mr. Gingrich; Jon Huntsman Sr., patron to his son; Foster Friess, patron to Mr. Santorum.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: A Billionaire’s Backing and Digging Deeper on ‘Downton’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adelson, Sheldon G', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Graydon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wintour, Anna', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conde Nast Publications Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Politico, The', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T13:38:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ceb32c9-049a-561b-8c23-78c5fd7b730b', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ceb32c9-049a-561b-8c23-78c5fd7b730b'}, {'abstract': 'By the way, quiet cars on the Acela often aren’t.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/be-vewy-vewy-quiet/', 'snippet': 'By the way, quiet cars on the Acela often aren’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Rosenthal gets a bit of a laugh out of Mitt Romney’s insistence that the only reason anyone would talk about inequality is the “politics of envy”, and that if the subject is discussed at all, it should only be in “quiet rooms”.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Be Vewy, Vewy Quiet', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_