38-e205c3ed07e4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d319fc45-8a98-59ce-9a38-e205c3ed07e4'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney is making his second run at his party’s nomination, but this time he is playing the part of Senator John McCain from 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/romney-treads-familiar-path-toward-nomination/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney is making his second run at his party’s nomination, but this time he is playing the part of Senator John McCain from 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the first two Republican presidential primaries of the 2012 campaign now over, there are similarities to the 2008 contest — and lessons for Mitt Romney as he moves toward the general election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Treads Familiar Path Toward Nomination', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T13:54:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0137bd68-aaac-575b-aa8a-110c7b9255b0', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0137bd68-aaac-575b-aa8a-110c7b9255b0'}, {'abstract': 'Patients who are more involved in their health care are less likely to smoke, be obese or go the emergency room than those who are less engaged. Now doctors are trying to figure out the best way to get them involved.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/getting-patients-to-take-charge-of-their-health/', 'snippet': 'Patients who are more involved in their health care are less likely to smoke, be obese or go the emergency room than those who are less engaged. Now doctors are trying to figure out the best way to get them involved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One afternoon, I heard a colleague let out an exasperated groan in front of the hospital computers. His patient had been admitted. Again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Patients to Take Charge of Their Health', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T14:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15349b12-82e3-5136-9973-dddca656c696', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15349b12-82e3-5136-9973-dddca656c696'}, {'abstract': 'Bnter, a start-up company that lets people save and post their witty exchanges online, is rejiggering its site and adding the ability to post via text message, a feature designed with Siri in mind.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/bnter-turns-into-banters-and-lets-you-post-via-text/', 'snippet': 'Bnter, a start-up company that lets people save and post their witty exchanges online, is rejiggering its site and adding the ability to post via text message, a feature designed with Siri in mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bnter, a New York start-up company that lets people artfully post their witty text, Twitter and instant-message exchanges online, has attracted just 60,000 users since it began in\xa0October 2010. So it is making some changes, updating its site’s design and letting users post via text message, a feature designed with Siri in mind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bnter Turns Into Banters and Lets You Post via Text', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T14:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/981fee25-c43d-5345-87c5-3773884a90d3', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/981fee25-c43d-5345-87c5-3773884a90d3'}, {'abstract': 'In his latest solo project, Wang has hatched an oblique yet incisive commentary on the swirling intersections of the free market economy, the art world and the environment.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/out-there-michael-wangs-carbon-copies/', 'snippet': 'In his latest solo project, Wang has hatched an oblique yet incisive commentary on the swirling intersections of the free market economy, the art world and the environment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out There | Michael Wang’s ‘Carbon Copies’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T14:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin McGarry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGarry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1175a13-0fc2-5294-ac50-93c14c10b156', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1175a13-0fc2-5294-ac50-93c14c10b156'}, {'abstract': 'A few months after restarting its superhero story lines at issue No. 1, DC Comics is canceling six series and introducing six new ones, including titles written by Grant Morrison and China Miéville.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/out-with-the-new-in-with-the-newer-at-dc-comics/', 'snippet': 'A few months after restarting its superhero story lines at issue No. 1, DC Comics is canceling six series and introducing six new ones, including titles written by Grant Morrison and China Miéville.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few months into a DC Comics initiative under which the superhero publisher restarted its long-running series at issue No. 1, some of those narratives will go no further: the company announced on Thursday morning that it is canceling six of its comic books and introducing six new ones, keeping the total amount of its continuing titles at the magic number of 52.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Out With the New, In With the Newer at DC Comics', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mieville, China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morrison, Grant', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DC Comics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marvel Comics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T14:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f70a6976-d675-5118-98c2-0360df1df6a5', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f70a6976-d675-5118-98c2-0360df1df6a5'}, {'abstract': 'The London Metal Exchange, the world’s largest metal futures market, plans to review initial takeover offers at a board meeting on Feb. 23.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/london-metal-exchange-to-review-takeover-bids-in-february/', 'snippet': 'The London Metal Exchange, the world’s largest metal futures market, plans to review initial takeover offers at a board meeting on Feb. 23.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The London Metal Exchange, the world’s largest metal futures market, plans to review initial takeover offers at a board meeting on Feb. 23.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Metal Exchange to Review Takeover Bids in February', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None,