 week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Touch-Screen Gorilla Glass Slims Down', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glass', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Consumer Electronics Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Corning Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T15:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8384a549-b642-57f9-a595-40bde49d6b02', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8384a549-b642-57f9-a595-40bde49d6b02'}, {'abstract': 'In honor of the best moments from Oscar hopefuls thus far this week, the Bagger presents the Thursdays, and Rooney Mara, Christopher Plummer and Jessica Chastain are among the winners.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/a-new-set-of-awards-courtesy-of-the-carpetbagger/', 'snippet': 'In honor of the best moments from Oscar hopefuls thus far this week, the Bagger presents the Thursdays, and Rooney Mara, Christopher Plummer and Jessica Chastain are among the winners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was inevitable: after years of covering awards season, the Bagger has come up with some prizes of our own. They are the Thursdays, in honor of the best moments from Oscar hopefuls thus far this week (and the fact that Thursday is also the day our column appears is just a coincidence, surely). The first round of winners are here. But as always there were still more worthy folks who deserved recognition. The Bagger is nothing if not generous with the praise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Set of Awards, Courtesy of the Carpetbagger', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chastain, Jessica', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Irons, Jeremy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mara, Rooney', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Donnell, Rosie", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Plummer, Christopher', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Film Critics Circle', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T15:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c93613b5-8e0d-53ab-a194-1f6ebfd29622', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c93613b5-8e0d-53ab-a194-1f6ebfd29622'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese hackers have deployed a new cyber weapon that is aimed at the federal agencies and United States  businesses, security researchers say.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/malicious-software-attacks-security-cards-used-by-pentagon/', 'snippet': 'Chinese hackers have deployed a new cyber weapon that is aimed at the federal agencies and United States  businesses, security researchers say.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Chinese hackers have deployed a new cyber weapon that is aimed at the Defense Department, the Department of Homeland Security, the State Department and potentially a number of other United States government agencies and businesses, security researchers say. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Malicious Software Attacks Security Cards Used by Pentagon', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Malware', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T15:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a1f02d3-2db4-5aca-8003-1757632aa468', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a1f02d3-2db4-5aca-8003-1757632aa468'}, {'abstract': 'Robert Ballard is famous around the globe as the man who found the wreckage of the Titanic, but now he has grown weary of having to always talk about it.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/yes-he-discovered-the-titanic-no-he-doesnt-want-to-talk-about-it/', 'snippet': 'Robert Ballard is famous around the globe as the man who found the wreckage of the Titanic, but now he has grown weary of having to always talk about it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert Ballard has made quite a few notable discoveries in deep waters around the world in the last 27 years. But most people still want to hear him use the T-word.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yes, He Discovered the Titanic. No, He Doesn’t Want to Talk About It.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shipwrecks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Titanic (Ship)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ballard, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T15:01:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a29b3586-dff4-5935-9126-850751da64d5', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a29b3586-dff4-5935-9126-850751da64d5'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/what-were-reading-350/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MSNBC: The dodginess of third-party audits rather than government inspections has been highlighted by a Congressional investigation of a cantelope-borne listeria outbreak that killed 30 people last year. The auditor awarded Jensen Farms in Colorado, the source of the tainted fruit, a “superior” rating just before the outbreak. — Glenn Collins', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T15:05:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55a746e9-846f-50b2-a807-cac50789d200', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55a746e9-846f-50b2-a807-cac50789d200'}, {'abstract': 'The ING Group is abandoning plans for an initial public offering of its combined Asian and European businesses, citing turbulence in the equity markets.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/ing-revises-i-p-o-plans/', 'snippet': 'The ING Group is abandoning plans for an initial public offering of its combined Asian and European businesses, citing turbulence in the equity markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ING Group is abandoning plans for an initial public offering of its combined Asian and European businesses, citing turbulence in the equity markets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ING Revises I.P.O. Plans', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Capital One Financial Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ING Groep N.V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMSTERDAM (NETHERLANDS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T15:06:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1105f67-ab76-568e-b005-b4c054ed4618', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1105f67-ab76-568e-b005-b4c054ed4618'}, {'abstract': 'This week we pair W .S. Merwin’s “January” with a 2011 article about enjoying the season despite the cold.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/poetry-pairing-january/', 'snippet': 'This week we pair W .S. Merwin’s “January” with a 2011 article about enjoying the season despite the cold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s Poetry Pairing matches W. S. Merwin’s “January” with a 2011 story about enjoying the season despite the cold — “Snow Forecast? Set Up the Patio.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | ‘January’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T15:09:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc86319e-d492-508b-b1b0-ade6b97a774c', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc86319e-d492-508b-b1b0-ade6b97a774c'}, {'abstract': 'The lack of flurries this winter comes as a relief to many, but for others the absence has upset the rhythms of the season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/nyregion/no-snow-in-new-york-but-a-wintry-mix-of-opinion.html', 'snippet': 'The lack of flurries this winter comes as a relief to many, but for others the absence has upset the rhythms of the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Where is the snow? That is the question swirling — unlike actual flurries — across New York City and its suburbs, where sidewalks have been relentlessly gray and yards stubbornly green this winter. After a decade of higher-than-average snowfalls, including last year’s snowiest January ever, nary a flake has fallen since the freak October storm.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/nyregion/SNOW1/SNOW1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/nyregion/SNOW1/SNOW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/nyregion/SNOW1/SNOW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wintry Mix of Opinions on a Season’s Missing Snow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wintry Mix of Opinions On a Season’s Missing Snow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CENTRAL PARK (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T15:11:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa W. Foderaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Foderaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/233c9555-8338-517f-8b20-e9c0f40436bf', 'word_count': 1116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/233c9555-8338-517f-8b20-e9c0f40436bf'}, {'abstract': 'With all the pressures of this weekend’s series against Ohio State, Chris Brown provides some comic relief about Michigan’s team and past experiences of playing outdoors.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/michigan-diary-getting-to-know-the-boys/', 'snippet': 'With all the pressures of this weekend’s series against Ohio State, Chris Brown provides some comic relief about Michigan’s team and past experiences of playing outdoors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This Sunday at Progressive Field, home of the Cleveland Indians, the Wolverines of Michigan will be capping a weekend series with the Buckeyes of Ohio State in the Frozen Diamond Faceoff. With all the pressures of this series (the first game is Friday in Columbus), I’m here to provide some comic relief about our team and past experiences of playing outdoors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan Diary: Getting to Know the Boys', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ohio State University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Progressive Field (Cleveland,', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T15:14:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c225b926-21bb-5863-af4f-7ba4ece7d514', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c225b926-21bb-5863-af4f-7ba4ece7d514'}, {'abstract': 'In a season dominated by dispiriting headlines, Baylor quarterback Robert Griffin III was a shot of sunshine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/sports/the-good-news-bear.html', 'snippet': 'In a season dominated by dispiriting headlines, Baylor quarterback Robert Griffin III was a shot of sunshine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You have to hand it to Robert Griffin III. It was no small feat bringing joy to this college football season. He not only won a Heisman Trophy while lifting Baylor into a level of the sport’s atmosphere it hardly knew existed, he also made a lot of people happy just watching him play, equal parts glittering talent and spunk and an electrifying sense of occasion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/13leading1/13leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/13leading1/13leading1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/13leading1/13leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 646, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/13leading1/13leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/13leading1/13leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Good News Bear', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Good News Bear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T15:21:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/beea6d14-13d7-5364-86a5-5fe40ce0c1e4', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/beea6d14-13d7-5364-86a5-5fe40ce0c1e4'}, {'abstract': 'America’s binge drinking on a map, unemployed mortgage holders get extension on payments, publishers cater to the Downton Abbey crowd and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/thursday-reading-americas-binge-drinking-on-a-map/', 'snippet': 'America’s binge drinking on a map, unemployed mortgage holders get extension on payments, publishers cater to the Downton Abbey crowd and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday Reading: America’s Binge Drinking, on a Map', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T15:21:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cee51bc-1355-5c21-9daf-5d5b7fe848d9', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cee51bc-1355-5c21-9daf-5d5b7fe848d9'}, {'abstract': 'The public editor asks for help from readers on determining how and when The Times should set the record straight on untruths in the news pages.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/should-the-times-be-a-truth-vigilante/', 'snippet': 'The public editor asks for help from readers on determining how and when The Times should set the record straight on untruths in the news pages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m looking for reader input on whether and when New York Times news reporters should challenge “facts” that are asserted by newsmakers they write about.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should The Times Be a Truth Vigilante?', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T15:29:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arthur S. Brisbane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arthur', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Brisbane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f24da45-9a1b-578f-aab6-70244cdff2a5', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f24da45-9a1b-578f-aab6-70244cdff2a5'}, {'abstract': 'On January 1, 2012, a controversial series of marine reserves that restrict fishing went into effect in Southern California.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/science/100000001281203/californias-coastline-controversy.html', 'snippet': 'On January 1, 2012, a controversial series of marine reserves that restrict fishing went into effect in Southern California.', 'lead_paragrap