roposals to attract, reward and evaluate teachers; open 100 new schools, including 50 charters; increase  partnerships and efforts to connect students to college and careers; and help students obtain financial aid.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/12/bloomberg-unveils-ambitious-proposals-for-schools/', 'snippet': "Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg's State of the City address includes proposals to attract, reward and evaluate teachers; open 100 new schools, including 50 charters; increase  partnerships and efforts to connect students to college and careers; and hel...", 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg Unveils Ambitious Proposals for Schools ', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T18:40:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By FERNANDA SANTOS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SANTOS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41c82080-b72f-5a20-bb18-9c34f24bee4d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41c82080-b72f-5a20-bb18-9c34f24bee4d'}, {'abstract': 'The BBC reports a fivefold increase in the number of self-immolations since the revolution that toppled the Tunisian president last January and ushered in a more democratic government.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/spate-of-self-immolations-reported-in-tunisia/', 'snippet': 'The BBC reports a fivefold increase in the number of self-immolations since the revolution that toppled the Tunisian president last January and ushered in a more democratic government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a year after the self-immolation in Tunisia that incited the first revolution of the Arab Spring, Tunisians are setting themselves on fire at a disturbingly high rate, with at least four people doing so in the last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spate of Self-Immolations Reported in Tunisia', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immolation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bouazizi, Mohamed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tunisia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T18:40:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fd42f9b-93e9-5cac-86ce-abd42aec12e1', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fd42f9b-93e9-5cac-86ce-abd42aec12e1'}, {'abstract': 'A work that is part sculpture, part micro-hotel, atop the Southbank Centre’s Queen Elizabeth Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/london-underground-a-room-for-london/', 'snippet': 'A work that is part sculpture, part micro-hotel, atop the Southbank Centre’s Queen Elizabeth Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A wonderfully surreal vision comes into view as you walk across Waterloo Bridge: a boat moored atop the Southbank Centre’s Queen Elizabeth Hall. And this is not just any boat. A collaboration between the architect David Kohn and the artist Fiona Banner, it is part sculpture, part micro-hotel. “A Room for London,” as it is known, is the result of a design competition run by two inspired clients — Living Architecture, which commissions and rents vacation houses designed by cutting-edge architects, and Artangel, which commissions contemporary art projects — to offer a unique, one-bedroom accommodation with some of the best views in London, and a program of live performances and events. (“A Room for London” has a one-night, two-person limit, and rates start at 120 pounds, or about $185.65.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Underground | A Room for London', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T18:43:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elias Redstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elias', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Redstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/901b957f-2b43-50c6-8b70-449e5e8541e0', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/901b957f-2b43-50c6-8b70-449e5e8541e0'}, {'abstract': 'A new center in Chelsea includes a cooking school, sales of food and cookware, and party space.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/havens-kitchen-to-offer-classes-catering-and-retail/', 'snippet': 'A new center in Chelsea includes a cooking school, sales of food and cookware, and party space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alison Schneider, a food-loving, stay-at-home Manhattan mother of five, conducted some Greenmarket tours and taught informal cooking classes here and there. Then she wanted more. So she started pursuing a master’s degree in food studies at New York University. And now she is opening Haven’s Kitchen, an elegantly designed shop, cooking school, catering kitchen and party rooms on two floors of a 19th-century carriage house in Chelsea.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Haven’s Kitchen to Offer Classes, Catering and Retail', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T18:44:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabrcant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabrcant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23163a0e-33a4-532b-969b-f61133ebfb82', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23163a0e-33a4-532b-969b-f61133ebfb82'}, {'abstract': 'President Asif Ali Zardari visited Dubai briefly on Thursday for a wedding before returning to Pakistan, as the judiciary was drawn into tensions between the civilian government and the country’s powerful military.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/world/asia/amid-crisis-pakistan-president-asif-ali-zardari-heads-again-to-dubai.html', 'snippet': 'President Asif Ali Zardari visited Dubai briefly on Thursday for a wedding before returning to Pakistan, as the judiciary was drawn into tensions between the civilian government and the country’s powerful military.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — President Asif Ali Zardari flew to Dubai, in the United Arab Emirates, on Thursday on what an aide said was a short visit for a wedding from which he would return overnight. The move was surprising, coming as tensions between the civilian government and the country’s powerful military have risen sharply and drawn in the judiciary.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Crisis, President of Pakistan Visits Dubai', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid Crisis, President Of Pakistan Visits Dubai', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dubai (United Arab Emirates)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zardari, Asif Ali', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T18:46:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87e09bfd-be2b-573f-b427-7d43ba9a1949', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87e09bfd-be2b-573f-b427-7d43ba9a1949'}, {'abstract': 'A North Korean state television report on the plan to embalm the remains of the late Dear Leader included an interview with a woman in an ostentatiously well-stocked supermarket who explained her delight at the news.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/north-korean-television-reports-plan-to-embalm-kims-body/', 'snippet': 'A North Korean state television report on the plan to embalm the remains of the late Dear Leader included an interview with a woman in an ostentatiously well-stocked supermarket who explained her delight at the news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Choe Sang-Hun reports, North Korea announced on Thursday that it would place the embalmed body of Kim Jong-il on permanent display in a Pyongyang mausoleum, alongside that of his father, Kim Il-sung, who died in 1994 but still holds the title of president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': []