officer recommended that Pfc. Bradley Manning, accused of leaking confidential government documents to WikiLeaks, face court martial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The military officer who presided over an evidentiary hearing on charges against Pfc. Bradley Manning, accused of leaking hundreds of thousands of confidential government documents to WikiLeaks, recommended on Friday that Private Manning face court martial.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Martial Recommended in WikiLeaks Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court-Martial Urged in WikiLeaks Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Bradley E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T20:57:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cd846d1-af60-59d0-b7fe-ca1c17fb0c39', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cd846d1-af60-59d0-b7fe-ca1c17fb0c39'}, {'abstract': 'ABC comes out on top in the 18-to-49 set while CBS rakes in the most viewers over all.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/split-decision-in-prime-time-battle/', 'snippet': 'ABC comes out on top in the 18-to-49 set while CBS rakes in the most viewers over all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The broadcast networks settled for a ratings split on Wednesday night with ABC’s comedy block taking the top spot in the 18-to-49 demographic while the broadcast of the 38th annual People’s Choice Awards drew enough total viewers (8.9 million) to give CBS the win in that category, according to Nielsen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Split Decision in Prime-Time Battle', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Handler, Chelsea', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Media Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T20:58:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fccc63c0-541f-5d2f-90e8-8106eb4e69fd', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fccc63c0-541f-5d2f-90e8-8106eb4e69fd'}, {'abstract': 'When Grandma sends a determined tomboy frilly clothes, some readers suspect an agenda.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/parental-quandary-considered-grandma-gives-frilly-gifts-to-a-tomboy/', 'snippet': 'When Grandma sends a determined tomboy frilly clothes, some readers suspect an agenda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Teaching children to\xa0graciously receive a gift they are not thrilled with is a common etiquette question, but last week, a parenting quandary came in that took the problem just a little farther. What if those unwanted gifts also bring an unwanted message? Gretchen’s daughter Mia (all names have been changed) has always worn boys’ clothing — not just gender-neutral clothing, but emphatically boys’ clothes, right down to the skin. She’s always said she wished she’d been born a boy. But Mia’s grandmother (Gretchen’s mother-in-law) sends boxes after boxes of fabulously frilly pink dresses, tights and bows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parental Quandary Considered: Grandma Gives Frilly Gifts to a Tomboy', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T20:58:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/128efe95-22c4-5f8a-bb04-88477d053936', 'word_count': 1132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/128efe95-22c4-5f8a-bb04-88477d053936'}, {'abstract': 'More documentary news, this time from the Academy and the Directors Guild.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/as-the-directors-make-their-documentary-picks-new-oscar-rules-take-effect/', 'snippet': 'More documentary news, this time from the Academy and the Directors Guild.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Academy’s Board of Governors made it official today: to qualify for the documentary feature Oscar, a film must be reviewed in The New York Times and/or The Los Angeles Times, in addition to the previously required weeklong run in both New York and Los Angeles. Once a film qualifies, the entire Documentary Branch will vote in a process explained here and debated here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As the Directors Make Their Documentary Picks, New Oscar Rules Take Effect', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berlinger, Joe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Steve', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marsh, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Press, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scorsese, Martin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sinofsky, Bruce', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e682b37-a14d-5ac0-8017-c314cc1f53e3', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e682b37-a14d-5ac0-8017-c314cc1f53e3'}, {'abstract': 'Saudi Arabia and its Arab neighbors have said they will fill any gap in energy supplies for countries that yield to pressure from Washington to curtail purchases of Iranian crude.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/world/asia/asia-buyers-of-iran-crude-get-assurances-of-alternate-supply.html', 'snippet': 'Saudi Arabia and its Arab neighbors have said they will fill any gap in energy supplies for countries that yield to pressure from Washington to curtail purchases of Iranian crude.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Pressure on Iran mounted on Thursday, with the United States saying it was determined to isolate the country’s central bank, and three of Iran’s largest oil customers — Japan, South Korea and China — getting assurances that Saudi Arabia and other Persian Gulf producers would help make up any gap in supplies if they curtailed oil purchases from Iran.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/world/13OIL/13OIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/world/13OIL/13OIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/world/13OIL/13OIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gulf Nations Aid U.S. Push to Choke Off Iran Oil Sales', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gulf Nations Aid U.S. Push To Choke Off Iran Oil Sales', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:04:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler and Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4fe3c0b-3c0d-5182-80e6-0a9d36a195ab', 'word_count': 1353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4fe3c0b-3c0d-5182-80e6-0a9d36a195ab'}, {'abstract': 'The Turkish play “Lick But Don’t Swallow!,” about a reluctant angel sent to join the cast of a low-budget skin flick, is running at La MaMa as part of the Under the Radar festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/theater/reviews/lick-but-dont-swallow-part-of-under-the-radar-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Turkish play “Lick But Don’t Swallow!,” about a reluctant angel sent to join the cast of a low-budget skin flick, is running at La MaMa as part of the Under the Radar festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So what if hookers have hearts of gold? Porn stars, as it turns out, are angels. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saving Wayward Souls With Pleasures of the Flesh', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Lick But Don’t Swallow!'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saving Wayward Souls With Pleasures of the Flesh', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Under the Radar Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:09:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2278dce3-56ce-5fbe-b4af-73a2863239d3', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2278dce3-56ce-5fbe-b4af-73a2863239d3'}, {'abstract': 'New games from WowWee work with Android and Apple devices and some physical object that provides a augmented reality playing field.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/wowwee-creates-games-that-blend-the-physical-and-virtual-worlds/', 'snippet': 'New games from WowWee work with Android and Apple devices and some physical object that provides a augmented reality playing field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — At the International Consumer Electronics Show WowWee unveiled a previously announced line of toys it calls “Appcessories,” which are game pieces, collectable figures and toys that control games on Android or Apple devices.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'WowWee Creates Games That Blend the Physical and Virtual Worlds', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WowWee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:10:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c59c07ad-8434-597a-99ce-b87023fe757c', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c59c07ad-8434-597a-99ce-b87023fe757c'}, {'abstract': 'The case involving ChinaCast took a bizarre turn this week, the Deal Professor says. After the company held its annual meeting in Beijing, one board member sued, saying his representative was locked out.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/china-case-reveals-risks-of-investing-in-a-foreign-company/', 'snippet': 'The case involving ChinaCast took a bizarre turn this week, the Deal Professor says. After the company held its annual meeting in Beijing, one board member sued, saying his representative was locked out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The management of the ChinaCast Education Corporation appears to have a novel response to board elections: ignore them. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Case Reveals Risks of Investing in a Foreign Company', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ChinaCast Education Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:13:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e182e9d-e67b-5c19-b4b1-d4d0bb2bdfc2', 'word_count': 1240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e182e9d-e67b-5c19-b4b1-d4d0bb2bdfc2'}, {'abstract': 'My boyfriend and I spent a happy Christmas together, and then he disappeared, without a word.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/fashion/exit-left-wordlessly.html', 'snippet': 'My boyfriend and I spent a happy Christmas together, and then he disappeared, without a word.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A STORY that haunts me involves a woman I know whose fiancé went out to inspect a potential apartment for their married life and never came back. He wasn’t dead in a ditch. He was just gone, without clarification. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/fashion/15MODERNLOVE/15MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 672, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/fashion/15MODERNLOVE/15MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/fashion/15MODERNLOVE/15MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Exit Left, Wordlessly', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exit Left, Wordlessly', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:14:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aimee Lee Ball', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aimee', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Ball', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efb54b51-166d-5da2-8f7f-08c60110484b', 'word_count': 1532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efb54b51-166d-5da2-8f7f-08c60110484b'}, {'abstract': 'How the makeup artist Dick Page transforms a performer into a young (and old) Susan Sontag for a show at the Public Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/vain-glorious-sontag-reborn-the-makeup/', 'snippet': 'How the makeup artist Dick Page transforms a performer into a young (and old) Susan Sontag for a show at the Public Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five years ago, in the Builders Association production of “Super Vision,” the makeup artist Dick Page  turned the actress Moe Angelos into a Sri Lankan grandmother. Now, for the multimedia show “Sontag: Reborn,” currently at the Public Theater, he’s transformed the performer into a young (and old) Susan Sontag. “It was an unusual mandate, because I don’t normally get asked to make people look older, ” Page said, referring to his usual beat: fashion photo shoots and runway shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "Vain Glorious | ‘Sontag: Reborn': the Makeup", 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:16:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sandra Ballentine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ballentine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9f4a5f1-ba0a-51f5-98dd-d746bc941da4', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9f4a5f1-ba0a-51f5-98dd-d746bc941da4'}, {'abstract': 'He was for it before he was against it, and against it before he claimed credit for it.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/romney-and-the-bailout/', 'snippet': 'He was for it before he was against it, and against it before he claimed credit for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like a lot of people, I was fairly startled by Mitt Romney’s new defense of his work at Bain: it was just like the auto bailout!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney and the Bailout', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:16:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/289f5b0f-13d0-5e99-9a14-467125358d7d', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/289f5b0f-13d0-5e99-9a14-467125358d7d'}, {'abstract': 'The streaming music service Rdio is expanding to Germany; some limits to listening to Spotify; and more.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/digital-notes-streaming-across-borders/', 'snippet': 'The streaming music service Rdio is expanding to Germany; some limits to listening to Spotify; and more.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:32 p.m. | Updated Daily updates on the business of digital music:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital Notes: New Facebook Tool Lets Users Listen Together', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rdio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Spotify', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:20:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b32b1719-ec3e-5973-bc2d-c21a0b1cdef6', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b32b1719-ec3e-5973-bc2d-c21a0b1cdef6'}, {'abstract': 'Getting the best of a bad host with a steady course of compliments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/fashion/host-without-the-most.html', 'snippet': 'Getting the best of a bad host with a steady course of compliments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was recently at a dinner party and watched our 82-year-old host berate his 62-year-old wife at every turn. He told her he hated her outfit within five minutes of our arrival. From there, he seemed to criticize every step she took to make the evening pleasant. I was squirming in my chair and couldn’t wait to leave. I don’t know whom to confront about this abusive relationship. What’s a good friend to do? Anonymous', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Host Without the Most', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Host Without the Most', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:21:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f92ae88e-993b-564b-a22d-d7cee16101dc', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f92ae88e-993b-564b-a22d-d7cee16101dc'}, {'abstract': 'Looking at the entire population of college graduates — rather than just those with full-time jobs — the answer is yes. The median male college grad earns 12 percent less today than he did in 1969.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/do-college-grads-earn-less-now-than-40-years-ago/', 'snippet': 'Looking at the entire population of college graduates — rather than just those with full-time jobs — the answer is yes. The median male college grad earns 12 percent less today than he did in 1969.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday I wrote about how a college degree has gotten more economically valuable in the last few decades. A number of readers wrote in asking whether the numbers might be skewed by incomes at the very top. After all, the top 1 percent has received huge raises in the last few decades, and that group is mostly college-educated.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do College Grads Earn Less Now Than 40 Years Ago?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:26:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91c4be8d-22f8-51f1-acf4-f5b40d3e143b', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91c4be8d-22f8-51f1-acf4-f5b40d3e143b'}, {'abstract': 'A tutorial between the offensive football minds of the Patriots and the Florida Gators in 2005 helped shape the unit led by Tom Brady in New England.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/sports/football/like-tebow-patriots-sharpened-spread-offense-at-florida.html', 'snippet': 'A tutorial between the offensive football minds of the Patriots and the Florida Gators in 2005 helped shape the unit led by Tom Brady in New England.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tim Tebow was still a high school phenomenon in Ponte Vedra Beach, Fla., not yet the prototypical quarterback for an offense that had begun to sweep college football, when the first phone call from Foxborough, Mass., was made to Gainesville, Fla. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/13spread-1/13spread-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/13spread-1/13spread-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/13spread-1/13spread-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/13spread-1/13spread-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/13spread-1/13spread-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Like Tebow, Patriots Sharpened Offense at Florida', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Like Tebow, Patriots Sharpened Offense at Florida', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Florida', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:29:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f77b3abd-182c-57b5-bd9e-a3c9d03c00e7', 'word_count': 1090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f77b3abd-182c-57b5-bd9e-a3c9d03c00e7'}, {'abstract': 'The country music singer has been forced to to rest his voice since doctors removed a benign polyp from one of his vocal cords late last year.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/keith-urban-books-first-post-surgery-gig-at-grand-ole-opry/', 'snippet': 'The country music singer has been forced to to rest his voice since doctors removed a benign polyp from one of his vocal cords late last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Keith Urban will return to the stage for the first time since undergoing surgery on his vocal cords late last year when he sings at the Grand Ole Opry in February, the Opry announced Thursday. Mr. Urban has been forced to rest his voice since doctors at Vanderbilt University Medical Center removed a benign polyp from one of his vocal cords. Left untreated polyps can bleed when a singer is performing, leading to scarring on the vocal cords that can alter a voice’s timbre. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keith Urban Books First Post-Surgery Gig, at Grand Ole Opry', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Urban, Keith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grand Ole Opry House', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:36:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08cead4b-2aa0-5503-b327-17235e8fbc99', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08cead4b-2aa0-5503-b327-17235e8fbc99'}, {'abstract': 'A work by Gerhard Richter, wrongly thought to have been sold to the collector Bernard Arnault, will be donated to the Israel Museum by the true owner, Lily Safra.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/arts/design/israel-museum-receiving-a-work-by-gerhard-richter.html', 'snippet': 'A work by Gerhard Richter, wrongly thought to have been sold to the collector Bernard Arnault, will be donated to the Israel Museum by the true owner, Lily Safra.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trouble with art-world gossip is that it is often wrong, yet it goes around and around so fast that speculation becomes fact. Here’s a recent example: After the best of a group of abstract canvases by Gerhard Richter sold at Sotheby’s in November for $20.8 million, some spectators at the sale decided that the anonymous telephone buyer had been the French billionaire Bernard Arnault. It was an educated guess; Mr. Arnault is a big collector of contemporary art with deep pockets. He also happens to be planning to build a $200 million museum in Paris designed by the Los Angeles architect Frank Gehry.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13VOGEL1/13VOGEL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 781, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13VOGEL1/13VOGEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13VOGEL1/13VOGEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Surprise! Israel Museum Is Receiving a Richter', 'kicker': 'Inside Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surprise! Israel Museum Is Receiving a Richter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richter, Gerhard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schutz, Dana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e079c369-ab78-5802-b043-4a1b2b4b84cd', 'word_count': 934, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e079c369-ab78-5802-b043-4a1b2b4b84cd'}, {'abstract': 'The Baylor crowd offered support to the Oklahoma State’s women’s basketball team, whose head coach and assistant were killed in a plane crash in November, before the Lady Bears handed it a defeat Wednesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/in-victory-baylor-women-recognize-deeper-loss/', 'snippet': 'The Baylor crowd offered support to the Oklahoma State’s women’s basketball team, whose head coach and assistant were killed in a plane crash in November, before the Lady Bears handed it a defeat Wednesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Krista Pirtle of The Lariat at Baylor University will file reports about the top-ranked Baylor Lady Bears throughout the season for The Quad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Vict