rnational Consumer Electronics Show after Mr. Elop introduced a new phone that will be sold by AT&T, the Lumia 900:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/12/blogs/elop/elop-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One on One: Stephen Elop, Nokia Chief', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elop, Stephen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nokia Oyj', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:55:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f30409b8-400c-5a84-81e9-b2820c79d826', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f30409b8-400c-5a84-81e9-b2820c79d826'}, {'abstract': 'In business since 1938, the restaurant has a menu that changes perhaps only once in a generation, and the regulars like it that way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/15/nyregion/20120115JOINTss.html', 'snippet': 'In business since 1938, the restaurant has a menu that changes perhaps only once in a generation, and the regulars like it that way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In business since 1938, the restaurant has