w.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/theater/theater-listings-jan-13-19.html', 'snippet': 'A critical guide to theater productions, including those opening and in previews, in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theater', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Listings: Jan. 13 — 19', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T21:59:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/f38b3f87-31a8-5361-8d06-2dcf28e7130c', 'word_count': 3853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f38b3f87-31a8-5361-8d06-2dcf28e7130c'}, {'abstract': 'With its love for craftsmanship and design, the Ace Hotel finds a kindred spirit in the Tokyo-based fashion house Beams.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/ace-x-beams-beams-x-ace/', 'snippet': 'With its love for craftsmanship and design, the Ace Hotel finds a kindred spirit in the Tokyo-based fashion house Beams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today, the Ace Hotel unveils its latest collaboration with the Tokyo-based fashion house Beams.\xa0Founded in 1976, Beams is both a private clothing label and department store, as well as a major force within the Japanese retail scene. (The brand operates upwards of 100 locations throughout Japan and Hong Kong, offering music, furniture and art that caters to the ever-changing and expanding tastes of the youth demographic.) Finding something of a kindred spirit in the Japanese brand, the Ace Hotel, another purveyor of hipness, recently collaborated with the company on two one-off projects: a boxing-inspired collection produced with Canada’s Wings + Horns and luggage accessories with the iconic Porter brand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ace x Beams, Beams x Ace', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calderwood, Alex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ace Hotel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T22:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Dool', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dool', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3eb5796d-a528-5555-9200-c3d2e4c82104', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3eb5796d-a528-5555-9200-c3d2e4c82104'}, {'abstract': 'Recent theater, including the Under the Radar festival, has reflected the role that recorded reality and screens large and small play in virtually every aspect of everyday life.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/theater-talkback-the-stage-the-screen-and-the-screen-on-stage/', 'snippet': 'Recent theater, including the Under the Radar festival, has reflected the role that recorded reality and screens large and small play in virtually every aspect of everyday life.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:11 p.m. | Updated  Can film and theater live happily together in the same room? It’s not as if they haven’t had a long relationship already, with each regularly borrowing stories and stars from the other. But now these separate but equal art forms are attempting to practice cohabitation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: The Stage, the Screen and the Screen on Stage', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T22:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c223121-b7c1-5fba-9515-b98861d06d7e', 'word_count': 1457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c223121-b7c1-5fba-9515-b98861d06d7e'}, {'abstract': 'On the top of Christopher Clarey’s wish list for the 2012 tennis season is a rich rivalry in women’s tennis. What else do fans want to see this year?', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/compiling-a-wish-list-for-the-2012-tennis-season/', 'snippet': 'On the top of Christopher Clarey’s wish list for the 2012 tennis season is a rich rivalry in women’s tennis. What else do fans want to see this year?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year before the Australian Open, Christopher Clarey, who covers tennis for The Times and The International Herald Tribune, puts together his wish list for the year in tennis. This year his No. 1 wish is something to revive the women’s game. He writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Compiling a Wish List for the 2012 Tennis Season', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T22:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE NEW YORK TIMES', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5505420a-935a-5059-bc55-5a2be621afa9', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5505420a-935a-5059-bc55-5a2be621afa9'}, {'abstract': 'Just as the United States is entering a delicate moment in its dealings with the Taliban, a video has surfaced showing four Marines urinating on three dead Taliban fighters.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/fallout-from-urination-video-spreads/', 'snippet': 'Just as the United States is entering a delicate moment in its dealings with the Taliban, a video has surfaced showing four Marines urinating on three dead Taliban fighters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Graham Bowley reports on the widening condemnation from American officials, the NATO authorities in Afghanistan and the Afghan government of a video showing four Marines urinating on three dead Taliban fighters. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fallout From Urination Video Spreads', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geneva Conventions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marine Corps Base Camp Lejeune (SC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T22:01:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/196b7fed-029c-580c-bf03-4c87e98ede04', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/196b7fed-029c-580c-bf03-4c87e98ede04'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Homeland Security generated a list of Web sites and blogs that its staff members should monitor. Some of the recommendations, including Hulu and MySpace, seem unlikely choices.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/what-does-homeland-security-read/', 'snippet': 'The Department of Homeland Security generated a list of Web sites and blogs that its staff members should monitor. Some of the recommendations, including Hulu and MySpace, seem unlikely choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the last year, the Department of Homeland Security has been routinely monitoring social networking sites like Facebook, Twitter, YouTube and even MySpace. It is an avid reader of The Huffington Post, Jihad Watch, Technorati and, oddly, TruckingInfo.com. But apparently it has no interest in Techmeme and TechCrunch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Does Homeland Security Read?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T22:02:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b668b9a-fd0e-5562-9b8a-8e0911946d2d', 'word_count': 270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b668b9a-fd0e-5562-9b8a-8e0911946d2d'}, {'abstract': 'The idea of going to Green Bay in 2008 for an improbable championship game with the Giants wasn’t even on my radar. Until the Giants beat the Cowboys, that is, and Wilson, my law school roommate, called to say he had an extra ticket.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/eight-men-in-vintage-2008/', 'snippet': 'The idea of going to Green Bay in 2008 for an improbable championship game with the Giants wasn’t even on my radar. Until the Giants beat the Cowboys, that is, and Wilson, my law school roommate, called to say he had an extra ticket.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifty years ago, if the Giants were headed to Green Bay to play the Packers in the postseason, fans in New York might have considered themselves lucky to catch the game on television. Today, with tickets available online and frequent-flier miles accruing with every credit-card purchase, fans can dare to dream a little more boldly. Six members of a Chatham, N.J., softball team — a mix of lawyers, Wall Streeters and computer software salesmen — are set to travel to Lambeau Field for Sunday’s showdown between the Giants and the Packers. It will be a trip of cheap hotel rooms and high hopes, cramped rental cars and unexpectedly good seats at the game. The men — they will be joined by two pals in Milwaukee — have agreed to create a Titletown travelogue. Their hopes are to stay friends, keep their jobs and, well, see the Giants win.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eight Men In: Vintage 2008', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Favre, Brett', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tynes, Lawrence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Cowboys', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lambeau Field', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denmark', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milwaukee (Wis)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T22:05:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doug Chase', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doug', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chase', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07e78998-24b6-5f71-b656-407866a1c24a', 'word_count': 1046, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07e78998-24b6-5f71-b656-407866a1c24a'}, {'abstract': 'The Nocturnalist may have hung up her five gowns, but the party keeps rolling at Scene City.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/raise-a-glass-and-flash-a-smile/', 'snippet': 'The Nocturnalist may have hung up her five gowns, but the party keeps rolling at Scene City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Nocturnalist may have hung up her five gowns, but the party keeps rolling at Scene City.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raise a Glass and Flash a Smile', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Criss, Darren', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T22:05:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ad37b8b-9097-5f97-b413-ab22604a715a', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ad37b8b-9097-5f97-b413-ab22604