8731bf'}, {'abstract': '“Lula: Son of Brazil” is an unabashed hagiography of Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva, whose early life of poverty prepared him to lead the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/movies/lula-son-of-brazil-directed-by-fabio-barreto-review.html', 'snippet': '“Lula: Son of Brazil” is an unabashed hagiography of Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva, whose early life of poverty prepared him to lead the country.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Lula: Son of Brazil” is an unabashed hagiography that follows the rise from poverty to national prominence of Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva, who served as president of Brazil from 2003 through 2010. The film ends in 1980, the year his beloved mother died while he was in prison. In the same year he helped found the left-wing Workers Party, which stood up against the country’s right-wing military government.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13LULA_SPAN/13LULA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13LULA_SPAN/13LULA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13LULA_SPAN/LULA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13LULA_SPAN/13LULA_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13LULA_SPAN/13LULA_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Labor Hero’s Route to Leading a Nation', 'ki