derground springs. Huge, slow-moving snowflakes gently settle on my hair. In the dusk I can see just a few vague figures across the pond-size area — other women barely visible through the steam.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/travel/15NEXT1_SPAN/15NEXT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/travel/15NEXT1_SPAN/15NEXT1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/travel/15NEXT1_SPAN/15NEXT1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/travel/15NEXT1_SPAN/15NEXT1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/travel/15NEXT1_SPAN/15NEXT1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Niseko, Japan’s Own St. Moritz', 'kicker': 'Next Stop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Niseko, Japan’s Own St. Moritz', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Adventure Travel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T22:54:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ondine Cohane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ondine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1212c243-6249-58ac-9cd6-cf229726e4b4', 'word_count': 1694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1212c243-6249-58ac-9cd6-cf229726e4b4'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Ryder-Jones explains how an Italo Calvino novel inspired his new album, and how that music has now inspired a series of short films.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/12/the-italo-calvino-soundtrack/', 'snippet': 'Bill Ryder-Jones explains how an Italo Calvino novel inspired his new album, and how that music has now inspired a series of short films.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, the Liverpudlian musician and composer Bill Ryder-Jones — known previously for his guitar work with the British rock band The Coral, and also for his boyish good looks — released his first solo effort, “If…” (Domino). It is an album of mostly instrumental music, written as a kind of soundtrack to the Italo Calvino novel “If on a Winter’s Night a Traveler.” NPR is now streaming the entire record, which came out late last year in Britain to rave reviews.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Italo Calvino Soundtrack', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T23:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03ca71b7-4385-57b2-97c1-53576278af43', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03ca71b7-4385-57b2-97c1-53576278af43'}, {'abstract': 'The years and milestones whoosh by in “Sing Your Song,” a documentary about Harry Belafonte’s big bountiful life as singer, actor and activist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/movies/sing-your-song-documentary-about-harry-belafonte-review.html', 'snippet': 'The years and milestones whoosh by in “Sing Your Song,” a documentary about Harry Belafonte’s big bountiful life as singer, actor and activist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s only fitting that Harry Belafonte’s big, bountiful life has inspired an expansive, understandably hagiographic documentary, “Sing Your Song.” Silky voiced and snake hipped, with a supernova smile that dazzled Americans and helped demolish racial prejudices, he remains perhaps best known for his lilting version of the Caribbean folk tune “The Banana Boat Song” (“Day-O”), a requiem for the exhausted working man. Given his decades of tireless globe-sprinting crusading — alongside the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. and African activists alike — it’s clear that Mr. Belafonte rarely embraced the plaintive refrain of “Day-O”: “Daylight come and me wan’ go home.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13SING_SPAN/13SING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13SING_SPAN/13SING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13SING_SPAN/13SING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13SING_SPAN/13SING_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13SING_SPAN/13SING_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Struggle and Song Define a Life', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Sing Your Song'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Struggle And Song Define A Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belafonte, Harry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T23:01:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/eccf13aa-f7cf-5057-a6eb-49be6ebb8098', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eccf13aa-f7cf-5057-a6eb-49be6ebb8098'}, {'abstract': 'Studios, clubs and gyms are offering classes in bhangra, the high-energy dancing from Indian weddings and Bollywood movies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/arts/dance/bhangra-the-wedding-dance-thats-also-a-workout.html', 'snippet': 'Studios, clubs and gyms are offering classes in bhangra, the high-energy dancing from Indian weddings and Bollywood movies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATTENDING Indian weddings and ending up the night sweaty and tired from hours of bhangra dancing have been regular parts of my weekend repertory since I was a child. The catchy music can entice even the most die-hard wallflower to move. But though my heart beats fast, and my legs end up sore, I’ve never thought of bhangra as a workout.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13URBAN_SPAN/13URBAN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13URBAN_SPAN/13URBAN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13URBAN_SPAN/13URBAN_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13URBAN_SPAN/13URBAN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13URBAN_SPAN/13URBAN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wedding Dance That’s Also a Workout', 'kicker': 'Urban Athlete', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wedding Dance That’s Also a Workout', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T23:07:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f8bf867-06b8-5696-b0b6-c3b639a0b03e', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f8bf867-06b8-5696-b0b6-c3b639a0b03e'}, {'abstract': 'In “Contraband,” Mark Wahlberg has to smuggle in money from Panama, but the story is upstaged by the cinematography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/movies/contraband-with-mark-wahlberg-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Contraband,” Mark Wahlberg has to smuggle in money from Panama, but the story is upstaged by the cinematography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The absurdity of the story in the largely thrill-free thriller “Contraband,” its hairpin twists and outrageous coincidences, may keep even hungry action fans away. That’s too bad because the story doesn’t matter. (It rarely does.) If anything, the film’s adherence to implausibility as a defining narrative principle — a reliably winning Mark Wahlberg plays a New Orleans super-smuggler on a fast boat to Panama who faces a wolf, an armored truck and a drip painting — is part of its low-key kick, as is the director Baltasar Kormakur’s fondness for industrial landscapes. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13CONTRA_SPAN/13CONTRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13CONTRA_SPAN/13CONTRA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13CONTRA_SPAN/13CONTRA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13CONTRA_SPAN/13CONTRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13CONTRA_SPAN/13CONTRA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Quite an Honest Day’s Work', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Contraband'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Quite An Honest Day’s Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wahlberg, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ribisi, Giovanni', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foster, Ben', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T23:07:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ddb2b8a-4a3b-5044-94f5-a9b099c7f5d9', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ddb2b8a-4a3b-5044-94f5-a9b099c7f5d9'}, {'abstract': '“Hotsy Totsy Burlesque,” a soap opera of a burlesque show; selections from “The Gershwins’ Porgy and Bess” sung by Audra McDonald and Norm Lewis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/theater/strippers-with-a-plot-audra-mcdonald-and-sharon-van-etten.html', 'snippet': '“Hotsy Totsy Burlesque,” a soap opera of a burlesque show; selections from “The Gershwins’ Porgy and Bess” sung by Audra McDonald and Norm Lewis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gyms are packed with people who resolved to get fit in the new year, and while we’re all for getting healthy, nothing depresses us more than watching a roomful of hungry New Yorkers fight over free weights and climb Stairmasters to nowhere. The Miser is on vacation this week, living it up in the hedonist’s paradise of New Orleans, so we think it’s safe to assume that she’d prefer to kick back with a martini and a dish of salted peanuts and watch women of all shapes and sizes get their (and their audience’s) heart rates up the old-fashioned way: with stripping and high drama.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13MISER_SPAN/13MISER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13MISER_SPAN/13MISER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13MISER_SPAN/13MISER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13MISER_SPAN/13MISER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13MISER_SPAN/13MISER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Strippers With a Plot; Audra McDonald and Sharon Van Etten', 'kicker': 'Weekend Miser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Burlesque', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-12T23:08:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaux Laskey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaux', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Laskey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbb05b70-ad09-5d31-9e45-4bc14abe0758', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbb05b70-