ree works in two programs over several nights as part of the American Realness festival, at the Abrons Arts Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2007, after Daniel Linehan unveiled his earnest solo “Not About Everything,” he didn’t get my vote for most likely to succeed. In that piece, which he reprised at the Abrons Arts Center on Tuesday evening, he made a circle of reading material on the stage — along with a copy of Vogue, there was a book about the visual artist Francis Alÿs —\xa0and within that structure, he started spinning while reciting lines like, “This is not about therapy.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13MONTAGE_SPAN/MONTAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13MONTAGE_SPAN/MONTAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13MONTAGE_SPAN/MONTAGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 861, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13MONTAGE_SPAN/MONTAGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13MONTAGE_SPAN/MONTAGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Juxtaposing Movement And Speech', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Juxtaposing Movement And Speech', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABRONS ARTS CENTER', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank