t', 'value': 'Cooperatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T00:08:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rendon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rendon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab82ed33-4671-52d6-8c49-c551be4879f9', 'word_count': 1170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab82ed33-4671-52d6-8c49-c551be4879f9'}, {'abstract': 'In “Man on a Mission” Richard Garriott, a video-game millionaire and astronaut’s son, makes his dream come true by flying into space on a Russian flight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/movies/man-on-a-mission-with-richard-garriott-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Man on a Mission” Richard Garriott, a video-game millionaire and astronaut’s son, makes his dream come true by flying into space on a Russian flight.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Man on a Mission,” the most expensive home movie ever made, is one man’s genial account of his trip into outer space. What’s odd about it is that while you can certainly sense the joy that this fellow, Richard Garriott, feels in achieving a lifelong dream, you’re unlikely to be interested in imitating him. Cramped quarters, bulky wardrobe, unappetizing-looking food: it seems like a Worst Vacation Ever candidate.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/arts/13RDP_MANSPAN/13RDP_MANSPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/13/a