exas agree that online crimes are a problem, but they contend that Lamar Smith’s SOPA bill would do more harm than good.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/us/anti-piracy-bill-sopa-by-lamar-smith-gets-texas-pushback.html', 'snippet': 'Technology companies and business advocates in Texas agree that online crimes are a problem, but they contend that Lamar Smith’s SOPA bill would do more harm than good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'United States Representative Lamar Smith says online piracy is damaging the United States economy and putting American lives at risk. Foreign Web sites that distribute American-made entertainment and counterfeit products, like fake pharmaceuticals, are “stealing our profits, they’re stealing our jobs and they may be endangering the health of Americans,” said Mr. Smith, a Republican from San Antonio. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/us/13TTTECH/13TTTECH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Texan’s Anti-Piracy Bill Gets Home State Pushback', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texan’s Anti-Piracy Bill Gets Home State Pushback', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Lamar S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intellectual Property', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T00:54:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Becca Aaronson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Becca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aaronson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9bf143e-68c3-5575-a848-14f37bcc1052', 'word_count': 986, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9bf143e-68c3-5575-a848-14f37bcc1052'}, {'abstract': 'Somali militants have attacked a Kenyan police post near the Kenya-Somalia border, killing at least six people and kidnapping several others, Kenyan officials said Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/world/africa/somalia-rebels-attack-kenya.html', 'snippet': 'Somali militants have attacked a Kenyan police post near the Kenya-Somalia border, killing at least six people and kidnapping several others, Kenyan officials said Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Somali militants have attacked a Kenyan police post near the Kenya-Somalia border, killing at least six people and kidnapping several others, Kenyan officials said Thursday. The officials said that three police officers, a civil servant and a teacher were among the dead in the raid at Gerille on Wednesday, and that several government employees were missing. The Shabab militant group posted a message on Twitter saying its forces had “seized Kenyan vehicles, communication equipment and a cache of weapons.” Somali militants have staged several hit-and-run attacks inside Kenya since October, when Kenyan forces crossed into Somalia to fight the Shabab. The Shabab said Thursday that they were “responding to aggressive Kenyan invasion against Muslims of Somalia.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Somalia: Rebels Attack Kenya', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So