an lacks feasible alternatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/world/asia/nuclear-power-emerges-as-election-issue-in-taiwan.html', 'snippet': 'The leading challenger in Taiwan’s presidential election wants to end the country’s reliance on nuclear energy, but her critics say that Taiwan lacks feasible alternatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAIPEI, Taiwan — When voters here choose a president and a new legislature on Saturday, their decisions will also determine whether Taiwan pulls the plug on a state-backed nuclear power industry that provides the country with a fifth of its electricity. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vote Holds Fate of Nuclear Power in Taiwan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vote Holds Fate of Nuclear Power in Taiwan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chinese Nationalist Party (Taiwan)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Progressive Party (Taiwan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ma Ying-jeou', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsai Ing-wen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T01:42:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6762489-952a-51d2-aadd-ff09ece1dd59', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6762489-952a-51d2-aadd-ff09ece1dd59'}, {'abstract': 'Taiwan can serve as a model for democratizing forces in China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/opinion/why-taiwans-future-matters.html', 'snippet': 'Taiwan can serve as a model for democratizing forces in China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR most of its history, Taiwan’s destiny was determined by three great powers — China, Japan and America. Now, as the 18th-largest economy in the world and a thoroughly democratized nation, Taiwan is still perceived by some in Washington as a potential bargaining chip in crafting a new relationship with China. This is a mistake.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Taiwan’s Future Matters', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Taiwan’s Future Matters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T01:43:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Su Chi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Su', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd182b0e-0332-5980-a281-5d422aff8610', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd182b0e-0332-5980-a281-5d422aff8610'}, {'abstract': 'Saturday in Houston, Deena Kastor, the 2004 Olympic bronze medalist, will run her first marathon since London in April 2010, hoping to qualify for the 2012 Games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/sports/deena-kastor-sees-olympic-marathon-trials-as-a-new-start.html', 'snippet': 'Saturday in Houston, Deena Kastor, the 2004 Olympic bronze medalist, will run her first marathon since London in April 2010, hoping to qualify for the 2012 Games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — Marathon training was out of the question. Still, Deena Kastor, the 2004 Olympic bronze medalist, figured she could run for 20 or 30 minutes a day during her pregnancy. She was wrong. Aching in her sides and her back grew so acute that even walking the dog around the block sometimes forced her to sit and rest.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/y-marathon/y-marathon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 567, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/y-marathon/y-marathon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/sports/y-marathon/y-marathon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kastor, After Pregnancy, Sees Trials as New Start', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kastor, After Pregnancy, Sees Trials as New Start', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kastor, Deena', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marathon Running', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2