nt nuclear plant closes in the next few years, the 2,000 megawatts of electricity that it produces will have to come from somewhere else.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If anyone, or any business, can get a good deal on electricity, it ought to be Consolidated Edison, which buys loads of it every year and then sells it to three million customers in New York City and the suburbs. Like most traditional utility companies, it has gotten out of the power generation business in recent years and is now a distribution company. It buys the electricity that it delivers from generators run by independent companies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vision for Affordable Energy Even if Indian Point Nuclear Plant Is Shut Down', 'kicker': 'About New York', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trying to Supply the City With Affordable Power Even if an Aging Plant Closes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian Point Nuclear Power Plant (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consolidated Edison Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brennan, James F', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T01:55:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role'