ublicans Asked to Bash Obama, Not One Another', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican National Committee', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T02:20:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/096515eb-cdf2-50a4-a2b1-a38d00e7c71b', 'word_count': 755, 'uri': 'nyt://article/096515eb-cdf2-50a4-a2b1-a38d00e7c71b'}, {'abstract': 'The boat, docked at a marina on Westchester Creek in the Bronx, crushed a small, empty boat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/nyregion/bronx-houseboat-capsizes-on-westchester-creek.html', 'snippet': 'The boat, docked at a marina on Westchester Creek in the Bronx, crushed a small, empty boat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The two-story houseboat had been docked on a quiet creek in a hidden corner of the Bronx for a decade. It had withstood the strong winds of Tropical Storm Irene, and as far as its owner could tell, no serious repairs were needed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/nyregion/BOAT/BOAT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/nyregion/BOAT/BOAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/nyregion/BOAT/BOAT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Houseboat Tips Over, but All Onboard Escape', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Houseboat Tips Over, But All Aboard Escape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Houseboats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boats and Boating', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T02:21:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Stelloh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelloh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2c74c9b-1afc-503c-9f50-1904ce6751ef', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2c74c9b-1afc-503c-9f50-1904ce6751ef'}, {'abstract': 'The Kettle of Fish is a haven for displaced Green Bay fans, who gather at the bar weekly to watch their beloved Packers and feast on cheese and bratwurst.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/sports/football/packers-fans-find-a-home-in-greenwich-village.html', 'snippet': 'The Kettle of Fish is a haven for displaced Green Bay fans, who gather at the bar weekly to watch their beloved Packers and feast on cheese and bratwurst.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York, for all of its diversity, is also a city of defined communities, like the group of men who, for years, have gathered in the back of the Kettle of Fish in Greenwich Village. There, around a round oak table that is supposed to seat six but can be home to a few more, and not far from the gaze of a bobblehead Ray Nitschke doll, they watch their Green Bay Packers play — week after winter week, pleasant enough to other fans who share their allegiances yet protective of their small bit of turf deep inside the low-ceilinged bar.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Packers Fans Find a Home in Greenwich Village', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bratwurst, N.Y.C.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T02:24:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ryan Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d0a1b16-cb65-52b5-94bd-e50ab3b91a72', 'word_count': 1057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d0a1b16-cb65-52b5-94bd-e50ab3b91a72'}, {'abstract': 'Tougher international sanctions have had some effect on Iran, but talks are also needed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/opinion/dangerous-tension-with-iran.html', 'snippet': 'Tougher international sanctions have had some effect on Iran, but talks are also needed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With tensions rising over Iran’s nuclear program,\xa0the Obama administration has now warned the country’s supreme leader, Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, that Iran’s threat to close the Strait of Hormuz would provoke an American response. Earlier this week, international monitors confirmed that Iran has begun enriching uranium at a new underground plant. The United States and\xa0 Europe are tightening sanctions to choke off Iranian oil revenues. On Wednesday, an Iranian nuclear scientist died in a bomb attack en route to work, and a government newspaper signaled that the Islamic Revolutionary Guards Corps might retaliate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dangerous Tension With Iran', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dangerous Tension With Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Strait of Hormuz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T02:26:54+0000', 'document_type': '