r for discrimination was unwise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the case of Cheryl Perich, a teacher fired by a church-run school, the Supreme Court ruled on Wednesday that the Constitution’s protection of religious freedom bars her from suing the church under federal workplace discrimination law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ministerial Exception', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Ministerial Exception', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perich, Cheryl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clergy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T02:30:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7faa3c6d-4ae4-5b19-a7d3-faeae0d08071', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7faa3c6d-4ae4-5b19-a7d3-faeae0d08071'}, {'abstract': 'Candlestick Park, which is expected to be demolished within the next decade, got a tune-up but no costly new electrical parts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/us/city-patches-candlestick-park-power-system-and-waits.html', 'snippet': 'Candlestick Park, which is expected to be demolished within the next decade, got a tune-up but no costly new electrical parts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gambling that the lights will stay on at Candlestick Park during a nationally televised football playoff game this weekend, the City of San Francisco decided to punt on plans to replace two aging electrical switches that were blamed for blackouts during the 49ers’ final regular-season home game last month. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Patches Stadium’s Power, and Waits', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Patches Stadium’s Power, and Waits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Candlestick Park', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T02:32:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Upton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Upton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3491aa13-4dae-5beb-95d8-024e6b6f8bf2', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3491aa13-4dae-5beb-95d8-024e6b6f8bf2'}, {'abstract': '“Super PACs” and changes in how delegates are awarded are helping keep the Republican field crowded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/us/politics/pacs-aid-allows-mitt-romneys-rivals-to-extend-race.html', 'snippet': '“Super PACs” and changes in how delegates are awarded are helping keep the Republican field crowded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Under the old political rules, Mitt Romney arrived in South Carolina this week the prohibitive Republican front-runner: flush with cash, awash in endorsements from a party establishment starting to coalesce behind him and buoyed by victories in Iowa and New Hampshire.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/us/13campaign2_span/13campaign2_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/13/us/13campaign2_span/13campaign2_span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/us/13campaign2_span/13campaign2_span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/13/us/13campaign2_span/13campaign2_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/13/us/13campaign2_span/13campaign2_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'PACs’ Aid Allows Romney’s Rivals to Extend Race', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'PACs’ Aid Allows Romney’s Rivals to Extend Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T02:32:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore and Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9f3e9ff-a27f-5e2b-81a2-07fdb8c0d769', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9f3e9ff-a27f-5e2b-81a2-07fdb8c0d769'}, {'abstract': 'Ross Mirkarimi, San Francisco’s new sheriff who took office on Sunday, has some people wondering if he understands the law he swore to uphold.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/us/public-concern-over-mirkarimis-private-matter.html', 'snippet': 'Ross Mirkarimi, San Francisco’s new sheriff who took office on Sunday, has some people wondering if he understands the law he swore to uphold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scott James is a columnist for The Bay Citizen. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Public Concern Over San Francisco Sheriff’s ‘Private Matter’', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker'