the company, the Detroit International Bridge Company, had avoided fulfilling its contract to help build ramps connecting two freeways to the bridge. The state partnered with the company in 2004 to build the ramps, spending $230 million on the project. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan: Bridge Owner Is Jailed', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan: Bridge Owner Is Jailed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T05:04:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a63d42a-9d0b-54b5-82f4-f565d7010fa4', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a63d42a-9d0b-54b5-82f4-f565d7010fa4'}, {'abstract': 'Police officers killed a gunman in a shootout on Thursday after a car chase and the discovery of shooting victims in a New Orleans home', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/us/louisiana-gunman-3-others-killed.html', 'snippet': 'Police officers killed a gunman in a shootout on Thursday after a car chase and the discovery of shooting victims in a New Orleans home', 'lead_paragraph': ' Police officers killed a gunman in a shootout on Thursday after a car chase and the discovery of shooting victims in a New Orleans home. The police said the chase ensued when a car fled a home in the eastern part of the city where five people had been shot, three fatally. After the car crashed, a man emerged, firing at the police. He was killed and two people with him were wounded, the police said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Louisiana: Gunman, 3 Others Killed', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Louisiana: Gunman, 3 Others Killed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T05:07:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b00ddbeb-f685-5718-99e7-bb098a292b11', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b00ddbeb-f685-5718-99e7-bb098a292b11'}, {'abstract': 'Major League Soccer held its draft Thursday in Kansas City, Mo.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/m-l-s-hot-stove-how-super-is-the-m-l-s-superdraft/', 'snippet': 'Major League Soccer held its draft Thursday in Kansas City, Mo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It does not quite reach the heights of Orwellian Newspeak, hyperbole is probably good enough, but what exactly is so super about Major League Soccer’s so-called SuperDraft? (This from the outfit that has given us “soccer-specific stadiums” that are anything but specific to soccer.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Super is the M.L.S. SuperDraft?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 's