act': 'The secret underbelly of Bangladesh is the quiet, determined improvement in the health and well-being of its people.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/feral-cats-and-social-indicators-in-bangladesh/', 'snippet': 'The secret underbelly of Bangladesh is the quiet, determined improvement in the health and well-being of its people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DHAKA, Bangladesh — Last month there was an extraordinary attack at the Dhaka Children’s Hospital. One of the dozens of stray cats that call the hospital home reportedly walked into a neonatal ward, mounted a bed where a six-day-old girl was receiving phototherapy treatment for jaundice and tried to take her as prey. According to the Daily Star, the cat had pulled the newborn off her bed and onto the floor, and dragged her partway to the ward’s open door before anyone noticed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feral Cats and Social Indicators', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cats', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dhaka (Bangladesh)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T10:59:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Morrison', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morrison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efc207f7-2624-5b55-a862-32c9bb7f9b29', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efc207f7-2624-5b55-a862-32c9bb7f9b29'}, {'abstract': 'After