ners | The 2011 ‘Year in Rap’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T12:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/944decd0-a05d-59f3-813a-2948a62621e7', 'word_count': 1349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/944decd0-a05d-59f3-813a-2948a62621e7'}, {'abstract': 'I came to the conclusion that maybe I didn’t know what I didn’t know.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/why-i-decided-to-join-vistage/', 'snippet': 'I came to the conclusion that maybe I didn’t know what I didn’t know.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As kids, when we used to wrestle and play around, we had an expression for when someone had you pinned, and you were in enough pain that you wanted to concede — you would yell, “calf rope!” The rodeo term is not one I have used in running my business. At least not until recently.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why I Decided to Join Vistage', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T12:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By MP Mueller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mp', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mueller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'org