ising tensions between Iran and the West.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the first post in the Viewfinder series, a roundup of opinion and commentary from international media.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Prospect of War With Iran', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T12:02:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Politi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Politi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50d207f3-f484-56fb-aa1b-e71c2c89aaf9', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50d207f3-f484-56fb-aa1b-e71c2c89aaf9'}, {'abstract': 'In an election climate largely defined by the anxieties of the middle class, working people are now more likely than not to face a choice in November between two candidates who sometimes seem to have trouble relating to them.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/obama-and-romney-face-a-tough-fight-for-key-group/', 'snippet': 'In an election climate largely defined by the anxieties of the middle class, working people are now more likely than not to face a choice in November between two candidates who sometimes seem to have trouble relating to them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Both are Harvard-educated millionaires. Both have been criticized as elitist and technocratic. Both have struggled to handle the populist anger coursing through politics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama and Romney Face a Tough Fight for Key Group', 'kicker': None, 'content_ki