ith whom he studied many years ago.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15cello1_span/mag-15Cello-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15cello1_span/mag-15Cello-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15cello1_span/mag-15Cello-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15cello1_span/15cello1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/magazine/15cello1_span/15cello1_span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Selling a 300-Year-Old Cello', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dispossessed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenhouse, Bernard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lesser, Laurence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stradivari, Antonio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Violins', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellos', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T15:17:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8406ecff-0887-52cc-98be-adf181a08ce0', 'word_count': 2891, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8406ecff-0887-52cc-98be-adf181a08ce0'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists suggest that focusing on 14 ways to cut emissions of those heat-trapping substances could reduce projected global warming by nearly one degree by 2050.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/on-our-radar-reducing-soot-and-methane/', 'snippet': 'Scientists suggest that focusing on 14 ways to cut emissions of those heat-trapping substances could reduce projected global warming by nearly one degree by 2050.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reiterating that carbon dioxide need not be the only focus, an international team of scientists suggests 14 ways of controlling emissions of methane and soot, from cleaning up cookstoves to changing cultivation methods for rice paddies. If adopted more widely, the scientists calculate, these methods would reduce projected global warming by 0.9 degrees Fahrenheit by the year 2050. [Associated Press].', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Reducing Soot and Methane', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Methane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sharks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Donnell, Rosie", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Geological Survey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T15:27:13+0000', 'document_typ