 'Not for Vampires Only', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not for Vampires Only', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Noise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Light', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:22:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Constance Rosenblum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Constance', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenblum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de54226b-98dd-53fd-bfb1-6aa65060f70e', 'word_count': 1912, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de54226b-98dd-53fd-bfb1-6aa65060f70e'}, {'abstract': 'Winning the Chopin Competition early in his career did not stop the pianist Garrick Ohlsson from insisting on musical challenges from styles and periods outside his specialty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/arts/music/garrick-ohlsson-chopin-expert-sets-his-sights-on-liszt.html', 'snippet': 'Winning the Chopin Competition early in his career did not stop the pianist Garrick Ohlsson from insisting on musical challenges from styles and periods outside his specialty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLASSICAL music listeners, like anyone else, tend to categorize their heroes, if only for the sake of quickly identifying a player’s strengths or a composer’s style. Garrick Ohlsson has spent the 42 years since he won the gold medal at the International Chopin Piano Competition in Warsaw balancing the benefits of having a recognized specialty with his preference, a reputation for breadth.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15GARRICK1_SPAN/15GARRICK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15GARRICK1_SPAN/15GARRICK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15GARRICK1_SPAN/15GARRICK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15GARRICK1_SPAN/15GARRICK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15GARRICK1_SPAN/15GARRICK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Specializing In Spreading His Wings', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Specializing In Spreading His Wings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ohlsson, Garrick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:22:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f968545-b58d-5099-8fc8-78d5f1943df1', 'word_count': 1592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f968545-b58d-5099-8fc8-78d5f1943df1'}, {'abstract': 'Playing musical chairs with celebrities like Meryl Streep and Patton Oswalt at the Critics’ Choice Awards.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/meryl-streep-michelle-williams-and-a-game-of-musical-chairs/', 'snippet': 'Playing musical chairs with celebrities like Meryl Streep and Patton Oswalt at the Critics’ Choice Awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bagger always enjoys the Critics’ Choice, the first televised awards show of the season: it moves briskly, and there’s a fun game of musical chairs to be played during commercial breaks, when everyone hobnobs around the room as the disembodied voice of a showrunner counts down the seconds until airtime. Quick: shoot over to Meryl Streep, then zigzag to Michelle Williams! Ninety seconds left – can you make it over to Patton Oswalt? (The Bagger did. “We’re all back here getting wasted,” he reported of his castmates at the “Young Adult” table, though they seemed pretty well-behaved to us.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meryl Streep, Michelle Williams and a Game of Musical Chairs', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:23:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/879fbb26-fc06-5593-a264-ff096ace2dc4', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/879fbb26-fc06-5593-a264-ff096ace2dc4'}, {'abstract': 'Amnesty International is releasing “Chimes of Freedom,” a four-CD benefit album with covers of Bob Dylan songs, into a market that has changed since the days when pop music and social activism became bonded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/