iddle age; Alexander Star talks about Friedrich Nietzsche’s impact on American readers; Julie Bosman with notes from the field; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2012/01/13/books/review/13books_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week, Patricia Cohen discusses her new book about the science of middle age; Alexander Star talks about Friedrich Nietzsche’s impact on American readers; Julie Bosman with notes from the field; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tan...', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Patricia Cohen discusses her new book about the science of middle age; Alexander Star talks about Friedrich Nietzsche’s impact on American readers; Julie Bosman with notes from the field; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:38:05+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/70a49a68-673e-54bb-9a55-ca9202611e25', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/70a49a68-673e-54bb-9a55-ca9202611e25'}, {'abstract': 'In honor of Dr. Martin Luther King Day, the dean of the UCLA School of Law looks at the legacy of Brown v. Board of Education and Dr. King, and writes:  "Without a strong sense of how liberty shapes our personhood and dignity, equality can mean little more than a race to the bottom for the unfortunate and disadvantaged."', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/13/for-dr-king-freedom-and-education-were-intertwined/', 'snippet': 'In honor of Dr. Martin Luther King Day, the dean of the UCLA School of Law looks at the legacy of Brown v. Board of Education and Dr. King, and writes:  "Without a strong sense of how liberty shapes our personhood and dignity, equality can mean li...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Dr. King, Freedom and Education Were Intertwined', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:40:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By RACHEL F. MORAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'MORAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34163540-5357-5460-ac5c-034ea4e0e91a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34163540-5357-5460-ac5c-034ea4e0e91a'}, {'abstract': 'Furious at a system that she thought was unjust, Clark refused to be represented in court, trumpeted revolutionary action and ended up with a 75-year sentence that she is still serving.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/writing-about-radicals-then-and-now/', 'snippet': 'Furious at a system that she thought was unjust, Clark refused to be represented in court, trumpeted revolutionary action and ended up with a 75-year sentence that she is still serving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tom Robbins has a terrific story in the magazine on Sunday about the making — and unmaking — of the ’60s radical Judith Clark. Clark drove one of the getaway cars during the Brink’s holdup in 1981 when two police officers and an armored-car guard were killed. Furious at a system that she thought was unjust, Clark refused to be represented in court, trumpeted revolutionary action and ended up with a 75-year sentence that she is still serving. Over many visits and phone conversations, Robbins explored Clark’s life behind bars and her slow transformation from unrepentant young radical to a reflective, deeply regretful model inmate. Clark talks a great deal about the importance of her relationship with her daughter — who was 11 months old at the time of the crime — in changing her. And the role her parents played in nurturing that relationship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Writing About Radicals, Then and Now', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Egan, Jennifer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Brink's Inc", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich (Conn)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:40:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ilena Silverman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ilena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silverman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ac922f5-b049-500a-9919-2667c4503f23', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ac922f5-b049-500a-9919-2667c4503f23'}, {'abstract': 'The Nets have been only sporadically competitive under Mikhail D. Prokhorov, who said his candidacy for president of Russia did not diminish his interest in the team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/sports/basketball/brooklyn-awaits-but-nets-destination-as-a-team-is-still-unclear.html', 'snippet': 'The Nets have been only sporadically competitive under Mikhail D. Prokhorov, who said his candidacy for president of Russia did not diminish his interest in the team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — The question of where the Nets are headed as an organization and as a basketball team leads only to a host of potential destinations that range from exhilaration to dread, with an occasional detour into comic relief. Technically, and temporarily, the Nets are in Newark, on their way to a new home next season in Brooklyn. By all other practical means of appraisal, their dateline should be limbo.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/nets/nets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/nets/nets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/nets/nets-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brooklyn Awaits Nets, but Their Destination as a Team Is Unclear', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brooklyn Awaits Nets, But Their Destination As a Team Is Unclear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Brook', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Dwight', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Nets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Deron', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prokhorov, Mikhail D', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:47:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30c760c0-15c9-57e5-9316-308d9668fa53', 'word_count': 1513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30c760c0-15c9-57e5-9316-308d9668fa53'}, {'abstract': 'An American author flies to Germany weighed down with 60 copies of a quixotic anthology.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/books/review/my-berlin-airlift.html', 'snippet': 'An American author flies to Germany weighed down with 60 copies of a quixotic anthology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Smuggling Afghan heroin or women from Odessa would have been more reprehensible, but more logical. You know you’re a fool when what you’re doing makes even the post office seem efficient. Everything I was packing into this unwieldy, 1980s-vintage suitcase was available online. I don’t mean that when I arrived in Berlin I could have ordered more Levi’s 510s for next-day delivery. I mean, I was packing books.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/books/review/15cohen-img/15cohen-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/books/review/15cohen-img/15cohen-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/books/review/15cohen-img/15cohen-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Berlin Airlift', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Means of Delivery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:47:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/305765df-f60a-58f7-a8bf-328026a941d9', 'word_count': 1176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/305765df-f60a-58f7-a8bf-328026a941d9'}, {'abstract': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/books/review/paperback-row.html', 'snippet': 'Paperback books of particular interest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE VIEW FROM LAZY POINT: A Natural Year in an Unnatural World,  by Carl Safina. Illustrations by Trudy Nicholson. Maps by Jon Luoma (Picador/John Macrae, $18.) Safina, a marine ecologist, reflects on nature’s connectedness in a series of field reports from his home on the shore of eastern Long Island and his travels to the Arctic, the Antarctic, the Caribbean and the Pacific Islands.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paperback Row', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paperback Row', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:49:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subse