)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carpenter, J E R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:51:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian S. Toy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Toy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8923f7ec-df14-5e11-b165-e0590583fd47', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8923f7ec-df14-5e11-b165-e0590583fd47'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to a recent review of Peter Ackroyd’s “The Death of King Arthur.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/books/review/the-legend-of-camelot.html', 'snippet': 'A reader responds to a recent review of Peter Ackroyd’s “The Death of King Arthur.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Legend of Camelot', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Legend of Camelot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:52:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/c02144c2-35a5-5a1b-8d7f-d522ed73d150', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c02144c2-35a5-5a1b-8d7f-d522ed73d150'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to a recent review of Laurent Dubois’s “Haiti: The Aftershocks of History.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/books/review/carpentiers-kingdom.html', 'snippet': 'A reader responds to a recent review of Laurent Dubois’s “Haiti: The Aftershocks of History.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carpentier’s ‘Kingdom’', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carpentier’s ‘Kingdom’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:52:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/877afc6b-631b-58f7-ade1-67801210387b', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/877afc6b-631b-58f7-ade1-67801210387b'}, {'abstract': 'In a collection of nonfiction pieces, the novelist William Gibson reveals our own world to us as a science-fictional marvel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/books/review/distrust-that-particular-flavor-by-william-gibson-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'In a collection of nonfiction pieces, the novelist William Gibson reveals our own world to us as a science-fictional marvel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On one of his trips to New York, William Gibson stopped before an antiques shop that would end up haunting him. He tried the door. It was locked. Over the years, he searched for the shop window many times — it seemed to wander around SoHo and materialize on unpredictable streets. When\xadever he peered through it at the treasures within, he felt as if he were glimpsing the props from a dream. “There is no knowing what might appear there,” Gibson writes in one of the essays collected in “Distrust That Particular Flavor.” Once, he spied a collection of toy-size missiles.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/books/review/Kennedy01/Kennedy01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 871, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/books/review/Kennedy01/Kennedy01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/books/review/Kennedy01/Kennedy01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'William Gibson’s Future Is Now', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rewiring Reality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibson, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science Fiction', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:54:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pagan Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pagan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc9d3bf2-2824-51df-bc02-812ded9a20a5', 'word_count': 1350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc9d3bf2-2824-51df-bc02-812ded9a20a5'}, {'abstract': 'In Jennifer E. Smith’s Y.A. novel, a chance meeting on a flight to London redirects a girl’s fate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/books/review/the-statistical-probability-of-love-at-first-sight-by-jennifer-e-smith-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'In Jennifer E. Smith’s Y.A. novel, a chance meeting on a flight to London redirects a girl’s fate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As much as teenagers and adults alike try to strategize over the search for love, in the end whether two people connect is a kind of elusive, slippery magic, up to the gods or to some unseen force, and it always comes down to one thing: timing. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strangers on a Plane', 'kicker': "Children's Books", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strangers on a Plane', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Jennifer E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:55:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Whitney Joiner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Whitney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Joiner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bb18d81-b8b1-5116-9233-1ff377ec7fdc', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bb18d81-b8b1-5116-9233-1ff377ec7fdc'}, {'abstract': 'Today, Charlotte Stockdale adds the title of style editor of Jo Malone to her ever-evolving C.V.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/vain-glorious-jo-malone-gets-a-style-editor/', 'snippet': 'Today, Charlotte Stockdale adds the title of style editor of Jo Malone to her ever-evolving C.V.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charlotte Stockdale’s career is an inspired one. The British-born beauty is a multitalented success, having done everything from serving as a muse to her good friend Karl Lagerfeld to styling the Victoria’s Secret runway show and holding down the fashion director post at i-D. Today, Stockdale adds the title of style editor of Jo Malone London to her ever-evolving C.V.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Jo Malone London Gets a Style Editor', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T16:55:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Nima', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nima', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe5e7a86-8c91-5f4d-9684-09352d965b4b', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe5e7a86-8c91-5f4d-9684-09352d965b4b'}, {'abstract': 'Vanilla Ice, whose “Ice Ice Baby” was a 1990 monster hit, has a show on the DIY Network about home remodeling: “The Vanilla Ice Project.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/arts/television/the-vanilla-ice-project-on-the-diy-network.html', 'snippet': 'Vanilla Ice, whose “Ice Ice Baby” was a 1990 monster hit, has a show on the DIY Network about home remodeling: “The Vanilla Ice Project.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAKE WORTH, Fla. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15VANILLA_SPAN/15VANILLA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15VANILLA_SPAN/15VANILLA_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15VANILLA_SPAN/15VANILLA_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cr