ganization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f937358-6eca-5033-b764-f9f44a5dca1c', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f937358-6eca-5033-b764-f9f44a5dca1c'}, {'abstract': 'With 2,113 residents nestled into 1.3 square miles of hilly, tree-lined terrain, Essex Fells is the smallest community in Essex County and also one of its most desirable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/realestate/essex-fells-nj-living-in-holding-fast-to-old-fashioned-ways.html', 'snippet': 'With 2,113 residents nestled into 1.3 square miles of hilly, tree-lined terrain, Essex Fells is the smallest community in Essex County and also one of its most desirable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVERY year about this time in Essex Fells, after the first wintry gusts have swept the leaves off the trees and residents have gathered around to watch the annual lighting of the borough’s Christmas tree, a large pond off Fells Road turns into the borough’s meeting place.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/realestate/15SUBLIVINGIN_SPAN/sub-living-in-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/realestate/15SUBLIVINGIN_SPAN/sub-living-in-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/realestate/15SUBLIVINGIN_SPAN/sub-living-in-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 492, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/realestate/15SUBLIVINGIN_SPAN/sub-living-in-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': '