D homage to the choreographer Pina Bausch, that it’s easy to overlook another documentary that is also competing for the Academy Award for foreign-language film. “José and Pilar,” directed by Miguel Gonçalves Mendes, is Portugal’s submission, and it too comes with an impressive pedigree. Co-produced by the directors Pedro Almodóvar and Fernando Meirelles (“City of God”), it examines the relationship of love and support that sustains José Saramago, the Portuguese novelist who won the Nobel Prize for literature in 1998, and his wife, Pilar del Rio, as Saramago battled to write one last novel before his death in 2010 at the age of 87. Mr. Gonçalves Mendes, 33, is in the United States this month for festival showings of the film and spoke by telephone from Palm Springs. Here is an edited version of what he had to say:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking Wisdom From José Saramago', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALMODOVAR, PEDRO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bausch, Pina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meirelles, Fernando', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saramago, Jose', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wenders, Wim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T17:59:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa110154-a280-5aff-8e16-6878949819b0', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa110154-a280-5aff-8e16-6878949819b0'}, {'abstract': 'Lohri celebrations in Amritsar, Punjab.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/image-of-the-day-january-13/', 'snippet': 'Lohri celebrations in Amritsar, Punjab.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: January 13', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T18:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04949153-2a23-525a-a1e0-583399d0afcd', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04949153-2a23-525a-a1e0-583399d0afcd'}, {'abstract': 'With a Spielberg movie, a newly translated biography and a place atop The Times’s graphic books best-seller list, the Belgian comic book character Tintin is having a genuine American moment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'With a Spielberg movie, a newly translated biography and a place atop The Times’s graphic books best-seller list, the Belgian comic book character Tintin is having a genuine American moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THUNDERING TYPHOONS: Growing up, my brothers and I passed many happy days working our way through the “Tintin” comic books, sprawled on our floors with no concern for the stories’ literary or cultural status. We weren’t hipsters; we were kids. But we were also, apparently, in some kind of vanguard. Now that the Belgian Tintin is having a genuine American moment — a Spielberg movie; a newly translated biography of his creator, Hergé (reviewed next week); a place atop The New York Times’s graphic books best-seller list — we’re hearing that nobody but the elect was in on the secret back then. “Though beloved in most parts of the world,” Charles McGrath wrote in The Times recently, Tintin “is practically unknown in the United States.” Huh. It’s a little weird, finding out you were every bit as out of touch as you feared. While I wouldn’t go as far as the British critic Nicholas Lezard, who compared Spielberg’s film adaptation to a rape, it is disconcerting to see the icons of your youth being pawed at by the mainstream. Next thing you know, they’ll make a movie of the Smurfs.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/books/review/22insidelist-img/22insidelist-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 190, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/books/review/22insidelist-img/22insidelist-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/books/review/22insidelist-img/22insidelist-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': 'TBR', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T18:02:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gregory Cowles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gregory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/717ed5b1-85cc-55ff-9f3d-3304040a47d6', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/717ed5b1-85cc-55ff-9f3d-3304040a47d6'}, {'abstract': 'Raro Video has released “Il Cappotto,” Alberto Lattuada’s adaptation of the Gogol short story “The Overcoat,” on DVD.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/movies/homevideo/a-version-of-gogols-short-story-the-overcoat-on-dvd.html', 'snippet': 'Raro Video has released “Il Cappotto,” Alberto Lattuada’s adaptation of the Gogol short story “The Overcoat,” on DVD.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GOGOL’S short story “The Overcoat” is both compact and richly metaphorical: a humble government clerk becomes a new man when he spends his life savings on a fine coat, but is destroyed when it is stolen. It’s a perfect combination for the movies, and the tale has been filmed many times, most notably by the Soviet experimental filmmakers Grigori Kozintsev and Leonid Trauberg in 1926, and by the Italian director Alberto Lattuada in 1952. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15KEHR_SPAN/15KEHR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15KEHR_SPAN/15KEHR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15KEHR_SPAN/15KEHR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15KEHR_SPAN/15KEHR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/arts/15KEHR_SPAN/15KEHR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mantle of Dreams Yields a Nightmare', 'kicker': 'Video', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mantle of Dreams Yields a Nightmare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DVD (Digital Versatile Disc)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lattuada, Alberto', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T18:03:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'DVD', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Kehr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kehr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/335f7208-63da-572c-94bb-2fa43714f18f', 'word_count': 1001, 'uri': 'nyt://article/335f7208-63da-572c-94bb-2fa43714f18f'}, {'abstract': 'With more than 50 dispatches from around the city, readers provided a detailed supplement to the mayor’s State of the City address.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/the-state-of-the-city-in-your-words/', 'snippet': 'With more than 50 dispatches from around the city, readers provided a detailed supplement to the mayor’s State of the City address.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Crumbling curb cuts in Rego Park. Yellow rivers in the East 70s. A neighborhood-sustaining tamale vendor at a South Bronx subway stop. Seeking a more granular supplement to the mayor’s sweeping State of the City address, we asked you for the State of your Block. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The State of the City, in Your Words', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T18:04:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9afae7c5-fdff-5593-b074-ca5c04cf0eab', 'word_count': 1453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9afae7c5-fdff-5593-b074-ca5c04cf0eab'}, {'abstract': 'Guided by a Coast Guard icebreaker, a Russian tanker carrying emergency fuel to the stranded Alaska town of Nome reportedly neared the coast.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/update-russian-tanker-within-miles-of-alaska-town/', 'snippet': 'Guided by a Coast Guard icebreaker, a Russian tanker carrying emergency fuel to the stranded Alaska town of Nome reportedly neared the coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Guided by a Coast Guard icebreaker, a Russian tanker carrying emergency fuel to the stranded Alaska town of Nome neared the coast on Friday, The Alaska Dispatch reported. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russian Tanker Within Miles of Alaska Town', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Icebreakers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Coast Guard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nome (Alaska)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T18:07:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d365a38-dc28-561b-b500-148e5e6fc546', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d365a38-dc28-561b-b500-148e5e6fc546'}, {'abstract': 'Skirmishes broke out at Beijing’s flagship Apple store as large crowds gathered and the doors did not open as scheduled.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/video-of-skirmishes-at-apple-stores-in-china/', 'snippet': 'Skirmishes broke out at Beijing’s flagship Apple store as large crowds gathered and the doors did not open as scheduled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 7:00 p.m. As our colleague Sharon LaFraniere reports, crowds of would-be shoppers threw eggs and brawled in front of Apple’s flagship store in a tony neighborhood of Beijing on Friday after the store did not open as planned. The company later said in a statement that it had decided to suspend sale of its new iPhone 4S at five of its mainland stores for the safety of customers and employees. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video of Skirmishes at Apple Store in Beijing', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T18:08:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman and Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ebcaad4-b661-5d00-aa48-c77e0ac0367c', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ebcaad4-b661-5d00-aa48-c77e0ac0367c'}, {'abstract': 'In a season with just one triple-double so far, Jason Kidd’s absence from the court is conspicuous. The star guard talks about the accomplishment he has helped to define.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/jason-kidd-on-the-disappearing-triple-double/', 'snippet': 'In a season with just one triple-double so far, Jason Kidd’s absence from the court is conspicuous. The star guard talks about the accomplishment he has helped to define.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Jan. 1, Rajon Rondo of the Celtics had 18 points, 14 rebounds and 11 assists in a win over the Wizards. Of the 158 games this season, that is the only triple-double recorded so far.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jason Kidd on the Disappearing Triple-Double', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T18:09:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By BENJAMIN HOFFMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'HOFFMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5708ed22-62a2-5996-8790-28f3fc3ac654', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5708ed22-62a2-5996-8790-28f3fc3ac654'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich called on the “super PAC” supporting him to edit or take down a pseudodocumentary attacking Mitt Romney’s record at Bain Capital after fact checkers found inaccuracies.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/gingrich-asks-super-pac-to-address-errors-in-ad-against-romney/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich called on the “super PAC” supporting him to edit or take down a pseudodocumentary attacking Mitt Romney’s record at Bain Capital after fact checkers found inaccuracies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORLANDO, Fla. — Newt Gingrich called on the “super PAC” supporting him to edit or take down a 28-minute pseudodocumentary attacking Mitt Romney’s record at the investment firm Bain Capital after news media fact checkers found a number of inaccuracies. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Asks ‘Super PAC’ to Address Errors in Ad Against Romney', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T18:27:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d0b17e8-71a5-5177-a7b2-9e65e5495d91', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d0b17e8-71a5-5177-a7b2-9e65e5495d91'}, {'abstract': 'The latest volume of “The Unwritten,” a series partly inspired by the creator of Winnie the Pooh and his son, went on sale this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/graphic-books-best-sellers-and-the-return-of-the-unwritten/', 'snippet': 'The latest volume of “The Unwritten,” a series partly inspired by the creator of Winnie the Pooh and his son, went on sale this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The manga list is in flux this week, with seven newcomers. They include regulars on the list, like the latest volume of “Naruto,” about the ninja in training, which lands at No. 1. The other series involve battles (“Yu-Gi-Oh GX,” at No. 2), pirates and treasures (“One Piece,” at No. 3), werewolves and vampires (“Rosario+Vampire,” Season II, at No. 4), a demon bridge (“Black Bird,” at No. 5), romance (“Skip Beat!,” at No. 6) and mourning (“Dengeki Daisy,” at No. 10).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers and the Return of ‘The Unwritten’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ''