nd apple pie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week Martha Rose Shulman encourages home cooks to get more creative with apples, taking her recipes beyond traditional dishes like applesauce and apple pie. She also encourages home chefs to leave the skin on when possible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beyond Apple Pie', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'APPLES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T20:15:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c31e7f4b-c472-5128-89b1-10681aaa80c6', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c31e7f4b-c472-5128-89b1-10681aaa80c6'}, {'abstract': 'TPG, the private equity firm, has reached out to a number of potential partners, though it has not yet decided whether it will pursue an investment, according to a person briefed on the matter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/tpg-considers-1-billion-investment-in-olympus/', 'snippet': 'TPG, the private equity firm, has reached out to a number of potential partners, though it has not yet decided whether it will pursue an investment, according to a person briefed on the matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TPG Capital is weighing a potential investment in the Olympus Corporation of Japan, in which it would join with a strategic partner to invest as much as $1 billion, a person briefed on the matter said on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TPG Is Said to Consider $1 Billion Investment in Olympus', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TPG Capital', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T20:19:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/346592bb-8de6-580e-9759-bfe879938a28', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/346592bb-8de6-580e-9759-bfe879938a28'}, {'abstract': 'Although the class snobbery among brokerage firms is fading, people of modest means still find it hard to receive reasonably priced financial advice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/your-money/financial-advice-for-those-with-hummingbird-nest-eggs.html', 'snippet': 'Although the class snobbery among brokerage firms is fading, people of modest means still find it hard to receive reasonably priced financial advice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Merrill Lynch recently discouraged its thundering herd of brokers from taking on new clients with under $250,000 in assets available for investing, it wasn’t a big surprise.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/business/Moneyjp1/Moneyjp1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 937, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/business/Moneyjp1/Moneyjp1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/14