ead_paragraph': 'In this weekend’s Your Money column, I return to a topic that I’ve come at in various ways in recent years: The question of how the merely middle class and semi-affluent among us can get good, ethical, reasonably priced financial advice without having to watch our backs and our wallets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'LearnVest, Merrill Edge and Financial Planning for the Middle Class', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Planners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T20:43:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93c4d1ac-acdb-572d-8aaf-3a75285fde31', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93c4d1ac-acdb-572d-8aaf-3a75285fde31'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to its advantageous location in the Teton Valley, Grand Targhee ski resort in Wyoming has had 142 inches of snow since early November and is offering free skiing and snowboarding to lodge guests with a 2012 season pass to any ski resort in the United States or Canada.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/wyoming-resort-will-take-ski-passes-from-anywhere/', 'snippet': 'Thanks to its advantageous location in the Teton Valley, Grand Targhee ski resort in Wyoming has had 142 inches of snow since early November and is offering free skiing and snowboarding to lodge guests with a 2012 season pass to any ski resort in ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'While many North American ski resorts are suffering from a lack of early-season snowfall, some, like Grand Targhee in Wyoming, have enough to share.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wyoming Resort Will Take Ski Passes From Anywhere', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wyoming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T20:45:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb1a5085-da6f-5a5d-b148-627a2b5a9e61', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb1a5085-da6f-5a5d-b148-627a2b5a9e61'}, {'abstract': 'What, exactly, is it about Broncos quarterback Tim Tebow that so fascinates and provokes us? Why do some people project onto him the best of this country — and the worst?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/sports/football/fascinated-by-tim-tebow-on-more-than-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'What, exactly, is it about Broncos quarterback Tim Tebow that so fascinates and provokes us? Why do some people project onto him the best of this country — and the worst?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Saturday night in Massachusetts, a Jim Thorpe-Fabio hybrid in a New England Patriots uniform will emerge from the Foxborough shadows with all the confidence granted by good looks, athletic gifts and the home-field advantage: Tom Brady, the quarterback ideal. A three-time Super Bowl champion. Married to a world-famous model. So laserlike in his throws that he could hit the 11 bus in Boston, 30 miles away — in the numbers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/football/TEBOW/TEBOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/football/TEBOW/TEBOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/football/TEBOW/TEBOW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/football/TEBOW/TEBOW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/football/TEBOW/TEBOW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He’s a Quarterback, He’s a Winner, He’s a TV Draw, He’s a Verb', 'kicker': 'This Land', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He’s a Quarterback, He’s a Winner, He’s a TV Draw, He’s a Verb', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Broncos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebow, Tim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T20:51:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c609ae7c-4d64-590a-a7ff-8a83523e7135', 'word_count': 1532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c609ae7c-4d64-590a-a7ff-8a83523e7135'}, {'abstract': 'E.P.A. suggests revisions to New York’s planned controls on hydraulic fracturing.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/evaluating-feedback-on-fracking-rules/', 'snippet': 'E.P.A. suggests revisions to New York’s planned controls on hydraulic fracturing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I reported in Thursday’s paper, New York State environmental regulators are sorting through more than 20,000 public comments as they develop the final rules for high-volume hydraulic fracturing, the much-debated process to extract natural gas from underground shale formations. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Evaluating Feedback on Fracking Rules', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T20:51:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f7363c8-8c1e-5df1-8aaf-79e18d872853', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f7363c8-8c1e-5df1-8aaf-79e18d872853'}, {'abstract': 'Ricky Strauss, the president of Participant Media, was picked to replace M T Carney, who resigned on Monday. Ms. Carney had no film experience; Mr. Strauss, Disney stressed, has 25 years of Hollywood experience.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/walt-disney-studios-quickly-fills-chief-marketing-post/', 'snippet': 'Ricky Strauss, the president of Participant Media, was picked to replace M T Carney, who resigned on Monday. Ms. Carney had no film experience; Mr. Strauss, Disney stressed, has 25 years of Hollywood experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walt Disney Studios on Friday named a Hollywood veteran to lead its worldwide marketing and publicity efforts: Ricky Strauss, the president of Participant Media, a progressive-minded production company with credits like “The Help” and the documentary “An Inconvenient Truth.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walt Disney Studios Quickly Fills Chief Marketing Post', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, M T', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, Rich', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Participant Media LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T20:53:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bf74718-98ac-588a-a1e7-d0f968c79ec6', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bf74718-98ac-588a-a1e7-d0f968c79ec6'}, {'abstract': 'Zubin Mehta is leading his former orchestra in Bruckner’s strenuous Eighth Symphony.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/arts/music/mehta-leads-philharmonic-in-bruckner-review.html', 'snippet': 'Zubin Mehta is leading his former orchestra in Bruckner’s strenuous Eighth Symphony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If one word could summarize the performance of Bruckner’s Eighth Symphony that the conductor Zubin Mehta delivered with the New York Philharmonic at Avery Fisher Hall on Thursday evening, the likeliest would be “noble.” For nearly as long as Mr. Mehta has been in the public eye — more than 50 years now — he has shown a clear affinity for Bruckner, whose Promethean symphonies require an intensity and focus that do not come easily to every conductor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/PHIL/PHIL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/PHIL/PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/PHIL/PHIL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Return for a Noble, Promethean Climb', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Return for a Noble, Promethean Climb', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mehta, Zubin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruckner, Anton', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T20:55:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/949b1e1a-6c74-524f-bd04-5967a66089df', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/949b1e1a-6c74-524f-bd04-5967a66089df'}, {'abstract': 'The Bagger previews the Golden Globes on TimesCast and other odds and ends in awards-related news.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/previewing-the-golden-globes-and-more/', 'snippet': 'The Bagger previews the Golden Globes on TimesCast and other odds and ends in awards-related news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The workweek may be coming to a close, but with the Golden Globes on Sunday, Hollywood is clocking some overtime. Before then, we offer these awards odds and ends:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Previewing the Golden Globes and More', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FunnyOrDie.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76fa981f-4de2-55ca-ac27-0281eeea6678', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76fa981f-4de2-55ca-ac27-0281eeea6678'}, {'abstract': 'More on mixing the visceral with the rational in conveying climate science in social context.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/climate-messages-from-beyond-the-nerd-loop/', 'snippet': 'More on mixing the visceral with the rational in conveying climate science in social context.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regular readers of Dot Earth will know I’m a fan of Randy Olson, the author of “Don’t Be Such a Scientist” and maker of offbeat, provocative films, including “Sizzle.” After my post the other day looking at a Norwegian effort to use a man walking a leashed dog to illustrate the difference between trend and variation, I got in touch with Olson afresh, both to get his reaction to that animation and talk more generally about ways to get beyond what he calls “the nerd loop” in climate communication. Here’s the resulting Q&A: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Climate Messages from Beyond the ‘Nerd Loop’', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Speaking', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gore, Al', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olson, Randy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Wildlife Fund', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74b5e1ff-c72d-53cb-b8e3-7e748c189211', 'word_count': 1037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74b5e1ff-c72d-53cb-b8e3-7e748c189211'}, {'abstract': 'Plenty of players remain unsigned, but the most prominent of all, by far, is Prince Fielder.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/prince-fielder-leads-the-unsigned-all-stars/', 'snippet': 'Plenty of players remain unsigned, but the most prominent of all, by far, is Prince Fielder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scott Boras does not get everything he seeks in every negotiation. But it is wise not to doubt him. This is the agent who persuaded teams to give seven-year, $126 million contracts to Barry Zito and Jayson Werth, and persuaded another to hand not one, but two player options to Rafael Soriano.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prince Fielder Leads the Unsigned All-Stars', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boras, Scott', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fielder, Prince', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matsui, Hideki', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, Cody', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:02:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a526b162-54d2-53e6-9480-562be5d303da', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a526b162-54d2-53e6-9480-562be5d303da'}, {'abstract': 'A new batch of food links for the new year.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/links-for-the-new-year/', 'snippet': 'A new batch of food links for the new year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s something so inoffensive and old-fashioned about saying “happy new year” that makes it incredibly pleasurable. You can say it with warmth, genuine-ness, sincerity and with a profound lack of irony. I love it. So let me be the last to say “happy new year” everyone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Links for the New Year', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyer, Danny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Hardee's Food Systems Inc", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Humane Society of the United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MARKS & SPENCER PLC', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McDonald's Corporation", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monsanto Company', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:04:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f7e2fcc-269b-5aab-83fc-42be59627fac', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f7e2fcc-269b-5aab-83fc-42be59627fac'}, {'abstract': 'I clicked “Add Friend.” He accepted within minutes. Stunned, I wondered if he had forgotten raping me.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/defriending-my-rapist/', 'snippet': 'I clicked “Add Friend.” He accepted within minutes. Stunned, I wondered if he had forgotten raping me.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook suggested I friend him. I guess our social networks overlapped. I guided the mouse toward his photo, and the little pointed hand hovered over his face. Fear and anger swelled up but curiosity won out and I clicked “Add Friend.” He accepted within minutes. Stunned, I wondered if he had forgotten raping me, or if he thought I had. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Defriending My Rapist', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:05:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorri Olds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11221738-6628-510e-b32c-70929b09a33d', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11221738-6628-510e-b32c-70929b09a33d'}, {'abstract': 'Many American-branded cars at the Detroit auto show reflected global design influences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/15/automobiles/autoshow/15design-slideshow.html', 'snippet': 'Many American-branded cars at the Detroit auto show reflected global design influences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many American-branded cars at the Detroit auto show reflected global design influences.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/automobiles/autoshow/15design-slideshow-slide-PWCL/15design-slideshow-slide-PWCL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 