an apparently bottomless American hunger for dark and sexy science fiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the frenzy for “Downton Abbey” runs its course, two new series remind us that not all television imports from Britain and its former dominions are so genteel.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/FADES/FADES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/FADES/FADES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/FADES/FADES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/FADES/FADES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/FADES/FADES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It Can Be So Hard to Save the World When Those Hormones Kick In', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It Can Be So Hard to Save the World When Those Hormones Kick In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:07:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/90821312-7072-58f2-9e5a-00d41b437de8', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90821312-7072-58f2-9e5a-00d41b437de8'}, {'abstract': 'Issue Project Room officially moves into its new home, in a McKim, Mead & White building in downtown Brooklyn, with a Dutch music festival later this month.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/avant-garde-arts-space-inaugurates-new-home-finally/', 'snippet': 'Issue Project Room officially moves into its new home, in a McKim, Mead & White building in downtown Brooklyn, with a Dutch music festival later this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four years ago Issue Project Room, an avant-garde arts space that has had several homes in Manhattan and Brooklyn, hit a kind of real estate jackpot: a 20-year, rent-free lease on 5,000 square feet in a McKim, Mead & White building in downtown Brooklyn. The catch: the tiny group would be responsible for $3.6 million in renovations and improvements.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Avant-Garde Arts Space Inaugurates New Home, Finally', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:10:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aae81b20-5787-52e8-a396-15a55a4d21f0', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aae81b20-5787-52e8-a396-15a55a4d21f0'}, {'abstract': 'A viral video released this week in Russia tries to discredit Prime Minister Vladimir Putin’s chief antagonist, the charismatic blogger Aleksei Navalny, by comparing him to Hitler.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/russian-ad-compares-putin-foe-with-hitler/', 'snippet': 'A viral video released this week in Russia tries to discredit Prime Minister Vladimir Putin’s chief antagonist, the charismatic blogger Aleksei Navalny, by comparing him to Hitler.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While Republican voters in South Carolina are being warned in a new ad not to trust Mitt Romney because, “like John Kerry, he speaks French,” politicking in Russia, where a new president will be elected in March, is a good deal less subtle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russian Ad Compares Putin Foe to Hitler', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Neo Nazi Groups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navalny, Aleksei N', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:10:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey and Glenn Kates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa8e0f43-d37e-52ce-89aa-9b1eda5362d1', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa8e0f43-d37e-52ce-89aa-9b1eda5362d1'}, {'abstract': 'It’s certainly a part of everyone’s vocabulary, but for me it’s a word that especially permeates sports culture in regard to team logos and uniforms. It often means one thing: Quality.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/making-that-old-school-sports-logo-new/', 'snippet': 'It’s certainly a part of everyone’s vocabulary, but for me it’s a word that especially permeates sports culture in regard to team logos and uniforms. It often means one thing: Quality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to this definition of the term “old school,” I was a child when anything I could technically consider “old school” came into existence. It’s certainly a part of everyone’s vocabulary, but for me it’s a word that especially permeates sports culture in regard to team logos and uniforms. It often means one thing: quality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Old School’ Logos', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trademarks and Trade Names', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilkins, Dominique', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Atlanta Hawks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Pistons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Antonio Spurs', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Texas Tech University', 'rank': 1