 night.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/canadiens-make-a-dramatic-trade-of-cammalleri/', 'snippet': 'The Canadiens made another move in their chaotic season by trading forward Mike Cammalleri to Calgary in the middle of a game in Boston Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are some strange things, and a lot of losing, going down in Montreal, and Canadiens fans are in an uproar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canadiens Trade Cammalleri in a Flash', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cammalleri, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calgary Flames', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Montreal Canadiens', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:17:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/509c364e-09e1-57ae-a809-18a210f0991f', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/509c364e-09e1-57ae-a809-18a210f0991f'}, {'abstract': 'Ads started running in The Casper Star-Tribune asking for photographs and video of the former Vice President Dick Cheney last month; Showtime announced the project on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/showtime-plans-cheney-documentary-as-producers-reach-out-to-wyoming/', 'snippet': 'Ads started running in The Casper Star-Tribune asking for photographs and video of the former Vice President Dick Cheney last month; Showtime announced the project on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, ads started running in The Casper Star-Tribune in Wyoming asking for photographs and video of the former Vice President Dick Cheney, who represented the state in Congress and still maintains a home there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Showtime Plans Cheney Documentary, as Producers Reach Out to Wyoming', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheney, Dick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knight, Suge', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pryor, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Death Row Records', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Showtime', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wyoming', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:24:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e534a75-4ad5-5180-98e6-9e6a5aed38a2', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e534a75-4ad5-5180-98e6-9e6a5aed38a2'}, {'abstract': 'The Canadian National Railway said the hedge fund manager William A. Ackman’s plan to put E. Hunter Harrison in charge of the Canadian Pacific Railway would violate Mr. Harrison’s retirement contract.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/canadian-pacific-rival-tells-ex-chief-to-stay-away-from-ackman/', 'snippet': 'The Canadian National Railway said the hedge fund manager William A. Ackman’s plan to put E. Hunter Harrison in charge of the Canadian Pacific Railway would violate Mr. Harrison’s retirement contract.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:15 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canadian Pacific Rival Warns Ex-Chief to Stay Away From Ackman', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ackman, William A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Canadian National Railway Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Canadian Pacific Railway Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pershing Square Capital Management', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:27:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1ff3bbe-8f5a-5155-8f39-f8fc66964b40', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1ff3bbe-8f5a-5155-8f39-f8fc66964b40'}, {'abstract': 'New research that shows a stronger link between S.S.R.I. use in mothers and pulmonary hypertension in infants can only make an already difficult choice harder.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/antidepressant-use-linked-to-increased-pulmonary-hypertension-risk-in-infants/', 'snippet': 'New research that shows a stronger link between S.S.R.I. use in mothers and pulmonary hypertension in infants can only make an already difficult choice harder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A study published in the British Medical Journal this week provides stronger evidence that taking some antidepressants during pregnancy doubles the risk of a baby developing pulmonary hypertension. Researchers have long suspected a link between the use of selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors, or S.S.R.I.’s, and the condition, but previous studies have been small and inconclusive (with results ranging from there being no link to a six times greater risk). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Antidepressant Use Linked to Increased Pulmonary Hypertension Risk in Infants', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BIRTHS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pulmonary Hypertension', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:27:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d775e1e6-06b7-545e-8fca-0e23eb51f583', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d775e1e6-06b7-545e-8fca-0e23eb51f583'}, {'abstract': 'The city is becoming a hub of vintage-motorcycle sales activity, with three prominent auction houses conducting events there this week.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/motorcycle-auction-tripleheader-comes-to-las-vegas/', 'snippet': 'The city is becoming a hub of vintage-motorcycle sales activity, with three prominent auction houses conducting events there this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — A restored, fully operational 1920 Henderson Four Model K was the top sale Thursday at the Auctions America by RM event at the Rio Las Vegas Hotel and Casino, as a three-day, three-auction marathon kicked off at three locations here. Including a 12 percent sales commission, the Henderson changed hands for $50,960, slightly below its preauction estimate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Motorcycle-Auction Tripleheader Comes to Las Vegas', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bonhams', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harley-Davidson Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:29:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c5da514-bb82-5595-8da0-3150262b7430', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c5da514-bb82-5595-8da0-3150262b7430'}, {'abstract': 'The big numbers for “Big Bang Theory” also give “Rob” a boost on CBS.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/cbs-tramples-the-competition/', 'snippet': 'The big numbers for “Big Bang Theory” also give “Rob” a boost on CBS.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CBS once again managed to dominate prime time among the broadcast networks on Thursday night, easily taking first place in all ratings categories. According to Nielsen, a very large percentage of the 15.9 million people who watched “Big Bang Theory” stayed put and sampled the series premiere of “Rob.” Although that comedy has been poorly received critically, it drew 13.5 million viewers. The new drama “Person of Interest” also did well as it posted its best numbers ever and reached 14.7 million people. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'CBS Tramples the Competition', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nielsen Media Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:31:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/461b243b-d712-5318-9393-172a70b551a1', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/461b243b-d712-5318-9393-172a70b551a1'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said in an interview published on Saturday that new economic sanctions against Iran could succeed if combined with a threat of military action.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/world/middleeast/israeli-leader-benjamin-netanyahu-says-sanctions-on-iran-could-succeed-if-paired-with-military-threat.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said in an interview published on Saturday that new economic sanctions against Iran could succeed if combined with a threat of military action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel said in an interview published Saturday that new economic sanctions aimed at stopping Iran’s contentious nuclear program appeared to be having an effect and, if combined with a threat of military action led by the United States, could succeed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Says Sanctions Hurt Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel Says Sanctions Hurt Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:35:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92b800b9-903c-5145-af50-63d068a696d8', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92b800b9-903c-5145-af50-63d068a696d8'}, {'abstract': 'With its whimsical details, the Louis Vuitton prefall collection is an absolute delight.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/just-one-look-louis-vuitton/', 'snippet': 'With its whimsical details, the Louis Vuitton prefall collection is an absolute delight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Louis Vuitton prefall collection is an absolute delight. Rounded silhouettes on coats, cap-sleeved baby-doll dresses in peach and yellow and a return of the beloved Stephen Sprouse leopard in blue/navy on a smart suit, all possess the same whimsy we saw at Marc Jacobs’s most recent spring collection. Star accessories include grommeted berets and sharp heels — kitten-height and higher — with shiny steel-toe tips. Fur is sprinkled liberally throughout, on coat pockets, collars and shoes (making feet look like puppy paws; it’s quite fun). Here, a dress with the collection’s signature Sgt. Pepper’s trompe l’oeil gets a pop of pretty pink.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Louis Vuitton', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vuitton, Louis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:35:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9350a8f-e08f-5209-8717-19f89f88cc8c', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9350a8f-e08f-5209-8717-19f89f88cc8c'}, {'abstract': 'Photo: a lovely day to go to the beach, no matter what the costume.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/coney-island-jan-3-1915/', 'snippet': 'Photo: a lovely day to go to the beach, no matter what the costume.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Library of Congress has been gradually posting to Flickr its trove of more than 40,000 photos from the Bain Collection, comprising the surviving photos of the Bain News Service, a photo agency founded by George Grantham Bain that flourished in the early 20th century.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coney Island, Jan. 3, 1915', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Library of Congress', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CONEY ISLAND (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:37:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06321d6e-19ff-559a-86d4-1dbc5219a579', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06321d6e-19ff-559a-86d4-1dbc5219a579'}, {'abstract': 'Our Wisconsin buds are loyal Packers fans who made their own trek to New Jersey early in December. We had friendly, competitive exchanges down to the wire.  I would expect the banter and wagering to escalate as we approach the game on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/eight-men-in-wearing-giants-blue-ready-for-green-bay/', 'snippet': 'Our Wisconsin buds are loyal Packers fans who made their own trek to New Jersey early in December. We had friendly, competitive exchanges down to the wire.  I would expect the banter and wagering to escalate as we approach the game on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifty years ago, if the Giants were headed to Green Bay to play the Packers in the postseason, fans in New York might have considered themselves lucky to catch the game on television. Today, with tickets available online and frequent-flier miles accruing with every credit-card purchase, fans can dare to dream a little more boldly. Six members of a Chatham, N.J., softball team — a mix of lawyers, Wall Streeters and computer software salesmen — traveled to Lambeau Field for Sunday’s showdown between the Giants and the Packers. It was a trip of cheap hotel rooms and high hopes, cramped rental cars and unexpectedly good seats at the game. The men — they were joined by two pals in Milwaukee — agreed to create a Titletown travelogue. Their hopes were to stay friends, keep their jobs and, well, see the Giants win.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eight Men In: Wearing Giants Blue, Ready for Green Bay', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Road Trips', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schroeder, Andrew', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lambeau Field', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MetLife Stadium (NJ)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yankee Stadium (NYC)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:45:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By STEPHEN COSTELLO and ANDREW SCHROEDER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'COSTELLO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SCHROEDER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None,