ngrich-perry-and-huntsman-lose-virginia-ballot-fight/', 'snippet': 'Only Mitt Romney and Ron Paul will be on the ballot for Virginia’s Republican primary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge in Virginia on Friday denied Rick Perry, Newt Gingrich, Rick Santorum and Jon M. Huntsman Jr. spots on the state’s presidential primary ballot.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich, Perry, Santorum and Huntsman Lose Virginia Ballot Fight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:50:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35d52302-b1de-54c8-8491-0dfc22b68a6d', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35d52302-b1de-54c8-8491-0dfc22b68a6d'}, {'abstract': 'The Argentine director Mariano Pensotti talks about his piece “El Pasado Es un Animal Grotesco” (“The Past Is a Grotesque Animal”).', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/under-the-radar-festival-5-questions-about-the-past-is-a-grotesque-animal/', 'snippet': 'The Argentine director Mariano Pensotti talks about his piece “El Pasado Es un Animal Grotesco” (“The Past Is a Grotesque Animal”).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years in the lives of three couples in Argentina spin, quite slowly, in “El Pasado Es un Animal Grotesco” (“The Past Is a Grotesque Animal”), from the Argentine writer and director Mariano Pensotti. The piece, making its U.S. premiere in a co-production of the Coil and Under the Radar festivals, features actors performing on a slowly rotating set to a soundtrack that includes music from the band Of Montreal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Under the Radar Festival: 5 Questions About ‘The Past Is a Grotesque Animal’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Under the Radar Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pensotti, Mariano', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Of Montreal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:51:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7656430f-530f-5980-8c9f-20e81b499e4b', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7656430f-530f-5980-8c9f-20e81b499e4b'}, {'abstract': 'This weekend, Nike and Reebok are beginning big marketing campaigns. Reebok’s is the broader of the two, with a $50 million budget; Nike’s is for a new Kobe Bryant shoe.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/its-winter-so-here-come-the-sneaker-ads/', 'snippet': 'This weekend, Nike and Reebok are beginning big marketing campaigns. Reebok’s is the broader of the two, with a $50 million budget; Nike’s is for a new Kobe Bryant shoe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The early days of winter may seem an odd time to bring out new athletic footwear, but there are some good reasons: for one, millions of consumers have vowed to exercise more in the new year; for another, there are lots of sports events on TV that draw big audiences filled with shoe buyers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Winter, So Here Come the Sneaker Ads', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sneakers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bryant, Kobe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NIKE Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reebok International Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T21:52:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/379a6aac-5635-55ce-b72e-99b7d9f23bf0', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/379a6aac-5635-55ce-b72e-99b7d9f23bf0'}, {'abstract': 'The government’s controlling stake in General Motors proves that ownership and regulation are inherently incompatible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/business/government-ownership-and-gm-regulation-dont-mix.html', 'snippet': 'The government’s controlling stake in General Motors proves that ownership and regulation are inherently incompatible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s say you’re the biggest owner of a global auto company. You take the company’s flagship new vehicle, twist it, crash it, poke it and leave it outside in the elements for weeks until its battery catches fire. Then you generate a storm of publicity and watch the share price and the value of your ownership stake decline.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/