port.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This video provides a calming capstone to a frenetic week. It is evidently a hooded crow*, apparently in Russia (post if you know for sure), and almost assuredly shows a bird at play (note the multiple tracks in the rooftop snow from earlier “snowboarding” trips):', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Crow Appears to Find a Source of Winter Sport', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T22:11:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d746327-76e6-541a-956a-9994af939372', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d746327-76e6-541a-956a-9994af939372'}, {'abstract': 'Part of the success of Kirk and Nate Mueller, identical twins who design iPad apps and Web sites, lies in how meticulously they’ve shaped their image.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/fashion/kirk-and-nate-mueller-capitalize-on-being-twins.html', 'snippet': 'Part of the success of Kirk and Nate Mueller, identical twins who design iPad apps and Web sites, lies in how meticulously they’ve shaped their image.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN person, the identical twins Kirk and Nate Mueller are an uncanny sight. The neatly coiffed hair, the ASOS leather boots, the red lapel flowers from Hook & Albert, the brown wool Topman suits — everything about them is almost exactly the same. Even their jobs: designing sleek iPad apps and Web sites, which has made them overnight design celebrities.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/fashion/15NOTICED/15NOTICED-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 679, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/fashion/15NOTICED/15NOTICED-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/fashion/15NOTICED/15NOTICED-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two People, One Identity', 'kicker': 'Noticed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two People, One Identity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Multiple Births', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Twins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T22:15:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Considine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Considine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e3b7954-4bab-5644-a3ee-52b4e75111bf', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e3b7954-4bab-5644-a3ee-52b4e75111bf'}, {'abstract': 'A new Gallup poll finds a correlation between household income and concern over the deficit.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/class-warfare/', 'snippet': 'A new Gallup poll finds a correlation between household income and concern over the deficit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Mitt Romney had his way, we’d only talk about income inequality in “quiet rooms”—I’m picturing wood-paneling and cigar smoke. If Rick Santorum had his way, we wouldn’t even use the term “middle class” since, apparently, “there are no classes in America.” Middle-income people, maybe, he says, but no middle-class people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Class Warfare', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T22:15:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4b295aa-3b99-526b-a8b5-1e827489607e', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4b295aa-3b99-526b-a8b5-1e827489607e'}, {'abstract': 'What we expect from life’s events can determine how we react to them — and those expectations can be managed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/your-money/the-importance-of-setting-expectations-whether-high-or-low.html', 'snippet': 'What we expect from life’s events can determine how we react to them — and those expectations can be managed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY father recently had his second knee operation in a year. The first time, things went poorly. His rehabilitation was difficult and months later, he still could not walk well or, even more important to him, play tennis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Did You Expect? It Makes a Difference', 'kicker': 'Shortcuts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Did You Expect? It Makes a Difference', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Susan Keane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T22:18:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alina Tugend', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tugend', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7dac0a5a-b446-5dca-9336-0a86d2b13bd2', 'word_count': 1318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dac0a5a-b446-5dca-9336-0a86d2b13bd2'}, {'abstract': 'A new beer shop on the Lower East Side will feature a bar where customers can order food.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/tops-hops-to-open-with-700-beers/', 'snippet': 'A new beer shop on the Lower East Side will feature a bar where customers can order food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An arms race seems to have sprung up among the new breed of beer stores that specialize in imports and craft labels. If one offers 250 different brews, the next stockpiles 400. Now, Ted Kenny, a former beer salesman, is raising the ante with at least 700, including 20 on tap, at Top Hops Beer Shop, the new store he plans to open Saturday on the Lower East Side.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top Hops to Open, With 700 Beers', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glover, Russell', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-13T22:31:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea2f00e3-d2a5-5258-9f2e-19e3017fe7e7', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea2f00e3-d2a5-5258-9f2e-19e3017fe7e7'}, {'abstract': 'Teachers call in to WNYC\'s Brian Lehrer Show in response to the mayor\'s State of the City address.  Many of them, says the host, told WNYC that the idea of merit pay was "good in theory, wouldn\'t work in practice.\'\'', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/13/some-teachers-skeptical-of-merit-pay/', 'snippet': 'Teachers call in to WNYC\'s Brian Lehrer Show in response to the mayor\'s State of the City address.  Many of them, says the host, told WNYC that the idea of merit pay was "good in theory, wouldn\'t work in practice.\'\'', 'lead_paragraph': '', 