e would sit back comfortably and just, ahhhhhhh, soak in the big gems from the Gershwin score.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/BESS-JP/BESS-JP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/BESS-JP/BESS-JP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/BESS-JP/BESS-JP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shorter, Modern and Less Than Opera', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shorter, Modern And Less Than Opera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Diedre L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulus, Diane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonald, Audra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parks, Suzan-Lori', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gershwin, George', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T00:27:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46047ade-63d6-53e4-8639-18f60ed23ba0', 'word_count': 1367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46047ade-63d6-53e4-8639-18f60ed23ba0'}, {'abstract': 'Meg Stuart’s “Blessed,” with Francisco Camacho, is having its North American premiere at New York Live Arts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/arts/dance/meg-stuarts-blessed-at-new-york-live-arts-review.html', 'snippet': 'Meg Stuart’s “Blessed,” with Francisco Camacho, is having its North American premiere at New York Live Arts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The man sits inside the dubious shelter of his little cardboard shack, staring out at strangers. The strangers stare back. His body makes little twitches. The palm tree and giant swan, also cardboard, are slowly wilting, as is his roof. It has been raining, and hard, for a long time now. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/BLESSED/BLESSED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/BLESSED/BLESSED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/BLESSED/BLESSED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/BLESSED/BLESSED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/BLESSED/BLESSED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Forget About a Paper Moon: This Swan’s Cardboard', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Forget About a Paper Moon: This Swan’s Cardboard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stuart, Meg', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Live Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T00:28:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f798a23-3921-56fd-9fb6-a8204a18a7d4', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f798a23-3921-56fd-9fb6-a8204a18a7d4'}, {'abstract': '“Napoleon Dynamite” makes its way to the small screen — with the same creators, cast and story — as an animated series on Fox.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/arts/television/napoleon-dynamite-animated-series-on-fox-review.html', 'snippet': '“Napoleon Dynamite” makes its way to the small screen — with the same creators, cast and story — as an animated series on Fox.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Has it really been only seven and a half years since “Napoleon Dynamite” was in theaters? It seems longer, perhaps because so many geeky antiheroes have followed Napoleon onto our screens, or perhaps because the film’s deadpan humor was so vaporous that it seemed to vanish as you watched.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/14NAPOLEON/14NAPOLEON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 364, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/14NAPOLEON/14NAPOLEON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 364}},