d the region. Subjects include the expansion of Terminal 4 at Kennedy Airport, an overturned houseboat in the Bronx, and the mayor’s State of the City address.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is a slide show of photographs from the past week in New York City and the region. Subjects include the expansion of Terminal 4 at Kennedy International Airport, an overturned houseboat in the Bronx and the mayor’s State of the City address.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Week in Pictures for Jan. 13', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T00:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64accfd0-da24-5ba5-bf96-9702279e2b1c', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64accfd0-da24-5ba5-bf96-9702279e2b1c'}, {'abstract': 'At Café Carlyle, Paulo Szot mixed his formal operatic voice and pop naturalness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/arts/music/an-evening-with-paulo-szot-at-cafe-carlyle-review.html', 'snippet': 'At Café Carlyle, Paulo Szot mixed his formal operatic voice and pop naturalness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To hear Paulo Szot apply his heroic baritone to “If Ever I Would Leave You,” Sir Lancelot’s oratorical love song from “Camelot,” is to hear a flowery list of sweet nothings transformed into sweet somethings by the sheer force of delivery. Its blandishments include a description of “lips red as flame” and a “face with a luster that puts gold to shame.” There was a time when such flattery might get a dedicated suitor well beyond first base. Nowadays, Alan Jay Lerner’s rhetoric sounds so artificial that a strikeout seems more likely. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaching the Border Between Pop and Opera', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Breaching the Border Between Pop and Opera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cafe Carlyle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Szot, Paulo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T00:31:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/63ab6743-9faa-5b26-855d-61be89b30727', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63ab6743-9faa-5b26-855d-61be89b30727'}, {'abstract': 'El-Sayyid A. Nosair had been found guilty in 1995 of conspiring to blow up New York landmarks and of the murder of Rabbi Meir Kahane.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/nyregion/el-sayyid-a-nosair-killer-of-rabbi-kahane-is-denied-new-trial.html', 'snippet': 'El-Sayyid A. Nosair had been found guilty in 1995 of conspiring to blow up New York landmarks and of the murder of Rabbi Meir Kahane.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge in Manhattan has refused to grant a new trial to a man convicted in 1995 of conspiring to blow up New York landmarks and of the murder of Rabbi Meir Kahane.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Convicted in Terrorism Conspiracy Is Denied New Trial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Convicted in Terrorism Conspiracy Is Denied New Trial', 'name': None, 'seo':