s a Good Beat, and a Star’s Endorsement', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Headphones and Headsets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': '50 CENT', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iovine, Jimmy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Polizzi, Nicole', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beats Electronics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T00:42:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/901eb64c-45cc-5484-b065-5b2d1bfff939', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/901eb64c-45cc-5484-b065-5b2d1bfff939'}, {'abstract': 'Theodore Roosevelt, when he was police commissioner, tried to crack down on New Yorkers’ alcohol consumption. It didn’t go well.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/opinion/a-new-anti-alcohol-campaign-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Theodore Roosevelt, when he was police commissioner, tried to crack down on New Yorkers’ alcohol consumption. It didn’t go well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MAYOR Michael R. Bloomberg has made it clear that he wants New Yorkers to smoke less, eat healthier food, and now, according to The New York Post, also cut back on excessive drinking. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/opinion/0114OPEDcontino/0114OPEDcontino-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/14/opinion/0114OPEDcontino/0114OPEDcontino-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/opinion/0114OPEDcontino/0114OPEDcontino-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/opinion/0114OPEDcontino/0114OPEDcontino-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/14/opinion/0114OPEDcontino/0114OPEDcontino-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Dry We Aren’t', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Dry We Aren&#8217;t', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Theodore', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T00:46:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Zacks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zacks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a786841a-c8a3-5117-ba82-76a40b4ceafa', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a786841a-c8a3-5117-ba82-76a40b4ceafa'}, {'abstract': 'As the uproar over his last-minute grants of clemency continued, former Gov. Haley Barbour showed no sign of backing down on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/us/mississippi-barbour-defends-pardons.html', 'snippet': 'As the uproar over his last-minute grants of clemency continued, former Gov. Haley Barbour showed no sign of backing down on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the uproar over his last-minute grants of clemency continued, former Gov. Haley Barbour showed no sign of backing down on Friday, giving a news conference and appearing on Fox News. Mr. Barbour, a Republican whose second term ended this week, described himself as “very comfortable” with the decision to grant clemency, and mostly full pardons, to 215 convicts in his last days in office. He emphasized that 189 of the convicts were not in prison, and that half of the others were given suspended sentences for medical reasons. He said the tradition of granting clemency was “rooted in the Christian idea of giving second chances.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mississippi: Barbour Defends Pardons ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mississippi: Barbour Defends Pardons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barbour, Haley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T00:59:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c048575-df63-55fe-8e94-89d53e2252c8', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c048575-df63-55fe-8e94-89d53e2252c8'}, {'abstract': 'In his bid to join the Republican presidential contest, Stephen Colbert is a serious performer playing a silly character, while the media and political world are deeply silly but pretending to be serious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/arts/stephen-colbert-stirs-up-political-campaign-and-media.html', 'snippet': 'In his bid to join the Republican presidential contest, Stephen Colbert is a serious performer playing a silly character, while the media and political world are deeply silly but pretending to be serious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stephen Colbert teasing South Carolina about a run for the presidency is becoming one of America’s great political traditions, right up there with awkward photographs of candidates eating corn dogs at the Iowa State Fair. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/COMEDY-JP/COMEDY-JP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 685, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/COMEDY-JP/COMEDY-JP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/14/arts/COMEDY-JP/COMEDY-JP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Beneath a Deeply Silly Campaign, a Deeply Serious Performer', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beneath a Deeply Silly Campaign, a Deeply Serious Performer',