 visited (a Saturday in December) combined fat chunks of succulent lobster meat with a delicate mix of truffle oil, parsley and parsley oil. The lobster was stuffed into a house-made potato roll spread with apple butter and topped with crisp-fried shallots; accompanying it were thick-cut fries sprinkled with a flavorsome mix of celery salt, paprika, homemade garlic powder and cayenne that made it easy to forgive the less-than-crisp fries.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15SUBDINECT2_SPAN/15SUBDINECT2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15SUBDINECT2_SPAN/15SUBDINECT2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15SUBDINECT2_SPAN/15SUBDINECT2_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eclecticism by the Sea', 'kicker': 'Connecticut Dining | Mystic', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eclecticism By the Sea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mystic (Conn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T02:11:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Lyness', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyness', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cbf77a5-0296-5c1b-b30d-e35b4243c9c0', 'word_count': 1020, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cbf77a5-0296-5c1b-b30d-e35b4243c9c0'}, {'abstract': 'Organizers of the parade in New Jersey called it off because the mayor pushed to have it held on a weekday after the event last year ended with violence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/nyregion/st-patricks-day-parade-in-hoboken-is-canceled.html', 'snippet': 'Organizers of the parade in New Jersey called it off because the mayor pushed to have it held on a weekday after the event last year ended with violence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There will not be a St. Patrick’s Day parade in Hoboken, N.J., this year, but organizers say they may go elsewhere to march.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Parade in Hoboken to Celebrate St. Patrick’s', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Parade In Hoboken To Celebrate St. Patrick’s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hoboken (NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "St Patrick's Day", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmer, Dawn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T02:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4b3837f-958b-5a88-b690-6bec1b7c8f27', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4b3837f-958b-5a88-b690-6bec1b7c8f27'}, {'abstract': 'After a few weeks of calm, austerity measures freeze the weakened European economies. It is time to shift course.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/opinion/a-long-bleak-winter.html', 'snippet': 'After a few weeks of calm, austerity measures freeze the weakened European economies. It is time to shift course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The European Central Bank’s cheap lending to euro-area banks may have briefly stabilized the financial markets. But the respite won’t last. The decision by Standard & Poor’s on Friday to downgrade the credit ratings of nine euro-zone countries, including France, Italy and Spain, should remind European leaders that their economic strategy based on austerity for all is just not working. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Long Bleak Winter', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Long Bleak Winter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monti, Mario', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Standard & Poor's Corp", 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T02:14:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2095cb57-c160-5f2a-977f-92d8c250c17c', 'word_count': 547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2095cb57-c160-5f2a-977f-92d8c250c17c'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Marine Corps identified the four Marines shown in a video urinating on what appear to be dead Taliban fighters, and has named a lead investigating officer to decide whether they should be charged, Marine officials said. Also, an in-depth look at conduct on the battlefield, a place where reprehensible behavior is an ever-present risk in young soldiers thrown into battle, according to combat veterans and military experts.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/13/the-urination-video-and-pressures-of-battle/', 'snippet': 'The United States Marine Corps identified the four Marines shown in a video urinating on what appear to be dead Taliban fighters, and has named a lead investigating officer to decide whether they should be charged, Marine officials said. Also, an ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States Marine Corps has identified the four Marines shown in a video urinating on what appear to be dead Taliban fighters, and has named a lead investigating officer to decide whether they should be charged, Marine officials said. In an article in Saturday’s issue of The Times, Elisabeth Bumiller and Matthew Rosenberg report that Marine officials were also attempting to identify the person who shot the controversial video.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Urination Video and Pressures of Battle', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T02:17:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46152b53-7dc9-5477-81dc-49b8d0147187', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46152b53-7dc9-5477-81dc-49b8d0147187'}, {'abstract': 'A video of Marines urinating on Taliban corpses that has gone viral on the Internet harms American interests in Afghanistan and couldn’t have come at a worse time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/opinion/self-inflicted-wound.html', 'snippet': 'A video of Marines urinating on Taliban corpses that has gone viral on the Internet harms American interests in Afghanistan and couldn’t have come at a worse time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even after seven years, the photos of Army soldiers abusing detainees at the Abu Ghraib prison are an ugly black mark on the American presence in Iraq. Now there is a new scar on the country’s reputation. Four Marines were filmed urinating on what appear to be the corpses of three dead Taliban fighters in Afghanistan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Self-Inflicted Wound', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Self-Inflicted Wound', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T02:18:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e905b123-489d-59b0-a967-fda748640619', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e905b123-489d-59b0-a967-fda748640619'}, {'abstract': 'From a physiological standpoint, experts said, playing football in extreme cold generally affects a player’s ability to feel and his ability to breathe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/sports/football/in-bitter-cold-sharp-passes-are-least-of-bodys-worries.html', 'snippet': 'From a physiological standpoint, experts said, playing football in extreme cold generally affects a player’s ability to feel and his ability to breathe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — In addition to facing Aaron Rodgers, Greg Jennings and the rest of the Green Bay Packers on Sunday, the Giants will also be forced to battle paresthesia, bronchoconstriction and a persistent though not necessarily overwhelming sensation that they have to urinate.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/cold/cold-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/cold/c