on Friday, ending a nearly two-week waiting game for both teams. The Rams and Fisher were negotiating a contract on Friday afternoon.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fisher Picks Rams Over the Dolphins', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fisher Picks St. Louis Over Miami', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Rams', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradford, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Jeff', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Dolphins', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T02:28:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d4927fd-5fc8-5eba-b265-4d15602b6b9c', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d4927fd-5fc8-5eba-b265-4d15602b6b9c'}, {'abstract': 'Savory Thai Cooking in Flemington is easy to miss, but once inside you will find solid fare and a menu of mostly classics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/nyregion/at-savory-thai-cooking-a-tightly-edited-menu-review.html', 'snippet': 'Savory Thai Cooking in Flemington is easy to miss, but once inside you will find solid fare and a menu of mostly classics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF you had never been to Savory Thai Cooking before, it would be easy to drive past it. It is set perpendicular to the road; on my two visits, its storefront looked dark except for the restaurant’s name and a small lighted “Open” sign; there were very few cars in the parking lot. Inside, though, is a kitchen turning out solid Thai fare.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15DINENJ1/15DINENJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15DINENJ1/15DINENJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15DINENJ1/15DINENJ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Piece of Thailand in an Inconspicuous Spot', 'kicker': 'New Jersey Dining | Flemington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Piece of Thailand In an Inconspicuous Spot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T02:29:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karla Cook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cook', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2370428e-7370-5984-94fb-e587289c77db', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2370428e-7370-5984-94fb-e587289c77db'}, {'abstract': 'Jack Mannino, who spent time in prison thinking about his life in Georgia, is accused of robbing a Brooklyn bank two weeks ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/nyregion/jack-mannino-the-seven-second-bandit-is-accused-in-brooklyn-robbery.html', 'snippet': 'Jack Mannino, who spent time in prison thinking about his life in Georgia, is accused of robbing a Brooklyn bank two weeks ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the Federal Bureau of Investigation and some medical records are correct, a tough-looking mob associate named Jack Mannino robbed a Brooklyn bank two weeks ago while wearing an adult diaper. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 877, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/14/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wanted by the F.B.I., but Still Popular With the Ex-Mother-in-Law', 'kicker': 'Crime Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wanted by the F.B.I., but Still Popular With the Ex-Mother-in-Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bensonhurst (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gambino Crime Family', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T02:29:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifi