the deaths of the following Americans this week: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T02:42:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/626393d8-6482-5c1a-a94e-8d4d11d9c139', 'word_count': 64, 'uri': 'nyt://article/626393d8-6482-5c1a-a94e-8d4d11d9c139'}, {'abstract': 'A young woman who learned as a child that she had multiple sclerosis is now headed to college, after receiving help from the Neediest Cases Fund.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/opinion/working-twice-as-hard.html', 'snippet': 'A young woman who learned as a child that she had multiple sclerosis is now headed to college, after receiving help from the Neediest Cases Fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2000, just two weeks after her fifth-grade graduation, Karla Mejia woke up with numbness on the right side of her body. The diagnosis was multiple sclerosis. She spent almost a year in the hospital, relearning to walk and to write, but her anger and depression over the years left her unable to concentrate on schoolwork. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Working Twice as Hard', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Working Twice as Hard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Community Service Society of New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Multiple Sclerosis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T02:42:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/735ee9ed-4441-58bf-b03f-bfd4d8649c95', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/735ee9ed-4441-58bf-b03f-bfd4d8649c95'}, {'abstract': 'A growing number of Long Island wineries are offering their products by the keg.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/nyregion/more-long-island-wines-sold-by-the-keg.html', 'snippet': 'A growing number of Long Island wineries are offering their products by the keg.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long Island wines are increasingly sold from taps in restaurants on the Island and in New York City. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Future Sans Corkscrews', 'kicker': 'Long Island Vines', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Future Sans Corkscrews', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T02:44:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard G. Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/564e8145-8932-5dda-acc7-b267b1e14d69', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/564e8145-8932-5dda-acc7-b267b1e14d69'}, {'abstract': 'Verona Ristorante, an Italian restaurant in Farmingdale, exudes warmth and generosity, with after-dinner drinks and bread on the house.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/nyregion/at-verona-ristorante-an-old-fashioned-touch-review.html', 'snippet': 'Verona Ristorante, an Italian restaurant in Farmingdale, exudes warmth and generosity, with after-dinner drinks and bread on the house.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VERONA RISTORANTE, a five-year-old Italian restaurant in Farmingdale, is anything but trendy. Not only does it still serve patrons a free bread basket — a vanishing amenity — but it also includes a house-made focaccia and three additional breads from a local bakery. That basket is accompanied by butter, marinated olives and chickpeas, and a bowl of chopped tomatoes and onions for making do-it-yourself bruschetta.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15DINELI1/15DINELI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 822, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15DINELI1/15DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15DINELI1/15DINELI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Old-Fashioned Touch With Classic Italian', 'kicker': 'Long Island Dining | Farmingdale', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Old-Fashioned Touch With Classic Italian', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Farmingdale (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T02:44:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Starkey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Starkey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d836515c-64d9-5f56-940a-c14cff9f9203', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d836515c-64d9-5f56-940a-c14cff9f9203'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks’ offense has sputtered through 11 games, even with a healthy Carmelo Anthony, because of too many new faces, too little practice time and the absence of a true point guard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/sports/basketball/carmelo-anthonys-injury-forces-knicks-to-adjust.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks’ offense has sputtered through 11 games, even with a healthy Carmelo Anthony, because of too many new faces, too little practice time and the absence of a true point guard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OKLAHOMA CITY — Twenty-seven percent of the Knicks’ offense will be missing Saturday night, and maybe that will not be the worst thing for the team.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anthony’s Injury Forces Knicks to Adjust', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anthony’s Injury Forces Knicks to Adjust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "Stoudemire, Amar'e", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'p