et and Lowdown,” will revisit the experience at the Picture House in Pelham.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EARLY in 1998, the guitarist Howard Alden got a call from the pianist Dick Hyman, a longtime collaborator of Woody Allen’s, asking whether he would like to work on Mr. Allen’s latest movie, “Sweet and Lowdown.” All he would need to do, Mr. Hyman said, was lay down tracks in the style of the gypsy guitarist Django Reinhardt — a style with which Mr. Alden was deeply familiar. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15ARTSWE_SPAN/15ARTSWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15ARTSWE_SPAN/15ARTSWE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15ARTSWE_SPAN/15ARTSWE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15ARTSWE_SPAN/15ARTSWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15ARTSWE_SPAN/15ARTSWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Guitarists, as Heard in a Woody Allen Film', 'kicker': 'Arts | Westchester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Guitarists, as Heard in a Woody Allen Film', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alden, Howard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pizzarelli, Bucky', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value':