ucation, a topic he has returned to over the years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg devoted more than half of his State of the City address on Thursday to education. Throughout Mr. Bloomberg’s 10 years as mayor, it has been a consistent theme of the annual speeches. Following are excerpts:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Mayor’s State of the City Addresses, a Recurring Theme', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Mayor’s State of the City Addresses, a Recurring Theme', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the City Message (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T03:18:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fernanda Santos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/5abb7b3f-c723-5056-8a15-12b001ae0962', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5abb7b3f-c723-5056-8a15-12b001ae0962'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees moved quickly to get two starting pitchers from the Seattle Mariners, Michael Pineda and Jose Campos, and agreed to a one-year deal with Hiroki Kuroda.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/sports/baseball/yankees-trade-jesus-montero-for-michael-pineda.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees moved quickly to get two starting pitchers from the Seattle Mariners, Michael Pineda and Jose Campos, and agreed to a one-year deal with Hiroki Kuroda.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For weeks, people around baseball have marveled at the relative inactivity of the Yankees this off-season. Normally one of the most aggressive actors in baseball in terms of acquiring marquee players, the team was quiet almost to the point of drawing suspicion. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/14/sports/YANKEES/YANKEES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Two Deals, Yanks Trade Montero but Bolster Pitching', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Two Deals, Yanks Trade Montero but Bolster Pitching', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pineda, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Mariners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trades (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Montero, Jesus', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuroda, Hiroki', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T03:18:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4804f70d-f239-526e-a7d7-11b69ae577fb', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4804f70d-f239-526e-a7d7-11b69ae577fb'}, {'abstract': 'Great Organ Music at Yale, produced by the Institute of Sacred Music, and the Horowitz Piano Series, a set of concerts run by the School of Music’s piano department, are running concurrently.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/nyregion/yale-music-season-showcases-organ-and-piano-work.html', 'snippet': 'Great Organ Music at Yale, produced by the Institute of Sacred Music, and the Horowitz Piano Series, a set of concerts run by the School of Music’s piano department, are running concurrently.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SIMON PRESTON, an organist with a wit as dry as his talent is prodigious, had just concluded a solo concert in Yale University’s Woolsey Hall last November when he was asked to draw a broad comparison between the hall’s monumental Newberry Memorial Organ — on which he had rendered Bach, Mozart, Liszt and Olivier Messiaen to sustained applause — and the other great organs he had played.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15ARTSCT1_SPAN/15ARTSCT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15ARTSCT1_SPAN/15ARTSCT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600