}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tom Ardolino Dies at 56; Drummer for NRBQ for Three Decades', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tom Ardolino, 56, Drummer For NRBQ for Three Decades', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NRBQ', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T04:13:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Keepnews', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keepnews', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/42a48edf-e7ba-544e-8b9d-5e05ab4e13d1', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42a48edf-e7ba-544e-8b9d-5e05ab4e13d1'}, {'abstract': 'The playwright Katori Hall is in the middle of a busy theater season, but she spends Sundays avoiding writing and appreciating reality television and Southern cuisine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/nyregion/katori-hall-playwright-relaxes-with-reality-tv-on-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'The playwright Katori Hall is in the middle of a busy theater season, but she spends Sundays avoiding writing and appreciating reality television and Southern cuisine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The playwright Katori Hall, a self-described workaholic, is in the middle of a busy theater season: shortly after her play “The Mountaintop,” about the last hours of the life of the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr., closes on Broadway on Jan. 22, her newest play, “Hurt Village,” about a soldier returning from Iraq, will open at the Signature Theater Company on Feb. 7. Ms. Hall, 30, who was born in Memphis, lives in Washington Heights with her fiancé, Alan Tumusiime, 28, a video editor and photographer. She spends Sundays avoiding writing, playing guitar and appreciating both reality television and Southern cuisine.  ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE_SPAN/15ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE_SPAN/15ROUTINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE_SPAN/15ROUTINE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE_SPAN/15ROUTINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE_SPAN/15ROUTINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Twitter, Eggs and ‘Mob Wives’', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twitter, Eggs and ‘Mob Wives’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Katori', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T04:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Okeowo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Okeowo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16c1726b-39d9-57c9-b640-f1fca9cc68bf', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16c1726b-39d9-57c9-b640-f1fca9cc68bf'}, {'abstract': 'Neville Bardos, the horse who survived a barn fire last May, was named the international Horse of the Year for 2011 by the United States Equestrian Federation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/sports/neville-bardos-horse-who-survived-fire-honored.html', 'snippet': 'Neville Bardos, the horse who survived a barn fire last May, was named the international Horse of the Year for 2011 by the United States Equestrian Federation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neville Bardos, the horse who survived a barn fire last May, was named the international Horse of the Year for 2011 by the United States Equestrian Federation. Neville was among 11 horses in a\xa0 barn in West Grove, Pa., when it caught fire in late May. Six of the horses died. Three months later, Neville\xa0 is on a short list of Summer Olympics contenders. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inspiring Horse Honored', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Equestrian', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inspiring Horse Honored', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horsemanship and Equestrian Events', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T04:15:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Pilon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eb25046-5d22-50b6-aa44-1e8b82930b40', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eb25046-5d22-50b6-aa44-1e8b82930b40'}, {'abstract': 'Tibetans in Gansu Province protested the death of a Tibetan man whom the police had shot dead, according to a report released this week by International Campaign for Tibet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/world/asia/china-tibetans-ransack-police-station-after-killing-of-suspect-group-says.html', 'snippet': 'Tibetans in Gansu Province protested the death of a Tibetan man whom the police had shot dead, according to a report released this week by International Campaign for Tibet.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Tibetans in Gansu Province protested the death of a Tibetan man whom the police had shot dead after suspecting him of being involved in stealing equipment from an airport construction site, according to a report released this week by International Campaign for Tibet, an advocacy group based in Washington. The Tibetan man, Gurgo Tsering, in his mid-30s, was killed on Jan. 8 in a late night raid in Achok, in Xiahe County. The new airport in Achok was approved by officials in 2009, but locals have expressed concerns because it is being built near a sacred mountain. Tibetans ransacked the Achok police station after the fatal shooting, and the riot police were called in to put down the unrest, the report said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Tibetans Ransack Police Station After Killing of Suspect, Group Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Tibetans Ransack Police Station After Killing of Suspect, Group Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gansu Province (China)', 