s', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Billionaire Claims Signatures to Challenge Putin for President', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Billionaire Claims Signatures To Challenge Putin for President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prokhorov, Mikhail D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ad4d2ff-102c-5c56-880b-f6f91f090bae', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ad4d2ff-102c-5c56-880b-f6f91f090bae'}, {'abstract': 'Julie Andrews will direct a musical version of her children’s book, “The Great American Mousical,” for Goodspeed Musicals.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/julie-andrews-to-direct-mousical-based-on-her-childrens-book/', 'snippet': 'Julie Andrews will direct a musical version of her children’s book, “The Great American Mousical,” for Goodspeed Musicals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Julie Andrews will direct a new musical, “The Great American Mousical,” based on the children’s book of the same name co-written with her daughter, Emma Walton Hamilton. Goodspeed Musicals will put on a developmental production of the show on its second stage, the Norma Terris Theater in Chester, Conn.,, from Nov. 8 to Dec. 2, theater leaders are scheduled to announce on Saturday afternoon. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Julie Andrews to Direct ‘Mousical’ Based on Her Children’s Book', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDREWS, JULIE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, Hunter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gattelli, Christopher', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Emma Walton', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walton, Emma', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walton, Tony', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goodspeed Musicals', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T05:01:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Heller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e4604b8-7a70-5e47-b622-8a81f9b1762b', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e4604b8-7a70-5e47-b622-8a81f9b1762b'}, {'abstract': 'The Berlin Zoo and the association of its supporters announced the winning design on Friday for a bronze statue of Knut, the world-famous polar bear who died last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/world/europe/germany-a-bear-will-dream-in-bronze.html', 'snippet': 'The Berlin Zoo and the association of its supporters announced the winning design on Friday for a bronze statue of Knut, the world-famous polar bear who died last year.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Plans are now set for Knut the polar bear’s memorial. The Berlin Zoo and the association of its supporters announced the winning design on Friday for a bronze statue of the world-famous bear who died last year. The design, “Knut — The Dreamer” by Josef Tabachnyk, was chosen out of more than 40 proposals and depicts the young polar bear in repose, head on paws, lying on a slab of granite. The $19,000 cost of the memorial is being financed through donations. Knut became a worldwide media sensation as a cub in 2007 after his mother rejected him and zookeepers decided to raise him. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany: A Bear Will Dream in Bronze', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany: A Bear Will Dream in Bronze', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berlin Zoo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polar Bears', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T05:04:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/77e04ab2-f79e-50af-8c57-c929e9449cce', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77e04ab2-f79e-50af-8c57-c929e9449cce'}, {'abstract': 'A critically acclaimed Iranian film director has written a letter to the Culture Ministry challenging its order to close the House of Cinema, Iran’s umbrella guild for cinema professionals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/world/middleeast/iran-acclaimed-director-protest-shutdown-of-cinema-guild.html', 'snippet': 'A critically acclaimed Iranian film director has written a letter to the Culture Ministry challenging its order to close the House of Cinema, Iran’s umbrella guild for cinema professionals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A critically acclaimed Iranian film director has written a letter to the Culture Ministry challenging its order to close the House of Cinema, Iran’s umbrella guild for cinema professionals and the only domestic organization that supports independent film. The ministry’s order, which has been widely protested by many of the organization’s members, threatens to effectively silence Iran’s last remaining autonomous forum for free expression in the visual arts. The director, Asghar Farhadi, whose movie “A Separation” is favored to win the top honors at the Golden Globe awards on Sunday, told Ministry officials in the letter that “If the decision to dissolve the House of Cinema is based on the idea that the majority of the film community and members of the guild are in agreement with your method, then I suggest that you take a vote on this decision among the few thousand members of the House of Cinema.” An excerpt of the letter was published by the Web site of Shargh, an Iranian reformist newspaper that has often been shut down by the government. Mr. Farhadi’s film, about the breakup of a family, has shattered box-office office records in Iran and won nearly three dozen awards. The Culture Ministry’s order was supposed to take effect this week, and it remains unclear whether House of Cinema’s management committee will seek a way to nullify it.\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran: Acclaimed Director Protest Shutdown of Cinema Guild', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farhadi, Asghar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T05:13:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b474f3c9-0cfd-5b3c-909b-898d6f54b31f', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b474f3c9-0cfd-5b3c-909b-898d6f54b31f'}, {'abstract': 'Blue Ivy Carter, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s State of the City address, Jorge Posada and Stephen Colbert were popular among New Yorkers on Twitter in the past week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/nyregion/trendingnyc-the-week-on-twitter.html', 'snippet': 'Blue Ivy Carter, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s State of the City address, Jorge Posada and Stephen Colbert were popular among New Yorkers on Twitter in the past week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pity Blue Ivy Carter. Her very birth upset many New Yorkers amid reports that her parents, Beyoncé and Jay-Z, had unleashed a small security army on the maternity ward at Lenox Hill Hospital in Manhattan, hassling other parents.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '#trendingnyc: The Week on Twitter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '#Trending N.Y.C.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Stephen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knowles, Beyonce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posada, Jorge', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jay-Z', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the City Message (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T05:13:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad6612e4-1837-5dd4-b1ae-fb9df0bc4f2c', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad6612e4-1837-5dd4-b1ae-fb9df0bc4f2c'}, {'abstract': 'The group running the video, a pro-Gingrich “super PAC,” made no move to alter the work and gave no indication of retreat from using its excerpts in television commercials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/us/politics/gingrich-calls-for-withdrawal-of-ad-against-romney-and-bain.html', 'snippet': 'The group running the video, a pro-Gingrich “super PAC,” made no move to alter the work and gave no indication of retreat from using its excerpts in television commercials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Misleading and exaggerated claims in a film portraying Mitt Romney as a heartless job killer led Newt Gingrich to ask on Friday that the group behind it change or withdraw it, even though Mr. Gingrich is the intended beneficiary of the film. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Reversal, Gingrich Calls for Withdrawal of Film Attacking Romney and Bain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Reversal, Gingric