 among its people. It was one of the first countries to ban “The Satanic Verses” by Salman Rushdie. Lawsuits forced the Indian painter Maqbool Fida Husain to live in exile during the last several years of his life. An academic book about the 17th-century warrior known as Shivaji was banned for fear of offending Shivaji’s modern-day fans, until the Supreme Court lifted the prohibition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s Courts Grapple With Web Censorship', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rushdie, Salman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T05:47:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddf1f645-ba82-5b98-931d-838f74ed1a9f', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddf1f645-ba82-5b98-931d-838f74ed1a9f'}, {'abstract': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/nyregion/events-in-westchester.html', 'snippet': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A guide to cultural and recreational events in the Hudson Valley. Items for the calendar should be sent at least three weeks in advance to westweek@nytimes.com.', 'pr