et': 'Houston running back Arian Foster has a big, new fan — Baltimore’s veteran linebacker Ray Lewis. The two are certain to meet on the field on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'He is not the stereotypical N.F.L. running back. Start with Arian Foster’s first name, an abbreviated version of Aquarians, chosen by his father and meaning “holder of knowledge.” After Foster scores a touchdown, he eschews aggressive celebratory displays and places his hands together and bows, a gesture of respect in India, in his case to the game he plays. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/sports/dog-texans/dog-texans-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/sports/dog-texans/dog-texans-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/sports/dog-texans/dog-texans-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/sports/dog-texans/dog-texans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/sports/dog-texans/dog-texans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Running Back on Rise and Linebacker in Career Twilight Become Friends', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Running Back on Rise and Linebacker in Career Twilight Become Friends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Texans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value':