l', 'snippet': 'Whatever the feelings of Mississippi voters, hundreds of last-minute pardons have not dulled former Gov. Haley Barbour’s prospects in the private sector.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JACKSON, Miss. — But who will pardon the governor?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/us/BARBOUR/BARBOUR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/us/BARBOUR/BARBOUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/us/BARBOUR/BARBOUR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite Uproar Over Clemency, Barbour Finds Lucrative Nest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite Uproar Over Clemency, Barbour Finds Lucrative Nest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barbour, Haley', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T18:06:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e604af98-f9ac-5560-a576-8463a2170a34', 'word_count': 1231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e604af98-f9ac-5560-a576-8463a2170a34'}, {'abstract': 'Two former imperial powers, France and Turkey, are vying to exert their political influence over Arab countries in upheaval.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/opinion/sunday/the-empires-strike-back.html', 'snippet': 'Two former imperial powers, France and Turkey, are vying to exert their political influence over Arab countries in upheaval.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS Egyptians and Tunisians vote to replace ousted despots and the Syrian government teeters on the brink, two old imperial powers are competing to exert their political influence over Arab countries in upheaval. And they are not America and Russia. After years of cold-war competition over the Middle East and North Africa, it is now France and Turkey that are vying for lucrative business ties and the chance to mold a new generation of leaders in lands that they once controlled.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/sunday-review/15RUSSIA/15RUSSIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/sunday-review/15RUSSIA/15RUSSIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/sunday-review/15RUSSIA/15RUSSIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/sunday-review/15RUSSIA/15RUSSIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'cr