2012/01/15/business/a-wireless-way-around-data-center-traffic-jams.html', 'snippet': 'To battle information overload at data centers, researchers are testing a new option: high-frequency wireless links that can help move the data along during crunch times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE vast data centers that process information for the Facebooks and Amazons of the Web work at a brisk clip. But even so, they can’t always keep up. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/business/15-NOVEL1/15-NOVEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/business/15-NOVEL1/15-NOVEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 240}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/business/15-NOVEL1/15-NOVEL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/business/15-NOVEL1/15-NOVEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/business/15-NOVEL1/15-NOVEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wireless Road Around Data Traffic Jams', 'kicker': 'Novelties', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wireless Answer To Data Traffic Jams', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Centers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T22:17:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NAT', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Eisenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eisenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/555f5c1f-87ce-5196-aded-e5a3ebe327a8', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/555f5c1f-87ce-5196-aded-e5a3ebe327a8'}, {'abstract': 'Basic differences about Scripture, the afterlife and the nature of God lead many, though not all, Christians to conclude that Mormons cannot be considered Christian.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/us/politics/evangelical-christians-unease-with-romney-is-theological.html', 'snippet': 'Basic differences about Scripture, the afterlife and the nature of God lead many, though not all, Christians to conclude that Mormons cannot be considered Christian.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Rev. R. Philip Roberts, the president of a Southern Baptist seminary in Kansas City, Mo., is an evangelist with a particular goal: countering Mormon beliefs. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/us/MORMON/MORMON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/us/MORMON/MORMON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/us/MORMON/MORMON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/us/MORMON/MORMON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/us/MORMON/MORMON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Theological Differences Behind Evangelical Unease With Romney', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Theological Differences Behind Evangelical Unease With Romney', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evangelical Movement', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T22:38:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laurie Goodstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c132d70-67b0-5d11-924c-f2a4c75818ae', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c132d70-67b0-5d11-924c-f2a4c75818ae'}, {'abstract': 'A statement of support from evangelicals could get voters to take another look at Rick Santorum at the expense of other conservatives.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/backing-of-evangelicals-could-resuscitate-santorum-in-south-carolina/', 'snippet': 'A statement of support from evangelicals could get voters to take another look at Rick Santorum at the expense of other conservatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Polling in the early stages of the nomination race can be extremely fluid, but ordinarily a candidate who is in fourth place with a week to go would have little chance of winning a state primary. This is why the FiveThirtyEight forecast model is skeptical about Rick Santorum’s chances of winning South Carolina, where his numbers have slumped since his near-victory in Iowa on Jan 3.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backing of Evangelicals Could Resuscitate Santorum in South Carolina', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T22:51:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26ea0bc3-cbbd-519e-9867-38aec808fdc6', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26ea0bc3-cbbd-519e-9867-38aec808fdc6'}, {'abstract': 'In the 1973 decision, the judge said the film’s “alleged story lines are the facade, the sheer negligee” that hid the producer’s purpose of showing hard-core pornography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/nyregion/joel-j-tyler-judge-who-ruled-deep-throat-obscene-dies-at-90.html', 'snippet': 'In the 1973 decision, the judge said the film’s “alleged story lines are the facade, the sheer negligee” that hid the producer’s purpose of showing hard-core pornography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joel J. Tyler, who as a Manhattan judge ruled, in a particularly explicit and colorful opinion, that the pornographic film “Deep Throat” was obscene and that the New York City theaters showing it were breaking the law, inadvertently helping it become perhaps the most popular X-rated movie of all time, died in Yonkers on Nov. 9. He was 90.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/dog-TYLER1-obit/dog-TYLER1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 554, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/dog-TYLER1-obit/dog-TYLER1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/nyregion/dog-TYLER1-obit/dog-TYLER1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Joel J. Tyler, Judge Who Pronounced ‘Deep Throat’ Obscene, Dies at 90', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Joel J. Tyler, Judge Who Pronounced ‘Deep Throat’ Obscene, Dies at 90', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indecency, Obscenity and Profanity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Judges', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pornography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyler, Joel J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T22:52:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b76a125-fadd-51c0-b523-d94afc3805c9', 'word_count': 1090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b76a125-fadd-51c0-b523-d94afc3805c9'}, {'abstract': 'The Northern California International tournament, which ended last Sunday, was modeled on ones in Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/crosswords/chess/as-california-chess-grows-a-shining-specimen-of-play.html', 'snippet': 'The Northern California International tournament, which ended last Sunday, was modeled on ones in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is not surprising that California is a center of chess in the United States. But in the last couple of years, there has been a burst of activity there, with a large number of international tournaments that have given players a chance to qualify for grandmaster and international master titles. Two groups are behind those events. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California’s Reputation Grows With New Events', 'kicker': 'Chess', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California’s Reputation Grows With New Events', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T22:53:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bcbe9c4-647a-52be-bcf8-d4595de278f5', 'word_count': 464, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bcbe9c4-647a-52be-bcf8-d4595de278f5'}, {'abstract': 'And now the weather forecast, from Finn Vigeland.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/weather/', 'snippet': 'And now the weather forecast, from Finn Vigeland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — Everyone have their umbrellas out? You’re going to need one for today’s delightful puzzle by the Columbia University student Finn Vigeland. The only warning I would give you is that these drops are likely to be a bit heavier than usual, so make sure that umbrella is reinforced. Concrete would probably be good.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday: Weather Report', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T23:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/316c8309-0d28-54f4-baf3-a63e0be0bf1e', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/316c8309-0d28-54f4-baf3-a63e0be0bf1e'}, {'abstract': 'With for-profit colleges under siege in Washington over accusations that they defraud students, Mitt Romney’s endorsement of them puts him in the middle of a political debate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/us/politics/mitt-romney-offers-praise-for-a-donors-business.html', 'snippet': 'With for-profit colleges under siege in Washington over accusations that they defraud students, Mitt Romney’s endorsement of them puts him in the middle of a political debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — At a town-hall-style meeting in New Hampshire last month, listeners pressed Mitt Romney on the soaring cost of higher education. His solution: students should consider for-profit colleges like the little-known Full Sail University in Florida. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/us/JP-PROFIT/JP-PROFIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/us/JP-PROFIT/JP-PROFIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/us/JP-PROFIT/JP-PROFIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/us/JP-PROFIT/JP-PROFIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/15/us/JP-PROFIT/JP-PROFIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Offers Praise for a Donor’s Business', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney Praises A Business Run By A Big Donor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'For-Profit Schools', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-14T23:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_na