ugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97743017-5771-55cf-9108-b6e57dd3f4b9', 'word_count': 24, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97743017-5771-55cf-9108-b6e57dd3f4b9'}, {'abstract': 'Juan Rangel, of the United Neighborhood Organization, has leveraged close ties to Chicago’s political leaders to create one of the city’s largest charter-school networks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/us/a-lifetime-of-close-ties-and-growing-influence.html', 'snippet': 'Juan Rangel, of the United Neighborhood Organization, has leveraged close ties to Chicago’s political leaders to create one of the city’s largest charter-school networks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Rahm Emanuel’s first public appearance after resigning as White House chief of staff in October 2010, he showed up in the Pilsen neighborhood accompanied by Juan Rangel, the community activist. Mr. Emanuel and Mr. Rangel had spoken for the first time only days earlier, yet Mr. Rangel soon would become a co-chairman of Mr. Emanuel’s successful bid for mayor.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/us/15CNCRONGEL1/15CNCRONGEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/us/15CNCRONGEL1/15CNCRONGEL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/us/15CNCRONGEL1/15CNCRONGEL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lifetime of Close Ties and Growing Influence', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Lifet