'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Gollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1be72fba-ea6a-574a-9602-a75af11b2905', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1be72fba-ea6a-574a-9602-a75af11b2905'}, {'abstract': 'A preliminary account of the final moments of the luxury cruise ship Costa Concordia, according to the Coast Guard.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/01/14/world/europe/map-of-the-area-where-the-italian-cruise-run-aground.html', 'snippet': 'A preliminary account of the final moments of the luxury cruise ship Costa Concordia, according to the Coast Guard.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A preliminary account of the final moments of the luxury cruise ship Costa Concordia, according to the Coast Guard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where the Italian Cruise Ship Ran Aground', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-15T00:43:49+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/9564f3c1-f2d9-53f5-91a8-4721055891b4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/9564f3c1-f2d9-53f5-91a8-4721055891b4'}, {'abstract': 'Our intrepid group of Giants fans finds plenty of blue jerseys and just a few naysayers on the first legs of the trip to Lambeau Field.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/14/eight-men-in-the-road-trip-to-lambeau-takes-off/', 'snippet': 'Our intrepid group of Giants fans finds plenty of blue jerseys and just a few naysayers on the first legs of the trip to Lambeau Field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifty years ago, if the Giants were headed to Green Bay to play the Packers in the postseason, fans in New York might have considered themselves lucky to catch the game on television. Today, with tickets available online and frequent-flier miles accruing with every credit-card purchase, fans can dare to dream a little more boldly. Six members of a Chatham, N.J., softball team — a mix of lawyers, Wall Streeters and computer software salesmen — are set to travel to Lambeau Field for Sunday’s showdown between the Giants and the Packers. It will be a trip of cheap hotel rooms and high hopes, cramped rental cars and unexpectedly good seats at the game. The men — they will be joined by two pals in Milwaukee — have agreed to create a Titletown travelogue. Their hopes are to stay friends, keep their jobs and, well, see the Giants win.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eight Men In: The Road Trip to Lambeau Takes Off', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Road Trips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Green Bay Packers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lambeau Field', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milwaukee (Wis)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-15T00:58:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By STEPHEN COSTELLO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'COSTELLO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdbfe252-af39-5b07-8e09-c93e79d649e9', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdbfe252-af39-5b07-8e09-c93e79d649e9'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration said it would not support central elements of efforts in Congress to enforce copyrights on the Internet, all but killing the current versions of the legislation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/us/white-house-says-it-opposes-parts-of-2-antipiracy-bills.html', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration said it would not support central elements of efforts in Congress to enforce copyrights on the Internet, all but killing the current versions of the legislation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Obama administration said Saturday that it strongly opposed central elements of two Congressional efforts to enforce copyrights on the Internet, all but killing the current versions of legislation that has divided both political parties and pitted Hollywood against Silicon Valley.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'White House Says It Opposes Parts of Two Antipiracy Bills', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'White House Takes Issue With 2 Antipiracy Bills', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-15T00:59:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0d70eec-bac6-53c0-8642-dc8ee044220a', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0d70eec-bac6-53c0-8642-dc8ee044220a'}, {'abstract': 'In a Washington Post interview, the former Penn State coach Joe Paterno said he did not know how to handle a report in 2002 of suspected sexual abuse by Jerry Sandusky.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/sports/ncaafootball/joe-paterno-talks-about-his-role-in-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'In a Washington Post interview, the former Penn State coach Joe Paterno said he did not know how to handle a report in 2002 of suspected sexual abuse by Jerry Sandusky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joe Paterno, who was fired as Penn State’s football coach on Nov. 9 in the wake of allegations that his former defensive coordinator Jerry Sandusky had sexually abused boys, said in an interview published Saturday that he reported a suspected assault in 2002 to his superiors because he was unsure how to handle the matter. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paterno Describes His Uncertainty Over Allegation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paterno Describes His Uncertainty Over Allegation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterno, Joe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-15T01:03:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b4aeb4c-7ebb-5838-9b2d-bc50c1a89246', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b4aeb4c-7ebb-5838-9b2d-bc50c1a89246'}, {'abstract': 'Shalane Flanagan, the bronze medalist in the 10,000 meters in Beijing, broke the United States trials record in only her second marathon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/sports/track-star-flanagan-will-return-to-olympics-in-womens-marathon.html', 'snippet': 'Shalane Flanagan, the bronze medalist in the 10,000 meters in Beijing, broke the United States trials record in only her second marathon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — After a slow, tactical start, the United States women’s Olympic marathon trials began at 20 miles to distill itself to the three eventual qualifiers for the 2012 London Games: Shalane Flanagan (2 hours 25 minutes 38 seconds), Desiree Davila (2:25:55) and Kara Goucher (2:26:06).', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/15/sports/YRACE/YRACE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/15/sports/YRACE/YRACE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'c