agraph': 'Before the big themes emerge, there are the snapshots, images and moments that linger when a show ends, the buyers file out and the cameras are packed away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Milan, the Moments that Linger', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-15T17:18:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/339d4269-20db-5109-acda-ef84a6fc414e', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/339d4269-20db-5109-acda-ef84a6fc414e'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Santorum said the vote of support by evangelical leaders on Saturday should persuade Republicans in South Carolina that he deserves to be that alternative.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/santorum-and-gingrich-scramble-for-the-conservative-vote/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Santorum said the vote of support by evangelical leaders on Saturday should persuade Republicans in South Carolina that he deserves to be that alternative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Rick Santorum and Newt Gingrich both pleaded with conservatives on Sunday to unite behind their candidacies in a last-ditch effort to stop Mitt Romney’s march to the Republican presidentialnomination.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Santorum and Gingrich Scramble for the Conservative Vote', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Ne