nt downgrade of French debt, though not unexpected, adds to the challenges facing the incumbent, Nicolas Sarkozy, as he seeks re-election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/world/europe/frances-gloomy-economic-outlook-haunts-presidential-race.html', 'snippet': 'The recent downgrade of French debt, though not unexpected, adds to the challenges facing the incumbent, Nicolas Sarkozy, as he seeks re-election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Hakim Benselama, 32, an industrial engineer, nearly had a job in autumn 2008, but as the world economic crisis hit, he said, “I got phone call after phone call telling me that the projects I had interviewed for were all canceled.” He has been jobless since.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/16/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/16/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/16/world/FRANCE/FRANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As French Vote Nears, Sarkozy Is Haunted by Grim Economy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France’s Gloomy Economic Outlook Haunts Nation’s Presidential Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-15T19:13:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1cc8241-c9cf-5952-85a5-9ebe71bdb5ae', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1cc8241-c9cf-5952-85a5-9ebe71bdb5ae'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Close, the star of “Albert Nobbs,” and Ms. Streep, who plays Margaret Thatcher in “The Iron Lady,” are competitors at the Golden Globes tonight.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/meryl-streep-on-glenn-close-the-battle-of-the-blondes-and-women-audiences-at-bafta-tea/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Close, the star of “Albert Nobbs,” and Ms. Streep, who plays Margaret Thatcher in “The Iron Lady,” are competitors at the Golden Globes tonight.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I have a bone to pick with you,” Meryl Streep said to the Bagger. That sound you don’t hear is our heart stopping just a little.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meryl Streep on Glenn Close, the Battle of the Blondes and Women Audiences at BAFTA Tea', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Close, Glenn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Meryl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Film Critics Circle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-15T19:24:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e81f04bf-45e2-55af-acb3-048215f4f69a', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e81f04bf-45e2-55af-acb3-048215f4f69a'}, {'abstract': 'At an age when most lawyers are done with their careers, four practitioners have decided to form a new firm.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/a-new-law-firm-with-161-years-of-experience/', 'snippet': 'At an age when most lawyers are done with their careers, four practitioners have decided to form a new firm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Norman Siegel and Herbert Teitelbaum were classmates at New York University law school. Mr. Siegel is married to Saralee Evans, a former acting State Supreme Court justice. Their wedding ceremony was performed by Emily Jane Goodman, a Supreme Court justice. They all come from Brooklyn. Collectively, they have 161 years of legal experience and a record of impact in and out of court. And now, when most of their contemporaries are contemplating retirement or have already quit, the four of them are starting a new law firm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Law Firm With 161 Years of Experience', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evans, Saralee', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'SIEGEL, NORMAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teitelbaum, Herbert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-15T19:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96fdacab-a1e6-55ee-8d08-230f72b5a703', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96fdacab-a1e6-55ee-8d08-230f72b5a703'}, {'abstract': 'Even less mobility ahead?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/the-great-gatsby-curve/', 'snippet': 'Even less mobility ahead?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alan Krueger, the chairman of the Council of Economic Advisers — who is not only a colleague of mine at Princeton, but gets a lot of my mail and vice versa — gave a very informative speech on inequality last week that should have received more press than it did. Much of it was stuff that inequality mavens already know, but he had one striking result that was what I suspected but hadn’t seen demonstrated: a clear negative relationship between inequality at a point in time and intergenerational social mobility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great Gatsby Curve', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-15T19:34:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c600d1ff-93bf-57f0-851f-e97b74a7f9da', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c600d1ff-93bf-57f0-851f-e97b74a7f9da'}, {'abstract': 'Milan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/15/fashion/bottega_fa