ican-realness-review.html', 'snippet': 'Jennifer Lacey pondered the future of performance in “Gattica,” a somewhat satirical work that was part of the American Realness festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A performance about the future of performance: doesn’t sound like something to look forward to, does it? Fortunately, the person assigned the topic for the American Realness festival at the Abrons Arts Center Underground Theater on Friday was Jennifer Lacey, an American artist based in Paris. Her lecture-performance “Gattica” approached the subject semisatirically and had some fun with it. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/16/arts/gattica/gattica-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 987, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/16/arts/gattica/gattica-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/16/arts/gattica/gattica-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trying to Divine the Future Despite a Few Limitations', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trying to Divine the Future Despite a Few Limitations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lacey, Jennifer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Realness Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-15T23:13:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None