7af3318-0e79-53f7-afdc-4b140fdcecdb'}, {'abstract': 'The tenor Joseph Calleja portrays Faust and the bass Ferruccio Furlanetto is Méphistophélès in the Metropolitan Opera’s new production of Gounod’s “Faust.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/arts/music/faust-with-joseph-calleja-at-the-met-review.html', 'snippet': 'The tenor Joseph Calleja portrays Faust and the bass Ferruccio Furlanetto is Méphistophélès in the Metropolitan Opera’s new production of Gounod’s “Faust.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cast changes can transform flawed opera productions. When Luc Bondy’s version of Puccini’s “Tosca” opened at the Metropolitan Opera in 2009 it was criticized and booed. Seven months later, with three new leads, it suddenly worked.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/16/arts/sub-joseph/sub-joseph-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 936, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/16/arts/sub-joseph/sub-joseph-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/16/arts/sub-joseph/sub-joseph-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Pared-Down Surroundings, a Faust of Quiet Astonishment', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Pared-Down Surroundings, A Faust of Quiet Astonishment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Furlanetto, Ferruccio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gounod, Charles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major'