ias Wegner seems to walk on walls thanks to acrobatics and sleight of hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lots of people who live in closet-size apartments in New York know all too well what it feels like to be alone and isolated in a small space. Oh, if they only had acrobatic training.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/16/arts/leo/leo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 654, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/16/arts/leo/leo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/16/arts/leo/leo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Defying Gravity Proves Easier Than Escaping From Loneliness', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'Leo'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defying Gravity Proves Easier Than Escaping From Loneliness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACROBATS AND ACROBATICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Briere, Daniel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T03:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia La Rocco', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d993a2ac-1079-5ee5-a5b1-442837f1d25f', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d993a2ac-1079-5ee5-a5b1-442837f1d25f'}, {'abstract': 'Zahra Nahim and Fawzi Hasab fled Baghdad when their sons were killed and have struggled in America with illness, language and poverty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/nyregion/iraqi-refugees-find-hardships-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Zahra Nahim and Fawzi Hasab fled Baghdad when their sons were killed and have struggled in America with illness, language and poverty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a warm December afternoon, Zahra Nahim stood in her narrow kitchen pulling flat ovals of bread out of the oven, piling plates with yellow rice and shredded chicken — and thoroughly dusting the front of her black abaya with white flour. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/16/nyregion/16NEEDIEST/16NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/16/nyregion/16NEEDIEST/16NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/16/nyregion/16NEEDIEST/16NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/16/nyregion/16NEEDIEST/16NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/16/nyregion/16NEEDIEST/16NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Violence in Iraq to Hardships in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Violence in Iraq to Hardships in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Community Service Society of New York', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T03:04:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48397505-184c-52e6-a8f1-6ee30b38ffee', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48397505-184c-52e6-a8f1-6ee30b38ffee'}, {'abstract': 'Frederik Nielsen, whose grandfather Kurt Nielsen is the only Danish man to make a Grand Slam final, reached the Australian Open draw by winning three qualifying matches but lost quickly in the first round.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/15/danish-player-cant-live-up-to-family-legacy/', 'snippet': 'Frederik Nielsen, whose grandfather Kurt Nielsen is the only Danish man to make a Grand Slam final, reached the Australian Open draw by winning three qualifying matches but lost quickly in the first round.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia – Frederik Nielsen of Denmark was expanding his family’s tennis legacy the hard way – earning a spot in the main draw of the 2012 Australian Open by winning three qualifying matches.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Danish Player Can’t Live Up to Family Legacy', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T03:06:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOH