 receiving end of multiple poor calls by officials. The former overseer of N.F.L. officials agreed.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/pereira-agrees-giants-were-victims-of-bad-calls/', 'snippet': 'Giants fans complained that their team was on the receiving end of multiple poor calls by officials. The former overseer of N.F.L. officials agreed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much of the commentary from Giants fans on our live blog of the Giants-Packers game was not about the joy of victory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pereira Agrees: Giants Were Victims of Bad Calls', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T12:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/581ede41-28aa-5971-a47a-d5004a6e7328', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/581ede41-28aa-5971-a47a-d5004a6e7328'}, {'abstract': 'PeriGen, a provider of obstetrics services for hospitals like Lenox Hill Hospital in Manhattan, is hiring Matthew Sappern as its new chief executive.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/perigen-hires-new-chief-executive/', 'snippet': 'PeriGen, a provider of obstetrics services for hospitals like Lenox Hill Hospital in Manhattan, is hiring Matthew Sappern as its new chief executive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PeriGen, a provider of obstetrics services for hospitals like Lenox Hill Hospital in Manhattan, plans to announce on Monday that it has hired Matthew Sappern as its chief executive. Mr. Sappern was most recently a senior vice president at Allscripts. The move by PeriGen, which is owned by private equity firms including Trident Capital, may set the company up for deal-making later this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'PeriGen Hires Chief Executive', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T12:35:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4abb8050-850b-5f9d-8fa7-39cdef6c7715', 'word_count': 64, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4abb8050-850b-5f9d-8fa7-39cdef6c7715'}, {'abstract': 'NYT Front Page for 01/16/2012', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2012/01/16/multimedia/16frontpage.html', 'snippet': 'NYT Front Page for 01/16/2012', 'lead_paragraph': 'NYT Front Page for 01/16/2012', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NYT Front Page for 01/16/2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T12:37:48+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/83e9d26f-a91d-5a9b-9574-2fba195a19ae', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/83e9d26f-a91d-5a9b-9574-2fba195a19ae'}, {'abstract': 'Within minutes of the news breaking Sunday night that Jon M. Huntsman Jr. had decided to abandon his White House bid and endorse Mitt Romney, his campaign went into overdrive trying to remove its biting online campaign videos about Mr. Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/huntsman-campaign-tries-to-wipe-romney-slate-clean/', 'snippet': 'Within minutes of the news breaking Sunday night that Jon M. Huntsman Jr. had decided to abandon his White House bid and endorse Mitt Romney, his campaign went into overdrive trying to remove its biting online campaign videos about Mr. Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can a presidential candidate erase his campaign? And how fast can that happen? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Huntsman Campaign Tries to Wipe Romney Slate Clean', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T13:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99a858ee-2d6c-5cef-ad7f-b50d1fd95f1c', 'word_count': 840, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99a858ee-2d6c-5cef-ad7f-b50d1fd95f1c'}, {'abstract': 'As food-friendly as wines from the Canary Islands are, the challenge was finding a dish that could deliver a bold swagger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/dining/sweet-and-sour-sardines-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'As food-friendly as wines from the Canary Islands are, the challenge was finding a dish that could deliver a bold swagger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Name your quaff. White, red, still, sparkling, sweet or dry? We sampled them all in our tasting of wines from the Canary Islands. And as food-friendly as these well-balanced wines were, deciding exactly what food would work best with them was the challenge. Some sort of marinated fish seemed to be the best idea, especially one that delivered bold swagger to welcome a red wine. Mackerel, sardines, wahoo or tuna were possible draft choices; a dozen fresh sardines on ice in the market made the team. And dressed in a bright, lemony wine sauce enriched with honey, like a Venetian in saor preparation, they also flattered the wines, whether white, red or sparkling. Sweet would not have been off base either, but deserved to be saved for a cheese course or dessert.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/dining/18PAIR_SPAN/18PAIR_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/18/dining/18PAIR_SPAN/18PAIR_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/dining/18PAIR_SPAN/18PAIR_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/dining/18PAIR_SPAN/18PAIR_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/dining/18PAIR_SPAN/18PAIR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/18/dining/18PAIR_SPAN/18PAIR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/dining/18PAIR_SPAN/18PAIR_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pairings: Sweet-and-Sour Sardines', 'kicker': 'Recipe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pairings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canary Islands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seafood', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T13:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39ac880d-4b17-5027-8dbc-6d877e72c93a', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39ac880d-4b17-5027-8dbc-6d877e72c93a'}, {'abstract': 'The wine panel tasted bottles from the Canary Islands, where visually striking vineyards produce wines that are light and elegant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/dining/reviews/wines-of-the-canary-islands-review.html', 'snippet': 'The wine panel tasted bottles from the Canary Islands, where visually striking vineyards produce wines that are light and elegant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TO drink only the best-known wines from time-honored regions is a little like eating in the same restaurants over and over. You can’t go wrong, perhaps, but without the rewards of exploration, you are missing out on so much more.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/dining/18WINE_SPAN/18WINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/18/dining/18WINE_SPAN/18WINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/dining/18WINE_SPAN/18WINE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/dining/18WINE_SPAN/18WINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/18/dining/18WINE_SPAN/18WINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grapes Born of Volcano and Sea', 'kicker': 'Wines of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grapes Born of Volcano and Sea', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canary Islands', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T13:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Dining & Wine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bf1a862-28ba-5d15-8083-06c4f029746e', 'word_count': 1043, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bf1a862-28ba-5d15-8083-06c4f029746e'}, {'abstract': 'As of Friday, I am an undocumented person in my own country, Russia, courtesy of the peculiar rules governing that peculiar Soviet vestige: the internal passport.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/russias-internal-passport-is-a-soviet-vestige/', 'snippet': 'As of Friday, I am an undocumented person in my own country, Russia, courtesy of the peculiar rules governing that peculiar Soviet vestige: the internal passport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — As of last Friday, I am an undocumented person in my own country. I cannot open or close a bank account, receive medical care at a state clinic, buy a cellphone, return a purchase to a store or enter into a contract, which my job requires me to do several times a day. All of these operations and many more require a valid internal passport, a peculiar document that may be the most significant vestige of the U.S.S.R. in modern Russian society.Back when we lived behind the Iron Curtain, these passports entitled us to travel only within the confines of the Soviet Union. Anyone lucky enough to be allowed to travel abroad was issued a special foreign-travel passport just for the occasion and had to surrender it upon returning home. When Russians acquired the right to travel freely, they got to keep their foreign-travel passports. But the internal passport refused to die. So now each adult Russian citizen has two passports. The documents look alike, except that the one for internal use is printed on lighter paper stock, making it feel less substantial.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Passport for Life', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Passports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T13:03:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acfcc25e-8775-536a-b315-f71cd16af9b8', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acfcc25e-8775-536a-b315-f71cd16af9b8'}, {'abstract': 'India’s premier investigative magazine grows up.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/a-conversation-with-shoma-chaudhury/', 'snippet': 'India’s premier investigative magazine grows up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since it started more than a decade ago, Tehelka has been one of the most aggressive investigative news outlets in India, reporting on and often using sting operations to uncover everything from cricket match-fixing to corruption in the defence industry, toppling government figures, sparking widespread investigations and sometimes raising questions about its methods along the way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Shoma Chaudhury', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tehelka', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T13:04:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ce714a3-c3b7-56ef-95a6-3557b08cc934', 'word_count': 2157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ce714a3-c3b7-56ef-95a6-3557b08cc934'}, {'abstract': 'Skiers discover where the snow is, Zappos says it was hacked, mourning in a digital age and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/monday-reading-where-the-snow-is/', 'snippet': 'Skiers discover where the snow is, Zappos says it was hacked, mourning in a digital age and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Monday Reading: Where the Snow Is', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T13:31:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25c6e69a-fb1f-5561-a22e-b7d3e3afac41', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25c6e69a-fb1f-5561-a22e-b7d3e3afac41'}, {'abstract': 'Inflation in India may be slowing.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/image-of-the-day-january-16/', 'snippet': 'Inflation in India may be slowing.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: January 16', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline':