e Taliban made a victory declaration, even though roughly 130,000 coalition troops were still fighting in Afghanistan — and keeping the Afghan government firmly in power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Mullah Muhammad Omar, the Taliban’s one-eyed leader, seems to have taken a page from George W. Bush’s playbook.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taliban Declares Victory, as Fighting Goes On', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Omar, Muhammad (Taliban Leader)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T17:36:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdc39327-c0b6-5d33-9585-53cb097838d9', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdc39327-c0b6-5d33-9585-53cb097838d9'}, {'abstract': 'In this edition: Iowa, New Hampshire, steak dinners and more.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/reads-reactions-17/', 'snippet': 'In this edition: Iowa, New Hampshire, steak dinners and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this edition: Iowa, New Hampshire, steak dinners and more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reads & Reactions', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T17:38:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da3d2c52-e29d-5de5-9198-0ce2cc3cdf9d', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da3d2c52-e29d-5de5-9198-0ce2cc3cdf9d'}, {'abstract': 'On the centenary of Robert Falcon Scott’s arrival at the South Pole, a London publisher is issuing copies of the 12-volume South Pole Times, which captured the substance and spirit of his expeditions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/science/scotts-south-pole-times-penguins-hockey-and-serious-stuff-too.html', 'snippet': 'On the centenary of Robert Falcon Scott’s arrival at the South Pole, a London publisher is issuing copies of the 12-volume South Pole Times, which captured the substance and spirit of his expeditions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British explorer Robert Falcon Scott finally reached his destination a century ago, Jan. 17, 1912, more than a month too late to claim victory in the race to be first to the South Pole. But the triumphant Norwegian Roald Amundsen could not deny him at least one distinction: Scott was the founder of The South Polar Times, the first magazine to be produced on the Antarctic continent.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/science/17POLE_SPAN/17POLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/17/science/17POLE_SPAN/17POLE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/science/17POLE_SPAN/17POLE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'heigh