, 'lead_paragraph': 'MONROVIA, Liberia — President Ellen Johnson Sirleaf of Liberia inaugurated a second six-year term on Monday, calling for political reconciliation after a runoff election that was tarnished by an opposition boycott and street clashes between protesters and the police. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liberia’s President Stresses Reconciliation in Second Inaugural Speech', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Liberia’s President Stresses Reconciliation in Second Inaugural Speech', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson Sirleaf, Ellen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Liberia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inaugurations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T18:59:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf64183e-bb5d-56fb-a1c1-3dd1b258709e', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf64183e-bb5d-56fb-a1c1-3dd1b258709e'}, {'abstract': 'Hulu said Sunday that it would add more original programming to its Web site with the introduction of its first scripted series, “Battleground,” and a documentary series by the writer and director Richard Linklater.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/hulu-adds-to-its-original-programming-lineup/', 'snippet': 'Hulu said Sunday that it would add more original programming to its Web site with the introduction of its first scripted series, “Battleground,” and a documentary series by the writer and director Richard Linklater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lining up more original programming for its Web site, Hulu said Sunday that it would introduce its first scripted series, “Battleground,” and a documentary series by the writer and director Richard Linklater.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hulu Adds to Its Original Programming Lineup', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hulu.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T19:04:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbba8753-19e4-581f-97d5-f484e46eb7bf', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbba8753-19e4-581f-97d5-f484e46eb7bf'}, {'abstract': 'Is child care that’s available at all hours the wave of the future?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/day-care-thats-available-at-night-too/', 'snippet': 'Is child care that’s available at all hours the wave of the future?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good day care is hard to find. Good “day” care for the night shift? Impossible, or at least it used to be. Sabrina Tavernise reports that as working hours change (about 40 percent of the American labor force works nonstandard hours now, particularly in the growing fields of nursing, retail and food service), some child-care centers are changing, too. Centers providing “after hours” care make up a large part of growth for a company that runs employer-sponored child-care centers, and many independent child-care centers are offering expanded hours — dinner, homework help and bedtime included. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Day Care That’s Available at Night, Too', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T19:04:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d1d9154-e943-5d3f-8bd2-2d3439009697', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d1d9154-e943-5d3f-8bd2-2d3439009697'}, {'abstract': 'Called “Battleground,” the series is described as a documentary-style political drama set in Wisconsin.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/hulu-announces-first-original-script-based-program/', 'snippet': 'Called “Battleground,” the series is described as a documentary-style political drama set in Wisconsin.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:02 p.m. | Updated The online video service Hulu, most of whose programming consists of material licensed from television and film companies, has commissioned its first original script-based program, which is scheduled to be available on Hulu’s free web service, rather than its premium pay Hulu Plus site, as of the middle of next month. Called “Battleground,” the new series is described as a faux documentary-style political drama-comedy set in Wisconsin– which in real life has emerged as a frontline in combat between liberals and conservatives since Republican governor Scott Walker took office a year ago. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hulu Commissions Its First Original Scripted Programming', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hulu.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T19:04:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/964d24b2-14ec-538a-8b87-d807eda0192e', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/964d24b2-14ec-538a-8b87-d807eda0192e'}, {'abstract': 'Leonardo DiCaprio bumping into Jane Fonda, Michelle Williams drinking with Busy Phillips: celebrity run-ins are common after the Goldon Globes.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/leonardo-dicaprios-mom-meet-jane-fonda/', 'snippet': 'Leonardo DiCaprio bumping into Jane Fonda, Michelle Williams drinking with Busy Phillips: celebrity run-ins are common after the Goldon Globes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — It seems appropriate to use a traffic metaphor here. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leonardo DiCaprio’s Mom, Meet Jane Fonda', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fonda, Jane', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monroe, Marilyn', 'rank': 