t', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T20:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By SCHOOLBOOK', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Schoolbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb59a0e3-a8b5-5256-9b9a-0f9a6320c9d1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb59a0e3-a8b5-5256-9b9a-0f9a6320c9d1'}, {'abstract': 'Still, the telecast was a win for NBC, giving the network its biggest audience since last year’s Globes, excluding sports.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/slightly-fewer-viewers-for-this-years-golden-globes/', 'snippet': 'Still, the telecast was a win for NBC, giving the network its biggest audience since last year’s Globes, excluding sports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a year in which nine of the top 10 movies at the box office have been sequels, perhaps it was appropriate that Ricky Gervais served up a slightly less compelling version of last year’s Golden Globe Awards. NBC said on Monday that its live Globes telecast on Sunday night drew 16.8 million viewers, down a whisker from last year’s 17 million. About 4 percent fewer people in the target demographic, adults age 18 to 49, tuned in, as measured by raw ratings points. (A 5.0 this year compared to a 5.2 last year.) NBC had heavily promoted Mr. Gervais’s acerbic comedic style as a reason to watch. As promised, he delivered a crude monologue – a repeat performance of 2011, when his remarks drew gasps – but shocking people twice with the same shtick is hard to pull off. Other factors possibly affecting interest in the show: NBC has limited ability to promote itself (the network’s overall schedule remains in the ratings basement), and the Globes also celebrated a batch of smaller films like “The Artist” that have produced limited box-office results. Still, the telecast was a win for NBC, delivering the network’s biggest audience, excluding sporting events, since last year’s Globes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slightly Fewer Viewers for This Year’s Golden Globes', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gervais, Ricky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T20:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86a39241-1dfa-500b-acad-067b61a3e57b', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86a39241-1dfa-500b-acad-067b61a3e57b'}, {'abstract': 'Evolutionary biologists say that depression, like ordinary sadness, may confer advantages. But clinicians see the devastation that depression can cause.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/is-depression-a-natural-condition/', 'snippet': 'Evolutionary biologists say that depression, like ordinary sadness, may confer advantages. But clinicians see the devastation that depression can cause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In today’s Science Times, Dr. Richard A. Friedman, a psychiatrist, explores a growing trend in academic circles to view depression as a “natural” condition that, like ordinary sadness, may provide evolutionary advantages. He writes:', 'source': 