ire primary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'National Polls Suggest Romney Is Overwhelming Favorite for G.O.P. Nomination', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T20:15:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dcf544b-2d41-55bd-b588-bf1cf7a25159', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dcf544b-2d41-55bd-b588-bf1cf7a25159'}, {'abstract': 'The country serves as a cautionary tale for those who argue that Greece could regain competitiveness by reintroducing its currency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/business/global/17iht-hungary17.html', 'snippet': 'The country serves as a cautionary tale for those who argue that Greece could regain competitiveness by reintroducing its currency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUDAPEST — Zoltan Zsoter, an 80-year-old retiree, would seem to be about as far from the world of currency speculation as a person can get. Yet he is an example of how the workings of the global financial system, amplified by the policies of a single political leader, can have a devastating effect on ordinary people. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/business/17hungary-web/17hungary-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/17/business/17hungary-web/17hungary-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 60