ue': 'Vogue', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T21:55:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/864e8e53-7e9e-5d6a-86f2-5410a7204247', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/864e8e53-7e9e-5d6a-86f2-5410a7204247'}, {'abstract': '“William Finn: Songs of Innocence and Experience” presents 19 works by the Broadway lyricist and composer in which the words sometimes spill over the music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/arts/music/william-finn-songs-of-innocence-and-experience-review.html', 'snippet': '“William Finn: Songs of Innocence and Experience” presents 19 works by the Broadway lyricist and composer in which the words sometimes spill over the music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the casual listener the theater songs of William Finn may sound like the agitated stream of consciousness of a compulsive talker running off at the mouth — their loose structures held together by seemingly haphazard internal rhymes. The words sometimes spill over the music. But if you pay close attention to a song like “How to Make Delicious Chocolate Pudding,” a jolly banjo-inflected number sung by Megan Lawrence at the Allen Room on Saturday evening as part of Lincoln Center’s American Songbook series, you discover a witty short story that follows its own unconventional songwriting logic. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/arts/finn/finn-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 862, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/arts/finn/finn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/17/arts/finn/finn-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tunes in Which Everything Is So Complicated', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tunes in Which Everything Is So Complicated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Playwrights Horizons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finn, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Songbook (Music Series)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T21:57:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb92247f-e8d0-5ddf-956a-60f494216bb4', 'word_count': 448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb92247f-e8d0-5ddf-956a-60f494216bb4'}, {'abstract': 'Wikipedia is the latest Web site to plan a blackout for Wednesday to protest two Congressional bills intended to curtail copyright violations on the Internet.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/wikipedia-plans-to-go-dark-on-wednesday-to-protest-sopa/', 'snippet': 'Wikipedia is the latest Web site to plan a blackout for Wednesday to protest two Congressional bills intended to curtail copyright violations on the Internet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wave of online prote