mann and Barber.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the last couple of seasons, audiences in New York have had ample opportunities to get to know the work of Fabio Luisi, the Metropolitan Opera’s principal conductor, who has been taking over most of the performances the ailing James Levine has had to withdraw from. But on Sunday afternoon Mr. Luisi, conducting the Met Orchestra at Carnegie Hall, revealed another dimension to his artistry. Who would have expected this Italian maestro to be so at home conducting Copland’s jazzy Clarinet Concerto, let alone an aria from “Wuthering Heights,” the only opera by Bernard Herrmann, of “Psycho” fame?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/arts/met/met-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1016, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/arts/met/met-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/17/arts/met/met-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Luisi Crosses Border To American Territory', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Luisi Crosses Border To American Territory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luisi, Fabio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fleming, Renee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera Orchestra', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T22:54:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb111003-ea6d-59d5-8349-ab5b9ee988d6', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb111003-ea6d-59d5-8349-ab5b9ee988d6'}, {'abstract': 'The president, trying to contain Iran’s nuclear ambitions, must balance choices that could harm either the economic recovery or his image as a firm leader.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/world/middleeast/faceoff-with-iran-complicates-obamas-re-election-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'The president, trying to contain Iran’s nuclear ambitions, must balance choices that could harm either the economic recovery or his image as a firm leader.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The escalating American confrontation with Iran poses a major new political threat to President Obama as he heads into his campaign for re-election, presenting him with choices that could harm either the economic recovery or his image as a firm leader.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Face-Off Testing Obama the Candidate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Face-Off Testing Obama The Candidate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T22:55:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f4d8577-3ecb-53d9-baf1-65a9988a7fc0', 'word_count': 1215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f4d8577-3ecb-53d9-baf1-65a9988a7fc0'}, {'abstract': 'After five rounds and nearly two years of negotiations aimed at producing a merger, the Screen Actors Guild and the American Federation of Television and Radio Artists, the two main unions representing actors and other performing artists, have agreed on the terms of an agreement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/arts/television/a-merger-proposal-for-actors-unions.html', 'snippet': 'After five rounds and nearly two years of negotiations aimed at producing a merger, the Screen Actors Guild and the American Federation of Television and Radio Artists, the two main unions representing actors and other performing artists, have agr...', 'lead_paragraph': 'After five rounds and nearly two years of negotiations aimed at producing a merger, the Screen Actors Guild and the American Federation of Television and Radio Artists, the two main unions representing actors and other performing artists, have agreed on the terms of an agreement, leaders of both groups said on Monday. No specifics of the accord were officially announced, but news reports said that all differences regarding a new constitution, dues-paying procedures and a governing structure had been resolved. The boards of both groups are scheduled to vote on the agreement on Jan. 28; the guild represents about 125,000 actors, and the federation’s approximately 70,000 members include broadcasters, singers and dancers as well as actors.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Merger Proposal For Actors’ Unions', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Merger Proposal For Actors’ Unions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Screen Actors Guild', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF TELEVISION AND RADIO ARTISTS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-16T22:56:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6946b51-85b5-5282-a241-18b9c1f3c3df', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6946b51-85b5-5282-a241-18b9c1f3c3df'}, {'abstract': 'As “American Idol” begins its new season on Fox on Wednesday, it faces competitors in “The X Factor,” also on Fox, and “The Voice” on NBC.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/arts/television/american-idol-returns-to-rivals-x-factor-and-voice.html', 'snippet': 'As “American Idol” begins its new season on Fox on Wednesday, it faces competitors in “The X Factor,” also on Fox, and “The Voice” on NBC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PASADENA, Calif. — “American Idol” is returning to the Fox network this week amid a growing roster of competitors, but its stars and producers say they sense no threat from the other singing contest on Fox this season, “The X Factor,” and especially not from the version on NBC, “The Voice,” that will start a second season next month. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/arts/17idol/17idol-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/18/arts/17idol/17idol-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/arts/17idol/17idol-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/arts/17idol/17idol-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/18/arts/17idol/17idol-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As ‘Idol’ Returns, It Must Face New Rivals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As ‘Idol’ Returns, It Must Face New Rivals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Jennifer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Entertainment Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Cee Lo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seacrest, 