rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T01:55:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/14bd3e9e-3d00-5760-bce3-7efbed7987d0', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14bd3e9e-3d00-5760-bce3-7efbed7987d0'}, {'abstract': 'The right-hander Phil Hughes agreed to a one-year deal, but the Yankees’ crowded rotation makes his future uncertain.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/16/hughes-gets-one-year-deal-but-future-isnt-secure/', 'snippet': 'The right-hander Phil Hughes agreed to a one-year deal, but the Yankees’ crowded rotation makes his future uncertain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees avoided arbitration with the right-hander Phil Hughes on Monday by agreeing on a one-year, $3.2 million contract, with performance bonuses, for the 2012 season. But that may not be the final transaction for Hughes this year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hughes Gets One-Year Deal, but Future Isn’t Secure', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, Phil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T01:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6938e915-3a64-5bce-b275-0d0a98dc3438', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6938e915-3a64-5bce-b275-0d0a98dc3438'}, {'abstract': 'Banks have gotten better at preventing online fraud, but criminals aren’t giving up. So financial institutions need to do a lot more to increase protections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/opinion/banking-online-is-convenient-but-how-secure.html', 'snippet': 'Banks have gotten better at preventing online fraud, but criminals aren’t giving up. So financial institutions need to do a lot more to increase protections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to a survey commissioned by the American Bankers Association last year, 62 percent of Americans preferred to do their banking online rather than at a branch or ATM. Banks and their online customers also lost more than $2 billion in 2010 because of payment card scams, fraudulent wire transfers and other Internet swindles, according to data from the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation as reported by The Financial Times. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Convenient, but How Secure?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Convenient, but How Secure?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BANKERS ASSN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T01:58:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2eed2709-08e4-51d4-b184-f8ac304ec28f', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2eed2709-08e4-51d4-b184-f8ac304ec28f'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Bellone is the new county executive of Suffolk County on Long Island, and, thankfully, he has opened his tenure with a more inclusive tone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/opinion/a-new-day-in-suffolk-heres-hoping.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Bellone is the new county executive of Suffolk County on Long Island, and, thankfully, he has opened his tenure with a more inclusive tone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suffolk County on Long Island got a new county executive this month, Steve Bellone. In his inaugural speech, he went down the list of things he intended to do, like fix the county’s budget woes, hold the line on taxes, make government more efficient, create jobs and affordable housing, and invest in “clean water infrastructure.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Day in Suffolk? Here’s Hoping', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Day in Suffolk? Here’s Hoping', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Suffolk County (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bellone, Steven', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levy, Steven A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T02:01:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/85bf9f0a-8518-5b74-b1c2-994fb3433ce4', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85bf9f0a-8518-5b74-b1c2-994fb3433ce4'}, {'abstract': 'Before a fourth killing in Orange County, Calif., an Iraq war veteran who was later arrested warned his homeless father to be careful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/us/suspect-in-killings-of-homeless-men-has-family-link-to-homelessness.html', 'snippet': 'Before a fourth killing in Orange County, Calif., an Iraq war veteran who was later arrested warned his homeless father to be careful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YORBA LINDA, Calif. — The man charged on Tuesday with the stabbing deaths four homeless men in Orange County over the last month, Itzcoatl Ocampo, has a personal connection to the area’s group of homeless: his father lives among them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/us/HOMELESS-1/HOMELESS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1020, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspect in Killings of Homeless Men Has Family Link to Homelessness', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suspect in Killings of Homeless Men Has Family Link to Homelessness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ocampo, Itzcoatl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders