ed partisan crowd at Rod Laver Arena.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — Samantha Stosur, the reigning United States Open champion, became the highest seed to fall from the Australian Open on Tuesday, losing her first-round match to Sorana Cirstea of Romania, 7-6 (2), 6-3, before a stunned partisan crowd at Rod Laver Arena.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/sports/subTENNIS/subTENNIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/17/sports/subTENNIS/subTENNIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/sports/subTENNIS/subTENNIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/sports/subTENNIS/subTENNIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/17/sports/subTENNIS/subTENNIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stosur, U.S. Open Champion, Topples Out in Melbourne', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stosur, U.S. Open Champion, Topples Out in Melbourne', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stosur, Samantha', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cirstea, Sorana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T06:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2499282-53a1-59f0-a599-25a701fdfb13', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2499282-53a1-59f0-a599-25a701fdfb13'}, {'abstract': 'The activist harnesses government agencies and organizations to combat child trafficking in northeast India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/hasina-kharbhih-raising-the-stakes-against-child-trafficking/', 'snippet': 'The activist harnesses government agencies and organizations to combat child trafficking in northeast India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hasina Kharbhih, 40, has spent the better part of her life working for human rights. She started a nonprofit, Impulse, and developed a comprehensive strategy to prevent child trafficking called the Meghalaya Model, which is being applied in eight Indian states. The activist, who is based in Shillong in the northeastern state of Meghalaya, was in Delhi earlier this month to receive a North East Excellence Award from the Indian Chamber of Commerce. The award honored her service in the field of human rights and trafficking, HIV and AIDS intervention, and for providing livelihood support for individuals in the rural areas of the northeast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hasina Kharbhih: Raising the Stakes Against Child Trafficking', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Entity for Gender Equality and the Empowerment of Women', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T07:19:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sruthi Gottipati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85ecaf21-f945-59c5-9ca2-e26b8c4b1eba', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85ecaf21-f945-59c5-9ca2-e26b8c4b1eba'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/news-quiz-jan-17-2012/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries in today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Jan. 17, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T07:19:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenan Christiansen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Christiansen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f20eb004-71a1-50ce-a60d-18ba2ccc1c05', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f20eb004-71a1-50ce-a60d-18ba2ccc1c05'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 17, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/pageoneplus/corrections-january-17.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 17, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The Ne