snippet': 'On Jan. 17, 1893, Hawaii’s monarchy was overthrown when a group of businessmen and sugar planters forced Queen Liliuokalani to abdicate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Jan. 17, 1893, Hawaii’s monarchy was overthrown when a group of businessmen and sugar planters forced Queen Liliuokalani to abdicate. The coup led to the dissolving of the Kingdom of Hawaii two years later, its annexation as a U.S. territory and eventual admission as the 50th state in the union.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jan. 17, 1893 | Hawaiian Monarchy Overthrown by America-Backed Businessmen', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T09:01:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1607aab6-59b2-5eda-9c6c-9e06ca264752', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1607aab6-59b2-5eda-9c6c-9e06ca264752'}, {'abstract': 'Can you use context clues to choose the word that best completes a sentence?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/test-yourself-english-jan-17-2012/', 'snippet': 'Can you use context clues to choose the word that best completes a sentence?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the Op-Ed article “The Rise of the New Groupthink.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Jan. 17, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T09:22:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/129cae47-b385-5fcd-b6c8-c3b0f39b6e24', 'word_count': 46, 'uri': 'nyt://article/129cae47-b385-5fcd-b6c8-c3b0f39b6e24'}, {'abstract': 'Twenty tears after leaving his homeland, Hiroyuki Ito returned to Tokyo to bury his Father. He felt out of place and sad.  “Even when the sky was clear, I kept seeing red rain, as if a filter was over my eyes.” After an intense season of loss, the red rain itself also vanished.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/red-rain-and-loss-in-tokyo/', 'snippet': 'Twenty tears after leaving his homeland, Hiroyuki Ito returned to Tokyo to bury his Father. He felt out of place and sad.  “Even when the sky was clear, I kept seeing red rain, as if a filter was over my eyes.” After an intense season of loss, the...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soon after shooting memorial concerts on the 10th anniversary of the Sept. 11 attacks, my sister called to tell me that our father had died unexpectedly. Two days later, I returned to Japan for the first time in 20 years to attend his funeral. I felt constant vertigo, like I had been violently cut and pasted from New York to Tokyo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lost and Alone Under Tokyo’s Red Rain', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokyo (Japan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T10:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroyuki Ito', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroyu