India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramdev (Swami)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T10:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f969e6ab-b2aa-5fcc-be31-2ec3a96a423a', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f969e6ab-b2aa-5fcc-be31-2ec3a96a423a'}, {'abstract': 'Some elements of President Obama’s plan to consolidate government departments make little sense, but abolishing the Small Business Administration is an excellent place to start, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/the-pros-and-cons-of-obamas-reorganization-plan/', 'snippet': 'Some elements of President Obama’s plan to consolidate government departments make little sense, but abolishing the Small Business Administration is an excellent place to start, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. He is the author of the forthcoming book “The Benefit and the Burden: Tax Reform – Why We Need It and What It Will Take.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pros and Cons of Obama’s Reorganization Plan', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T11:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0162a095-faa7-5393-a3d1-fbf925f2d244', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0162a095-faa7-5393-a3d1-fbf925f2d244'}, {'abstract': 'The action followed an investigation opened by the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration in October.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/nearly-90000-minis-recalled-for-fire-hazard/', 'snippet': 'The action followed an investigation opened by the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration in October.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After an investigation by the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration, Mini is recalling almost 89,000 of its turbocharged models because they could catch fire when the engine is off.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nearly 90,000 Minis Recalled for Fire Hazard', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recalls and Bans of Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T11:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1814de18-d2a7-5e29-b470-32d67454bd5e', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1814de18-d2a7-5e29-b470-32d67454bd5e'}, {'abstract': 'Britain’s largest modern and contemporary art show, the London Art Fair, will present works from more than 120 major galleries from Jan. 18 through Jan. 22', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/london-art-fair-to-showcase-modern-works/', 'snippet': 'Britain’s largest modern and contemporary art show, the London Art Fair, will present works from more than 120 major galleries from Jan. 18 through Jan. 22', 'lead_paragraph': 'Britain’s largest modern and contemporary art show, the London Art Fair, will present works from more than 120 major galleries from Jan. 18 through Jan. 22 at the Business Design Centre, 52 Upper Street. Novices will find themselves side-by-side with museum curators, gallery dealers and artists, all eager to see the paintings, drawings, large-scale sculpture, installations, photography and video on offer. Twenty-four thousand people attended last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Art Fair to Showcase Modern Works', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T11:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerie Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0000ada3-0e6f-57c2-9ea8-3ad4072033d2', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0000ada3-0e6f-57c2-9ea8-3ad4072033d2'}, {'abstract': 'It’s hard not to get a little nostalgic with the 49ers deep in the playoffs. In a video series, Bill Walsh, with the help of Joe Montana, explains the West Coast offense.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/49ers-nostalgia-revisiting-walsh-and-montana/', 'snippet': 'It’s hard not to get a little nostalgic with the 49ers deep in the playoffs. In a video series, Bill Walsh, with the help of Joe Montana, explains the West Coast offense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the 49ers deep in the playoffs for the first time in a long time, it’s hard not to get a little nostalgic. In the video above, Bill Walsh, with Joe Montana going over some steps, explains the West Coast offense. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '49ers Nostalgia: Revisiting Walsh and Montana', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T11:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98598e44-dfff-5d22-8635-f9bc4ff86d46', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98598e44-dfff-5d22-8635-f9bc4ff86d46'}, {'abstract': 'A handful of colleges ask for references not only from teachers and counselors — but from an applicant’s parents. The stories they tell are often insightful and at times heartbreaking.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/parents-admissions-letters/', 'snippet': 'A handful of colleges ask for references not only from teachers and counselors — but from an applicant’s parents. The stories they tell are often insightful and at times heartbreaking.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:10 p.m. | Updated Among the nearly two dozen comments this post has generated this morning is one from Sally Rubenstone, senior advisor of College Confidential, who describes her typically positive reaction when “parent letters” arrived in her in-box when she worked in admissions at Smith College.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Please Submit a Transcript, Essay and… Reference Letter From Your Dad?', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T11:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa526c0c-6492-5ff9-861c-483bb4056c8e', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa526c0c-6492-5ff9-861c-483bb4056c8e'}, {'abstract': 'Student Opinion | Do you prefer to work alone or take part in group projects at school?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/what-is-the-right-amount-of-group-work-in-school/', 'snippet': 'Student Opinion | Do you prefer to work alone or take part in group projects at school?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Group work — love it or hate it, it’s a regular part of the school or work day for many of us. Do you enjoy collaborating with your classmates on projects? Do you learn better as part of a group or by working independently? Do you prefer one style or the other? Why? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Is the Right Amount of Group Work in School?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T11:02:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63df8064-6d84-5c63-a97f-4273edcfd403', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63df8064-6d84-5c63-a97f-4273edcfd403'}, {'abstract': 'Japanese bidders led by the Sumitomo Mitsui Financial Group agreed o buy the Royal Bank of Scotland’s aircraft leasing business for $7.3 billion, the biggest divestiture yet by the British bank.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/japanese-firms-to-pay-7-3-billion-for-r-b-s-aircraft-leasing-unit/', 'snippet': 'Japanese bidders led by the Sumitomo Mitsui Financial Group agreed o buy the Royal Bank of Scotland’s aircraft leasing business for $7.3 billion, the biggest divestiture yet by the British bank.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:20 a.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japanese Firms to Pay $7.3 Billion for R.B.S. Aircraft Leasing Unit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T11:40:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/647250d1-05ab-54ea-a82f-6234bacd96d0', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/647250d1-05ab-54ea-a82f-6234bacd96d0'}, {'abstract': 'Donte Whitner’s brutal helmet-to-helmet hit against Pierre Thomas was perfectly legal. But why would a mother and father allow their son to play a sport in which that is true?', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/should-a-hit-like-whitners-be-legal/', 'snippet': 'Donte Whitner’s brutal helmet-to-helmet hit against Pierre Thomas was perfectly legal. But why would a mother and father allow their son to play a sport in which that is true?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Fifth Down reader, RM from Honolulu, sent this comment after the 49ers-Saints game:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should a  Hit Like Whitner’s Be Legal?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitner, Donte', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T11:51:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4719a726-f354-5011-891f-aa8371d429ab', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4719a726-f354-5