ct', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T14:17:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cff0f8c-06c3-56ff-9856-f3e7e4f7ceec', 'word_count': 1085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cff0f8c-06c3-56ff-9856-f3e7e4f7ceec'}, {'abstract': 'Retailers are usually quick to turn holidays into sales events, but not the day reserved to remember the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/when-freedoms-ring-isnt-a-cash-register-or-a-cellphone/', 'snippet': 'Retailers are usually quick to turn holidays into sales events, but not the day reserved to remember the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.', 'lead_paragraph': ' You would have been hard-pressed to find a New York politician or civic leader who didn’t feel duty-bound to invoke the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. on Monday, the day his birthday was observed. But there was one vital group of New Yorkers who, as usual, gave Dr. King a pass. They were those who keep this city’s commerce humming.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Freedom’s Ring Isn’t a Cash Register’s', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T14:18:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/806b2cac-a3fa-55c0-8d37-381505a687fc', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/806b2cac-a3fa-55c0-8d37-381505a687fc'}, {'abstract': 'Transcripts of conversations published in the Italian media revealed tense exchanges with the captain of the Costa Concordia, who apparently underplayed the extent of the damage to the stricken ship.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/transcripts-of-calls-to-cruise-ship-captain-published-by-italian-media/', 'snippet': 'Transcripts of conversations published in the Italian media revealed tense exchanges with the captain of the Costa Concordia, who apparently underplayed the extent of the damage to the stricken ship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | 1:54 p.m. In a testy, dramatic conversation late Friday night, an Italian coast guard official ordered the captain of the sinking Costa Concordia to return to the stricken cruise ship. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Confusion and Then Anger Heard in Audio Recordings of Calls to Cruise Ship Captain', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T14:23:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman and Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0df00daa-e51e-543b-84c5-9ef5f4cc439e', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0df00daa-e51e-543b-84c5-9ef5f4cc439e'}, {'abstract': 'Today Draghi, tomorrow the world.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/the-golden-age-of-impersonation/', 'snippet': 'Today Draghi, tomorrow the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the old days, impersonating someone was hard — you had to find some way to convince people in person that you were someone else, and it was especially hard if the individual you were trying to impersonate was fairly well known.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Golden Age Of Impersonation', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T14:24:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e17429a-231f-5a9a-9f1f-e3c4e39716ef', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e17429a-231f-5a9a-9f1f-e3c4e39716ef'}, {'abstract': 'Morton L. Janklow’s program aims to enhance the business skills of cultural leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/literary-agent-helps-create-training-program-at-syracuse-for-arts-leaders/', 'snippet': 'Morton L. Janklow’s program aims to enhance the business skills of cultural leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having served on several cultural boards, the literary agent Morton L. Janklow found that many arts leaders lacked basic business skills necessary to manage their institutions. So he has spearheaded a new master’s of arts degree program at Syracuse University, which is to be announced Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Literary Agent Helps Create Training Program at Syracuse for Arts Leaders', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levin, Kate D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowry, Glenn D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walters, Barbara', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syracuse University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syracuse (NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T14:26:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98436289-ab89-5c42-a648-a71a23673b14', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98436289-ab89-5c42-a648-a71a23673b14'}, {'abstract': 'China’s urban population exceeded its rural population in 2011 for the first time in the nation’s history, a government agency reported.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/world/asia/majority-of-chinese-now-live-in-cities.html', 'snippet': 'China’s urban population exceeded its rural population in 2011 for the first time in the nation’s history, a government agency reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — China’s urban population exceeded its rural population in 2011 for the first time in the nation’s history, the government’s National Bureau of Statistics reported, continuing a trend that has helped drive its rapid economic growth but poses an increasingly difficult social transition for scores of millions of Chinese. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/world/SHANGHAI-FLOATER/SHANGHAI-FLOATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/18/world/SHANGHAI-FLOATER/SHANGHAI-FLOATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/world/SHANGHAI-FLOATER/SHANGHAI-FLOATER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/world/SHANGHAI-FLOATER/SHANGHAI-FLOATER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/18/world/SHANGHAI-FLOATER/SHANGHAI-FLOATER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Majority of Chinese Now Live in Cities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Majority of Chinese Now Live in Cities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T14:27:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': No