imes.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/tuesday-reading-daily-aspirin-may-not-be-for-everyone/', 'snippet': 'Daily aspirin may not be for everyone, selling boarding perks to forlorn fliers, colleges seek letters of recommendation from mom and dad, and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Daily Aspirin May Not Be for Everyone', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T14:36:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4790582-3fd8-5948-89c6-b328707c0677', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4790582-3fd8-5948-89c6-b328707c0677'}, {'abstract': 'Philipp Petzschner wanted a triple bagel at the Australian Open. He came close.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/petzschners-bid-for-punishing-perfection-falls-just-short/', 'snippet': 'Philipp Petzschner wanted a triple bagel at the Australian Open. He came close.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia–All Philipp Petzschner wanted was perfection. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Petzschner’s Bid for Punishing Perfection Falls Just Short', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_