5c25-b713-16df0585b1f2', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caafb94f-e649-5c25-b713-16df0585b1f2'}, {'abstract': 'George Harrison’s estate is working with an application publisher to create a virtual showroom of his personal trove of guitars that will show off the instruments and use many of his personal recordings.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/look-at-them-all-george-harrisons-guitar-collection-gets-ipad-app/', 'snippet': 'George Harrison’s estate is working with an application publisher to create a virtual showroom of his personal trove of guitars that will show off the instruments and use many of his personal recordings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though it has been some years since their owner left this plane of existence, the guitars of George Harrison need not weep for loneliness or lack of use: they are about to be shown off and shared in a new iPad app planned for release next month. On Tuesday the George Harrison estate said that it was working with Bandwdth Publishing, which makes applications for mobile devices, to create a virtual showroom of that singer-songwriter’s trove of guitars that will make use of many of his personal recordings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look at Them All: George Harrison’s Guitar Collection Gets iPad App', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guitars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrison, George', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Brien, Conan", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T15:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1059789-0095-54ed-a537-47494f70f290', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1059789-0095-54ed-a537-47494f70f290'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Harrison plays tough but loses to Andy Murray at the Australian Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/harrison-falls-to-murray-in-four-sets/', 'snippet': 'Ryan Harrison plays tough but loses to Andy Murray at the Australian Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia – Andy Murray of Britain overcame a faltering start to eliminate Ryan Harrison of the United States, 5-7, 6-3, 6-4, 6-2 in a first-round match at the 2012 Australian Open.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harrison Falls to Murray in Four Sets', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T15:20:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN MARTIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MARTIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbc2cffe-972a-59d5-91be-a4ff49d741f0', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbc2cffe-972a-59d5-91be-a4ff49d741f0'}, {'abstract': 'Walid Chammah is not the only executive to recently announce plans to leave Morgan Stanley. The bank’s former chief, John J. Mack,  with whom Mr. Chammah was seen as aligned, retired last year.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/walid-chammah-to-retire-from-morgan-stanley/', 'snippet': 'Walid Chammah is not the only executive to recently announce plans to leave Morgan Stanley. The bank’s former chief, John J. Mack,  with whom Mr. Chammah was seen as aligned, retired last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walid A. Chammah, the chairman of Morgan Stanley International, is retiring, according to a memorandum sent on Tuesday to employees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walid Chammah to Retire From Morgan Stanley', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorman, James P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T15:21:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6708ca2-85b6-5d80-988d-20a46954e04b', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6708ca2-85b6-5d80-988d-20a46954e04b'}, {'abstract': 'Ford’s new fall collection was surprisingly neutral in comparison to brighter seasons past.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/milan-top-5-tom-ford-2/', 'snippet': 'Ford’s new fall collection was surprisingly neutral in comparison to brighter seasons past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tom Ford was in town to present a new fall collection that was surprisingly neutral in comparison to brighter seasons past. The handpicked house models walked around the hyper-elegant and intimate showroom so that the clothes’ most tactile qualities could be properly appreciated. Argentine coyote, which has a rougher texture that Ford prefers, topped the lapels of this luxurious tweed coat worn with the softest buttoned knit and a checked, pleated trouser, all in toffee brown tones.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milan Top 5 | Tom Ford', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T15:30:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59190d87-9b2b-54b5-83a3-b5ea25c6063b', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59190d87-9b2b-54b5-83a3-b5ea25c6063b'}, {'abstract': 'The race is on to prevent the escape of fuel or other pollutants from the capsized Costa Concordia cruise ship.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/on-our-radar-ships-sinking-stirs-environmental-fears/', 'snippet': 'The race is on to prevent the escape of fuel or other pollutants from the capsized Costa Concordia cruise ship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With an estimated 2,380 metric tons of fuel on board, the wrecked Costa Concordia cruise ship is “an ecological time bomb,” the mayor of the Tuscan island of Giglio said. The waters are treasured by divers. A Dutch salvage vessel is expected to start removing the ship’s fuel within days; the process could take two to four weeks. [The Guardian]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Capsized Ship Stirs Environmental Worries', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T15:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7ea65f4-ec12-5d7a-b3a8-cf6fff497037', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7ea65f4-ec12-5d7a-b3a8-cf6fff497037'}, {'abstract': 'The actor and director describe shooting their film “The Grey” in the frozen Canadian tundra, and talk about what they really think of each other.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000002966525/timestalks-neeson-carnahan-preview.html', 'snippet': 'The actor and director describe shooting their film “The Grey” in the frozen Canadian tundra, and talk about what they really think of each other.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The actor and director describe shooting their film “The Grey” in the frozen Canadian tundra, and talk about what they really think of each other.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/multimedia/tt-neeson/tt-neeson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/06/26/multimedia/tt-neeson/tt-neeson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/multimedia/tt-neeson/tt-neeson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/06/26/multimedia/tt-neeson/tt-neeson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'captio