': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b0e7336-3290-592f-bbf4-3aa8d5883b54', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b0e7336-3290-592f-bbf4-3aa8d5883b54'}, {'abstract': 'The organizers also set April 26 as the cutoff date for Broadway shows to open and be considered eligible for Tony nominations and awards.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/a-date-for-the-tony-awards/', 'snippet': 'The organizers also set April 26 as the cutoff date for Broadway shows to open and be considered eligible for Tony nominations and awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 66th annual Tony Awards ceremony will be held on Sunday, June 10, at the Beacon Theater in New York and broadcast live on CBS, organizers of the ceremony announced on Tuesday. The Tonys are the best-known awards for Broadway musicals and plays, voted on by hundreds of producers, tour presenters, directors and others in the theater industry. (Off Broadway and regional shows are not eligible.) The organizers also set April 26 as the cutoff date for Broadway shows to open and be eligible for Tony nominations and awards; the nominations are expected to be announced the week of April 30.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Date for the Tony Awards', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beacon Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T15:38:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e6510d3-a99c-5413-8fcc-50dcac1dea09', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e6510d3-a99c-5413-8fcc-50dcac1dea09'}, {'abstract': 'A shortened N.B.A. season features a lot of bad teams — and even the good teams are playing bad basketball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/sports/bring-back-the-lockout.html', 'snippet': 'A shortened N.B.A. season features a lot of bad teams — and even the good teams are playing bad basketball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We interrupt this N.F.L. playoff season with the disturbing news that the N.B.A. season is going on. While the conclusion of the league’s shameful lockout did bring a few benefits, including festive Christmas Day openers and a blissfully shortened season, it turns out the benefits quickly developed downsides. Christmas Day was, alas, only one day. And the blissfully shortened season came with a microscopic preseason, creating teams with all the organization of New Jersey traffic, and has been condensed like a can of tomato soup. There are games on top of games on top of games, all held together by xanthan gum. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/sports/18leading1/18leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 741, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/sports/18leading1/18leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/18/sports/18leading1/18leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bring Back the Lockout!', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bring Back the Lockout!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T15:40:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6fdb7c1-aa29-5bf7-88e1-45b9f5a515ae', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6fdb7c1-aa29-5bf7-88e1-45b9f5a515ae'}, {'abstract': 'On the set of “Star Wars,” “Raiders of the Lost Ark” and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/17/magazine/22lucas.html', 'snippet': 'On the set of “Star Wars,” “Raiders of the Lost Ark” and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the set of “Star Wars,” “Raiders of the Lost Ark” and more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/magazine/22lucas-slide-5I3X/22lucas-slide-5I3X-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 822, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/17/magazine/22lucas-slide-5I3X/22lucas-slide-5I3X-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/17/magazine/22lucas-slide-5I3X/22lucas-slide-5I3X-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'George Lucas, Hitmaker', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucas, George', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value':