-510d-a497-40b251aee53b', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c274412b-42b8-510d-a497-40b251aee53b'}, {'abstract': 'The American Cinema Editors revealed their nominations, including two for films overlooked by the Golden Globes: “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo” and “Bridesmaids.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/dragon-tattoo-and-bridesmaids-earn-editors-nods/', 'snippet': 'The American Cinema Editors revealed their nominations, including two for films overlooked by the Golden Globes: “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo” and “Bridesmaids.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — “The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo” and “Bridesmaids” may have been shut out at the Golden Globes, but they are still very much a part of the Oscar conversation, as evidenced by the American Cinema Editors nominations, announced on Monday. Both films made the cut, along with other Oscar favorites like “The Descendants,” “Hugo,” “The Artist,” “Midnight in Paris,” “Moneyball” and “War Horse,” which has otherwise been faltering lately. An editing award is considered a must for a best-picture win at the Oscars – no film has received that top prize without at least an editing nomination since 1981 – and the editors’ group has a lot of overlap with the Academy voters in its membership, so its choices are usually an above-average predictor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Dragon Tattoo’ and ‘Bridesmaids’ Earn Editors’ Nods', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T16:07:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f165d084-434d-5a03-b749-82406bf547e2', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f165d084-434d-5a03-b749-82406bf547e2'}, {'abstract': 'The nephew of Ayrton Senna is joining the team for which his uncle was driving when he was killed in a racing accident in 1994.', 'web_url': 'https://formulaone.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/bruno-senna-joins-williams-team/', 'snippet': 'The nephew of Ayrton Senna is joining the team for which his uncle was driving when he was killed in a racing accident in 1994.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Williams announced Tuesday that Bruno Senna would drive for the team in 2012. The announcement carried far more emotional undertone than any other so far this year as Williams was the team for which Senna’s uncle, Ayrton Senna, was driving when he was killed in a crash at the San Marino Grand Prix in Imola, Italy, in 1994. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bruno Senna Joins Williams Team', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrichello, Rubens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heidfeld, Nick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Senna, Ayrton', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Frank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WilliamsF1', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T16:07:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brad Spurgeon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spurgeon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://arti