 before its stand-up performers were chosen by Eddie Brill, a stand-up comedian who is a respected and contentious figure in his field.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/late-show-replaces-its-longtime-comedy-booker/', 'snippet': 'The CBS late-night program is returning to a system it used before its stand-up performers were chosen by Eddie Brill, a stand-up comedian who is a respected and contentious figure in his field.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:05 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Late Show’ Replaces Its Longtime Comedy Booker', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brill, Eddie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Letterman, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T17:32:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a28b4c6-c7e0-5110-bbaa-4954e28d6bf2', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a28b4c6-c7e0-5110-bbaa-4954e28d6bf2'}, {'abstract': 'Advertisers distributed more than 272 billion coupons in free-standing inserts in 2011, according to a report from Kantar Media, a decline of 6.5 percent from 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/business/media/accounts-and-people-of-note-in-the-ad-industry.html', 'snippet': 'Advertisers distributed more than 272 billion coupons in free-standing inserts in 2011, according to a report from Kantar Media, a decline of 6.5 percent from 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Advertisers distributed more than 272 billion coupons in free-standing inserts in 2011, according to a report from Kantar Media, part of WPP, a decline of 6.5 percent from 2010. The drop came after two years of increases, of 8 percent in 2009 and 7.2 percent in 2010. The amount of promotion pages from retailers that appeared in the inserts, which are typically carried in Sunday newspapers, rose 30.7 percent last year compared with 2010, the report said; the retailers included Walmart, Dollar General, Target and Walgreens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Ad Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Webdenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T17:32:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f23652fa-7824-5dbd-a77c-a429a6fc0631', 'word_count': 1644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f23652fa-7824-5dbd-a77c-a429a6fc0631'}, {'abstract': 'A Dutch marine salvage company is preparing to pump half a million gallons of fuel from the stricken Costa Concordia cruise liner, the first step toward determining whether to save or scrap it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/science/salvage-efforts-begin-for-capsized-cruise-ship-costa-concordia.html', 'snippet': 'A Dutch marine salvage company is preparing to pump half a million gallons of fuel from the stricken Costa Concordia cruise liner, the first step toward determining whether to save or scrap it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Dutch marine salvage company prepared on Tuesday to begin pumping half a million gallons of fuel from the stricken cruise ship Costa Concordia, the first step toward hauling the luxury liner away for a complete overhaul or cutting it up for scrap.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ship Salvage Workers Roll Up Their Sleeves', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ship Salvage Workers Roll Up Their Sleeves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Costa Crociere SpA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salvage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruises', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tuscany (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T17:33:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Fountain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fountain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55b8550a-5b68-5a52-b2e3-436c5f32b632', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55b8550a-5b68-5a52-b2e3-436c5f32b632'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations Security Council renewed discussions about the Syrian conflict but appeared no closer to a diplomatic breakthrough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/world/middleeast/new-wave-of-killings-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations Security Council renewed discussions about the Syrian conflict but appeared no closer to a diplomatic breakthrough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Violence surged in Syria on Tuesday as activists reported that at least 34 people had been killed in several towns and cities across the country, including six soldiers who had defected and three members of the security forces.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Least 34 People Killed in Syria as Monitors Are Unable to Quell Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Least 34 People Killed in Syria as Monitors Are Unable to Quell Violence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T17:41:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Bakri', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakri', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f79147e5-d778-55d2-9c6f-bd4dec59f63b', 'word_count': 969, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f79147e5-d778-55d2-9c6f-bd4dec59f63b'}, {'abstract': 'A compendium of G.O.P. punch lines from the South Carolina debate.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/the-south-carolina-debate-and-gop-golden-oldies/', 'snippet': 'A compendium of G.O.P. punch lines from the South Carolina debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The people of South Carolina should be grateful. The Republicans competing for their party’s nomination are subjecting them to only two of the carnival sideshows that pass for presidential debates. The first was Monday night and the second will be on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The South Carolina Debate and G.O.P. Golden Oldies', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T17:44:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d64ff40-6b43-51d5-a1a5-b50861fbb292', 'word_count': 688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d64ff40-6b43-51d5-a1a5-b50861fbb292'}, {'abstract': 'Laurie Jon Moran worked at Le Manoir aux Quat’Saisons near Oxford, England, Daniel and  Per Se.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/a-new-pastry-chef-for-le-bernardin/', 'snippet': 'Laurie Jon Moran worked at Le Manoir aux Quat’Saisons near Oxford, England, Daniel and  Per Se.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Ripert, the exectuive chef and a partner in Le Bernardin, has hired Laurie Jon Moran as its new pastry chef. He replaces Michael Laiskonis, who left, as planned, on Dec. 31 to pursue opportunites outside the restaurant world. Mr. Moran, 30, is from England, where he worked at Le Manoir aux Quat’Saisons near Oxford, before joining Daniel here. Most recently he was pastry sous-chef at Per Se. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Pastry Chef for Le Bernardin', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T17:51:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5241afa6-2d7c-5dc3-8f35-c6a02e96968d', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5241afa6-2d7c-5dc3-8f35-c6a02e96968d'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Cotter, the founder of a motorsports public relations firm and the author of several books, is charged with executing the plan for a grand prix in New Jersey in 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/former-marketing-executive-to-lead-formula-one-grand-prix-into-new-jersey/', 'snippet': 'Tom Cotter, the founder of a motorsports public relations firm and the author of several books, is charged with executing the plan for a grand prix in New Jersey in 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tom Cotter, a former motorsports marketing entrepreneur who has worked as an automotive writer for the last decade, was named the president of the Formula One Grand Prix of America at Port Imperial on Tuesday. He will be charged with executing the contract to bring a Formula One race to New Jersey in June 2013.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Marketing Executive to Lead Formula One Grand Prix Into New Jersey', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'ke