yt://article/258cd7bb-529b-5e93-982c-1a7c7854911a'}, {'abstract': 'Yemen’s foreign minister, Abu Bakr al-Qirbi, said that it would be “difficult” to hold the elections on Feb. 21 as planned, adding to fears of a worsening political crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/world/middleeast/yemeni-official-hints-at-election-delay.html', 'snippet': 'Yemen’s foreign minister, Abu Bakr al-Qirbi, said that it would be “difficult” to hold the elections on Feb. 21 as planned, adding to fears of a worsening political crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Adding to fears of a worsening political crisis in Yemen, a top government official hinted at a possible delay in presidential elections set for February that would mark the formal end of President Ali Abdullah Saleh’s 33-year rule.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/18/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/world/YEMEN/YEMEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemeni Official Suggests Delay in Presidential Vote', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yemeni Official Suggests Delay in Presidential Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleh, Ali Abdullah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T18:23:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12c23c77-6236-56ef-aec3-c9a1f12bfeb1', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12c23c77-6236-56ef-aec3-c9a1f12bfeb1'}, {'abstract': 'Aabar Investments, an investment vehicle for Abu Dhabi’s sovereign wealth fund, said on Tuesday that it would increase its stake in Italian bank UniCredit to 6.5 percent as UniCredit is expected to gain investor backing to raise 7.5 billion euros, or $9.6 billion, in a so-called rights offering.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/unicredit-gaining-investor-support-for-9-6-billion-rights-issue/', 'snippet': 'Aabar Investments, an investment vehicle for Abu Dhabi’s sovereign wealth fund, said on Tuesday that it would increase its stake in Italian bank UniCredit to 6.5 percent as UniCredit is expected to gain investor backing to raise 7.5 billion euros,...', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Aabar Investments, an investment vehicle for Abu Dhabi’s sovereign wealth fund, said on Tuesday that it would increase its stake in the Italian bank UniCredit to 6.5 percent from 5 percent after the Milan-based firm completes a so-called rights offering at the end of the month. The deal would make Aabar the largest individual investor in UniCredit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'UniCredit Gaining Investor Support for $9.6 Billion Rights Issue', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aabar Investments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Unicredito Italiano SpA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T18:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6086474b-f001-526c-b865-294c7c3ed56f', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6086474b-f001-526c-b865-294c7c3ed56f'}, {'abstract': 'The bonus caps reflect the difficulties that new financial regulations and the debt turmoil in Europe have posed to Morgan Stanley and its rival firms.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/morgan-stanley-to-cap-cash-bonuses-at-125000/', 'snippet': 'The bonus caps reflect the difficulties that new financial regulations and the debt turmoil in Europe have posed to Morgan Stanley and its rival firms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Morgan Stanley employees may want to put their kitchen renovations off until next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morgan Stanley Is Said to Cap Cash Bonuses at $125,000', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T18:29:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52682987-af0c-53c9-af0a-30cc9bfaea3c', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52682987-af0c-53c9-af0a-30cc9bfaea3c'}, {'abstract': 'In an isolated corner of Portugal, searching for Mirandese, the country’s second official language, means a new — and frugal — reason to travel.', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/in-portugal-mirandese-spoken-here-and-only-here/', 'snippet': 'In an isolated corner of Portugal, searching for Mirandese, the country’s second official language, means a new — and frugal — reason to travel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An old woman in a plain gray dress and a shopping bag full of oblong orange squashes called out to me from down the street. I had no idea what she was saying – and that couldn’t have made me happier. After all, I had come to her rural village – Malhadas, in the northeast corner of Portugal – with the specific hope of not understanding anyone. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Portugal, Mirandese Spoken Here — and Only Here', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portugal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T18:34:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 't