, 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T19:03:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5eba8b90-fd8b-5f35-a86b-8b226c3347bd', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5eba8b90-fd8b-5f35-a86b-8b226c3347bd'}, {'abstract': 'The play about the rivalry and friendship between Larry Bird and Magic Johnson has a Broadway theater and a complete cast.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/magicbird-to-land-at-the-longacre-theater/', 'snippet': 'The play about the rivalry and friendship between Larry Bird and Magic Johnson has a Broadway theater and a complete cast.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Magic/Bird,” Eric Simonson’s play about the rivalry and friendship between Larry Bird, the former Boston Celtics forward, and Magic Johnson, the Los Angeles Lakers point guard, has a Broadway theater and a complete cast. The play, to be directed by Thomas Kail, will open on April 11 at the Longacre Theater, the show’s producers announced Tuesday. Previews begin March 21.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Magic/Bird’ To Land at the Longacre Theater', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bird, Larry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Earvin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kail, Thomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simonson, Eric', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Lakers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T19:04:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38b587c4-bd38-5d0a-b9dc-e97a73607620', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38b587c4-bd38-5d0a-b9dc-e97a73607620'}, {'abstract': 'Vijay Kumar Singh, India’s Army chief, says he is 60. Officials records say he is 61. At stake is his ability to stay in his post.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/world/asia/india-army-chief-vijay-kumar-singh-disputes-age.html', 'snippet': 'Vijay Kumar Singh, India’s Army chief, says he is 60. Officials records say he is 61. At stake is his ability to stay in his post.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Certainly, India’s army already has plenty to keep it busy. To the northeast lies China, which is quietly but rapidly expanding its military presence along the border. To the northwest lies nuclear-armed Pakistan, which has already fought three wars with India and is now wobbling with political instability. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/world/INDIA/INDIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/18/world/INDIA/INDIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/world/INDIA/INDIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 566, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/world/INDIA/INDIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/18/world/INDIA/INDIA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For India’s Army, Age Dispute Rattles Leadership', 'kicker': 'Memo From New Delhi', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For India’s Army, Dispute Over Chief’s Age Rattles Leadership', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T19:08:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a18b662-2ce8-5b6a-9f64-0295e78de7de', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a18b662-2ce8-5b6a-9f64-0295e78de7de'}, {'abstract': 'Vernon Davis and Rob Gronkowski joined Kellen Winslow on the list of greatest performances by a tight end in a postseason game. But Winslow’s big day may still be the best of the bunch.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/daviss-performance-recalls-winslows-epic-day/', 'snippet': 'Vernon Davis and Rob Gronkowski joined Kellen Winslow on the list of greatest performances by a tight end in a postseason game. But Winslow’s big day may still be the best of the bunch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is fitting that in the Year of the Tight End, two of the greatest postseason performances by a player at that position would occur.', 'source': 'The N