one}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1060134-d031-57cb-8637-069efd37be6a', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1060134-d031-57cb-8637-069efd37be6a'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmaker-stars of “Declaration of War,” France’s foreign-language Oscar entry, based their tale of an infant with a tumor on the story of their older son.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/frances-oscar-hopes-depend-on-its-health-care-system/', 'snippet': 'The filmmaker-stars of “Declaration of War,” France’s foreign-language Oscar entry, based their tale of an infant with a tumor on the story of their older son.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Other than Italy, no country has a better track record with the Academy Award for best foreign-language film than France, which has received 36 nominations and 12 Oscars (with 27 and 13 for Italy). But last year’s competition was disappointing for the French: the highly acclaimed “Of Gods and Men,” which won the Grand Prix at Cannes, failed even to make the shortlist, while an Algerian film set in France and spoken largely in French, “Outside the Law,” was one of the five finalists.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France’s Oscar Hopes Depend on Its Health Care System', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T19:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/542eef1f-79e8-58a4-a2c1-a4520af7d102', 'word_count': 1264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/542eef1f-79e8-58a4-a2c1-a4520af7d102'}, {'abstract': 'What have you learned from people outside your professional sphere?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/what-start-ups-can-learn-from-a-crime-boss/', 'snippet': 'What have you learned from people outside your professional sphere?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What lurks in the hearts of mild-mannered software developers? Donald DeSantis’s answer may surprise you. The 29-year-old Seattle techie recently penned a tale of unlikely inspiration called “Everything I need to know about start-ups, I learned from a crime boss.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Start-Ups Can Learn From a Crime Boss', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mentors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T20:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Bruder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b41d8e81-e1a2-5776-8cd7-d590c77f0957', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b41d8e81-e1a2-5776-8cd7-d590c77f0957'}, {'abstract': 'The income inequality debate is about to get more personal.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/mitt-romneys-taxes/', 'snippet': 'The income inequality debate is about to get more personal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having suggested at Monday night’s debate that he would release his 2011 tax returns in April, Mitt Romney must have realized he would need to inoculate himself against the inevitable public backlash over his annual income, where it comes from and how little tax he pays on it. He started this process Tuesday morning, when he told reporters in South Carolina that his effective tax rate is about 15 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitt Romney’s Taxes', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffett, Warren E', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T20:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/791d0678-54e2-52e1-934c-b7b2b7300812', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/791d0678-54e2-52e1-934c-b7b2b7300812'}, {'abstract': 'Danilo Scarpati’s Milan fashion week photo diary.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/photos-of-the-moment-brioni/', 'snippet': 'Danilo Scarpati’s Milan fashion week photo diary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of the Moment | Brioni', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-17T20:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danilo Scarpati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danilo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scarpati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'ro