1263492d-3cbe-5698-a758-134d3a0221bc'}, {'abstract': 'The World Series winners from St. Louis are honored at the White House on the day Michelle Obama turns 48.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/cardinals-and-the-first-lady-celebrate/', 'snippet': 'The World Series winners from St. Louis are honored at the White House on the day Michelle Obama turns 48.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The St. Louis Cardinals were at the White House on Tuesday to celebrate their World Series championship but shared the moment with Michelle Obama – an avowed Chicago Cubs fan – to mark her 48th birthday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cardinals and the First Lady Celebrate', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T01:51:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/636dfc18-a3ee-57bb-a76f-69133bf1f87a', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/636dfc18-a3ee-57bb-a76f-69133bf1f87a'}, {'abstract': 'The co-founder of the once-dominant Web portal left as the company undergoes a wrenching examination of its future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/technology/jerry-yang-chief-yahoo-steps-down-from-board.html', 'snippet': 'The co-founder of the once-dominant Web portal left as the company undergoes a wrenching examination of its future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Jerry Yang has left Yahoo, the stumbling Internet company he co-founded 17 years ago, the company announced Tuesday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedi