le/871fc388-b1cb-59e9-b2bd-eb1617b8ab65', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/871fc388-b1cb-59e9-b2bd-eb1617b8ab65'}, {'abstract': 'Someone lend Chris Handman a jack. He’s going to need it.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/17/frolicker/', 'snippet': 'Someone lend Chris Handman a jack. He’s going to need it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY’S PUZZLE — Yes, I know. Chris Handman did not, technically speaking, add a SPARE TIRE or even a TIRE to each of the starred entries as the payoff at 64 Across indicates. He added the letters T, I, R, and E to each of the entries (Update: this is a correction to my previous statement that there was an S in the theme entries), but taken in the aggregate, and looked at through the forgiving lens of artistic license, I believe he pulled this theme off very well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday: Bewhiskered Frolicker', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T03:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93342ec7-16eb-5e98-b394-2d069ecf3277', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93342ec7-16eb-5e98-b394-2d069ecf3277'}, {'abstract': 'A new production of Athol Fugard’s “Road to Mecca” stars Rosemary Harris as a sculptor in 1970s South Africa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/theater/reviews/road-to-mecca-at-american-airlines-theater-review.html', 'snippet': 'A new production of Athol Fugard’s “Road to Mecca” stars Rosemary Harris as a sculptor in 1970s South Africa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Rosemary Harris says the word, “darkness” is a thing with tentacles that clutch and choke and smother. It erupts from her with a soul-deep rumble late in the first act of Athol Fugard’s “Road to Mecca,” which opened on Tuesday night at the American Airlines Theater. And once Ms. Harris has said “darkness”— or said it that way — it’s impossible to look on her character or the play in which she appears with the comfort of detachment.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/arts/ROAD/ROAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/18/arts/ROAD/ROAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/arts/ROAD/ROAD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/arts/ROAD/ROAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/18/arts/ROAD/ROAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Those Who Seek to Make Art Often Find Themselves Alone', 'kicker': "Theater Review | 'The Road to Mecca' ", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Those Who Seek to Make Art Often Find Themselves Alone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fugard, Athol', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roundabout Theater Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Rosemary', 'rank': 3, 'major': '