closed temporarily while officials investigated a device thrown from a crowd of protesters affiliated with the Occupy movement.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/smoke-bomb-tossed-over-fence-at-white-house/', 'snippet': 'The north entrance to the White House was closed temporarily while officials investigated a device thrown from a crowd of protesters affiliated with the Occupy movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A smoke bomb was lobbed over the north fence of the White House on Tuesday night from a crowd of protesters affiliated with the Occupy movement participating in demonstrations aimed at lawmakers returning for the next session of Congress. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smoke Bomb Tossed Over Fence at White House', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White House (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T06:55:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09a1aef8-3399-5c56-bf15-b413311aac57', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09a1aef8-3399-5c56-bf15-b413311aac57'}, {'abstract': 'Christina McHale used patience, agile footwork and booming groundstrokes to rally from behind on Wednesday to defeat Marina Erakovic in three sets at the 2012 Australian Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/mchales-patience-propels-her-into-third-round/', 'snippet': 'Christina McHale used patience, agile footwork and booming groundstrokes to rally from behind on Wednesday to defeat Marina Erakovic in three sets at the 2012 Australian Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia – Trailing by a set and surrounded by about 100 fans encouraging her opponent to “Put her away!”, Christina McHale of the United States worked her way back from the brink of defeat on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McHale’s Patience Propels Her Into Third Round', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T08:04:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN MARTIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MARTIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebda07f2-064f-5014-a8d8-428d390b93e6', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebda07f2-064f-5014-a8d8-428d390b93e6'}, {'abstract': 'The author’s appearance at the Jaipur Literary Festival remains a mystery.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/rushdies-uncertain-date-with-jaipur/', 'snippet': 'The author’s appearance at the Jaipur Literary Festival remains a mystery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Will Salman Rushdie show up or won’t he? That is the question everyone is asking days ahead of the Jaipur Literature Festival, which starts on Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rushdie’s Uncertain Date With Jaipur', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': '