ial aid. But on Wednesday the network is launching a Facebook application to help students efficiently navigate the financial aid morass.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MTV’s Latest Facebook App is About Scholarships, Not Snooki', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'College Board', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T11:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/767f0709-3b32-5040-8fc3-f3900b93f70f', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/767f0709-3b32-5040-8fc3-f3900b93f70f'}, {'abstract': 'A cement scientist has developed a high-gloss, chromelike material that bonds to aluminum, protecting it from scratches and the dulling effects of oxidation.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/from-m-i-t-a-chromeless-response-to-chromes-drawbacks/', 'snippet': 'A cement scientist has developed a high-gloss, chromelike material that bonds to aluminum, protecting it from scratches and the dulling effects of oxidation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chrome, that onetime ubiquitous detailing material with the come-hither glint, is making a comeback, if not in its original form.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From M.I.T., a Chromeless Response to Chrome’s Drawbacks', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T11:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tudor Van Hampton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tudor', 'middlename': 'Van', 'lastname': 'Hampton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3b71d09-d03d-51cd-a58f-bd5738bc354b', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3b71d09-d03d-51cd-a58f-bd5738bc354b'}, {'abstract': 'Using the alt-tab combination on Windows (or command-tab on Macs) allows you to quickly jump from one application to another.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/tip-of-the-week-easy-app-switching-on-your-pc/', 'snippet': 'Using the alt-tab combination on Windows (or command-tab on Macs) allows you to quickly jump from one application to another.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Do you have a bunch of programs open on a PC or Mac and want to switch around between them without fumbling for the mouse? On a Windows system, just hold down the Alt key while pressing the Tab key to see a box showing your open windows and applications. Keep holding down the Alt key while pressing the Tab key to cycle through the icons and let go when you get to the program or window you want to use. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Easy Switching Among Programs', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'k