arters in their final regular-season game?', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/giants-playing-like-2010-packers/', 'snippet': 'Should the Packers have played Aaron Rodgers and some other starters in their final regular-season game?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Serving up links as the Giants-Niners and Patriots-Ravens games approach:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Playing Like 2010 Packers', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T12:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8455344b-1034-5019-833c-77e70adc418d', 'word_count': 657, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8455344b-1034-5019-833c-77e70adc418d'}, {'abstract': 'A new New York Times/CBS News poll shows Mitt Romney drawing support from critical Republican base groups around the country.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/romney-holds-solid-lead-over-rivals/', 'snippet': 'A new New York Times/CBS News poll shows Mitt Romney drawing support from critical Republican base groups around the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney has solidified a sizable coalition of Republican primary voters nationwide over his rivals for the G.O.P. nomination, fracturing key blocs of the party’s base, according to the latest New York Times/CBS News poll. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Holds Solid Lead Over Rivals', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS News', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T12:04:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allison Kopicki', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kopicki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35224fda-5b18-5fef-9d7c-8e6ffd6efc2a', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35224fda-5b18-5fef-9d7c-8e6ffd6efc2a'}, {'abstract': 'President Jacob Zuma blames the West for the African Union’s weaknesses and poor relations with the United Nations, but he is also responsible.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/south-africa-must-recognize-its-role-in-african-union-problems/', 'snippet': 'President Jacob Zuma blames the West for the African Union’s weaknesses and poor relations with the United Nations, but he is also responsible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHANNESBURG — President Jacob Zuma of South Africa gave an unusual speech at the U.N. Security Council last week. In a plea for better relations between the United Nations and the African Union, he blamed the West for the weakness of the ties between the two organizations. Citing the intervention in Libya last spring, he accused NATO of running roughshod over the African Union’s preferences for how to prevent and resolve conflicts in Africa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mind the U.N.-A.U. Gap', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuma, Jacob G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN UNION', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T12:07:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eusebius McKaiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eusebius', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKaiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b1fcc89-9f09-593d-9a9a-57b0e396b943', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b1fcc89-9f09-593d-9a9a-57b0e396b943'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of upcoming English-language literary events in Berlin.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/on-berlins-literary-calendar-for-english-speakers/', 'snippet': 'A roundup of upcoming English-language literary events in Berlin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Berlin’s rich and diverse literary scene is a crucial component of the city’s creative makeup. Since reunification, it has attracted a number of established and aspiring writers — all drawn to its openness and support for artistic expression.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Berlin’s Literary Calendar (for English-Speakers)', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carre, John Le', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickens, Charles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T12:21:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Molly Hannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Molly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e55ca53b-fc84-502b-9af8-427a3a0d0857', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e55ca53b-fc84-502b-9af8-427a3a0d0857'}, {'abstract': 'Visa, the credit card company, has added support for making wireless payments through some smartphones, which would replace its plastic cards. But wireless Visa payments will initially work at only 150,000 retail locations in the United States even though Visa has about 8 million merchants.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/visa-digital-wallet/', 'snippet': 'Visa, the credit card company, has added support for making wireless payments through some smartphones, which would replace its plastic cards. But wireless Visa payments will initially work at only 150,000 retail locations in the United States eve...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good news for people suffering from discomfort caused by sitting on a thick wallet full of credit cards and credit card receipts for a long duration: Visa, the credit card company, said it supported making wireless payments through some smartphones, though it would replace the plastic Visa cards issued by banks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/technology/18bits-mobile-payment-pic/18bits-mobile-payment-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Digital Wallet Now Available on Some Smartphones', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LG Electronics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Research In Motion Ltd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T12:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d2e4e65-05de-5f54-9a8c-afe261edfdf5', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d2e4e65-05de-5f54-9a8c-afe261edfdf5'}, {'abstract': 'A brain is not a MacBook Air, true. But there is common ground between machine and mind.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/prediction-and-the-brain-a-response/', 'snippet': 'A brain is not a MacBook Air, true. But there is common ground between machine and mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sincere thanks for all the thoughtful reactions to my post on the thrifty and predictive brain. I was cheered that so many posts found value or resonance in the piece, and I am especially grateful for the various suggestions of additional concrete examples in our daily life. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prediction and the Brain: A Response', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T12:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2a13d28-aea2-52c6-a201-172e287c4872', 'word_count': 467, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2a13d28-aea2-52c6-a201-172e287c4872'}, {'abstract': 'A start-up called Chegg that rents physical textbooks is releasing a new online service on Wednesday that lets people read electronic textbooks on iPads and computers.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/digital-textbooks-from-a-company-not-named-apple/', 'snippet': 'A start-up called Chegg that rents physical textbooks is releasing a new online service on Wednesday that lets people read electronic textbooks on iPads and computers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s an old saying that if you want to be a leader and you see a parade, jump in front of it. So it is with digital textbooks, an area that’s about to experience the high-tech equivalent of the Macy’s Thanksgiving Day Parade as Apple prepares to push into the business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/technology/18bits-ebook-post/18bits-ebook-post-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 622, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital Textbooks From a Company Not Named Apple', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T12:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e01998a-d279-5c23-a06b-ad4762c53e39', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e01998a-d279-5c23-a06b-ad4762c53e39'}, {'abstract': 'Izzy, a four-legged inspector armed with a keen sense of smell, is trained to sniff out contraband food inside baggage at Kennedy International Airport.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/cute-but-tough-with-a-nose-for-the-food-in-your-bags/', 'snippet': 'Izzy, a four-legged inspector armed with a keen sense of smell, is trained to sniff out contraband food inside baggage at Kennedy International Airport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City does not lack for exotic and specialty food shops, but perhaps the most diverse display of ever-changing imported produce can be found in what is called the grinding room in the customs area of John F. Kennedy International Airport’s Terminal 4, the major gateway for international arrivals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cute but Tough, With a Nose for the Food in Your Bags', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Immigration and Customs Enforcement (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy International Airport (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T12:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9dbe332-5ed2-530e-825a-a48b0699e289', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9dbe332-5ed2-530e-825a-a48b0699e289'}, {'abstract': 'A study commissioned by a Massachusetts state agency finds no conclusive evidence that the sounds of wind turbines affect the human balance system or cause illnesses like diabetes.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/wind-turbines-and-health-hazards/', 'snippet': 'A study commissioned by a Massachusetts state agency finds no conclusive evidence that the sounds of wind turbines affect the human balance system or cause illnesses like diabetes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no conclusive evidence so far that wind turbines are responsible for health problems ranging from balance problems to diabetes, an independent panel of health experts reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wind Turbines and Health Hazards', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Environmental Protection (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T12:40:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0069bf8-7091-5d81-95c8-e18ffb6a5bca', 'word_count': 480, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0069bf8-7091-5d81-95c8-e18ffb6a5bca'}, {'abstract': 'Since the founding of their family production company 50 years ago, the Barretos of Brazil have helped make more than 80 films.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/movies/lula-is-latest-from-the-barretos-brazils-film-family.html', 'snippet': 'Since the founding of their family production company 50 years ago, the Barretos of Brazil have helped make more than 80 films.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOMETIMES they limit themselves simply to producing movies, though on many other occasions they have also written, directed or actually filmed them. But by any standard the Barretos — Luiz Carlos and Lucy and their children, Bruno, Fábio and Paula — are the first family of cinema in Brazil.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22BARRETOS1/22BARRETOS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22BARRETOS1/22BARRETOS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth':