 The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/wednesday-reading-obesity-rates-stall-but-dont-decline/', 'snippet': 'Obesity rates stall but don’t decline, Visa’s digital wallet is available on some smartphones, Sewanee offers a four-year tuition guarantee and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and online in our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: Obesity Rates Stall, but Don’t Decline', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T14:01:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/293cd32b-ed3f-5117-bc20-5ab7078f0312', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/293cd32b-ed3f-5117-bc20-5ab7078f0312'}, {'abstract': 'If your business is struggling, here are 10 issues to consider. Not having a handle on any one of them can be disastrous.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/how-to-diagnose-whats-wrong-with-your-business/', 'snippet': 'If your business is struggling, here are 10 issues to consider. Not having a handle on any one of them can be disastrous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the years, I have met a lot of entrepreneurs who have been frustrated by low profits, lack of growth, or the stress of the never-ending demands. Many struggle with all three. While every business is different, there are common denominators. In fact, I believe there are 10. The tricky part is that failing to have a handle on just one of these areas can result in mediocre performance, a stressful existence, or ultimate and intimate failure. That is one reason the failure rate for small businesses is so high (here are some others).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Diagnose What’s Wrong With Your Business', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T14:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Goltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdf301c4-72a0-5f5f-8a36-13c3befd82da', 'word_count': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdf301c4-72a0-5f5f-8a36-13c3befd82da'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Chris Christie, seen as a potential candidate for president in 2016, and Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, another potential candidate for president, offer differing views on what kind of taxes their constituents should pay.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/christie-takes-mild-swipe-at-cuomo-on-tax-plan/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Chris Christie, seen as a potential candidate for president in 2016, and Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, another potential candidate for president, offer differing views on what kind of taxes their constituents should pay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey struck a remarkably friendly tone in his State of the State speech on Tuesday, but that didn’t stop him from taking a swipe across the Hudson River at Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo (though he did call him “my friend Andrew Cuomo”).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Christie Takes Mild Swipe at Cuomo on Tax Plan', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the State Message (NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T14:35:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zernike', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ab80fc5-d2b9-5dd5-9ecc-b15bda377033', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ab80fc5-d2b9-5dd5-9ecc-b15bda377033'}, {'abstract': 'In an unusual display of offline activism, members of the New York technology world on Wednesday gathered for a rally in Midtown to protest two controversial antipiracy bills in Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/techies-plan-to-take-sopa-prote