d his bedridden wife in 1986, was scheduled to be executed by lethal injection today in Ohio. But the Sixth Circuit court isn’t going to let that happen, which is good news for those of us who oppose capital punishment. (We also wrote on our editorial page today about the Delaware governor’s decision to commute a prisoner’s death sentence to life without parole, so there are really two bits of good news.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death Penalty Death Watch: Ohio', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frost, Gregory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T15:05:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/402e5ef3-4775-562e-a769-13811c21c6d8', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/402e5ef3-4775-562e-a769-13811c21c6d8'}, {'abstract': 'Peixe Urbano, Brazil’s first online daily deal company, has closed a round of financing with mutual funds and accounts managed by Morgan Stanley Investment Management and T. Rowe Price Associates. General Atlantic and Tiger Global Management  also participated.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/mutual-funds-invest-in-brazilian-online-deals-company/', 'snippet': 'Peixe Urbano, Brazil’s first online daily deal company, has closed a round of financing with mutual funds and accounts managed by Morgan Stanley Investment Management and T. Rowe Price Associates. General Atlantic and Tiger Global Management  also...', 'lead_paragraph': 'SÃO PAULO, Brazil — Peixe Urbano, Brazil’s first online daily deal company, has closed a series C round of financing with mutual funds and institutional accounts managed by Morgan Stanley Investment Management and T. Rowe Price Associates. General Atlantic and Tiger Global Management, who had previously backed the company, also participated. The size of investment was not disclosed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mutual Funds Invest in Brazilian Online Deals Company', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T15:20:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vinod Sreeharsha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vinod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sreeharsha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b887a95-9404-5a9b-b844-98bcde664445', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b887a95-9404-5a9b-b844-98bcde664445'}, {'abstract': 'Alanna Heiss, the founder of the gallery that became MoMA PS1, wants to recreate the collaborative art spirit of ’70s New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/fashion/the-spirit-of-youth-circa-1970-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Alanna Heiss, the founder of the gallery that became MoMA PS1, wants to recreate the collaborative art spirit of ’70s New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NOT long ago Alanna Heiss, the renowned curator and self-described art radical, brandished two guns at the Clocktower Gallery, the nonprofit art space she runs in Lower Manhattan. “They’re props,” she said with a grin, adding, “but they’re also for critics.”', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/fashion/19ZSUBUPCLOSE_SPAN/19ZSUBUPCLOSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/19/fashion/19ZSUBUPCLOSE_SPAN/19ZSUBUPCLOSE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/fashion/19ZSUBUPCLOSE_SPAN/19ZSUBUPCLOSE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/fashion/19ZSUBUPCLOSE_SPAN/19ZSUBUPCLOSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/fashion/19ZSUBUPCLOSE_SPAN/19ZSUBUPCLOSE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Spirit of Youth, Circa 1970 New York', 'kicker': 'Up Close', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Spirit Of Youth, Circa 1970 New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heiss, Alanna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MoMA PS1', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T15:23:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08c6e786-4747-5f06-8b03-ccab0c46c1f5', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08c6e786-4747-5f06-8b03-ccab0c46c1f5'}, {'abstract': 'The cause of the disease, known as Montipora White Syndrome, remains unknown. It involves the loss of tissue, which exposes the coral’s underlying white skeleton.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/on-our-radar-ailing-rice-coral-in-hawaii/', 'snippet': 'The cause of the disease, known as Montipora White Syndrome, remains unknown. It involves the loss of tissue, which exposes the coral’s underlying white skeleton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scientists have discovered an outbreak of a disease in rice coral in Kaneohe Bay off Oahu, a popular spot frequented by snorkelers, bathers, divers, boaters and fishermen. [United States Geological Survey]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Ailing Rice Coral in Hawaii', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T15:23:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/acb6d9a0-3d4c-50ea-be82-63d655f968d4', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acb6d9a0-3d4c-50ea-be82-63d655f968d4'}, {'abstract': 'The flexible singer Santigold was backed by two tough sentries and a shimmering band at Music Hall of Williamsburg on Monday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/arts/music/santigold-at-music-hall-of-williamsburg-review.html', 'snippet': 'The flexible singer Santigold was backed by two tough sentries and a shimmering band at Music Hall of Williamsburg on Monday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two tough sentries guarded Santigold at all times on Monday night.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/arts/santigold/santigold-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/19/arts/santigold/santigold-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/arts/santigold/santigold-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/arts/santigold/santigold-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/arts/santigold/santigold-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Performer Disappears Into Her Songs', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Performer Disappears Into Her Songs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T15:29:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/833aacff-8dd9-5854-abd8-6b5d530451d6', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/833aacff-8dd9-5854-abd8-6b5d530451d6'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of earnest ads extolling performances, here are “for your consideration” promos we wish studios took out.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/for-your-consideration-ads-we-wish-they-ran/', 'snippet': 'Instead of earnest ads extolling performances, here are “for your consideration” promos we wish studios took out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The “For Your Consideration” ad, paid for by studios and directed at Academy voters, started appearing in Hollywood trade publications sometime in the 1950s and are often quite elaborate, even for movies that don’t have a shot at winning an Oscar. (Michael Jordan, best actor in “Space Jam,” anyone?) As with everything Oscars related, they have their own artistry and market-tested logic. But though they are designed to promote an actor’s performance or a film’s good reception, they are not always entirely accurate. We know, you’re shocked, shocked!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Your Consideration, Ads We Wish They Ran', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T15:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e36e2123-f9d4-5e75-8b2a-7c1964486469', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e36e2123-f9d4-5e75-8b2a-7c1964486469'}, {'abstract': 'Getting through the day without a mainstay of the Web, Wikipedia, is a test for anyone who has taken for granted the information it provides daily.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/how-im-surviving-or-trying-to-without-wikipedia-at-my-fingertips/', 'snippet': 'Getting through the day without a mainstay of the Web, Wikipedia, is a test for anyone who has taken for granted the information it provides daily.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Internet is broken today. Hitting that “all known thought” button on my toolbar gives me a quick, maddening glimpse of Wikipedia that is then overtaken by a black screen that asks me to “Imagine a world without free knowledge.” I just did and I didn’t like it, now can I have my Wikipedia back?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How I’m Surviving (or Trying to) Without Wikipedia at My Fingertips', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikipedia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T15:38:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c642b03-9232-5b8e-b79b-d20b4bb6eac2', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c642b03-9232-5b8e-b79b-d20b4bb6eac2'}, {'abstract': 'A gathering of recent philosophy-related links.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/stone-links-17/', 'snippet': 'A gathering of recent philosophy-related links.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A gathering of recent philosophy-related links.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stone Links', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T15:38:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff6ef313-c5c4-52c4-8bbb-2bffe81da32c', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff6ef313-c5c4-52c4-8bbb-2bffe81da32c'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to the Internet, it’s possible for just about anyone with a spare room to post a listing for a vacation rental. Here’s an overview of several sites to help simplify your search.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/travel/vacation-rental-sites.html', 'snippet': 'Thanks to the Internet, it’s possible for just about anyone with a spare room to post a listing for a vacation rental. Here’s an overview of several sites to help simplify your search.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH hotel rates on the rise, vacation rentals are looking attractive, often providing more space and amenities for less than you would spend on a hotel. But finding that apartment in Paris or seaside cottage in Florida can be a daunting task.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22PRAC/22PRAC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 830, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22PRAC/22PRAC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22PRAC/22PRAC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Surfing for a Vacation Rental', 'kicker': 'Practical Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surfing for a Vacation Rental', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roomorama', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TripAdvisor.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HomeAway Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Airbnb', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T15:41:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e724cba6-f546-582a-ae82-000267745803', 'word_count': 1163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e724cba6-f546-582a-ae82-000267745803'}, {'abstract': 'A principal considers a conundrum in education today: That even as more schools are expected to try to put children with all different abilities into an "integrated\'\' classroom, and teachers are expected to understand that all children learn in different ways, schools still expect all children to reach the same academic goals in the same time frame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/18/of-parrots-paras-and-time/', 'snippet': 'A principal considers a conundrum in education today: That even as more schools are expected to try to put children with all different abilities into an "integrated\'\' classroom, and teachers are expected to understand that all children learn in di...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Of Parrots, Paras and Time ', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By MAXINE NODEL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maxine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'NODEL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8e70b6a-afb4-5efb-a925-c7b9c44c3e54', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8e70b6a-afb4-5efb-a925-c7b9c44c3e54'}, {'abstract': 'Liberals think so. They may be wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/are-inequality-and-immobility-identical/', 'snippet': 'Liberals think so. They may be wrong.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve written a number of posts and pieces\xa0pushing the idea that American conservatives need what I’ve called an opportunity agenda — one that focuses more on the problems of upward mobility and stagnating wages than does the current standard Republican line, but doesn’t share contemporary liberalism’s tendency to blame the struggles of downscale Americans almost entirely on the richest 1 percent. I thought I’d use this post to respond to the most plausible left-wing critique of this idea. (I’ll tackle the most plausible right-wing critique in a later post.) First, here’s Matt Yglesias, pivoting off an excellent piece by my colleague Jason DeParle to question the idea that there’s any real distinction between fighting inequality and fighting immobility:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are Inequality and Immobility Inseparable?', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T16:02:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca0e5291-6e11-5cbe-97ad-f533aec38ab6', 'word_count': 1335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca0e5291-6e11-5cbe-97ad-f533aec38ab6'}, {'abstract': 'The usually sexy Gucci guy has turned refreshingly romantic thanks to Frida Giannini.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/milan-top-5-gucci/', 'snippet': 'The usually sexy Gucci guy has turned refreshingly romantic thanks to Frida Giannini.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rich jacquard roses sprouting throughout Frida Giannini’s fall collection, an ode to the tortured prose of Wilde and Rimbaud, added a refreshingly romantic note to the usually sexy Gucci guy. A drop-shouldered, double-faced coat slouched over a low-cut sweater and scarf atop those slim floral pants, in a style Giannini describes as “Visconti grunge,” stood out most and was hardly a look for the tormented wallflower type who inspired it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milan Top 5 | Gucci', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T16:06:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e21394e5-c529-5f8a-87cb-0b30d934eef0', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e21394e5-c529-5f8a-87cb-0b30d934eef0'}, {'abstract': 'The Colts’ firing of Jim Caldwell puts the spotlight on Peyton Manning’s future while the playoff field contemplates how New England’s offense will fare against Baltimore’s defense in the A.F.C. championship game.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/leading-off-whats-next-in-indy/', 'snippet': 'The Colts’ firing of Jim Caldwell puts the spotlight on Peyton Manning’s future while the playoff field contemplates how New England’s offense will fare against Baltimore’s defense in the A.F.C. championship game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even with the surprise value of the Colts firing Coach Jim Caldwell on Tuesday ranking near zero — when you lose your quarterback to injury but the rest of the team plays like it should be hospitalized, it does not look good on a coaching\xa0résumé\xa0— it did immediately bring a much larger issue to the top of the pile. With the Colts seemingly intent on ridding all vestiges of the Peyton Manning era, what does this mean for Peyton Manning?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: What’s Next in Indy?', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belichick, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caldwell, Jim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evans, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fish, Mardy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flacco, Joe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grigson, Ryan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guerrero, Vladimir', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Irsay, Jim', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Junkin, Trey', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'val