-32 record, and were right in the thick of what would become a 26-game losing streak. LeBron James had sneaked out in the night (as much as one can “sneak out” on national television), Anderson Varejao had been ruled out for the season with an ankle injury, and Mo Williams – the Cavs’ top remaining player – had been injured just days earlier.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cavs Aren’t Terrible. How Come?', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T16:45:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By ROB MAHONEY', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MAHONEY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64e44776-56ea-56fd-b75d-f26ff2dc92ce', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64e44776-56ea-56fd-b75d-f26ff2dc92ce'}, {'abstract': 'The critics weigh in on Tuesday’s shows in Milan.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/runway-in-review-32/', 'snippet': 'The critics weigh in on Tuesday’s shows in Milan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Diesel Black GoldDesigner: Roberto LorenziDate and Location: Tuesday, Jan. 17, Via Savona, 56Photos: slide show', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Runway in Review', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T16:45:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison S. Cohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization':