'abstract': 'Tiësto, the Dutch trance music master, releases a 10-part video series that is intended to turn him into something of a reality-show star.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/a-d-j-master-talks-about-dance-music/', 'snippet': 'Tiësto, the Dutch trance music master, releases a 10-part video series that is intended to turn him into something of a reality-show star.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tiësto may be one of the older D.J.’s on the booming dance-music circuit these days, but the Dutch dance music master was one of the first musicians to prove a D.J. could compete with pop and rock acts in filling arenas. He is one of the biggest-drawing electronic acts in the world. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A D.J. Master Talks About Dance Music', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disc Jockeys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deadmau5', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skrillex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T17:17:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfad60be-de30-5004-a625-efa154222110', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfad60be-de30-5004-a625-efa154222110'}, {'abstract': 'The research is inconclusive. So why is the question of whether a woman should have an epidural when giving birth so hotly debated?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/are-the-dangers-of-epidurals-overstated/', 'snippet': 'The research is inconclusive. So why is the question of whether a woman should have an epidural when giving birth so hotly debated?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Does the question of whether or not a woman should have an epidural during the birth of her child really need to be a polarizing one? On Slate, Melinda Wenner Moyer considers the claims of both sides of the issue — all of which were impressed upon her during her pregnancy last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are the Dangers of Epidurals Overstated?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anesthesia and Anesthetics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caesarean Section', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T17:17:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e2c49c8-9643-5f50-92c2-dc228d3fa997', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e2c49c8-9643-5f50-92c2-dc228d3fa997'}, {'abstract': '“Clybourne Park,” the 2011 Pulitzer Prize winner for drama by Bruce Norris, will open on Broadway at the Walter Kerr Theater on April 12.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/clybourne-park-coming-to-broadway-in-april/', 'snippet': '“Clybourne Park,” the 2011 Pulitzer Prize winner for drama by Bruce Norris, will open on Broadway at the Walter Kerr Theater on April 12.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A critically acclaimed production of “Clybourne Park,” the 2011 Pulitzer Prize winner for drama by Bruce Norris, will open on Broadway at the Walter Kerr Theater on April 12, a spokesman for the show said on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Clybourne Park’ Coming to Broadway in April', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Clybourne Park (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norris, Bruce', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Playwrights Horizons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T17:27:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4111f6c9-8426-513f-978c-20006671e87f', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4111f6c9-8426-513f-978c-20006671e87f'}, {'abstract': 'William Burris told his fellow franchisees that they could either start paying him a franchise fee — or they could leave.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/a-franchisee-decides-to-take-charge/', 'snippet': 'William Burris told his fellow franchisees that they could either start paying him a franchise fee — or they could leave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week we published a case study about William Burris, one of 10 franchisees who learned that their Australia-based franchiser, Rent Your Boxes, had gone bankrupt. Mr. Burris, who had invested more than $100,000 to purchase three territories in the Washington area, rallied by creating a new company, Rent Our Boxes, for himself and his nine fellow franchisees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Franchisee Decides to Take Charge', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Franchises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intellectual Property', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T17:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Darren Dahl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Darren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dahl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c915b9e-57a9-58b7-9994-e766f16204f2', 'word_count': 934, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c915b9e-57a9-58b7-9994-e766f16204f2'}, {'abstract': 'The vivid, memorable show involved freshly inked models in cargo pants and military style jackets.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/milan-top-5-umit-benan/', 'snippet': 'The vivid, memorable show involved freshly inked models in cargo pants and military style jackets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The unmistakable sound of a tattoo gun could be heard coming from backstage while we waited for the start of Umit Benan’s fall show. Curiosity overtaking decorum, I popped behind the curtain to see an already inked model getting another actual tattoo, with a pretty raw arm to show for it. He was one of a group of real guys taking part in a barracks tableau, jubilantly postwar, that included a naked “soldier” showering (eventually he got dressed for his trip down the runway), a bruiser boxing and other assorted military types. It was a fine line to walk for a presentation, but it steered clear of cliché by committing wholeheartedly (and bodily) to the enactment. Though at times a bit too literal an interpretation, the clothing featured a lot of clever riffs on the theme, with the actual tattoo artist’s rig being the most clever. He wore a high-buttoned vest with oversize envelope pockets over a striped shirt and tie with cropped cargo pocket pants, and carried a military style jacket with leather sleeves. It was a vivid, memorable show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Milan Top 5 | Umit Benan', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T17:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b25f5956-5c9c-5ee2-a70e-904dfd3df94b', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b25f5956-5c9c-5ee2-a70e-904dfd3df94b'}, {'abstract': 'Buzz Feed has posted what appears to be John McCain’s entire opposition research file on Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/the-book-on-mitt/', 'snippet': 'Buzz Feed has posted what appears to be John McCain’s entire opposition research file on Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When John McCain endorsed Mitt Romney just before the New Hampshire primary, there was some tittering about all the nasty things the Senator from Arizona said about his former rival during the 2008 Republican nominating contest—like when he called Mr. Romney a “phony” in an ad. That was a little embarrassing, especially since the John McCain who ran for president, and lost, was also a “phony” hard-righter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Book on Mitt', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T17:34:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d5e0500-d3f0-59db-81d4-5a211feb37c6', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d5e0500-d3f0-59db-81d4-5a211feb37c6'}, {'abstract': 'As Mitt Romney defends his tenure at Bain Capital on the presidential campaign trail, some on Wall Street wonder how running a private equity firm compares to running the country.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/the-united-states-economy-through-a-private-equity-lens/', 'snippet': 'As Mitt Romney defends his tenure at Bain Capital on the presidential campaign trail, some on Wall Street wonder how running a private equity firm compares to running the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine how Mitt Romney would campaign if he actually ran as a private equity executive, dangerous though that may be in this era of the Tea Party and Occupy Wall Street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Debt? Bain Might Leverage It', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T17:40:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesse Eisinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesse', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eisinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c0dae21-8ad3-5aff-b2ac-8597e629b1b5', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c0dae21-8ad3-5aff-b2ac-8597e629b1b5'}, {'abstract': 'Christopher Clarey, who covers tennis for The Times and The International Herald Tribune, answers questions from readers.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/federer-murray-and-dolgopolov-answers-to-readers-questions/', 'snippet': 'Christopher Clarey, who covers tennis for The Times and The International Herald Tribune, answers questions from readers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christopher Clarey, who covers tennis for The Times and The International Herald Tribune, answers questions from readers. Additional answers will be posted on Straight Sets throughout the Australian Open.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federer, Murray, and Dolgopolov: Answers to Readers’ Questions', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T17:40:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_