lden ribbon for best of show. Today, he’s the talk of the town, but tomorrow he’ll be converted into a pile of melted grease to be mixed in with liquid manure. He’s part of the show’s famous 1,000-pound butter sculpture, and he’s going to be recycled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Down on the Farm, a Sculpture Finds a Second Life', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biofuels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Butter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AGRICULTURE DEPARTMENT', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T18:20:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nuwer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nuwer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c54318d1-26e1-5973-856f-3e5742fc2394', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c54318d1-26e1-5973-856f-3e5742fc2394'}, {'abstract': 'Replacing the words “demeaning” and “racially charged” with insulting.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/inside-debate-prep-at-fox-news-a-discussion-over-race-question/', 'snippet': 'Replacing the words “demeaning” and “racially charged” with insulting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MYRTLE BEACH, S.C.\xa0— The frosty exchange over race and social welfare between Juan Williams and Newt Gingrich during Monday night’s Fox News debate has become a breakout moment of the South Carolina primary. For many conservatives, it demonstrates how liberals defend a broken entitlement system. And for many liberals, it shows how minorities are often unfairly caricatured\xa0as addicted to government aid.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside Debate Prep at Fox News, a Discussion Over Race Question', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Juan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T18:27:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01f63d9b-fbca-5e64-99cf-321966434ed3', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01f63d9b-fbca-5e64-99cf-321966434ed3'}, {'abstract': 'A Brooklyn letterpress operator says desktop publishing has made his work a precious commodity.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/for-the-love-of-ink-and-paper/', 'snippet': 'A Brooklyn letterpress operator says desktop publishing has made his work a precious commodity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earl Kallemeyn insists that he is not a designer. He is not a businessman. He is not an artist or an engineer. He’s just the person who puts the ink on the paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For the Love of Ink and Paper', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Printing and Allied Trades', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kallemeyn, Earl', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kallemeyn Press', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenpoint (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T18:29:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Wall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c0a13bf-9dd8-5a06-bf2a-ba41a3bc7afa', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c0a13bf-9dd8-5a06-bf2a-ba41a3bc7afa'}, {'abstract': 'The decision does not preclude later approval of the Keystone XL oil pipeline, but it sets up a partisan fight that will likely persist through the election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/us/state-dept-to-put-oil-pipeline-on-hold.html', 'snippet': 'The decision does not preclude later approval of the Keystone XL oil pipeline, but it sets up a partisan fight that will likely persist through the election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama on Wednesday rejected, for now, the proposed Keystone XL oil pipeline, saying the $7 billion project could not be adequately reviewed within the 60-day deadline set by Congress. While the president’s action does not preclude later approval of the project, it sets up a baldly partisan fight over energy, jobs and regulation that will most likely persist through the November election.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/us/PIPELINE-2/PIPELINE-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rejecting Pipeline Proposal, Obama Blames Congress', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Proposed Oil Pipeline Is Bogged Down by Politics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Keystone Pipeline System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TransCanada Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T18:29:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder and Dan Frosch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/691f7c1c-3d94-5cdb-971f-12a5971656bd', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/691f7c1c-3d94-5cdb-971f-12a5971656bd'}, {'abstract': 'Experiments in teaching about the connections between climate and society.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/climate-in-classrooms/', 'snippet': 'Experiments in teaching about the connections between climate and society.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s much to explore about the challenges in teaching about the evolving relationship between people and their climate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Climate in Classrooms', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'David, Laurie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Science Teachers Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T18:40:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03cd4e3a-61ea-514e-828e-1d63caf69786', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03cd4e3a-61ea-514e-828e-1d63caf69786'}, {'abstract': 'The belted overcoat with its nipped-in waist and flared hemline is the coat to beat at the moment.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/coming-soon-belted-coats/', 'snippet': 'The belted overcoat with its nipped-in waist and flared hemline is the coat to beat at the moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming Soon | Belted Coats', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T18:42:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ce8bc18-ec4b-5af8-91e7-5240f9e670c6', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ce8bc18-ec4b-5af8-91e7-5240f9e670c6'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich’s latest taunt in his increasingly testy back-and-forth with Mitt Romney: I’ll show you mine. Now you show me yours.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/gingrich-says-his-tax-rate-was-31-percent/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich’s latest taunt in his increasingly testy back-and-forth with Mitt Romney: I’ll show you mine. Now you show me yours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WINNSBORO, S.C. — I’ll show you mine. Now you show me yours. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Says His Tax Rate Was 31 Percent', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T18:48:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/732ebb21-cbae-54c2-8191-9e3bd991b0ab', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/732ebb21-cbae-54c2-8191-9e3bd991b0ab'}, {'abstract': 'The virtual movement to protest two antipiracy bills in Congress has provoked a wide range of reactions around the Web, from people cheering the protest to others who say that limiting access to information is not an effective way to cause change in Washington. Here is a sampling.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/reactions-to-the-webs-protests-against-piracy-bills/', 'snippet': 'The virtual movement to protest two antipiracy bills in Congress has provoked a wide range of reactions around the Web, from people cheering the protest to others who say that limiting access to information is not an effective way to cause change ...', 'lead_paragraph': ' On Wednesday morning, as people tried to gain access to \xa07,000 sites around the Web — including Flickr, Tumblr, Wikipedia, Google and Reddit — they were greeted with gloomy black boxes and error messages.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reactions to the Web’s Protests Against Piracy Bills', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T18:48:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4503913-bf37-58bf-9d0c-0bf5db463983', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4503913-bf37-58bf-9d0c-0bf5db463983'}, {'abstract': 'Biting into a Twinkie is like biting into a different era. For Hostess, which has again filed for bankruptcy, that may be the problem.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/some-comments-on-the-rise-and-fall-of-twinkies/', 'snippet': 'Biting into a Twinkie is like biting into a different era. For Hostess, which has again filed for bankruptcy, that may be the problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The third-to-last of the nearly 40 ingredients that make up a Twinkie is listed on the package as “sorbic acid (to retain freshness).” It’s the only ingredient that comes with an explanation of its purpose, as if it’s essential for us to understand that this Twinkie is as good as it was when it was made.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Comments on the Rise and Fall of Twinkies', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Buffalo Bob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CVS Caremark Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hostess Brands', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T18:55:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Meyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a78d898b-4b6b-52d8-9b87-436d6121b079', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a78d898b-4b6b-52d8-9b87-436d6121b079'}, {'abstract': 'Heavy rains may have an impact when the Giants play the 49ers in San Francisco Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/the-giants-get-ready-for-some-stormy-weather/', 'snippet': 'Heavy rains may have an impact when the Giants play the 49ers in San Francisco Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. – As the Giants began practice Wednesday for the N.F.C. championship game this weekend, they did so with a virtually full complement of players. Running back Ahmad Bradshaw was the only player not working in early drills, and linebacker Mark Herzlich – who has been out with an ankle injury – returned to the field for the first time since Nov. 28.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Giants Get Ready for Some Stormy Weather', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradshaw, Ahmad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gore, Frank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herzlich, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Brandon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Candlestick Park', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T18:57:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'