tle discussed, have been the focus of recent academic seminars, personal memoirs and other forums.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JAKARTA — As a solitary voice intoned a traditional Indonesian harvest song, dancers acted out the gathering of rice. Members of the audience joined in — most knew the words — until the song was overtaken by a vigorous hip-hop backbeat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/world/indonesia2/indonesia2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 793, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Veil of Silence Lifted in Indonesia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indonesia Chips Away At the Enforced Silence Around a Dark History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Communism (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T19:41:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Schonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e909a56-f29e-5803-9ba2-df979d01623b', 'word_count': 1273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e909a56-f29e-5803-9ba2-df979d01623b'}, {'abstract': 'Rachel McAdams, Jessica Alba, and Catherine Zeta Jones keep it simple in sleek black coats.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/winter-wonders-dark-stars/', 'snippet': 'Rachel McAdams, Jessica Alba, and Catherine Zeta Jones keep it simple in sleek black coats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There comes a time in every woman’s winter when nothing but a simple black coat will do. Here, the actress Rachel McAdams goes bare-legged in one with cool buckle closures; the actress Jessica Alba chooses a collarless style with shiny shoulder embellishments (an easy complement to all that color underneath); and the actress Catherine Zeta-Jones elevates a sharper duster with a cherry red clutch and heels.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winter Wonders | Dark Stars', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T19:45:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b148bfb4-8389-53b8-ba8a-31a388793858', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b148bfb4-8389-53b8-ba8a-31a388793858'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge ruled that R. Allen Stanford, accused of defrauding thousands of investors in a $7 billion Ponzi scheme, will go on trial next week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/business/trial-set-for-texas-financier.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge ruled that R. Allen Stanford, accused of defrauding thousands of investors in a $7 billion Ponzi scheme, will go on trial next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — A federal judge ruled on Wednesday that R. Allen Stanford, the Texas financier accused of defrauding thousands of investors in a $7 billion Ponzi scheme, will go on trial next week, nearly three years after his arrest. ', 'print_section': 'B'