': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99e1933d-0a93-5ab3-84b2-4753f3a94297', 'word_count': 1676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99e1933d-0a93-5ab3-84b2-4753f3a94297'}, {'abstract': 'The Tigers’ offense took a hit Tuesday when it was announced Victor Martinez would miss the entire season with a knee injury.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/tigers-lose-martinez-to-knee-injury-mull-signing-a-replacement/', 'snippet': 'The Tigers’ offense took a hit Tuesday when it was announced Victor Martinez would miss the entire season with a knee injury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hopes of the Detroit Tigers took a big jolt when the team announced on Tuesday that the valuable designated hitter Victor Martinez sustained a torn anterior cruciate ligament and could miss the 2012 season. Martinez’s injury occurred last week, during an agility workout to prepare for spring training and the upcoming season. He is in the process of seeking other opinions on his treatment options, but the outcome is expected to be the same: reconstruction surgery and many months of rehab.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tigers Lose Martinez to Knee Injury, Mull Signing a Replacement', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cabrera, Miguel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dombrowski, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martinez, Victor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T20:15:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5c19671-f64d-59e3-ab6b-cb06e0043b56', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5c19671-f64d-59e3-ab6b-cb06e0043b56'}, {'abstract': 'Not only would soon-to-be public shareholders have no power over the Carlyle Group, the firm is also seeking to force all shareholder legal claims into arbitration.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/carlyle-readies-an-unfriendly-i-p-o-for-shareholders/', 'snippet': 'Not only would soon-to-be public shareholders have no power over the Carlyle Group, the firm is also seeking to force all shareholder legal claims into arbitration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is quite possible that the Carlyle Group, the private equity firm that is preparing to go public, is proposing the most shareholder-unfriendly corporate governance structure in modern history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carlyle Readies an Unfriendly I.P.O. for Shareholders', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Conway, William Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubenstein, David', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T20:19:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a93d029-5fd7-5e72-8bec-6f357d973277', 'word_count': 1037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a93d029-5fd7-5e72-8bec-6f357d973277'}, {'abstract': '“The Mountaintop” will recoup its $3.1-million budget when it closes on Broadway this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/the-mountaintop-recoups-on-broadway/', 'snippet': '“The Mountaintop” will recoup its $3.1-million budget when it closes on Broadway this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway production of “The Mountaintop,” Katori Hall’s drama about the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr.’s final night before his assassination, has recouped its entire capitalization of $3.1 million, the lead producers Jean Doumanian and Sonia Friedman announced on Wednesday. The play opened to mixed reviews in October, but ticket sales proved durable in part because of the drawing power of its stars, Samuel L. Jackson (as King) and Angela Bassett (as a mysterious motel maid).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Mountaintop’ Recoups On Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bassett, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doumanian, Jean', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Sonia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Katori', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Samuel L', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Signature Theater Co', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T20:19:34+0000', 'docum