wards in Los Angeles ended on Sunday, one of the brashest parties was given by InStyle magazine and Warner Brothers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/fashion/after-the-globes-show-the-party-rush.html', 'snippet': 'After the Golden Globes Awards in Los Angeles ended on Sunday, one of the brashest parties was given by InStyle magazine and Warner Brothers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF it weren’t for the wall-to-wall celebrities, the Beverly Hilton Hotel in Los Angeles might have been mistaken for the Los Angeles airport. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/fashion/10ZSCENE2/10ZSCENE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/19/fashion/10ZSCENE2/10ZSCENE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/fashion/10ZSCENE2/10ZSCENE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 874, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/fashion/10ZSCENE2/10ZSCENE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/fashion/10ZSCENE2/10ZSCENE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After the Globes Show, the Party Rush', 'kicker': 'Scene City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the Globes Show, the Party Rush', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golden Globes (Awards)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hilton Worldwide', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T20:28:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bee-Shyuan Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bee-shyuan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89501dd8-3655-51a7-b4b3-2f1a06b7f22c', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89501dd8-3655-51a7-b4b3-2f1a06b7f22c'}, {'abstract': 'Fresh installments of “Glee” and “New Girl” helped Fox among 18- to 49-year-old adults.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/new-episodes-lift-fox-on-slow-night/', 'snippet': 'Fresh installments of “Glee” and “New Girl” helped Fox among 18- to 49-year-old adults.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a monthlong holiday hiatus, “Glee” and “New Girl” returned with new episodes to give Fox a lift in the broadcast television ratings on an otherwise sluggish Tuesday night. How sluggish? According to Nielsen data, CBS was still the No. 1 network in total viewers despite a full slate of repeats on the schedule. Fox was first in the advertiser-coveted 18-to-49-year-old demographic, as “New Girl” was the highest-rated program of the night in that category. The show also had a total audience of 6.9 million viewers. “Glee” finished with more viewers (7.5 million) but was second among adults 18 to 49.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Episodes Lift Fox on Slow Night', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T20:29:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5963c3d2-70c0-5724-ba51-6cf089d597ca', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5963c3d2-70c0-5724-ba51-6cf089d597ca'}, {'abstract': 'Joining its hometown industry and betting on the success of YouTube’s new initiative to promote original content, the Museum of Contemporary Art in Los Angeles announced that it would start an online video channel in July featuring news and talk-show programming, among other art-focused shows.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/museum-of-contemporary-art-to-create-original-programming-for-youtube/', 'snippet': 'Joining its hometown industry and betting on the success of YouTube’s new initiative to promote original content, the Museum of Contemporary Art in Los Angeles announced that it would start an online video channel in July featuring news and talk-s...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joining its hometown industry and betting on the success of YouTube’s new initiative to promote original content, the Museum of Contemporary Art in Los Angeles announced that it would start an online video channel in July featuring news and talk-show programming, among other art-focused shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Museum of Contemporary Art to Create Original Programming for YouTube', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': N