 them – had expired. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian Trial of American Antiquities Dealer Comes to an End', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hecht, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'True, Marion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Getty, J Paul, Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T20:44:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e9a74d6-3d5d-5ba2-a2a1-dd7b3535645e', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e9a74d6-3d5d-5ba2-a2a1-dd7b3535645e'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s Campaign Stops column.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/mitts-best-friend/', 'snippet': 'This week’s Campaign Stops column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s some buzz today about a Gingrich surge, based on a national Rasmussen poll showing him rising after this week’s debate performances, as well as non-statistical indicators like Sarah Palin’s kinda-sorta endorsement and the Romney camp’s decision to stop ignoring the former speaker and start attacking once again. In the absence of any hard data on the South Carolina race, though, I’m sticking by my assessment in this week’s Campaign Stops column, which argues that Gingrich has been an ideal rival for Romney:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitt’s Best Friend', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T20:45:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49aef426-35da-5196-9cfc-04403cf14d0b', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49aef426-35da-5196-9cfc-04403cf14d0b'}, {'abstract': 'A versatile accessory for the day-to-night conundrum.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/the-get-marni-clutch/', 'snippet': 'A versatile accessory for the day-to-night conundrum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This two-in-one Marni clutch has a girlish pink polka dot on one face and a bolder, more Marniesque green and black print on the flip side. Big enough to carry your BlackBerry and Kindle but not so big that you lose your lipstick in it, the versatile accessory tackles mood swings as easily as it does the whole day-to-night dressing thing. What to do? Just switcheroo!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Marni Clutch', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T20:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mallory Schlau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mallory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schlau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe787f64-eb21-5806-b7b4-496a86d621e2', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe787f64-eb21-5806-b7b4-496a86d621e2'}, {'abstract': 'Television networks covering antipiracy legislation before Congress this week have had to consider whether to disclose the positions of their parent companies — virtually all of which have campaigned in favor of it.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/on-tv-antipiracy-coverage-may-include-a-disclosure/', 'snippet': 'Television networks covering antipiracy legislation before Congress this week have had to consider whether to disclose the positions of their parent companies — virtually all of which have campaigned in favor of it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As television networks have covered Internet companies’ positions against antipiracy legislation before Congress this week, they have had to consider whether to disclose the positions of their parent companies — virtually all of which have campaigned in favor of it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On TV, Antipiracy Coverage May Include a Disclosure', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC News', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T20:50:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f28bc1e8-ddd6-5923-ac82-6df860ef478c', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f28bc1e8-ddd6-5923-ac82-6df860ef478c'}, {'abstract': 'The time was purchased in Michigan, Virginia, Ohio and North Carolina — all states with significant numbers of electoral votes', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/obama-to-start-advertising-as-early-as-thursday/', 'snippet': 'The time was purchased in Michigan, Virginia, Ohio and North Carolina — all states with significant numbers of electoral votes', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s campaign has begun buying advertising time in a handful of key battleground states, making his first purchase of television time so far this election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama to Start Advertising as Early as Thursday', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T20:54:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1d0c12a-0345-5633-9251-fe305830b2d3', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1d0c12a-0345-5633-9251-fe305830b2d3'}, {'abstract': 'According to a new research report from Nielsen, there were so many purchases of iPhones around the holidays that Apple sharply whittled down the market share lead of Android smartphones in the United States by the end of the year. In December, less than three percentage points separated the share of Android devices and iPhones among new smartphone owners.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/gap-narrows-between-android-and-iphone/', 'snippet': 'According to a new research report from Nielsen, there were so many purchases of iPhones around the holidays that Apple sharply whittled down the market share lead of Android smartphones in the United States by the end of the year. In December, le...', 'lead_paragraph': ' It looks like the holidays were very big for the iPhone. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/technology/18bits-apple/18bits-apple-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/technology/18bits-apple/18bits-apple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/18/technology/18bits-apple/18bits-apple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gap Narrows Between Android and iPhone', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T20:57:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10c8bb6f-577a-5e0a-8831-391f7ee5069a', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10c8bb6f-577a-5e0a-8831-391f7ee5069a'}, {'abstract': 'In joining the protests against antipiracy legislation by blacking out some content or popping up political messages, some commercial Web sites were putting advertising revenue at risk. But they had to worry about another possible consequence too: hurting their ranks in search results.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/how-the-web-went-dark/', 'snippet': 'In joining the protests against antipiracy legislation by blacking out some content or popping up political messages, some commercial Web sites were putting advertising revenue at risk. But they had to worry about another possible consequence too:...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Web sites on Wednesday of, clockwise from top left, Google, Mozilla, Wired and Wikipedia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Web Sites Aim to Join Protests While Keeping Their Mojo', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T21:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dcb2a67-1f29-52ae-85d4-f0e0451d4c98', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dcb2a67-1f29-52ae-85d4-f0e0451d4c98'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate Agriculture Committee is exploring regulatory changes following pleas from farmers, cattle ranchers and other futures industry customers who seek stronger protections for their money.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/new-laws-possible-in-wake-of-mf-global/', 'snippet': 'The Senate Agriculture Committee is exploring regulatory changes following pleas from farmers, cattle ranchers and other futures industry customers who seek stronger protections for their money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawmakers are considering new policies aimed at preventing a repeat of the MF Global debacle, in which the futures brokerage firm misused an estimated $1.2 billion in customer money as it collapsed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Laws Possible In Wake of MF Global’s Demise', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Futures and Options Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stabenow, Debbie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T21:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f39e1290-7e26-5b41-bd48-3ad17e136cb2', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f39e1290-7e26-5b41-bd48-3ad17e136cb2'}, {'abstract': 'Romney faces a tough patch in South Carolina as he seeks to wrap up the nomination.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/romney-hits-some-bumps-in-south-carolina/', 'snippet': 'Romney faces a tough patch in South Carolina as he seeks to wrap up the nomination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SPARTANBURG, S.C. — Just a week ago, Mitt Romney, flush from a big victory in the New Hampshire primary, was all high hopes and big smiles as he boarded a charter flight to South Carolina — “It’s a lovely state, can’t wait to be there,” he said, before adding that he expected South Carolina, a state where he finished fourth four years ago, to be a “challenge.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Hits Some Bumps in South Carolina', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T21:02:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00964960-65df-5fde-bcf0-a2b12e86c791', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00964960-65df-5fde-bcf0-a2b12e86c791'}, {'abstract': 'January 18, 2012 — In South Carolina, Rick Santorum and Newt Gingirich are dueling to be the more conservative alternative to Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/politics/100000001294578/timescast-scs-conservative-vote.html', 'snippet': 'January 18, 2012 — In South Carolina, Rick Santorum and Newt Gingirich are dueling to be the more conservative alternative to Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'January 18, 2012 — In South Carolina, Rick Santorum and Newt Gingirich are dueling to be the more conservative alternative to Mitt Romney.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subt