ract': 'The Web is still learning how to stage protests online. On Wednesday people tried a number of tactics to get their views across about SOPA and PIPA. They blacked out entire Web sites and placed “STOP SOPA” banners on their Twitter and Facebook avatars.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/for-online-protests-throwing-spaghetti-against-the-internet/', 'snippet': 'The Web is still learning how to stage protests online. On Wednesday people tried a number of tactics to get their views across about SOPA and PIPA. They blacked out entire Web sites and placed “STOP SOPA” banners on their Twitter and Facebook ava...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The World Wide Web is still learning how to stage protests online, with people and companies trying different tactics, throwing spaghetti against the Internet and trying to see what sticks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Online Protests, Throwing Spaghetti Against the Internet', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intellectual Property', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walk, Hunter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Fred', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Flickr', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizati