a Sunday Review essay that asserted that people are more creative and successful working alone rather than in groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/opinion/19LETTERS/19LETTERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 806, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/opinion/19LETTERS/19LETTERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/opinion/19LETTERS/19LETTERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Key to Creativity: Solitude or Teams?', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Key to Creativity: Solitude or Teams?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Creativity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:14:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ccc495d-113d-58b3-9165-45a15a476a37', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ccc495d-113d-58b3-9165-45a15a476a37'}, {'abstract': 'Have you seen worse product placement than a recent Subway spot smack-dab in the middle of an episode of “Hawaii Five-O” on CBS? Does this sort of thing drive you crazy, or do you consider it just revenge for the fact you’ve been fast-forwarding through commercials on your digital video recorder for the last five years?', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/a-commercial-sandwiched-between-lines-of-dialogue-on-hawaii-five-0/', 'snippet': 'Have you seen worse product placement than a recent Subway spot smack-dab in the middle of an episode of “Hawaii Five-O” on CBS? Does this sort of thing drive you crazy, or do you consider it just revenge for the fact you’ve been fast-forwarding t...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Product placement in scripted television shows has quickly become a fact of life, as struggling networks seek new ways to make money. Sometimes it’s done subtly, sometimes with a sledgehammer. But this example from “Pu’olo,” Monday’s episode of “Hawaii Five-0″ on CBS, was particularly egregious — the most jarring, disruptive and insulting example I’ve seen. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Commercial, Sandwiched Between Lines of Dialogue on ‘Hawaii Five-0’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park, Grace', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Subway Restaurants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:15:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49040454-a900-5a77-962a-67443a62c9d5', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49040454-a900-5a77-962a-67443a62c9d5'}, {'abstract': 'Cautious the collections were, but not meret