'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nicotine Replacement', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nicotine Replacement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nicotine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/51628433-1e2c-5cbc-b12a-357b1ef4e7f6', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51628433-1e2c-5cbc-b12a-357b1ef4e7f6'}, {'abstract': 'The new animated series “Unsupervised,” which begins on Thursday on FX, follows two teenage losers who are also striving for suburban domesticity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/arts/television/unsupervised-with-justin-long-and-kristen-bell-on-fx-review.html', 'snippet': 'The new animated series “Unsupervised,” which begins on Thursday on FX, follows two teenage losers who are also striving for suburban domesticity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The timing of the animated series “Unsupervised” is unfortunate. A kind of reversed “Beavis and Butt-Head” — in which the teenage heroes, while losers in just about every way, are also social strivers yearning for suburban domesticity and dispensing Oprah Winfrey-style affirmations — it has the bad luck of coming along three months after the original was revived by MTV. The new show looks awfully pale by comparison.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/arts/19unsupervised/19unsupervised-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/19/arts/19unsupervised/19unsupervised-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/arts/19unsupervised/19unsupervised-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/arts/19unsupervised/19unsupervised-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/arts/19unsupervised/19unsupervised-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Teenagers on the Bottom Rung, Yearning to Improve Their Uncool Status', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Teenagers on the Bottom Rung, Yearning to Improve Their Uncool Status', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX (TV Network)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Long, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bell, Kristen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:23:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/65dfaa66-d47e-5005-a0e5-a3a218f1ed54', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65dfaa66-d47e-5005-a0e5-a3a218f1ed54'}, {'abstract': 'The social media service already seems simple, but it has many features and widgets to make it even easier to use.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/technology/personaltech/nine-things-you-didnt-know-about-twitter.html', 'snippet': 'The social media service already seems simple, but it has many features and widgets to make it even easier to use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twitter, the minimalist-format social network that claims to have 100 million users, has built its reputation around its simplicity. Members can post to the service only in text messages of 140 characters or less. They can include a link to another site, or to a photo or video. They can repost other users’ messages on their own pages. They can send each other equally spartan private messages. That’s about it — or so it seems.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/business/19-BASICS/19-BASICS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/business/19-BASICS/19-BASICS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/business/19-BASICS/19-BASICS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nine Things You Didn’t Know About Twitter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nine Things You Didn’t Know About Twitter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}