Obama Is Faulted By Swing Voters In A New Survey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:32:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny and Dalia Sussman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Dalia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sussman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1d7475f-4128-5b8b-a6d2-2eccc59d7560', 'word_count': 1187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1d7475f-4128-5b8b-a6d2-2eccc59d7560'}, {'abstract': 'The latest New York Times/CBS News Poll is based on telephone interviews conducted Jan. 12 through 17 with 1,154 adults throughout the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/us/politics/how-the-poll-was-conducted.html', 'snippet': 'The latest New York Times/CBS News Poll is based on telephone interviews conducted Jan. 12 through 17 with 1,154 adults throughout the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest New York Times/CBS News Poll is based on telephone interviews conducted Jan. 12 through 17 with 1,154 adults throughout the United States. Of these, 1,021 said they were registered to vote.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Poll Was Conducted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How the Poll Was Conducted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:32:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c14e1041-bd84-5b6b-bda3-9da0e9ef04ca', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c14e1041-bd84-5b6b-bda3-9da0e9ef04ca'}, {'abstract': 'The Victory lamp made by Novaled features a new type of light source: organic light-emitting diodes, or OLEDs, which produce a more diffuse light than traditional LEDs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/garden/the-victory-lamp-from-novaled-features-oleds.html', 'snippet': 'The Victory lamp made by Novaled features a new type of light source: organic light-emitting diodes, or OLEDs, which produce a more diffuse light than traditional LEDs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The carbon fiber Victory lamp made by Novaled, a German company, features a new type of light source: organic light-emitting diodes, or OLEDs, a technology that uses thin layers of film to produce a more diffuse light than traditional LEDs. “If you look into the light source, there’s no glare whatsoever,” said Uli Petzold, founder of the Miami lighting design company Uli+friends, the exclusive distributor of the $7,500 lamp in the United States. “The color temperature is very warm.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/garden/19LIGHTING/19CURRENTS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 894, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/garden/19LIGHTING/19CURRENTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/garden/19LIGHTING/19CURRENTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharp Edges, but a Soft Glow', 'kicker': 'Currents | Lighting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sharp Edges, but a Soft Glow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organic Light-Emitting Diodes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Light-Emitting Diodes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lamps and Lampshades', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lighting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:33:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ae49bdd-8bc4-5184-92fd-8005ce1a8ae6', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ae49bdd-8bc4-5184-92fd-8005ce1a8ae6'}, {'abstract': 'The health and wellness company Sabi has developed a range of visually appealing products for the management of medications and vitamins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/garden/pill-organizers-pretty-enough-to-come-out-of-the-cabinet.html', 'snippet': 'The health and wellness company Sabi has developed a range of visually appealing products for the management of medications and vitamins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hoping to remedy an everyday annoyance — the management of medications and vitamins — the health and wellness company Sabi has developed a range of products. Created by the industrial designer Yves Béhar, they can be used to dispense, organize, carry, crush and cut pills. With shapely, ergonomic curves, the pieces are intended to be easily used by an aging population, but visually appealing to all generations.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/garden/19GOODS-SPAN/19GOODS-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/19/garden/19GOODS-SPAN/19GOODS-SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/garden/19GOODS-SPAN/19CURRENTS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/garden/19GOODS-SPAN/19GOODS-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/garden/19GOODS-SPAN/19GOODS-SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pill Organizers Pretty Enough to Come Out of the Cabinet', 'kicker': 'Currents | Goods', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pill Organizers: Pretty Enough to Come Out of the Cabinet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:33:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organizati