in the Flatiron district will carry her entire collection of fabrics, pillows and rugs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been almost 14 years since Madeline Weinrib, the granddaughter of the ABC Carpet & Home founder Max Weinrib, introduced her first collection of rugs there. Several years later, she turned an area on the sixth floor of the store into what she called her Atelier, which sold the rugs, as well as pillows, napkins and other objects she designed.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/garden/19OPEN/19CURRENTS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/garden/19OPEN/19CURRENTS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/garden/19OPEN/19CURRENTS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Madeline Weinrib Branches Out', 'kicker': 'Currents | Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Textile Designer Branches Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pillows', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carpets and Rugs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:33:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organizat