 'nyt://article/97f94214-ff27-5f52-80c6-4886e73482e5', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97f94214-ff27-5f52-80c6-4886e73482e5'}, {'abstract': 'After delivering the State of the Union message next Tuesday, the president will spend three days traveling to five battleground states.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/obama-plans-trip-to-five-states/', 'snippet': 'After delivering the State of the Union message next Tuesday, the president will spend three days traveling to five battleground states.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Obama plans three days of travel to five battleground states after he delivers his nationally televised State of the Union address next Tuesday, a trip that the White House bills as official but one that has all the markings of his first campaign swing of the year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Plans Trip to Five States', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:52:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05c0a8ad-7ed3-5747-9ef2-5b9cc6d5266d', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05c0a8ad-7ed3-5747-9ef2-5b9cc6d5266d'}, {'abstract': 'The activist investor disclosed on Wednesday that he had raised his stake in WebMD to 11.64 percent from 9.99 percent and called on the online health company to buy back up to $1 billion of its shares.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/icahn-raises-bet-on-webmd/', 'snippet': 'The activist investor disclosed on Wednesday that he had raised his stake in WebMD to 11.64 percent from 9.99 percent and called on the online health company to buy back up to $1 billion of its shares.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl C. Icahn won’t be deterred by WebMD‘s woes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Icahn Raises Bet on WebMD', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Icahn, Carl C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WebMD Health Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:55:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3b5f2f6-54b9-5906-a12b-9bb8ffc1c9a0', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3b5f2f6-54b9-5906-a12b-9bb8ffc1c9a0'}, {'abstract': 'What do you look for in noise-canceling headphones? Music fidelity? Reasonable price? Bose has dominated the market, but here’s a look at the latest models from 10 other companies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/technology/personaltech/finding-headphones-to-shut-out-the-world-state-of-the-art.html', 'snippet': 'What do you look for in noise-canceling headphones? Music fidelity? Reasonable price? Bose has dominated the market, but here’s a look at the latest models from 10 other companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the olden days, you didn’t need much to enjoy air travel: a pair of goggles, a trusty biplane and a song in your heart. These days, the equipment list is slightly longer: a roll-on bag, a neck pillow and an eye mask — not to mention T.S.A.-friendly slip-on shoes, a fold-out laptop case and an all-plastic watch.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/06/01/technology/Pogue-190-for-Email/Pogue-190-for-Email-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/06/01/technology/Pogue-190-for-Email/Pogue-190-for-Email-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Headphones to Shut Out the World', 'kicker': 'State of the Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Headphones To Shut Out The World', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Noise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Headphones and Headsets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:56:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee2db1f9-8621-55af-8d54-4c09e98e3198', 'word_count': 1305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee2db1f9-8621-55af-8d54-4c09e98e3198'}, {'abstract': 'In “Grey Matter” Kivu Ruhorahoza gathers recollections of the months of massacres in Rwanda and the effects of the bloodshed on those who survived.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/movies/grey-matter-a-rwandan-film-review.html', 'snippet': 'In “Grey Matter” Kivu Ruhorahoza gathers recollections of the months of massacres in Rwanda and the effects of the bloodshed on those who survived.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a revealing image late in “Grey Matter”: a lingering close-up of wind chimes made from keys and shards of green glass. Shortly before, the glass was part of a bottle, shattered by a young man as a means to slit his own throat. From despair, art.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/movies/grey-matter/grey-matter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/18/movies/grey-matter/grey-matter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/movies/grey-matter/grey-matter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/movies/grey-matter/grey-matter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/18/movies/grey-matter/grey-matter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Unearthing the Meaning in a Massacre', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Grey Matter'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Unearthing The Meaning In a Massacre', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:57:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By David DeWitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeWitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e58b3a4e-aa68-5159-a316-a08057b9f68b', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e58b3a4e-aa68-5159-a316-a08057b9f68b'}, {'abstract': 'Greg Norman was inclined to turn down an invitation to play golf with President Bill Clinton in 1994. He said yes, however, and the two have become friends.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/norman-finds-comfort-zone-with-clinton/', 'snippet': 'Greg Norman was inclined to turn down an invitation to play golf with President Bill Clinton in 1994. He said yes, however, and the two have become friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LA QUINTA, Calif. — Greg Norman did not expect to like President Bill Clinton, whose politics he opposed. So when the call came from the White House inviting Norman to play golf with Clinton in Norman’s native Australia in 1994, he was inclined to turn it down. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Norman Finds Comfort Zone With Clinton', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norman, Greg', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:58:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a7d2595-b557-54ea-b817-7a48efde8493', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a7d2595-b557-54ea-b817-7a48efde8493'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Jerry Brown strongly endorsed a disputed $98.5 billion train project in an upbeat State of the State speech.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/us/gov-brown-high-speed-rail-projects.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Jerry Brown strongly endorsed a disputed $98.5 billion train project in an upbeat State of the State speech.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SACRAMENTO — Gov. Jerry Brown on Wednesday threw his unequivocal support behind a $100 billion high-speed rail line that has come under fire here in California and across the country, embracing it in a strikingly optimistic State of the State speech in which he asserted that government should pursue ambitious ventures even during times of economic strife.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/us/CALIFORNIA/CALIFORNIA-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/us/CALIFORNIA/CALIFORNIA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/us/CALIFORNIA/CALIFORNIA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brown Asks California to Cheer Rail Project', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brown Asks California To Cheer Rail Project', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Speed Rail Projects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-18T23:59:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nagourney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nagourney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported',