rs who alerted the military authorities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/world/asia/afghanistan-report-of-molestation-by-british-troops-is-being-investigated.html', 'snippet': 'The investigation comes after two servicemen in Afghanistan were accused of filming the children and showing the images on laptop computers to other soldiers who alerted the military authorities.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The British Defense Ministry said Wednesday that the Royal Military Police had begun an investigation into allegations of inappropriate behavior by two servicemen in Afghanistan after a report of child abuse. The British newspaper The Sun reported that the two servicemen had been questioned about claims that they had encouraged a boy and girl, both about 10, to “touch them through their clothes.” The servicemen are accused of filming the children and showing the images on laptop computers to other soldiers who alerted the military authorities, the newspaper reported. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghanistan: Report of Molestation by British Troops Is Being Investigated', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghanistan: Report of Molestation By British Troops Is Being Investigated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T01:23:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/86c300ba-8c09-5763-91e6-ea81adad03bf', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86c300ba-8c09-5763-91e6-ea81adad03bf'}, {'abstract': 'Four years after Mitt Romney’s beliefs contributed to a fourth-place finish, South Carolina primary voters seem more focused on choosing the best candidate to defeat President Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/us/politics/in-south-carolina-romneys-mormon-beliefs-dont-carry-as-much-weight.html', 'snippet': 'Four years after Mitt Romney’s beliefs contributed to a fourth-place finish, South Carolina primary voters seem more focused on choosing the best candidate to defeat President Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENVILLE, S.C. — Four years ago, Mitt Romney’s Mormon faith was a point of considerable concern, if not contention, for many Republican voters in South Carolina, a state where many voters are evangelical Christians and one that is known for its bare-knuckled politics.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/us/MORMON-1/MORMON-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Year, Voters Focus More on a Man Than on His Religion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Year, Voters Focus More on a Man Than on His Religion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evangelical Movement', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T01:25:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Serge F. Kovaleski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Kovaleski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c32b7f5-d548-5a82-9c80-4bc676179e21', 'word_count': 1278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c32b7f5-d548-5a82-9c80-4bc676179e21'}, {'abstract': 'The success of Alex Smith this season has not surprised David Carr, who plays behind Eli Manning and was a 49ers backup last season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/sports/football/alex-smiths-success-no-surprise-to-david-carr-of-giants.html', 'snippet': 'The success of Alex Smith this season has not surprised David Carr, who plays behind Eli Manning and was a 49ers backup last season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — While the rise of San Francisco 49ers quarterback Alex Smith this season has surprised many around the N.F.L., the Giants backup quarterback David Carr is not among those stunned. As a former backup to Smith, the No. 1 overall pick in 2005, Carr saw how he handled a difficult season in 2010 — which included a stadium full of 49ers fans chanting for him to be benched — and came away impressed by Smith’s mental toughness.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'm