vening of Jan. 10, about an hour into Mahler’s Ninth Symphony. During the introspective, achingly beautiful fourth movement, an audience member’s cellphone loudly rang. And rang. And rang again. It was the kind of marimba riff we’ve all heard at some point on the street from a stranger’s phone. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Maestro Sets the Tone', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Maestro Sets the Tone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T01:40:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Masello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2280215e-a08f-5531-af0d-7b5fb8b351c2', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2280215e-a08f-5531-af0d-7b5fb8b351c2'}, {'abstract': 'MELBOURNE — Rare is the professional athlete who takes much interest in the interviewer across the table, but Kim Clijsters, finding out that I had three daughters, quickly asked a few questions of her own on Wednesday: “How old are they?” “How do you handle the schooling if you’re going back and forth between Europe and the States?”', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/sitting-down-with-kim-clijsters-mama-champion/', 'snippet': 'MELBOURNE — Rare is the professional athlete who takes much interest in the interviewer across the table, but Kim Clijsters, finding out that I had 