'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed10ae0e-f52a-55e1-8920-917715f03724', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed10ae0e-f52a-55e1-8920-917715f03724'}, {'abstract': 'Joe Flacco, the quarterback whose knowledge of the Ravens’ offense was questioned this week by his teammate Ed Reed, is used to dealing with criticism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/sports/football/joe-flacco-of-ravens-is-used-to-criticism.html', 'snippet': 'Joe Flacco, the quarterback whose knowledge of the Ravens’ offense was questioned this week by his teammate Ed Reed, is used to dealing with criticism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OWINGS MILLS, Md. — For a brief moment Wednesday afternoon, Ray Rice morphed from Baltimore’s star running back into an M.C., welcoming the quarterback with more victories in his first four seasons than any other in N.F.L. history. When that quarterback, Joe Flacco, reached the podium, Rice leaped toward him. Flacco did not move.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/sports/Y-RAVENS/Y-RAVENS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/sports/Y-RAVENS/Y-RAVENS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/sports/Y-RAVENS/Y-RAVENS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ravens’ Flacco Is Used to Getting Little Credit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_he