 evict protesters from the Occupy London encampment that has surrounded St. Paul’s Cathedral since October, a British court said Wednesday. A prompt appeal was expected. The battle between protesters and the Corporation of London, the authority overseeing the land outside the historic cathedral, began late last year when the demonstrators refused to heed eviction notices pinned to tents. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: Protesters’ Eviction Approved', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Protesters’ Eviction Approved', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evictions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St Paul's Cathedral (London)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T02:13:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c534cf1-8914-50c4-8d1c-e22089cd47bd', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c534cf1-8914-50c4-8d1c-e22089cd47bd'}, {'abstract': 'The British government agreed to assess the possibility of easing heavy congestion at Heathrow and other airports by building an $80 billion airport on an island in the Thames River estuary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/world/europe/britain-weighing-new-london-airport.html', 'snippet': 'The British government agreed to assess the possibility of easing heavy congestion at Heathrow and other airports by building an $80 billion airport on an island in the Thames River estuary.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The British government agreed Wednesday to assess the possibility of easing heavy congestion at Heathrow and other airports by building an $80 billion airport on an island in the Thames River estuary. Heathrow draws criticism from among its 70 million annual passengers, and from neighbors who complain about the noise pollution from its 480,000 flights a year. Mayor Boris Johnson of London and others have said a replacement is essential if Britain is to remain competitive as an international aviation hub. Environmentalists opposing the plan say the favored site, on the Isle of Grain, 35 miles east of London, is a major center for wintering birds and a summer breeding ground for bird species like avocets and marsh harriers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: Weighing New London Airport', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Weighing New London Airport', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T02:20:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/297bc395-2bb7-5927-b838-22175cbec29d', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/297bc395-2bb7-5927-b838-22175cbec29d'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney is the favorite in Saturday’s primary, but his campaign has faced a barrage of negative ads and new questions about his religion and taxes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/us/romneys-lead-narrows-in-south-carolina-as-negative-advertising-heats-up.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney is the favorite in Saturday’s primary, but his campaign has faced a barrage of negative ads and new questions about his religion and taxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOUNT PLEASANT, S.C. — For Mitt Romney, the South Carolina primary probably can’t come soon enough, as he faced a day of nonstop negative ads,\xa0 questions about his religion and his taxes, and new poll numbers that showed his comfortable lead narrowing.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/us/Campaign-1/Campaign-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/us/Campaign-1/Campaign-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/us/Campaign-1/Campaign-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Attacks Heat Up, Romney’s Lead Narrows in S.C.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney’s Lead Narrows in South Carolina as Negative Advertising Heats Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'G