 those bills have run into an unstoppable force: an outcry by Internet companies led by Google and Wikipedia that culminated in an extraordinary online protest on Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Piracy and Political Overreach', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Online Piracy and Political Overreach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intellectual Property', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikipedia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cornyn, John', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wyden, Ron', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T02:34:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/94f044ec-df20-59d7-8a09-18cc4e3c5588', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94f044ec-df20-59d7-8a09-18cc4e3c5588'}, {'abstract': 'On Wednesday, law enforcement officials announced the indictment of 35 people charged in a drug-dealing ente