t the foul line, methodically putting away a low-scoring game with a series of free throws.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/19/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/19/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Suns and Nash Deal D’Antoni 4th Straight Loss', 'kicker': 'Suns 91, Knicks 88', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Suns and Nash Deal D’Antoni 4th Straight Loss', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "Stoudemire, Amar'e", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nash, Steve', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "D'Antoni, Mike", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Phoenix Suns', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T03:23:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c001d102-8890-5968-8409-07350baf65dd', 'word_count': 934, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c001d102-8890-5968-8409-07350baf65dd'}, {'abstract': 'The drop appeared to reflect new anxiety about the impact of Western economic sanctions on the country’s Central Bank and worries about the government’s ability to counter it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/world/middleeast/irans-rial-falls-to-new-low-against-dollar.html', 'snippet': 'The drop appeared to reflect new anxiety about the impact of Western economic sanctions on the country’s Central Bank and worries about the government’s ability to counter it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iran’s currency, the rial, fell to its lowest level ever against the dollar on Wednesday in unofficial foreign exchange transactions in Tehran, Iranian news agencies reported. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran’s Currency at Low vs. Dollar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran’s Currency at Low vs. Dollar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'US Dollar (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T03:38:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8200362-a75f-5c78-8f4f-1e324a55a255', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8200362-a75f-5c78-8f4f-1e324a55a255'}, {'abstract': 'Some of Mitt Romney’s rivals for the Republican presidential nomination are proposing tax cuts that would widen the deficit even more than his plan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/us/politics/romneys-tax-bill-and-gop-deficit-problems.html', 'snippet': 'Some of Mitt Romney’s rivals for the Republican presidential nomination are proposing tax cuts that would widen the deficit even more than his plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mitt Romney suggested this week that he pays a lower tax rate than most wealthy Americans do, he refocused attention on his tax proposals — which, like those of his major Republican rivals, would largely cut taxes for the rich while driving down tax collections and widening the nation’s deficit.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Higher Deficits Seen in Romney’s Tax Plan, and His Rivals’, Too', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Higher Deficits Seen In Romney’s Tax Plan, And His Rivals’, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T03:41:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper and David Kocieniewski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kocieniewski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8bea9b4-1ded-58f0-8a0f-c9116a0e09e5', 'word_count': 1006, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8bea9b4-1ded-58f0-8a0f-c9116a0e09e5'}, {'abstract': 'Why Mitt Romney will probably leap out ahead of President Obama. For a while.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/governor-romney-meet-governor-dukakis/', 'snippet': 'Why Mitt Romney will probably leap out ahead of President Obama. For a while.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of months ago, Mitt Romney was a hapless would-be frontrunner who couldn’t stay ahead of a motley crew of unelectable cranks, extremists and vanity candidates. (There’s some overlap in these categories.) Then he won the first two states. Now, ahead in the polls in South Carolina and Florida, Romney is on track for the Republican nomination in the worst election year for an incumbent party since — well, since 2008.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Governor Romney, Meet Governor Dukakis', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Jimmy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Gerald Rudolph Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T03:41:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Gelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d36ced49-ec7a-5c83-b0bb-c9c46fe26aa3', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d36ced49-ec7a-5c83-b0bb-c9c46fe26aa3'}, {'abstract': 'The City Council of Troy has voted to save a transit infrastructure project it voted down in December.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/us/michigan-officials-revive-transit-plan.html', 'snippet': 'The City Council of Troy has voted to save a transit infrastructure project it voted down in December.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The City Council of Troy has voted to save a transit infrastructure project it voted down in December. Construction costs for the project have been scaled back to $6.3 million, from $8.5 million, to win the vote of a council member who had expressed concerns about the cost, though the federal government fully financed construction. The city will seek “a business model that will relieve the local taxpayer of ongoing operating costs” of $30,000 per year, said Michele Hodges, president of the Chamber of Commerce. Mayor Janice Daniels, a Republican who is active in Tea Party politics and led the opposition to the project, said that she had not changed her opinion, but that “it is in my best interest, and all of Troy’s best interest, to work toward making this a fiscally responsible venture.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan: Officials Revive Transit Plan ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan: Officials Revive Transit Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Troy (Mich)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building (Construction)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T03:43:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/448a31b4-b845-5369-9520-1b8abf3cecc5', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/448a31b4-b845-5369-9520-1b8abf3cecc5'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 19, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/pageoneplus/corrections-january-19.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 19, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: January 19', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T03:49:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/deb713d3-1ebd-5c66-bad7-881d5cbd90c7', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/deb713d3-1ebd-5c66-bad7-881d5cbd90c7'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the Republican candidates’ tax plans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/01/19/us/politics/details-of-the-candidate