ork Jets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, Santonio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanchez, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomlinson, Ladainian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T04:04:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70e44934-c106-5168-a0e8-6ce1fe6ac8c7', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70e44934-c106-5168-a0e8-6ce1fe6ac8c7'}, {'abstract': 'A former president of Madison Square Garden and the Knicks was named chairman and C.E.O. of a food service and premium ticketing marketing company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/sports/dave-checketts-is-on-way-back-to-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'A former president of Madison Square Garden and the Knicks was named chairman and C.E.O. of a food service and premium ticketing marketing company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past decade, Dave Checketts’s sports interests have taken him out of New York, where he had been the president of Madison Square Garden for seven years and the president of the Knicks for three. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Checketts on Way Back to New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Checketts on Way Back to New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Checketts, Dave', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hospitality Management', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T04:14:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/695cba61-e687-5e7f-aef4-f9ea09b03c8b', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/695cba61-e687-5e7f-aef4-f9ea09b03c8b'}, {'abstract': 'A group that planned to protest at a Manhattan courthouse around the second anniversary of the Supreme Court’s decision in the Citizens United case, which eliminated barriers to corporations’ political speech and spending, sued a federal agency after its permit was denied.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/18/group-sues-over-denial-of-permit-to-protest-at-courthouse/', 'snippet': 'A group that planned to protest at a Manhattan courthouse around the second anniversary of the Supreme Court’s decision in the Citizens United case, which eliminated barriers to corporations’ political speech and spending, sued a federal agency af...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group that is planning to protest at a Manhattan courthouse around the second anniversary of the Supreme Court’s decision in the Citizens United case, which eliminated barriers to corporations’ political speech and spending, sued federal officials on Wednesday after its request for a permit to gather was denied.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Sues Over Denial of Permit to Protest at Courthouse', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court De