 Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jan. 19, 1937 | Howard Hughes Breaks His Own Transcontinental Flight Record', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T09:02:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE LEARNING NETWORK', 'person': [], 'organization': 'THE LEARNING NETWORK'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7316a50a-7d3e-5520-ab0e-0803b001d767', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7316a50a-7d3e-5520-ab0e-0803b001d767'}, {'abstract': 'Seventeen people were killed in two bombings in southern Helmand Province, and a suicide bomber killed six civilians at a NATO base’s entrance in Kandahar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/world/asia/bombings-kill-17-in-southern-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'Seventeen people were killed in two bombings in southern Helmand Province, and a suicide bomber killed six civilians at a NATO base’s entrance in Kandahar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANDAHAR, Afghanistan — More than two dozen people were killed in a four insurgent attacks in southern Afghanistan that began late Wednesday and continued through Thursday afternoon, Afghan authorities said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/world/asia/20afghanistan/20afghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/20/world/asia/20afghanistan/20afghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/world/asia/20afghanistan/20afghanistan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'lega