37, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dae565a-2469-5961-9822-9693100f799c'}, {'abstract': 'Decades of performances, from the film “Little Darlings” to Tony Award-winning play “Rabbit Hole.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/22/magazine/cynthia-nixons-past-roles.html', 'snippet': 'Decades of performances, from the film “Little Darlings” to Tony Award-winning play “Rabbit Hole.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Decades of performances, from the film “Little Darlings” to Tony Award-winning play “Rabbit Hole.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/20120122_NIXON-slide-7585/20120122_NIXON-slide-7585-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/20120122_NIXON-slide-7585/20120122_NIXON-slide-7585-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/20120122_NIXON-slide-7585/20120122_NIXON-slide-7585-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cynthia Nixon, All Grown Up', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Cynthia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T09:59:16+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/2cc54e07-e150-5759-bdf7-80918edb8b5b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/2cc54e07-e150-5759-bdf7-80918edb8b5b'}, {'abstract': 'Post-Miranda, post-men and post-cancer, Cynthia Nixon returns to where she has always felt most like herself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/magazine/cynthia-nixon-wit.html', 'snippet': 'Post-Miranda, post-men and post-cancer, Cynthia Nixon returns to where she has always felt most like herself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Cynthia Nixon was 9, she played an impostor on “To Tell the Truth.” “There was a little girl who was a professional horse rider who had won all these blue ribbons,” she recalled, “and the cool thing about her was she rode a Shetland pony, and I pretended to be her. My mother worked on the show; her job was to brief the impostors, coach them in pretending. But I couldn’t believe that no one on the panel recognized me, because I was around the studio a lot. So when I rode out on the horse with a cowboy hat on, I was like this” — she ducked her head low — “because I knew they absolutely remembered me.” Even now, her face fell. “And no one recognized me.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22nixon1/mag-22Nixon-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22nixon1/mag-22Nixon-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 730}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22nixon1/mag-22Nixon-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22nixon1/mag-22Nixon-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22nixon1/mag-22Nixon-t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Life After ‘Sex’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Life After ‘Sex’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Cynthia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Witchel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witchel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f19a3a34-bb88-5320-82da-450c5d65f67a', 'word_count': 2756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f19a3a34-bb88-5320-82da-450c5d65f67a'}, {'abstract': 'To know the future of Egypt, watch what happens to Mohamed Beltagy, the embattled hero of the revolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/magazine/mohamed-beltagy-future-of-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'To know the future of Egypt, watch what happens to Mohamed Beltagy, the embattled hero of the revolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent winter evening, a gray Mitsubishi sedan made its way slowly down the narrow main street of Qalyubiya, a farming town in the Nile River delta, hemmed in on all sides by shouting fruit vendors, bumping donkey carts, strings of colored lights and tiny bakeries and butcher shops. Election posters were plastered to every available surface, and a voice squawked loudly over a distant, tinny loudspeaker: “God willing, we will all soon live in an era of social justice. The revolution taught us that we are all equal.” As the sedan reached a crowded election rally outside a mosque, the back door opened and out stepped a striking man with deep-set eyes and a broad forehead. “He is here!” someone shouted. “The hero of the revolution!” Almost instantly, a murmur rippled through the crowd, and the man was surrounded by adoring fans. A pair of burly aides grabbed his arms and bustled him through. “God is great!” the crowd chanted as he smiled and waved, making his way toward a brightly lighted stage. “Freedom and Justice! Tomorrow we will be strong!”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22egypt1_span/mag-22Egypt-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 456, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22egypt1_span/mag-22Egypt-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 456}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22egypt1_span/mag-22Egypt-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22egypt1_span/mag-22Egypt-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22egypt1_span/mag-22Egypt-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Human Bellwether', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Man in the Middle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ghonim, Wael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T10:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert F. Worth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Worth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed9e2e3d-17c9-5807-be42-0975761a3c66', 'word_count': 5523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed9e2e3d-17c9-5807-be42-0975761a3c66'}, {'abstract': 'Erika Larsen spent three years photographing — and learning to understand — the Sami people in Scandinavia.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/washing-dishes-herding-reindeer/', 'snippet': 'Erika Larsen spent three years photographing — and learning to understand — the Sami people in Scandinavia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Erika Larsen may have discovered the solution to that enduring question: How do you fund a long-term photojournalism endeavor?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Washing Dishes, Herding Reindeer', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T10:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kerri MacDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kerri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/633bcb40-848e-5e4f-a55d-93e2f50bc7d6', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/633bcb40-848e-5e4f-a55d-93e2f50bc7d6'}, {'abstract': 'A report commissioned by a lobbying group for the securities industry should not be taken as objective analysis of the impact of a rule to restrict risky trading activities by large banks, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/should-we-trust-paid-experts-on-the-volcker-rule/', 'snippet': 'A report commissioned by a lobbying group for the securities industry should not be taken as objective analysis of the impact of a rule to restrict risky trading activities by large banks, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson, the former chief economist at the International Monetary Fund, is the co-author of “13 Bankers.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should We Trust Paid Experts on the Volcker Rule?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Volcker, Paul A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities Industry and Financial Markets Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T10:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d91bce3d-23e7-5b18-84b2-053d8a6c8dca', 'word_count': 1312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d91bce3d-23e7-5b18-84b2-053d8a6c8dca'}, {'abstract': 'Student Opinion | Tell us how you feel about sharing passwords, whether with a significant other or with friends or family members. Do you think it is a sign of trust and intimacy? Has doing so ever led to trouble for you or for someone you know?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/who-would-you-share-your-passwords-with/', 'snippet': 'Student Opinion | Tell us how you feel about sharing passwords, whether with a significant other or with friends or family members. Do you think it is a sign of trust and intimacy? Has doing so ever led to trouble for you or for someone you know?', 'lead_paragraph': 'A  recent article described the “intimate custom” of teenage couples expressing affection for each other by sharing their passwords to e-mail, Facebook and other accounts. Have you ever shared your passwords with someone else? What do you think of the practice in general? Do you know any stories of password-sharing gone awry? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whom Would You Share Your Passwords With?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T10:06:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecc286e8-aedd-53f5-b63b-1671d273125d', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecc286e8-aedd-53f5-b63b-1671d273125d'}, {'abstract': 'The Occupy movement took hold at some campuses, and students are still holding their ground. But how strong is their will?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/education/edlife/the-new-student-activism.html', 'snippet': 'The Occupy movement took hold at some campuses, and students are still holding their ground. But how strong is their will?', 'lead_paragraph': 'ASHLEY WARD, an aspiring idealist with waning faith in the world, was standing in the newsroom of her college paper at Humboldt State University in Northern California when a fellow student rushed in with startling news.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/education/22edlife-HP-thumb/22edlife-HP-thumb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 267, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/education/22edlife-HP-thumb/22edlife-HP-thumb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/education/22edlife-HP-thumb/22edlife-HP-thumb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Student Activism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The New Student Activism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T11:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b92c145-a49d-5c39-acf3-59078d425d7d', 'word_count': 1681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b92c145-a49d-5c39-acf3-59078d425d7d'}, {'abstract': 'How to subtract 10 years from the age of your brain? Get a college degree.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/education/edlife/a-sharper-mind-middle-age-and-beyond.html', 'snippet': 'How to subtract 10 years from the age of your brain? Get a college degree.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN 1905, at age 55, Sir William Osler, the most influential physician of his era, decided to retire from the medical faculty of Johns Hopkins. In a farewell speech, Osler talked about the link between age and accomplishment: The “effective, moving, vitalizing work of the world is done between the ages of 25 and 40 — these 15 golden years of plenty.”', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/education/edl-22middleage-t_CA0/edl-22middleage-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/education/edl-22middleage-t_CA0/edl-22middleage-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/education/edl-22middleage-t_CA0/edl-22middleage-t_CA0-jumbo.j