ès will take over as the company’s chief executive on Feb. 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Swiss Re, the world’s second-largest reinsurer, said on Thursday that Michel M. Liès will take over as the company’s chief executive on Feb. 1.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Swiss Re Appoints New Chief Executive', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Swiss Re', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T11:33:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c39f553-067f-51dc-a1cd-e4cced68be53', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c39f553-067f-51dc-a1cd-e4cced68be53'}, {'abstract': 'LaDainian Tomlinson said the Jets’ rowdy roster was a direct reflection of the team’s coach and general manager.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/tomlinson-says-rex-ryan-should-tone-it-down/', 'snippet': 'LaDainian Tomlinson said the Jets’ rowdy roster was a direct reflection of the team’s coach and general manager.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the Steelers traded Santonio Holmes to the Jets for a fifth-round pick in April 2010, this question was posed on The Fifth Down:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tomlinson Says Rex Ryan Should Tone It Down', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holmes, Santonio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Rex', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomlinson, Ladainian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T11:41:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a64637bd-7449-548e-897c-73ae455c29bb', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a64637bd-7449-548e-897c-73ae455c29bb'}, {'abstract': 'A great vegetable tempura deserves an amazing sauce. Some monkish devotion required.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/magazine/eat-vegetable-tempura-sauce.html', 'snippet': 'A great vegetable tempura deserves an amazing sauce. Some monkish devotion required.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of years ago, a friend told me that a vegan Japanese restaurant called Kajitsu was doing “the best food in the city.” I ignored him. (Typical: I ignored him when he told me about Noma, and I at first ignored friends who told me about Momofuku, El Bulli and, in 1987, the young chefs Jean-Georges Vongerichten and Thomas Keller. So much for the vision thing.) After this friend called me stupid once or twice, I made it over to the place, which is in the East Village, just down the block from the Good Beer Store. The word “best” should not be thrown around, but I will say that Kajitsu is distinctive, astonishing and wonderful.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '48', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22eat1_span/22eat1_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22eat1_span/22eat1_span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22eat1_span/22eat1_span-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22eat1_span/22eat1_span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1012, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22eat1_span/22eat1_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22eat1_span/22eat1_span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22eat1_span/22eat1_span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sauce Worth Slaving Over', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Worcestershire the Hard Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kajitsu (NYC Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T11:55:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13e96555-11ef-54e3-b961-46d2c02bea23', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13e96555-11ef-54e3-b961-46d2c02bea23'}, {'abstract': 'Business group members say that, in their male-dominated industries, men tend to bully them to try to get what they want: “They think that because you’re a woman, you’re just going to cave at some point.”', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/do-men-treat-female-business-owners-differently/', 'snippet': 'Business group members say that, in their male-dominated industries, men tend to bully them to try to get what they want: “They think that because you’re a woman, you’re just going to cave at some point.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many ways a factory can botch an order of dresses. Susan Parker spent the last month of 2011 dealing with a couple of them. She shared her experiences during the most recent meeting of our business group, and we wandered into a discussion of the challenges faced by women who own businesses, especially those operating in male-dominated industries like the garment business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do Men Treat Female Business Owners Differently?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T12:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/285e4bcf-a1ae-5b6c-8821-2deeb1198b97', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/285e4bcf-a1ae-5b6c-8821-2deeb1198b97'}, {'abstract': 'A document more than 200 years old is much smaller, both in dollars spent and in the number of pages filled, but in some ways has hints of what critics assail as pork-barrel spending.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/examining-a-post-revolutionary-war-federal-budget/', 'snippet': 'A document more than 200 years old is much smaller, both in dollars spent and in the number of pages filled, but in some ways has hints of what critics assail as pork-barrel spending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is going to sound unpleasantly like a question on a high school history exam: Compare and contrast the federal budget of 1797-98 with the federal budget of 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Federal Budget of Just $10 Million, but Something’s Familiar', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Winter Antiques Show', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T12:05:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f032e355-6911-540b-8b31-35925d0bb30b', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f032e355-6911-540b-8b31-35925d0bb30b'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney’s unofficial victory in the 2012 Iowa caucus will now have an asterisk.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/the-iowa-caucuses-will-have-no-official-winner/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney’s unofficial victory in the 2012 Iowa caucus will now have an asterisk.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:25 p.m. | Updated  Rick Santorum’s campaign claimed a belated victory in the Iowa caucuses on Thursday morning after certified results from the contest showed him leading Mitt Romney by 34 votes, a reversal from the eight-vote edge for Mr. Romney on caucus night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Santorum Edges Ahead of Romney in Iowa', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T12:13:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear and Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f3cdfdc-962f-53a4-b5e6-5039d2680d4a', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f3cdfdc-962f-53a4-b5e6-5039d2680d4a'}, {'abstract': 'Milos Raonic has recovered from a hip injury last year to resume his climb in men’s tennis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/sports/tennis/20iht-tennis20.html', 'snippet': 'Milos Raonic has recovered from a hip injury last year to resume his climb in men’s tennis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — It is the shot, the gift, that could make Milos Raonic a big tennis star in an era already brimming with them. It begins with Raonic selecting the most promising of three balls and stepping to the baseline.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/tennis/20iht-arena20/20iht-arena20-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 846, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/tennis/20iht-arena20/20iht-arena20-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/tennis/20iht-arena20/20iht-arena20-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Serve, Bright Future for a Young Canadian', 'kicker': 'In the Arena', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Serve, Bright Future For a Young Canadian', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montenegro', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petzschner, Philipp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T12:17:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a59cd416-085f-5bbc-934b-25f224bed73c', 'word_count': 1136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a59cd416-085f-5bbc-934b-25f224bed73c'}, {'abstract': 'Egypt’s revolutionaries have been left out in the cold by mainstream Egyptians, who now favor stability over more radical change.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/egypts-revolutionaries-abandoned-by-the-mainstream/', 'snippet': 'Egypt’s revolutionaries have been left out in the cold by mainstream Egyptians, who now favor stability over more radical change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — When I first met Sally Toma last year, she was flush with victory. After 18 days of protests in Tahrir Square, Hosni Mubarak, Egypt’s long-time strongman, had been toppled and the credit went to the Coalition of Revolution Youth, the 17-member committee of representatives from different youth groups that had started the protests. Toma, a 33-year-old psychiatrist, was the only woman and Coptic Christian member.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What a Difference a Year Makes', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and 