 in the fourth quarter was the Wall Street firm’s global wealth management division.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/morgan-stanley-reports-a-loss-as-settlement-weighs-on-results/', 'snippet': 'The one main bright spot in the fourth quarter was the Wall Street firm’s global wealth management division.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Morgan Stanley, hit hard by a big legal charge and a difficult economy, swung into the red in the fourth quarter, reporting a loss of $275 million. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morgan Stanley Reports Loss as Settlement Weighs on Results', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorman, James P', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T12:56:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eda12fd3-632d-51eb-b357-3ab80fea5df7', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eda12fd3-632d-51eb-b357-3ab80fea5df7'}, {'abstract': '“Red Tails” is a whiz-bang action film about the Tuskegee Airmen, African-American fighter pilots in World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/movies/red-tails-george-lucass-tale-of-tuskegee-airmen-review.html', 'snippet': '“Red Tails” is a whiz-bang action film about the Tuskegee Airmen, African-American fighter pilots in World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Patriotic,” “jingoistic,” “old-fashioned,” “corny” and “inspirational for teenage boys.” Those are the words of George Lucas, the executive producer of “Red Tails,” describing his whiz-bang action film about African-American fighter pilots in World War II on “The Daily Show With Jon Stewart.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/movies/red-tails/red-tails-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/18/movies/red-tails/red-tails-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/movies/red-tails/red-tails-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/18/movies/red-tails/red-tails-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/18/movies/red-tails/red-tails-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pilots Who Fought to Soar Above Racism', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Red Tails'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pilots Who Fought To Soar Above Racism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tuskegee Airmen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucas, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gooding Jr, Cuba', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Terrence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Red Tails (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T13:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/67a46d96-d88a-5ee6-98c9-f198c1fa0e41', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67a46d96-d88a-5ee6-98c9-f198c1fa0e41'}, {'abstract': 'The play “Peter and the Starcatcher” will transfer to Broadway in March.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/peter-and-the-starcatcher-will-land-on-broadway-in-march/', 'snippet': 'The play “Peter and the Starcatcher” will transfer to Broadway in March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peter Pan is coming back to Broadway – though not the flying, singing Peter who audiences know well. Rick Elice’s play “Peter and the Starcatcher,” which had a well-reviewed Off Broadway run at New York Theater Workshop last spring, will begin preview performances at the Brooks Atkinson Theater on March 28 and open on April 15, the producers of the show said on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Peter and the Starcatcher’ Will Land on Broadway in March', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Peter and the Starcatcher (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barry, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borle, Christian', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chanler-Berat, Adam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elice, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pearson, Ridley', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rees, Roger', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Timbers, Alex', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Disney, Walt, Theatrical Productions', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Theater Workshop', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T13:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82546c07-1cec-59a0-8cff-c8e1fb727b79', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82546c07-1cec-59a0-8cff-c8e1fb727b79'}, {'abstract': 'Turnovers are the least consistent, most random aspects of team performance, which is why my efficiency model puts the Giants as the superior team.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/title-game-probabilities-giants-should-be-favored/', 'snippet': 'Turnovers are the least consistent, most random aspects of team performance, which is why my efficiency model puts the Giants as the superior team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recency bias is when we overemphasize the importance of recent events, just as many observers are doing this week with the most recent Ravens and Patriots games. Baltimore eked out a win over the Texans with a lackluster performance on offense, while New England dominated the Broncos on both sides of the ball. Don’t put too much stock in those two games. In Baltimore’s case, keep in mind that Houston owned one of the very best defenses this season, allowing only 5.2 yards per pass attempt and yielding only a 39 percent run success rate, good for second and seventh in the league. And regarding New England, remember that Denver was overmatched in several departments and had backed into the playoffs with a mediocre record.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Title Game Probabilities: Giants Should Be Favored', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T13:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27ef3bb4-fc57-502d-8392-cc5aaebb61f9', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27ef3bb4-fc57-502d-8392-cc5aaebb61f9'}, {'abstract': 'The number of veterans receiving government assistance for their energy bills hit a new high last year.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/more-veterans-receive-help-with-heating-bills/', 'snippet': 'The number of veterans receiving government assistance for their energy bills hit a new high last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The number of low-income veterans receiving government assistance for their heating and cooling bills hit a new high last year, according to a survey by a federal energy-assistance program.Over the last four years, the survey found, the number of low-income households with at least one military veteran receiving federal energy assistance rose by about 1.1 million households, to 1.78 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '