rain’s aging process by up to a decade, adding a new twist to the cost-benefit analysis of higher education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Research shows that education is an essential element to keeping the brain fit as it ages, an issue explored by the New York Times reporter Patricia Cohen in the latest issue of Education Life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boosting Mental Fitness in Middle Age', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intelligence (IQ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T15:22:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c4f5a7f-437b-5db2-a64c-fbf57c68ebff', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c4f5a7f-437b-5db2-a64c-fbf57c68ebff'}, {'abstract': 'After a giant New York Lottery sign crashed onto a highway last week, questions arose over whether such signs are even legal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/nyregion/years-after-nyc-billboard-ban-loopholes-remain.html', 'snippet': 'After a giant New York Lottery sign crashed onto a highway last week, questions arose over whether such signs are even legal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, the debate about the giant advertising signs that line New York City’s highways has centered on whether they are hazardous as distractions to drivers, not as man-made sequoias that could topple over and destroy cars and buildings.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'sourc