7f-5ef0-a23d-ebaf2a33c7d7'}, {'abstract': 'Corporate sponsors are back en mass at the Sundance Film Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/sundance-brought-to-you-by-your-brand-here/', 'snippet': 'Corporate sponsors are back en mass at the Sundance Film Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — As Sundance devotees swarmed this ski town for another orgy of indie film — required accoutrements: iPhone, messy haircut, precious-looking glasses — they encountered creatures that have been relatively scarce in recent years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sundance, Brought to You by (Your Brand Here)', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Pictures Entertainment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sundance Institute', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park City (Utah)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T15:32:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f187732c-eeb7-5e66-a26c-edf1c73935c4', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f187732c-eeb7-5e66-a26c-edf1c73935c4'}, {'abstract': 'A group is selling carbon credits to finance wetlands restoration along the Gulf Coast.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/calculating-the-carbon-value-of-a-swamp/', 'snippet': 'A group is selling carbon credits to finance wetlands restoration along the Gulf Coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A nonprofit organization and a Gulf Coast electric company have come up with a way that might raise money to help protect New Orleans and surrounding areas from storms made worse by climate change – by collecting funds from people who feel bad about their carbon dioxide emissions. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calculating the Carbon Value of a Swamp', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wetlands', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Entergy Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf Coast (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T15:41:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ad8deea-e594-5177-ab42-a122700df7d2', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ad8deea-e594-5177-ab42-a122700df7d2'}, {'abstract': 'Rick Santorum may have edged out Mitt Romney in Iowa, after all. But it doesn’t matter.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/and-the-official-winner-in-iowa-is-who-cares/', 'snippet': 'Rick Santorum may have edged out Mitt Romney in Iowa, after all. But it doesn’t matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I travel to Iowa for the caucuses every four years, like all political journalists, but I’ve never quite understood the point. Yes, I know Iowa is commonly referred to as the first delegate selection contest in the nation. But it’s not. No delegates are actually selected at the caucuses. It’s supposed to be a bellwether for the nation, but it’s not. The Iowa caucuses, especially the Republican ones, have a mixed record at predicting the next nominee, and a fairly bad one at predicting the next president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'And the Official Winner in Iowa Is … Who Cares?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T15:42:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bcadb03-8b47-5298-9e7e-5c3d4b46d690', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bcadb03-8b47-5298-9e7e-5c3d4b46d690'}, {'abstract': 'The British government may strip Frederick A. Goodwin of his knighthood because of his role as chief executive in the failure of the Royal Bank of Scotland, which had to be bailed out by the government.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/to-sir-with-regret/', 'snippet': 'The British government may strip Frederick A. Goodwin of his knighthood because of his role as chief executive in the failure of the Royal Bank of Scotland, which had to be bailed out by the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Frederick A. Goodwin, the former chief executive of Royal Bank of Scotland, might be stripped of his knighthood because of his role in the failure of the bank, which had to be bailed out by the government.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Sir, With Regret', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodwin, Frederick A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Scotland PLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T15:44:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72a57374-a187-5566-a7d4-8fd52f2f375e', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72a57374-a187-5566-a7d4-8fd52f2f375e'}, {'abstract': 'Jarryd Wallace, a champion runner in high school, lost his right leg but not his determination to compete. He is now a contender to participate in the 2012 London Paralympics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/sports/paralympian-jarryd-wallace-stil-has-races-to-be-won.html', 'snippet': 'Jarryd Wallace, a champion runner in high school, lost his right leg but not his determination to compete. He is now a contender to participate in the 2012 London Paralympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS, Ga. — Jarryd Wallace came home from church on a springtime Sunday in 2008 to an afternoon any runner would find inviting, especially a middle-distance high school state champion like him who was passionate about his sport. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/20paralympian1/20paralympian1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/20paralympian1/20paralympian1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/20paralympian1/20paralympian1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/20paralympian1/20paralympian1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/20paralympian1/20paralympian1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Losing a Leg, New Races to Be Won', 'kicker': None, 'content_ki