1399-6083-504b-ad6b-cb498897b978'}, {'abstract': 'Big mistakes almost always start as small mistakes, and then people delay doing something about them.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/why-youre-waiting-too-long-to-fix-money-mistakes/', 'snippet': 'Big mistakes almost always start as small mistakes, and then people delay doing something about them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a certified financial planner in Park City, Utah. His new book, “The Behavior Gap,” was published earlier this month. His sketches are archived here on the Bucks blog. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why You’re Waiting Too Long to Fix Money Mistakes', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T15:55:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/adcb1c27-be1b-56c4-aedf-6b2781f53dc5', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adcb1c27-be1b-56c4-aedf-6b2781f53dc5'}, {'abstract': 'City Room seeks suggestions for a replacement to the semipermanent stickers that the City Council called “unnecessarily punitive” to motorists whose vehicles interfere with street cleaning.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/wanted-a-friendlier-sign-of-parking-shame/', 'snippet': 'City Room seeks suggestions for a replacement to the semipermanent stickers that the City Council called “unnecessarily punitive” to motorists whose vehicles interfere with street cleaning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What warm soapy water, rubbing alcohol and razor blades could not do, the City Council accomplished on Wednesday with a unanimous voice vote: the hated yellow-green Sticker of Shame that the city affixes semipermanently to cars that dare to interfere with street cleaning is being done away with.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wanted: A Friendlier Sign of Parking Shame', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parking', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T15:58:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76e0046f-4d8e-5482-b094-77044ff3c0bf', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76e0046f-4d8e-5482-b094-77044ff3c0bf'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Tachman’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/photos-of-the-moment-mugler-2/', 'snippet': 'Kevin Tachman’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of the Moment | Mugler', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T16:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Tachman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tachman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9bdf62b-4632-5ea9-8744-28e07d6b5ae3', 'word_count': 32, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9bdf62b-4632-5ea9-8744-28e07d6b5ae3'}, {'abstract': 'A photographic tour of the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/22/travel/22HAMBURG.html', 'snippet': 'A photographic tour of the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A photographic tour of the city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22HAMBURG-slide-VHXT/22HAMBURG-slide-VHXT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22HAMBURG-slide-VHXT/22HAMBURG-slide-VHXT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22HAMBURG-slide-VHXT/22HAMBURG-slide-VHXT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours: Hamburg, Germany', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamburg (Germany)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T16:05:02+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/b8ae12b6-90cd-5287-b978-3550d3ad78d2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b8ae12b6-90cd-5287-b978-3550d3ad78d2'}, {'abstract': 'More gilt than grit in Germany’s second city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/travel/36-hours-hamburg-germany.html', 'snippet': 'More gilt than grit in Germany’s second city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NO one tells you how pretty Hamburg is. That’s because so few people mention Hamburg in the first place. American tourists and businesspeople gravitate toward other German cities: Berlin, Munich, Frankfurt. And so Hamburg, bigger than all but Berlin, remains a bit of a mystery, poised to become a thrilling discovery. Did you know about the lake? It’s smack dab in the city center and skirted by regal buildings, a postcard-ready tableau if there ever was one. And the canals? They lattice the part of the city nearest the Elbe River, allowing Hamburg to joust with Stockholm, Amsterdam and Bruges for informal rights to call itself the Venice of northern Europe. Hamburg in winter is cold and often gray. No getting around that. But the indoors migration of many Hamburg residents gives the city a quiet and peace that I relished on a recent visit. Sure, the blustery weather persuaded me to skip the lake ferries and Elbe cruises recommended in summertime. But it wasn’t an obstacle to appreciating Hamburg’s formidable charms.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22HOURS3_SPAN/22HOURS3_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22HOURS3_SPAN/22HOURS3_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22HOURS3_SPAN/22HOURS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22HOURS3_SPAN/22HOURS3_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22HOURS3_SPAN/22HOURS3_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours: Hamburg, Germany', 'kicker': '36 Hours ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hamburg, Germany', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hamburg (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T16:05:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f0de22e-5d14-5cf1-8684-cf87b36f3e20', 'word_count': 1453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f0de22e-5d14-5cf1-8684-cf87b36f3e20'}, {'abstract': 'The repeated aid efforts come as Iran has aimed belligerent warnings aimed at the Navy’s Fifth Fleet, which has patrolled the Persian Gulf for decades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/world/middleeast/united-states-navy-says-it-assists-third-iranian-crew-in-distress.html', 'snippet': 'The repeated aid efforts come as Iran has aimed belligerent warnings aimed at the Navy’s Fifth Fleet, which has patrolled the Persian Gulf for decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the third time in less than a month, an American naval vessel came to the aid of Iranian mariners near the Persian Gulf, providing food and water to the crew of a sinking fishing dhow in the central Arabian Sea, the Navy said Thursday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Navy Says It Assists Third Iranian Crew in Distress', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Navy Says It Assists Third Iranian Crew in Distress', 'name': None, 'se