ginal': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6e5a83a-860c-56f0-955c-4b2df429fce9', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6e5a83a-860c-56f0-955c-4b2df429fce9'}, {'abstract': 'For Broadway veterans, nothing less than pride is on the line when “Smash,” the prime-time soap about the making of a musical, opens on Feb. 6 on NBC.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/arts/television/smash-on-nbc-about-broadway-with-katharine-mcphee.html', 'snippet': 'For Broadway veterans, nothing less than pride is on the line when “Smash,” the prime-time soap about the making of a musical, opens on Feb. 6 on NBC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DECADES before his elaborate film productions like “E.T.” and “Saving Private Ryan,” Steven Spielberg cut his teeth as a high school stage manager in Phoenix, feeding lines to forgetful actors in “Guys and Dolls” and trying to keep the members of a large “Brigadoon” cast from turning into bumper cars. Backstage drama provided the first adrenaline rush of his career, he said, and always struck him as good material. So much so that, a few years ago, Mr. Spielberg began shopping around a television series set on Broadway, but he met with rejection from HBO (where he made “Band of Brothers”) and the broadcast networks.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22SMASH_SPAN/22SMASH_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22SMASH_SPAN/22SMASH_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22SMASH_SPAN/22SMASH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22SMASH_SPAN/22SMASH_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22SMASH_SPAN/22SMASH_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Broadway’s Big Prime-Time Moment', 'kicker': 'Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Broadway’s Big Prime-Time Moment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Messing, Debra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huston, Anjelica', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T17:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67cb781b-19db-57a5-9964-a603ba20e155', 'word_count': 1855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67cb781b-19db-57a5-9964-a603ba20e155'}, {'abstract': 'After three years in second place, General Motors reclaimed its title due to strong sales in every region of the globe. The automaker surpassed Volkswagen as Toyota fell to third.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/business/gm-back-on-top-in-world-automaking.html', 'snippet': 'After three years in second place, General Motors reclaimed its title due to strong sales in every region of the globe. The automaker surpassed Volkswagen as Toyota fell to third.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — After three years of settling for second place, General Motors reclaimed its title as the world’s largest automaker in 2011, a year when its sales grew in every region of the globe while Toyota sales were hampered by major natural disasters.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.M. Regains the Top Spot in Global Automaking', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.M. Regains The Top Spot In Global Automaking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen A.G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T17:03:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bunkley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bunkley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12c74ba6-f7cb-545e-a840-2e2cd20ac378', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12c74ba6-f7cb-545e-a840-2e2cd20ac378'}, {'abstract': 'An antithesis of the season’s ubiquitous minipack.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/the-get-victoria-beckham-shopper/', 'snippet': 'An antithesis of the season’s ubiquitous minipack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For spring Victoria Beckham is introducing a half-canvas version of her signature shopper, available in mid-February. Featuring an extra-large open interior, rigid body and short, strict handles, this bag is the antithesis of the season’s ubiquitous minipack and is, most likely, a lot more functional. Clean with modern finishes (light gold hardware, single zipper pouch inside) and not a logo in sight, the canvas shopper also comes in navy, orange and yellow leather. Get ready to literally hold everything.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Victoria Beckham Shopper', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckham, Victoria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Net-A-Porter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T17:06:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c69d6a3-6dad-5a28-9e65-0eeba8d33a92', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c69d6a3-6dad-5a28-9e65-0eeba8d33a92'}, {'abstract': 'Jeremy Gleick’s favorite learning material.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/education/edlife/gleicks-picks.html', 'snippet': 'Jeremy Gleick’s favorite learning material.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few of Jeremy Gleick’s favorite learning experiences:', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gleick’s Picks', 'kicker': 'Lifelong Learning', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gleick’s Picks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'k