com/2012/01/22/education/edlife/common-app-4-0.html', 'snippet': 'The all-purpose form is getting a digital makeover. For students, that could mean no more cut off wor ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR the current crop of high school sophomores as well as those bobbing behind them in middle school, the technical process of applying to college using the Common Application is likely to be more streamlined (and less frustrating) than it was for their older brothers and sisters, to say nothing of their parents.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/education/edl-22choice-t_CA0/edl-22choice-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 125, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/education/edl-22choice-t_CA0/edl-22choice-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 125}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/education/edl-22choice-t_CA0/edl-22choice-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/education/edl-22choice-t_CA0/edl-22choice-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/education/edl-22choice-t_CA0/edl-22choice-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Common App 4.0', 'kicker': 'The Choice | Admissions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Common App 4.0', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Common Application, The', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98872108-5cfa-5289-9a86-35bc9e13b52e', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98872108-5cfa-5289-9a86-35bc9e13b52e'}, {'abstract': 'Stock options allow companies to create incentives for employees that don’t involve cash, but they also create a complicated and costly administrative burden. We went looking for an alternative.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/giving-employees-a-stake-in-the-outcome/', 'snippet': 'Stock options allow companies to create incentives for employees that don’t involve cash, but they also create a complicated and costly administrative burden. We went looking for an alternative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Compensation is one of the most complex and challenging topics I have come across during my eight years as chief executive of TerraCycle. By definition, it is a highly personal topic that is charged with emotion for employees and can involve their personal aspirations, their sense of self worth and pressures they feel at home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giving Employees a Stake in the Outcome', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stock Options and Purchase Plans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TerraCycle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Szaky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szaky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/582ea4a0-90d1-58ba-8026-03b18a194858', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/582ea4a0-90d1-58ba-8026-03b18a194858'}, {'abstract': 'A preview of a column in The Times’s Education Life Supplement about forthcoming changes to the universal form for applying to more than 450 colleges and universities.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/common-app-4-0/', 'snippet': 'A preview of a column in The Times’s Education Life Supplement about forthcoming changes to the universal form for applying to more than 450 colleges and universities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Common Application has become such a ubiquitous mode of transport on the road to college — an estimated 750,000 students have used the universal form to apply to more than 450 colleges this school year alone — that it may be hard for today’s applicants to appreciate that the form is younger than most of their parents (it’s 36) and was typically submitted by paper (via the U.S. Postal Service) as recently as a decade ago. In fact, the form has grown so popular so quickly that it will soon outstrip the capacity of its technological underpinnings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coming Soon to a Laptop Near You: Common Application 4.0', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84c55366-944d-5ad1-a010-2b4af8c9e972', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84c55366-944d-5ad1-a010-2b4af8c9e972'}, {'abstract': 'At the Walt Disney World Resort in Orlando, President Obama announced several initiatives intended to encourage more foreign tourists to visit the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/in-florida-obama-to-announce-new-tourism-policies/', 'snippet': 'At the Walt Disney World Resort in Orlando, President Obama announced several initiatives intended to encourage more foreign tourists to visit the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:00 p.m. | Updated Brazilians and Chinese who want to visit the United States will have a much easier time under an executive order issued by President Obama on Thursday, and that’s fuel for the economy of Florida, where he traveled to get as much political mileage as possible from the change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Florida, Obama Announces New Tourism Policies', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c0ecfe2-6b82-526e-be1f-d8b4c9707e88', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c0ecfe2-6b82-526e-be1f-d8b4c9707e88'}, {'abstract': 'The ratings for the season premiere of Fox’s “American Idol” on Wednesday were down more than 25 percent from last year.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/idol-premiere-draws-fewer-viewers-to-fox/', 'snippet': 'The ratings for the season premiere of Fox’s “American Idol” on Wednesday were down more than 25 percent from last year.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:16 p.m. | Updated Is this the year that television’s powerhouse will start to lose its mojo?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Idol’ Premiere Draws Fewer Viewers to Fox', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rating Systems (Media and Entertainment)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:08:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aceb7bba-4b2f-59b8-b7bf-bc05a0a5ee82', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aceb7bba-4b2f-59b8-b7bf-bc05a0a5ee82'}, {'abstract': 'A campaign that could have been, and a candidate who wasn’t up to it.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/exit-perry/', 'snippet': 'A campaign that could have been, and a candidate who wasn’t up to it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just after Rick Perry’s first appearance in a Republican primary debate, I wrote the following:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exit Perry', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:22:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edadb00a-1eed-50e0-bd83-6365f1bf7bf1', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edadb00a-1eed-50e0-bd83-6365f1bf7bf1'}, {'abstract': 'The unseeded Vania King, who upset Anastasia Pavlyuchenkova at the Australian Open, is also known for her singing, even though performing makes her nervous.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/for-vania-king-an-upset-and-then-a-song/', 'snippet': 'The unseeded Vania King, who upset Anastasia Pavlyuchenkova at the Australian Open, is also known for her singing, even though performing makes her nervous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia – She sang only a few phrases of “Dream a Little Dream of Me,” but they spoke volumes about unseeded Vania King, a 22-year-old American who had just pulled an upset at the Australian Open.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Vania King, an Upset and Then a Song', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:27:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN MARTIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MARTIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecadff5a-e0c5-5bcd-94e3-76eecb99c4f2', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecadff5a-e0c5-5bcd-94e3-76eecb99c4f2'}, {'abstract': 'Gen. Martin E. Dempsey is expected to focus on Iran’s nuclear program, as well as the challenges posed by the past year’s regional upheavals and the American military exit from Iraq.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/world/middleeast/top-united-states-military-general-martin-dempsey-in-israel-for-talks-on-iran.html', 'snippet': 'Gen. Martin E. Dempsey is expected to focus on Iran’s nuclear program, as well as the challenges posed by the past year’s regional upheavals and the American military exit from Iraq.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Gen. Martin E. Dempsey, chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, arrived in Israel on Thursday for a 24-hour visit with the country’s top leaders that is expected to focus on Iran’s nuclear program as well as the challenges posed by the past year’s regional upheavals and the American military exit from Iraq.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. General Visits Israel for Discussions on Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. General Visits Israel For Discussions on Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joint Chiefs of Staff', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Martin E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:28:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ethan Bronner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ethan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bronner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6d44fec-d467-5dc4-a6e2-017e2c527f32', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6d44fec-d467-5dc4-a6e2-017e2c527f32'}, {'abstract': 'The Sundance Film Festival’s programmers are predicting that the documentary “Searching for Sugar Man,” about a forgotten 1970s-era rocker, will be this year’s world cinema audience favorite.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/at-sundance-an-instance-audience-award-contender/', 'snippet': 'The Sundance Film Festival’s programmers are predicting that the documentary “Searching for Sugar Man,” about a forgotten 1970s-era rocker, will be this year’s world cinema audience favorite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — Sundance’s programmers know their festival extremely well. In 2010, insiders predicted that Josh Radnor’s “Happythankyoumoreplease” would win the audience award. It did. Last year, the whisper from Sundance headquarters involved Peter Richardson’s “How to Die in Oregon,” a heart-wrenching documentary about assisted suicide. It could be a strong contender for best documentary. Yep; it won.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Sundance, an Instant Audience-Award Contender', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Radnor, Josh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park City (Utah)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2eff2b3d-6183-5b85-82d9-2e8aeb692475', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2eff2b3d-6183-5b85-82d9-2e8aeb692475'}, {'abstract': 'The long search for a suspect in a fatal shooting in 2010 ended last week with a routine vehicle stop.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/from-killing-to-arrest-16-months/', 'snippet': 'The long search for a suspect in a fatal shooting in 2010 ended last week with a routine vehicle stop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Riddled with bullets, the victim’s body fell in the courtyard of a building on the southern edge of Chinatown, in the shadow of 1 Police Plaza. The gunman ran. But who killed Anthony Evans, a suspected drug dealer, took little time for Fifth Precinct detectives to surmise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From a Killing to an Arrest: 16 Months', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Civilian Complaint Review Board', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:31:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a60c46f3-f989-5abc-b494-7866941be50a', 'word_count': 948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a60c46f3-f989-5abc-b494-7866941be50a'}, {'abstract': 'Advice on dealing with relatives’ dietary restrictions, an inedible restaurant dish and a fiancé who demands meat at every meal.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/dear-flofab-how-to-feed-a-family-with-so-many-taboos/', 'snippet': 'Advice on dealing with relatives’ dietary restrictions, an inedible restaurant dish and a fiancé who demands meat at every meal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Valentine’s Day approaches, with its perilous combination of food, romance and tricky etiquette, Florence Fabricant would love to help with advice on the fine points of entertaining at home and eating in restaurants. Have a question concerning the holiday — or any dining dilemma? Ask FloFab.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dear FloFab: How to Feed a Family With So Many Taboos?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:32:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2837ae68-3741-5baa-bfac-f95e17f815af', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2837ae68-3741-5baa-bfac-f95e17f815af'}, {'abstract': 'After winning his first four sets at the Australian Open in convincing fashion, Andy Roddick retired because of an injury in his second-round match against Lleyton Hewitt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/sports/tennis/roddick-quits-australian-open-with-hamstring-injury.html', 'snippet': 'After winning his first four sets at the Australian Open in convincing fashion, Andy Roddick retired because of an injury in his second-round match against Lleyton Hewitt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — After winning his first four sets at the Australian Open in convincing fashion, the No. 15 seed Andy Roddick was forced to retire Thursday because of an injury after the third set of his second-round match against his longtime rival Lleyton Hewitt. Hewitt was ahead, 3-6, 6-3, 6-4.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/tennis/20roddick2/20roddick2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/tennis/20roddick2/20roddick2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/tennis/20roddick2/20roddick2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Roddick’s Frustration, Injury Curtails a Strong Start', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Roddick’s Frustration, Injury Curtails A Strong Start', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hewitt, Lleyton', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roddick, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Melbourne (Australia)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}],