, 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Etro: Fall 2012 Menswear', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:50:58+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Men's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/9ad1e95c-f8bf-54dc-9324-61bf04ace03e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/9ad1e95c-f8bf-54dc-9324-61bf04ace03e'}, {'abstract': 'Testimony by Secretary of State Clinton would highlight the pipeline divide, which Congressional Republicans have turned into an election-year issue.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/on-our-radar-house-panel-summons-clinton-on-pipeline/', 'snippet': 'Testimony by Secretary of State Clinton would highlight the pipeline divide, which Congressional Republicans have turned into an election-year issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fred Upton, the Republican chairman of the House Energy and Commerce Committee, says a subcommittee has asked Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton to testify next week on the Obama administration’s decision not to approve the Keystone XL pipeline. The pipeline project has emerged as a deeply partisan election-year issue. [The Hill]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: House Panel Summons Clinton on Keystone Pipeline', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:51:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4767230-f6bd-5b88-b0ed-162d143b3720', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4767230-f6bd-5b88-b0ed-162d143b3720'}, {'abstract': 'This is the last tax season that banks will be offering refund-anticipation loans.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/after-this-year-no-more-tax-refund-loans/', 'snippet': 'This is the last tax season that banks will be offering refund-anticipation loans.', 'lead_paragraph': '1/20/12 | Updated with elaboration on loan terms and comment from Republic Bank and Jackson Hewitt.This is the last tax season that any banks will be offering “refund anticipation loans,” according to the National Consumer Law Center.\xa0 The loans, called R.A.L.’s in the industry, are short term, repaid with a borrower’s income tax refund. Typically, the loans carried fat fees and were marketed through tax-preparation outlets to lower-income borrowers who wanted fast cash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After This Year, No More Tax Refund Loans', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'REFUNDS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'H&R Block Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internal Revenue Service', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:53:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5131397-d951-56b3-8b93-38addfe03633', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5131397-d951-56b3-8b93-38addfe03633'}, {'abstract': 'Construction of single-family homes reached a new low in 2011, but there are indications that an upturn is in the offing.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/signs-of-a-bottom-in-housing/', 'snippet': 'Construction of single-family homes reached a new low in 2011, but there are indications that an upturn is in the offing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A reminder that there is a housing crash in progress:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Signs of a Bottom in Housing', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:54:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcc57195-c8d2-5cb0-a0d2-3d015d9d2fbe', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcc57195-c8d2-5cb0-a0d2-3d015d9d2fbe'}, {'abstract': 'Investigators made two arrests and were pursuing at least a dozen rogue military officers and expatriates suspected of plotting to topple the government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/world/asia/bangladesh-army-claims-to-thwart-coup-attempt.html', 'snippet': 'Investigators made two arrests and were pursuing at least a dozen rogue military officers and expatriates suspected of plotting to topple the government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — The Bangladeshi Army announced Thursday that it had foiled a plot by rogue military officers and expatriate Bangladeshis that was intended to destabilize the democratic process and topple the elected government of Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina Wazed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bangladesh Army Claims to Thwart Coup Attempt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bangladesh Army Claims to Thwart Coup Attempt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:56:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sruthi Gottipati and Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee7d8c24-4eef-5d03-ac66-b0af366cf43d', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee7d8c24-4eef-5d03-ac66-b0af366cf43d'}, {'abstract': 'Bruce Springsteen’s new album, coming out March 6, is called “Wrecking Ball.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/new-springsteen-album-coming-on-march-6/', 'snippet': 'Bruce Springsteen’s new album, coming out March 6, is called “Wrecking Ball.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' Bruce Springteen announced on his Web site Thursday that he would release a new album, “Wrecking Ball,” on March 6, and he released the lead-off single to whet the appetite of his fans. Called “We Take Care of Our Own,” the track is musically upbeat but alludes to the economic and political climate in the United States, with lyrics like “Where’s the promise, from sea to shining sea?” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Springsteen Album Coming on March 6', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clemons, Clarence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springsteen, Bruce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'E Street Band', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T18:57:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89facf70-e9c8-5b72-aa09-e36087a47177', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89facf70-e9c8-5b72-aa09-e36087a47177'}, {'abstract': 'Chagrined by the failure of delegates to embrace agriculture as a formal priority in climate change talks in Durban, a group of experts calls for more research and advocacy on the world’s food system.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/agriculture-and-climate-change-revisited/', 'snippet': 'Chagrined by the failure of delegates to embrace agriculture as a formal priority in climate change talks in Durban, a group of experts calls for more research and advocacy on the world’s food system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Agriculture has long been a stepchild in global negotiations over the climate. Hopes had risen that this might change at the latest big global climate session, in Durban, South Africa, in December. It did not.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Agriculture and Climate Change, Revisited', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United Nations Framework Convention on Climate Change', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Science (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Durban (South Africa)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T19:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca1fa2c4-86f6-5315-a553-f242000e673a', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca1fa2c4-86f6-5315-a553-f242000e673a'}, {'abstract': 'Vehicles from the Swedish automaker’s museum, including the first Saab passenger car prototype, are to be auctioned Friday as part of the company’s ongoing bankruptcy restructuring.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/for-bankrupt-saab-a-wrenching-farewell-to-its-heritage/', 'snippet': 'Vehicles from the Swedish automaker’s museum, including the first Saab passenger car prototype, are to be auctioned Friday as part of the company’s ongoing bankruptcy restructuring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 100 Saabs, from the streamlined 1947 prototype known as the Ursaab to a 2010 9-5 sedan, are to be taken from their home at the company’s museum in Trollhattan, Sweden, and sold to the highest bidder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Bankrupt Saab, a Wrenching Farewell to Its Heritage', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antique and Classic Cars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Petersen Automotive Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saab Automobile AB', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T19:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2481b6fc-63d2-5281-8f8d-cf18ea9461fb', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2481b6fc-63d2-5281-8f8d-cf18ea9461fb'}, {'abstract': 'The FiveThirtyEight model now shows Newt Gingrich and Mitt Romney in a virtual tie in South Carolina, with each having about a 50 percent chance of winning the primary.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/gingrich-tied-with-romney-in-south-carolina-forecast/', 'snippet': 'The FiveThirtyEight model now shows Newt Gingrich and Mitt Romney in a virtual tie in South Carolina, with each having about a 50 percent chance of winning the primary.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Tied With Romney in South Carolina Forecast', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T19:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f49eff2-1841-5c80-8620-d0ec51f82d70', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f49eff2-1841-5c80-8620-d0ec51f82d70'}, {'abstract': 'When Adrien Brody wasn’t preparing for his modeling turn in the Prada show on Sunday, he was talking about trends in men’s facial hair.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/all-the-buzz-with-adrien-brody/', 'snippet': 'When Adrien Brody wasn’t preparing for his modeling turn in the Prada show on Sunday, he was talking about trends in men’s facial hair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Adrien Brody wasn’t preparing for his modeling turn in the Prada show on Sunday, he was talking about trends in men’s facial hair. Mr. Brody, who is turning into a veritable style guru, also has a relationship with Gillette, currently promoting something called a Fusion ProGlide Styler, which is a multitasking razor that is designed for trimming and edging.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia