market and restaurant, has begun selling house-made salamis and other pork products.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/il-buco-is-selling-its-own-salumi/', 'snippet': 'Il Buco Alimentari & Vineria, a market and restaurant, has begun selling house-made salamis and other pork products.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Il Buco Alimentari & Vineria, the newest of the city’s Italian market-restaurants, has just started selling assorted salamis and other cured pork products that it is making in-house. Among them are a tangy finocchiona salami lightly kissed with fennel; a lusty hunter’s sausage called cacciatorino; peppery Tuscan salami; a sweetly rich culatello, (similar to prosciutto; and an elegant nutty-sweet lonza (cured loin). Fatty products like guanciale, pancetta and lardo are deliciously buttery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Il Buco Is Selling Its Own Salumi', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pork', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Il Buco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bowery (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T20:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20d1bfbf-0471-5806-9e11-23da438f4a93', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20d1bfbf-0471-5806-9e11-23da438f4a93'}, {'abstract': 'Milan', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/15/fashion/runway-mens/burberry-prorsum-fall-2012-menswear.html', 'snippet': 'Milan', 'lead_paragraph': 'Milan', 'sourc