 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABC Worked for Months to Get Marianne Gingrich Interview', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Marianne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ross, Brian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Rhonda', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC News', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drudge Report', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T20:41:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b0d865e-917b-567c-8b62-d7661938e835', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b0d865e-917b-567c-8b62-d7661938e835'}, {'abstract': 'Sloane Stevens lost to Svetlana Kuznetsova in the Australian Open’s second round, but showed many strengths in her game.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/stephenss-talent-promise-evident-in-loss/', 'snippet': 'Sloane Stevens lost to Svetlana Kuznetsova in the Australian Open’s second round, but showed many strengths in her game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sloane Stephens’s close loss to the veteran Svetlana Kuznetsova in the second round of the Australian Open Thursday was filled with subtle lessons. She had chances to win the first set, but Kuznetsova prevailed, 8-6, in the tiebreaker. The set took 69 minutes and Stephens came away with nothing. It is perhaps the harshest aspect of the tennis scoring system: sets and games — no matter how close — are winner take all. Other sports (football and basketball come to mind) stop at halftime and each team still has a chance to win. In other words, the losing team’s points are not erased.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stephens’s Talent and Promise Evident in Loss', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T20:45:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By GEOFF MACDONALD', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MACDONALD', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd59da09-b92b-54b5-b51a-d1c289bf8e72', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd59da09-b92b-54b5-b51a-d1c289bf8e72'}, {'abstract': 'White Collar Watch examines the next steps in the government’s insider trading case against a “circle of friends” that prosecutors say included a co-founder of the Level Global hedge fund.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/yet-another-insider-case-begins-to-unfold/', 'snippet': 'White Collar Watch examines the next steps in the government’s insider trading case against a “circle of friends” that prosecutors say included a co-founder of the Level Global hedge fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The government has moved yet again in its effort to crack down on insider trading, filing charges against seven defendants with ties to hedge funds who federal prosecutors say operated as a “circle of friends” by trading information. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yet Another Insider Trading Case Begins to Unfold', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Level Global Investors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T20:47:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2ef8cb6-5bd3-5c7c-85c5-2a8154bff493', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2ef8cb6-5bd3-5c7c-85c5-2a8154bff493'}, {'abstract': 'House Republicans want Secretary of State Hillary Clinton to testify before a subcommittee on a decision to forgo a permit for the Keystone XL pipeline. Aides say she will probably send a top expert.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/state-department-readies-an-r-s-v-p/', 'snippet': 'House Republicans want Secretary of State Hillary Clinton to testify before a subcommittee on a decision to forgo a permit for the Keystone XL pipeline. Aides say she will probably send a top expert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Congressional Republicans,\xa0furious over President Obama’s rejection of the proposed Keystone XL pipeline, are calling for Secretary of State Hillary Clinton to address the State Department’s review of the project at a House hearing next week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State Department Readies an R.S.V.P.', 'kicker': 'Green', 'conte