ization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9dbed04-f094-5c56-ac1d-8e939bd58fee', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9dbed04-f094-5c56-ac1d-8e939bd58fee'}, {'abstract': 'It’s safe to assume that Rick Santorum did in fact win the Iowa caucuses, but that news is not liable to change anything now.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/the-semantics-and-statistics-of-santorums-win-in-iowa/', 'snippet': 'It’s safe to assume that Rick Santorum did in fact win the Iowa caucuses, but that news is not liable to change anything now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid the swirl of developments on Thursday came word from the Iowa Republican Party that it had certified the results from the state’s Jan. 3 caucuses — and that Rick Santorum, not Mitt Romney, had gotten more votes. Mr. Santorum received 29,839 votes in the state’s certified tally, 34 more than Mr. Romney, who had 29,805.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Semantics and Statistics of Santorum’s Win in Iowa', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T23:13:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c7c56df-c228-5b46-8ec9-3d3333f1e9f2', 'word_count': 1887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c7c56df-c228-5b46-8ec9-3d3333f1e9f2'}, {'abstract': 'Top runners race in Washington Heights, and champion squash players face off at Grand Central Terminal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/sports/high-level-track-and-field-and-squash-to-enjoy.html', 'snippet': 'Top runners race in Washington Heights, and champion squash players face off at Grand Central Terminal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miser’s new year exercise regime has not quite kicked in. No matter. This weekend is better for watching sports than for playing them. There’s a lot to choose from: squash at Grand Central Terminal and track and field at the Armory. Then next week there’s wrestling, the first tournament of the NYC Mayor’s Cup 2012 season, at the Harlem Armory.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/20MISER_SPAN/20MISER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/20MISER_SPAN/20MISER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/20MISER_SPAN/20MISER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/20MISER_SPAN/20MISER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/20MISER_SPAN/20MISER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'High-Level Track and Field and Squash to Enjoy', 'kicker': 'Weekend Miser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 