he 200-pound markers have vanished.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/realestate/streetscapes-the-trip-calculator-of-another-time.html', 'snippet': 'Before GPS, milestones gave riders and drivers of horses an idea of where they were. Today, most of the 200-pound markers have vanished.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEFORE GIS, before GPS, before Google Earth, there was the milestone. These heavy markers, inscribed with distances to City Hall or other locations, went up in series as early as 1769, and once numbered 40 or 50 in all. About two dozen now survive, mostly in museums. Even at several feet high and weighing 200 pounds, the markers have proved remarkably difficult to track. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/realestate/22STREET/streets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/realestate/22STREET/22STREET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/realestate/22STREET/22STREET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Trip Calculator of Another Time', 'kicker': 'STREETSCAPES/Milestones', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Trip Calculator of Another Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Signals and Signs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-19T23:17:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Gray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15e39922-fda0-5f6b-b4fe-76b9e478a349', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15e39922-fda0-5f6b-b4fe-76b9e478a349'}, {'abstract': 'The 2014 Olympic favorite from Canada died from injuries sustained last week in a fall during a training run in a 22-foot halfpipe at Park City Mountain Resort in Utah.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/sports/skiing/sarah-burke-canadian-freestyle-skier-dies-from-injuries.html', 'snippet': 'The 2014 Olympic favorite from Canada died from injuries sustained last week in a fall during a training run in a 22-foot halfpipe at Park City Mountain Resort in Utah.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hurtling down a towering halfpipe on a pair of skis, no maneuver is routine. But Sarah Burke had done this one, the 540 Flat Spin, countless times.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/20burke-2/20burke-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/20burke-2/20burke-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/20burke-2/20burke-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sarah Burke, Freestyle Skier, Dies From Injuries in Training', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ca