0-8928-b48b52197c46', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd964c38-52e2-5210-8928-b48b52197c46'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Sheirer, 65, led the Office of Emergency Management during the terrorist attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/richard-j-sheirer-city-emergency-chief-on-911-dies/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Sheirer, 65, led the Office of Emergency Management during the terrorist attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard J. Sheirer, the former head of the city’s Office of Emergency Management who led the agency during the Sept. 11 attacks, died on Thursday morning while driving to work in Manhattan, the city said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Richard J. Sheirer, City Emergency Chief on 9/11, Dies', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheirer, Richard J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'von Essen, Thomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Emergency Management (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T00:09:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7bd8ca7-9b2d-5213-8976-1bf7e9a1a9aa', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7bd8ca7-9b2d-5213-8976-1bf7e9a1a9aa'}, {'abstract': 'Jang Hun’s “Front Line,” a Korean War drama opening Friday in New York and Los Angeles, is South Korea’s submission for the Academy Award for best foreign language film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/movies/the-front-line-jang-huns-korean-war-drama-review.html', 'snippet': 'Jang Hun’s “Front Line,” a Korean War drama opening Friday in New York and Los Angeles, is South Korea’s submission for the Academy Award for best foreign language film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The barren expanse of rocks and dirt where most of Jang Hun’s Korean War drama, “The Front Line,” takes place is a hilly wasteland that has nothing of value beyond its strategic location near the disputed border of North Korea and South Korea. To watch the soldiers scrambling up and down slopes scarred with trenches and foxholes is to observe a maddening exercise in futility. Each engagement produces a new round of slaughter.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/20FRONTLINE_SPAN/20FRONTLINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/20FRONTLINE_SPAN/20FRONTLINE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/20FRONTLINE_SPAN/FRONT-LINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/20FRONTLINE_SPAN/20FRONTLINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/20FRONTLINE_SPAN/20FRONTLINE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Koreas, at War but Closely Entwined', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'The Front Line'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_hea