 Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moralizing’s High Cost', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moralizing&#8217;s High Cost', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Marianne', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Callista', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T00:26:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec366903-271e-5799-8e0f-918f33e6fd17', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec366903-271e-5799-8e0f-918f33e6fd17'}, {'abstract': 'Zack Parker’s “Scalene” is a disturbingly clever drama of triangulated tension among a mother, her mute son and his caregiver.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/movies/margo-martindale-in-zack-parkers-scalene-review.html', 'snippet': 'Zack Parker’s “Scalene” is a disturbingly clever drama of triangulated tension among a mother, her mute son and his caregiver.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Structured much like the triangle from which it takes its name, “Scalene” opens with a scene so volcanic and mystifying that we are immediately ensnared.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/movies/20RDP_SCALENE_SPAN/20RDP_SCALENE_