connection to security threats, calling the suggestion a “wild rumor.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rwanda: 4 Military Officers Arrested', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rwanda: 4 Military Officers Arrested', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Congo, Democratic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rwanda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T01:18:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/da893f96-32a0-5d36-9463-8cceb0052843', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da893f96-32a0-5d36-9463-8cceb0052843'}, {'abstract': 'The Elric brothers of “Fullmetal Alchemist” return to the animated screen to continue their quest for a philosopher’s stone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/movies/fullmetal-alchemist-the-sacred-star-of-milos-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Elric brothers of “Fullmetal Alchemist” return to the animated screen to continue their quest for a philosopher’s stone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome back the Elric brothers, Edward and Alphonse, heroes of the “Fullmetal Alchemist” franchise. You may not know them, but plenty of anime fanatics do: a manga that began in 2001, the property later became two television series (one still on the Cartoon Network) and later a feature. (“The Sacred Star of Milos” is the sequel.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/movies/20RDP_ALCHEMIST_SPAN/20RDP_ALCHEMIST_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/20/movies/20RDP_ALCHEMIST_SPAN/20RDP_ALCHEMIST_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/movies/20RDP_ALCHEMIST_SPAN/20RDP_ALCHEMIST_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/movies/20RDP_ALCHEMIST_SPAN/20RDP_ALCHEMIST_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/20/movies/20RDP_ALCHEMIST_SPAN/20RDP_ALCHEMIST_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anime Heroes to the Rescue', 'kicker': "Movie Review | 'Fullmetal Alchemist: The Sacred Star of Milos'", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T01:19:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/00639bf9-930b-5d65-a40c-6e8f479fee6a', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00639bf9-930b-5d65-a40c-6e8f479fee6a'}, {'abstract': 'A turquoise triangle that has become a part of the debate about online privacy is part of an ad campaign by the Digital Advertising Alliance, a group of digital advertising trade organizations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/business/media/the-push-for-online-privacy-advertising.html', 'snippet': 'A turquoise triangle that has become a part of the debate about online privacy is part of an ad campaign by the Digital Advertising Alliance, a group of digital advertising trade organizations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOMETHING viewed online billions of times a month would seem to need no further promotion, but that assumption falls short when the something in question — a turquoise triangle in the upper right-hand corner of banner ads — is a critical piece of the debate about online privacy. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/20/business/Adco/Adco-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/20/business/Adco/Adco-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Online Privacy, Click Here', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Online Privacy, Click Here', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T01:23:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/148aba13-2c29-5d32-a0ee-6982d74d0df2', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/148aba13-2c29-5d32-a0ee-6982d74d0df2'}, {'abstract': 'After CNN’s John King opened the debate with a direct question about the ABC News report on Marianne Gingrich’s allegations, Mr. Gingrich seized the opportunity.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/gingrich-angrily-denies-open-marriage-request-at-debate/', 'snippet': 'After CNN’s John King opened the debate with a direct question about the ABC News report on Marianne Gingrich’s allegations, Mr. Gingrich seized the opportunity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There may have been no better way for Newt Gingrich to hammer back at the personal allegations from his ex-wife than to make the media the enemy for telling her story.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Angrily Denies ‘Open Marriage’ Request at Debate', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T01:23:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c64cb452-479f-5184-b192-c37efc8c6939', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c64cb452-479f-5184-b192-c37efc8c6939'}, {'abstract': 'As Mitt Romney dances around calls for him to release his tax returns, a question about U.S. tax policy comes up: Why do the rich bear a startlingly light tax burden?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/opinion/krugman-taxes-at-the-top.html', 'snippet': 'As Mitt Romney dances around calls for him to release his tax returns, a question about U.S. tax policy comes up: Why do the rich bear a startlingly light tax burden?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Call me peculiar, but I’m actually enjoying the spectacle of Mitt Romney doing the Dance of the Seven Veils — partly out of voyeurism, of course, but also because it’s about time that we had this discussion.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-kru