pet': 'Aon, the giant Chicago-bred insurance brokerage, is moving 20 top executives so the company can be closer to emerging markets and to the major insurance center in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Warren is a columnist for the Chicago News Cooperative. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aon’s Move to Britain and a Fleeting Notion of Corporate Citizenship', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aon’s Move to Britain and a Fleeting Notion of Corporate Citizenship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AON CORP', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T01:31:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Warren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9369ea8-5a85-57be-a6b7-3123c793a3c0', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9369ea8-5a85-57be-a6b7-3123c793a3c0'}, {'abstract': 'Factoring corporate, state and local taxes into what the wealthiest — and other Americans — pay.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/more-on-romneys-tax-rate-and-everyone-elses/', 'snippet': 'Factoring corporate, state and local taxes into what the wealthiest — and other Americans — pay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are any number ways to calculate a household’s tax rate. You can look at just the federal income tax and conclude that almost half of Americans don’t pay taxes, or look at all taxes and conclude that a vast majority of Americans do pay taxes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More on Romney’s Tax Rate (and Everyone Else’s)', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T01:34:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e0ff3cf-0ae1-5463-9172-83bc8e5af336', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e0ff3cf-0ae1-5463-9172-83bc8e5af336'}, {'abstract': 'The Arab League must raise the pressure on President Bashar al-Assad and his cronies to stop the killing and make clear to them that their time has run out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/opinion/syrias-rising-toll.html', 'snippet': 'The Arab League must raise the pressure on President Bashar al-Assad and his cronies to stop the killing and make clear to them that their time has run out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The death toll from the brutal 10-month war by President Bashar al-Assad of Syria against his own people is now more than 5,400, according to the United Nations and others. Yet the international community still has not mustered the tough pressure that might force Mr. Assad to stop the killing, or Syria’s Army and business elite to toss him out.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria’s Rising Toll', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria&#8217;s Rising Toll', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T01:36:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c28d02e1-d6c6-5d4c-b55c-5926b4c3a45f', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c28d02e1-d6c6-5d4c-b55c-5926b4c3a45f'}, {'abstract': 'Whitney Sudler-Smith’s documentary about Halston demonstrates little interest in fashion and even less insight into that designer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/movies/ultrasuede-a-look-at-halston-and-the-70s-review.html', 'snippet': 'Whitney Sudler-Smith’s documentary about Halston demonstrates little interest in fashion and even less insight into that designer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early in “Ultrasuede: In Search of Halston,” Liza Minnelli, dressed in Halston stretch velvet leggings (“wonderful!”), gives the director, Whitney Sudler-Smith, a great pi