ng jobs, in the future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/opinion/a-milestone-in-fisheries-management.html', 'snippet': 'The limits set by the government on federally managed fish species will ensure that there will be fish, and fishing jobs, in the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration is about to reach a historic achievement. By May, the agency will have set annual catch limits for every federally managed fish species, more than 500 in all. What’s more, this vital task has been accomplished in a genuinely bipartisan manner. The law requiring annual limits, the Magnuson-Stevens Fishery Conservation and Management Act, was reauthorized in 2007 with support from President George W. Bush and has been carried out by the Obama administration. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Milestone in Fisheries Management', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Milestone in Fisheries Management', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T02:05:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e03aff80-e4aa-556a-98c9-0710aecd3645', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e03aff80-e4aa-556a-98c9-0710aecd3645'}, {'abstract': 'After playing in just one playoff game in his first 10 seasons, Justin Smith, an All-Pro defensive lineman, is enjoying leading the 49ers’ defense in the postseason.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/sports/football/49ers-justin-smith-is-finally-in-the-spotlight.html', 'snippet': 'After playing in just one playoff game in his first 10 seasons, Justin Smith, an All-Pro defensive lineman, is enjoying leading the 49ers’ defense in the postseason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTA CLARA, Calif. — \xa0The legend of Justin Smith began long before he shoved a Pro Bowl left tackle backward into his own quarterback, as if steering a child’s push toy, on national television. It began even before he chased down a wide receiver in the open field to cause a fumble earlier this season. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/NINERS2/NINERS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/NINERS2/NINERS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/NINERS2/NINERS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Brute Force Behind the 49ers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Brute Force Behind the 49ers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Justin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T02:07:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b18d850-bc7d-5b01-89cc-91eab0c00309', 'word_count': 1044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b18d850-bc7d-5b01-89cc-91eab0c00309'}, {'abstract': 'The Republican presidential candidates — minus one, after Rick Perry dropped out earlier Thursday — take the stage in Charleston, S.C., for the final debate before Saturday’s South Carolina primary.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/19/charleston-s-c-debate-live-blog/', 'snippet': 'The Republican presidential candidates — minus one, after Rick Perry dropped out earlier Thursday — take the stage in Charleston, S.C., for the final debate before Saturday’s South Carolina primary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican presidential candidates — minus one, after Rick Perry dropped out earlier Thursday — take the stage in Charleston, S.C., at 8 p.m. Eastern time Thursday for the final debate before Saturday’s South Carolina primary. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charleston, S.C., Debate Live Blog', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charleston (S