k Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Isner Falls in Five Sets to Lopez', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T09:29:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN MARTIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MARTIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea196cd3-6de4-5d77-be08-7efbbdae2fca', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea196cd3-6de4-5d77-be08-7efbbdae2fca'}, {'abstract': 'Amid a growing backlash over the power of the international ratings agencies, calls rise to set up a home-grown alternative to the U.S.-based big three — S.&P., Moody’s, and Fitch. In the meantime, central bankers say, pay them less attention.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/europe-downgrades-ratings-agencies/', 'snippet': 'Amid a growing backlash over the power of the international ratings agencies, calls rise to set up a home-grown alternative to the U.S.-based big three — S.&P., Moody’s, and Fitch. In the meantime, central bankers say, pay them less attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The sting caused by Standard & Poor’s downgrade of nine euro zone countries and the euro zone’s  temporary bailout fund is not mellowing with time. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Downgrades Ratings Agencies', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barnier, Michel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Mervyn A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westerwelle, Guido', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of England', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fitch Ratings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Investors Service Inc", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T09:30:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Archives', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/844700c8-cda3-5bce-914b-00dc9e29671d', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/844700c8-cda3-5bce-914b-00dc9e29671d'}, {'abstract': 'The author was targeted by assassins, he said, so won’t attend Asia’s largest literature festival.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/salman-rushdies-full-statement-on-the-jaipur-lit-fest/', 'snippet': 'The author was targeted by assassins, he said, so won’t attend Asia’s largest literature festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Author Salman Rushdie put out a statement Friday afternoon about his decision not to attend the Jaipur Literature Festival. Here is is in full: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Salman Rushdie’s Full Statement on the Jaipur Lit Fest', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T09:41:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE NEW YORK TIMES', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/042e8a23-eea0-5350-ac6b-bc529a0899e4', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/042e8a23-eea0-5350-ac6b-bc529a0899e4'}, {'abstract': 'Vodafone should not have to pay more than $4 billion in taxes related to a 2007 deal, the Supreme Court said.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/reactions-to-the-supreme-court-decision-on-vodafone/', 'snippet': 'Vodafone should not have to pay more than $4 billion in taxes related to a 2007 deal, the Supreme Court said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'India’s Supreme Court said Friday afternoon that Vodafone Group was not liable for about $2.5 billion in back taxes (and interest and fees that would have brought the figure above $5 billion) related to its 2007 purchase of the Indian assets of Hong Kong’s Hutchison Telecommunications International. The case has been closely watched by foreign investors and local businesses alike, who said before the decision that it could seriously impact investment in India in the future. For Vodafone, which has been expanding rapidly in emerging markets, with mixed results, the decision will free up cash which could be put towards further investment in India. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reactions to the Supreme Court Decision on Vodafone', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vodafone Group Plc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T09:41:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fddbce93-10bb-5fbc-95e0-697b0bc288e4', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fddbce93-10bb-5fbc-95e0-697b0bc288e4'}, {'abstract': 'David Nalbandian was fined $8,000 for unsportsmanlike conduct following his five-set loss to John Isner this week, the largest fine so far issued at this year’s Australian Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/nalbandian-fined-following-overrule-controversy/', 'snippet': 'David Nalbandian was fined $8,000 for unsportsmanlike conduct following his five-set loss to John Isner this week, the largest fine so far issued at this year’s Australian Open.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:50 p.m. | Updated MELBOURNE, Australia — Argentine David Nalbandian was fined $8,000 for unsportsmanlike conduct following a controversy-plagued five-set loss to John Isner in the second round earlier this week. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nalbandian Is Fined Following Overrule Controversy', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T09:45:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03ab69e1-db94-5b77-b91e-b7de17c0a8b9', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03ab69e1-db94-5b77-b91e-b7de17c0a8b9'}, {'abstract': 'Why is the Obama administration trying out a new course with respect to illegal immigrants?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/in-legal-limbo/', 'snippet': 'Why is the Obama administration trying out a new course with respect to illegal immigrants?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO are being permitted to remain in the United States? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Legal Limbo', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T09:46:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/265b6781-b0f5-550d-9626-51bcbb0a21f7', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/265b6781-b0f5-550d-9626-51bcbb0a21f7'}, {'abstract': 'By avoiding direct confrontations with his opponents while giving evasive answers on a range of issues in debates this week, Mitt Romney has allowed Newt Gingrich to become the slight favorite to win in South Carolina.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/romneys-prevent-defense-yielding-big-gains-to-opponents/', 'snippet': 'By avoiding direct confrontations with his opponents while giving evasive answers on a range of issues in debates this week, Mitt Romney has allowed Newt Gingrich to become the slight favorite to win in South Carolina.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most football fans have learned to hate the “prevent defense,” a strategy that is employed when a team holds a lead late in the game. In theory, the strategy involves being willing to yield short completions to the offense in an effort to prevent a big gain. In reality, it seems to yield plenty of short completions — but also its share of big gains as the offense takes advantage of the soft coverage. Hence the aphorism “the prevent defense only prevents you from winning.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s ‘Prevent Defense’ Yielding Big Gains to Opponents', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T09:49:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6870cc8-1625-5c79-8f80-d692f0af7e30', 'word_count': 914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6870cc8-1625-5c79-8f80-d692f0af7e30'}, {'abstract': 'When push came to shove, could you put others before yourself in a crisis?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/do-you-think-youre-brave/', 'snippet': 'When push came to shove, could you put others before yourself in a crisis?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scorn has been heaped on the captain of the Costa Concordia, the cruise ship that ran aground off the coast of Italy last weekend, for failing to stay on the ship, as is a captain’s duty. Some have even called him a coward. Are you brave? How do you think you would act in such a situation?  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do You Think You’re Brave?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T10:21:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9adb3b31-16e7-52b9-becf-1d6e290cdc63', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9adb3b31-16e7-52b9-becf-1d6e290cdc63'}, {'abstract': 'At some point, we may reasonably assume, spending on health care will not increase faster than gross domestic product, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/is-u-s-health-spending-finally-under-control/', 'snippet': 'At some point, we may reasonably assume, spending on health care will not increase faster than gross domestic product, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:36 a.m. | Updated  to correct reference to lines in Chart 3.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is U.S. Health Spending Finally Under Control?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T11:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Uwe E. Reinhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Uwe', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Reinhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52bd9b55-4c34-58e9-9b68-1672bc9c46f5', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52bd9b55-4c34-58e9