cker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ninety-Second Street Y', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T12:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25f529ce-b2f5-54c8-9261-275c80913df0', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25f529ce-b2f5-54c8-9261-275c80913df0'}, {'abstract': 'At the end of last year, I was looking over a list of Toronto’s Best Albums of 2011 in the Toronto-based publication The Grid (full disclosure: I am from Toronto) when something struck me: The list of best albums from Toronto in 2011 could have easily doubled as a list of the best albums of 2011, full-stop.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/toronto-is-having-a-seattle-moment/', 'snippet': 'At the end of last year, I was looking over a list of Toronto’s Best Albums of 2011 in the Toronto-based publication The Grid (full disclosure: I am from Toronto) when something struck me: The list of best albums from Toronto in 2011 could have ea...', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the end of last year, I was looking over a list of Toronto’s Best Albums of 2011 in the Toronto-based publication The Grid (full disclosure: I am from Toronto) when something struck me: The list of best albums from Toronto in 2011 could have easily doubled as a list of the best albums of 2011, full-stop.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toronto Is Having a Seattle Moment', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor