rst-round-entergy-1-vermont-0/', 'snippet': 'A federal court ruling suggesting that Vermont overreached in seeking to shut down a nuclear plant allows the plant’s owner to avoid having to decide whether to keep the plant running while the legal battle unfolds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I wrote in Friday’s New York Times, the first round in federal court has gone to Entergy, the electrical power production company that does not want to shut down its Vermont Yankee nuclear plant. The state of Vermont has been seeking to close the plant when its initial 40-year federal operating license expires on March 21. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Round: Entergy 1, Vermont 0', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murtha, J Garvan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Entergy Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vermont Yankee Nuclear Power Plant', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vermont', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T15:13:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/840fc436-bbba-50d8-afd9-a04176dac573', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/840fc436-bbba-50d8-afd9-a04176dac573'}, {'abstract': 'Salman Rushdie cancels, citing assassination threat.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/a-macabre-start-to-the-sprawling-jaipur-lit-fest/', 'snippet': 'Salman Rushdie cancels, citing assassination threat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Jaipur Literature Festival got off to a macabre start on Friday with organizers announcing that the Indian-born author Salman Rushdie would not attend the event because of a new assassination threat against him. Instead, Mr. Rushdie said he would address the event via a video link.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Macabre Start to the Sprawling Jaipur Lit Fest', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rushdie, Salman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T15:17:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj and Sruthi Gottipati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4bf6292-6e7b-561e-b283-91e0e27fe960', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4bf6292-6e7b-561e-b283-91e0e27fe960'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court on Friday instructed a lower court in Texas to take a fresh look at election maps it had drawn in place of a competing set of maps from the Texas Legislature, saying the lower court had not paid enough deference to the Legislature’s choices.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/supreme-court-rejects-judge-drawn-maps-in-texas-redistricting-case/', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court on Friday instructed a lower court in Texas to take a fresh look at election maps it had drawn in place of a competing set of maps from the Texas Legislature, saying the lower court had not paid enough deference to the Legislatur...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court on Friday instructed a lower court in Texas to take a fresh look at election maps it had drawn in place of a competing set of maps from the Texas Legislature. The justices said the lower court had not paid enough deference to the Legislature’s choices and had improperly substituted its own values for those of elected officials.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Rejects Judge-Drawn Maps in Texas Redistricting Case', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Redistricting and Reapportionment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T15:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5d2623a-2c87-54ab-be8b-434daca606d4', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5d2623a-2c87-54ab-be8b-434daca606d4'}, {'abstract': 'To make “Wings,” the 1927 silent film about World War I pilots, the director William A. Wellman mounted cameras in the cockpits of planes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/movies/homevideo/william-a-wellmans-wings-with-clara-bow-on-blu-ray.html', 'snippet': 'To make “Wings,” the 1927 silent film about World War I pilots, the director William A. Wellman mounted cameras in the cockpits of planes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Academy Award nominations for 2011, which will be announced on Tuesday, will most likely include a few nods to “The Artist,” Michel Hazanavicius’s careful if sometimes condescending pastiche of silent-era filmmaking. Most people seeing “The Artist” will probably be seeing a movie without (much) spoken dialogue for the first time; the trick will be getting them to see a second example, preferably an authentic one. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22KEHR_SPAN/22KEHR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22KEHR_SPAN/22KEHR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22KEHR_SPAN/22KEHR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 792, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22KEHR_SPAN/22KEHR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22KEHR_SPAN/22KEHR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pilot’s-Eye View of the War in the Air', 'kicker': 'DVD', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pilot’s-Eye View of the War in the Air', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and D