Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19e40e55-4ac9-580f-836a-fbd7a0c3fb50', 'word_count': 943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19e40e55-4ac9-580f-836a-fbd7a0c3fb50'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary “Queen of Versailles” is the subject of a lawsuit by its subject, but footage at the premiere raises questions.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/documentary-footage-raises-questions-about-lawsuit/', 'snippet': 'The documentary “Queen of Versailles” is the subject of a lawsuit by its subject, but footage at the premiere raises questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — David Siegel, a Florida time-share mogul, is suing the Sundance Institute and Lauren Greenfield, the director of a documentary about his family, “The Queen of Versailles,” for defamation. The plot twist: Mr. Siegel’s lawsuit may turn out to be more embarrassing for him than Ms. Greenfield’s film.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Documentary Footage Raises Questions About Lawsuit', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenfield, Lauren', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Siegel, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park City (Utah)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:06:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be8135e5-65e9-5521-9c4b-a8fafea68377', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be8135e5-65e9-5521-9c4b-a8fafea68377'}, {'abstract': 'Tracing a star from Nirvana to the Foo Fighters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/books/review/this-is-a-call-the-life-and-times-of-dave-grohl-by-paul-brannigan-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'Tracing a star from Nirvana to the Foo Fighters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among musicians, drummers are a breed apart. On the one hand, the drummer is the timekeeper, the one who counts off the song and keeps the other band members on the beat. On the other, the drummer sits behind everyone else and usually doesn’t write songs or sing them, so often he’s “only the \xaddrummer.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/books/review/sub-22-KIRBY/sub-22-KIRBY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 777, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/books/review/sub-22-KIRBY/sub-22-KIRBY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/books/review/sub-22-KIRBY/sub-22-KIRBY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dave Grohl: From Antsy Student to Nirvana to Foo Fighters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On His Beat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grohl, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foo Fighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nirvana', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:08:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Kirby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kirby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/61400332-6eca-5d05-bdee-b7b9abaa93c0', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61400332-6eca-5d05-bdee-b7b9abaa93c0'}, {'abstract': 'At the Blu Ice Bar, in Two Harbors, much of the restaurant is as perishable as the catch of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/travel/restaurant-review-blu-ice-bar-and-splashing-rock-restaurant-two-harbors-minn.html', 'snippet': 'At the Blu Ice Bar, in Two Harbors, much of the restaurant is as perishable as the catch of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At restaurants on Lake Superior’s North Shore in Minnesota, the fish tends to be fresh and local. At the Blu Ice Bar, in Two Harbors, much of the restaurant is as perishable as the catch of the day.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22BITES_SPAN/22BITES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22BITES_SPAN/22BITES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22BITES_SPAN/22BITES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22BITES_SPAN/22BITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22BITES_SPAN/22BITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Review: Blu Ice Bar and Splashing Rock Restaurant, Two Harbors, Minn.', 'kicker': 'Bites ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'TWO HARBORS, MINN.: Blu Ice Bar and Splashing Rock Restaurant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Two Harbors (Minn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blu Ice Bar and Splashing Rock Restaurant (Two Harbors, Minn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:09:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Lillegard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lillegard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e54926ee-f218-51e6-8c24-43f74481ef41', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e54926ee-f218-51e6-8c24-43f74481ef41'}, {'abstract': 'Scarcity turns modest policy differences into showdowns between “haves” and “have-nots,” Thomas Edsall writes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/books/review/the-age-of-austerity-how-scarcity-will-remake-american-politics-by-thomas-byrne-edsall-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'Scarcity turns modest policy differences into showdowns between “haves” and “have-nots,” Thomas Edsall writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most books about contemporary politics are designed for quick obsolescence. A notable exception to the rule is the work of Thomas Byrne Edsall, whose five careful books, starting with “The New Politics of Inequality” in 1984, are still found on the shelves and in the footnotes of everyone who writes about politics — left and right, academics and journalists alike. Edsall’s distinctive method combines his own reporting with rigorous use of data from across the social sciences, including psychology and anthropology. Though his previous book, “Building Red America,” seemed poorly timed when it appeared in 2006 just as Karl Rove’s quest for permanent Republican dominance collapsed, its insights into conservative attitudes about authority and autonomy remain as useful as anything written more recently about the Tea Party and the right-wing resurgence.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/books/review/22-SCHMITT/22-SCHMITT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 919, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/books/review/22-SCHMITT/22-SCHMITT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/books/review/22-SCHMITT/22-SCHMITT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Political Price of Austerity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Within Limits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/14dc03d0-0f35-5dcc-a51a-1e784848b409', 'word_count': 1242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14dc03d0-0f35-5dcc-a51a-1e784848b409'}, {'abstract': 'The season is here for temple oranges, a short-lived treat.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/temple-oranges-here-today/', 'snippet': 'The season is here for temple oranges, a short-lived treat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m no great fan of snow or the groundhog, but one arrival I look forward to each winter is temple oranges — shiny, spongy to the touch and deeply rutted with pores, like a cartoonist’s idea of an orange. I spotted a temple-like pyramid (a ziggurat?) of them the other day in front of Fairway on the Upper West Side.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Temple Oranges, Here Today …', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citrus Fruits', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:12:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Farrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2157b858-2296-566b-9cb8-aed98dca7e7f', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2157b858-2296-566b-9cb8-aed98dca7e7f'}, {'abstract': 'Coriolanus seems like a fantasy modern politician. But the true moral of this political fable, newly adapted by Ralph Fiennes, isn’t one we’re eager to embrace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/magazine/revisiting-shakespeares-coriolanus.html', 'snippet': 'Coriolanus seems like a fantasy modern politician. But the true moral of this political fable, newly adapted by Ralph Fiennes, isn’t one we’re eager to embrace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some women swoon for swashbuckling Antony or bodice-ripping Othello, but I’ve always had a soft spot for prideful, imperious Coriolanus. Next to Shakespeare’s other tragic figures, who sometimes sound like Freudian case studies — Hamlet, that whiny, dithering ball of nerves who accidentally murders his girlfriend’s father; Lear, who judges his daughters so egregiously in a vicious game of favorites that he deserves to be left out on the moors — Coriolanus comes across as downright noble. Uniquely among these figures, this war hero turned disgraced politician does nothing truly wrong: he is punished without having committed a crime. In fact, his worst fault might be his refusal to speak anything less than exactly what he believes.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22riff2/22riff2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 840, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22riff2/22riff2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/magazine/22riff2/22riff2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Revisiting Shakespeare’s ‘Coriolanus’', 'kicker': 'Riff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘His Worst Fault Might Be His Refusal to Speak Anything Less Than Exactly What He Believes’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Coriolanus (Play)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Coriolanus (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fiennes, Ralph', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:13:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth Franklin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Franklin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f1c899b-734c-54ce-ba7a-494f7243fdbd', 'word_count': 1808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f1c899b-734c-54ce-ba7a-494f7243fdbd'}, {'abstract': 'NBC’s morning show focuses this morning on a topic of much discussion around kitchen tables, particularly among families with high school seniors.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/choice-on-today-fin-aid/', 'snippet': 'NBC’s morning show focuses this morning on a topic of much discussion around kitchen tables, particularly among families with high school seniors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Visit msnbc.com for breaking news, world news, and news about the economy', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "The Choice on ‘Today': Tips on Fafsa, and Net-Price Calculators", 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7024d208-c5fd-594a-88fa-865948fa7b91', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7024d208-c5fd-594a-88fa-865948fa7b91'}, {'abstract': 'On Brazil’s southern coast, the town of Praia do Rosa is both sleepy and chic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/travel/praia-do-rosa-brazil-refined-but-untouched.html', 'snippet': 'On Brazil’s southern coast, the town of Praia do Rosa is both sleepy and chic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FROM the balcony of Quinta do Bucanero, a pousada in the center of Praia do Rosa, the appeal of the Brazilian seaside town is obvious. Perched on top of a cliff, the 10-room hotel is surrounded by a tropical jungle and forested mountains, with views of a long, sweeping stretch of golden sand and two lagoons. Surfers dot the waves, and orchids scent the air.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22NEXT1_SPAN/22NEXT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22NEXT1_SPAN/22NEXT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22NEXT1_SPAN/22NEXT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/travel/22NEXT1_SPAN/22NEXT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name':