ype': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/20/fashion/0120ysl-slide-PLZD/0120ysl-slide-PLZD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yves Saint Laurent: Fall 2012 Menswear', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:39:37+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': "Men's Runway", 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c49924e9-a896-5058-a1e5-d0c727545bd1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c49924e9-a896-5058-a1e5-d0c727545bd1'}, {'abstract': 'Exxon Mobil will pay the state of Montana $300,000 in cash and spend $1.3 million on environmental projects there.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/on-our-radar-compensation-for-yellowstone-spill/', 'snippet': 'Exxon Mobil will pay the state of Montana $300,000 in cash and spend $1.3 million on environmental projects there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Exxon Mobil agrees to pay $1.6 million in penalties to the state of Montana for pollution caused by a pipeline break last summer that fouled dozens of miles of shoreline along the Yellowstone River. Of that amount, $300,000 is a cash fine and the rest is to go toward future environmental projects. Exxon says that more than 63,000 gallons of crude swept into the river. [The Associated Press]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Compensation for Yellowstone Spill', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:40:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2a94381-8013-5cce-bcdd-131abae51da2', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2a94381-8013-5cce-bcdd-131abae51da2'}, {'abstract': 'Dispute over the slave trade looms large in Barry Unsworth’s follow-up to “Sacred Hunger.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/books/review/the-quality-of-mercy-by-barry-unsworth-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'Dispute over the slave trade looms large in Barry Unsworth’s follow-up to “Sacred Hunger.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few of its readers are likely to forget Barry Unsworth’s “Sacred Hunger,” a co-winner of the Booker Prize in 1992. The novel contains a vision of hell on earth unlike any in contemporary fiction, largely because its account of the unimaginable cruelties of the slave trade is told in the well-wrought prose of an old-fashioned 19th-century novel with an omniscient narrator. The effect is uncanny: its intelligent, controlled and immensely readable sentences glow with a deathly pallor.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/books/review/Vernon/Vernon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 873, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/books/review/Vernon/Vernon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/books/review/Vernon/Vernon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Monster in the Age of Abolition', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Safe Passage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Unsworth, Barry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:47:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Vernon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vernon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/14a2f4df-93bb-53f9-b1de-8914971e95c0', 'word_count': 1184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14a2f4df-93bb-53f9-b1de-8914971e95c0'}, {'abstract': 'In Ben Marcus’s novel, the sound of children’s speech has become lethal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/books/review/the-flame-alphabet-by-ben-marcus-book-review.html', 'snippet': 'In Ben Marcus’s novel, the sound of children’s speech has become lethal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a career spanning nearly 20 years, Ben Marcus has written just four spare volumes: a story collection, two novels and a chapbook. Formally inventive, dark and dryly comic, this work has earned him critical praise and a small army of devoted fans. His prose is heavily metaphorical yet coolly ironic; it traffics in the language of scholarship, myth and history, and until now has forsaken the conventional trappings of narrative. Indeed, the pieces in “The Age of Wire and String” (1995) function more like prose poems than stories; their emotional impact is derived from their distinctive diction and syntax. The opener, “Argument,” might serve as a map of Marcus’s early career, with its stated goal of “cataloging a culture” through “an array of documents settling within the chief concerns of the society, of any society, of the world and its internal areas.” The book’s archness is both bracing and absurd; it attempts to reinvent story by repurposing, gleefully, the jargon ordinarily used to analyze it.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/books/review/Lennon/Lennon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 335, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/books/review/Lennon/Lennon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/books/review/Lennon/Lennon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Children’s Speech Turns Lethal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Parents Get It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marcus, Ben', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:48:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. Robert Lennon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'Robert', 'lastname': 'Lennon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b3baf2a-ea0c-575f-b0d9-5ce1cc71487e', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b3baf2a-ea0c-575f-b0d9-5ce1cc71487e'}, {'abstract': 'A long-term research program in the McMurdo Dry Valleys of Antarctica incorporates studies of streams, lakes, glaciers and soil to gauge the local effects a changing climate is likely to have.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/ecological-connectivity-as-climate-warms/', 'snippet': 'A long-term research program in the McMurdo Dry Valleys of Antarctica incorporates studies of streams, lakes, glaciers and soil to gauge the local effects a changing climate is likely to have.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alia Khan, a graduate student at the University of Colorado, Boulder, writes from the McMurdo Dry Valleys in Antarctica, where she is studying ephemeral glacier-fed streams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ecological Connectivity as Climate Warms', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glaciers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:56:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alia Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2c416ec-9bb3-5808-9d15-1c485bc55e99', 'word_count': 701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2c416ec-9bb3-5808-9d15-1c485bc55e99'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. James, most often referred to as a rhythm and blues singer, is in both the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame and the Blues Hall of Fame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/arts/music/etta-james-singer-dies-at-73.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. James, most often referred to as a rhythm and blues singer, is in both the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame and the Blues Hall of Fame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Etta James, whose powerful, versatile and emotionally direct voice could enliven the raunchiest blues as well as the subtlest love songs, most indelibly in her signature hit, “At Last,” died on Friday morning in Riverside, Calif. She was 73. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/music/20james-span/20james-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 367, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/music/20james-span/20james-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 367}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/music/20james-span/20james-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 881, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/music/20james-span/20james-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/20/arts/music/20james-span/20james-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Etta James Dies at 73; Voice Behind ‘At Last’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Etta James Dies at 73; Voice Behind ‘At Last’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Etta', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gospel Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:56:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Keepnews', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keepnews', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d81c162-4af8-5804-8de2-bac2db2983a6', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d81c162-4af8-5804-8de2-bac2db2983a6'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich compares himself to Abraham Lincoln, Ronald Reagan, Henry Clay, Charles de Gaulle…', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/hes-so-vain-hed-be-right-in-thinking-this-post-is-about-him/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich compares himself to Abraham Lincoln, Ronald Reagan, Henry Clay, Charles de Gaulle…', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am not one of those people who think the president should be “just like me.” He should be in touch with the needs and aspirations and fears of ordinary Americans, sure. But how many of your neighbors would you like to see with the nuclear trigger in their hands?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'He’s So Vain, He’d Be Right in Thinking This Post Is About Him', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T16:58:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f76fb56d-d0a3-51d9-b135-35058478a30c', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f76fb56d-d0a3-51d9-b135-35058478a30c'}, {'abstract': 'On Sunda