iest and most obsessive viewers who have a favorite writer on that NBC late-night sketch show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the post-Al Franken, post-Robert Smigel, post-Tina Fey era of “Saturday Night Live,” it is perhaps only its nerdiest and most obsessive viewers who have a favorite writer on that NBC late-night sketch show. But since joining the “S.N.L.” writing staff for its 2008-09 season, John Mulaney has found himself a place in the hearts of completists and casual fans alike: a Chicago-born standup comic, Mulaney has gained recognition as a creator and writer of Stefon, the ultra-hip nightlife correspondent played in frequent “Weekend Update” appearances by Bill Hader; and for his own occasional riffs, delivered as himself from the “Update” desk. (Also joining him in this modern-day pantheon is his fellow “S.N.L.” writer and Internet microcelebrity Mike O’Brien.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Big Profile: John Mulaney', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cort, Bud', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fey, Tina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Demetri', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michaels, Lorne', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'VH1', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T17:11:25+0000', 'document_type': 'arti