stname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b25eb32a-8fa2-5d59-aefa-a457358a82b9', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b25eb32a-8fa2-5d59-aefa-a457358a82b9'}, {'abstract': 'Aaron Hernandez and the All-Pro Rob Gronkowski have been potent weapons at tight end as the Patriots prepare to host Baltimore Sunday in the A.F.C. championship game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/sports/football/aaron-hernandez-patriots-other-tight-end-is-also-a-handful.html', 'snippet': 'Aaron Hernandez and the All-Pro Rob Gronkowski have been potent weapons at tight end as the Patriots prepare to host Baltimore Sunday in the A.F.C. championship game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOXBORO, Mass. — On the fourth play of the Patriots’ divisional playoff game against Denver, Aaron Hernandez broke a 43-yard run to the Broncos 7-yard line. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/sports/21patriots1/21patriots1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/sports/21patriots1/21patriots1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/21/sports/21patriots1/21patriots1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Agile Patriot Thrives in a Teammate’s Hulking Shadow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Agile Patriot Thrives in a Teammate’s Hulking Shadow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Aaron (1989- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gronkowski, Rob', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T17:17:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter May', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'May', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82843841-eec2-5c64-b61b-a22a518f5a16', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82843841-eec2-5c64-b61b-a22a518f5a16'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/weekend-fare-77/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chinese New Year commences Monday, but some restaurants will jump-start their celebrations and offer special menus this weekend. At Masak, 432 East 13th Street (between First Avenue and Avenue A), in the East Village, a preview menu is offered today through Sunday, with items like arrowroot chips and roasted quail stuffed with rice, chestnuts, lotus seeds, kale and a salted duck yolk. A more extensive New Year menu is offered starting Tuesday. To celebrate the Year of the Dragon, Chinatown Brasserie, 380 Lafayette Street (Great Jones Street), in NoHo, will cook up dim sum specials, traditional Chinese fare and an assortment of desserts starting on Sunday. Culinary tours led by Adventure on a Shoestring this weekend include a walking tour of Manhattan’s Chinatown at 1 and 3 p.m. with samplings of dumplings, pastries and ice cream. The tours will meet at the southeast corner of Canal and Mott Streets. The fee is $10 and does not include food. Call (212) 265-2663 for more information.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T17:18:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e83ccf40-3d17-59eb-bd7a-76f4852784db', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e83ccf40-3d17-59eb-bd7a-76f4852784db'}, {'abstract': 'The number of new passenger cars registered in the European Union declined 15.8 percent from 2007 to 2011. Registrations fell in 17 of the 24 European countries with populations over 1 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/01/20/business/New-Car-Registrations-Decline-in-Europe.html', 'snippet': 'The number of new passenger cars registered in the European Union declined 15.8 percent from 2007 to 2011. Registrations fell in 17 of the 24 European countries with populations over 1 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The number of new passenger cars registered in the European Union declined 15.8 percent from 2007 to 2011. Registrations fell in 17 of the 24 European countries with populations over 1 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off the Charts: New-Car Registrations Decline in Europe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Registration and License Plates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value':