both Tokyo and the City of Light, the clothes paid homage to the legendary fashion illustrator Antonio Lopez, an artist with links to both fashion capitals. Lopez’s drawings were brought vividly to life in a group of graphic, patterned (and LV-monogrammed) blanket coats with coordinating scarves pinned at the neck. A vicuna double-breasted, belted coat (see Coming Soon: Belted Coats) worn with a mink scarf, kimono-style shirt and gray double-faced pajama trousers made references to both East and West in the most luxurious way possible.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Top 5 | Louis Vuitton', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T17:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/347e6aaf-1201-56f7-bad7-2e8eccf6244a', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/347e6aaf-1201-56f7-bad7-2e8eccf6244a'}, {'abstract': 'Signs of a recovery in automobile demand in late 2009 vanished as the sovereign debt crisis emerged, first in Greece and then in other countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/business/global/in-debt-laden-europe-new-cars-stay-in-showroom.html', 'snippet': 'Signs of a recovery in automobile demand in late 2009 vanished as the sovereign debt crisis emerged, first in Greece and then in other countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE new passenger car is becoming an increasingly rare item in some European countries.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Europe, Cars Stay in Showroom', 'kicker': 'Off the Cha