C. has a problem perhaps too serious to be called a quandary. A few months ago, she says, her family received a flier from the local sheriff. A registered sex offender was moving to her street of small, single-family homes. Hers is a long street, though, and she expected the offender to be some distance away and easily avoidable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parental Quandary: The Sex Offender Next Door', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T18:22:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca5b1e25-4bd6-5d58-a592-f02c486bf167', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca5b1e25-4bd6-5d58-a592-f02c486bf167'}, {'abstract': 'There were reasons for optimism in the numbers: the new morning broadcast gained viewers as the week progressed. But total viewership was 10 percent lower than what its predecessor pulled in for the same week last year.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/first-ratings-for-cbs-this-morning-highlight-steep-challenges-ahead/', 'snippet': 'There were reasons for optimism in the numbers: the new morning broadcast gained viewers as the week progressed. But total viewership was 10 percent lower than what its predecessor pulled in for the same week last year.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:39 p.m. | Updated The ratings for the first week of “CBS This Mor