n the hardcover graphic books best-seller list this week. When an international incident sends hatred of mutants into a new frenzy, Cyclops and Wolverine are divided in their response and cause a rift in the team. This collected edition contains the five issues of “Schism,” written by Jason Aaron with each issue illustrated by a different powerhouse artist (Carlos Pacheco, Frank Cho, Daniel Acuna, Alan Davis and Adam Kubert). It also includes the standalone special “X-Men: Regenesis,” written by Kieron Gillen and illustrated by Billy Tan, in which the other X-Men choose whether they will stand with Cyclops or Wolverine. The X-Men are synonymous with change, with the characters getting reshuffled into new teams every few years, so the fracture among the heroes may be temporary. (Particularly with a huge conflict with the Avengers coming right around the corner.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: X-Men Take Over Top Spot', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'X-Men', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T18:44:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40fbd81a-8c2a-5b26-b3bd-30a55cfc5323', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40fbd81a-8c2a-5b26-b3bd-30a55cfc5323'}, {'abstract': 'Texas liberals thought President Perry was a lock. Boy, were we wrong.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/overmisunderestimating-rick-perry/', 'snippet': 'Texas 