: 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6a4eac17-8c24-57bc-983a-d13f4b6fa5fe', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6a4eac17-8c24-57bc-983a-d13f4b6fa5fe'}, {'abstract': 'Fifty years ago, large families were unusual in evangelical Protestantism, but there has been a shift.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/us/more-protestants-oppose-birth-control.html', 'snippet': 'Fifty years ago, large families were unusual in evangelical Protestantism, but there has been a shift.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican presidential field has produced a lot of babies. There is Mitt Romney, father of five sons. Ron Paul, an obstetrician by training, is also a father of five, and his campaign Web site credits him with bringing 4,000 babies into the world. Newt Gingrich and the recent dropout Rick Perry have only two children each, but Rick Santorum, who has said contraception is “not O.K.,” has seven children, and so does another former candidate, Jon M. Huntsman Jr. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 846, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/21/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Many Evangelicals See Something to Admire in Candidates’ Broods', 'kicker': 'Beliefs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Many Evangelicals See Something to Admire In Candidates’ Broods', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evangelical Movement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T19:40:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Oppenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oppenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db98d016-8b4d-5f2e-b733-50011603acb0', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db98d016-8b4d-5f2e-b733-50011603acb0'}, {'abstract': 'Head-to-toe romantic detailing, courtesy of Valentino’s prefall collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/just-one-look-valentino-2/', 'snippet': 'Head-to-toe romantic detailing, courtesy of Valentino’s prefall collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a lot to get excited about at Valentino this morning. The accessories, for one, are stellar and studded: the season’s new loafer, pictured here, is stamped on top with a large gold pyramid stud; the combat boot, another favorite, is ruffled in the front; the brogues come in patent leather with spiky metal toe caps (similar to the ones we just saw at the men’s shows in Europe). Romantic, rose-embellished and decorated with bows and lace, the dresses and skirt looks are lovely and expertly tailored. Just what you expect from the Italian house — though it’s the suit story made of nipped silk satin tuxedos and soft, tie-neck blouses that caught this editor’s attention. Here, the rippling asymmetrical lapel on a blush-pink jacket flirts with Le Smoking without going all the way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Valentino', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T19:45:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5d10a7f-a825-54ec-a9cb-4e6ca5057999', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5d10a7f-a825-54ec-a9cb-4e6ca5057999'}, {'abstract': 'Danio Gallinari, who was a favorite of fans when he was with the Knicks, returns to Madison Square Garden with the Nuggets Saturday night.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/for-gallinari-a-long-awaited-return-to-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Danio Gallinari, who was a favorite of fans when he was with the Knicks, returns to Madison Square Garden with the Nuggets Saturday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Danilo Gallinari is ready to come back to New York. It was Feb. 22 of last year when “il Gallo,” one of most popular players during Coach Mike D’Antoni’s tenure with the Knicks, was involved in the trade that brought Carmelo Anthony to New York. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Gallinari, a Long-Awaited Return to New York', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T19:49:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By MITJA VIOLA', 'person': [{'firstname': '