line': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/35026989-a65d-50d2-ab2e-569d09c8ec1b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/35026989-a65d-50d2-ab2e-569d09c8ec1b'}, {'abstract': 'For all of this Brooklyn neighborhood’s isolation and industrial grit, many of its residents describe it with immense pride and fondness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/realestate/wallabout-brooklyn-living-in-at-the-intersection-of-history-and-industry.html', 'snippet': 'For all of this Brooklyn neighborhood’s isolation and industrial grit, many of its residents describe it with immense pride and fondness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SLOPING down from Myrtle Avenue to the walled fortress of the Brooklyn Navy Yard Industrial Park, and bisected by the rumbling equator of the elevated Brooklyn-Queens Expressway, the two-block-wide semi-industrial neighborhood of Wallabout would seem to have some unenviable physical challenges. It lacks subways, and although it shares a name with nearby Wallabout Bay, its residents are cut off by the Navy Yard from the tantalizingly close waterfront.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/realestate/22LIVING_SPAN/22LIVING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/realestate/22LIVING_SPAN/22LIVING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/realestate/22LIVING_SPAN/22LIVING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/realestate/22LIVING_SPA