s courts in Australia to a World Cup skeleton race in Switzerland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/20/sports/20120120photoreplay.html', 'snippet': 'A look at the day in sports, from the tennis courts in Australia to a World Cup skeleton race in Switzerland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look at the day in sports, from the tennis courts in Australia to a World Cup skeleton race in Switzerland.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/20120120photoreplay-slide-FJL5/20120120photoreplay-slide-FJL5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 560, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/20120120photoreplay-slide-FJL5/20120120photoreplay-slide-FJL5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/20/sports/20120120photoreplay-slide-FJL5/20120120photoreplay-slide-FJL5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Photo Replay: January 20', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speedskating', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skeleton (Sport)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T20:54:23+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/ac21e292-f43c-5612-b860-682665f4d74b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/ac21e292-f43c-5612-b860-682665f4d74b'}, {'abstract': 'Last season, Rei Kawakubo used bridal lace in her men’s collection; this time, she went for old-time pink roses on gray suiting, sweet polka dots and boxy shorts.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/fashion-silhouettes-sharply-drawn/', 'snippet': 'Last season, Rei Kawakubo used bridal lace in her men’s collection; this time, she went for old-time pink roses on gray suiting, sweet polka dots and boxy shorts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last season, Rei Kawakubo used bridal lace in her men’s collection; this time, she went for old-time pink roses on gray suiting, sweet polka dots and boxy shorts or culottes with jackets that evoked the classic Chanel cardigan. And the shoes came with little heels and socks with boldly colored ribbing, while the models wore Joan Jett wigs, at times with a beribboned bowler hat. All these elements felt warmly and securely Comme des Garçons, but perhaps the most appealing thing about the show today was the silhouette: longish and free at the waist, with those full shorts (or knee-length skirts) and, naturally, hairy calves before the splash of pink at the ankles. One impulse was romantic — Jane Eyre, I thought — the other punk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion Silhouettes, Sharply Drawn', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kawakubo, Rei', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tisci, Riccardo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comme des Garcons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Givenchy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T20:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f955caac-9797-5680-b142-3e684b64d59a', 'word_count': 244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f955caac-9797-5680-b142-3e684b64d59a'}, {'abstract': 'Philip Babcock, an economist at the University of California, Santa Barbara, suggests that a lot of it has to do with homework.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/why-students-leave-the-engineering-track/', 'snippet': 'Philip Babcock, an economist at the University of California, Santa Barbara, suggests that a lot of it has to do with homework.', 'lead_paragraph': '1/21/12 | Updated to correct Professor Babcock’s academic affiliation.Amid broader discussions about the future of the American work force, the National Science Foundation has just released a comprehensive report on the state of engineering and science in America. There’s a lot of meat in the report, but I found this chart to be particularly striking:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Students Leave the Engineering Track', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engineering and Engineers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T20:56:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e989ba9-5821-526f-a6fb-78ff2d4f01f6', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e989ba9-5821-526f-a6fb-78ff2d4f01f6'}, {'abstract': 'Rick Perry suffered an affliction common to candidates who are drafted late in campaigns: he came in vastly overconfident and under-prepared.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/debates-arent-to-blame-for-perrys-failure/', 'snippet': 'Rick Perry suffered an affliction common to candidates who are drafted late in campaigns: he came in vastly overconfident and under-prepared.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nineteen times this political season, the Republican candidates for president have stood shoulder to shoulder on a stage, regardless of how much money they had raised or how many endorsements they had won, and passionately laid out for the voters the ideas and qualifications that they believe make them the best choice for the nation’s highest office. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debates Aren’t to Blame for Perry’s Failure', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T20:58:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Bai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6de20247-20d0-512b-b219-5a39f5147dbd', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6de20247-20d0-512b-b219-5a39f5147dbd'}, {'abstract': 'All the fashion news of the week that’s fit to reprint.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/chic-in-review-carey-mulligan-double-dipped-a-dress/', 'snippet': 'All the fashion news of the week that’s fit to reprint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All the fashion news of the week that’s fit to reprint.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chic in Review | Carey Mulligan Double-Dipped a Dress', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T20:59:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe0a5819-b1c9-574b-bdbf-d78fd9c443a8', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe0a5819-b1c9-574b-bdbf-d78fd9c443a8'}, {'abstract': 'Some high bidders at a Barrett-Jackson charity auction in Scottsdale re-donated their prizes and matched winning bids with direct donations.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/auction-winners-pay-it-forward-in-arizona/', 'snippet': 'Some high bidders at a Barrett-Jackson charity auction in Scottsdale re-donated their prizes and matched winning bids with direct donations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SCOTTSDALE, Ariz. — Charitable organizations that assist wounded American veterans received unexpectedly large windfalls Thursday at the Barrett-Jackson classic car auctions here, with help from the prominent motorsports figures Roger Penske and Mario Andretti.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Auction Winners Pay It Forward in Arizona', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keselowski, Brad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Penske, Roger