eb_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/indian-authors-protest-threats-to-rushdie-by-reading-from-his-satanic-verses/', 'snippet': 'After Salman Rushdie canceled an appearance at a literary festival in India on Friday, following death threats, two authors read aloud from his novel “The Satanic Verses,” which remains banned in India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleagues Vikas Bajaj and Sruthi Gottipati report, the Indian-born author Salman Rushdie canceled a planned appearance at a literary festival in India on Friday, citing recent death threats.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Authors Protest Threats to Rushdie by Reading From His ‘Satanic Verses’', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rushdie, Salman', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T21:23:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61b4f175-c88b-54aa-9650-30f62a867bb6', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61b4f175-c88b-54aa-9650-30f62a867bb6'}, {'abstract': 'The bike targets young riders with budgets between $5,000 and $10,000, a long-overlooked segment of the marketplace.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/honda-nc700x-set-for-u-s-sales/', 'snippet': 'The bike targets young riders with budgets between $5,000 and $10,000, a long-overlooked segment of the marketplace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Honda kicked off the 2012 New York motorcycle show early, revealing a new model on Thursday night intended for the American market. The NC700X was first introduced at the EICMA industry show in Milan in November, but was described then as a Europe-only model.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honda NC700X Set for U.S. Sales', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN HONDA MOTOR CO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Honda Motor Co Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T21:26:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel McDermon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDermon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1969dec1-3ade-546f-bc47-49c8d25ee95b', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1969dec1-3ade-546f-bc47-49c8d25ee95b'}, {'abstract': 'The Volkswagen Eos convertible is rare indeed. It is the only car on the road with a folding power hardtop that also has a power tilt-and-slide sunroof. The roof has 470 individual components.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/automobiles/under-the-vw-big-top-even-the-sky-isnt-the-limit.html', 'snippet': 'The Volkswagen Eos convertible is rare indeed. It is the only car on the road with a folding power hardtop that also has a power tilt-and-slide sunroof. The roof has 470 individual components.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TESTED 2012 Volkswagen Eos Lux', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/automobiles/22BLOCK/22BLOCK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 264, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/automobiles/22BLOCK/22BLOCK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 264}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/automobiles/22BLOCK/22BLOCK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/automobiles/22BLOCK/22BLOCK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/automobiles/22BLOCK/22BLOCK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Under the VW Big Top, Even the Sky Isn’t the Limit', 'kicker': 'Around the Block', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Under the VW Big Top, Even the Sky Isn’t the Limit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Convertibles (Autos)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen A.G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T21:26:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ezra Dyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ezra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aedef764-4749-5334-87d6-41515e83c38f', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aedef764-4749-5334-87d6-41515e83c38f'}, {'abstract': '“The Extraordinary Life of Josef Ganz” is an intriguing book about a Jewish engineer whose designs in the 1930s laid out the basics for the Volkswagen Beetle championed by Hitler.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/automobiles/in-beetles-creation-story-a-plot-twist.html', 'snippet': '“The Extraordinary Life of Josef Ganz” is an intriguing book about a Jewish engineer whose designs in the 1930s laid out the basics for the Volkswagen Beetle championed by Hitler.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE tale is intriguing: a Jewish engineer and journalist, whose designs and published work in the 1930s laid out the basics for the Volkswagen Beetle championed by Hitler, was arrested, chased from Germany and nearly airbrushed out of history. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/automobiles/22BOOK1/22BOOK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/automobiles/22BOOK1/22BOOK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/automobiles/22BOOK1/22BOOK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/automobiles/22BOOK1/22BOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/automobiles/22BOOK1/22BOOK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth':