 support, and a safe haven.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN their undergrad uniforms of fleece and sweats, a clutch of Rutgers students gathered on the worn red couches of their dorm’s common room and told their stories. A good-looking, fun-loving 23-year-old named Greg described arriving at college freshman year with a daily pot-smoking habit and a close relationship with alcohol. He soon followed the lead of his alcoholic father and was binge drinking (five drinks or more in a row). “It was pretty scary,” he said.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/education/edl-22recovery-t_CA0/edl-22recovery-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/education/edl-22recovery-t_CA0/edl-22recovery-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/education/edl-22recovery-t_CA0/edl-22recovery-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bridge to Recovery on Campus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bridge to Recovery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'orga