, 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faef381b-5382-5670-bb1b-ccaeedeb4754', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faef381b-5382-5670-bb1b-ccaeedeb4754'}, {'abstract': 'Twice this week, Mitt Romney’s foreign-policy advisers have offered views that differ from the candidate’s.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/on-foreign-policy-romney-breaks-with-advisers/', 'snippet': 'Twice this week, Mitt Romney’s foreign-policy advisers have offered views that differ from the candidate’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In October, Mitt Romney announced a roster of national security advisers that lent his campaign instant gravitas. Studded with heavyweight names, many from the Bush administration, the list suggested that Mr. Romney was the clear choice of the Republican foreign-policy establishment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Foreign Policy, Romney Breaks With Advisers', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolton, John R', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hayden, Michael V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reiss, Mitchell B', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shane, Scott', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foreign Policy (Magazine)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T22:58:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/244da848-14fa-59b1-9dc4-d0d7440f4ad4', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/244da848-14fa-59b1-9dc4-d0d7440f4ad4'}, {'abstract': 'Craig Finn, the singer for the Hold Steady, on a break from the band, is releasing his first solo album, “Clear Heart Full Eyes.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/arts/music/craig-finn-of-the-hold-steady-on-clear-hearts-full-eyes.html', 'snippet': 'Craig Finn, the singer for the Hold Steady, on a break from the band, is releasing his first solo album, “Clear Heart Full Eyes.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'CRAIG FINN has always been a religious guy. He sees God as just but also notices that he has a wicked sense of humor. The barflies, losers and knock-around guys that he writes about in the songs for his band, the Hold Steady, often end up on their knees, sometimes retching, but more often praying for that moment when everything both aligns and goes off the rails at the same time. It’s a moment of clarity, often seen through beer goggles: “Went down with a tallboy can and he woke up in a cargo van,” he sings on “Barfruit Blues” from the band’s 2004 debut album, “Almost Killed Me.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22FINN1_SPAN/22FINN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22FINN1_SPAN/22FINN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22FINN1_SPAN/22FINN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22FINN1_SPAN/22FINN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22FINN1_SPAN/22FINN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Believer Packing Beer and Guitars', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Believer Packing Beer And Guitars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hold Steady', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T22:59:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc81cdb3-c54b-5774-9c21-e5d03132e9ee', 'word_count': 1524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc81cdb3-c54b-5774-9c21-e5d03132e9ee'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s plan to double American exports in five years is on track. Exports are now about $180 billion a month, up from $140 billion a month two years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/business/us-on-track-to-meet-goal-of-higher-exports.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s plan to double American exports in five years is on track. Exports are now about $180 billion a month, up from $140 billion a month two years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Two years ago, President Obama popped a surprise into his State of the Union address: His administration would double American exports in five years, helping to create two million jobs. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Vow on Exports Is on Track, With Help', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Vow On Exports Is on Track, With Help', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T22:59:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/074638c5-3174-53ea-b507-6026d3613d86', 'word_count': 1046, 'uri': 'nyt://article/074638c5-3174-53ea-b507-6026d3613d86'}, {'abstract': 'The British media regulator said the network Press TV had failed to address concerns over its editorial independence and had not paid a fine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/world/europe/britain-revokes-license-of-iran-network-press-tv.html', 'snippet': 'The British media regulator said the network Press TV had failed to address concerns over its editorial independence and had not paid a fine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Britain’s media regulator revoked the broadcast license for the Iranian state-owned television network Press TV on Friday, saying the network had failed to address concerns over its editorial independence and had not paid a fine. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain Revokes Iranian TV Network’s License', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain Revokes Iranian TV Network’s License', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Press TV', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T23:02:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd456234-d68f-5887-8931-056d22524656', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd456234-d68f-5887-8931-056d22524656'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Egypt, Bahrain, Syria and Israel.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/pictures-of-the-day-egypt-and-elsewhere-23/', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Egypt, Bahrain, Syria and Israel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Egypt, Bahrain, Syria and Israel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Egypt and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_k