'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69fecdc9-9a85-52b0-a074-9c9f019269fc', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69fecdc9-9a85-52b0-a074-9c9f019269fc'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich’s spontaneity about strategic decisions sometimes forces his campaign into a cycle of shifting messages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/us/politics/a-test-for-gingrich-as-political-strategist.html', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich’s spontaneity about strategic decisions sometimes forces his campaign into a cycle of shifting messages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLESTON, S.C. — If Newt Gingrich soars on his strong debate performances this week, overcomes the blowback within his party from attacking Mitt Romney as a corporate buyout king, and goes on to do well when South Carolina voters go to the polls on Saturday, one political strategist will get both blame for the stumbles and credit for successes: Mr. Gingrich himself.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/us/politics/21gingrich1/21gingrich1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/21/us/politics/21gingrich1/21gingrich1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/us/politics/21gingrich1/21gingrich1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/us/politics/21gingrich1/21gingrich1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/21/us/politics/21gingrich1/21gingrich1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disdainful of Strategists, Gingrich Acts as His Own', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Week of Shifting Messages in South Carolina Tests Gingrich as Political Strategist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T23:22:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c54baf8e-52cd-5bec-9562-a41fb42bee03', 'word_count': 1153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c54baf8e-52cd-5bec-9562-a41fb42bee03'}, {'abstract': 'The 2012 Beetle abandons the arched silhouette of its predecessor and in the process shifts its style, personality and target market. VW wants to draw more men.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/reviewing-the-volkswagen-beetle/', 'snippet': 'The 2012 Beetle abandons the arched silhouette of its predecessor and in the process shifts its style, personality and target market. VW wants to draw more men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In