e5-4048-5f9b-810f-77b2bfe9b357'}, {'abstract': 'Jeff Mangum, playing the Brooklyn Academy of Music, sings at full throttle, with some help from the audience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/arts/music/jeff-mangum-of-neutral-milk-hotel-at-bam-review.html', 'snippet': 'Jeff Mangum, playing the Brooklyn Academy of Music, sings at full throttle, with some help from the audience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sex, devastation, war, death, God, reincarnation and “how strange it is to be anything at all” were some of the things Jeff Mangum sang about on “In the Aeroplane Over the Sea,” the second album by his band Neutral Milk Hotel, released in 1998. Then he made himself scarce, rarely performing in public until 2010. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Neutral Milk Hotel’s Frontman Does Most of the Work Himself, Including Horns', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Neutral Milk Hotel’s Frontman Does Most of the Work Himself, Including Horns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Neutral Milk Hotel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Academy of Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T23:42:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cc405b1-9b47-5526-8743-fbe5011f86e5', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cc405b1-9b47-5526-8743-fbe5011f86e5'}, {'abstract': 'A pending $3.6 billion transfer of spectrum will give Comcast, the nation’s largest cable company, a presence in select Verizon Wireless retail locations, where Comcast salesmen will offer Verizon customers special offers if they sign up for the cable company’s Xfinity service.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/new-in-your-wireless-store-the-cable-guy/', 'snippet': 'A pending $3.6 billion transfer of spectrum will give Comcast, the nation’s largest cable company, a presence in select Verizon Wireless retail locations, where Comcast salesmen will offer Verizon customers special offers if they sign up for the c...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Customers walking into a Verizon Wireless store in Portland, Ore., or Seattle this week may notice something unusual: cable salesmen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New in Your Wireless Store: The Cable Guy', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T23:44:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea0d7254-f6fe-5f1a-ac2f-8ed127349528', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea0d7254-f6fe-5f1a-ac2f-8ed127349528'}, {'abstract': 'The United States women’s national team will open the Concacaf Olympic qualifying tournament in Vancouver with a game against the Dominican Republic late Friday night.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/olympic-qualifying-u-s-women-vs-dominican-republic/', 'snippet': 'The United States women’s national team will open the Concacaf Olympic qualifying tournament in Vancouver with a game against the Dominican Republic late Friday night.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:37 a.m. | Final Score: U.S. 14, Dominican Republic 0 The United States women’s national team opened the Concacaf Olympic qualifying tournament by thrashing the Dominican Republic, 14-0, on Friday night in Vancouver, but the joy of a record-setting night was tempered by what was described as a “serious” knee injury sustained by defender Ali Krieger. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Olympic Qualifying: U.S. Women vs. Dominican Republic', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Women's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T23:47:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b309ac1-49aa-5d80-9603-ddd511a0f0de', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b309ac1-49aa-5d80-9603-ddd511a0f0de'}, {'abstract': 'Kate Beckinsale returns as the vampire Selene (now a mother) to fight werewolves in “Underworld: Awakening.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/movies/underworld-awakening-with-kate-beckinsale-review.html', 'snippet': 'Kate Beckinsale returns as the vampire Selene (now a mother) to fight werewolves in “Underworld: Awakening.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Milla Jovovich may have the zombie post-apocalypse covered with the “Resident Evil” series (guided by her husband, Paul W. S. Anderson). But in vampire-werewolf warfare, Kate Beckinsale rules, with the “Underworld” movies (guided by her husband, Len Wiseman). No wan, moony “Twilights” these: we’re talking more than a thousand years of battle between Lycans (werewolves) and vampires, recounted in three installments before the latest, “Underworld: Awakening.” (“Underworld” scholars, see Chapter 3, “Rise of the Lycans,” for some origin details.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/arts/UNDER/UNDER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/21/arts/UNDER/UNDER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/arts/UNDER/UNDER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 956, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/arts/UNDER/UNDER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/21/arts/UNDER/UNDER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Long Nap Didn’t Improve Her Mood All That Much'