of a copyright infringement suit against the streaming service Grooveshark, has responded to a subpoena it received in the case. A pair of anonymous comments on the blog, purportedly written by Grooveshark employees, have become central pieces of evidence in the major record labels’ case against the service, and last weekend Grooveshark served Digital Music News with a subpoena for information about those comments. Paul Resnikoff, the blog’s publisher, explained in a detailed post on Friday addressed to Grooveshark’s lawyers why he would not comply with the subpoena. He noted that to protect the identity of anonymous commenters, the site “flushes” relevant data after 24 hours and that he is entitled to the protection of state shield laws for journalists. He wrote:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital Notes: Blogger Rejects Subpoena in Grooveshark Case', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grooveshark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ReDigi Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T23:51:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/117aa45e-a389-5362-b6cb-b3ffa17f5698', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/117aa45e-a389-5362-b6cb-b3ffa17f5698'}, {'abstract': 'A vote for wigs in the face of all the cosmetic and surgical options that are possible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/fashion/her-wigs-are-not-a-problem.html', 'snippet': 'A vote for wigs in the face of all the cosmetic and surgical options that are possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My boyfriend’s mother, who is in excellent health and has a full head of hair, has taken to wearing wigs. She photographs herself in them and texts the pictures to us. My strategy has been to ignore the photos and hope the wigs go away. My boyfriend responds by saying how much better she looks with her own hair. Should we come right out and tell her we don’t like the wigs? ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Roots of a Problem', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Roots of a Problem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T23:54:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b47953a6-f06c-51ab-b183-a05fe4dc1392', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b47953a6-f06c-51ab-b183-a05fe4dc1392'}, {'abstract': 'LaChanze sang at the Allen Room as part of Lincoln Center’s American Songbook series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/arts/music/lachanze-sings-at-the-allen-room-review.html', 'snippet': 'LaChanze sang at the Allen Room as part of Lincoln Center’s American Songbook series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month LaChanze, the winsome Broadway star who won a 2006 Tony Award for best performance by a leading actress in a musical (“The Color Purple”), turned 50. That milestone wouldn’t be worth noting had she not announced it on Thursday night at the Allen Room, where she appeared as part of Lincoln Center’s American Songbook series. Her concert was also a 10th anniversary; she last visited the series in 2002 at the Stanley H. Kaplan Penthouse. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/arts/SONG/SONG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/arts/SONG/SONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/21/arts/SONG/SONG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Good-Humored Maturity When Life Proves Tough', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good-Humored Maturity When Life Proves Tough', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaChanze', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Songbook (Music Series)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T23:56:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/90d1cde2-5657-5ca1-bbc7-7ad4c84396a1', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90d1cde2-5657-5ca1-bbc7-7ad4c84396a1'}, {'abstract': 'Teenagers’ access to the Internet should not be restricted, says an expert on social research who says she benefited from it herself when she was young.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/fashion/danah-boyd-cracking-teenagers-online-codes.html', 'snippet': 'Teenagers’ access to the Internet should not be restricted, says an expert on social research who says she benefited from it herself when she was young.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH her coordinated zebra-striped scarf, tights and arm warmers (arm warmers?), spiky out-to-there hat and pierced tongue, 34-year-old Danah Boyd provides an electric Gen Y contrast to the staid gray lobby of Microsoft Research in Cambridge, Mass., which she enters in a flurry of animated conversation, Elmo-decorated iPhone in hand. In a juxtaposition that causes her no end of mischievous delight, her laptop bears a sticker of Snow White, whose outstretched arm gently cradled the Apple logo.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/fashion/22BOYD_SPAN/22BOYD_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/fashion/22BOYD_SPAN/22BOYD_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/fashion/22BOYD_SPAN/22BOYD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/fashion/22BOYD_SPAN/22BOYD_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/fashion/22BOYD_SPAN/22BOYD_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cracking Teenagers’ Online Codes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cracking Teenagers’ Online Codes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-20T23:56:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamela Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2ca9e8d-5099-5842-baa2-97a22e7ec284', 'word_count': 1457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2ca9e8d-5099-5842-baa2-97a22e7ec284'}, {'abstract': 'Banks have used quiet emergency loans from the European Central Bank, which has resisted buying up government debt in its own right, to come to their governments’ rescue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/world/european-central-bank-eases-euro-crisis-a-bit.html', 'snippet': 'Banks have used quiet emergency loans from the European Central Bank, which has resisted buying up government debt in its own right, to come to their governments’ rescue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Throughout the month, countries caught in the eye of the European financial storm, including Italy, Spain and France, have repeatedly defied expectations, selling big batches of bonds to the public at interest rates significantly lower than investors demanded at the height of the euro crisis late last year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/world/JP-EURO/JP-EURO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/21/world/JP-EURO/JP-EURO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth':