71c2f77b3', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dd46d41-5dea-58dd-a010-ba371c2f77b3'}, {'abstract': 'Krystle Ortiz described Hilda Santiago’s death after they bought drugs in East Harlem, an episode followed by the indictment of 35 people on narcotics charges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/nyregion/watching-a-friend-smoking-pcp-catch-fire-and-die.html', 'snippet': 'Krystle Ortiz described Hilda Santiago’s death after they bought drugs in East Harlem, an episode followed by the indictment of 35 people on narcotics charges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last hour of Hilda Santiago’s life began in a pew at the Roman Catholic Church of St. Paul in East Harlem. An odd place to find someone on her way to buy drugs, but there she was last Sunday, between Masses, with her friend and partner in crime, Krystle Ortiz. They made this trip often from their apartments in the Bronx: the No. 4 train downtown to the No. 6 train, then to church, then to 1780 Madison Avenue to “cop some dust,” as they called buying PCP. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/21/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/nyregion/CRIMESCENE/CRIMESCENE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbna