less common, and unmarried cohabitation less attractive?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2012/01/20/the-gingrich-question-cheating-vs-open-marriage/', 'snippet': 'If more couples considered monogamy optional, would divorce and cheating be less common, and unmarried cohabitation less attractive?', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gingrich Question: Cheating vs. Open Marriage', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T01:13:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb8edae6-4b9b-5d36-aedb-ef250a9109e6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb8edae6-4b9b-5d36-aedb-ef250a9109e6'}, {'abstract': 'Eli Manning’s arm strength — essentially a measure of a passer’s ability to throw the most difficult passes powerfully — is rooted in proper footwork and the building of his legs and core.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/sports/football/giants-manning-develops-arm-strength-by-working-from-the-feet-up.html', 'snippet': 'Eli Manning’s arm strength — essentially a measure of a passer’s ability to throw the most difficult passes powerfully — is rooted in proper footwork and the building of his legs and core.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — One day last week, a visitor walking by the weight room at the Giants’ practice facility could look through the glass windows and see Eli Manning, in a gray T-shirt, slowly and deliberately doing bicep curls with medium-sized dumbbells. Half a room away, offensive lineman Chris Snee was also lifting weights — with a barbell that looked to be sagging from all the pounds plated at each end. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multi