iddlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/348d602f-afb7-5e0a-9398-505204c93286', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/348d602f-afb7-5e0a-9398-505204c93286'}, {'abstract': 'Kezar Stadium, the 49ers’ home until 1970, boasts a history at once colorful and star-crossed, and remains dear to San Francisco’s heart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/sports/football/colorful-history-of-kezar-stadium-49ers-former-home.html', 'snippet': 'Kezar Stadium, the 49ers’ home until 1970, boasts a history at once colorful and star-crossed, and remains dear to San Francisco’s heart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — N.F.L. Hall of Famers called it home. It was where the alley-oop was invented. The 49ers’ founding owner died in his seat at the 50-yard line while watching a game. And it was there, atop a midfield hash mark, where Dirty Harry shot a serial killer called Scorpio. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/sports/YKEZAR1/YKEZAR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/sports/YKEZAR1/YKEZAR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/21/sports/YKEZAR1/YKEZAR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'West Coast Brew Gave Kezar Stadium Its Color', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'West Coast Brew Gave Kezar Stadium Its Color', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value'