 '2012-01-21T01:54:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e080635-ca49-5343-ac6e-87fa2c00f54a', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e080635-ca49-5343-ac6e-87fa2c00f54a'}, {'abstract': 'Badly needed regulations will require manufacturers of drugs, medical devices and medical supplies to disclose all payments they make to physicians or teaching hospitals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/opinion/who-else-is-paying-your-doctor.html', 'snippet': 'Badly needed regulations will require manufacturers of drugs, medical devices and medical supplies to disclose all payments they make to physicians or teaching hospitals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It took longer than expected, but the Obama administration is finally poised to enact badly needed regulations requiring that the manufacturers of drugs, medical devices and medical supplies disclose all payments they make to doctors or teaching hospitals. The information, which would be posted on a government Web site, will allow patients to decide whether they need to worry about any possible conflicts of interest. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Else Is Paying Your Doctor?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Else Is Paying Your Doctor?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T01:56:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/57184948-9a55-5445-a535-60201bdea252', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57184948-9a55-5445-a535-60201bdea252'}, {'abstract': 'Released to commemorate the sixth anniversary of a well-known fatality, a report illustrates, the public advocate says, that “the dots are not being connected” in a city agency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/nyregion/report-describes-trends-in-deaths-of-abused-and-neglected-children.html', 'snippet': 'Released to commemorate the sixth anniversary of a well-known fatality, a report illustrates, the public advocate says, that “the dots are not being connected” in a city agency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The child who came to be known as Case No. 95-2011-00009 was the fourth born into a home where abuse and neglect were practically a family tradition. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sobering Report Describes Trends in Deaths of Abused and Neglected Children', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sobering Report Describes Trends in Deaths of Abused and Neglected Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Nixzmary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Administration for Children's Services (NYC)", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Office of Children and Family Services (NYS)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T01:56:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jo Craven McGinty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jo', 'middlename': 'Craven', 'lastname': 'McGinty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4df7cc95-be94-5a1a-984c-0863108c200e', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4df7cc95-be94-5a1a-984c-0863108c200e'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Ketchum, who worked in publishing in New York, moved to a farm in Vermont and co-founded Country Journal with a fellow expatriate in 1974.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/us/richard-ketchum-country-journal-co-founder-dies-at-89.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Ketchum, who worked in publishing in New York, moved to a farm in Vermont and co-founded Country Journal with a fellow expatriate in 1974.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard M. Ketchum, an author and editor who co-founded Country Journal, a magazine that offered a blend of the bucolic and the practical, particularly to city folk who had opted for the rural life, died on Jan. 12 at a retirement home in Shelburne, Vt. He was 89 and until four years ago had lived on his nearly 1,000-acre farm, Saddleback, in Dorset, Vt.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/us/KETCHUM-obit/KETCHUM-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width'