rich/', 'snippet': 'Two separate e-mails sent to South Carolina Republicans claimed that Newt Gingrich had pressured his second wife, Marianne Gingrich, to have an abortion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENVILLE, S.C. — Newt Gingrich was the subject of an ugly and false smear campaign on Friday, the day before South Carolina Republican voters were set to go to the polls. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Is Victim of False Smear Campaign', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T02:02:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters and Serge F. Kovaleski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Kovaleski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f43ac11b-55ec-565f-8ed3-cd68c4ddecec', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f43ac11b-55ec-565f-8ed3-cd68c4ddecec'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees avoided arbitration with one of their outfielders.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/20/yankees-and-gardner-agree-to-contract/', 'snippet': 'The Yankees avoided arbitration with one of their outfielders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yankees avoided arbitration with outfielder Brett Gardner by agreeing to a one-year contract worth $2.8 million in Gardner’s first year of arbitration eligibility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {