ke Nuclear Arms', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Leader Warns Iran Not to Make Nuclear Arms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wen Jiabao', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T02:09:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc168b92-4114-5f20-8d77-f093f80d1eb6', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc168b92-4114-5f20-8d77-f093f80d1eb6'}, {'abstract': 'The poet Lawrence Ferlinghetti had given up watching football, in favor of baseball and soccer, until he stumbled on the fantastic finish of the 49ers-Saints playoff game last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/sports/football/lawrence-ferlinghetti-revives-his-love-of-the-49ers-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'The poet Lawrence Ferlinghetti had given up watching football, in favor of baseball and soccer, until he stumbled on the fantastic finish of the 49ers-Saints playoff game last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having given up watching football about five years ago because it had grown too violent and far less interesting than baseball and soccer, sports he finds much more poetic, Lawrence Ferlinghetti stumbled into watching the second half of the 49ers’ victory over the Saints last weekend. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/sports/YJPPOET/YJPPOET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 736, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/sports/YJPPOET/YJPPOET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/21/sports/YJPPOET/YJPPOET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '49ers Reclaim a Famous Fan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '49ers Reclaim a Famous Fan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Lights Bookstore', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferlinghetti, Lawrence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T02:10:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90977d58-4d20-5f55-8ece-3a9d7decd616', 'word_count': 671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90977d58-4d20-5f55-8ece-3a9d7decd616'}, {'abstract': 'Those “stickers of shame” work. Mayor Michael Bloomberg should veto a bill passed by the New York City Council to get rid of them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/opinion/sticky-stickers-cleaner-streets.html', 'snippet': 'Those “stickers of shame” work. Mayor Michael Bloomberg should veto a bill passed by the New York City Council to get rid of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to the question of cleaner streets or cleaner windows on cars parked illegally on those streets, the New York City Council has now sided with the vehicles and their owners.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sticky Stickers, Cleaner Streets', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sticky Stickers, Cleaner Streets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Council (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic and Parking Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T02:13:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/78686ddb-b9b4-593a-9b6c-90cf09a623b7', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78686ddb-b9b4-593a-9b6c-90cf09a623b7'}, {'abstract': 'The Heckscher Museum of Art is showing the photographs of Joseph Szabo, who captured many of his best subjects at the Long Island high school where he had taught.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/nyregion/joseph-szabos-teen-spirit-at-the-heckscher-museum-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Heckscher Museum of Art is showing the photographs of Joseph Szabo, who captured many of his best subjects at the Long Island high school where he had taught.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photography may be a technological medium, but photographs themselves differ from most products of technology in one significant way: Rather than becoming obsolete, they often get better, or at least more interesting, with age. An example of this can be seen in “Coming of Age in America: The Photography of Joseph Szabo” at the Heckscher Museum of Art in Huntington. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/nyregion/22ARTSLI1_SPAN/22ARTSLI1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/nyregion/22ARTSLI1_SPAN/22ARTSLI1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/nyregion/22ARTSLI1_SPAN/22ARTSLI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/nyregion/22ARTSLI1_SPAN/22ARTSLI1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/nyregion/22ARTSLI1_SPAN/22ARTSLI1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Teen Spirit, With ’80s Hair', 'kicker': 'Arts | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tee