 about security come as violence continues between the government and opposition groups.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/world/middleeast/us-may-close-embassy-in-damascus-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The American concerns about security come as violence continues between the government and opposition groups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAMASCUS, Syria — The continuing violence in Syria prompted the United States on Friday to warn that it may close its embassy here in the capital unless the Syrian government acts on a request to bolster security around the compound.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Warns It May Close Embassy in Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Warns It May Close Embassy In Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T02:55:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/babc08ae-2b71-5ca4-94a2-9b6bcd8931f2', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/babc08ae-2b71-5ca4-94a2-9b6bcd8931f2'}, {'abstract': 'His plan seems to be to appeal to an ugly, gut-level anger and animosity among a sizable portion of the Republican electorate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/opinion/blow-newts-southern-strategy.html', 'snippet': 'His plan seems to be to appeal to an ugly, gut-level anger and animosity among a sizable portion of the Republican electorate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Up with Newt. Down with dignity. That’s the way it goes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Newt’s Southern Strategy', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Newt’s Southern Strategy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T02:56:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles M. Blow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0066e4f2-2a77-5c32-96d0-8b30f124c021', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0066e4f2-2a77-5c32-96d0-8b30f124c021'}, {'abstract': 'Worsening economic conditions are sabotaging hopes for a democratic future. The new government must make reforms if it wants to spur investment and growth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/opinion/egypts-economic-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'Worsening economic conditions are sabotaging hopes for a democratic future. The new government must make reforms if it wants to spur investment and growth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the year since President Hosni Mubarak was ousted, Egypt has faced many challenges: the military-led government’s brutality against protesters and pro-democracy groups, its resistance to handing power to civilian leaders and the rise of Islamists in the country’s first free elections. Now worsening economic conditions are further sabotaging hopes for a democratic future.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Economic Crisis', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt’s Economic Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T02:57:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6041276-3a10-5418-b252-5b9dcada33c9', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6041276-3a10-5418-b252-5b9dcada33c9'}, {'abstract': 'A grant from The New York Times Neediest Cases Fund allowed 59 seniors on the Lower East Side continued access to an emergency alarm response system at an affordable rate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/nyregion/ears-system-gives-older-new-yorkers-independence.html', 'snippet': 'A grant from The New York Times Neediest Cases Fund allowed 59 seniors on the Lower East Side continued access to an emergency alarm response system at an affordable rate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a time when Angelo Boccino did not mind falling — if it was from an airplane and he had a parachute. In fact, Mr. Boccino jumped out of planes on combat missions when he was an Army paratrooper in World War II, he said. Today, he is 93, and falling can be hazardous to his health. So Mr. Boccino, who uses a wheelchair, an electric scooter and a walker to get around, depends on an emergency alert bracelet he wears on his left wrist.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/21/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/21/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Small Devices, Older New Yorkers Gain Independence and Peace of Mind', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Small Devices, Older New Yorkers Gain Independence and Peace of Mind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UJA-Federation of New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emerge