 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2559a279-f51b-5e29-ad39-a8437e9b8eca', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2559a279-f51b-5e29-ad39-a8437e9b8eca'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Mario Monti proposed a package that includes efforts to liberalize certain industries and services, and a $7.1 billion investment in infrastructure projects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/world/europe/italy-plans-new-measures-to-liberalize-economy.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Mario Monti proposed a package that includes efforts to liberalize certain industries and services, and a $7.1 billion investment in infrastructure projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — In a bold effort to transform Italy’s protectionist economy and to foster growth amid a deepening recession, Prime Minister Mario Monti on Friday announced a new set of measures aimed at reviving Italy’s sluggish economy by investing $7.1 billion in infrastructure and opening up professional guilds to competition. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy Announces New Steps to Get Economy Moving', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy Announces New Steps to Get Economy Moving', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monti, Mario', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T03:11:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo and Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1b67e7a-4e33-5e86-9af0-9920130cffbc', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1b67e7a-4e33-5e86-9af0-9920130cffbc'}, {'abstract': 'At Mario Batali and Joe Bastianich’s new restaurant in Westport, a creative menu grafts sophisticated concepts onto old standbys, going far beyond what one expects of a pizzeria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/nyregion/in-westport-complexity-and-intrigue-amid-the-old-standbys.html', 'snippet': 'At Mario Batali and Joe Bastianich’s new restaurant in Westport, a creative menu grafts sophisticated concepts onto old standbys, going far beyond what one expects of a pizzeria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOMETIMES having too many projects — and the restaurateurs Mario Batali and Joe Bastianich have many — can dilute even a fine concept. But that is not the case at one of the pair’s newest ventures, Tarry Lodge Enoteca Pizzeria in Westport. A sister to the well-known Tarry Lodge that opened in Port Chester more than three years ago, it is a smoothly run hands-on effort by Mario La Posta, the chef, and Andy Nusser, executive chef and managing partner with Nancy Selzer — all from the Port Chester team. And the bill for a lunch or dinner is reasonable, bucking the current Fairfield County trend of rising prices, which may explain why so many young couples dine there.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'Th