ow/f7977273-dc41-5d49-99c3-bf87d21710e9'}, {'abstract': 'A new survey found that lawyers were more likely to steer whites to Chapter 7 of the bankruptcy code and blacks to the more expensive Chapter 13.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/business/blacks-face-bias-in-bankruptcy-study-suggests.html', 'snippet': 'A new survey found that lawyers were more likely to steer whites to Chapter 7 of the bankruptcy code and blacks to the more expensive Chapter 13.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Blacks are about twice as likely as whites to wind up in the more onerous and costly form of consumer bankruptcy as they try to dig out from their debts, a new study has found.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/business/Bankrupt/Bankrupt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/21/business/Bankrupt/Bankrupt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/business/Bankrupt/Bankrupt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 781, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/business/Bankrupt/Bankrupt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/21/business/Bankrupt/Bankrupt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blacks Face Bias in Bankruptcy, Study Suggests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blacks Face Bias In Bankruptcy, Study Suggests', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lawless, Robert M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Dov', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Bankruptcies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of Empirical Legal Studies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T03:38:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51434c8e-c7dd-5db9-aa67-f7de4a12b08f', 'word_count': 1266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51434c8e-c7dd-5db9-aa67-f7de4a12b08f'}, {'abstract': 'The Commerce Department agreed to investigate a trade complaint by Whirlpool that said residential washing machines made in South Korea and Mexico were being sold below cost in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/business/global/us-investigates-trade-complaint-on-washers.html', 'snippet': 'The Commerce Department agreed to investigate a trade complaint by Whirlpool that said residential washing machines made in South Korea and Mexico were being sold below cost in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Commerce Department agreed to investigate a trade complaint by Whirlpool that said residential washing machines made in South Korea and Mexico were being sold below cost in America. The United States imported $1.1 billion of the washers from the two nations in 2010, the agency said. Whirlpool is requesting antidumping duties on LG and Samsung imports from South Korea and Mexico. The department also is considering whether to impose countervailing duties against the Korean products, to offset benefits of subsidies. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Investigates Trade Complaint on Washers', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Regulatory News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Investigates Trade Complaint On Washers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whirlpool Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commerce Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Washing Machines and Dryers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T03:39:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f61a133b-8c14-5293-b32c-932827ce4fa2', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f61a133b-8c14-5293-b32c-932827ce4fa2'}, {'abstract': 'Market Bistro has rough-hewn ceiling beams and brick walls, inventive food and a popularity partly owing to its owners, who also run the West End Cafe in Carle Place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/nyregion/market-bistro-in-jericho-draws-a-crowd-review.html', 'snippet': 'Market Bistro has rough-hewn ceiling beams and brick walls, inventive food and a popularity partly owing to its owners, who also run the West End Cafe in Carle Place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN the owners of a highly regarded restaurant open another place, the new spot is often on a fast track to popularity. Such is the case with Market Bistro in Jericho, which was opened in November by Bill Holden and Bob Caras, proprietors of the well-liked, 20-year-old West End Cafe in Carle Place, along with Adam Acerra, a former bartender at West End.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/nyregion/22DINELI3/22DINELI3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/nyregion/22DINELI3/22DINELI3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/nyregion/22DINELI3/22DINELI3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Rustic Bistro (Comes With a Crowd)', 'kicker': 'Long Island Dining | Jericho', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Rustic Bistro (Comes With a Crowd)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Market Bistro (Jericho, NY Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T03:43:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne Starkey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Starkey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/af78c773-1dba-5297-99d2-1b2d62c1af53', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af78c773-1dba-5297-99d2-1b2d62c1af53'}, {'abstract': 'David R. Slaine, a former Galleon Group employee who helped the authorities investigate the hedge fund’s co-founder, Raj Rajaratnam, was sentenced to probation for three years for securities fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/business/probation-for-a-former-galleon-group-employee.html', 'snippet': 'David R. Slaine, a former Galleon Group employee who helped the authorities investigate the hedge fund’s co-founder, Raj Rajaratnam, was sentenced to probation for three years for securities fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David R. Slaine, a former Galleon Group employee who helped the authorities investigate the hedge fund’s co-founder, Raj Rajaratnam, was sentenced to probation for three years for securities fraud. Mr. Slaine wore a hidden device to record dozens of conversations with suspects including Zvi Goffer, a former Galleon trader. Judge Richard J. Sullivan of United States District in Manhattan, who sentenced Mr. Slaine, also ordered him to perform 300 hours of community service and pay a $500,000 fine. The judge praised Mr. Slaine’s cooperation, which began in 2007. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Probation for a Former Galleon Group Employee', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Legal News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Probation For a Former Galleon Group Employee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 4, 'majo