ants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T03:45:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97a5e775-39c9-55a0-867e-b948df231808', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97a5e775-39c9-55a0-867e-b948df231808'}, {'abstract': 'Just one night before Carmelo Anthony faces his old team, he went 11 for 26 from the floor and got ejected from the game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/sports/basketball/anthony-and-knicks-struggle-as-losing-streak-hits-5.html', 'snippet': 'Just one night before Carmelo Anthony faces his old team, he went 11 for 26 from the floor and got ejected from the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The night before the Knicks have to face the possibility that the Denver Nuggets may have stolen their future, Brandon Jennings and the Milwaukee Bucks handed them their fifth straight loss Friday in part by making important steals with the alarming ease of practiced pickpockets. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/sports/subKNICKS/subKNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/21/sports/subKNICKS/subKNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/21/sports/subKNICKS/subKNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main'