s for three people under investigation for possible connections to WikiLeaks are appealing to a federal court to reveal which Internet companies have been asked to reveal information about them to the Justice Department.', 'lead_paragraph': ' This much is known: In its hunt for information about three people it believes to be associated with the whistle-blower site WikiLeaks, the Justice Department has sought to extract details about them and their communications on Twitter. What is not yet known is where else the Justice Department went looking. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Move to Investigate the Investigators in WikiLeaks Case', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T06:47:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ef11c05-c9bc-578e-afc1-b3fbe43cb6eb', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ef11c05-c9bc-578e-afc1-b3fbe43cb6eb'}, {'abstract': 'Ana Ivanovic survived a closely fought match and defeated American Vania King on Saturday at the Australian Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/ivanovic-closes-out-kings-musical-run/', 'snippet': 'Ana Ivanovic survived a closely fought match and defeated American Vania King on Saturday at the Australian Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia – Vania King’s quest for a berth in the Round of 16 ended without a victory song on Saturday when Ana Ivanovic of Serbia prevailed, 6-3, 6-4, in a closely fought match before about 8,000 fans at the 2012 Australian Open.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ivanovic Closes Out King’s Musical Run', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T07:28:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN MARTIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MARTIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61dbf49c-b36c-57df-8aa0-16effa27219e', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61dbf49c-b36c-57df-8aa0-16effa27219e'}, {'abstract': 'Top stories from across India this week from the regional press.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/newswallah-bharat-edition-20/', 'snippet': 'Top stories from across India this week from the regional press.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jammu and Kashmir: The Indian Air Force has been asked by the Jammu and Kashmir government to airlift people stranded by heavy snowfall between Srinagar and the Jammu region. The Jammu-Srinagar national highway, an important road link connecting the state to other parts of the country, remained closed for passenger traffic since the last one week, affected by landslides and snowfall, Kashmir Live reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Bharat Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink',