d his way back into the business end of a major tournament, reaching the second week of the 2012 Australian Open with a surprising four-set win over the Canadian Milos Raonic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — Though he is nearly 10 years removed from his last Grand Slam title, Lleyton Hewitt pushed his way back into the business end of a major tournament, reaching the second week of the 2012 Australian Open with a surprising four-set win over the Canadian Milos Raonic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hewitt Conjures Some Old Magic to Defeat Raonic', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T14:43:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN ROTHENBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROTHENBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8e31bd9-9823-542d-a7bb-5bd926e16b18', 'word_count': 400, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8e31bd9-9823-542d-a7bb-5bd926e16b18'}, {'abstract': 'Rising in the polls, Newt Gingrich awaits what he hopes will be his big moment.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/gingrich-shows-confidence-as-voting-begins/', 'snippet': 'Rising in the polls, Newt Gingrich awaits what he hopes will be his big moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newt Gingrich began a busy day of brief drop-by stops at restaurants and a school across South Carolina’s conservative northern tier. First up was the Grapevine Restaurant in Boiling Springs, where some breakfast patrons already had their small “I voted” stickers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Confident as Voting Begins', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'co