 playoffs, and has become one of football’s celebrated spikers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOXBOROUGH, Mass. — Conan O’Brien featured him in a parody of the song “St. Elmo’s Fire” on TV last week. The Worcester Sharks of the American Hockey League are paying him $7,500 to “spike” a hockey puck before one of their games next month.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/ypatriots/ypatriots-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/ypatriots/ypatriots-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/ypatriots/ypatriots-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gronkowski Earning Name for Scores and Spikes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scores With Frequency, Spikes With Ferocity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gronkowski, Rob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T16:28:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter May', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'May', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b96f59a3-d9f4-57e3-8a5d-bb800b3a1021', 'word_count': 1039, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b96f59a3-d9f4-57e3-8a5d-bb800b3a1021'}, {'abstract': 'Under scrutiny for his taxes, Mitt Romney assails Newt Gingrich on his consulting.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/romney-urges-gingrich-disclosure-on-freddie-mac/', 'snippet': 'Under scrutiny for his taxes, Mitt Romney assails Newt Gingrich on his consulting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENVILLE, S.C. — As South Carolina residents began voting Saturday morning, Mitt Romney stopped to thank supporters and volunteers at his campaign office here, and he called on Newt Gingrich to release the details of his contract with Freddie Mac.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Urges Gingrich Disclosure on Freddie Mac', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haley, Nikki', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T16:36:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c3d91c1-244a-5167-8440-d169a417d661', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c3d91c1-244a-5167-8440-d169a417d661'}, {'abstract': 'Brendan Steele, the PGA Tour golfer, grew up in a place few would have thought could produce an elite professional player.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/sports/golf/For-Brendan-Steele-Road-to-PGA-Was-Mountain-to-Descend.html', 'snippet': 'Brendan Steele, the PGA Tour golfer, grew up in a place few would have thought could produce an elite professional player.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IDYLLWILD, Calif. — The sign welcoming visitors into this town’s snug embrace reads: Home of Adventure, Music, Art and Harmony. Nestled like a dogleg in the San Jacinto Mountains, it is protected by tall pines, pocked by boulders and redolent of cedar, and has neither a golf course nor a driving range. It would seem infertile ground for raising a professional golfer, and yet it is where Brendan Steele, the reigning Texas Open champion, grew up. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YGOLF2/YGOLF2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YGOLF2/YGOLF2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YGOLF2/YGOLF2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YGOLF2/YGOLF2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': '