i': 'nyt://article/21c65a2e-8851-5130-b690-98df54036da4'}, {'abstract': 'Clint Dempsey scored his second hat trick in the past 14 days as Fulham defeated Newcastle in England’s Premier League Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/dempsey-on-a-roll/', 'snippet': 'Clint Dempsey scored his second hat trick in the past 14 days as Fulham defeated Newcastle in England’s Premier League Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If this keeps up someone might mistake Clint Dempsey for a prolific Brazilian goal-scorer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dempsey on a Roll', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Clint', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fulham (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United State Soccer Federation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T19:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0008f97-6fc3-5f17-aab9-3b3d087b4d85', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0008f97-6fc3-5f17-aab9-3b3d087b4d85'}, {'abstract': 'A program of the United States Tennis Association features smaller courts and rackets; lower nets; slower, less bouncy balls; and less emphasis on competition.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/trying-to-appeal-to-u-s-under-10-generation-by-shrinking-the-games-scale/', 'snippet': 'A program of the United States Tennis Association features smaller courts and rackets; lower nets; slower, less bouncy balls; and less emphasis on competition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Australian Open, the news looked grim again for American tennis. For the first time since 1973, no American man reached the fourth round there, and entering the tournament’s second week, Serena Williams is the only American left in the singles draws.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trying to Appeal to U.S. Under-10 Generation by Shrinking the Game’s Scale', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T19:07:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By STUART MILLER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MILLER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a35e91d-25bd-5901-a335-049064c2b0e4', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a35e91d-25bd-5901-a335-049064c2b0e4'}, {'abstract': 'A preview of the U.S. friendly match Saturday night against Venezuela.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/preview-u-s-vs-venezuela/', 'snippet': 'A preview of the U.S. friendly match Saturday night against Venezuela.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of Jurgen Klinsmann’s first-choice players have games in Europe this weekend, so he will run out the best of his B and C list on Saturday night for a friendly against Venezuela in Glendale, Ariz. (8:09 p.m. | Updated With Lineups, Below)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Men vs. Venezuela', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinsmann, Jurgen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shea, Brek', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zusi, Graham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T19:12:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ff6de91-86d7-5904-bcb3-857161b43357', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ff6de91-86d7-5904-bcb3-857161b43357'}, {'abstract': 'Safety Ed Reed and linebacker Ray Lewis are the heart and soul of the Ravens’ defense. This could be their last chance at a Super Bowl.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/sports/football/for-ravens-leaders-the-time-is-now.html', 'snippet': 'Safety Ed Reed and linebacker Ray Lewis are the heart and soul of the Ravens’ defense. This could be their last chance at a Super Bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OWINGS MILLS, Md. — If he listened closely, Cory Redding could hear the men laughing. The sounds, deep and resonant, were coming from around the corner, in the Baltimore Ravens’ training room, where Redding found Ray Lewis on one table and Ed Reed on another, cracking jokes and poking fun at each other. When Lewis offered advice to a younger teammate, Reed interrupted, pleading not to believe him: “He told me that, too, and it didn’t work.”', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YRAVENS/YRAVENS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YRAVENS/YRAVENS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YRAVENS/YRAVENS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YRAVENS/YRAVENS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YRAVENS/YRAVENS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ravens for the Ages, Running Out of Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ravens for the Ages, Running Out of Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Ed', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, Ray', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T19:14:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd3396df-a987-534f-b7d1-881776ba1f6d', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd3396df-a987-534f-b7d1-881776ba1f6d'}, {'abstract': 'Ethan Hawke looks back on “Reality Bites” and remembers what it was like to be a Gen X poster boy.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/reality-bites-and-the-perils-of-being-a-generations-touchstone/', 'snippet': 'Ethan Hawke looks back on “Reality Bites” and remembers what it was like to be a Gen X poster boy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — The 20-something hipsters partying on Main Street here make us feel old enough. Does “Reality Bites” really need to be a Sundance “rediscovered in the archive” selection?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Reality Bites’ and the Perils of Being a Generation’s Touchstone', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawke, Ethan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loeb, Lisa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryder, Winona', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stiller, Ben', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T19:45:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb117d00-4519-506f-86a4-5308f5e32339', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb117d00-4519-506f-86a4-5308f5e32339'}, {'abstract': 'Gingrich’s late momentum could be an important factor in the results from South Carolina.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/south-carolina-primary-overview-and-forecast/', 'snippet': 'Gingrich’s late momentum could be an important factor in the results from South Carolina.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just days ago, Mitt Romney appeared to be on a glide path to the Republican nomination. Coming off a big victory in New Hampshire and an apparent win in Iowa, he had just received the endorsement of Jon M. Huntsman Jr., and had as much as a 23-point lead in some national polls of Republican voters. He also led in South Carolina polls, sometimes by double digits, and attacks by Republican rivals on Mr. Romney’s tenure at Bain Capital did not appear to be harming him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Carolina Primary Overview and Forecast', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intrade', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marist College', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southern States (US)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T19:46:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90e3b0fa-61b2-5627-844a-86f9fa49b81f', 'word_count': 1558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90e3b0fa-61b2-5627-844a-86f9fa49b81f'}, {'abstract': 'Attacks by the Islamist sect Boko Haram in northern Nigeria’s largest city struck police buildings, immigration offices and an office of the secret police.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/world/africa/dozens-killed-by-radical-islamic-sect-in-nigeria.html', 'snippet': 'Attacks by the Islamist sect Boko Haram in northern Nigeria’s largest city struck police buildings, immigration offices and an office of the secret police.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABUJA, Nigeria — More than 100 people have been killed in a series of attacks in northern Nigeria’s largest city, officials said Saturday, in what appears to be the deadliest strike yet by a radical Islamist group.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/world/sub-nigeria/sub-nigeria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/world/sub-nigeria/sub-nigeria-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/world/sub-nigeria/sub-nigeria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop