avard, the star Bruins forward, said Saturday that he still has headaches and short-term memory loss a year after his last concussion.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Year Later, Concussions Keep Savard Off the Ice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Year Later, Concussions Keep Savard Off the Ice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savard, Marc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T19:58:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c57b90f2-1d42-56f3-b7de-89757aee7e04', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c57b90f2-1d42-56f3-b7de-89757aee7e04'}, {'abstract': 'Shortly after the former president, Marc Ravalomanana, boarded a commercial flight from South Africa, the island nation closed its airspace.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/world/africa/madagascars-ousted-president-is-rebuffed-in-bid-to-return.html', 'snippet': 'Shortly after the former president, Marc Ravalomanana, boarded a commercial flight from South Africa, the island nation closed its airspace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHANNESBURG — A commercial airliner carrying the ousted president of Madagascar back to that country’s capital was turned around midflight, after government officials abruptly closed the nation’s airspace on Saturday, apparently to prevent the flight from landing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/world/madagascar/madagascar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/world/madagascar/madagascar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/world/madagascar/madagascar-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ousted Leader Is Thwarted in a Return to Madagascar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ousted Leader Is Thwarted In a Return to Madagascar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajoelina, Andry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ravalomanana, Marc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madagascar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T20:01:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lydia Polgreen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lydia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polgreen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1447d134-438a-58d5-93cb-df4b114d2b9c', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1447d134-438a-58d5-93cb-df4b114d2b9c'}, {'abstract': 'In England’s Premier League, Manchester United is scheduled to play Arsenal on Sunday morning, live on U.S. network television.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/sports/soccer/qa-with-manchester-uniteds-alex-ferguson.html', 'snippet': 'In England’s Premier League, Manchester United is scheduled to play Arsenal on Sunday morning, live on U.S. network television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alex Ferguson, marking his 25th season as Manchester United’s manager, turned 70 on Dec. 31. A former player, he began coaching in 1974 with East Stirlingshire in Scotland, which gave him £2,000 (about $3,100) to acquire five players. His 1999 United team won three titles, sweeping championships in England’s Premier League, F.A. Cup and the Champions League. Fox will televise United’s game against Arsenal at 11 a.m. Eastern on Sunday, the first live Premier League match on that network. In an interview with Claire Bloomfield for the British online magazine Sabotage Times , Ferguson recently reflected on how the game, and his job, had changed over the years.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YFERGUSON/YFERGUSON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YFERGUSON/YFERGUSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YFERGUSON/YFERGUSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. & A. With Manchester United’s Alex Ferguson', 'kicker': 'Q. & A.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Retirement Is for Young People, Not Older People’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferguson, Alex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester United (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Arsenal (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T20:03:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6b4d458-c30c-54e3-9db9-7d40b5c3e7f2', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6b4d458-c30c-54e3-9db9-7d40b5c3e7f2'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview with Claire Bloomfield for the British online magazine Sabotage Times, Alex Ferguson recently reflected on how the game, and his job, had changed over the years', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/q-a-with-manchester-uniteds-alex-ferguson/', 'snippet': 'In an interview with Claire Bloomfield for the British online magazine Sabotage Times, Alex Ferguson recently reflected on how the game, and his job, had changed over the years', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alex Ferguson, marking his 25th season as Manchester United’s manager, turned 70 on Dec. 31. A former player, he began coaching in 1974 with East Stirlingshire in Scotland, which gave him £2,000 (about $3,100) to acquire five players. His 1999 United team won three titles, sweeping championships in England’s Premier League, F.A. Cup and the Champions League. Fox will televise United’s game against Arsenal at 11 a.m. Eastern on Sunday, the first live Premier League match on that network. In Claire Bloomfield for the British online magazine Sabotage Times, Ferguson recently reflected on how the game, and his job, had changed over the years. Read the interview here. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. & A. With Manchester United’s Alex Ferguson', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferguson, Alex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Arsenal (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manchester United (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T20:06:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c877aa16-5ebb-53d2-9233-13a3e166b391', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c877aa16-5ebb-53d2-9233-13a3e166b391'}, {'abstract': 'This season’s 49ers seem to be an echo of their glory years, when the owner Eddie DeBartolo empowered an inner circle of Bill Walsh and John McVay to act on its own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/sports/football/49ers-remind-san-francisco-of-glory-years.html', 'snippet': 'This season’s 49ers seem to be an echo of their glory years, when the owner Eddie DeBartolo empowered an inner circle of Bill Walsh and John McVay to act on its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Last weekend at Candlestick Park, it felt the way it used to feel when “Montana” and “Young” and “Rice” were stitched onto jerseys, when the 49ers boasted a franchise as successful as any in sports.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YOWNER/YOWNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 858, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}