t do.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/needed-more-political-dimensions/', 'snippet': 'It’s 2012, and let’s face it, the old way of sizing up candidates on the left-to-right spectrum just will not do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One dimension — left to right — doesn’t suffice to deal with today’s political reality. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Needed: More Political Dimensions', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T20:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Perry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e03f8acd-1b07-5ead-89eb-4d53bcf9fecc', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e03f8acd-1b07-5ead-89eb-4d53bcf9fecc'}, {'abstract': 'Disclosure has often become an endpoint in the chain of responsibility, an act of compliance with the letter of the law rather than the spirit of transparency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/sunday-review/hard-truths-about-disclosure.html', 'snippet': 'Disclosure has often become an endpoint in the chain of responsibility, an act of compliance with the letter of the law rather than the spirit of transparency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN New York and a growing number of American cities, diners are encountering sanitary grades in restaurants’ windows — A, B or C. That system is an example of helpful disclosure, researchers say: information that is simple and comprehensible, important to recipients and easily acted upon. I recently chose between outwardly identical Japanese noodle shops on East Ninth Street in Manhattan based on the system, walking into the A rather than the B. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sunday-review/22COVER-1327088722894/22COVER-1327088722894-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/sunday-review/22COVER-1327088722894/22COVER-1327088722894-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 608}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sunday-review/22COVER-1327088722894/22COVER-1327088722894-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1006, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sunday-review/22COVER-1327088722894/22COVER-1327088722894-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/sunday-review/22COVER-1327088722894/22COVER-1327088722894-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Disclose ... Nothing', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Disclose ... Nothing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T20:34:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cd0290a-92fc-5716-9c62-cc776b613435', 'word_count': 1620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cd0290a-92fc-5716-9c62-cc776b613435'}, {'abstract': 'Even going into its sixth year, the N.H.L.’s Winter Classic retains the capacity to delight and astonish, as evidenced by last week’s reports that the game next Jan. 1 will be played at Michigan Stadium.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/target-for-the-next-winter-classic-104174/', 'snippet': 'Even going into its sixth year, the N.H.L.’s Winter Classic retains the capacity to delight and astonish, as evidenced by last week’s reports that the game next Jan. 1 will be played at Michigan Stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even going into its sixth year, the N.H.L.’s Winter Classic retains the capacity to delight and astonish, as evidenced by last week’s reports that the game next Jan. 1 will be played at Michigan Stadium in Ann Arbor and will feature the Detroit Red Wings and the Toronto Maple Leafs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Target for the Next Winter Classic: 104,174', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T20:44:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein and Stu Hackel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Stu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hackel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/952e3c82-ab52-52b7-82d2-5f800ead0575', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/952e3c82-ab52-52b7-82d2-5f800ead0575'}, {'abstract': 'Rick Santorum said he would be pleased with a third-place finish in South Carolina Saturday but vowed to stay in the presidential race through the Florida primary no matter what.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/santorum-says-he-will-remain-in-race-through-florida/', 'snippet': 'Rick Santorum said he would be pleased with a third-place finish in South Carolina Saturday but vowed to stay in the presidential race through the Florida primary no matter what.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHAPIN, S.C. — Rick Santorum said he would be pleased with a third-place finish in South Carolina Saturday but vowed to stay in the presidential race through the Florida primary no matter what.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Santorum Says He Will Remain in Race Through Florida', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T21:06:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3850abb-cad2-55bc-a18f-bccb1e168058', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3850abb-cad2-55bc-a18f-bccb1e168058'}, {'abstract': 'The two best teams in the East and perhaps in the N.H.L., the Rangers and the Bruins, played Saturday for the first time this season and it was razor close from start to finish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/sports/hockey/gaboriks-overtime-goal-lifts-rangers-over-bruins.html', 'snippet': 'The two best teams in the East and perhaps in the N.H.L., the Rangers and the Bruins, played Saturday for the first time this season and it was razor close from start to finish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — It was a showdown of two of the N.H.L.’s best teams this season, a first meeting between voracious opponents who play a similarly relentless style. And when it was over Saturday afternoon, only 3.6 seconds from the end of overtime, the Rangers stood alone, victorious. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YRANGERS/YRANGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YRANGERS/YRANGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YRANGERS/YRANGERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YRANGERS/YRANGERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/YRANGERS/YRANGERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Showdown, Penalty by Bruins Leads to Injury and Victory for Rangers', 'kicker': 'Rangers 3, Bruins 2, OT', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Showdown, Penalty by Bruins Leads to Injury and Victory for Rangers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaborik, Marian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Bruins', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T21:10:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ca87d30-d2ec-5080-b365-de494c423439', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ca87d30-d2ec-5080-b365-de494c423439'}, {'abstract': 'The discovery of tainted rice 35 miles from a damaged nuclear plant has Japan scrambling to plug gaps in its food-screening measures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/world/asia/wary-japanese-take-food-safety-into-their-own-hands.html', 'snippet': 'The discovery of tainted rice 35 miles from a damaged nuclear plant has Japan scrambling to plug gaps in its food-screening measures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ONAMI, Japan — In the fall, as this valley’s rice paddies ripened into a carpet of gold, inspectors came to check for radioactive contamination.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/world/radiation1/radiation1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/world/radiation1/radiation1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/world/radiation1/radiation1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/world/radiation1/radiation1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/world/radiation1/radiation1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Japanese Struggle to Protect Their Food Supply', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japanese Struggle to Protect Their Food Supply', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T21:13:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca760158-45c5-5630-87b5-fce9f2075f6e', 'word_count': 1448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca760158-45c5-5630-87b5-fce9f2075f6e'}, {'abstract': 'Readers post their comments on my column about the transformative power of teachers.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/the-most-important-job-in-america/', 'snippet': 'Readers post their comments on my column about the transformative power of teachers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column returns to education, and the importance of teaching as a way to improve education outcomes. I think education is, in the long run, the most important challenge America faces and the one where we’re in greatest difficulties. If we want to maintain economic competitiveness and chip away at poverty, we simply have to improve high school graduation rates and college attendance — and that in turn will depend on an overhaul of the entire education system, starting with early childhood education.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Most Important Job in America', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T21:19:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/716b0aee-b824-56f0-8702-1aec439c7081', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/716b0aee-b824-56f0-8702-1aec439c7081'}, {'abstract': 'The law granting Ali Abdullah Saleh, the departing president, freedom from prosecution was criticized by Human Rights Watch and antigovernment activists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/world/middleeast/yemens-parliament-approves-immunity-for-president-saleh.html', 'snippet': 'The law granting Ali Abdullah Saleh, the departing president, freedom from prosecution was criticized by Human Rights Watch and antigovernment activists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yemen’s Parliament approved immunity on Saturday to free President Ali Abdullah Saleh from prosecution, following through on a requirement in a deal for him to give up power. The lawmakers extended the legislation to grant immunity for politically motivated crimes committed by all officials working under Mr. Saleh, according to the state-run Saba news agency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/world/yemen/yemen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 477, 'width': 338, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/world/yemen/yemen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/world/yemen/yemen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yemen Legislators Approve Immunity for the President', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Immunity Approved For Leader Of Yemen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and H