T funds should be used primarily for expansion or maintenance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A battle is brewing between top Bay Area Rapid Transit leaders over a billion-dollar rail extension to Livermore. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/us/22BCExtension/22BCExtension-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/us/22BCExtension/22BCExtension-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/us/22BCExtension/22BCExtension-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Deep Conflict Looms Over Billion-Dollar BART Extension to Livermore', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deep Conflict Looms Over Billion-Dollar BART Extension to Livermore', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bay Area Rapid Transit', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco Bay Area (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suburbs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T22:10:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zusha Elinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zusha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8c57344-5900-53ae-873a-a0f5c7546055', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8c57344-5900-53ae-873a-a0f5c7546055'}, {'abstract': 'The tsunami in Japan last year is spurring innovations like a mini-ark called “Noah” and a 3-D emergency communication system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/business/inventions-offer-tools-to-endure-future-disasters.html', 'snippet': 'The tsunami in Japan last year is spurring innovations like a mini-ark called “Noah” and a 3-D emergency communication system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN the devastating earthquake and tsunami struck northern Japan last March, the home of Shoji Tanaka, more than 200 miles south of the quake’s epicenter, was spared any major damage. But he worked as a volunteer in the disaster zone, supplying clothing and helping with clean-up, and said he was “appalled by the horrifying damage.” ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/business/22-PROTO4/22-PROTO4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/business/22-PROTO4/22-PROTO4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/business/22-PROTO4/22-PROTO4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/business/22-PROTO4/22-PROTO4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/business/22-PROTO4/22-PROTO4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From One Tragedy, Tools to Fight the Next', 'kicker': 'Prototype', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From One Tragedy, Tools to Fight the Next', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-21T22:16:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole LaPorte', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LaPorte', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6afd2fb-7180-511d-9e58-97606f325ca1', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6afd2fb-7180-511d-9e58-97606f325ca1'}, {'abstract': 'Americans spend more than patients in any other country, but with very mixed results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/opinion/sunday/the-money-traps-in-us-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'Americans spend more than patients in any other country, but with very mixed results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why does an appendectomy in Germany cost roughly a quarter what it costs in the United States? Or an M.R.I. scan cost less than a third as much, on average, in Canada?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Money Traps in U.S. Health Care', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Quality Control', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Money Traps In U.S. Health Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Edi