on': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a7fc713-9b10-5701-9c90-610c719bb6fd', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a7fc713-9b10-5701-9c90-610c719bb6fd'}, {'abstract': 'Kim Jong-il has been dead for a month, and the embalmers are said to be at their work. Reports from Moscow say that Russian scientists are guiding North Korean doctors in giving Mr. Kim the same treatments that have kept Vladimir Lenin in the pink since 1924.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/how-the-dear-leader-will-be-kept-in-the-pink/', 'snippet': 'Kim Jong-il has been dead for a month, and the embalmers are said to be at their work. Reports from Moscow say that Russian scientists are guiding North Korean doctors in giving Mr. Kim the same treatments that have kept Vladimir Lenin in the pink...', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Kim Jong-il has been dead for just over a month, and the embalmers in Pyongyang are reportedly at their work — draining blood, scooping out internal organs, removing the brain and preserving the genitals. Even in death, Mr. Kim’s remarkable bouffant hairdo will remain intact.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Keep the Dear Leader Well Preserved', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Il-sung', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong Il', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T02:06:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organizat