nd of the Humana Challenge and was in fine form, at least sartorially. As Clinton stood on the first tee box at the Palmer Private course at PGA West, a fan in the stands shouted, “Those are gorgeous shoes, Mr. President.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/CLINTON/CLINTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/CLINTON/CLINTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/CLINTON/CLINTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clinton Plays to Crowd at PGA Tournament', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clinton Plays to Crowd at PGA Tournament', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PGA Tour Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarron, Scott', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norman, Greg', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T02:33:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f87b386b-c957-5c13-8869-a9e99af07a67', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f87b386b-c957-5c13-8869-a9e99af07a67'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 22, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/pageoneplus/corrections-january-22.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 22, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: January 22', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T02:35:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NewsDesk', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbc15828-a4d1-5f82-bd09-82b255cdb1e2', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbc15828-a4d1-5f82-bd09-82b255cdb1e2'}, {'abstract': 'How the Battle of Mill Springs changed the course of the Civil War in the Western Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/21/the-fog-of-war/', 'snippet': 'How the Battle of Mill Springs changed the course of the Civil War in the Western Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the morning fog of Jan. 19, 1862, gave way to the haze of musket and cannon smoke around Logan’s Crossroads, Ky., Confederate Gen. Felix Zollicoffer gingerly approached a regiment of Kentuckians. After imploring the Kentuckians not to shoot one of their own in the confusion of battle, one of the men – perhaps the unit’s leader, Col. Speed S. Fry of nearby Danville – identified Zollicoffer, a Tennessean, as an enemy commander. There was a hail of lead and the white-coated Zollicoffer lay dying on the battlefield. He was the first Confederate commander to die in battle in the Western Theater, but far from the last. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fog of War', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 