 that the United States would start negotiations in Qatar next week, making it clear that there was a long way to go.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/world/asia/taliban-talks-a-long-way-off-us-envoy-says.html', 'snippet': 'An American envoy rejected reports that the United States would start negotiations in Qatar next week, making it clear that there was a long way to go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — No peace talks with the Taliban this week: That was the short message on Sunday from the American envoy charged with starting those negotiations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Talks With Taliban a Long Way Off, American Envoy Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Talks With Taliban a Long Way Off, American Envoy Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grossman, Marc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T17:48:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/139ad5f4-12e6-56d5-bb55-6c46dea2a407', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/139ad5f4-12e6-56d5-bb55-6c46dea2a407'}, {'abstract': 'Kelly Clarkson unleashed her angst and paid tribute to Etta James on Saturday night at Radio City Music Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/arts/music/kelly-clarkson-at-radio-city-music-hall-review.html', 'snippet': 'Kelly Clarkson unleashed her angst and paid tribute to Etta James on Saturday night at Radio City Music Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first song Kelly Clarkson sang for “American Idol” judges 10 years ago was “At Last,” the well-worn number popularized by Etta James that is used by bluesy performers to show their mettle. Maybe Ms. Clarkson rushed it a bit back then, smiled too much, did not quite nail the languor of the song. But she was delicate with the lyrics, and she showed off a voice that moved in all sorts of ways, without ever appearing to strain. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22clarkson-web/22clarkson-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22clarkson-web/22clarkson-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22clarkson-web/22clarkson-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22clarkson-web/22clarkson-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/22/arts/22clarkson-web/22clarkson-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Happily Up to Her Ears in Angst', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Happily Up to Her Ears In Angst', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarkson, Kelly', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio City Music Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T17:49:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/361ba999-bc53-5229-b576-c36ab4aaa8be', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/361ba999-bc53-5229-b576-c36ab4aaa8be'}, {'abstract': 'Despite winter storms in parts of the country, moviegoers flocked to the latest installment in Sony’s “Underworld” vampire series.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/underworld-awakening-leads-at-the-box-office/', 'snippet': 'Despite winter storms in parts of the country, moviegoers flocked to the latest installment in Sony’s “Underworld” vampire series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is why Hollywood keeps churning out sequels: The fourth movie in Sony’s “Underworld” vampire series, “Underworld Awakening,” was an easy No. 1 at the North American box office over the weekend, taking in about $25.4 million despite winter storms that kept business light in parts of the United States. Solid ticket sales for “Underworld Awakening” were fueled by turnout for higher-priced Imax screens. Even so, this 3-D movie will need to perform well overseas to justify its cost of about $70 million, sharply higher than the budget for “Underworld: Rise of the Lycans” in 2009.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Underworld Awakening’ Leads at the Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vampires', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lucas, George', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T17:50:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67c29a4f-0bac-5f45-b338-b93bb20932eb', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67c29a4f-0bac-5f45-b338-b93bb20932eb'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Tachman’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/photos-of-the-moment-dior-homme-2/', 'snippet': 'Kevin Tachman’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of the Moment | Dior Homme', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T18:02:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Tachman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tachman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b731fb1-cc3f-5e68-a40c-105f3d725666', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b731fb1-cc3f-5e68-a40c-105f3d725666'}, {'abstract': 'Business models be damned. Bargeloads of money move back and forth, following the herd’s assessment of any given start-up’s recent fortunes. This is Silicon Valley, where decisions are not always made based on revenue or potential business models but instead seem to be driven by a herd mentality and a yearning to be a part of a potential next big thing.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/disruptions-the-sloshing-sound-of-tech-valuations/', 'snippet': 'Business models be damned. Bargeloads of money move back and forth, following the herd’s assessment of any given start-up’s recent fortunes. This is Silicon Valley, where decisions are not always made based on revenue or potential business models ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent Thursday night I stood motionless and perplexed on the dance floor of a San Francisco club. As I looked around, 300 or so people danced and darted back and forth to a free open bar while laser lights shot overhead. Cellphones glowed, like a video of luminescent jellyfish, as people snapped pictures and slung moments of the evening onto dozens of social networks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/business/22disrupt3/22disrupt3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disruptions: Tech Valuations Defy the Restraints of Reality', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Path.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T18:24:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a18df870-d7f2-5d09-a95f-ec786a87d4e1', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a18df870-d7f2-5d09-a95f-ec786a87d4e1'}, {'abstract': 'Sonny Vandevelde’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/photos-of-the-moment-hermes-4/', 'snippet': 'Sonny Vandevelde’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of the Moment | Hermès', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T18:43:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonny Vandevelde', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vandevelde', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9d5c2c4-ad11-5562-ac44-4a3773a25c8b', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9d5c2c4-ad11-5562-ac44-4a3773a25c8b'}, {'abstract': 'Both of the deaths in China were notable because neither victim reported any contact with birds in the month preceding his illness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/world/asia/china-reports-2nd-bird-flu-death-in-month.html', 'snippet': 'Both of the deaths in China were notable because neither victim reported any contact with birds in the month preceding his illness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — A man died in southern China on Sunday from the H5N1 bird flu virus, the Health Ministry reported. It was China’s second such death in less than a month.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Reports a Second Bird Flu Death in Less Than a Month', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Reports a Second Bird Flu Death in Less Than a Month', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avian Influenza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T19:25:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c183bd87-1d04-5c8f-b6cb-1a4a41e085b7', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c183bd87-1d04-5c8f-b6cb-1a4a41e085b7'}, {'abstract': 'The conductor Leon Botstein and the American Symphony Orchestra offered selections that reflected both Stravinsky’s Russian heritage and the aesthetics of his adopted homelands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/arts/music/american-symphonys-stravinsky-at-carnegie-review.html', 'snippet': 'The conductor Leon Botstein and the American Symphony Orchestra offered selections that reflected both Stravinsky’s Russian heritage and the aesthetics of his adopted homelands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has been much debate about the Russian-ness of Stravinsky, who lived and worked away from his native country for most of his life. In a program called “Stravinsky Outside Russia,” on Friday evening at Carnegie Hall, the conductor Leon Botstein and the American Symphony Orchestra offered selections that reflected both Stravinsky’s Russian heritage and the aesthetics of his adopted homelands.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/arts/leon-2/leon-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 960, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/arts/leon-2/leon-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/23/arts/leon-2/leon-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stravinsky’s Travels, Recounted in Melody', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stravinsky’s Travels, Recounted in Melody', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN SYMPHONY ORCHESTRA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Collegiate Chorale', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stravinsky, Igor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Keith (Musician)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Botstein, Leon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phan, Nicholas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quintero, Ann McMahon', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T19:27:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/36debabb-c3c5-5a6c-be53-74e95c70bcd9', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36debabb-c3c5-5a6c-be53-74e95c70bcd9'}, {'abstract': 'The announcement by the Arizona Democrat comes about a year after a shooting attack that left 6 people dead and 13 wounded — including Ms.Giffords.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/gabrielle-giffords-says-shes-leaving-the-house/', 'snippet': 'The announcement by the Arizona Democrat comes about a year after a shooting attack that left 6 people dead and 13 wounded — including Ms.Giffords.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:49 p.m. | Updated The full report of this article is available here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gabrielle Giffords Says She’s Leaving the House', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tucson Shooting (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giffords, Gabrielle', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Green, Christina Taylor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loughner, Jared Lee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roll, John M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T19:42:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03e3d90d-cc08-5104-95f7-c85e452575d5', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03e3d90d-cc08-5104-95f7-c85e452575d5'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Tachman’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/photos-of-the-moment-miharayasuhiro/', 'snippet': 'Kevin Tachman’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of the Moment | Miharayasuhiro', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T19:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Tachman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tachman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1e86b57-0b7d-59c3-9311-cfcccc2f168b', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1e86b57-0b7d-59c3-9311-cfcccc2f168b'}, {'abstract': 'Jerry Sandusky said that “nobody will be able to take away the memories we all shared of a great man.”', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/sandusky-issues-statement-about-paterno/', 'snippet': 'Jerry Sandusky said that “nobody will be able to take away the memories we all shared of a great man.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reaction to the death of Joe Paterno has come from retired and current coaches, former Penn State players and even a former president of the United States. But one statement may get a little more scrutiny than the others. Jerry Sandusky, the former assistant coach under Paterno who is accused of sexually abusing young boys — accusations that roiled the Penn State community and eventually led to Paterno’s firing last year — released a comment through his lawyer on Paterno’s death:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sandusky Issues Statement About Paterno', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterno, Joe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T19:51:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/892ca7de-cb46-5fba-a439-dd84ebb00093', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/892ca7de-cb46-5fba-a439-dd84ebb00093'}, {'abstract': 'As the world economy is reshaped by the technology revolution and globalization, two new gilded ages are emerging: one in the West and one in developing nations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/business/global/wrenching-the-globe-into-a-new-economic-orbit.html', 'snippet': 'As the world economy is reshaped by the technology revolution and globalization, two new gilded ages are emerging: one in the West and one in developing nations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — On a bitter evening in mid-January, a group of bankers and book publishers gathered on the 42nd floor of Goldman Sachs’s global headquarters here. The setting could not have been more New York — skyscrapers twinkled out the windows to the north and a jazz ensemble played softly in the corner. But the appetizers, reflecting the theme of the event, were an international mishmash: thumb-sized potato pancakes with sour cream and caviar, steaming Chinese dumplings, Indian samosas and Turkish kebabs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/world/23gilded2/23gilded2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/23/world/23gilded2/23gilded2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/world/23gilded2/23gilded2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/world/23gilded2/23gilded2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/23/world/23gilded2/23gilded2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Some See Two New Gilded Ages, Raising Global Tensions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Some See 2 New Gilded Ages, Raising Global Tensions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T19:56:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By CHRYSTIA FREELAND', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chrystia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'FREELAND', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a18ff0aa-3fc4-57dc-886e-59f6048d024a', 'word_count': 1883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a18ff0aa-3fc4-57dc-886e-59f6048d024a'}, {'abstract': 'In Bill T. Jones’s newest work, “Story/Time,” he narrates one-minute stories while dancers whirl around him in restless eddies of nonnarrative movement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/arts/dance/story-time-by-bill-t-jones-at-montclair-state-review.html', 'snippet': 'In Bill T. Jones’s newest work, “Story/Time,” he narrates one-minute stories while dancers whirl around him in restless eddies of nonnarrative movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTCLAIR, N.J. — Bill T. Jones has long talked about his simultaneous attraction toward narration and abstraction, and about how his desire to lay claim to both of these artistic traditions has often left him in conflict. How to tell a good yarn but not be yoked to it structurally?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '