bject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Nevada, Las Vegas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Dave', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Augmon, Stacey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T22:12:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By William C. Rhoden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Rhoden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85514899-0d64-591a-a0b9-eb01ab2e1ef8', 'word_count': 1293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85514899-0d64-591a-a0b9-eb01ab2e1ef8'}, {'abstract': 'The Judah L. Magnes Museum has reopened as the Magnes Collection of Jewish Art and Life, and is now part of the library at the University of California, Berkeley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/arts/design/magnes-judaica-museum-joins-berkeley-library-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Judah L. Magnes Museum has reopened as the Magnes Collection of Jewish Art and Life, and is now part of the library at the University of California, Berkeley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERKELEY, Calif. — The story of how the Judah L. Magnes Museum — whose collection of Judaica is the third largest in the country — became the Magnes Collection of Jewish Art and Life at the Bancroft Library of the University of California, Berkeley, might not seem terribly ripe with complication or implication. In recent years small private museums facing financial strain have often sought refuge by negotiating new lives within universities. Perhaps on Sunday, when the Magnes opened its doors to the public in a building it had long owned near the campus here, it was simply inaugurating another phase of its 50-year life. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/arts/23JUDAICA/23JUDAICA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/23/arts/23JUDAICA/23JUDAICA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/arts/23JUDAICA/23JUDAICA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/arts/23JUDAICA/23JUDAICA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/23/arts/23JUDAICA/23JUDAICA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Jewish Museum Shifts Identity', 'kicker': 'Exhibition Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Jewish Museum Shifts Identity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Magnes, Judah L, Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Berkeley', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T22:16:03+0000', '