, 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-22T22:23:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mohamed Ibrahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohamed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ibrahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7da42090-1710-5001-af04-b0b2e5276ae6', 'word_count': 862, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7da42090-1710-5001-af04-b0b2e5276ae6'}, {'abstract': 'George Pelecanos’s latest book, “What It Was,” takes place in Washington in 1972; Carol O’Connell’s “Chalk Girl” visits New York City’s Special Crimes Unit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/books/what-it-was-and-chalk-girl-crime-novels-review.html', 'snippet': 'George Pelecanos’s latest book, “What It Was,” takes place in Washington in 1972; Carol O’Connell’s “Chalk Girl” visits New York City’s Special Crimes Unit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Pelecanos’s latest book, “What It Was,” sends his best stock character into an extended 40-year flashback. It begins in a Washington bar, where a song by the Dramatics gets Derek Strange to thinking about the summer of 1972. He was 26. Bell-bottoms and Afros were everywhere. “Fly” was an adjective, as in “regal and fly in their natural hairstyles and up-to-the-minute fashions.” The soundtrack from “Superfly” was on every jukebox not playing the soundtrack from “Shaft.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/arts/jp-book/jp-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 771, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbn