h': 'Esquire magazine, a monument to male vitality, seemed about to keel over in 2009. Famous for laying down a much-followed literary track with an article in 1966 by Gay Talese titled “Frank Sinatra Has a Cold,” the magazine found itself gasping for breath and fighting for survival. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/12/business/media/carr-50/carr-50-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/12/business/media/carr-50/carr-50-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Esquire Survived Publishing’s Dark Days', 'kicker': 'The Media Equation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Esquire Survived Publishing’s Dark Days', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Granger, David M (1956- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESQUIRE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hearst Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T00:39:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f476968c-e934-52e2-9392-c88a287e0c8e', 'word_count': 1368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f476968c-e934-52e2-9392-c88a287e0c8e'}, {'abstract': 'At a campaign event, Mitt Romney made pointed reference to Newt Gingrich’s ties to Freddie Mac, the federally run mortgage giant, which was met with “boos” from the crowd.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/22/in-florida-romney-seeks-to-link-gingrich-to-foreclosure-crisis/', 'snippet': 'At a campaign event, Mitt Romney made pointed reference to Newt Gingrich’s ties to Freddie Mac, the federally run mortgage giant, which was met with “boos” from the crowd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORMOND BEACH, Fla., — Less than 24 hours after his disappointing showing in the South Carolina primary, Mitt Romney took his campaign fight to Florida, linking the mortgage foreclosure crisis here – the nation’s worst – to his rival, Newt Gingrich, the victor in the South Carolina contest. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Florida, Romney Seeks to Link Gingrich to Foreclosure Crisis', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T00:46:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Saulny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saulny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/158b6031-a1a9-5dd9-ad06-62b92e2ea929', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/158b6031-a1a9-5dd9-ad06-62b92e2ea929'}, {'abstract': 'Defensive end Dave Tollefson goes through an unusual rite before every Giants game: he calls his mother on the phone for a profanity-laced pep talk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/sports/football/mothers-love-and-her-pregame-profanity-sustain-giants-tollefson.html', 'snippet': 'Defensive end Dave Tollefson goes through an unusual rite before every Giants game: he calls his mother on the phone for a profanity-laced pep talk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — An hour before each opening kickoff, Dave Tollefson retreats to a quiet area of the Giants’ locker room to perform his pregame ritual: a call to his mother. She, in turn, provides support in a manner more mouthy than motherly: a loud, profanity-laced pep talk.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/sports/YTOLLEFSON/YTOLLEFSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/23/sports/YTOLLEFSON/YTOLLEFSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/sports/YTOLLEFSON/YTOLLEFSON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/sports/YTOLLEFSON/YTOLLEFSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/23/sports/YTOLLEFSON/YTOLLEFSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mother’s Love and Her Pregame Profanity Sustain a Giant in the Trenches', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Mother&#8217;s Love and Her Pregame Profanity Sustain a Giant in the Trenches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'org