: 'An Appraisal', '_id': 'nyt://article/4405b258-ffcb-5f94-b26f-924b6616375e', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4405b258-ffcb-5f94-b26f-924b6616375e'}, {'abstract': 'Labor representatives are rightly pushing back against a Republican-oriented agenda of less regulation and lower corporate tax rates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/opinion/dissent-in-the-jobs-council.html', 'snippet': 'Labor representatives are rightly pushing back against a Republican-oriented agenda of less regulation and lower corporate tax rates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Disney World last week, President Obama announced new executive orders to speed up visas for foreign tourists to the United States. The measure, a priority for the travel industry, was one of several sensible recommendations made in the last year by Mr. Obama’s Council on Jobs and Competitiveness, a 27-member panel of corporate executives, academics, investors and labor leaders. The White House has carried out 17 others so far.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dissent in the Jobs Council', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dissent in the Jobs Council', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporate Taxes', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council on Jobs and Competitiveness', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T01:58:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/607217c0-7f90-557a-b66c-429f01192d64', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/607217c0-7f90-557a-b66c-429f01192d64'}, {'abstract': 'Communications changes that the Fed plans to introduce this week include sharing officials’ predictions about the level at which they intend to set short-term rates over the next three years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/business/fed-set-to-introduce-communications-policies-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Communications changes that the Fed plans to introduce this week include sharing officials’ predictions about the level at which they intend to set short-term rates over the next three years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Federal Reserve, which does not like to surprise financial markets, has worked unusually hard to prepare the public for the changes to its communications policies that it plans to introduce on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/world/23fed/23fed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 314, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/23/world/23fed/23fed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 314}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/world/23fed/23fed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 536, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/world/23f