the same spot in broad daylight three days earlier.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Short of a Win, Garrigus Happy to Have Been in Such a Position', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garrigus, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T05:34:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c21e139a-7643-5ef5-a193-c5d668e174f3', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c21e139a-7643-5ef5-a193-c5d668e174f3'}, {'abstract': 'And then there were two: The Patriots and the Giants will face meet in Indianapolis for Super Bowl XLVI. Can the Giants pull off a rematch victory, or will the Patriots prevail?', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/early-look-at-giants-patriots-matchup/', 'snippet': 'And then there were two: The Patriots and the Giants will face meet in Indianapolis for Super Bowl XLVI. Can the Giants pull off a rematch victory, or will the Patriots prevail?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New England Patriots are back in the Super Bowl, despite the best efforts of their opponents and the preferences of millions of fans who are weary of their mix of arrogant excellence and excellent arrogance. The Jets tried to beat them with rhetoric, the Denver Broncos with an Elvis-strength cultural juggernaut, the Baltimore Ravens with everything but a healthy kicker. But nothing could stop Bill Belichick and Tom Brady from returning to the Super Bowl for the fifth time in 11 seasons. Judging by the chip-shot field goal the Ravens missed at the end of the Patriots’ 23-20 A.F.C. championship game victory, New England is again augmenting its considerable skill with some timely doses of good luck, the way it did in its rise to dominance a decade ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Early Look at Giants-Patriots Matchup', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T06:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Tanier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/386f9508-8f43-5917-b9c9-b9689b9c7dcb', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/386f9508-8f43-5917-b9c9-b9689b9c7dcb'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the Giants’ 20-17 victory over the 49ers in San Francisco, which sent the Giants to the Super Bowl against the New England Patriots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/22/sports/SPTSNFC0122.html', 'snippet': 'A look at the Giants’ 20-17 victory over the 49ers in San Francisco, which sent the Giants to the Super Bowl against the New England Patriots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look at the Giants’ 20-17 victory over the 49ers in San Francisco, which sent the Giants to the Super Bowl against the New England Patriots.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/22/sports/S