main': 'Manchester 2, London 0', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T06:10:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38832355-acdc-5439-af82-6db26a940005', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38832355-acdc-5439-af82-6db26a940005'}, {'abstract': '1:29 p.m. | Updated  Europe agrees to impose oil embargo and other sanctions on Iran.  In the campaign to curb Tehran’s nuclear ambitions, it appears one’s enemy’s enemy is one’s friend. Case in point, some eminent Americans met up in Paris with a group the U.S. State Department considers terrorists, days ahead of Monday’s E.U. meeting to consider tougher sanctions.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/strange-bedfellows-in-the-conflict-with-iran/', 'snippet': '1:29 p.m. | Updated  Europe agrees to impose oil embargo and other sanctions on Iran.  In the campaign to curb Tehran’s nuclear ambitions, it appears one’s enemy’s enemy is one’s friend. Case in point, some eminent Americans met up in Paris with a...', 'lead_paragraph': '1:29 p.m. | Updated  Europe agrees to impose oil embargo and other sanctions on Iran', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Strange Bedfellows in the Conflict with Iran', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuliani, Rudolph W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mukasey, Michael B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Mujahedeen of Iran", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Camp Ashraf (Iraq)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T06:30:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a6a5089-e8bd-5907-a07b-8497425dbccb', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a6a5089-e8bd-5907-a07b-8497425dbccb'}, {'abstract': 'Williams, the last American singles player left in Melbourne, lost to unseeded Ekaterina Makarova of Russia, 6-2, 6-3.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/sports/tennis/australian-open-serena-williams-loses-in-fourth-round.html', 'snippet': 'Williams, the last American singles player left in Melbourne, lost to unseeded Ekaterina Makarova of Russia, 6-2, 6-3.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — It is still a surprise when Serena Williams fails to claw her way out of a bad place against an unseeded player, but it was no shock that it happened at the Australian Open this year.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/sports/SUB-tennis2/SUB-tennis2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/23/sports/SUB-tennis2/SUB-tennis2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlarg