an Open on Monday with a five-set upset victory over Jo-Wilfred Tsonga of France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia – Kei Nishikori of Japan barged into the quarterfinals of the Australian Open on Monday with a five-set upset victory over Jo-Wilfried Tsonga of France. Struggling from a set down, Nishikori surged back into the match after an unusual 10-minute suspension while officials and workers punctured and tamped down a section of court that had bubbled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tsonga Falls to Nishikori in 5-Set Drama', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T06:45:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN MARTIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MARTIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d52a0b5-75c0-52c1-9b57-61522f12774e', 'word_count': 914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d52a0b5-75c0-52c1-9b57-61522f12774e'}, {'abstract': 'Buddhist monks will determine the fate of the damaged monasteries.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/rattled-heritage-sikkims-monasteries-after-the-quake/', 'snippet': 'Buddhist monks will determine the fate of the damaged monasteries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a week after the Sept. 18 earthquake, many towns in Sikkim were cut off from the outside world. The roads slowly became passable and as they did, photographs and video clips began to circulate. Rumors traveled too, especially that the major monasteries – Pemayangtse, Dubdi, Tashiding and Ringhim – were barely standing and that some of the smaller monasteries in Khechiperi and Hongdi had been obliterated. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rattled Heritage: Sikkim’s Monasteries after the Quake', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monasteries and Monks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sikkim (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T06:53:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chetan Raj Shrestha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chetan', 'middlename': 'Raj', 'lastname': 'Shrestha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6191a7aa-59d3-55ab-a46d-b712488bcab2', 'word_count': 1174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6191a7aa-59d3-55ab-a46d-b712488bcab2'}, {'abstract': 'The Patriots hadn’t even carried their A.F.C. championship trophy off the podium on Sunday and already Tom Brady was discussing the one person who had nearly kept them from winning it at all. Namely, Tom Brady.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/the-patriots-have-no-shot-against-the-giants-just-ask-them/', 'snippet': 'The Patriots hadn’t even carried their A.F.C. championship trophy off the podium on Sunday and already Tom Brady was discussing the one person who had nearly kept them from winning it at all. Namely, Tom Brady.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Patriots hadn’t even carried their A.F.C. championship trophy off the podium on Sunday and already Tom Brady was discussing the one person who had nearly kept them from winning it at all. Namely, Tom Brady.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Patriots Have No Shot Against the Giants. Just Ask Them.', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belichick, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T07:25:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/402c6371-9931-58c8-a8e4-3c44304b91ef', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/402c6371-9931-58c8-a8e4-3c44304b91ef'}, {'abstract': 'Martina Navratilova criticized the play of Caroline Wozniacki and the ranking system that places her No. 1. Wozniacki is the only player ranked ahead of Petra Kvitova.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/navratilova-backs-kvitova-criticizes-ranking-system/', 'snippet': 'Martina Navratilova criticized the play of Caroline Wozniacki and the ranking system that places her No. 1. Wozniacki is the only player ranked ahead of Petra Kvitova.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — It shouldn’t be surprising to hear one Czech lefty standing by another, but the conviction with which Martina Navratilova defended No. 2-ranked Petra Kvitova was something to be noticed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Navratilova Backs Kvitova; Criticizes Ranking System', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T07:48:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name'