h.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Belichick may beat the Giants in the Super Bowl in two weeks. He will almost certainly wind up in the Pro Football Hall of Fame. And, Spygate or no Spygate, he may one day be considered the game’s greatest coach. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooking With Bill Belichick', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belichick, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T12:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7d9879c-d2dd-51f6-980b-81363f90e545', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7d9879c-d2dd-51f6-980b-81363f90e545'}, {'abstract': 'For anyone who needs visual inducement to see “Richard III” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, there is Haydn Gwynne’s hair.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/a-retro-futuristic-coif/', 'snippet': 'For anyone who needs visual inducement to see “Richard III” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, there is Haydn Gwynne’s hair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For anyone who needs visual inducement to see “Richard III” at the Brooklyn Academy of Music, there is Haydn Gwynne’s hair. Coiled to perfection in a manner reminiscent of Wallis Simpson, it lends authority to Queen Elizabeth, Ms. Gwynne’s steely character, and provides the production with a moment of chic. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Retro-Futuristic Coif', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T12:00:23+0000', 'docum