opped.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/why-bradshaws-fumble-wasnt-a-fumble/', 'snippet': 'The Giants had a dangerous moment when Ahmad Bradshaw was separated from the ball late in the fourth quarter. But the officials ruled that his forward progress had been stopped.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.F.C. title game had become a stalemate. It seemed that a turnover might be decisive. The Niners’ Kyle Williams had two. And the Giants had none — with one very close call.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Bradshaw’s Fumble Wasn’t a Fumble', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T13:08:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e35aca47-5b44-5b80-98d9-d87ed40e6606', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e35aca47-5b44-5b80-98d9-d87ed40e6606'}, {'abstract': "A middle school teacher writes about one of her students: 'The true danger of bullying is the way that it changes kids.  After weeks of feeling defensive and guarded, Rocky began to hide her sweet softness. Enough of this transformation in children, and the environment of a school is changed.'", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/23/bullying-changes-a-school-one-child-at-a-time/', 'snippet': "A middle school teacher writes about one of her studen