.com/2012/01/23/image-of-the-day-january-23/', 'snippet': 'India’s Agni 4 missile featured in the Republic Day dress rehearsal in New Delhi.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: January 23', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T13:21:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/187818be-eed2-55b6-9eb4-a228602c0265', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/187818be-eed2-55b6-9eb4-a228602c0265'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/morning-take-out-406/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bad Year for Wall St. Not Reflected in Chiefs’ Pay \xa0|\xa0 Wall Street stocks and profits took a beating in 2011. But there is one corner of the Street that took a lighter hit: the compensation paid to chief executives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T13:23:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32cf62c6-5cc7-5838-a0ac-97c42a9677e7', 'word_count': 2254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32cf62c6-5cc7-5838-a0ac-97c42a9677e7'}, {'abstract': 'Also, how N.F.L. Films took over the rest of the week and a Murdoch critic turns cub reporter.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/the-breakfast-meeting-ruperts-man-for-now-and-looking-up-at-esquire/', 'snippet': 'Also, how N.F.L. Films took over the rest of the week and a Murdoch critic turns cub reporter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chase Carey, the president and chief operating officer of News Corporation, was long seen as a placeholder until one of the Murdoch children could take full control of the company. But the hacking scandal in London has complicated succession plans, and Mr. Carey, the blunt long-time aide, has filled the vacuum, writes Amy Chozick: “Never in the $60 billion media company’s history has an executive other than Mr. Murdoch taken such a major role in running the daily operations.” He has, she writes, become particularly critical in getting Rupert Murdoch to focus on the stock price and in soothing Wall Street.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Rupert’s Man for Now and Looking Up at Esquire', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carey, Chase', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Tom', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESQUIRE', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News of the World', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NFL Films', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T13:36:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cfb5917-1d64-50da-94ec-7cc7ae8d314b', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cfb5917-1d64-50da-94ec-7cc7ae8d314b'}, {'abstract': 'Morgan Stanley is looking to offload Quilter to focus its wealth management business on high-net-worth customers, those who typically have more than $1 million to invest.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/morgan-stanley-to-sell-british-wealth-management-unit/', 'snippet': 'Morgan Stanley is looking to offload Quilter to focus its wealth management business on high-net-worth customers, those who typically have more than $1 million to invest.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:46 a.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morgan Stanley Said to Be Near Sale of British Wealth Manager', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T13:45:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91929205-e11c-5643-8d40-0e93948f8e70', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91929205-e11c-5643-8d40-0e93948f8e70'}, {'abstract': 'The Giants quarterback is an N.F.L.’s iron man, with the longest active streak of consecutive starts among quarterbacks. He needed all his toughness against the Niners’ defense.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/eli-mannings-durability-on-display/', 'snippet': 'The Giants quarterback is an N.F.L.’s iron man, with the longest active streak of consecutive starts among quarterbacks. He needed all his toughness against the Niners’ defense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You might remember that Brett Favre was the leader in N.F.L. consecutive starts. And then that Peyton Manning took over that title among quarterbacks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eli Manning’s Durability on Display', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Favre, Brett', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T13:46:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20417564-983f-5ab5-ad13-e7f13a87f64c', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20417564-983f-5ab5-ad13-e7f13a87f64c'}, {'abstract': 'Fearing the bond vigilantes — but not the Republicans — in December 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/larry-and-the-invisibles/', 'snippet': 'Fearing the bond vigilantes — but not the Republicans — in December 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ryan Lizza’s new piece on policymaking in the Obama administration is out. One of the documents the piece rests on is a December 2008 policy memo from Larry Summers to Obama on the size and composition of stimulus; Ryan shared it with me to get my take, and some of what I said is reflected in his article.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Larry and the Invisibles', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T13:57:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c19b4818-0892-5453-9ff1-ca3ae7a1f021', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c19b4818-0892-5453-9ff1-ca3ae7a1f021'}, {'abstract': 'Joseph Cedar, the director of Israel’s foreign-language Oscar hope, “Footnote,” is a four-time veteran of the Academy Award process. But for him the most interesting part may take place after the Oscars, when starving actresses finally sit down to eat.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/for-an-israeli-director-the-oscar-ceremony-gets-interesting-after-its-over/', 'snippet': 'Joseph Cedar, the director of Israel’s foreign-language Oscar hope, “Footnote,” is a four-time veteran of the Academy Award process. But for him the most interesting part may take place after the Oscars, when starving actresses finally sit down to...', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the age of 43, the American-born Israeli director Joseph Cedar is already a veteran of the Oscar process. Israel has submitted all four of the feature films he has made as official selections. His previous project, “Beaufort,” about Israeli soldiers in the waning days of the war in Lebanon, was a nominee for the Oscar for best foreign-language film in 2008, and his latest film, “Footnote,” was named this week to the shortlist of nine films contending for this year’s Oscar. On Tuesday, he’ll find out if he’s one of the five nominees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For an Israeli Director, the Oscar Ceremony Gets Interesting After It’s Over', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cedar, Joseph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaufman, Andy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sellers, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T14:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/427aa04d-794e-5646-9c17-10677b1629aa', 'word_count': 1323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/427aa04d-794e-5646-9c17-10677b1629aa'}, {'abstract': 'The Lanvin runway show took the lion’s share of this season’s trends and solidified them in a singular stroke.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/paris-top-5-lanvin-2/', 'snippet': 'The Lanvin runway show took the lion’s share of this season’s trends and solidified them in a singular stroke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lanvin runway show took the lion’s share of this season’s trends and solidified them in a singular stroke. The designers Alber Elbaz and Lucas Ossendrijver combined the many amazing but disparate sides of the season –– belted coats, drop shoulders, soft tailoring, proportion, fabric mash-ups, leather and motocross –– and wrapped them all into a collection that was clear, understandable and one of the house’s most wearable yet. Here, a nylon bomber jacket “applied” to a coat over a black-tie outfit deftly interprets the unselfconscious, random art of layering during a big city winter. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Top 5 | Lanvin', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lanvin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T14:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b020218-6e93-5bed-aaa7-45bfac265244', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b020218-6e93-5bed-aaa7-45bfac265244'}, {'abstract': 'Austerity caused the slump rather than ending it.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/more-than-you-want-to-know-about-warren-harding/', 'snippet': 'Austerity caused the slump rather than ending it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday I mentioned that they’re still flogging the old line that Warren Harding proved that austerity works. I linked to my old demonstration that the 1921 economy was nowhere near the liquidity trap, and that there was substantial monetary easing, making comparisons to the current situation nonsense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Than You Want To Know About Warren Harding', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T14:07:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9e36f89-1cd8-5c34-9f7c-d6185843c816', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9e36f89-1cd8-5c34-9f7c-d6185843c816'}, {'abstract': 'Jack Gantos’s “Dead End in Norvelt” was deemed 2011’s most outstanding contribution to children’s literature.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/caldecott-and-newberry-prizes-to-be-awarded/', 'snippet': 'Jack Gantos’s “Dead End in Norvelt” was deemed 2011’s most outstanding contribution to children’s literature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sly, gothic and quasi-autobiographical tale of a boy who is grounded by his parents and sent to type obituaries for a neighbor, leading to a string of comic adventures, won the John Newbery Medal on Monday for the year’s most outstanding contribution to children’s literature.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tale of Comic Adventures Wins Newbery Medal', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caldecott Medal', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newbery Medal', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gantos, Jack', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raschka, Chris', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN LIBRARY ASSN', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T14:08:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6eaba88-8b10-57c7-ab88-7549e0a68ff5', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6eaba88-8b10-57c7-ab88-7549e0a68ff5'}, {'abstract': 'The success of the Islamists in Egypt’s parliamentary elections prompts reassuring words and dire predictions.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/egypts-islamist-parliament/', 'snippet': 'The success of the Islamists in Egypt’s parliamentary elections prompts reassuring words and dire predictions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Egypt’s Parliament holds its first session Monday following confirmation Saturday that Islamists had won nearly 70 percent of the seats, opinion writers are assessing what it could mean for the country and the region.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Islamist Parliament', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dejevsky, Mary', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL HAYAT', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jerusalem Post', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T14:09:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Politi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Politi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edbb292a-5345-5c21-b9f4-9e2e7fc6700f', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edbb292a-5345-5c21-b9f4-9e2e7fc6700f'}, {'abstract': 'The Giants and Patriots will be Super Bowl combatants thanks to luck, grit and heartbreaking mistakes by the 49ers and Ravens.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/leading-off-and-then-there-were-two/', 'snippet': 'The Giants and Patriots will be Super Bowl combatants thanks to luck, grit and heartbreaking mistakes by the 49ers and Ravens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the end, the Super Bowl combatants were not decided by magnificent touchdowns or beautiful interceptions. They were chosen by fate seemingly for their grit and stubbornness, two teams that don’t question themselves when doubt starts raining down on them. They just dig in and refuse to go away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: And Then There Were Two', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank