executive says he is not entertaining the idea of splitting the company into two separate businesses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New RIM Chief Not Looking to Split Company', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T14:30:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b9253a0-b2a1-5b9f-93bf-d68a0c469102', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b9253a0-b2a1-5b9f-93bf-d68a0c469102'}, {'abstract': 'There may be cross-border skirmishing over whether New York or New Jersey gets to organize the celebration if the Giants win the Super Bowl.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/after-giants-vs-patriots-it-could-be-christie-vs-bloomberg/', 'snippet': 'There may be cross-border skirmishing over whether New York or New Jersey gets to organize the celebration if the Giants win the Super Bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stunningly, some would go so far as to say miraculously, the New York Giants of New Jersey are going to the Super Bowl. You know what this means, don’t you? For the next two weeks there may be cross-border skirmishing over whether the west bank or the east bank of the Hudson River gets to organize the celebration if the team wins the big game, scheduled for Feb. 5 in Indianapolis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Giants vs. Patriots, It Could Be Christie vs. Bloomberg', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'ran