': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac9f1bb8-6cb5-5b27-9a72-f6e1c4a257c3', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac9f1bb8-6cb5-5b27-9a72-f6e1c4a257c3'}, {'abstract': 'A website hosting a searchable database of doctors who perform abortions seems intended to frighten the brave individuals who help women in difficult circumstances.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/abortiondocs-org/', 'snippet': 'A website hosting a searchable database of doctors who perform abortions seems intended to frighten the brave individuals who help women in difficult circumstances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You know those Western-style “Wanted” posters that anti-abortion activists liked to distribute? The ones with the names and addresses of doctors who perform the constitutionally protected procedure? That tactic has migrated to the Web.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'AbortionDocs.Org', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maddow, Rachel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Operation Rescue', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T14:47:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86583cae-abd4-5a44-b3e7-bd0e6a2e1136', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86583