urope/bodies-of-women-located-on-italian-ship-costa-concordia.html', 'snippet': 'Rescue workers located the bodies of two women on the wrecked cruise ship Costa Concordia, bringing the death toll to 15, Italian officials said Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GIGLIO, Italy — Rescue divers discovered the bodies of two women in the submerged Internet cafe lounge of the Costa Concordia shipwreck on Monday, raising the official death toll to 15, as salvage crews were authorized to start extracting the vessel’s half million gallons of fuel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fuel to Be Removed From Stricken Cruise Ship', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 More Bodies Found on Italian Ship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Costa Crociere SpA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruises', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tuscany (Italy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T15:56:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41274134-5cf6-5324-a4d6-3de954276b65', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41274134-5cf6-5324-a4d6-3de954276b65'}, {'abstract': 'For all of the different kinds of financing a small company can obtain from the S.B.A., the agency has not had a way to nurture fast-growing start-ups since 2004.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/s-b-a-readying-program-to-invest-in-start-ups/', 'snippet': 'For all of the different kinds of financing a small company can obtain from the S.B.A., the agency has not had a way to nurture fast-growing start-ups since 2004.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With its legislative agenda for job creation stuck for the foreseeable future, the Obama administration has turned inward, looking to the federal bureaucracy for new ways to jump-start the economy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.B.A. Readying Program to Invest in Start-Ups', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Venture Capital Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T16:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faeabe0e-1b66-5892-8a41-5243c5ef0b8b', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faeabe0e-1b66-5892-8a41-5243c5ef0b8b'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists in Antarctica encounter curious penguins and eerie relics on a visit to sites where the polar explorers of a century ago ate, slept, worked — and drank whiskey.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/a-glimpse-of-polar-history/', 'snippet': 'Scientists in Antarctica encounter curious penguins and eerie relics on a visit to sites where the polar explorers of a century ago ate, slept, worked — and drank whiskey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alia Khan, a graduate student at the University of Colorado, Boulder, writes from the McMurdo Dry Valleys in Antarctica, where she is studying ephemeral glacier-fed streams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Glimpse of Polar History', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mummies and Mummification', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Penguins', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Robert Falcon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T16:02:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alia Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51938921-0f96-592c-bb0f-726d5f409abd', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51938921-0f96-592c-bb0f-726d5f409abd'}, {'abstract': 'Islamists hold a majority in the first Parliament elected after the ouster of Mubarak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/23/world/middleeast/20120124Egypt_337_ss.html', 'snippet': 'Islamists hold a majority in the first Parliament elected after the ouster of Mubarak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Islamists hold a majority in the first Parliament elected after the ouster of Mubarak.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': '