n Monday, according to people close to the lawmaker, although the T.S.A. quickly disputed their account.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rand Paul Is Stopped by T.S.A. in Nashville', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nashville (Tenn)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T16:05:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baa7662b-46ea-55a9-908f-c7b72ee0483e', 'word_count': 670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baa7662b-46ea-55a9-908f-c7b72ee0483e'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Rice, the “Jesus Christ Superstar” lyricist and one-time collaborator of Mr. Lloyd Webber, said that a reality series to cast a new production of the musical was “tasteless” and “tacky.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/tim-rice-has-no-hosannas-for-andrew-lloyd-webbers-superstar-reality-show/', 'snippet': 'Tim Rice, the “Jesus Christ Superstar” lyricist and one-time collaborator of Mr. Lloyd Webber, said that a reality series to cast a new production of the musical was “tasteless” and “tacky.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Look at all the trials and tribulations of Andrew Lloyd Webber and Tim Rice. The one-time partners behind some of musical theater’s most successful (and lucrative) works are feuding again, this time over a British reality series that would cast the lead for a new production of “Jesus Christ Superstar.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tim Rice Has No Hosannas for Andrew Lloyd Webber’s ‘Superstar’ Reality Show', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reality Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lloyd Webber, Andrew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T16:07:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ce7989b-2073-5bd0-ad5b-3282fa5d0103', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ce7989b-2073-5bd0-ad5b-3282fa5d0103'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney raised the possibility that Newt Gingrich might have broken laws in representing corporate interests.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/romney-warns-of-october-surprises-if-gingrich-is-nominee/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney raised the possibility that Newt Gingrich might have broken laws in representing corporate interests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA — Mitt Romney raised the possibility that Newt Gingrich might have broken laws in representing corporate interests and warned of politically damaging “October surprises” if Mr. Gingrich became the Republican presidential nominee. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Warns of ‘October Surprises’ if Gingrich Is Nominee', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T16:07:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c89133ee-e53f-5590-aebc-86b9007a1b67', 'word_count': 1047, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c89133ee-e53f-5590-aebc-86b9007a1b67'}, {'abstract': 'A hundred coins. Five smart, greedy and mean pirates. How should they split the bounty?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/numberplay-5-pirate-puzzl/', 'snippet': 'A hundred coins. Five smart, greedy and mean pirates. How should they split the bounty?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five smart, greedy and mean pirates find themselves on a boat with 100 gold coins. The pirates are ranked according to seniority, from 1 to 5, the most senior being ranked 1. Here is the deal: the most senior pirate must make a proposal for splitting the coins among the pirates, including herself (no fractional coins!). If her proposal has at least 50 percent acceptance (she votes, too), she is fine; otherwise, the other four pirates throw her into the shark-infested sea. The remaining pirates play the same game, starting with a proposal from the next most senior pirate, that is, the pirate ranked 2.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: The Five-Pirate Puzzle', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Princeton University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scientific American', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Warwick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T16:11:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c31ab29-e251-556b-b9e2-83b4d321a805', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c31ab29-e251-556b-b9e2-83b4d321a805'}, {'abstract': 'Police officers opened fire on Tibetan protesters in western China on Monday in the largest violent confrontation in ethnic Tibetan areas of China since 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/world/asia/deadly-new-violence-reported-in-restive-tibetan-area-of-western-china.html', 'snippet': 'Police officers opened fire on Tibetan protesters in western China on Monday in the largest violent confrontation in ethnic Tibetan areas of China since 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Security forces opened fire on Tibetan protesters in western China on Monday, wounding at least 32 people and killing at least one of them in the largest violent confrontation in ethnic Tibetan areas of China since 2008, two Tibetan rights groups and the Tibetan exile government said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tibetans Fired Upon in Protest in China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tibetans Fired Upon In Protest In China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sichuan Province (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lunar New Year', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T16:21:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d68ece5-a685-5aef-9791-63416ae233a9', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d68ece5-a685-5aef-9791-63416ae233a9'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Tachman’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/photos-of-the-moment-lanvin-6/', 'snippet': 'Kevin Tachman’s Paris fashion week photo diary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of the Moment | Lanvin', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lanvin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T16:34:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Tachman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tachman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/290d7c1e-d5f0-5dc9-a8ac-08244bf5e680', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/290d7c1e-d5f0-5dc9-a8ac-08244bf5e680'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Kristol has been right all along.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/calling-mitch-daniels/', 'snippet': 'Bill Kristol has been right all along.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For months now, even as the rest of the conservative commentariat has gradually resigned itself to the existing presidential field, the Weekly Standard’s Bill Kristol has continued to pine — publicly, unstintingly, immune to either embarrassment or fatigue—\xa0for another candidate to jump into the race. He’s dreamed of Mitch Daniels, touted Chris Christie, talked up Paul Ryan and Marco Rubio, name-dropped Jeb Bush, and circled back to Daniels\xa0once more. He’s quoted poetry on behalf of his cause — Yeats, and (with some revisions) Andrew Marvell. He’s endured snark from the Huffington Post, eye-rolling from Slate, mockery from New York Magazine. But he’s continued undeterred — and in the wake of Newt Gingrich’s South Carolina victory, he was\xa0back at it again, throwing out a link to “a new online petition was launched Saturday night … at\xa0runmitchrun.com.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calling Mitch Daniels', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T16:34:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b062a959-a56d-5750-9b9f-5ff47a4d3572', 'word_count': 610, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b062a959-a56d-5750-9b9f-5ff47a4d3572'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich is exactly the sort of millionaire “small business” owner that Republicans are really trying to protect when they sloganeer about “job creators.”', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/taking-up-taxes-on-the-campaign-trail/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich is exactly the sort of millionaire “small business” owner that Republicans are really trying to protect when they sloganeer about “job creators.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican politicians talk a great deal about saving small businesses, and routinely play the mom-and-pop card when arguing against raising taxes, or charging a decent minimum wage, or providing everyone with access to health insurance. Last year, when the Senate was debating how to pay for a renewal of the payroll tax cut, Democrats proposed a surcharge on incomes over $1 million a year. Republicans screamed that this would hurt small businesses, and hence the economy, because small businesses are “job creators.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking Up Taxes on the Campaign Trail', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T16:36:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98d02a34-6e6b-5dd6-ad20-aac2631706ec', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98d02a34-6e6b-5dd6-ad20-aac2631706ec'}, {'abstract': 'The Duke Lemur Center lost a cherished animal over the weekend, but efforts to conserve and study lemurs are thriving.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/romeo-is-dead-but-lemur-conservation-endures/', 'snippet': 'The Duke Lemur Center lost a cherished animal over the weekend, but efforts to conserve and study lemurs are thriving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Duke Lemur Center’s “beloved Romeo” died this weekend at 19. He was the Western Hemisphere’s only successfully housed captive diademed sifaka, one of Madagascar’s increasingly rare lemur species. Still, his tale is one of hope, with efforts expanding to assure the survival of endangered lemur species. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Romeo’ Is Dead, but Lemur Conservation Endures', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T16:44:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nuwer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nuwer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cbf7a3b-659d-5452-931d-f0fafbce9353', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cbf7a3b-659d-5452-931d-f0fafbce9353'}, {'abstract': 'The rap group 2 Live Crew is planning to reunite and tour again.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/2-live-crew-to-live-again/', 'snippet': 'The rap group 2 Live Crew is planning to reunite and tour again.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The rap group 2 Live Crew, which set off a fierce debate over freedom of speech with its graphic sexual lyrics in the 1980s and early 1990s, plans to reunite and begin touring, The Associated Press reported. The group’s former leader, Luther Campbell, said at the Sundance Film Festival in Utah that the rappers, whose hits like “Me So Horny” drew fire, would get back together. “I just can’t wait to start practicing,” he said. Mr. Campbell, who is 51 and is also known as Luke, visited the festival to promote his appearance in a short film, “The Life and Freaky Times of Uncle Luke.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 Live Crew to Live Again', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T16:48:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb492ff1-f395-5e3f-af91-0f15304a6e66', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb492ff1-f395-5e3f-af91-0f15304a6e66'}, {'abstract': 'In a 5-4 decision, the Supreme Court on Monday unanimously ruled that the police violated the Constitution when they placed a Global Positioning System tracking device 