timedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reading List: Some Recent Books on Disgust', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reading List: Some Recent Books on Disgust', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T17:05:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2caccc8-a76d-5b9f-b9c6-bdcc8049f66e', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2caccc8-a76d-5b9f-b9c6-bdcc8049f66e'}, {'abstract': 'In my mind, there is an image of an Olympic-level runner. He is a human thoroughbred, powerful and graceful, like Michael Johnson, the world-record holder in the 400 meters. Oscar is certainly powerful, and graceful in his own way, but I could not look at him and say: this is the highest order of the human form.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/behind-the-cover-story-michael-sokolove-on-oscar-pistorius/', 'snippet': 'In my mind, there is an image of an Olympic-level runner. He is a human thoroughbred, powerful and graceful, like Michael Johnson, the world-record holder in the 400 meters. Oscar is certainly powerful, and graceful in his own way, but I could not...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Sokolove, a contributing writer for the magazine, wrote this week’s cover story on the double-amputee Olympic hopeful Oscar Pistorius. Sokolove is the author of three books: “Warrior Girls,” about the epidemic of injuries among young female athletes; “The Ticket Out: Darryl Strawberry”; and “Hustle: The Myth, Life, and Lies of Pete Rose.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Michael Sokolove on Oscar Pistorius', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker'