m. | Updated I had written on Saturday night, before the results of the South Carolina primary were known, that Mitt Romney could not necessarily bank on holding down a lead in Florida despite recently having had a double-digit advantage in the polls there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Florida Polls Show Big Swing to Gingrich', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T17:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fda76b1d-385c-5198-b142-cb813b1ea81e', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fda76b1d-385c-5198-b142-cb813b1ea81e'}, {'abstract': 'The victim was found by his father in the family’s home in South Ozone Park.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/queens-man-50-dies-in-explosion/', 'snippet': 'The victim was found by his father in the family’s home in South Ozone Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 6:09 p.m. | A 50-year-old man who may have been experimenting with fireworks died in an explosion at his home in South Ozone Park, Queens, on Monday morning, the police said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Queens Man, 50, Dies in Explosion', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fireworks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-