Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e5a7d57-e585-5830-b606-947fd57d5ea4', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e5a7d57-e585-5830-b606-947fd57d5ea4'}, {'abstract': 'After a pretrial investigative hearing, an investigator recommended dropping involuntary manslaughter charges against Specialist Ryan Offutt, who was implicated in the death of Pvt. Danny Chen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/nyregion/soldier-may-not-face-involuntary-manslaughter-charge-in-danny-chens-death.html', 'snippet': 'After a pretrial investigative hearing, an investigator recommended dropping involuntary manslaughter charges against Specialist Ryan Offutt, who was implicated in the death of Pvt. Danny Chen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A military investigator has recommended that the most serious charge be dropped against an American infantryman implicated in the death of Pvt. Danny Chen, a Chinese-American soldier from New York City who, relatives said, was brutally hazed by members of his Army unit in Afghanistan and then apparently killed himself. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Most Serious Charge in a Private’s Death May Be Dropped', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Investigator Recommends Dropping Involuntary Manslaughter Charge in a Private’s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, Danny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T17:53:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c41d6038-936a-5989-993c-4a896d8f2ade', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c41d6038-936a-5989-993c-4a896d8f2ade'}, {'abstract': 'Thomas Langmann, the producer of “The Artist,” talks about the influence of his filmmaker father, Claude Berri, and the hands-off approach of someone not known for backing off, Harvey Weinstein.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/thomas-langmann-the-man-who-took-a-chance-on-the-artist/', 'snippet': 'Thomas Langmann, the producer of “The Artist,” talks about the influence of his filmmaker father, Claude Berri, and the hands-off approach of someone not known for backing off, Harvey Weinstein.', 'lead_paragraph': ' American audiences were introduced to Thomas Langmann, a producer of “The Artist,” at the Golden Globes, when he gave one of the evening’s best speeches, about his father, the filmmaker Claude Berri, winning an Oscar in 1966 and not having enough money to come to the United States to accept it. The winning streak “The Artist” is now on – it picked up the top Producers Guild prize over the weekend – may give Mr. Langmann a chance to rectify that; the Bagger and everyone else will start to find out the fate of “The Artist” when Oscar nominations are announced on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thomas Langmann, the Man Who Took a Chance on ‘The Artist’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berri, Claude', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dujardin, Jean', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hazanavicius, Michel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pacino, Al', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soderbergh, Steven', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Truffaut, Francois', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weinstein, Harvey', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T17:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7076dcb3-c141-586e-b483-a5d4a6e7fca5', 'word_count': 1152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7076dcb3-c141-586e-b483-a5d4a6e7fca5'}, {'abstract': 'The hits on a theme that may resonate in Florida, which was hit hard by mortgage defaults and home foreclosures.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/new-romney-ad-hits-gingrich-on-freddie-mac/', 'snippet': 'The hits on a theme that may resonate in Florida, which was hit hard by mortgage defaults and home foreclosures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney is taking his attacks on Newt Gingrich up a notch in a new television ad that tries to link him to the implosion of the housing market. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Romney Ad Hits Gingrich on Freddie Mac', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T17:58:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5b035f4-6a2b-560e-9f22-f5b81d7b6f5e', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5b035f4-6a2b-560e-9f22-f5b81d7b6f5e'}, {'abstract': 'Rand Paul versus the Transportation Security Administration.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/dont-pat-on-me/', 'snippet': 'Rand Paul versus the Transportation Security Administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether or not you agree with them on the issues, it’s nice to find politicians who actually have principles and actually stick to them. Obviously, I’m not talking here about either Newt Gingrich or Mitt Romney. In fact, I’m not talking about the presidential race at all, although the politician I have in mind is at least related to one of the candidates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Pat On Me', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T18:04:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2a90d0f-9f09-58cb-a006-7433246d08ec', 'word_count': 349, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2a90d0f-9f09-58cb-a006-7433246d08ec'}, {'abstract': 'News for the week that was.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/corporate-rule-is-not-inevitable/', 'snippet': 'News for the week that was.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama formally rejected the Keystone XL pipeline. Fingers crossed there, but that, plus the evident death of the SOPA bill (and little things, like B of A, Verizon and Netflix all being forced to change their behavior after massive Web protests by their customers) give reason to hope. The campaign against Citizens United may well pick up steam as more people begin to feel the power. “Corporate rule,” as this piece details, “is not inevitable.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corporate Rule Is Not Inevitable', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fast Food Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deen, Paula', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Burger King Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citizens United', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "McDonald's Corporation", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Novo Nordisk A/S', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T18:10:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6839f20-12d1-557c-ab3c-b4ce0e8bde59', 'word_count': 510, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6839f20-12d1-557c-ab3c-b4ce0e8bde59'}, {'abstract': 'A truck driver with an affinity for the “Pirates of the Caribbean” film franchise is the subject of a Web series produced by Volvo Trucks.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/in-poland-a-pirate-of-the-highway/', 'snippet': 'A truck driver with an affinity for the “Pirates of the Caribbean” film franchise is the subject of a Web series produced by Volvo Trucks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Moving a trailer of beef along Interstate 80 like John Wayne driving a herd along the Chisholm Trail, many American truck drivers fancy themselves heirs to the cowboy tradition. For at least one of Poland’s knights of the highway, however, the romantic vision of his occupation is more surf than turf.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Poland, a Pirate of the Highway', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trucks and Trucking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AB Volvo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T18:11:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, '