upreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T18:16:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd843102-6c6f-5775-9382-25146ba3f0c1', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd843102-6c6f-5775-9382-25146ba3f0c1'}, {'abstract': 'Perhaps the most astounding thing about Etta James’s voice was how it traveled so freely in so many different musical circles.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/etta-james-one-of-their-own/', 'snippet': 'Perhaps the most astounding thing about Etta James’s voice was how it traveled so freely in so many different musical circles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps the most astounding thing about Etta James’s voice was how it traveled so freely in so many different musical circles, and that was again the most evident aspect of the tributes given to her over the weekend. On Saturday morning, she was featured on a rhythm-and-blues radio program; later that day, on a rock ‘n’ roll show. On Sunday morning, jazz radio was claiming her as one of their own, and she was even plastered all over the touch screen of the treadmill at my gym. And that seemed the most appropriate format, because no matter what James sang — R&B, rock, blues, jazz, pop — her voice was one that got your blood pumping.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Etta James: One of Everyone’s Own', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T18:20:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Hoerburger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoerburger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c368aee5-63db-5501-bde4-f566daa12620', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c368aee5-63db-5501-bde4-f566daa12620'}, {'abstract': 'The opening session of Egypt’s first democratically elected parliament erupted into a shouting match Monday as the Islamists dominating the chamber struggled to keep order.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/world/middleeast/new-egypt-parliament-elects-islamist-from-muslim-brotherhood-as-speaker.html', 'snippet': 'The opening session of Egypt’s first democratically elected parliament erupted into a shouting match Monday as the Islamists dominating the chamber struggled to keep order.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — As Egypt’s first freely elected Parliament in six decades held its opening session on Monday, the Muslim Brotherhood received a lesson in the unwieldiness of democracy when a dispute over choosing a speaker degenerated into a shouting match that overshadowed the day.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/world/EGYPT-1/EGYPT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/world/EGYPT-1/EGYPT-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/world/EGYPT-1/EGYPT-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chaotic Start to Egypt’s First Democratically Elected Parliament', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker