k City teachers and principals are not using the city's $80 million student information database, according to an audit by the city comptroller, John C. Liu,  released on Monday. Many teachers have not even logged into the ARIS system,...", 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "Audit Finds Limited Use of City's Data System", 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T19:20:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANNA M. PHILLIPS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7237b836-b265-54ba-8989-4caf7e29023f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7237b836-b265-54ba-8989-4caf7e29023f'}, {'abstract': 'On Sunday, Sotheby’s in New York sold an embroidered farm scene by a New Jersey schoolgirl from 1807 for $1.07 million (the top estimate had been $120,000), setting an auction record for a needlework sampler.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/schoolgirls-needlework-sampler-sells-for-1-07-million/', 'snippet': 'On Sunday, Sotheby’s in New York sold an embroidered farm scene by a New Jersey schoolgirl from 1807 for $1.07 million (the top estimate had been $120,000), setting an auction record for a needlework sampler.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1807, a New Jersey schoolgirl named Mary Antrim embroidered a farm scene with silk thread on linen. On Sunday, Sotheby’s in New York sold her view of livestock, picket fences and clapboarded outbuildings for $1.07 million (the top estimate had been $120,000), setting an auction record for a needlework sampler. The sale contained 198 lots from the collection of the needlework historian Betty Ring. Of all the colorful pastoral views at the Sotheby’s showroom, Mary Antrim’s piece “stood out in a unique way as a folk art statement,” said the dealer David Schorsch, who bought it for an undisclosed client. The auction’s other top prices were in the low six figures and shared by the specialist dealers Stephen and Carol Huber and Amy Finkel. A quarter of the Ring material did not sell, especially images of veiled mourners and gravestones sewn in memory of deceased relatives. The buzz in the field this week, Mr. Huber said, is that “the memorials all died.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Schoolgirl’s Needlework Sampler Sells for $1.07 Million', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finkel, Amy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T19:22:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve M. Kahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b4282ec-0c36-56c1-a9cb-bfc1c36bbb78', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b4282ec-0c36-56c1-a9cb-bfc1c36bbb78'}, {'abstract': 'Vince Cable, the business secretary, outlined several proposals on Monday to revamp corporate pay practices and make compensation more transparent.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/british-government-looks-to-rein-in-executive-pay/', 'snippet': 'Vince Cable, the business secretary, outlined several proposals on Monday to revamp corporate pay practices and make compensation more transparent.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:43 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Government Looks to Rein In Executive Pay', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cable, Vince', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T19:22:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4437e4b9-1a72-504d-b5e8-7392cd01494a', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4437e4b9-1a72-504d-b5e8-7392cd01494a'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Steven Kirk, who won President Obama’s Senate seat in 2010, was admitted to a Chicago-area hospital over the weekend after suffering a stroke.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/illinois-senator-kirk-hospitalized-following-stroke/', 'snippet': 'Mark Steven Kirk, who won President Obama’s Senate seat in 2010, was admitted to a Chicago-area hospital over the weekend after suffering a stroke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — Senator Mark Steven Kirk of Illinois, who won President Obama’s former seat in 2010, was admitted to a hospital over the weekend after suffering a major stroke. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senator Kirk of Illinois Suffers Stroke', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stroke', 'rank': 1, 'major': '