 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T19:29:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c503bc3d-367f-5ac5-b7de-e9c0670e9e4d', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c503bc3d-367f-5ac5-b7de-e9c0670e9e4d'}, {'abstract': 'British researchers found that a common American practice for in vitro fertilization was associated with more complications than the transfer of just two embryos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/health/research/use-of-3-or-more-in-vitro-embryos-is-too-risky-study-concludes.html', 'snippet': 'British researchers found that a common American practice for in vitro fertilization was associated with more complications than the transfer of just two embryos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 40 percent of in vitro fertilizations in the United States involve the transfer of three or more embryos, and more than 20 percent of pregnancies from IVF procedures result in multiple births. The health risks and expenses of these pregnancies are enormous.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regimens: Use of 3 or More Embryos Is Called Too Risky', 'kicker': 'Vital Signs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Regimens: Use of 3 or More Embryos Is Called Too Risky', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'In Vitro Fertilization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lancet, The (Journal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BIRTHS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T19:30:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df43ff84-95da-5873-a74a-642a3b4b9084', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df43ff84-95da-5873-a74a-642a3b4b9084'}, {'abstract': 'Behind-the-scenes footage shows actors auditioning for “The Artist.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/peek-at-the-auditions-for-the-artist/', 'snippet': 'Behind-the-scenes footage shows actors auditioning for “The Artist.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'First there was the producer Thomas Langmann’s appealing speech when “The Artist” won the Golden Globe. Then the film took the Producers Guild’s top prize. But long before Oscar nominations are announced (tomorrow) and even before awards season began, it had an advantage: as the Bagger’s colleague Michael Cieply explained, “The Artist” had a whopping 68 names on its cast list, and that may interest the actors who make up the Academy’s huge voting bloc. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peek at the Auditions for ‘The Artist’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T19:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 