 victims in “a cultural blind spot.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/health/as-victims-men-struggle-for-rape-awareness.html', 'snippet': 'A federal expansion of a crime definition draws attention to victims in “a cultural blind spot.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Keith Smith was 14 when he was raped by a driver who picked him up after a hockey team meeting. He had hitchhiked home, which is why, for decades, he continued to blame himself for the assault.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24RAPE_SPAN/24RAPE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24RAPE_SPAN/24RAPE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24RAPE_SPAN/24RAPE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24RAPE_SPAN/24RAPE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24RAPE_SPAN/24RAPE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Men Struggle for Rape Awareness', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Men Struggle for Rape Awareness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T20:25:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19eac6f5-9ab2-5f47-9b61-a5abdb1038d6', 'word_count': 1456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19eac6f5-9ab2-5f47-9b61-a5abdb1038d6'}, {'abstract': 'ICE is a customizable JavaScript library that will allow you to track changes in any element that is contenteditable, or in a TinyMCE or Wordpress text editor. At this early stage, ICE has some limitations, but we think it is a very useful tool and hope that others will help us expand the project. Patches and forks are welcome at our repository, https://github.com/NYTimes/ice/. An ICE demo is at http://nytimes.github.com/ice/demo/.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/introducing-ice-writing-for-the-web-first/', 'snippet': 'ICE is a customizable JavaScript library that will allow you to track changes in any element that is contenteditable, or in a TinyMCE or Wordpress text editor. At this early stage, ICE has some limitations, but we think it is a very useful tool an...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since NYTimes.com launched in 1996, the vast majority of our articles have been written for our print newspaper first and then converted (sometimes with great difficulty) for publication on the Web. Yes, we have a growing number of blogs that are Web native. But even when we began developing our in-house Web content management system (CMS), Scoop, five years ago, it was difficult to imagine a time when the old publishing paradigm of “Print First” would be seriously challenged, so entrenched were the habits and traditions of our newsroom. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'hea