o’s first prefall collection (it’s true!), Massimiliano Giornetti retraced the brand’s archives to design a travel-inspired capsule that includes a new set of trunk totes and updates on the favorite pointy-toe kitten heel in rich renditions of crocodile, ostrich and python. The mood of the collection was thoughtfully throwback: mod 1960s-style prints (like this emerald plaid pantsuit), python pleated skirts and a camel shift dress with a cape to match. We hear fall 2012 will sing a similar tune.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Salvatore Ferragamo', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ferragamo, Salvatore, Italia SpA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T20:50:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04c2892a-407b-5b9d-85f1-9ec55ceb50d2', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04c2892a-407b-5b9d-85f1-9ec55ceb50d2'}, {'abstract': 'The travel and tourism industry has gained 224,000 jobs since its low point of 7.3 million total jobs in December 2009, the U.S. Travel Association said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/business/for-travel-and-tourism-hiring-is-on-the-rise-cautiously.html', 'snippet': 'The travel and tourism industry has gained 224,000 jobs since its low point of 7.3 million total jobs in December 2009, the U.S. Travel Association said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the economy has begun to improve from its darkest days in late 2008 and 2009, hiring in the travel and tourism industry has become one of the bright spots.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/business/Tourism/Tourism-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Travel Hiring Is on the Rise', 'kicker': 'Itineraries', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Travel Hiring Is on the Rise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Travel Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T20:51:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harriet Edleson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harriet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edleson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9b3737a-0586-52a3-aa28-245f99926dc2', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9b3737a-0586-52a3-aa28-245f99926dc2'}, {'abstract': 'Under proposed amendments to the Federal Sentencing Guidelines, recommended punishments for insider trading are likely to increase, which will put more pressure on defendants to cooperate with the government in the hope of receiving a reduced sentence.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/greater-penalties-for-insider-trading/', 'snippet': 'Under proposed amendments to the Federal Sentencing Guidelines, recommended punishments for insider trading are likely to increase, which will put more pressure on defendants to cooperate with the government in the hope of receiving a reduced sent...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sentences for insider trading have been on the rise since the Justice Department began its latest crackdown in 2009 that started with the arrest of Raj Rajaratnam. The past year had the highest sentences ever given for this type of crime, including the 11-year prison term for Mr. Rajaratnam. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greater Penalties for Insider Trading', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T20:51:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/330f1d7b-ed13-5457-bcf9-e54985072dd5', 'word_count': 914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/330f1d7b-ed13-5457-bcf9-e54985072dd5'}, {'abstract': 'A large rise in the rate of twin births is seen as a result of the growing use of fertility drugs and more births to older women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/health/research/twin-births-in-the-us-like-never-before.html', 'snippet': 'A large rise in the rate of twin births is seen as a result of the growing use of fertility drugs and more births to older women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More twins are being born in the United States than ever before.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/health/24stat/24stat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1016, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Twin Births in the U.S., Like Never Before', 'kicker': 'Vital Statistics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Twin Births in the U.S., Like Never Before', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fertility Drugs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infertility', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Multiple Births', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Twins', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BIRTHS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T20:56:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0946a6c1-81f0-5ecf-b043-1689f4142181', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0946a6c1-81f0-5ecf-b043-1689f4142181'}, {'abstract': 'Anglo Irish Bank is poised to pay more than a billion euros to unsecured creditors amid mounting criticism from Irish taxpayers who are footing the bill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/business/global/bank-bondholders-to-be-paid-while-irish-public-howls.html', 'snippet': 'Anglo Irish Bank is poised to pay more than a billion euros to unsecured creditors amid mounting criticism from Irish taxpayers who are footing the bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Anglo Irish Bank is poised to pay more than a billion euros on Wednesday to unsecured creditors, drawing criticism from Irish taxpayers who are paying the enormous bill for the country’s bank bailout.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bank Bondholders to Be Paid While Irish Public Howls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bailed-Out Irish Bank’s Plan to Pay Bondholders Angers Taxpayers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anglo Irish Bank', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T20:58:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doreen Carvajal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doreen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carvajal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec3c7d42-b45d-5760-b810-9753cd0507bc', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec3c7d42-b45d-5760-b810-9753cd0507bc'}, {'abstract': 'European politicians have begun to insist that spending cuts can no longer be the sole answer to putting even the most heavily indebted economies on the path to a brighter future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/business/global/europe-sticks-to-austerity-but-finds-its-not-enough.html', 'snippet': 'European politicians have begun to insist that spending cuts can no longer be the sole answer to putting even the most heavily indebted economies on the path to a brighter future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — With much of Europe embarked on a program of budget-cutting and belt-tightening, doubts about whether more austerity is the answer to today’s economic troubles are popping up in the strangest places.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/business/Austerity/Austerity-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Europe, Arguing to Apply Some Stimulus Along With the Austerity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Europe, Arguing to Apply Some Stimulus Along With the Austerity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monti, Mario', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T21:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45c5e500-f443-5969-83c3-21d02e46a190', 'word_count': 1327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45c5e500-f443-5969-83c3-21d02e46a190'}, {'abstract': 'InterDigital announced on Monday that it has called off a sales process for its patent portfolio. It had failed to fetch offers for the entire collection, people briefed on the matter told DealBook.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/interdigital-said-to-call-off-patent-sale/', 'snippet': 'InterDigital announced on Monday that it has called off a sales process for its patent portfolio. It had failed to fetch offers for the entire collection, people briefed on the matter told DealBook.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:43 p.m. | Updated InterDigital confirmed on Monday that it has called off its patent sale. Terry Clontz, the company’s chairman, said in a statement: “The process over the past six months, although not resulting in an offer for the whole of the company, has helped to reaffirm our belief in the breadth and depth of the patent portfolio, the strength of the R&D team, and our technology vision for the future.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'InterDigital Calls Off Patent Sale', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'InterDigital Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T21:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26f0a804-fe11-53fd-93ee-7934d115b61a', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26f0a804-fe11-53fd-93ee-7934d115b61a'}, {'abstract': 'On Monday, the U.N. human rights chief criticized the Obama administration for failing to close the Guantanamo Bay detention center.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/the-high-cost-of-violating-human-rights/', 'snippet': 'On Monday, the U.N. human rights chief criticized the Obama administration for failing to close the Guantanamo Bay detention center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It used to be that the United Nations human rights commission denounced violations in some of the nastiest parts of the world – sub-Saharan Africa, South Africa, junta-dominated Latin American countries, Communist-occupied Europe. These days, that office denounces the United States. That’s what happens when you operate a prison on the margins of the law and justice, where people are held without trial, on tainted evidence, without consideration for their rights under international treaties or the laws of the nation that built the prison.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The High Cost of Violating Human Rights', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pillay, Navi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T21:07:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'titl