1/24/world/middleeast/israeli-police-arrest-2-protesting-palestinian-legislators.html', 'snippet': 'The arrests, along with remarks by a Muslim cleric, are seen as a blow to prospects for negotiations on restarting peace talks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Israel arrested two Palestinian legislators affiliated with Hamas as they staged a protest in the offices of the International Committee of the Red Cross in East Jerusalem on Monday, an act criticized by the Palestinian leadership as a blow to the first direct meetings between the Israeli and Palestinian sides in more than a year now under way in Jordan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/world/MIDEAST/MIDEAST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/world/MIDEAST/MIDEAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/world/MIDEAST/MIDEAST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '2 Palestinian Legislators Are Arrested in East Jerusalem Protest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Palestinian Legislators Are Arrested in East Jerusalem Protest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palestinian Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T21:12:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f83ea4e9-5ff2-5d5b-b84a-26fea850fe1a', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f83ea4e9-5ff2-5d5b-b84a-26fea850fe1a'}, {'abstract': 'The American Library Association announced the winners of the Newbery and Caldecott medals on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/childrens-book-awards-announced/', 'snippet': 'The American Library Association announced the winners of the Newbery and Caldecott medals on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American Library Association announced on Monday that the John Newbery Medal, considered the most prestigious award in children’s literature, went to “Dead End in Norvelt,” by Jack Gantos, and the Randolph Caldecott Medal for the most distinguished American picture book for children went to “A Ball for Daisy,” illustrated and written by Chris Raschka. Read more on the winning books at ArtsBeat. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Children’s Book Awards Announced', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T21:12:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54c19842-897c-5e89-bbf7-1ae693c768e7', 'word_count': 64, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54c19842-897c-5e89-bbf7-1ae693c768e7'}, {'abstract': 'Dangerously high levels have been detected in Northeastern songbirds as the most toxic form of the heavy metal moves through the food chain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/science/study-finds-mercury-in-more-northeastern-bird-species.html', 'snippet': 'Dangerously high levels have been detected in Northeastern songbirds as the most toxic form of the heavy metal moves through the food chain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The strict new federal standards limiting pollution from power plants are meant to safeguard human health. But they should have an important side benefit, according to a study being released on Tuesday: protecting a broad array of wildlife that has been harmed by mercury emissions. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24MERC2_SPAN/24MERC2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24MERC2_SPAN/24MERC2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24MERC2_SPAN/24MERC2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24MERC2_SPAN/24MERC2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24MERC2_SPAN/24MERC2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mercury’s Harmful Reach Has Grown, Study Suggests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mercury’s Harmful Reach Has Grown, Study Suggests', 'name': None, 'seo': None,