 New Yorker — provides insight into the advice Barack Obama, then president-elect, was getting as Wall Street teetered on the brink.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New Yorker‘s Ryan Lizza came out Monday with a nearly 11,000-word piece on President Obama‘s first term in office. The piece relies heavily on a series of confidential memos, never before published, that shed light on the president’s legislative agenda, including his budget process, his efforts to win over major interest groups and his efforts to shape bipartisan consensus in Washington.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summers Memo Provides Peek at Crisis Aftermath', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Summers, Lawrence H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T21:20:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06b23a06-fb11-5bdb-8076-4910d2e76d4a', 'word_count': 746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06b23a06-fb11-5bdb-8076-4910d2e76d4a'}, {'abstract': 'The third installment in in Vincent Dilio’s series of portraits from the art scene in Marfa, Tex.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/the-real-artists-of-marfa-ann-marie-nafziger/', 'snippet': 'The third installment in in Vincent Dilio’s series of portraits from the art scene in Marfa, Tex.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlide