mes', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/arts/thomas/thomas-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/24/arts/thomas/thomas-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/arts/thomas/thomas-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/arts/thomas/thomas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/arts/thomas/thomas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bank Facade, Statues and a Baritone', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bank Facade, Statues and a Baritone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hampson, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T22:23:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdf11752-d6a4-598d-a9d4-b2858fb929c0', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdf11752-d6a4-598d-a9d4-b2858fb929c0'}, {'abstract': 'A study suggests that dutasteride may slow or stop tumor growth in men who decide against surgery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/health/research/dutasteride-is-seen-to-curtail-cancer-left-in-prostate.html', 'snippet': 'A study suggests that dutasteride may slow or stop tumor growth in men who decide against surgery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fewer than 10 percent of the 100,000 men each year who get a diagnosis of early-stage prostate cancer and have the option of leaving the cancer in place while watching it actually do so. The rest want to just get rid of it, with surgery or radiation. But those treatments can have serious side effects like impotence and incontinence.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drug Seen to Curtail Cancer Left in Prostate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drug Seen To Curtail Cancer Left In Prostate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lancet, The (Journal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostate Gland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostate Specific Antigen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostate Cancer', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T22:24:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Research', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/498f48cf-aaa5-51a1-928b-f13f677a50f2', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/498f48cf-aaa5-51a1-928b-f13f677a50f2'}, {'abstract': 'Suze Orman promotes her Approved Card on the pages of O, The Oprah Magazine after promising not to do so on her television show.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/suze-orman-takes-to-o-magazine-to-promote-her-new-card/', 'snippet': 'Suze Orman promotes her Approved Card on the pages of O, The Oprah Magazine after promising not to do so on her television show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few weeks ago, I wrote about Suze Orman’s entrance into the prepaid debit card business with something called the Approved Card. In that piece, I asked her whether she thought the viewers of her CNBC show would be troubled by her making money off their everyday transactions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suze Orman Takes to O Magazine to Promote Her New Card', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orman, Suze', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winfrey, Oprah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'O: The Oprah Magazine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T22:25:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83cade61-45f3-5ea4-b6aa-94f63e757309', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83cade61-45f3-5ea4-b6aa-94f63e757309'}, {'abstract': 'Paris', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/0