nse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My piece in The Times Magazine, inspired by a series of visits to Kajitsu, detailed a recipe for vegan Worcestershire sauce that, if you have a few hours to spare, is not terribly difficult and worth the effort. But its length and detail reminded my friend Ed Schneider (former Bitten blogger and now a contributor to the Wall Street Journal and Washington Post, among others) of some of the nonsense recipes of the weirdo 19th century “nonsense poet” Edward Lear. That stuff is hilarious.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Would You Like a Side of Nonsense With That?', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lear, Edward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kajitsu (NYC Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-23T23:35:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd9bf9c3-f014-542d-80e8-830132517d2d', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd9bf9c3-f014-542d-80e8-830132517d2d'}, {'abstract': 'The bill criminalizes the denial of officially recognized genocides, including the Armenian genocide begun in 1915 — an event whose public affirmation in Turkey is treated as a crime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/world/europe/french-senate-passes-genocide-bill-angering-turks.html', 'snippet': 'The bill criminalizes the denial of officially recognized genocides, including the Armenian genocide begun in 1915 — an event whose public affirmation in Tur