'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/4693f67f-87aa-57a9-a3b0-1985fd5563cf', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4693f67f-87aa-57a9-a3b0-1985fd5563cf'}, {'abstract': 'The Greek government published a list of more than 4,000 people, including several household names, who owe a total of $19 billion to the cash-strapped state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/world/europe/greece-publishes-list-of-4000-tax-scofflaws.html', 'snippet': 'The Greek government published a list of more than 4,000 people, including several household names, who owe a total of $19 billion to the cash-strapped state.', 'lead_paragraph': ' In a name-and-shame campaign aimed at getting tax evaders to pay up, the Greek government published a list of more than 4,000 people, including several household names, who owe a total of $19 billion to the cash-strapped state. The list published late Sunday includes the veteran crooner Tolis Voskopoulos with debts of nearly $650,000; Pavlos Psomiadis, the owner of a defunct insurance firm, with arrears of nearly $2 million; and Giorgos Batatoudis, a former soccer club president who owes more than $3 million. Greece is under pressure from foreign creditors to curb endemic tax evasion, a key barrier to its economic recovery. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece Publishes List of 4,000 Tax Scofflaws', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece Publishes List of 4,000 Tax Scofflaws', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T00:34:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/143a36de-7249-5af9-a7fb-5967fd9d5ac7', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/143a36de-7249-5af9-a7fb-5967fd9d5ac7'}, {'abstract': 'The state appeared likely to become the seventh to allow gay couples to marry, after a state senator who had previously said she was undecided announced her support on Monday for a marriage bill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/us/washington-gay-marriage-wins-a-crucial-backer.html', 'snippet': 'The state appeared likely to become the seventh to allow gay couples to marry, after a state senator who had previously said she was undecided announced her support on Monday for a marriage bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The state appeared likely to become the seventh to allow gay couples to marry, after a state senator who had previously said she was undecided announced her support on Monday for a marriage bill moving through the Legislature. The measure, proposed by Gov. Christine Gregoire, a Democrat, has wide support in the House and had been just a few votes short in the Senate. After several undecided senators announced their support in recent weeks, Senator Mary Margaret Haugen, a Democrat, said she also would vote for the bill, becoming the decisive vote. A vote has not yet been scheduled. If the measure passes, opponents are expected to challenge it through a ballot referendum this fall. “For me personally, I have always believed in traditional marriage between a man and a woman,” Ms. Haugen said in a statement. “That is what I believe, to this day. But this issue isn’t about just what I believe. It’s about respecting others, including people who may believe differently than I. It’s about whether everyone has the same opportunities for love and companionship and family and security that I have enjoyed.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Washington: Gay Marriage Wins a Crucial Backer', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Northwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Washington: Same-Sex Marriage Wins Crucial Backer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haugen, Mary Margaret', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gregoire, Christine O', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T00:35:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1bb1906-dd8b-5901-a6fd-089253ed7d88', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1bb1906-dd8b-5901-a6fd-089253ed7d88'}, {'abstract': 'It may look like a victory dance, but an insect’s maneuver appears to have another purpose.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/science/dung-beetles-victory-dance-is-actually-a-getaway-move.html', 'snippet': 'It may look like a victory dance, but an insect’s maneuver appears to have another purpose.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After dung beetles collect the substance that gives them their name, they do a little dance, swinging around in one direction, and then sometimes the other.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24OBBEETLE1_SPAN/24OBBEETLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24OBBEETLE1_SPAN/24OBBEETLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24OBBEETLE1_SPAN/24OBBEETLE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 621, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24OBBEETLE1_SPAN/24OBBEETLE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/science/24OBBEETLE1_SPAN/24OBBEETLE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hasty Retreat of the Dung Beetle', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hasty Retreat Of the Dung Beetle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PLoS One', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T00:37:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94598f32-0c21-5818-8a48-a82e740cf80c', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94598f32-0c21-5818-8a48-a82e740cf80c'}, {'abstract': 'A destroyed house filled with the signatures and well-wishes of thousands of the volunteers who came to Joplin to help with the recovery after the deadly tornado last spring will be preserved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/us/missouri-message-laden-house-will-be-preserved.html', 'snippet': 'A destroyed house filled with the signatures and well-wishes of thousands of the volunteers who came to Joplin to help with the recovery after the deadly tornado last spring will be preserved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A destroyed house filled with the signatures and well-wishes of thousands of the volunteers who came to Joplin to help with the recovery after the deadly tornado last spring will be preserved, city leaders announced Monday. The house and the messages within had been decaying under the elements because the walls and roof were stripped off by the storm. A makeshift roof was erected to protect the building, which will be sealed on Tuesday with a type of shrink wrap to protect the messages from eroding further, said Patrick Tuttle, director of the Joplin Convention and Visitors Bureau. The house, he said, will soon be moved out of the rebuilding neighborhood and to a city-owned storage area until it can be incorporated into a museum or other public display. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missouri: Message-Laden House Will Be Preserved', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missouri: Message-Laden House Will Be Preserved', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{