e': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/business/Road/Road-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/business/Road/Road-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dearth of Disclosure About Expired Tickets', 'kicker': 'On the Road', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dearth of Disclosure About Expired Tickets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T00:54:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Sharkey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sharkey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/994a09e0-9f0d-5e79-b52c-8402bfe45993', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/994a09e0-9f0d-5e79-b52c-8402bfe45993'}, {'abstract': 'The executive vice president of marketing for GHX, a health care technology company, flies at least once a week, and seems to draw a lot of helpful people into his orbit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/business/cabdrivers-new-yorkers-even-darth-vader-everyones-nice.html', 'snippet': 'The executive vice president of marketing for GHX, a health care technology company, flies at least once a week, and seems to draw a lot of helpful people into his orbit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’M in marketing for a health care technology company and a typical road warrior, flying out every Monday from my office in Tulsa, Okla., to either our headquarters near Denver or to meet with clients. It’s tough flying anywhere direct from Tulsa, so I usually have to change planes, which can create some extensive delays.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/business/Flier/Flier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/business/Flier/Flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cabdrivers, New Yorkers, Even Darth Vader. Everyone’s Nice.', 'kicker': 'Frequent Flier', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cabdrivers, New Yorkers, Even Darth Vader. Everyone’s Nice.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T00:59:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Derek Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/071c4c04-c869-5df9-abf6-5db9a4f2e97d', 'word_count': 598, 'uri': 'nyt://article/071c4c04-c869-5df9-abf6-5db9a4f2e97d'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations is investigating allegations against peacekeepers in Haiti involving two cases of sexual abuse of minors, the organization’s spokesman said Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/world/americas/un-investigates-allegations-against-troops-in-haiti.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations is investigating allegations against peacekeepers in Haiti involving two cases of sexual abuse of minors, the organization’s spokesman said Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United Nations is investigating allegations against its police officers in Haiti involving two cases of sexual abuse of minors, the organization’s spokesman said Monday. The allegations were made against United Nations officers in Port-au-Prince, the capital, and in Gonaives. The officers have been removed from their duties while a team from New York investigates the allegations, said Martin Nesirky, the spokesman, adding that the leadership of the organization was “outraged” by the allegations. He declined to identify the nationality of the officers involved. There are about 11,000 United Nations peacekeepers in Haiti, about 3,500 of whom are police officers.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Investigates Allegations Against Troops in Haiti', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Investigates Allegations Against Troops in Haiti', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T01:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': 