S/DANIELS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A G.O.P. Counterweight to Obama, but So Far Just in Speech Response', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A G.O.P. Counterweight to Obama, but So Far Just in Speech Response', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daniels, Mitchell E Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T01:11:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbabb932-2b7a-5e97-a030-681c7fa87ce7', 'word_count': 926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbabb932-2b7a-5e97-a030-681c7fa87ce7'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney has received far more endorsements from Republican senators and governors than any other candidate, but the total among all candidates — 26 — represents barely more than a third of those possible.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/some-signs-g-o-p-establishments-backing-of-romney-is-tenuous/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney has received far more endorsements from Republican senators and governors than any other candidate, but the total among all candidates — 26 — represents barely more than a third of those possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sunday’s post on whether Newt Gingrich’s recent success has broken the paradigm in which party elites play a decisive role in determining presidential nominations drew hundreds of comments. Since there seems to be considerable interest in the topic, I would also encourage you to read the recent writings of the political scientists Seth Masket, John Sides and Jonathan Bernstein on the subject.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Some Signs G.O.P. Establishment’s Backing of Romney Is Tenuous', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T01:14:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6395ce7-3134-558c-ac18-04152ff30c97', 'word_count': 1460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6395ce7-3134-558c-ac18-04152ff30c97'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Ray was a colorful indie-film executive who helped steer art-house movies like “Bowling for Columbine” and “Hotel Rwanda” to the masses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/movies/bingham-ray-executive-who-championed-independent-films-dies-at-57.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Ray was a colorful indie-film executive who helped steer art-house movies like “Bowling for Columbine” and “Hotel Rwanda” to the masses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Bingham Ray, a colorful indie-film executive who helped steer art-house movies like “Bowling for Columbine” and “Hotel Rwanda” to the masses, died on Monday in a hospice in Provo, Utah. He was 57.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/movies/RAY-obit/RAY-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 905, 'width': 626, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/movies/RAY-obit/RAY-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/movies/RAY-obit/RAY-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bingham Ray, Executive Who Championed Independent Films, Dies at 57', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bingham Ray, 57, Executive Who Championed Independent Films', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'October Films', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ray, Bingham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T01:14:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c34b8d3-aca7-5dc1-abbe-b14e689b6a1f', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c34b8d3-aca7-5dc1-abbe-b14e689b6a1f'}, {'abstract': 'The French government said that the banned group was a terrorist organization training its members “for armed combat,” Interior Minister Claude Guéant said Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/world/europe/france-government-bans-domestic-islamist-group.html', 'snippet': 'The French government said that the banned group was a terrorist organization training its members “for armed combat,” Interior Minister Claude Guéant said Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The government has ordered the dissolution of a domestic Islamist group, saying that it was a terrorist organization training its members “for armed combat,” Interior Minister Claude Guéant said Monday. The Web site of the group, Forsane Alizza or “The Knights of Pride,” says its aim is to fight Islamophobia. The Web site is laced with anti-Semitic material and postings supporting organizations that are widely deemed to be terrorist groups, including the Afghan Taliban. A recent recruitment appeal by Forsane Alizza called for “soldiers,” and the group acknowledges some violent aims, in particular in the defense of Muslim women. The group gained attention last year through demonstrations against a French law banning the wearing of the full facial veil in public. A cofounder of the group, Mohammed Achamlane, said it would contest the dissolution order in court. “This is truly farcical,” he said in a telephone interview from Nantes in western France. “They have absolutely nothing against us.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France: Government Bans Domestic Islamist Group', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Government Bans Domestic Islamist Group', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T01:20:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/da8080b9-67cd-5862-87c5-08c6d1acc4a4', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da8080b9-67cd-5862-87c5-08c6d1acc4a4'}, {'abstract': 'With the next Republican primary in a state hard hit by the collapse of the housing bubble, free-market instincts collide with voters’ desperation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/us/politics/in-florida-facing-the-political-implications-of-housing-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'With the next Republican primary in a state hard hit by the collapse of the housing bubble, free-market instincts collide with voters’ desperation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORMOND BEACH, Fla.— When Mitt Romney swept into the contentious battleground state of Florida on Sunday, the first local issue he raised was the nation’s mortgage foreclosure crisis, which is arguably at its worst here, from this city on the northern coast to the ghost-town developments in what used to be farmland south of Miami.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/us/24housing1/24housing1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/24/us/24housing1/24housing1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/us/24housing1/24housing1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/us/24housing1/24housing1-thumbS