 an editorial, the paper, under new ownership, said it had “come to doubt the value” of endorsements.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/23/chicago-sun-times-ends-candidate-endorsements/', 'snippet': 'In an editorial, the paper, under new ownership, said it had “come to doubt the value” of endorsements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time since it began publishing 71 years ago, the editorial board of the Chicago Sun-Times announced late on Sunday that it would not endorse political candidates in the coming elections. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chicago Sun-Times Ends Candidate Endorsements', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barron, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCormick, Robert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Sun-Times', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T01:25:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/887f1490-d4c4-5253-bd13-3941ea48815a', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/887f1490-d4c4-5253-bd13-3941ea48815a'}, {'abstract': 'During the regular season, teams averaged 411.1 yards a game against the Patriots’ defense; in the playoffs, that has dropped to 325.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/sports/football/defense-goes-from-liability-to-asset-for-patriots.html', 'snippet': 'During the regular season, teams averaged 411.1 yards a game against the Patriots’ defense; in the playoffs, that has dropped to 325.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOXBOROUGH, Mass. — Over the course of the regular season, the New England Patriots won 13 games and earned the top seed in the A.F.C. , and did so without beating a team with a winning record and with a defense ranked dead last in the conference.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/sports/PATRIOTS2/PATRIOTS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 734, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/sports/PATRIOTS2/PATRIOTS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/sports/PATRIOTS2/PATRIOTS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Defense, Patriots Improve by Yards, if Not by a Mile', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Defense, Patriots Improve by Yards, if Not by a Mile', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T01:29:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter 