t-attack-on-mumbai.html', 'snippet': 'Authorities in Mumbai announced the arrest of two suspects on Monday in connection with a terrorist attack last July that killed 27 people in bombings across the city.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Authorities in Mumbai announced the arrest of two suspects on Monday in connection with a terrorist attack last July that killed 27 people in bombings across the city. Police investigators also blamed a domestic terrorist, Yasin Bhatkal, who remains at large and has been linked to a radical Islamic group known as the Indian Mujahedeen. Rakesh Maria, a top counterterrorism official in Mumbai, said the police had arrested two men from Bihar State, accused of being Mr. Bhatkal’s accomplices, and have identified others involved in the conspiracy. The attack consisted of explosions at three locations in Mumbai and investigators initially examined the possibility that the culprits were terrorist groups from Pakistan. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India: 2 Arrested in July Terrorist Attack on Mumbai', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India: 2 Arrested in July Terrorist Attack on Mumbai', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian Mujahedeen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T01:35:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d334cbf-7a69-5cff-8660-fe45377fa0db', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://articl