ar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Old, The New And The Familiar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tynes, Lawrence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belichick, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Umenyiora, Osi', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Brandon', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T02:11:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d52bd396-6b47-5d7a-9717-a67e992fa2e5', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d52bd396-6b47-5d7a-9717-a67e992fa2e5'}, {'abstract': 'As Steve Weatherford, the Giants’ holder, and Zak DeOssie, the long snapper, prepared for an expected rainy and muddy title game, they did not speak about a botched attempt in a 2003 playoff game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/sports/football/giants-field-goal-unit-needing-their-best-prepared-for-the-worst.html', 'snippet': 'As Steve Weatherford, the Giants’ holder, and Zak DeOssie, the long snapper, prepared for an expected rainy and muddy title game, they did not speak about a botched attempt in a 2003 playoff game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Steve Weatherford knew about the Giants’ recent history of last-second field goal tries at Candlestick Park. Of course he did. Everyone did. And even if he had not known before last week, it would have been impossible for him to ignore the questions and conversations about Trey Junkin’s bad snap and the disaster that was the end of the Giants’ collapse to the San Francisco 49ers in a 2003 playoff game.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/sports/SNAP1/SNAP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/24/sports/SNAP1/SNAP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/sports/SNAP1/SNAP1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 558, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/sports/SNAP1/SNAP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/sports/SNAP1/SNAP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants’ Field-Goal Unit, Needing Its Best, Prepared for the Worst', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s Good, and Not So Good: Giants Field-Goal Unit, Needing Its Best, Prepared for the Worst', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tynes, Lawrence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weatherford, Steve', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Candlestick Park', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeOssie, Zak', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T02:21:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/563ff03b-7af3-5c4f-8904-d5197365a6c2', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/563ff03b-7af3-5c4f-8904-d5197365a6c2'}, {'abstract': 'In the saga of Ryan Boatright, Part II, more evidence of how the N.C.A.A. wrecks careers, ignores due process and punishes the innocent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/opinion/nocera-living-in-fear-of-the-ncaa.html', 'snippet': 'In the saga of Ryan Boatright, Part II, more evidence of how the N.C.A.A. wrecks careers, ignores due process and punishes the innocent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was early in the evening of Jan. 13 when Ryan Boatright, the freshman basketball player at the University of Connecticut, learned that he was being suspended from the team for the second time this season. Earlier that day, he had flown into South Bend, Ind., with his teammates for a game against Notre Dame. The 19-year-old point guard was excited because some 400 people from his hometown, Aurora, Ill., were coming to see him play. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima