0000001307432/gingrich-and-romney-on-freddie-mac.html', 'snippet': 'From the Republican Debate', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the Republican Debate', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/multimedia/video-tampadebate-clip1/video-tampadebate-clip1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/23/multimedia/video-tampadebate-clip1/video-tampadebate-clip1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/23/multimedia/video-tampadebate-clip1/video-tampadebate-clip1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/23/multimedia/video-tampadebate-clip1/video-tampadebate-clip1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich and Romney on Freddie Mac', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T03:02:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'None None', 'person': [{'firstname': 'None', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'None', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/8e0450e8-30f8-5f0c-8a90-99bb645e14aa', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/8e0450e8-30f8-5f0c-8a90-99bb645e14aa'}, {'abstract': 'The state’s Supreme Court shows how the misguided Citizens United decision undermines the fight against political corruption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/opinion/montanas-challenge-to-citizens-united.html', 'snippet': 'The state’s Supreme Court shows how the misguided Citizens United decision undermines the fight against political corruption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years ago, when the Supreme Court struck down bans on independent corporate and union expenditures in elections in the Citizens United case, Justice Anthony Kennedy’s majority opinion claimed that money does not “give rise to corruption or the appearance of corruption.” While it might result in “influence over or access to elected officials,” he wrote, it is not the same as bribery. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Montana Takes on Citizens United', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Montana Takes On Citizens United', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supreme Courts (State)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T03:02:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b389b754-eb63-5cda-8f4e-0b8627e7c850', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b389b754-eb63-5cda-8f4e-0b8627e7c850'}, {'abstract': 'A court heard two versions of an early morning two years ago at the Plaza Hotel, where a woman says she was raped by Mustapha Ouanes, a member of the traveling entourage of a Saudi prince.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/nyregion/in-a-rape-trial-two-accounts-of-acts-by-a-man-with-royal-ties.html', 'snippet': 'A court heard two versions of an early morning two years ago at the Plaza Hotel, where a woman says she was raped by Mustapha Ouanes, a member of the traveling entourage of a Saudi prince.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It began as the sort of encounter that happens often and without note in the bars of Manhattan: an older married man vying for the attention of younger women with Champagne and meals at marquee hotels.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Rape Trial, Two Accounts of Acts by a Man With Royal Ties', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Rape Trial, Two Accounts Of Acts by a Man With Royal Ties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Plaza Hotel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T03:06:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Russ Buettner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Russ', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buettner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47f82add-75eb-5ec9-895f-25dae853d771', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47f82add-75eb-5ec9-895f-25dae853d771'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Chris Christie signed a long-overdue bill that permits pharmacies to sell a limited number of syringes to individuals without prescriptions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/opinion/saving-lives-in-new-jersey.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Chris Christie signed a long-overdue bill that permits pharmacies to sell a limited number of syringes to individuals without prescriptions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Chris Christie of New Jersey acted in the public interest when he signed a long-overdue bill that permits pharmacies to sell a limited number of syringes to individuals without prescriptions. This new law will save lives across the state by slowing the spread of blood-borne viruses like H.I.V.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saving Lives in New Jersey', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saving Lives in New Jersey', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hypodermic Needles and Syringes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T03:06:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a576214-f81a-592d-9a70-ae8701b8c390', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a576214-f81a-592d-9a70-ae8701b8c390'}, {'abstract': 'The winning numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'The winning numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jan. 23, 2012', 'print_sectio