'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/e9a49b35-ac7a-554a-a1bc-0d0993f540ca', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e9a49b35-ac7a-554a-a1bc-0d0993f540ca'}, {'abstract': 'Player ratings in soccer are by definition a subjective measure. John Godfrey — who regularly contributes ratings to the Goal blog — offers a few insights into what he’s thinking when he fills out his report card.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/player-ratings-one-mans-rules/', 'snippet': 'Player ratings in soccer are by definition a subjective measure. John Godfrey — who regularly contributes ratings to the Goal blog — offers a few insights into what he’s thinking when he fills out his report card.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Player ratings in soccer are by definition a subjective measure. One person’s 6 is another man’s 4. And since no two people view players or the game the same way, that is not likely to change. But because some readers have asked, John Godfrey — who regularly contributes ratings to the Goal blog — offers a few insights into what he’s thinking when he fills out his report card.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Player Ratings: One Man’s Rules', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T08:36:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Godfrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Godfrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e434bf53-62f7-5e68-95a9-e9a24b3e0367', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e434bf53-62f7-5e68-95a9-e9a24b3e0367'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/news-quiz-jan-24-2012/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries in today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Jan. 24, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T08:40:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd8ac1ce-8dc9-5689-be00-de76a024c43d', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd8ac1ce-8dc9-5689-be00-de76a024c43d'}, {'abstract': 'On Jan. 24, 1965, former British Prime Minister Winston Churchill died in London at age 90, nine days after suffering a severe stroke.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/jan-24-1965-winston-churchill-dies/', 'snippet': 'On Jan. 24, 1965, former British Prime Minister Winston Churchill died in London at age 90, nine days after suffering a severe stroke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Jan. 24, 1965, former British Prime Minister Winston Churchill died in London at age 90, nine days after suffering a severe stroke. “Winston Churchill’s struggle for life ended this morning, and the people he had cherished and inspired and led through darkness mourned him as they have no other in this age,” The New York Times reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jan. 24, 1965 | Winston Churchill Dies', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T09:05:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7d74475-f073-506d-9204-a743ae266ce7', 'word_count': 728, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7d74475-f073-506d-9204-a743ae266ce7'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the best synonym for the word “malicious”?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/test-yourself-english-jan-24-2012/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the best synonym for the word “malicious”?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the article “In Liverpool, Moment of Silence Followed by Impassioned Roar.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, Jan. 24, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T09:26:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f898287-7ba7-5a72-81f5-44394bcc9394', 'word_count': 48, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f898287-7ba7-5a72-81f5-44394bcc9394'}, {'abstract': 'Boise State’s Kellen Moore was one of the most productive and successful college quarterbacks in history. But there are several reasons to doubt his potential as a pro prospect.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/senior-bowl-day-1-impressions/', 'snippet': 'Boise State’s Kellen Moore was one of the most productive and successful college quarterbacks in history. But there are several reasons to doubt his potential as a pro prospect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a rainy day in Mobile, Ala., but spirits could not be dampened as the Senior Bowl got under way Monday. It began with the morning weigh-in, continued through practice in the afternoon, then through the evening at media night at the \xa0U.S.S. Alabama Battleship Memorial Park.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senior Bowl, Day 1 Impressions', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T09:35:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Waldman, Cecil Lammey and Jene Bramel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Cecil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lammey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Jene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bramel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ec44cb9-99b7-5584-a22c-2d98270c91b6', 'word_count': 1701, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ec44cb9-99b7-5584-a22c-2d98270c91b6'}, {'abstract': 'Why did the congresswoman decide to step down?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/gabrielle-giffords-resigns-from-congress/', 'snippet': 'Why did the congresswoman decide to step down?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHO was killed in the mass shooting in Tucson, on Jan. 8, 2011?WHO is governor of Arizona?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gabrielle Giffords Resigns From Congress', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T09:50:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Altavena', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Altavena', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9cbb5e0-ca42-5143-be24-ebff79a67e5d', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9cbb5e0-ca42-5143-be24-ebff79a67e5d'}, {'abstract': 'Born of the fervor of the 1970s, En Foco has gone from a community-based arts group to a national advocate for a dizzyingly diverse group of photographers. An exhibition at Sarah Lawrence College showcases that work.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/focusing-on-the-hidden-history/', 'snippet': 'Born of the fervor of the 1970s, En Foco has gone from a community-based arts group to a national advocate for a dizzyingly diverse group of photographers. An exhibition at Sarah Lawrence College showcases that work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perched somewhere above a “We Buy Gold” joint and a Latin restaurant on Kingsbridge Road in the Bronx, a darkroom turned storage closet was once a repository for an almost overlooked visual history. It was an unlikely spot for an equally unlikely – and unrivaled – collection that now comprises 700 photographs by Latino, African-American and Asian photographers and other artists of color.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Focusing on the Hidden History', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T10:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb76939a-7f93-5728-96c9-8797a70f4217', 'word_count': 1218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb76939a-7f93-5728-96c9-8797a70f4217'}, {'abstract': 'Although experience in a pro-style offense is becoming more common in college football, it still isn’t the norm.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/at-senior-bowl-a-wide-receiver-graduate-seminar/', 'snippet': 'Although experience in a pro-style offense is becoming more common in college football, it still isn’t the norm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOBILE, Ala. — To the untrained eye, a good wide receiver is a player who can run fast, jump high and catch the ball by any means necessary. This is a basic truth about the position, but there are several explosive athletes who can catch but never succeed in the N.F.L. That’s because of the complexity of the pro game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Senior Bowl, a Wide Receiver Graduate Seminar', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T10:02:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Waldman, Cecil Lammey and Jene Bramel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Cecil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lammey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Jene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bramel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/070795df-9e75-5ab0-a5e4-3da79650d3d0', 'word_count': 2056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/070795df-9e75-5ab0-a5e4-3da79650d3d0'}, {'abstract': 'Rajasthan officials say they received several warnings about threats against Salman Rushdie’s life.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/intel-about-rushdie-threats-was-real-rajasthan-says/', 'snippet': 'Rajasthan officials say they received several warnings about threats against Salman Rushdie’s life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Author Salman Rushdie cancelled an appearance at the Jaipur Literature Festival, which wraps up today, after he was informed by festival organizers of attempts against his life. News reports have cast doubts about that intelligence in recent days, suggesting it was fabricated, and Mr. Rushdie said he thinks he was “lied to.” Those doubts are “baseless,” the Rajasthan State government said in a statement issued late Monday evening. The full statement is below: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Intel About Rushdie Threats Was Real, Rajasthan Says', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rushdie, Salman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T10:07:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/340b5f78-dfd5-5f14-b056-6b40fe1cf750', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/340b5f78-dfd5-5f14-b056-6b40fe1cf750'}, {'abstract': 'How does independent, self-directed learning compare with the experience of learning in a classroom?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/what-would-you-like-to-learn-on-your-own/', 'snippet': 'How does independent, self-directed learning compare with the experience of learning in a classroom?', 'lead_paragraph': 'After homework, extracurricular activities, social life and leisure, you may have little time to do anything else. But have you ever made an effort to learn about something outside the classroom, not related to anything you’re studying in school? How would you use a daily “learning hour”? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Would You Like to Learn on Your Own?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T10:39:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Altavena and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Altavena', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d942954-0c7d-5542-a503-682b7156a08b', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d942954-0c7d-5542-a503-682b7156a08b'}, {'abstract': 'Profit in the last three months of 2011, which is Siemens’s fiscal first quarter, fell to $1.95 billion, a drop of 17 percent compared to a year earlier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/business/global/europe-debt-crisis-weighs-on-siemens.html', 'snippet': 'Profit in the last three months of 2011, which is Siemens’s fiscal first quarter, fell to $1.95 billion, a drop of 17 percent compared to a year earlier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FREIBURG, Germany — Siemens, an electronics and engineering giant that is a bellwether for German industry, said on Tuesday that profit and new orders fell late last year as the European debt crisis made customers more cautious about investing in new projects.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/business/SIEMENS/SIEMENS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 179, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/business/SIEMENS/SIEMENS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 179}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/business/SIEMENS/SIEMENS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 305, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Siemens, a German Bellwether, Reports a Decline in Profit', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Siemens, a German Bellwether, Reports a Decline in Profit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Siemens A.G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T10:41:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ca74b2d-2db7-5f1a-9f31-24b4f95bab02', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ca74b2d-2db7-5f1a-9f31-24b4f95bab02'}, {'abstract': 'An overhaul of the tax code might be possible, because both political parties have reasons to support it — but the debate would be improved if each side understood its own arguments, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/how-to-avoid-reinventing-the-wheel-on-tax-reform/', 'snippet': 'An overhaul of the tax code might be possible, because both political parties have reasons to support it — but the debate would be improved if each side understood its own arguments, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Avoid Reinventing the Wheel on Tax Reform', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simon, William E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/339dff4b-9196-5cdf-a1ed-0f19f79a1255', 'word_count': 996, 'uri': 'nyt://article/339dff4b-9196-5cdf-a1ed-0f19f79a1255'}, {'abstract': 'Blues-rock revivalists the Black Keys pay homage to the mediocre minivans that carried them to their earliest concerts.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/for-a-chart-topping-rock-group-a-fixation-with-the-humblest-of-band-vans/', 'snippet': 'Blues-rock revivalists the Black Keys pay homage to the mediocre minivan