ly on insects are taking in dangerous amounts of it.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/sounding-an-alarm-on-birds-and-mercury/', 'snippet': 'Mercury, which drifts into the Northeast largely from coal-burning power plants in the Midwest, is being deposited on dry land, and songbirds that survive solely on insects are taking in dangerous amounts of it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was in 2005 that I first accompanied David Evers into the cool dampness of a Catskills forest. At the time, Dr. Evers, a biologist and director of the Biodiversity Research Institute in Gorham, Me., was hunting for some pretty small game. He had draped a net between several trees in a section of the forest in upstate New York and, with the help of a portable cassette player that replicated the sound of songbirds trilling merrily away, was luring tiny wood thrushes into the trap.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sounding an Alarm on Birds and Mercury', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T12:16:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony DePalma', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DePalma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3f256e0-3b16-52c6-9f0e-0eb97425891a', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3f256e0-3b16-52c6-9f0e-0eb97425891a'}, {'abstract': 'Suzy Menkes speaks to the designer about her choice to return to the haute couture calendar, who the true clients are for her elaborate designs and how the brand is reaching a younger consumer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/fashion/100000001307608/an-interview-with-donatella-versace.html', 'snippet':