icle', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3746945a-8a58-5297-9bc6-43c71388e48f', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3746945a-8a58-5297-9bc6-43c71388e48f'}, {'abstract': 'The Versace presentation had a tension that might have been eliminated had Donatella Versace just staged a normal show.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/at-versace-calling-mr-demille/', 'snippet': 'The Versace presentation had a tension that might have been eliminated had Donatella Versace just staged a normal show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Versace was on the Quai Malaquais, so I went there at 10:30 a.m., killing a few minutes at the nearby Dries Van Noten shop to look at sale pieces and splash on some perfume. There was a crowd outside Versace, though nothing like the crowd that would be waiting at Dior a few hours later.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Calling Mr. DeMille', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T12:58:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6564aa96-14ef-53da-8537-01fc88784b90', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6564aa96-14ef-53da-8537-01fc88784b90'}, {'abstract': "It has been about a year since John Galliano’s scandalous departure from Christian Dior — and still no successor has been announced. In a haute couture special report, Suzy Menkes, the IHT’s fashion editor, calls Monday’s Dior show “rigorous, correct and undeniably ‘Dior'” And Suzy asks, “Is the elusive successor on the doorstep?”", 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/who-should-take-the-stage-at-dior/', 'snippet': 'It has been about a year since John Galliano’s scandalous departure from Christian Dior — and still no successor has been announced. In a haute couture special report, Suzy Menkes, the IHT’s fashion editor, calls Monday’s Dior show “rigorous, corr...', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been about a year since John Galliano’s scandalous departure from Christian Dior — and still no successor has been announced. Oh, there have been rumors, lots of them — although Bernard Arnault, chairman of LVMH Moët Hennessy Louis Vuitton, said Monday that the suspense will continue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Should Take the Stage at Dior?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dior, Christian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galliano, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menkes, Suzy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton SA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T12:59:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material':