er a Dispute With Official, Mirza and Vesnina Win Doubles Match', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T14:19:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By BEN ROTHENBERG', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'ROTHENBERG', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cacbdab2-53cb-574e-a93c-64e091c11ee3', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cacbdab2-53cb-574e-a93c-64e091c11ee3'}, {'abstract': 'Whenever negotiations resume between the M.T.A. and the Transport Workers Union, an important party will not be at the table — those who ride the subways and buses.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/a-voice-for-the-commuters-lost-amid-transit-talks/', 'snippet': 'Whenever negotiations resume between the M.T.A. and the Transport Workers Union, an important party will not be at the table — those who ride the subways and buses.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Publicly anyway, there’s a whole lot of nothing going on between managers of the city’s mass-transit system and the union that represents the men and women who keep the subways and buses running. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Voice for the Riders, Lost Amid Transit Talks', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Russianoff, Gene', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Straphangers Campaign', 'rank': 4, 'majo