: 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b5b0402-ae03-5c85-b4f2-8cf8acfaa2da'}, {'abstract': 'Wall Street shares were little changed as talks to resolve Greece’s debt crisis went on and analysts pointed to a possible lull after five days of gains.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/business/daily-stock-market-activity.html', 'snippet': 'Wall Street shares were little changed as talks to resolve Greece’s debt crisis went on and analysts pointed to a possible lull after five days of gains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stocks were mixed on Tuesday as European finance ministers and Greek bondholders were at a stalemate over how to resolve that nation’s debt crisis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Impasse Over Greece Sends S.&P. Down', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Impasse Over Greece Sends S.&P. Down', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T15:35:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c0101e9-4084-5113-967d-0b0251aa7962', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c0101e9-4084-5113-967d-0b0251aa7962'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Simon and Wynton Marsalis will perform together in April in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/simon-to-do-some-rhymin-with-wynton-marsalis/', 'snippet': 'Paul Simon and Wynton Marsalis will perform together in April in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Simon and Wynton Marsalis will give three concerts together in April, performing Mr. Simon’s songs in a rare collaboration between one of the leading pop song writers of the last 50 years and the virtuoso jazz trumpet player, Jazz at Lincoln Center announced Tuesday. The concerts will be staged at the Rose Theater at the organization’s headquarters on Columbus Circle. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Simon and Marsalis in Rare Collaboration', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marsalis, Wynton', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neville, Aaron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simon, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jazz at Lincoln Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rose Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'COLUMBUS CIRCLE (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T15:36:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/babefd00-90bd-525d-90ac-780a68c3af77', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/babefd00-90bd-525d-90ac-780a68c3af77'}, {'abstract': 'The growing income inequality between the ultrarich and the middle class is now debated in arenas where the primacy of laissez-faire capitalism was once taken for granted.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/davos-attendees-confront-a-new-wave-of-anger/', 'snippet': 'The growing income inequality between the ultrarich and the middle class is now debated in arenas where the primacy of laissez-faire capitalism was once taken for granted.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:12 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Davos, a Big Issue Is the Have-Lots vs. the Have-Nots', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T15:41:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8421716-89a2-520e-87f1-05e291a617e3', 'word_count': 1720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8421716-89a2-520e-87f1-05e291a617e3'}, {'abstract': 'Paris', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/24/fashion/0124chanelcouture-copy.html', 'snippet': 'Paris', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paris', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/fashion/runway/0124chanelcouture-slide-D0Q3/0124chanelcouture-slide-D0Q3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 681, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chanel Couture', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chanel, Coco', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagerfeld, Karl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T15:47:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/7de2f806-20f6-54c9-94ba-e7b974e8560d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/7de2f806-20f6-54c9-94ba-e7b974e8560d'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the records and near-records set in the nomination announcements.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/for-those-keeping-score-streep-sets-a-record-scorcese-has-a-chance-at-one/', 'snippet': 'A look at the records and near-records set in the nomination announcements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oscar-stat watchers are buzzing this morning with records made or about to be broken. As the Bagger’s colleagues Michael Cieply and Brooks Barnes have noted, Meryl Streep becomes the most-nominated actor in history, with 17 nominations to Jack Nicholson and Katharine Hepburn’s dozen each. “I am honored to be in company with such beautiful artists, and touched deeply by my fellow actors for their generosity in giving me this acknowledgment,” she said in a statement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Those Keeping Score:  Streep Sets a Record; Scorsese Has a Chance at One', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, WOODY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clooney, George', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Viola', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scorsese, Martin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Meryl', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T15:48:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7398c62-5935-5417-85cd-caf16cf414c1', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7398c62-5935-5417-85cd-caf16cf414c1'}, {'abstract': 'Fake electrical outlets trump mattresses as a hiding place for cash.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/putting-cash-under-the-mattress-is-so-old-school/', 'snippet': 'Fake electrical outlets trump mattresses as a hiding place for cash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With rates on savings accounts dwindling, you might be tempted to stash a little cash at home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Cash Under the Mattress Is So Old School', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Safes and Vaults', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T15:54:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29bc8d55-be04-5005-8133-19833afeb50a', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29bc8d55-be04-5005-8133-19833afeb50a'}, {'abstract': 'Alison Eighteen opens on Tuesday in the Flatiron district.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/alison-returns-but-not-on-dominick-street/', 'snippet': 'Alison Eighteen opens on Tuesday in the Flatiron district.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alison Eighteen, Alison Price Becker’s return to the Manhattan restaurant scene after an absence of almost 10 years, will evoke memories of her former restaurant, Alison on Dominick Street, when it opens next Tuesday. The chef, Robert Gurvich, is back, and the same designers, Asfour Guzy, have created the new Alison. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alison Returns, but Not on Dominick Street', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T15:57:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c3c3769-30e2-50fc-8fa2-0a258a03bbe1', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c3c3769-30e2-50fc-8fa2-0a258a03bbe1'}, {'abstract': 'Whenever couture is shown in the house, in the grand salons on the third floor, an enormous throng of spectators and paparazzi gathers outside.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/dior-holding-couture-to-the-light/', 'snippet': 'Whenever couture is shown in the house, in the grand salons on the third floor, an enormous throng of spectators and paparazzi gathers outside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 2:30 p.m. Monday, I arrived at Dior, on Avenue Montaigne. Whenever couture is shown in the house, in the grand salons on the third floor, an enormous throng of spectators and paparazzi gathers outside. It sounds far more glamorous than it really is. As I reached the main door, a black-suited security guard bellowed at people to clear the area so a guest’s car could pull up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dior: Holding Couture to the Light', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T15:59:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a0e65b7-577e-583b-9631-d7e2cd7e41b7', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a0e65b7-577e-583b-9631-d7e2cd7e41b7'}, {'abstract': 'A survey by Boston University shows that students are more concerned with academics when searching for college than almost anything else.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/boston-university-rigor/', 'snippet': 'A survey by Boston University shows that students are more concerned with academics when searching for college than almost anything else.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is an assumption, including among more than a few incredulous parents, that high school seniors often choose their colleges based less on academic offerings than on softer factors like campus amenities (think climbing walls and walk-in, dorm-room closets), the ratio of men to women in the class and even the institution’s tolerance for keg parties.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston University, Where Academic Rigor Is de Rigueur', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T15:59:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09f71bf7-7a50-5328-a928-0c0007e5d442', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09f71bf7-7a50-5328-a928-0c0007e5d442'}, {'abstract': 'The Giants-Patriots rematch promises two weeks of following a script, though detours are possible (and welcome).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/sports/deja-supe-super-bowl-rematch-promises-same-old-story-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'The Giants-Patriots rematch promises two weeks of following a script, though detours are possible (and welcome).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let us be the first to welcome you to Super Bowl matchup hangover day. This is the day when all the giddiness about the conference championship games fades and the excitement about a potentially thrilling Super Bowl is superseded by the knowledge that for the next 12 days you will be overrun by stories about two teams. Making heads throb even worse in much of the country, those two teams are from the New York and Boston areas, which is why Mike Vaccaro of The Post took today to apologize to the rest of the nation. We second his thought. Hang in there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Déjà Supe', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Déjà Supe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clijsters, Kim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belichick, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wozniacki, Caroline', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T15:59:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a49755cb-9397-56e7-b02b-dc58a027a941', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a49755cb-9397-56e7-b02b-dc58a027a941'}, {'abstract': 'A government program aims to promote gridless electricity as well as repair and extend power lines.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/on-our-radar-solar-kits-for-haitians/', 'snippet': 'A government program aims to promote gridless electricity as well as repair and extend power lines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Haiti’s president says he aims to double the number of rural households with electricity within two years by offering people loans to buy solar kits that can charge cellphones or computers. The $40 million program also calls for installing streetlights in the countryside and repairing power lines in the capital. Only 30 percent of the country’s population is estimated to have access to electricity. [Associated Press]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Solar Kits for Haitians', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cad869f-40af-577f-8adf-8f026711f489', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cad869f-40af-577f-8adf-8f026711f489'}, {'abstract': 'In a speech his campaign called a “pre-buttal” to Mr. Obama’s address Tuesday night, Mitt Romney lambasted the president’s handling of the economy.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/romney-attacks-obamas-state-of-the-union-speech-as-nothing-more-than-tall-tales/', 'snippet': 'In a speech his campaign called a “pre-buttal” to Mr. Obama’s address Tuesday night, Mitt Romney lambasted the president’s handling of the economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Mitt Romney on Tuesday charged that President Obama‘s State of the Union speech will be nothing more than “partisan plans for his re-election campaign,” and “tall tales about America.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Attacks Obama’s Address as Nothing More Than ‘Tall Tales’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:03:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c014813c-a034-5eb3-8045-cc4653d945ba', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c014813c-a034-5eb3-8045-cc4653d945ba'}, {'abstract': 'Quirky outfits like short leather bombers and trim tweed coats layered over colored sweaters felt more like great personal style statements than forced fashion.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/paris-top-5-ami/', 'snippet': 'Quirky outfits like short leather bombers and trim tweed coats layered over colored sweaters felt more like great personal style statements than forced fashion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arriving in Paris Wednesday night, I went straight from Charles de Gaulle airport to a trés Parisienne apartment off Place de la Republique for the designer Alexandre Mattiussi’s cocktail-party-as-fashion-presentation for Ami. Though Champagne and cigarettes abounded, this was no chic Rive Gauche affair; more like the Williamsburg-on-the-Seine scene of Rue Oberkampf or, as our in-the-know illustrator Richard Haines said: “So Bushwick L train/Morgan stop.” So true. It was an über-groovy crowd — hard to discern the models from the viewers — and a perfect welcome to the final leg of the European fashion show season. What’s more, it heralded the arrival of this new French sportswear brand, following the model of A.P.C., with its cult following and affordable prices. Quirky outfits like short leather bombers and trim tweed coats layered over colored sweaters and clashing untucked shirts (with the odd floral or plaid here and there) felt more like great personal style statements than forced fashion. A bright-eyed bearded fellow wore a tee with a floralized bearded fellow on it, along with a harvest-colored houndstooth vest, matching carrot-cut pants (imagine a slightly dropped crotch with full legs that narrow at the cuff) and a tonal, double-breasted plaid coat; an amusing outfit with Parisian charm that had me at “Bon soir.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Top 5 | Ami', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:06:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed9776b8-03b4-59ab-9e87-1f1bd13e2e2a', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed9776b8-03b4-59ab-9e87-1f1bd13e2e2a'}, {'abstract': 'Judy Battista, who covers the N.F.L. for The Times, will answer questions from readers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/have-n-f-l-questions-judy-battista-has-answers-10/', 'snippet': 'Judy Battista, who covers the N.F.L. for The Times, will answer questions from readers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coughlin vs. Belichick? Manning vs. Brady? Judy Battista, the N.F.L. reporter for The Times, will answer questions from readers this week. Use the comment field below for your questions. Answers will appear Friday on The Fifth Down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Have N.F.L. Questions? Judy Battista Has Answers', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Battista, Judy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:11:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9812da02-353d-585b-a34d-c9f3a3512146', 'word_count': 37, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9812da02-353d-585b-a34d-c9f3a3512146'}, {'abstract': 'The movie, nominated Tuesday for an Oscar for best picture, used almost 300 horses for one battle scene. The best acting was by Finders Key, who also appeared in “Seabiscuit.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/sports/finders-key-from-far-back-in-the-pack-to-the-lead-in-war-horse.html', 'snippet': 'The movie, nominated Tuesday for an Oscar for best picture, used almost 300 horses for one battle scene. The best acting was by Finders Key, who also appeared in “Seabiscuit.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before he went Hollywood, the thoroughbred gelding Finders Key accounted for only torn-up mutuel tickets at Los Alamitos Race Course, a track better known for quarter horse racing in Orange County, Calif. Winless in four $2,500 claiming races, he was beaten by a combined 30 lengths, never finishing higher than fifth. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/sports/25finders1/25finders1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/sports/25finders1/25finders1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/sports/25finders1/25finders1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/sports/25finders1/25finders1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/sports/25finders1/25finders1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Far Back in the Pack to the Lead in ‘War Horse’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "For Back in the Pack to the Lead in 'War Horse'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:11:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Christine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Christine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff8f30cc-6295-536f-beea-a59d12e89245', 'word_count': 1371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff8f30cc-6295-536f-beea-a59d12e89245'}, {'abstract': 'Some think the race has come down to “The Artist” vs. “Hugo,” which would make Oscar night the most self-referential in memory.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/if-its-the-artist-vs-hugo-hollywood-self-references-win/', 'snippet': 'Some think the race has come down to “The Artist” vs. “Hugo,” which would make Oscar night the most self-referential in memory.', 'lead_paragraph': '11:23 a.m. | Updated  LOS ANGELES—If you accept the theory advanced by some here that the Oscar race is now a showdown between “The Artist” and “Hugo,” then you are facing one of the weirder matchups in Academy Awards history. Both films are about the film business. But from Hollywood’s point of view, one picture comes from the outside and looks in, the other comes from the inside and looks out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If It’s ‘The Artist’ vs. ‘Hugo,’ Hollywood Self-References Win', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:14:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad63961e-2e12-5f95-9f53-3554dc7e2e65', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad63961e-2e12-5f95-9f53-3554dc7e2e65'}, {'abstract': 'Karl Lagerfeld spends enough time in the air to eventually think it might be a hoot to stage a Chanel show inside an airplane.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/flying-the-friendly-skies-of-chanel-couture/', 'snippet': 'Karl Lagerfeld spends enough time in the air to eventually think it might be a hoot to stage a Chanel show inside an airplane.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Karl Lagerfeld spends enough time in the air to eventually think it might be a hoot to stage a Chanel show inside an airplane. He has had icebergs hauled to Paris. He has created farm scenes, a formal garden and a monument to the quilted bag, all in the Grand Palais. What’s an airplane, with a drinks cart and fake clouds floating past the windows? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flying the Friendly Skies of Chanel Couture', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chanel SA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:15:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4aa340d1-f101-5174-b8b7-f957c49b7d76', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4aa340d1-f101-5174-b8b7-f957c49b7d76'}, {'abstract': 'Bruce Springsteen announced the dates Tuesday for this year’s “Wrecking Ball” tour, and they include a concert date in Newark, N.J.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/springsteen-tour-to-include-newark-concert/', 'snippet': 'Bruce Springsteen announced the dates Tuesday for this year’s “Wrecking Ball” tour, and they include a concert date in Newark, N.J.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Springsteen announced on Tuesday the dates for this year’s “Wrecking Ball” tour, and they include two concerts at Madison Square Garden, two gigs at the Izod Center in East Rutherford, N.J., and his first concert at the Prudential Center in Newark. The United States leg of the tour will kick off in Atlanta on March 18, a week and a half after Mr. Springsteen’s new album is to be released on Columbia Records. This tour is the first Mr. Springsteen and the E Street Band have done since the group’s longtime saxophonist, Clarence Clemons, died last year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Springsteen Announces U.S. Tour Dates', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springsteen, Bruce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia Records', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'E Street Band', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Izod Center (East Rutherford, NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madison Square Garden', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61ef4e06-b6c6-5e3e-938a-fb79ea7cf784', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61ef4e06-b6c6-5e3e-938a-fb79ea7cf784'}, {'abstract': 'Bob and Mike Bryan outlast Marcin Matkowski and Mariusz Frystenberg of Poland at the Australian Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/bryan-twins-win-midnight-marathon/', 'snippet': 'Bob and Mike Bryan outlast Marcin Matkowski and Mariusz Frystenberg of Poland at the Australian Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia – Bob and Mike Bryan of the United States outlasted Marcin Matkowski and Mariusz Fyrstenberg of Poland in a three-set marathon, 6-4, 6-7 (4), 6-4, to gain the semifinals of the Australian Open.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bryan Twins Win Midnight Marathon', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:17:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOHN MARTIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MARTIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61e3bbee-b5d5-569f-850e-82742d0215fe', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61e3bbee-b5d5-569f-850e-82742d0215fe'}, {'abstract': 'Comparing President Obama and Mitt Romney’s tax returns for 2011 to the typical taxpayer and the top 0.1 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/01/24/us/politics/the-candidates-tax-returns.html', 'snippet': 'Comparing President Obama and Mitt Romney’s tax returns for 2011 to the typical taxpayer and the top 0.1 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Comparing President Obama and Mitt Romney’s tax returns for 2011 to the typical taxpayer and the top 0.1 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Candidates’ Tax Returns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:18:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/7273cd94-0a3e-5907-9b7a-e30bdb5534fa', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/7273cd94-0a3e-5907-9b7a-e30bdb5534fa'}, {'abstract': 'Even if Woody Allen doesn’t attend the Oscars, nominations for his film “Midnight in Paris” and the Iranian drama “A Separation” make it a good day for Sony Pictures Classics.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/a-good-day-for-woody-allen-and-sony-pictures-classics/', 'snippet': 'Even if Woody Allen doesn’t attend the Oscars, nominations for his film “Midnight in Paris” and the Iranian drama “A Separation” make it a good day for Sony Pictures Classics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Is this the year Woody Allen warms up to the Oscars?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Good Day for Woody Allen and Sony Pictures Classics', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, WOODY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barker, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Pictures Entertainment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:22:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4d32b4d-f2f2-5bc2-b964-a9fdfede037a', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4d32b4d-f2f2-5bc2-b964-a9fdfede037a'}, {'abstract': 'For our 45 Places to Go in 2012 article we asked readers to tell us on Twitter where they want to go this year. Here are some highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/where-our-readers-wanttogo-in-2012/', 'snippet': 'For our 45 Places to Go in 2012 article we asked readers to tell us on Twitter where they want to go this year. Here are some highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For our 45 Places to Go in 2012 article we asked readers to tell us on Twitter where they want to go this year. Some highlights are below. Join the conversation in the comments below and tell us where you want to go in 2012.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Our Readers #WanttoGo in 2012', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:31:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6621deb-2c2e-5f77-9da6-a27296c2160b', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6621deb-2c2e-5f77-9da6-a27296c2160b'}, {'abstract': 'Three East Haven police officers and their supervisor were charged with beating and harassing Latinos, trying to cover up their actions and thwarting efforts to investigate their conduct.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/nyregion/connecticut-police-officers-accused-of-mistreating-latinos.html', 'snippet': 'Three East Haven police officers and their supervisor were charged with beating and harassing Latinos, trying to cover up their actions and thwarting efforts to investigate their conduct.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They were known as Miller’s Boys, police officers who worked the 4-to-midnight shift, patrolling the largely working-class town of East Haven, Conn., including the small but growing Hispanic community that has spread out in recent years from New Haven. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/nyregion/JP-EASTHAVEN1/JP-EASTHAVEN1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Gang Tyrannized Latinos, Indictment Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Police Gang Tyrannized Latinos, Indictment Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gallo, Leonard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maturo, Joseph A Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Haven (Conn)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:33:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Applebome', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Applebome', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3641bad7-c8e9-50e7-a17e-dda8e21c6abb', 'word_count': 1200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3641bad7-c8e9-50e7-a17e-dda8e21c6abb'}, {'abstract': 'One more round on the Republican Party’s Mario Cuomos.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/the-men-who-didnt-run/', 'snippet': 'One more round on the Republican Party’s Mario Cuomos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dismissing the argument in my previous post, Daniel Larison suggests that none of the alternative candidates for the Republican nomination possesses the unique skill set that my Sunday column identified as crucial to a successful presidential contender:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Men Who Didn’t Run', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:36:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cf24ab9-4d1c-5299-9fc9-388fcf224aa3', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cf24ab9-4d1c-5299-9fc9-388fcf224aa3'}, {'abstract': 'For spring/summer 2012, the atelier went back to the archives and rendered classic Dior silhouettes in translucent organdy.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/just-one-look-christian-dior-2/', 'snippet': 'For spring/summer 2012, the atelier went back to the archives and rendered classic Dior silhouettes in translucent organdy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the second season the house of Christian Dior has offered an haute couture collection without announcing a successor to its prior couturier, John Galliano. For spring/summer 2012 the atelier (helmed by Bill Gaytten) went back to the archives and rendered classic Dior silhouettes in translucent organdy. The idea was to create dresses that resembled X-ray images of Mr. Dior’s original designs (as if the pieces had been photographed by the likes of Nick Knight). For the clients it offers a rare opportunity to buy something classically Dior. So why not a ballgown? This one, in black silk, has a bodice of trapped sequins and a swirling skirt of plissé.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Christian Dior', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:43:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/535a531a-e4b7-53fc-8031-4dead95d70ad', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/535a531a-e4b7-53fc-8031-4dead95d70ad'}, {'abstract': 'Field Marshall Mohamed Hussein Tantawi said Tuesday that the military government would limit its use of extra-judicial arrests and detentions to cases of what he called “thuggery.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/world/middleeast/egypt-military-council-partly-curbs-state-of-emergency-law.html', 'snippet': 'Field Marshall Mohamed Hussein Tantawi said Tuesday that the military government would limit its use of extra-judicial arrests and detentions to cases of what he called “thuggery.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The army officer acting as Egypt’s de facto head of state said Tuesday that the military government would limit its use of extrajudicial arrests and detentions to cases of what he called “thuggery.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Military Council Partly Curbs State of Emergency Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt Military Council Partly Curbs State of Emergency Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tantawi, Mohamed Hussein', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 