b-9672-4e843b82556c'}, {'abstract': 'When a comedian posted a humorous video about breast feeding, a popular comedy Web site took it down and suspended her account.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/arts/television/funny-or-die-takes-down-and-then-restores-breast-feeding-video.html', 'snippet': 'When a comedian posted a humorous video about breast feeding, a popular comedy Web site took it down and suspended her account.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two months after she gave birth to twins, Ahna Tessler was feeling confined in her Manhattan apartment and in need of artistic expression. So on Jan. 14 Ms. Tessler, a comedian who lives on the Upper West Side, did what came naturally: she recorded a humorous skit that incorporated her routine of breast-feeding her babies, Madelyn and Elliot, and tried to post the video on the online comedy site Funny or Die. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/arts/leahgotajob/leahgotajob-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 639, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/arts/leahgotajob/leahgotajob-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/arts/leahgotajob/leahgotajob-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Breast Isn’t Best: Outcry Over Comic’s Post', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Breast Isn’t Best: Outcry Over Comic’s Post', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indecency, Obscenity and Profanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breastfeeding', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FunnyOrDie.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:57:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6589a09-b25e-554f-86a7-4b62a4810550', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6589a09-b25e-554f-86a7-4b62a4810550'}, {'abstract': 'The Timberwolves are trying to sign Kevin Love to an extension before the deadline.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/timberwolves-work-on-extension-for-love/', 'snippet': 'The Timberwolves are trying to sign Kevin Love to an extension before the deadline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is little doubt that power forward/center Kevin Love should be a keeper for the Minnesota Timberwolves. He’s averaging a career-high 24.9 points and 13.9 rebounds per game and logging more than 39 minutes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Timberwolves Work on Extension for Love', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T16:58:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOANNE C. GERSTNER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'GERSTNER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/239c1677-bbad-5a20-8fe2-9f6864aa5a91', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/239c1677-bbad-5a20-8fe2-9f6864aa5a91'}, {'abstract': 'A majority of Republicans approve of current tax policy that taxes capital gains at a lower rate than income from work, while Democrats and independents are more likely to want tax rates to be the same for both.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/poll-partisan-split-over-tax-policies/', 'snippet': 'A majority of Republicans approve of current tax policy that taxes capital gains at a lower rate than income from work, while Democrats and independents are more likely to want tax rates to be the same for both.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may come as no surprise, but Americans are deeply split along party lines when it comes to federal tax policy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poll: Partisan Split Over Tax Policies', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Gains Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allison Kopicki', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kopicki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/843e0823-ac79-5d21-8630-39eb8be7838f', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/843e0823-ac79-5d21-8630-39eb8be7838f'}, {'abstract': 'In separate studies, researchers have determined that in cold conditions, people’s calorie-gobbling brown fat uses ordinary fat as fuel — and that exercise may convert ordinary fat to brown fat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/health/brown-fat-burns-ordinary-fat-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'In separate studies, researchers have determined that in cold conditions, people’s calorie-gobbling brown fat uses ordinary fat as fuel — and that exercise may convert ordinary fat to brown fat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fat people have less than thin people. Older people have less than younger people. Men have less than younger women.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brown Fat, Triggered by Cold or Exercise, May Yield a Key to Weight Control', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brown Fat, Triggered by Cold or Exercise, May Yield a Key to Weight Control', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Calories', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa2829c0-fec6-56e7-afa3-453a54c80896', 'word_count': 1111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa2829c0-fec6-56e7-afa3-453a54c80896'}, {'abstract': 'He replaces Johnny Iuzzini, who resigned last year.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/joseph-murphy-named-pastry-chef-at-jean-georges/', 'snippet': 'He replaces Johnny Iuzzini, who resigned last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joseph Murphy has replaced Johnny Iuzzini as executive pastry chef at Jean Georges. Mr. Murphy has been the corporate pastry chef for Jean-Georges Management and the executive pastry chef of BLT Market and the Ritz-Carton New York. Mr. Iuzzini resigned at the end of last year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joseph Murphy Named Pastry Chef at Jean Georges', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f561814-a18b-505a-9375-742f00c3ee6a', 'word_count': 71, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f561814-a18b-505a-9375-742f00c3ee6a'}, {'abstract': 'Jeanie O’Hare, the dramaturg for the Royal Shakespeare Company, will succeed playwright Paula Vogel as chair of the Yale Drama School playwriting department.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/yale-turns-to-royal-shakespeare-company-for-its-new-playwriting-chair/', 'snippet': 'Jeanie O’Hare, the dramaturg for the Royal Shakespeare Company, will succeed playwright Paula Vogel as chair of the Yale Drama School playwriting department.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Yale School of Drama announced on Monday that Jeanie O’Hare, the company dramaturg for the Royal Shakespeare Company, would succeed Paula Vogel as chair of the Yale playwriting department beginning July 1.', 'source': 'The New York Times