'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c5a6c79-e3a0-575b-a1c4-bb607310dcab', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c5a6c79-e3a0-575b-a1c4-bb607310dcab'}, {'abstract': 'Debbie Bosanek, Warren Buffett’s secretary, will be the human face on a policy point during the State of the Union tonight.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/the-buffett-rule-isnt-about-mitt-romney-or-is-it/', 'snippet': 'Debbie Bosanek, Warren Buffett’s secretary, will be the human face on a policy point during the State of the Union tonight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are two words that President Obama is unlikely to utter when he talks about tax fairness during the State of the Union address: “Mitt Romney.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Buffett Rule Isn’t About Mitt Romney. Or Is It?', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:09:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John H. Cushman Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Cushman', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b353134c-3b10-5998-8f5d-e8aa1d8638bd', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b353134c-3b10-5998-8f5d-e8aa1d8638bd'}, {'abstract': 'Keynes first found fame when he resigned in 1918 from the Allied team imposing crippling reparations on Germany. He warned that deliberately impoverishing a country would encourage extreme political movements that might provoke a second world war. German Chancellor Angela Merkel and French President Nicholas Sarkozy run similar risks, an author writes.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/austerity-could-again-sow-seeds-of-extremism-in-europe/', 'snippet': 'Keynes first found fame when he resigned in 1918 from the Allied team imposing crippling reparations on Germany. He warned that deliberately impoverishing a country would encourage extreme political movements that might provoke a second world war....', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — Does this sound familiar?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/blogs/lepen-rdv-blog/lepen-rdv-blog-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 650, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/blogs/lepen-rdv-blog/lepen-rdv-blog-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/blogs/lepen-rdv-blog/lepen-rdv-blog-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Austerity Could Again Sow Seeds of Extremism in Europe', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Archives', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Wapshott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wapshott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0055c269-d681-5f8c-8058-49633341acff', 'word_count': 1622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0055c269-d681-5f8c-8058-49633341acff'}, {'abstract': 'The fashion designer discusses her beauty regimen.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/face-time-rachel-roy/', 'snippet': 'The fashion designer discusses her beauty regimen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rachel Roy is constantly in motion, with a namesake fashion collection and diffusion line, Rachel Rachel Roy, various collaborations and charitable work. The designer has even dabbled in makeup, creating a signature day-to-night eye shadow palette that stores couldn’t keep in stock. Next up: a partnership with OrphanAid Africa, an organization that benefits children in need. She also has two daughters, and is beautiful to boot! Naturally, I had some questions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Face Time | Rachel Roy', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Turnbow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ef4701e-ceea-591f-98b4-1986519c93fd', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ef4701e-ceea-591f-98b4-1986519c93fd'}, {'abstract': 'After putting major elements of the project on hold, the executive council of Abu Dhabi announced on Monday that it had approved construction plans for its multi-billion-dollar vision for a cultural tourist center to be constructed on an island just off the coast of the city, a hub that will include branches of the Guggenheim and the Louvre museums.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/abu-dhabi-greenlights-its-mega-museum-project/', 'snippet': 'After putting major elements of the project on hold, the executive council of Abu Dhabi announced on Monday that it had approved construction plans for its multi-billion-dollar vision for a cultural tourist center to be constructed on an island ju...', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was on. Then it was off. Now it’s back on again. The executive council of Abu Dhabi announced through its website on Monday that it had approved construction plans for its multi-billion-dollar vision for a cultural tourist center to be constructed on an island just off the coast of the city, a hub that will include branches of the Guggenheim and the Louvre museums.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Abu Dhabi Greenlights Its Mega-Museum Project', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gehry, Frank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louvre', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Abu Dhabi (United Arab Emirates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:20:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14af507b-955d-51c8-b701-d3e29b142b07', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14af507b-955d-51c8-b701-d3e29b142b07'}, {'abstract': 'The automaker has joined with Tendril, an energy management company, to create a demonstration home in California for the ActiveE electric vehicle.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/for-bmw-activee-a-home-base-that-speaks-fluent-e-v/', 'snippet': 'The automaker has joined with Tendril, an energy management company, to create a demonstration home in California for the ActiveE electric vehicle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BMW and 