ma, who managed the bakery there, are opening 606 R&D, a small homestyle restaurant and bar. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'City Bakery Chef Opens 606 R&D', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:22:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10bbb2ae-7198-5eaa-b030-94c607891060', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10bbb2ae-7198-5eaa-b030-94c607891060'}, {'abstract': 'Sonny Vandevelde’s couture fashion week photo diary.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/photos-of-the-moment-christian-dior-4/', 'snippet': 'Sonny Vandevelde’s couture fashion week photo diary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of the Moment | Christian Dior', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sonny Vandevelde', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sonny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vandevelde', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ca08380-43b3-5cdd-a1c0-214bdabbe1e1', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ca08380-43b3-5cdd-a1c0-214bdabbe1e1'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich and President Obama each pay a federal tax rate typical of most affluent Americans, with rates well above those of most middle-class households. Mitt Romney pays a federal tax rate more typical of an upper-middle-class household.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/putting-candidates-tax-rates-in-perspective/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich and President Obama each pay a federal tax rate typical of most affluent Americans, with rates well above those of most middle-class households. Mitt Romney pays a federal tax rate more typical of an upper-middle-class household.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is a quick way to put the recent flurry of tax numbers into perspective: Newt Gingrich and President Obama each pay a federal tax rate typical of most affluent Americans, with rates well above those of many middle-class households. Mitt Romney pays a federal tax rate more typical of an upper-middle-class household making perhaps $80,000 a year — higher than the rate of most households but not enormously so.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Candidates’ Tax Rates in Perspective', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Budget Office', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bd64d49-3e56-5ad6-8a5b-de0b1e25d28a', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bd64d49-3e56-5ad6-8a5b-de0b1e25d28a'}, {'abstract': 'Marky Ramone says that a leather jacket being auctioned as one that he wore onstage with the Ramones never belonged to him.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/marky-ramone-jacket-auction-fake/', 'snippet': 'Marky Ramone says that a leather jacket being auctioned as one that he wore onstage with the Ramones never belonged to him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, Jan. 25 The contested jacket was withdrawn from auction. Read the follow-up', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Punk-Rock History? Or Just a Leather Jacket?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ramones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:40:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aidan Gardiner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aidan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardiner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c331d1e1-2273-5713-9f80-cc73505de05f', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c331d1e1-2273-5713-9f80-cc73505de05f'}, {'abstract': 'What the editorial board would like President Obama to say tonight.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/state-of-the-union-wish-list/', 'snippet': 'What the editorial board would like President Obama to say tonight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite what some paranoid people on the Internet seem to think, \xa0the New York Times editorial board does not write the president’s speeches (and his speechwriters don’t draft our editorials). But with some regularity we discuss what we wish Barack Obama would say. And, of course, we always have a lot of opinions about what he said – and no, they are not always positive..', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'State of the Union Wish List', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:40:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79746195-7d91-5eab-84f0-8badb58b7f6c', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79746195-7d91-5eab-84f0-8badb58b7f6c'}, {'abstract': 'Celtics backup guard Avery Bradley proved the wisdom of a one-man press with his impressive performance against Orlando.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/bradley-revives-boston-defense-with-one-man-press/', 'snippet': 'Celtics backup guard Avery Bradley proved the wisdom of a one-man press with his impressive performance against Orlando.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Boston Celtics’ defensive domination over the Orlando Magic on Monday night was comprehensive and unrelenting. It began with a statement first quarter; the Celtics held the Magic –- who at the time boasted the N.B.A.’s second-best offense –- to 6-of-18 shooting from the field in the opening frame. Boston allowed just 20 points for the quarter – an impressive mark on its own and a lofty benchmark for the Celtics’ D the rest of the way.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bradley Revives Boston Defense With One-Man Press', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:41:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By ROB MAHONEY', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MAHONEY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d1456f9-5e3b-5bdf-b66c-58aaf519e064', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d1456f9-5e3b-5bdf-b66c-58aaf519e064'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney on Tuesday released documents that show he and his wife had an effective federal tax rate in 2010 of 13.9 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/us/politics/romneys-tax-returns-show-21-6-million-income-in-10.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney on Tuesday released documents that show he and his wife had an effective federal tax rate in 2010 of 13.9 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney and his wife, Ann, made $27 million in 2010. They held millions of dollars in a Swiss bank account and millions more in partnerships in the Cayman Islands. His family’s trusts sold thousands of shares in Goldman Sachs that were offered to favored clients when the storied investment house first went public. The couple’s effective federal tax rate for the year worked out to 13.9 percent, a rate typical of households earning about $80,000 a year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/us/sub-25tax/sub-25tax-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/us/sub-25tax/sub-25tax-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/us/sub-25tax/sub-25tax-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/us/sub-25tax/sub-25tax-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/us/sub-25tax/sub-25tax-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Romneys, Friendly Code Reduces Taxes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Romneys, Friendly Code Reduces Taxes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:42:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore and David Kocieniewski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kocieniewski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/441b4e6f-3bee-5c73-b636-a7b966a98d67', 'word_count': 1321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/441b4e6f-3bee-5c73-b636-a7b966a98d67'}, {'abstract': 'For the Couture edition of The Daily Shoe, T picks the most exquisite made-to-measures. Here, a classic but saucy pump by Chanel.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/the-daily-shoe-chanel-2/', 'snippet': 'For the Couture edition of The Daily Shoe, T picks the most exquisite made-to-measures. Here, a classic but saucy pump by Chanel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the Couture edition of The Daily Shoe, T picks the most exquisite made-to-measures.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Daily Shoe | Chanel', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chanel SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:46:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71da5dfb-f212-5029-84de-4e4e6aec4745', 'word_count': 54, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71da5dfb-f212-5029-84de-4e4e6aec4745'}, {'abstract': 'A growing number of adoptees are turning to DNA testing companies in hopes of learning about their biological past.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/adoption-and-the-dna-family-search/', 'snippet': 'A growing number of adoptees are turning to DNA testing companies in hopes of learning about their biological past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many (although far from all) adult adoptees are frustrated by their lack of access to their biological past. The relative openness of adoption records varies from state to state and from year to year, and while many adult adoptees have searched for and found birth relatives, their legal right to information is inconsistent at best. Last year, the adoption advocate Adam Pertman framed it as a civil rights issue: denying adult adoptees access to their original birth certificates, he said, is denying a minority group equal rights under the law.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adoption and the DNA Family Search', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADOPTIONS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swarns, Rachel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:46:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7885d064-683c-50e3-b9f1-db43498d7768', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7885d064-683c-50e3-b9f1-db43498d7768'}, {'abstract': 'Salvage and rescue workers reported the first possible sign of a contaminant slick beginning to ooze from the partly submerged Costa Concordia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/world/europe/very-thin-film-of-slick-reported-oozing-from-costa-concordia.html', 'snippet': 'Salvage and rescue workers reported the first possible sign of a contaminant slick beginning to ooze from the partly submerged Costa Concordia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GIGLIO, Italy — Salvage and rescue workers reported the first sign of a significant contaminant slick beginning to ooze from the partly submerged Costa Concordia on Tuesday as divers recovered the sodden body of the 16th victim from the Jan. 13 shipwreck.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Very Thin Film’ of Slick Reported from Stricken Cruise Ship', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Sign of Oil Slick Is Reported', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Costa Crociere SpA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruises', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tuscany (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:50:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4955475e-17a8-564e-b6e1-63a11f76b7ec', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4955475e-17a8-564e-b6e1-63a11f76b7ec'}, {'abstract': 'The nominees in the documentary and animation feature categories are interesting for some oversights, typical of those independent-minded branches of the Academy.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/documentarians-and-animators-go-their-own-ways/', 'snippet': 'The nominees in the documentary and animation feature categories are interesting for some oversights, typical of those independent-minded branches of the Academy.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:36 p.m. | Updated  Two groups of Academy voters have traditionally been independent-minded in their choices, and this year is no exception. The documentary branch, which has been roiled by  the changes to its nomination process that will affect selections in the coming years, still managed to have some noteworthy snubs this season, chief among them “Project Nim.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Documentarians and Animators Go Their Own Ways', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bausch, Pina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wenders, Wim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paramount Pictures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pixar Animation Studios', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:51:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d966718-32ab-594c-9cc7-993ea4e9c24b', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d966718-32ab-594c-9cc7-993ea4e9c24b'}, {'abstract': 'With the sale to Robert Bosch of Germany, the SPX Corporation will now focus on its flow technology business.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/spx-sells-auto-tools-business-for-1-15-billion/', 'snippet': 'With the sale to Robert Bosch of Germany, the SPX Corporation will now focus on its flow technology business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The SPX Corporation, an industrial conglomerate, said on Tuesday that it had agreed to sell its auto tools and solutions business to Robert Bosch of Germany for $1.15 billion in cash. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SPX Sells Auto Tools Business for $1.15 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SPX Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:51:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa8d9f9b-eb02-5d44-994b-234ab6a611f5', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa8d9f9b-eb02-5d44-994b-234ab6a611f5'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich uses Reagan’s name early and often, and in almost every debate.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/reagan-count-gingrich-55-romney-6/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich uses Reagan’s name early and often, and in almost every debate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Monday night’s debate in Tampa, Fla., Newt Gingrich, the former House speaker, mentioned Ronald Reagan just four words into his first answer of the night. It was the first of five times that Mr. Gingrich would mention Reagan; no other candidate did so even once.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reagan Count: Gingrich 55, Romney 6', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T17:55:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7caba66-38ef-5408-afd4-a5065bc766d8', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7caba66-38ef-5408-afd4-a5065bc766d8'}, {'abstract': 'The Italian-American cooking at Parm is completely faithful to your memories while being much, much better than you remembered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/dining/reviews/parm-restaurant-review-nyc.html', 'snippet': 'The Italian-American cooking at Parm is completely faithful to your memories while being much, much better than you remembered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF the meatball parmigiana hero were a Southern dish, scholars from Chapel Hill, N.C., to Tallahassee, Fla., would hold academic conferences every six months just to talk about it. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/dining/25REST1_SPAN/25REST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/dining/25REST1_SPAN/25REST1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/dining/25REST1_SPAN/25REST1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/dining/25REST1_SPAN/25REST1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'cro