Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/167823c2-989a-52e4-afce-839a3f43a9e0', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/167823c2-989a-52e4-afce-839a3f43a9e0'}, {'abstract': 'The Theater Hall of Fame names Ben Vereen and Tyne Daly among new honorees.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/tyne-daly-ben-vereen-among-theater-hall-of-fame-inductees/', 'snippet': 'The Theater Hall of Fame names Ben Vereen and Tyne Daly among new honorees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Theater Hall of Fame, which will hold its annual ceremony on Monday honoring lifetime achievement in American theater, has announced its new inductees. They are the actors Tyne Daly and Ben Vereen; the directors Daniel Sullivan and, posthumously, Paul Sills; the costumer designer Ann Roth; and the producers George C. White, Elliot Martin and Woodie King Jr.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tyne Daly, Ben Vereen Among Theater Hall of Fame Inductees', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daly, Tyne', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Woodie Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Ann', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sills, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vereen, Ben', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Theater Hall of Fame', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T18:36:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc77e980-d844-5d78-b52f-8c75ce4610e5', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc77e980-d844-5d78-b52f-8c75ce4610e5'}, {'abstract': 'Matthew Bowman’s timely new history offers rich context while delivering few opinions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/books/the-mormon-people-matthew-bowmans-timely-church-history-review.html', 'snippet': 'Matthew Bowman’s timely new history offers rich context while delivering few opinions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best musical number in “The Book of Mormon,” the Tony Award-winning play from the holy fools who created “South Park,” is a fantasia that features Hitler, Jeffrey Dahmer, Johnnie Cochran, Genghis Khan and dancing cups of Starbucks coffee. Its title is  “Spooky Mormon Hell Dream.”  ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/jp-book/jp-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/jp-book/jp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/jp-book/jp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'All-American Religion or Reason to Worry?', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Examining a Religion, Minus the Osmonds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major'