nyt://article/073f9cb4-666d-548f-a8b9-16eb087ba5a4', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/073f9cb4-666d-548f-a8b9-16eb087ba5a4'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers representing both Ronald Perelman and Donald Drapkin, his former business partner, were in court on Tuesday morning to settle some last minute issues and select a jury for the trial, which is expected to last roughly five days.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/opening-arguments-set-for-perelman-trial/', 'snippet': 'Lawyers representing both Ronald Perelman and Donald Drapkin, his former business partner, were in court on Tuesday morning to settle some last minute issues and select a jury for the trial, which is expected to last roughly five days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Opening arguments are set to begin Tuesday afternoon in trial covering the dispute between the billionaire financier Ronald O. Perelman and his former business partner. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opening Arguments Set for Perelman Trial', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perelman, Ronald O', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T18:45:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig and William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a524b774-d974-5277-a90d-4bc25a65e98c', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a524b774-d974-5277-a90d-4bc25a65e98c'}, {'abstract': 'Debbie Bosanek, who is Warren Buffett’s secretary, will be joining Michelle Obama in the first lady’s box seats during President Obama’s State of the Union address, John H. Cushman Jr. reported for The New York Times Caucus blog.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/the-buffett-rule-isnt-about-mitt-romney-or-is-it/', 'snippet': 'Debbie Bosanek, who is Warren Buffett’s secretary, will be joining Michelle Obama in the first lady’s box seats during President Obama’s State of the Union address, John H. Cushman Jr. reported for The New York Times Caucus blog.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Debbie Bosanek, who is Warren Buffett’s secretary, will be joining Michelle Obama in the first lady’s box seats during President Obama’s State of the Union address, John H. Cushman Jr. reported for The New York Times Caucus blog. Read more »', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Buffett Rule Isn’t About Mitt Romney. Or Is it?', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T18:49:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d971940-2b62-5b39-b82b-e429df9416b3', 'word_count': 41, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d971940-2b62-5b39-b82b-e429df9416b3'}, {'abstract': 'Raise a glass of tequila to Demian Bichir — that’s what he’d want you to do.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/a-nominee-toasts-to-his-good-fortune/', 'snippet': 'Raise a glass of tequila to Demian Bichir — that’s what he’d want you to do.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’m already drunk!” Demian Bichir announced when he called the Bagger from Mexico City on Tuesday morning, just a few hours after becoming a best actor nominee for his turn as an undocumented immigrant and gardener in “A Better Life.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Nominee Toasts His Good Fortune', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bichir, Demian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clooney, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitt, Brad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spacey, Kevin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weitz, Chris', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Screen Actors Guild', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T18:50:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07e7e866-1987-5cec-ba5b-a96b8e8b6c08', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07e7e866-1987-5cec-ba5b-a96b8e8b6c08'}, {'abstract': 'An eclectic set of technology predictions for 2012, from a fearlessly opinionated industry pundit.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/a-quirky-set-of-technology-predictions-for-2012/', 'snippet': 'An eclectic set of technology predictions for 2012, from a fearlessly opinionated industry pundit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The yearly technology forecasting game tends to be too earnest and too obvious. In part, that is because when the big research houses, like IDC and Gartner, prepare their lists, it is a consensus of their analysts. And why not? The strength of the large research firms is their deep benches — the breadth and depth of their industry smarts. The results, though, are works of what today is called collective intelligence and what used to be called a committee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Quirky Set of Technology Predictions for 2012', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Lohr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lohr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a6760a5-05b8-5d80-a363-70e0e9035693', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a6760a5-05b8-5d80-a363-70e0e9035693'}, {'abstract': 'The chatter at an annual tech conference in Munich is that the Web is booming — on a continent contemplating a tough net privacy law and better known recently for austerity and cutbacks.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/data-law-in-works-but-tech-booms-in-europe/', 'snippet': 'The chatter at an annual tech conference in Munich is that the Web is booming — on a continent contemplating a tough net privacy law and better known recently for austerity and cutbacks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Europe may be on the brink of passing what some tech firms and entrepreneurs view as a stifling law on data protection and the rights of consumers to have their data destroyed. But the chatter at an annual tech conference in Munich where E.U. Commissioner Viviane Reding laid out those data privacy plans this week seemed to be that the Web is booming on a continent better known lately for austerity and cutbacks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Data Law in Works, But Tech Booms in Europe', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reding, Viviane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Munich (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaf88a05-ae70-5811-b34e-982baf4e2e1c', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaf88a05-ae70-5811-b34e-982baf4e2e1c'}, {'abstract': 'On the eve of the Egyptian revolution’s first anniversary, one activist shares video he shot of the first hours of protest in Cairo on Jan. 25, 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/the-first-hours-of-egypts-revolution/', 'snippet': 'On the eve of the Egyptian revolution’s first anniversary, one activist shares video he shot of the first hours of protest in Cairo on Jan. 25, 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Egyptian activists and the military council that still rules the country are braced for planned demonstrations on Wednesday, the first anniversary of the start of the revolution that toppled former President Hosni Mubarak. Since our coverage of last year’s events was illuminated by online reports from activists who documented the uprising on social networks, The Lede discussed the anniversary with some of those bloggers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The First Hours of Egypt’s Revolution', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tear Gas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:08:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adel Abdel Ghafar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adel', 'middlename': 'Abdel', 'lastname': 'Ghafar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b29d587f-e820-56be-b6f2-9f61cf261a6f', 'word_count': 1472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b29d587f-e820-56be-b6f2-9f61cf261a6f'}, {'abstract': 'Playing some of the best tennis of his career, Roger Federer is winning a high percentage of first-serve points.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/federer-vs-del-potro-breaking-it-down/', 'snippet': 'Playing some of the best tennis of his career, Roger Federer is winning a high percentage of first-serve points.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The brilliance of Roger Federer is best found by not looking at Roger Federer at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federer vs. Del Potro: Breaking It Down', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:09:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': "By CRAIG O'SHANNESSY", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'SHANNESSY", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f6ea93f-397e-5306-83b8-c18303f1e811', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f6ea93f-397e-5306-83b8-c18303f1e811'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the loveliest frocks had voluminous sleeves and embroidery that nodded to Art Deco, like this short number edged in a fan and bird motif.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/just-one-look-chanel-2/', 'snippet': 'Some of the loveliest frocks had voluminous sleeves and embroidery that nodded to Art Deco, like this short number edged in a fan and bird motif.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Chanel haute couture, Karl Lagerfeld built the interior of an airplane in the attic of the Mini Palais and then set loose a collection of dresses rendered in every possible shade of sky. It soared. Each detail lifted the looks from cocktail to cool: the shoulder duster drop earrings in silver and sapphire, the mohawks and quiffs held high with jewels and feathers. Some of the loveliest frocks had voluminous sleeves and embroidery that nodded to Art Deco, like this short number edged in a fan and bird motif.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Chanel', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagerfeld, Karl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chanel SA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:09:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6c280b6-33a9-5900-bd81-b220d4c1804f', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6c280b6-33a9-5900-bd81-b220d4c1804f'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Daragjati, a white police officer, admitted to violating the civil rights of a black man on Staten Island, and also pleaded guilty to extortion.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/officer-pleads-guilty-to-civil-rights-violation/', 'snippet': 'Michael Daragjati, a white police officer, admitted to violating the civil rights of a black man on Staten Island, and also pleaded guilty to extortion.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:01 p.m. | Updated  A white New York City police officer pleaded guilty on Tuesday to violating the civil rights of a black man on Staten Island by charging him with resisting arrest knowing that there was no probable cause to support the charge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Officer Pleads Guilty to Civil Rights Violation', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daragjati, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fischetti, Ronald P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:10:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mosi Secret', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mosi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Secret', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cf0cb84-2077-5c4f-9bca-77d03ceb454c', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cf0cb84-2077-5c4f-9bca-77d03ceb454c'}, {'abstract': 'The reuse of municipal wastewater will be important to meeting future demand for freshwater in the United States, a new report from the National Academy of Sciences says.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/wasting-the-wastewater/', 'snippet': 'The reuse of municipal wastewater will be important to meeting future demand for freshwater in the United States, a new report from the National Academy of Sciences says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each day, American municipalities discharge treated wastewater back into natural sources at a rate that would fill an empty Lake Champlain within six months. Growing pressure on water supplies and calls for updating the ancient subterranean piping infrastructure have brought new scrutiny to this step in the treatment process, which is labeled wasteful and unnecessary by a spectrum of voices.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wasting the Wastewater', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:10:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0415ec19-d819-5bec-85ee-862383a298cf', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0415ec19-d819-5bec-85ee-862383a298cf'}, {'abstract': 'His own season derailed by injury, Peyton Manning has been watching his brother Eli’s run to the Super Bowl intently.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/sports/football/peyton-manning-fan-analyst-and-his-brothers-defender.html', 'snippet': 'His own season derailed by injury, Peyton Manning has been watching his brother Eli’s run to the Super Bowl intently.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Peyton Manning spends most of his time in the Indianapolis Colts’ weight room now, in a desperate race to rehabilitate from the neck injury that cost him the 2011 season and could imperil his career. That was where he watched the Giants’ run to the Super Bowl, an extremely well-informed fan with an extremely deep rooting interest. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/sports/25manning1/25manning1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/sports/25manning1/25manning1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/sports/25manning1/25manning1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 827, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/sports/25manning1/25manning1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/sports/25manning1/25manning1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}]