 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/24/sports/20120124photoreplay-slide-WI5Y/20120124photoreplay-slide-WI5Y-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Photo Replay: Jan. 24', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:24:26+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/53e41b82-951f-5263-b7cf-f03a4f9c8f54', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/53e41b82-951f-5263-b7cf-f03a4f9c8f54'}, {'abstract': 'An end to inspections could saddle companies and consumers with added costs, and officials are concerned it could deal a blow to Brooklyn’s already vulnerable port system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/nyregion/red-hook-facing-loss-of-customs-inspection-station.html', 'snippet': 'An end to inspections could saddle companies and consumers with added costs, and officials are concerned it could deal a blow to Brooklyn’s already vulnerable port system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The journey of a banana from Ecuador to Brooklyn is a precisely timed affair, from the moment it is sliced off a stalk and then packed onto a ship for a seven-day refrigerated cruise to the Red Hook Container Terminal. From there, the banana has one week to make it from container to distributor to grocery store.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/nyregion/PORTS1/PORTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/nyre