as-you-plan/', 'snippet': 'Before the Frugal Traveler heads to Texas, here are some tips on saving money on car trips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m not really your drive-across-America type — more of a train-through-India or Bolivia-by-bus kind of traveler. But I’ve long wanted to do a road trip in Texas. For someone like me, who has never lived west of the Hudson, it’s perhaps the most fascinating state in the nation. It’s vast without being empty, associated with powerful American symbols like cowboy boots and pickup trucks and high school football, carries more than half our border with Mexico, has at least a claim on the nation’s best barbecue (not to mention all that Tex-Mex), and has a long, complicated and fascinating history. It’s at once as American as apple pie and as alien as another planet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Road Trip! But First, Saving Money as You Plan', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:41:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bae20b9c-0e3a-531a-8ada-e4792dba92e3', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bae20b9c-0e3a-531a-8ada-e4792dba92e3'}, {'abstract': 'Analyzing campaign stump speeches and preparing original versions.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/on-the-stump-examining-the-form-and-function-of-campaign-speeches/', 'snippet': 'Analyzing campaign stump speeches and preparing original versions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | What is a stump speech, and what makes one effective? In this lesson, students analyze the stump speeches of presidential candidates, then write the stump speech they would use if they were running for president. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Stump: Examining the Form and Function of Campaign Speeches', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:42:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Kavanagh and Holly Epstein Ojalvo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kavanagh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Holly', 'middlename': 'Epstein', 'lastname': 'Ojalvo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73eade6f-e0e8-59ce-9a51-4d597b93cdb7', 'word_count': 1437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73eade6f-e0e8-59ce-9a51-4d597b93cdb7'}, {'abstract': 'The new racer will be campaigned in the 2013 season, that automaker said.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/nascar-and-ford-unveil-fusion-sprint-cup-car/', 'snippet': 'The new racer will be campaigned in the 2013 season, that automaker said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wearing the automaker’s new corporate face, the Ford Fusion Nascar Sprint Cup racecar was unveiled at a news conference by Ford and Nascar Tuesday afternoon at Charlotte Motor Speedway. The car will be campaigned in 2013, making its race debut at the Daytona 500 in February of next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nascar and Ford Unveil Fusion Sprint Cup Car', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nascar Sprint Cup Series', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Stock Car Auto Racing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:44:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69cfee62-e7a2-515b-9daf-6f267d1d28d0', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69cfee62-e7a2-515b-9daf-6f267d1d28d0'}, {'abstract': 'In answering a question on rape and abortion, the former senator from Pennsylvania has a Michael Dukakis moment.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/rick-santorums-adventures-on-the-loony-right/', 'snippet': 'In answering a question on rape and abortion, the former senator from Pennsylvania has a Michael Dukakis moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are moments in a political campaign when a sharply aimed question can reveal a great deal about the one thing that candidates most want to hide – their character.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rick Santorum’s Adventures on the Loony Right', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:45:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9318098-ae9f-5265-8763-63e518d1f9b0', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9318098-ae9f-5265-8763-63e518d1f9b0'}, {'abstract': 'Students: What do you think about the president’s election-year State of the Union address and the Republican rebuttal?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/whats-your-response-to-obamas-third-state-of-the-union-address/', 'snippet': 'Students: What do you think about the president’s election-year State of the Union address and the Republican rebuttal?', 'lead_paragraph': '10:55 p.m. | Updated The president of the United States gives an annual speech to Congress called the State of the Union address. President Obama’s third such speech was Tuesday night – and delivered it as his re-election campaign, and the Republican presidential nominating contest, are under way. Did you watch the speech? What did you think of his remarks, and of the Republican rebuttal?  ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Your Response to Obama’s Third State of the Union Address?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T19:50:14+0000', 'document_type': 'artic