nyt://article/787ef122-0be2-581e-af17-11bda3d29c40', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/787ef122-0be2-581e-af17-11bda3d29c40'}, {'abstract': 'Google will introduce new, shorter and more readable privacy policies and terms of service on March 1. The biggest change in the new policies goes to the heart of privacy concerns about Google’s new social search feature.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/google-to-update-its-privacy-policies-and-terms-of-service/', 'snippet': 'Google will introduce new, shorter and more readable privacy policies and terms of service on March 1. The biggest change in the new policies goes to the heart of privacy concerns about Google’s new social search feature.', 'lead_paragraph': ' 8:15 p.m. | Updated Google said Tuesday that it would revise its privacy policies and terms of service, to make them shorter and more readable and to change the way Google can use information that users provide. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/blogs/bitpix-google-logo2/bitpix-google-logo2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/12/10/blogs/bitpix-google-logo2/bitpix-google-logo2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/12/10/blogs/bitpix-google-logo2/bitpix-google-logo2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Google to Update Privacy Policy to Cover Wider Data Use', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T21:30:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47e2b934-e50e-5f30-8097-3d8a08078d08', 'word_count': 622, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47e2b934-e50e-5f30-8097-3d8a08078d08'}, {'abstract': 'The film editor Thelma Schoonmaker, up for her fourth Oscar, talks about her longtime collaboration with Martin Scorsese and the challenges posed by the 3D, digital “Hugo.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/for-hugos-editor-11-reasons-to-celebrate/', 'snippet': 'The film editor Thelma Schoonmaker, up for her fourth Oscar, talks about her longtime collaboration with Martin Scorsese and the challenges posed by the 3D, digital “Hugo.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Martin Scorsese goes into an editing room, what he likes to do, said Thelma Schoonmaker, his longtime editor, is just watch a little TV.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For ‘Hugo’s’ Editor, 11 Reasons to Celebrate', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beaton, Cecil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferretti, Dante', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powell, Sandy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schoonmaker, Thelma', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scorsese, Martin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': '