York Distilling Company in Williamsburg features impeccable drinks in a comfortable setting.', 'lead_paragraph': '79 Richardson Street (Leonard Street), Williamsburg, Brooklyn, (718) 878-3579, nydistilling.com/the-shanty', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/dining/25BRIEFSHANTY_SPAN/25BRIEFSHANTY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/dining/25BRIEFSHANTY_SPAN/25BRIEFSHANTY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/dining/25BRIEFSHANTY_SPAN/25BRIEFSHANTY_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/dining/25BRIEFSHANTY_SPAN/25BRIEFSHANTY_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/dining/25BRIEFSHANTY_SPAN/25BRIEFSHANTY_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Shanty', 'kicker': 'Dining Briefs | Bars', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Shanty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T21:43:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Dining & Wine', 'byline': {'original': 'By STEVEN STERN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'STERN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/19d107eb-e948-5007-9fd2-a46395c6fa5d', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19d107eb-e948-5007-9fd2-a46395c6fa5d'}, {'abstract': 'Cameron Diaz was having a private tour of the Givenchy spring couture collection, courtesy of Riccardo Tisci, when I popped in to see the clothes.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/givenchys-deco-punk/', 'snippet': 'Cameron Diaz was having a private tour of the Givenchy spring couture collection, courtesy of Riccardo Tisci, when I popped in to see the clothes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cameron Diaz was having a private tour of the Givenchy spring couture collection, courtesy of Riccardo Tisci, when I popped in to see the clothes. It was nearly nightfall. Some photographers were huddled under an awning in the Place Vendôme, trying to stay out of the rain that has drenched Paris. Mr. Tisci’s collection consisted of 10 outfits, most of which were displayed on suspended dress forms in three rooms, with gilt trim and creaky parquet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Givenchy’s Deco Punk', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mara, Rooney', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Givenchy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T21:45:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e344f896-f71e-5f08-aead-0905848ed3d3', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e344f896-f71e-5f08-aead-0905848ed3d3'}, {'abstract': 'This bar, an annex of the New York Distilling Company, is mostly about the gin.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/reviewing-the-shanty/', 'snippet': 'This bar, an annex of the New York Distilling Company, is mostly about the gin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Shanty, a new bar in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, that I reviewed this week, serves a whiskey cocktail they call the Lonesome Hero. It’s a terrific drink: an old-fashioned variant made with cherry liqueur and the Czech herbal bitters Becherovka. Yet ordering one feels a little bit like getting the salmon at Peter Luger. That’s because the Shanty – for the moment, at least – is mostly about the gin. The bar is an annex of the New York Distilling Company, which has been producing two types of gin since November. They’re not the only people to do the micro-distilling thing in the borough (there’s also the Kings County Distillery and Breuckelen Distilling in Sunset Park), but they’re the first with their own bar. The Shanty is clearly more than a gin joint, and no one will push you to order the company’s products. But after admiring their gorgeous German-made pot still through a window onto the distillery floor, it’s hard to choose something made elsewhere. This week, they have started distilling the rye that will be ready for bottling a year from now. They already have a great drink to use it in.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing the Shanty', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gin (Liquor)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T21:50:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Stern', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stern', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53b5ed85-939d-5639-8f5b-ce274324b32c', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53b5ed85-939d-5639-8f5b-ce274324b32c'}, {'abstract': 'Giambattista Valli’s second haute couture collection again showcased his considerable talents as a draper and festooner of evening wear.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/just-one-look-giambattista-valli-3/', 'snippet': 'Giambattista Valli’s second haute couture collection again showcased his considerable talents as a draper and festooner of evening wear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the Oscars become fashion’s talking point, actresses and presenters will be looking for glamorous, pretty gowns to get them through the night looking uncontroversially lovely. They could do little better than to turn to Giambattista Valli, whose second haute couture collection again showcased his considerable talents as a draper and festooner of evening wear. His strapless floral look — made of a beautiful devore-esque fabric — is simplicity and whimsy in a superluxurious stunner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Giambattista Valli', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T21:55:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_materi