ament because he was at the Barrett-Jackson automobile auction, bidding on the General Lee, the modified orange 1969 Dodge Charger that was the real star of the 1970s television show “The Dukes of Hazzard.”', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/watson-acquires-general-lee-his-dream-car/', 'snippet': 'Bubba Watson missed last week’s PGA tournament because he was at the Barrett-Jackson automobile auction, bidding on the General Lee, the modified orange 1969 Dodge Charger that was the real star of the 1970s television show “The Dukes of Hazzard.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN DIEGO — A scheduling conflict kept Bubba Watson from answering the call from President Clinton to play in last week’s Humana Challenge outside Palm Desert. Clinton, with his deep-fried Southern roots, might have given Watson his blessing if he had known how Watson spent the weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watson Acquires General Lee, His Dream Car', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Bubba', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T22:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6562f654-4180-58d8-a461-eb43d37072eb', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6562f654-4180-58d8-a461-eb43d37072eb'}, {'abstract': 'For better or worse, the taboo against Prussian militarism has lost enough of its sting for Germany to permit itself a yearlong, all-out celebration of Frederick the Great.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/world/europe/germany-marks-frederick-the-great-300th-birthday.html', 'snippet': 'For better or worse, the taboo against Prussian militarism has lost enough of its sting for Germany to permit itself a yearlong, all-out celebration of Frederick the Great.', 'lead_paragraph': 'POTSDAM, Germany — The official delegation honoring Frederick the Great’s 300th birthday had just finished laying a laurel wreath and a grand cross of white flowers at his grave here on Tuesday when a 70-year-old retiree quietly slipped in behind them and placed a small potato on the gray slab of stone that marks the monarch’s resting place.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany Permits Itself to Celebrate Prussian King', 'kicker': 'Potsdam Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany Permits Itself To Celebrate Prussian King', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frederick II, King of Prussia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'German