t to marvel at, which is, after all, the root meaning of the word “admire.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/HOW/HOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/HOW/HOW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/HOW/HOW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/HOW/HOW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/HOW/HOW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marveling at a Maestro of Glass, Steel and Light', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marveling at a Maestro of Glass, Steel and Light', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foster, Norman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T22:31:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5027ca81-0857-5403-816e-83325a18b7e1', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5027ca81-0857-5403-816e-83325a18b7e1'}, {'abstract': 'A long-gone Brooklyn high school taught Mr. Paterno to blend a passion for sports into a love of learning.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/where-the-best-defense-for-paterno-was-a-jesuit-prep-school/', 'snippet': 'A long-gone Brooklyn high school taught Mr. Paterno to blend a passion for sports into a love of learning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Jesuit high school Joe Paterno attended in Brooklyn, students wore jackets and ties and were taught by priests or by lay teachers in academic robes. The curriculum was also rigorously Old World: students took several years of Latin and many added three years of Greek, with three hours of homework per night the rule. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Brooklyn Prep, Paterno Learned Latin and Bravado', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterno, Joe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T22:31:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Berger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2caa9402-748a-5465-b8f9-1ab97c941486', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2caa9402-748a-5465-b8f9-1ab97c941486'}, {'abstract': 'The position has been advocated for years by restrictionist and conservative groups, and is central to tough anti-immigration laws passed in Arizona, Alabama and South Carolina, among other states.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/romneys-plan-for-self-deportation-has-conservative-support/', 'snippet': 'The position has been advocated for years by restrictionist and conservative groups, and is central to tough anti-immigration laws passed in Arizona, Alabama and South Carolina, among other states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mitt Romney said in the Republican debate on Monday night that he favored “self-deportation” as a solution to illegal immigration, it seemed to come out of the blue, perhaps an effort, as the race moves to Florida, to soften the hard line he has staked out on immigration. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Plan for ‘Self-Deportation’ Has Conservative Support', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T22:37:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3e07686-6676-5e0e-aa25-47e9531f193a', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3e07686-6676-5e0e-aa25-47e9531f193a'}, {'abstract': 'The debate, which was considered part of the “Rock Center” news magazine, had the second-highest total number of viewers — 7.4 million — from 9 p.m. to 10:30 p.m.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/g-o-p-debate-on-nbc-drew-over-7-million-viewers/', 'snippet': 'The debate, which was considered part of the “Rock Center” news magazine, had the second-highest total number of viewers — 7.4 million — from 9 p.m. to 10:30 p.m.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican debate on NBC on Monday night attracted the second-highest number of viewers of any debate in the current presidential election season, a little over seven million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Debate on NBC Drew Over 7 Million Viewers', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Universal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T22:39:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9b15eda-7ca2-5d07-abe2-47f0f01bf38f', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9b15eda-7ca2-5d07-abe2-47f0f01bf38f'}, {'abstract': 'The ad buy comes less than 24 hours after the group, Winning Our Future, received a pledge from a wealthy benefactor to donate $5 million.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/pro-gingrich-super-pac-to-spend-6-million-on-florida-ads/', 'snippet': 'The ad buy comes less than 24 hours after the group, Winning Our Future, received a pledge from a wealthy benefactor to donate $5 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A “super PAC” supporting Newt Gingrich said Tuesday that it was putting $6 million behind a new advertisement in Florida, giving the spots a major