e Web on Tuesday. Find more Scuttlebot items here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Steve Jobs’s Photo Plan, Piracy and Public Outrage', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T22:44:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91c0ac6b-823e-5ec5-88c3-49eeceb53f62', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91c0ac6b-823e-5ec5-88c3-49eeceb53f62'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook has begun to roll out the mandatory upgrade to a new profile layout called Timeline — and already some users are in a huff about the changes.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/facebook-readies-timeline-takeover/', 'snippet': 'Facebook has begun to roll out the mandatory upgrade to a new profile layout called Timeline — and already some users are in a huff about the changes.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Facebook announced on Tuesday that it would begin the global rollout of Timeline, a profile-page makeover that displays a user’s entire history of photos, links and other things shared on Facebook in chronological order, making them accessible with a single click. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook Readies Timeline Takeover', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T22:54:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9de84e52-8ff7-5586-9acc-db4f95c0a082', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9de84e52-8ff7-5586-9acc-db4f95c0a082'}, {'abstract': 'Bret McKenzie, Jonah Hill and Rooney Mara share their reactions to being nominated.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/the-first-times-surreal-for-muppet-man-or-dragon-tattoo-girl/', 'snippet': 'Bret McKenzie, Jonah Hill and Rooney Mara share their reactions to being nominated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We heard from a few more nominees today, including three first-timers: Bret McKenzie, Jonah Hill and Rooney Mara.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The First Time’s Surreal, for Muppet, Man or Dragon Tattoo Girl', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Carlinhos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Jonah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malick, Terrence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mara, Rooney', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKenzie, Bret', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Bennett', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitt, Brad', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorkin, Aaron', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zaillian, Steven', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Zealand', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T22:55:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik and Paula Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b471270-06bc-5c4b-9b27-355de93b6638', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b471270-06bc-5c4b-9b27-355de93b6638'}, {'abstract': 'Evidence of the private equity industry’s ability to create value is surprisingly uncertain, the Deal Professor says, but some university researchers found that acquisitions did benefit some companies.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/amid-attacks-on-private-equity-efforts-to-study-its-value/', 'snippet': 'Evidence of the private equity industry’s ability to create value is surprisingly uncertain, the Deal Professor says, but some university researchers found that acquisitions did benefit some companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Controversy swirls around private equity as attacks on Mitt Romney and the entire industry mount. Amid the name-calling, little in the way of evidence has been cited. So let’s take a look at some of the best research on this issue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Attacks on Private Equity, Efforts to Study Its Value', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T22:59:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Davidoff Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Davidoff', 'lastname': 'Solomon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/728237ee-b7fe-5291-9bf2-880c45c37a7c', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/728237ee-b7fe-5291-9bf2-880c45c37a7c'}, {'abstract': 'Marc Cenedella, a Republican businessman considering a campaign, said he did not know the authors of the posts on women, sex and drugs that appeared on a site he published.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/senate-hopeful-says-he-takes-full-responsibility-for-blog-posts/', 'snippet': 'Marc Cenedella, a Republican businessman considering a campaign, said he did not know the authors of the posts on women, sex and drugs that appeared on a site he published.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marc Cenedella, a Republican businessman laying the groundwork for a possible run for a United States Senate seat in New York, said on Tuesday that he took “full responsibility” for blog posts about sex, women and drugs that have drawn criticism.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Hopeful Says He Takes ‘Full Responsibility’ for Blog Posts', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cenedella, Marc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillibrand, Kirsten E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TheLadders.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T22:59:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raymond Hernandez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raymond', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hernandez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f4dc032-000e-5b62-ae66-31e6be2bf920', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f4dc032-000e-5b62-ae66-31e6be2bf920'}, {'abstract': 'In excerpts released early Tuesday evening, President Obama calls for “an economy built to last” and “responsibility from everybody.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/excerpts-from-the-state-of-the-union/', 'snippet': 'In excerpts released early Tuesday evening, President Obama calls for “an economy built to last” and “responsibility from everybody.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'As in years past, the Obama administration released excerpts of President Obama’s State of the Union address several hours before the start of the speech:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Excerpts From the State of the Union Address', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T23:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aac6f0ac-673e-5a77-a587-6934fae2db87', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aac6f0ac-673e-5a77-a587-6934fae2db87'}, {'abstract': 'This list is even more unrealistic than the editorial board’s.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/readers-sotu-wish-list/', 'snippet': 'This list is even more unrealistic than the editorial board’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier today I posted the editorial board’s wish list for Barack Obama’s State of the Union speech. We included issues we find important, without regard to political wisdom. Readers then added to the list in the comments section and on Facebook, and made it even less realistic—with one commenter, for instance, calling on Mr. Obama to argue for Medicare for all in lieu of the hard-won Affordable Care Act. Dream on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers’ SotU Wish List', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T23:01:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d01e9069-f8f9-5129-b7f1-c50c552700c5', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d01e9069-f8f9-5129-b7f1-c50c552700c5'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Gates said he would bring cassava to Davos to underline a pitch for his foundation’s efforts to eradicate hunger in places where food is scarce and crops are often blighted.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/gates-to-pitch-his-charity-work-in-davos/', 'snippet': 'Bill Gates said he would bring cassava to Davos to underline a pitch for his foundation’s efforts to eradicate hunger in places where food is scarce and crops are often blighted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — Some people come to the World Economic Forum expecting caviar. Bill Gates said he would bring cassava.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gates to Pitch His Charity Work at Davos', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gates, Bill and Melinda, Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T23:03:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1643a51-06dc-53b4-b3be-c41518f0507e', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1643a51-06dc-53b4-b3be-c41518f0507e'}, {'abstract': 'Photographs from Bahrain, Iraq, Spain and India.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/pictures-of-the-day-bahrain-and-elsewhere-5/', 'snippet': 'Photographs from Bahrain, Iraq, Spain and India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photographs from Bahrain, Iraq, Spain and India.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Bahrain and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bahrain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T23:04:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7aa9262b-ced3-5c67-8259-bdeb2f6e3e0b', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7aa9262b-ced3-5c67-8259-bdeb2f6e3e0b'}, {'abstract': 'The model in a sexy, equestrian look at the Berluti men’s show in Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/look-of-the-moment-natalia-vodianova-2/', 'snippet': 'The model in a sexy, equestrian look at the Berluti men’s show in Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Look: Country Strong. An elegant topcoat and tall lace-up boots over white leggings — it’s a study in neutrals that verges on equestrian but leans most certainly toward sexy, too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look of The Moment | Natalia Vodianova', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T23:05:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bddc38a8-23e8-5cea-991d-001724a2d6c4', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bddc38a8-23e8-5cea-991d-001724a2d6c4'}, {'abstract': 'With an election year ahead, President Obama set forth a long list of domestic economic proposals, many of which centered on jobs and changing the tax code.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/us/politics/state-of-the-union-2012.html', 'snippet': 'With an election year ahead, President Obama set forth a long list of domestic economic proposals, many of which centered on jobs and changing the tax code.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama pledged on Tuesday night to use government power to balance the scale between America’s rich and the rest of the public, trying to present an election-year choice between continued leadership toward an economy “built to last” and what he called irresponsible policies of the past that caused an economic collapse.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Address, Obama Makes Pitch for Economic Fairness', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Sets Goal Of Economy Built For The Long Run', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T23:07:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c77010e4-2024-51f0-99d5-2e09ed9ac7af', 'word_count': 1416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c77010e4-2024-51f0-99d5-2e09ed9ac7af'}, {'abstract': 'Chucho Valdés, a custodian of Cuban music, is on tour in the United States with his band, Afro-Cuban Messengers, and the flicker of evangelism in that name is surely no mistake.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/arts/music/chucho-valdes-plays-with-the-afro-cuban-messengers.html', 'snippet': 'Chucho Valdés, a custodian of Cuban music, is on tour in the United States with his band, Afro-Cuban Messengers, and the flicker of evangelism in that name is surely no mistake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During his final few moments onstage at Carnegie Hall on Saturday night, Chucho Valdés stopped playing, midphrase, to issue an instructive edict. He was well into his second encore then, alone at the piano, teasing out a Gershwin medley that had whimsically morphed into the Cuban standard “El Manisero.” The audience, elated, started clapping four beats to a bar. Immediately, his hands lifted from the keyboard to clap a son clave: one, two, three, one-two. He transferred this pattern to the keyboard, implying that the crowd was to follow his lead. Moments later, he was up and gone.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/valdes-1/valdes-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 729, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/valdes-1/valdes-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/valdes-1/valdes-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dignitary of Cuban Jazz Holds Court in Carnegie Hall', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dignitary of Cuban Jazz Holds Court in Carnegie Hall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Valdes, Chucho', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T23:07:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2b1859a-83e0-5d6e-b956-ff0bcdfbf37b', 'word_count': 674, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2b1859a-83e0-5d6e-b956-ff0bcdfbf37b'}, {'abstract': 'The Hamburg Symphony Orchestra performed “Des Canyons aux Étoiles” at Roulette on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/arts/music/hamburg-symphony-orchestra-at-roulette-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Hamburg Symphony Orchestra performed “Des Canyons aux Étoiles” at Roulette on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everything about Messiaen’s “Des Canyons aux Étoiles” (“From the Canyons to the Stars”) is vast. This audacious 100-minute work is scored for 44 individual instruments, including all manner of percussion, and features a formidable solo piano part. It was inspired by Messiaen’s 1972 visit to Bryce Canyon and Cedar Breaks in Utah, where he looked in awe at craggy rock formations and reddish-orange geological vistas. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/roulette/roulette-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/roulette/roulette-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/arts/roulette/roulette-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Formidable Piece by Messiaen, Inspired by Two Breathtaking Places', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Formidable Piece by Messiaen, Inspired by Two Breathtaking Places', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Messiaen, Olivier', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roulette', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T23:11:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba6c080c-67f1-56df-81cf-cd02e4cae16e', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba6c080c-67f1-56df-81cf-cd02e4cae16e'}, {'abstract': 'As the winter study of wolves and moose begins on Isle Royale in Lake Superior, scientists wonder what they will find and how much flight time the weather will allow.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/in-winter-weather-flying-to-find-wolves/', 'snippet': 'As the winter study of wolves and moose begins on Isle Royale in Lake Superior, scientists wonder what they will find and how much flight time the weather will allow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Vucetich, a wildlife ecologist from Michigan Technological University, leads the wolf-moose Winter Study at Isle Royale National Park.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Winter Weather, Flying to Find Wolves', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T23:11:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Vucetich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vucetich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06c791cd-c044-503d-ba07-5661a7d6446b', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06c791cd-c044-503d-ba07-5661a7d6446b'}, {'abstract': 'The mayor said that whoever decided to show the film had “exercised some terrible judgment.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/bloomberg-assails-showing-of-anti-muslim-film-to-police/', 'snippet': 'The mayor said that whoever decided to show the film had “exercised some terrible judgment.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY – Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg said Tuesday that whoever decided to show a film depicting American Muslims as extremists to nearly 1,500 city police officers “exercised some terrible judgment.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg Assails Showing of Anti-Muslim Film to  Police', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brennan Center for Justice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Academy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-24T23:15:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Eligon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eligon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af052a87-892d-56b5-8295-c5da6bf759fd', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af052a87-892d-56b5-8295-c5da6bf759fd'}, {'abstract': 'As a struggling Europe considers a sweeping new privacy law, Facebook’s chief operating officer, Sheryl Sandberg, calls for a friendly regulatory environment that promotes innovation.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/facebooks-sandberg-gently-warns-europe-about-privacy-rules/', 'snippet': 'As a struggling Europe considers a sweeping new privacy law, Facebook’s chief operating officer, Sheryl Sandberg, calls for a friendly regulatory environment that promotes innovation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Concerned about privacy? Maybe you should be concernedabout the economy instead. That was the subtext of a keynote speech by Sheryl Sandberg, Facebook’s chief operating officer, at a technology conference in the heart of Europe on Tuesday.', 'source