ype_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/33c13ad2-bec4-56e0-bda8-667196504a68', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33c13ad2-bec4-56e0-bda8-667196504a68'}, {'abstract': 'The Agnieszka Radwanska-Victoria Azarenka match was a textbook case of how aggressive play and offense beats risk-averse defense in big matches.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/azarenka-wears-down-radwanska-with-power-tennis/', 'snippet': 'The Agnieszka Radwanska-Victoria Azarenka match was a textbook case of how aggressive play and offense beats risk-averse defense in big matches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Agnieszka Radwanska-Victoria Azarenka match was a textbook case of how aggressive play and offense beats risk-averse defense in big matches. Although Radwanska took the first set, winning an error-filled tiebreaker 7-0 as Azarenka self-destructed, the rest of the match was a clinic in power tennis dominating a more conservative game plan. Azarenka began to take the ball early and move Radwanska mercilessly from side to side. The normally stingy Radwanska (she committed only 3 unforced errors in her fourth round win over Julia Gorges) began to crumble as Azarenka’s heavy groundstrokes found their mark. Radwanska made 31 unforced errors in the match, and gradually wore down under Azarenka’s constant pressure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Azarenka Wears Down Radwanska With Power Tennis', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T00:48:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By GEOFF MACDONALD', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MACDONALD', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '