n the Arab world. Overseas Chinese called for citizens to rise up in protest as well, but the small turnouts on the mainland were met with harsh measures by the police.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/is-it-poetry-subversion-or-both/', 'snippet': 'HONG KONG — A poem by the Chinese writer Zhu Yufu led to his indictment for subversion last week. Rendezvous now has an English translation of the piece, “It’s Time,” which was apparently written last year as rebellions were taking shape in the Ar...', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The poem seems to be to a call to arms, and maybe a call to feet. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It Poetry, Subversion or Both?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhu Yufu', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T02:06:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c5ec3f3-fb65-57d7-995b-8f1d98bc5fb0', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c5ec3f3-fb65-57d7-995b-8f1d98bc5fb0'}, {'abstract': 'Sylvia Brown moved her family to New York after a hip-hop producer promised two of her children recording careers that never materialized.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/nyregion/holding-on-to-music-dreams-despite-promoters-lies.html', 'snippet': 'Sylvia Brown moved her family to New York after a hip-hop producer promised two of her children recording careers that never materialized.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sylvia Brown knows the ending to the old saying: If something sounds too good to be true .... ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/nyregion/25NEEDIEST/25NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/nyregion/25NEEDIEST/25NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/nyregion/25NEEDIEST/25NEEDIEST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/nyregion/25NEEDIEST/25NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/nyregion/25NEEDIEST/25NEEDIEST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Family Holds On to Its Musical Dreams, Despite a Promoter’s Lies', 'kicker': 'The Neediest Cases', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Family Holds On to Its Musical Dreams, Despite a Promoter’s Lies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Catholic Charities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T02:08:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Farmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65c0808f-96f7-5546-9dc9-37dbfd6ea6d1', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65c0808f-96f7-5546-9dc9-37dbfd6ea6d1'}, {'abstract': 'The generals showed some sense in easing the dreaded state of emergency law. Now they need to go all the way and repeal it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/opinion/egypts-partial-step.html', 'snippet': 'The generals showed some sense in easing the dreaded state of emergency law. Now they need to go all the way and repeal it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Egypt’s military junta showed some political sense on Tuesday when it announced the easing of a longtime state of emergency law, a hated symbol of authoritarian rule under President Hosni Mubarak — and now. The generals clearly hope to placate activists who had planned new protests for Wednesday, the anniversary of the revolt that led to Mr. Mubarak’s ouster.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Partial Step', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt’s Partial Step', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T02:11:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Edito