resident used his State of the Union address to indirectly counter some of the fierce criticism he has received from Republicans over his decision to block construction of the 1,700-mile Keystone XL pipeline.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/obama-signals-expansion-of-oil-drilling/', 'snippet': 'The president used his State of the Union address to indirectly counter some of the fierce criticism he has received from Republicans over his decision to block construction of the 1,700-mile Keystone XL pipeline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The president used the address to indirectly counter some of the fierce criticism he has received from Republicans and oil industry officials over his decision last week to block construction of the 1,700-mile Keystone XL pipeline from oil formations in western Canada to refineries on the Gulf coast. President Obama did not mention the pipeline decision – which some Republicans have vowed to reverse – but he stressed the increase in oil and gas production over the past two years. He said that American oil production is the highest it has been in the past eight years and imports are lower than at any time in the past 16 years. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Signals Expansion of Oil Drilling', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T02:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. Broder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1aece84-63d2-5b27-8bd1-387daa029c1e', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1aece84-63d2-5b27-8bd1-387daa029c1e'}, {'abstract': 'The president and founder of Commercial Tenant Real Estate Representation and Healthcare Real Estate Advisors helps businesses find and set up commercial space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/realestate/commercial/the-30-minute-interview-marisa-manley.html', 'snippet': 'The president and founder of Commercial Tenant Real Estate Representation and Healthcare Real Estate Advisors helps businesses find and set up commercial space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ms. Manley is the president and founder of Commercial Tenant Real Estate Representation and Healthcare Real Estate Advisors. The companies, based in New York, help businesses find and set up commercial space. The businesses include the medical companies LabCorp, Quest and AmeriPath.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/business/Interview/Interview-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/business/Interview/Interview-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/business/Interview/Interview-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marisa Manley', 'kicker': 'Square Feet | The 30-Minute Interview', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marisa Manley', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T02:52:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Marino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None,