or maybe reruns of “The Big Bang Theory.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The State of the Union Address: And So It Begins', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T02:58:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfb5a05a-35a4-566c-a644-0d17e39bd85f', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfb5a05a-35a4-566c-a644-0d17e39bd85f'}, {'abstract': 'The publisher of The Atlanta Jewish Times resigned Tuesday after writing that Israel should consider assassinating President Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/us/georgia-publisher-quits-after-column-on-obama.html', 'snippet': 'The publisher of The Atlanta Jewish Times resigned Tuesday after writing that Israel should consider assassinating President Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The publisher of The Atlanta Jewish Times resigned Tuesday after writing that Israel should consider assassinating President Obama. Andrew B. Adler stepped down after an outcry over a recent column in which he suggested that the Israeli military might “take out a president deemed unfriendly to Israel.” Mr. Adler could not be reached but has apologized in other interviews. The Secret Service has said it is investigating the episode. On its Web site, the newspaper said it is seeking a successor for Mr. Adler, who is also the owner, and looks forward to trying to serve readers “more faithfully than ever in the future.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia: Publisher Quits After Column on Obama', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia: Publisher Quits After Column On Obama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T02:58:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robbie Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robbie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/29b687e7-d7fd-5d1d-bd90-8c982c801097', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29b687e7-d7fd-5d1d-bd90-8c982c801097'}, {'abstract': 'Exports fell slightly in the wake of last year’s devastating tsunami, tepid global demand and a punishingly strong yen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/business/global/rise-in-oil-imports-drives-a-rare-trade-deficit-in-japan.html', 'snippet': 'Exports fell slightly in the wake of last year’s devastating tsunami, tepid global demand and a punishingly strong yen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Japan reported its first annual trade deficit in 31 years last year, government data showed Wednesday, as fuel imports surged in the wake of its nuclear disaster at Fukushima.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rise in Oil Imports Drives a Rare Trade Deficit in Japan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rise in Oil Imports Drives a Rare Trade Deficit in Japan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yen (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T03:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec835102-c3bd-5131-abed-e15818f5b1d0', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec835102-c3bd-5131-abed-e15818f5b1d0'}, {'abstract': 'Gareth Bain puts a ring on it.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/24/forest/', 'snippet': 'Gareth Bain puts a ring on it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY’S PUZZLE — There’s a double trick to today’s puzzle, which pays off nicely at the central entry. “Indicators of age…” are TREE RINGS, the study of which is called dendrochronology and which is how one tells the age of a tree.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missing The Forest', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T03:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '