 Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eba3a26e-4781-59f4-be5e-53a0d5af51d7', 'word_count': 914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eba3a26e-4781-59f4-be5e-53a0d5af51d7'}, {'abstract': 'The United States is slowly recovering, but still struggling, and it is still in need of government action and strong political leadership.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/opinion/the-state-of-the-union-in-2012.html', 'snippet': 'The United States is slowly recovering, but still struggling, and it is still in need of government action and strong political leadership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago, after the last State of the Union address, we applauded President Obama for challenging the Republicans’ blame-government, slash-and-burn rhetoric. He explained why Washington must do more to help put millions of struggling people back to work and why any credible plan to wrestle down the deficit must include the wealthy paying a fairer share of taxes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The State of the Union in 2012', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The State of the Union in 2012', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics a