12-01-25T04:06:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8e5a64e-3ee2-5cf6-be21-39abd82fcdd8', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8e5a64e-3ee2-5cf6-be21-39abd82fcdd8'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 25, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/pageoneplus/corrections-january-25.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on January 25, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: January 25', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T04:11:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffdaba67-3613-5b4d-af4e-286f6985f63a', 'word_count': 634, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffdaba67-3613-5b4d-af4e-286f6985f63a'}, {'abstract': 'The Russian Jewish Congress said that it had sent a letter of protest over the decision to replace a memorial plaque to Jews killed in the Holocaust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/world/europe/russia-protest-by-jewish-group.html', 'snippet': 'The Russian Jewish Congress said that it had sent a letter of protest over the decision to replace a memorial plaque to Jews killed in the Holocaust.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Russian Jewish Congress announced on Tuesday that it had sent a letter of protest to regional officials over the decision to replace a memorial plaque to Jews killed in the Holocaust with one that mentions only “peaceful citizens of Rostov-on-Don and Soviet prisoners of war.” The plaque was in Zmiyevskaya Balka, near the southern city of Rostov-on-Don. Last November, officials removed a plaque hung in 2004, which read, “On the 11-12 of August 1942, Nazis killed more than 27,000 Jews here.” Where the old text refers to “the Holocaust,” the new one reads “mass killing by the fascists of captured Soviet citizens,” phraseology widely used during Soviet times, according to the Web site of the Russian Jewish Congress. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Protest by Jewish Group Over Memorial', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Protest by Jewish Group', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Russian Jewish Congress', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T04:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf4415cb-3912-5c48-8b4b-a3b374b6ff84', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf4415cb-3912-5c48-8b4b-a3b374b6ff84'}, {'abstract': 'A surge in high-tech start-ups and investment money has drawn recent college graduates who, unlike their peers in other parts of