d shoes walk differently from those who normally wear flats and may be at greater risk of strain injuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago, Neil J. Cronin, a postdoctoral researcher, and two of his colleagues at the Musculoskeletal Research Program at Griffith University in Queensland, Australia, were having coffee on the university’s campus when they noticed a young woman tottering past in high heels. “She looked quite uncomfortable and unstable,” Dr. Cronin says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Scientific Look at the Dangers of High Heels', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muscles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T05:01:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afde8753-04da-5118-9d4d-a2e8be4929c5', 'word_count': 922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afde8753-04da-5118-9d4d-a2e8be4929c5'}, {'abstract': 'The president used his State of the Union address to draw a bright economic line between himself and Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/us/politics/obama-sets-sights-on-romney-in-state-of-the-union.html', 'snippet': 'The president used his State of the Union address to draw a bright economic line between himself and Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGT