 that the Republican presidential candidate Mitt Romney was just following the tax laws.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/rubenstein-of-carlyle-defends-romneys-tax-rate/', 'snippet': 'At the World Economic Forum, David M. Rubenstein, co-founder of the Carlyle Group, said during a debate on the future of capitalism that the Republican presidential candidate Mitt Romney was just following the tax laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — It may be small comfort to the Republican presidential candidate Mitt Romney, but he received some moral support at the World Economic Forum on Wednesday from one of his compatriots in the private equity industry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rubenstein Defends Romney’s Tax Rate', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubenstein, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T12:41:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00d502f2-290f-575e-860e-ab47c663f3ad', 'word_count': 389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00d502f2-290f-575e-860e-ab47c663f3ad'}, {'abstract': 'It seems the Davos crowd gets a bit less hardy year to year. Participants who used to make a point of walking around town in chunky après-ski boots now opt for one of the many forms of motorized transport. There is even an electric-car shuttle service to transport conference-goers across the 100 or so meters that separate the registration area from the conference center.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/how-can-you-fix-the-global-economy-if-you-cant-brave-the-snow/', 'snippet': 'It seems the Davos crowd gets a bit less hardy year to year. Participants who used to make a point of walking around town in chunky après-ski boots now opt for one of the many forms of motorized transport. There is even an electric-car shuttle ser...', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s a little snow among friends?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Can You Fix the Global Economy if You Can’t Brave the Snow?', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T12:57:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb25e771-7665-5016-8ec7-d1fe0a28daeb', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb25e771-7665-5016-8ec7-d1fe0a28daeb'}, {'abstract': 'Jobs and jobs, not.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/mitch-daniels-doesnt-read-the-new-york-times/', 'snippet': 'Jobs and jobs, not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the Daniels reply to the State of Union:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitch Daniels Doesn’t Read the New York Times', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T12:58:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/279b340f-19d8-54a5-91b7-c0722ce30c97', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/279b340f-19d8-54a5-91b7-c0722ce30c97'}, {'abstract': 'In their Week 9 matchup, Eli Manning outplayed Tom Brady, and that was the difference in the game.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/giants-patriots-week-9-film-review/', 'snippet': 'In their Week 9 matchup, Eli Manning outplayed Tom Brady, and that was the difference in the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Benoit contributed weekly film analysis to The Fifth Down this season:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants-Patriots Week 9 Film Review', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T13:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization