ine': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T13:14:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc5e8281-effb-53e2-8cfb-450aeda51ee5', 'word_count': 2109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc5e8281-effb-53e2-8cfb-450aeda51ee5'}, {'abstract': 'A scientific look at the dangers of wearing high heels, the White House plans to propose a way to ease mortgage debt, Facebook will begin the rollout of Timeline, and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/wednesday-reading-a-scientific-look-at-the-dangers-of-high-heels/', 'snippet': 'A scientific look at the dangers of wearing high heels, the White House plans to propose a way to ease mortgage debt, Facebook will begin the rollout of Timeline, and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: A Scientific Look at the Dangers of High Heels', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T13:27:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2ef89a9-90d3-5b4c-bfbb-251118d796c1', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2ef89a9-90d3-5b4c-bfbb-251118d796c1'}, {'abstract': 'As if the world did not have enough to worry about, there are warnings that a solar superstorm could pose a threat to civilization. The message from scientists, after a radiation blast from the sun lit up skies above the poles: ‘Don’t panic!’', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/here-comes-the-sun/', 'snippet': 'As if the world did not have enough to worry about, there are warnings that a solar superstorm could pose a threat to civilization. The message from scientists, after a radiation blast from the sun lit up skies above the poles: ‘Don’t panic!’', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Solar storms: a potential threat to civilization as we know it, or just one more thing to worry about?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/blogs/solarstorm/solarstorm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/blogs/solarstorm/solarstorm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/blogs/solarstorm/solarstorm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Here Comes the Sun', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T13:32:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2d63695-2556-5a73-8137-169b7259c5da', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2d63695-2556-5a73-8137-169b7259c5da'}, {'abstract': 'Torrisi Italian Specialties has an unusual list of wines, but none are from Italy.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/italian-american-food-all-american-wine/', 'snippet': 'Torrisi Italian Specialties has an unusual list of wines, but none are from Italy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much has been written about Torrisi Italian Specialties, the terrific Italian-American restaurant on Mulberry Street, including Pete Wells’s review this week of the Torrisi spin-off, Parm. But almost none of the attention has focused on Torrisi’s unusual all-American wine list, which has grown from a half-dozen bottles when the restaurant opened two years ago to around 80 bottles now. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italian-American Food, All-American Wine', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T13:44:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2c5cdb1-c3ee-5763-96d0-6e33df4c55a2', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2c5cdb1-c3ee-5763-96d0-6e33df4c55a2'}, {'abstract': 'Russia’s Night Wolves motorcycle club puts on a children’s show that features the Snow Queen, the Statue of Liberty — and other menacing characters.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/a-putinesque-party/', 'snippet': 'Russia’s Night Wolves motorcycle club puts on a children’s show that features the Snow Queen, the Statue of Liberty — and other menacing characters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW— My 10-year-old daughter has just come home from a New Year’s celebration. These annual parties, which begin in mid-December and continue, relentlessly, through late January, are a longstanding Russian tradition in which children endure performances of various levels of vapidity, featuring Grandfather Frost and his granddaughter the Snowgirl. The kids are rewarded for their patience with a bag full of chocolate candy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Putinesque Party', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Russia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T13:48:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c95263f9-a722-55ca-881e-e22efaab2383', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c95263f9-a722-55ca-881e-e22efaab2383'}, {'abstract': 'Who’s first on Google’s Adwords and the Communist sportswriter who pushed for Jackie Robinson.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/the-breakfast-meeting-same-old-oscars-and-whos-missing-at-davos/', 'snippet': 'Who’s first on Google’s Adwords and the Communist sportswriter who pushed for Jackie Robinson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all the change whirling about the entertainment business (technological and other), the Oscar nominations announced Tuesday morning send an incongruous message: nothing has changed. Parsing the nine best picture nominees, Michael Cieply finds some recurring patterns: no animation (though, with “Hugo,” a 3-D movie was included); all but one from a major studio or a specialty division of same (“The Artist” is the exception); the settings are more past than present. He continues:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Same Old Oscars, and Who’s Missing at Davos?', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Rebekah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Jackie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scorsese, Martin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Depot Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Lowe's Companies Inc", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T13:50:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81e1d717-549d-5339-b3cc-166cef3658ab', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81e1d717-549d-5339-b3cc-166cef3658ab'}, {'abstract': 'Seattle and Arizona might be landing spots for Peyton Manning. The Jets? It seems highly unlikely.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/finding-a-place-for-peyton/', 'snippet': 'Seattle and Arizona might be landing spots for Peyton Manning. The Jets? It seems highly unlikely.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seems ever clearer that Peyton Manning will not play for the Colts next season. So where will he play if he decides not to retire?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding a Place for Peyton', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T13:51:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b48aefa-47da-5066-9d0c-483c89f2d4ce', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b48aefa-47da-5066-9d0c-483c89f2d4ce'}, {'abstract': 'Not every Super Bowl storyline is unimportant or misguided. Many, in fact, are significant and meaningful. But not on the seventh or eighth time around.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/top-10-super-bowl-story-lines-and-reasons-to-sigh/', 'snippet': 'Not every Super Bowl storyline is unimportant or misguided. Many, in fact, are significant and meaningful. But not on the seventh or eighth time around.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here are the Top 10 Super Bowl XLVI story lines that you may or may not get sick of in the next two weeks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top 10 Super Bowl Story Lines, and Reasons to Sigh', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T14:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Benoit', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Benoit', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bea9c43a-97ee-558f-b209-567d27d5ce0d', 'word_count': 1870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bea9c43a-97ee-558f-b209-567d27d5ce0d'}, {'abstract': 'Glenn Close received a nod for best actress, but more important to her, so did the makeup team that transformed her into the title character in “Albert Nobbs.”', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/glenn-close-already-thanking-her-makeup-team/', 'snippet': 'Glenn Close received a nod for best actress, but more important to her, so did the makeup team that transformed her into the title character in “Albert Nobbs.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Oscar attention that Glenn Close received on Tuesday for her passion project, “Albert Nobbs,” was really a triple win. Yes, she was nominated for best actress – her first recognition by the Academy in 23 years. (Although she’s been nominated five times before, she’s never won.) But her co-star Janet McTeer also got a nod, as best supporting actress. They sent congratulatory text messages to each other on Tuesday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Glenn Close, Already Thanking Her Makeup and Hair Team', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Close, Glenn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McTeer, Janet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T14:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4221d01-4fa4-5ae8-878e-4f56a397bf3f', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4221d01-4fa4-5ae8-878e-4f56a397bf3f'}, {'abstract': 'The model Karo Mrozkova transforms with makeup by Linda Contello and hair by Franco Gobbi.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/model-morphosis-karo-mrozkova-at-armani-prive/', 'snippet': 'The model Karo Mrozkova transforms with makeup by Linda Contello and hair by Franco Gobbi.', 'lead_paragr