n has filed a suit against Jay Leno, the “Tonight Show” host, for what he says are “racist” remarks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leno Sued Over Joke That Offended Sikhs', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sikhs and Sikhism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leno, Jay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golden Temple (Amritsar, India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T14:24:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cee34c8-50e8-5263-a451-f4bcfafe1a9e', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cee34c8-50e8-5263-a451-f4bcfafe1a9e'}, {'abstract': 'Should students be required to remain in school until age 18? That was the one concrete proposal for K-12 students in President Barack Obama\'s State of the Union speech on Tuesday night. The president, who focused his speech on "leveling the playing field" when it comes to taxes and economic policy, also had high praise for teachers and expressed his support for local authority in public education.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/25/obama-praises-teachers-calls-for-mandatory-attendance/', 'snippet': 'Should students be required to remain in school until age 18? That was the one concrete proposal for K-12 students in President Barack Obama\'s State of the Union speech on Tuesday night. The president, who focused his speech on "leveling the playi...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Praises Teachers and Calls for Mandatory Attendance', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T14:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARY ANN GIORDANO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Ann', 'lastname': 'GIORDANO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22c0f6bf-8ff9-5213-9efe-288def029a4e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22c0f6bf-8ff9-5213-9efe-288def029a4e'}, {'abstract': 'A new report from Environment California details which areas of the state have the most solar capacity.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/californias-lead-in-solar-is-slowly-eroding/', 'snippet': 'A new report from Environment California details which areas of the state have the most solar capacity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The growth of California’s local solar-power systems, not only on rooftops but in parking lots, farmers’ fields and vineyard irrigation ponds, has kept the state well ahead of others in the total power generated from photovoltaic systems.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California’s Lead in Solar Is Slowly Eroding', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 