ial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fa78383-88f9-571c-9d90-decbb2dae9ff', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fa78383-88f9-571c-9d90-decbb2dae9ff'}, {'abstract': 'The newest version of Google’s Android software, codenamed “Ice Cream Sandwich,” got a major makeover, and the overall operating system has been expanded to run on both smartphones and tablets, which would theoretically attract more programmers to make apps for Android.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/android-ice-cream-sandwich/', 'snippet': 'The newest version of Google’s Android software, codenamed “Ice Cream Sandwich,” got a major makeover, and the overall operating system has been expanded to run on both smartphones and tablets, which would theoretically attract more programmers to...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new wave of smartphones and tablets will be introduced this year with “Ice Cream Sandwich,” the latest version of Google’s Android software. The mobile operating system has been expanded to run on both smartphones and tablets, but it remains unclear how it will fix the problem that plagues Android at its core: fragmentation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/24/technology/24bits-icecream/24bits-icecream-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can New Android Software Unify Android Devices?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T14:48:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81b6b444-59dd-5ff9-9313-b3ff1a0bd4b7', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81b6b444-59dd-5ff9-9313-b3ff1a0bd4b7'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s Campaign Stops column.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/liberal-populism-and-2012/', 'snippet': 'This week’s Campaign Stops column.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s Campaign Stops column considers the president’s speech through the lens of the campaign to come:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liberal Populism and 2012', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T14:49:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f977dacc-4216-5079-85e5-693937dbb1c2', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f977dacc-4216-5079-85e5-693937dbb1c2'}, {'abstract': 'Indian politicians find a new way to milk the old outrage over Salman Rushdie and ‘‘The Satanic Verses.’’', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/rushdie-controversy-at-lit-festival/', 'snippet': 'Indian politicians find a new way to milk the old outrage over Salman Rushdie and ‘‘The Satanic Verses.’’', 'lead_paragraph': 'VARANASI, India — The current storm of censorship and intimidation over Salman Rushdie at the Jaipur Literature Festival is nothing more than a dodge by India’s politicians and Muslim leaders to cover their failure to improve the dreadful conditions in which many Indian Muslims live.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s Political Blasphemy', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_