/article/868a72cb-90ae-5647-a37b-82d8e62b04bd'}, {'abstract': 'The Adelsons’ multi-million dollar donations to a pro-Gingrich super PAC highlight the need for campaign finance reform.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/how-to-buy-friends-and-influence-politicians/', 'snippet': 'The Adelsons’ multi-million dollar donations to a pro-Gingrich super PAC highlight the need for campaign finance reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I almost feel bad for Sheldon and Miriam Adelson, who have contributed $10 million to the pro-Gingrich Winning Our Future super PAC. If it weren’t for the Supreme Court’s astonishingly wrongheaded Citizens United ruling, which among other things allows “independent” (hardly!) political committees to raise unlimited sums, the couple might have directed their millions to better use—like recapitalizing a casino or two.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Buy Friends and Influence Politicians', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adelson, Miriam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adelson, Sheldon G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Scott P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citizens United', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T14:52:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/151f543e-4a55-5b5c-ae23-0e40c32bcea9', 'word_count': 382, 'uri': 'nyt://article/151f543e-4a55-5b5c-ae23-0e40c32bcea9'}, {'abstract': 'At Givenchy, Riccardo Tisci was inspired by the cool glamour of Fritz Lang’s “Metropolis” and by early techno culture.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/just-one-look-givenchy-3/', 'snippet': 'At Givenchy, Riccardo Tisci was inspired by the cool glamour of Fritz Lang’s “Metropolis” and by early techno culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Givenchy, Riccardo Tisci was inspired by the cool glamour of Fritz Lang’s “Metropolis” and by early techno culture. The results were 10 long lean looks, encrusted with bugle beads, sequins and croc paillettes, that said red-carpet rebel, especially when finished with a jeweled nose ring (seen earlier this week at Givenchy men’s) and massive chandelier earrings. One exquisite example of why his influences were so cleverly paired: an Erté-worthy silhouette, fully embroidered on the bias, worn over a ribbed muscle tank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Givenchy', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T15:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c490f250-6588-565f-b6e4-7b33e0528014', 'word_count': 82, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c490f250-6588-565f-b6e4-7b33e0528014'}, {'abstract': 'At the World Economic Forum in Davos, the billionaire George Soros said policy makers should work on saving the rest of the euro bloc rather than focusing on Greece.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/soros-promotes-european-crisis-pla