00000001266466/tc.html', 'snippet': 'The story of Tiara Brown, a 23-year old female boxer who spends six hours per day in the gym and doesn’t plan to stop until she makes the Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The story of Tiara Brown, a 23-year old female boxer who spends six hours per day in the gym and doesn’t plan to stop until she makes the Olympics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/magazine/video-boxer-tiara/video-boxer-tiara-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/11/magazine/video-boxer-tiara/video-boxer-tiara-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/11/magazine/video-boxer-tiara/video-boxer-tiara-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/11/magazine/video-boxer-tiara/video-boxer-tiara-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bout Time: Tiara Brown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T15:31:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Sue Jaye Johnson and Matthew Orr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sue', 'middlename': 'Jaye', 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Orr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/3b823426-d4c3-5b85-b106-62202793f1ac', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/3b823426-d4c3-5b85-b106-62202793f1ac'}, {'abstract': 'This week brings “Born to Die,” Lana Del Rey’s major-label debut album, and by no means the first of her many lives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/arts/music/born-to-die-lana-del-reys-debut-album.html', 'snippet': 'This week brings “Born to Die,” Lana Del Rey’s major-label debut album, and by no means the first of her many lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT’S already difficult to remember Lana Del Rey, but let’s try. She was a meme of 2011, a singer who emerged seemingly fully formed from the ether who was in short order revealed to be, get this, a singer who was not always fully formed. That moll with the dangerous tastes in men and pastimes and the puffed-out lips and hair? That songwriter who used words like “velvet” and “exotic” in the tiki-lounge way of overemphasizing noir culture? Yep, it was a pose, cut from existing, densely patterned cloth. Just like all the other poses. And all the other cloths.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29DELREY1_SPAN/29DELREY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29DELREY1_SPAN/29DELREY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29DELREY1_SPAN/29DELREY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29DELREY1_SPAN/29DELREY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29DELREY1_SPAN/29DELREY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dissected Long Before Her Debut', 'kicker': 'Music', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dissected Long Before Her Debut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Del Rey, Lana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T15:33:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d494d685-fe54-5148-ba27-eac415006fe1', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d494d685-fe54-5148-ba27-eac415006fe1'}, {'abstract': 'The cost of production in France derailed the production for a few years, until a French tax credit changed the situation.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/midnight-in-paris-almost-didnt-happen-in-paris/', 'snippet': 'The cost of production in France derailed the production for a few years, until a French tax credit changed the situation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When she got the script for “Midnight in Paris,” Letty Aronson, Woody Allen’s longtime producer, wasn’t buying it. “When I first read the script, honestly, my impression was, who’s going to come to this movie?” said Ms. Aronson, who also happens to be the director’s sister. “Nobody even knows Gertrude Stein anymore.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Midnight in Paris’ Almost Didn’t Happen in Paris', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, WOODY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aronson, Letty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hemingway, Ernest', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Carla', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stein, Gertrude', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Owen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T15:33:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87040d9c-741e-56f6-a821-45a233aa6bc3', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87040d9c-741e-56f6-a821-45a233aa6bc3'}, {'abstract': 'But Mitt Romney did not mention Newt Gingrich in his speech.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/romney-calls-obama-detached-from-reality/', 'snippet': 'But Mitt Romney did not mention Newt Gingrich in his speech.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORLANDO, Fla. — Mitt Romney called President Obama “detached from reality” on Wednesday, accusing him of saying one thing during his State of the Union speech and doing another during his presidency.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Calls Obama ‘Detached From Reality’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pu