paragraph': 'For having sex with his freshman girlfriend when he was a senior in high school, Ken Thornsberry spent six years in a Michigan prison. Abigail Pesta of The Daily Beast reports on his story and on the growing number of parents outraged that older teenagers are being jailed, and added to sex offender registries, for having sex with younger teenagers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Sex Offender Is a Teenager in Love', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T16:06:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c054d3d-7c10-5848-994f-ae37ce31f7df', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c054d3d-7c10-5848-994f-ae37ce31f7df'}, {'abstract': 'A tussle over whether the euro will survive or not has divided this normally optimistic crowd. EMU — shorthand for the European Monetary Union — is now going to stand for “Even More Unemployment,” said Gerard Lyons, global chief economist at Standard Chartered, at a luncheon on the euro’s future.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/gloomy-debate-over-euro-darkens-davos/', 'snippet': 'A tussle over whether the euro will survive or not has divided this normally optimistic crowd. EMU — shorthand for the European Monetary Union — is now going to stand for “Even More Unemployment,” said Gerard Lyons, global chief economist at Stand...', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — For a usually optimistic crowd, there was a lot of gloom and doom being prophesied among the movers and shakers gathered here on the first day of the World Economic Forum. The subject of their angst: whether the euro zone will ever get out of its lingering troubles in one piece.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gloomy Debate over Euro Darkens Davos', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T16:09:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5d92347-aa26-5a8f-81cf-c3897a26d36d', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5d92347-aa26-5a8f-81cf-c3897a26d36d'}, {'abstract': 'What to do if you’re composing an e-mail in Gmail, but want to refer to an earlier message at the same time.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/tip-of-the-week-gmails-pop-out-feature/', 'snippet': 'What to do if you’re composing an e-mail in Gmail, but want to refer to an earlier message at the same time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Composing and replaying to Gmail