r revolution, on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tens of thousands of Egyptians gathered in Tahrir Square, the crucible of their revolution, on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/world/africa/20120126-EGYPT-slide-4KI1/20120126-EGYPT-slide-4KI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/world/africa/20120126-EGYPT-slide-4KI1/20120126-EGYPT-slide-4KI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/world/africa/20120126-EGYPT-slide-4KI1/20120126-EGYPT-slide-4KI1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anniversary of the Egyptian Uprising', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T16:25:57+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'World', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/93028b92-5ebd-5e3a-b2cc-04839c1dd14f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/93028b92-5ebd-5e3a-b2cc-04839c1dd14f'}, {'abstract': 'The announcements came year after year: Eight schools to shut down in Manhattan. Ten in the Bronx. Six in Brooklyn. Two in Queens. None on Staten Island. It was hard for Staten Islanders not to develop a degree of superiority when it came to school closings. But now a Staten Island school, P.S. 14, is on the list of 19 city schools to be closed. Some see it as a political decision to close a Staten Island school. And many say the school is facing daunting challenges in the poverty-related problems of its students.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/25/a-staten-island-school-blames-its-problems-on-location/', 'snippet': 'The announcements came year after year: Eight schools to shut down in Manhattan. Ten in the Bronx. Six in Brooklyn. Two in Queens. None on Staten Island. It was hard for Staten Islanders not to develop a degree of superiority when it came to schoo...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Staten Island School Blames Its Problems on Location', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T16:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By AMISHA PADNANI', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amisha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'PADNANI', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90cd9cb2-4ea4-5a84-9c74-ac02e81dcfad', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90cd9cb2-4ea4-5a84-9c74-ac02e81dcfad'}, {'abstract': 'If so, is it worth having to collect sales tax from states across the country?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/is-affiliate-marketing-a-useful-tool/', 'snippet': 'If so, is it worth having to collect sales tax from states across the country?', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ve just published an article that looks at how the new nexus tax laws affect affiliate marketing companies and the retailers that use their services. The nexus laws say, in essence, that any company advertising through an affiliate marketer — usually an online deal site or blog that publishes ads or coupons and collects commissions on sales that come through them — has to collect and remit sales tax in the states and jurisdictions where the affiliate marketer is located.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Affiliate Marketing a Useful Tool?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales and Excise Taxes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T16:40:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Mount', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mount', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcac3351-7fe9-5d48-ba71-9843687c26ad', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcac3351-7fe9-5d48-ba71-9843687c26ad'}, {'abstract': 'Interesting jobs and new ventures beat salary, study says.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/for-indias-mbas-money-does-not-come-first/', 'snippet': 'Interesting jobs and new ventures beat salary, study says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you were graduating from a topnotch business school, would you pick a great job profile or a tempting salary?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For India’s MBAs, Money Does Not Come First', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T16:47:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sruthi Gottipati', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sruthi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottipati', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f90f303d-fa4e-57eb-8f7f-f7daa7069736', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f90f303d-fa4e-57eb-8f7f-f7daa7069736'}, {'abstract': 'High-energy particles raining down around the polar regions generate intense auroras.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/on-our-radar-a-big-solar-storm/', 'snippet': 'High-energy particles raining down around the polar regions generate intense auroras.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The solar storm of the last few days was the largest since 2003, the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration says. Some aircraft flying over the North Pole were rerouted in anticipation of potential communication problems linked to proton radiation. [Discovery News]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: A Big Solar Storm', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T16:50:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45169840-eab0-5608-b113-16b23f4682f4', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45169840-eab0-5608-b113-16b23f4682f4'}, {'abstract': 'The sports club operator Town Sports International has switched to an annual fee, instead of monthly dues increases.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/sports-club-switches-to-annual-fee-in-lieu-of-monthly-increases/', 'snippet': 'The sports club operator Town Sports International has switched to an annual fee, instead of monthly dues increases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many members who last year joined fitness clubs owned by Town Sports International saw a $29 fee on their bill this month. The fee represents an annual rate lock payment, assessed in lieu of an increase in the members’ monthly dues, the company says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sports Club Switches to Annual Fee in Lieu of Monthly Increases', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Clubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Sports Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Town Sports International', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T16:51:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fd8533c-8cbd-5ab8-a93e-d3997ceae7e3', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fd8533c-8cbd-5ab8-a93e-d3997ceae7e3'}, {'abstract': 'Roger Federer and Rafael Nadal meet for the 27th time on Thursday (3:30 a.m. Eastern, ESPN2), in the semifinals of the Australian Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/federer-nadal-rivalry-adds-another-chapter/', 'snippet': 'Roger Federer and Rafael Nadal meet for the 27th time on Thursday (3:30 a.m. Eastern, ESPN2), in the semifinals of the Australian Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — The rivalry between Rafael Nadal and Roger Federer is now a fully formed, fully explored phenomenon, one that has put them on a first-name basis with much of the planet. They meet for the 27th time on Thursday (3:30 a.m. Eastern, ESPN2), in the semifinals of the Australian Open. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federer-Nadal Rivalry Adds Another Chapter', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T16:56:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By CHRISTOPHER CLAREY', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CLAREY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e41d159-fad1-5cde-b298-fd345f677fce', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e41d159-fad1-5cde-b298-fd345f677fce'}, {'abstract': 'There have been many attempts to replicate the experience of reading a real, tangible book on a screen. There is Google Books, of course, and this somewhat unconvincing page-flipping simulation. There is also Project Gutenberg, the vast online archive of public domain e-books, and, you know, the Kindle. But here’s the best version I’ve seen.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/new-books-for-the-old-internet/', 'snippet': 'There have been many attempts to replicate the experience of reading a real, tangible book on a screen. There is Google Books, of course, and this somewhat unconvincing page-flipping simulation. There is also Project Gutenberg, the vast online arc...', 'lead_paragraph': 'There have been many attempts to replicate the experience of reading a real, tangible book on a screen. There is Google Books, of course, and this somewhat unconvincing page-flipping simulation. There is also Project Gutenberg, the vast online archive of public domain e-books, and, you know, the Kindle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Books for the Old Internet', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T16:59:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Cwynar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cwynar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85fd01df-991a-5c93-9982-af87ef18320a', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85fd01df-991a-5c93-9982-af87ef18320a'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Christie says he wants voters to decide on gay marriage. That’s a punt, to say the least.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/marriage-equality-demagoguery-in-new-jersey/', 'snippet': 'Chris Christie says he wants voters to decide on gay marriage. That’s a punt, to say the least.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To borrow an old Washington joke about another self-promoting politician, the most dangerous place in politics is between Chris Christie and a TV crew. Most weeks, he clamors for national attention with rhetoric about small government (for the poor, that is, not the rich). This week, he’s taken up gay marriage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marriage Equality: Demagoguery in New Jersey', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T16:59:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6057ed54-03fa-5983-a265-96141b53d89f', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6057ed54-03fa-5983-a265-96141b53d89f'}, {'abstract': 'The writer-director of “Margin Call,” who was nominated for his screenplay, had quit filmmaking after a previous project fell apart. He was so superstitious about the new film working out that he didn’t tell his wife about it until he was getting ready to shoot.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/a-few-tears-on-oscar-nod-morning/', 'snippet': 'The writer-director of “Margin Call,” who was nominated for his screenplay, had quit filmmaking after a previous project fell apart. He was so superstitious about the new film working out that he didn’t tell his wife about it until he was getting ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like a producer of “Midnight in Paris,” the writer-director of the financial thriller “Margin Call,” J.C. Chandor, who received his first Oscar nomination on Tuesday for best original screenplay, also initially worried about finding an audience. “Our film has always suffered from the fact that it doesn’t sound that good on paper,” he said. “It’s not the most heartwarming, feel-good movie.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Few Tears on Oscar-Nod Morning', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'TriBeCa (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T17:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/045bc875-3a40-5746-bf74-b12370751eda', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/045bc875-3a40-5746-bf74-b12370751eda'}, {'abstract': 'It has been ten years since the good and the great came together to create the Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria. Many of them will feature in a new short film, and Bill Gates is expected to make an announcement connected to the anniversary at his news conference Thursday morning.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/luminaries-gather-virtually-to-mark-global-funds-10th-anniversary/', 'snippet': 'It has been ten years since the good and the great came together to create the Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria. Many of them will feature in a new short film, and Bill Gates is expected to make an announcement connected to the ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — One place where Davos luminaries will be gathering this year — at least virtually — is on the silver screen. To mark the 10th anniversary of the Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria, Fund supporters including Bill Gates, Bono, Tony Blair, Bill Clinton and Jeffrey Sachs will feature in a two-minute film that celebrates the Fund’s work, while calling for more efforts against the diseases that still kill millions of poor people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Luminaries Gather Virtually to Mark Global Fund’s 10th Anniversary', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Davos (Switzerland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T17:08:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5002a295-fc55-56b0-b814-4a61eb45a391', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5002a295-fc55-56b0-b814-4a61eb45a391'}, {'abstract': 'The cast and crew of the Luxury Collection Hotels and Resorts’s short film “Here,” divulged their check-in dos and don’ts.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/fete-accompli-here-to-stay/', 'snippet': 'The cast and crew of the Luxury Collection Hotels and Resorts’s short film “Here,” divulged their check-in dos and don’ts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fete Accompli | ‘Here’ to Stay', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 