stname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/227926f8-f29f-5c4f-aab0-95b9721c3f85', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/227926f8-f29f-5c4f-aab0-95b9721c3f85'}, {'abstract': 'Luxurious materials and leather were beautifully represented in belted calfskin coats, slim serge trousers, and suits in colors like ebony, licorice, plum and black.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/paris-top-5-hermes/', 'snippet': 'Luxurious materials and leather were beautifully represented in belted calfskin coats, slim serge trousers, and suits in colors like ebony, licorice, plum and black.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hermès collection, described as having a palette of “colorful blacks, dark harmonies,”\xa0was a quiet show that grew on me the more time I had to reflect on it. Luxurious materials, and leather — always a feature of the house and certainly a trend this show season — were beautifully represented in belted calfskin coats, slim serge trousers, and suits in colors like ebony, licorice, plum and black. Signature printed ties were noticeably absent, replaced with dark, solid neck wear and collared shirts buttoned all the way up. The look that stuck was simple but clever: a carbon-colored evening suit paired with a black crew-neck knit and a dark patterned scarf that came draped under the lapels (attached with a hidden zipper to keep it in place all evening long). It was a chic and sexy runway look — easy to envision on handsome young actors on red carpets everywhere.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paris Top 5 | Hermès', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T18:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b65414d-6a80-5a4d-871d-ea2d5338ebd7', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b65414d-6a80-5a4d-871d-ea2d5338ebd7'}, {'abstract': 'A Spanish-language radio ad run calling Mitt Romney “anti-immigrant” draws wide denunciations from Florida’s Hispanic leaders as Mr. Romney releases a spot accusing Newt Gingrich of offending Hispanics.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/gingrich-ad-faulting-romney-on-immigration-stirs-furor/', 'snippet': 'A Spanish-language radio ad run calling Mitt Romney “anti-immigrant” draws wide denunciations from Florida’s Hispanic leaders as Mr. Romney releases a spot accusing Newt Gingrich of offending Hispanics.', 'lead_paragraph': '2:17 p.m. | Updated Newt Gingrich faced a rising chorus of demands Wednesday that he pull a radio ad that calls Mitt Romney “anti-immigrant.” In a letter released by the Romney campaign, Hispanic leaders said the ad was “untrue, offensive and unbecoming a candidate for the Republican nomination for president.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Ad Faulting Romney on Immigration Stirs Furor', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martinez, Melquiades Rafael', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Herald', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Miami (Fla)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T18:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Mullany and Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mullany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2385811-25c1-56c8-a035-4d13f8bb3374', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2385811-25c1-56c8-a035-4d13f8bb3374'}, {'abstract': 'I know my 14-year-old doesn’t tell me everything, but we do talk, and if he thought for a minute I’d “narc” on his friends, he’d shut me out.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/why-i-dont-rat-out-my-sons-friends/', 'snippet': 'I know my 14-year-old doesn’t tell me everything, but we do talk, and if he thought for a minute I’d “narc” on his friends, he’d shut me out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let me say right off the bat: I have no interest in being the Narc Mom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why I Don’t Rat Out My Son’s Friends', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T18:01:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randye Hoder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randye', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6bbc84f-f5bd-57d2-bb21-745e494beb38', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6bbc84f-f5bd-57d2-bb21-745e494beb38'}, {'abstract': 'Thousands gather on the Egyptian uprising’s first anniversary | President Obama begins a three-day tour that includes battleground states.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000001311648/timescast--january-25-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Thousands gather on the Egyptian uprising’s first anniversary | President Obama begins a three-day tour that includes battleground states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thousands gather on the Egyptian uprising’s first anniversary | President Obama begins a three-day tour that includes battleground states.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/multimedia/video-tc--120125/video-tc--120125-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/multimedia/video-tc--120125/video-tc--120125-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/multimedia/video-tc--120125/video-tc--120125-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/multimedia/video-tc--120125/video-tc--120125-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | January 25, 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T18:07:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Zena Barakat, Kassie Bracken and Emily B. Hager', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barakat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kassie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bracken', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/2765a263-f9e4-5cb6-8d1e-561e122539f2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/2765a263-f9e4-5cb6-8d1e-561e122539f2'}, {'abstract': 'Leesa Evans, a costume designer for “Bridesmaids,” discusses her process.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/below-the-line-dressing-the-bridesmaids/', 'snippet': 'Leesa Evans, a costume designer for “Bridesmaids,” discusses her process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to costume designing, the Oscars tend to favor the past. In the same ways that dramas dominate the best picture category, period films are primarily the ones that get recognition in the costume design category. But costume design for contemporary films can present as many challenges as the ones involving corsets and long skirts. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Below the Line: Dressing the ‘Bridesmaids’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Bridesmaids (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Costumes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byrne, Rose', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Melissa', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rudolph, Maya', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiig, Kristen', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T18:09:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c36cb4dd-79bd-5a0e-a78f-773cc5673f60', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c36cb4dd-79bd-5a0e-a78f-773cc5673f60'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese officials know that the president must address his opponents’ claims that he has failed to stand up to Beijing, but that does not mean that they like it.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/how-obamas-tough-talk-plays-in-china/', 'snippet': 'Chinese officials know that the president must address his opponents’ claims that he has failed to stand up to Beijing, but that does not mean that they like it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — President Obama took a new swipe at China’s economic policies in his State of the Union speech on Tuesday, and leaders here are unlikely to be surprised. China’s rulers know that Mr. Obama faces a tough re-election battle, and they know that he must address his opponents’ repeated claims that he has failed to stand up to Beijing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Obama’s Tough Talk Plays in China', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T18:09:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ce22314-dddd-5a78-a34f-c373bd970889', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ce22314-dddd-5a78-a34f-c373bd970889'}, {'abstract': 'City Room is looking for the man whose intact leg was Photoshopped out of a city anti-obesity ad to make it look as if he’d lost it to diabetes.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/he-has-two-legs-but-what-about-his-name/', 'snippet': 'City Room is looking for the man whose intact leg was Photoshopped out of a city anti-obesity ad to make it look as if he’d lost it to diabetes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update, Jan. 29 | We found him, or, more accurately, he responded to us. He’s an actor named Cleo Berry who is not thrilled with the fictionalization of his body. Read the story.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'He Has Two Legs. But What About His Name?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T18:12:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1949e4e5-1ea5-5819-9a6d-d8f5b1fccfa7', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1949e4e5-1ea5-5819-9a6d-d8f5b1fccfa7'}, {'abstract': 'Minnesota and Colorado have powerful offenses but a weekend series puts the focus on goaltenders.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/with-split-at-colorado-college-minnesota-takes-conference-lead/', 'snippet': 'Minnesota and Colorado have powerful offenses but a weekend series puts the focus on goaltenders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throughout the college hockey season, Slap Shot will feature reports about some of the country’s top-ranked teams. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Split at Colorado College, Minnesota Takes Conference Lead', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colorado College', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T18:14:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Drew Claussen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Drew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Claussen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d02b5a8-2995-508f-a7b4-447a62419896', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d02b5a8-2995-508f-a7b4-447a62419896'}, {'abstract': 'A new multiracial production of “A Streetcar Named Desire” will play on Broadway at the Broadhurst Theater this spring.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/goodbye-rebecca-hello-stella-streetcar-will-open-on-broadway-this-spring/', 'snippet': 'A new multiracial production of “A Streetcar Named Desire” will play on Broadway at the Broadhurst Theater this spring.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The new multiracial production of Tennessee Williams’s “Streetcar Named Desire,” starring Blair Underwood, Nicole Ari Parker, Daphne Rubin-Vega and Wood Harris, will play the Broadhurst Theater this spring, according to a spokesman for the production. No performance dates were announced. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goodbye Rebecca, Hello Stella: ‘Streetcar’ Will Open on Broadway This Spring', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byrd, Stephen C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Nicole Ari', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Anika Noni', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Underwood, Blair', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Tennessee', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T18:19:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2254f3f1-3e0a-51f4-9bf4-4e0019ee6ef4', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2254f3f1-3e0a-51f4-9bf4-4e0019ee6ef4'}, {'abstract': 'The president sees Washington as the savior of American capitalism.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/the-essence-of-obamanomics/', 'snippet': 'The president sees Washington as the savior of American capitalism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even the liberal Matt Yglesias was exhausted by the president’s paean to industrial policy in last night’s speech, calling it “a strikingly retrograde, self-contradictory, and confused agenda of reviving American prosperity through mercantilism.” He goes on:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Essence of Obamanomics', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T18:24:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b0a7613-841b-5e30-a380-ebbf4ab0b517', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b0a7613-841b-5e30-a380-ebbf4ab0b517'}, {'abstract': 'Elie Saab’s haute couture show was as beaded and lacy as we have come to expect from this house.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/just-one-look-elie-saab-2/', 'snippet': 'Elie Saab’s haute couture show was as beaded and lacy as we have come to expect from this house.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elie Saab’s haute couture show, presented in the Grand Palais to an audience of Bollywood stars (Sonam Kapoor, gorgeous in kohl-lined eyes and a pale pink jeweled sari), Oscar hopefuls (Berenice Bejo) and clients from all the global wealthy pockets, was as beaded and lacy as we have come to expect from this house. The effect, for spring, was sweet, not sultry. Pastel dresses were entirely covered in tulle flowers, metallic embroideries and crystal beading. Since Saab is so well known for his red-carpet columns, it was refreshing to think about how his shorter offerings, all indisputably for evening, could fare on a big night. Consider, for example, an elegant little frock in white lace and pearls, so ridiculously pretty it registers angelic and wicked clever all at once.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Elie Saab', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T18:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sally Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sally', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c337e24-9b1b-5412-8a43-39d536cab628', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c337e24-9b1b-5412-8a43-39d536cab628'}, {'abstract': 'The Hornets have offered a contract extension to Eric Gordon, with the league’s approval.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/hornetsn-b-a-offer-gordon-contract-extension/', 'snippet': 'The Hornets have offered a contract extension to Eric Gordon, with the league’s approval.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a bit of a cliff-hanger, but the New Orleans Hornets, currently operated by the N.B.A., have arrived at a contract extension for guard Eric Gordon. According to Yahoo.com , the team is giving Gordon a four-year deal, after getting approval from the league.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hornets’ Gordon Offered Contract Extension', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T18:36:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By JOANNE C. GERSTNER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'GERSTNER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9acec35-985a-57e9-857e-4974a84b4d2c', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9acec35-985a-57e9-857e-4974a84b4d2c'}, {'abstract': 'Restore Our Future’s new ad asserts that Ronald Reagan, who died in 2004, did not return Newt Gingrich’s love.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/tv-ad-suggests-gingrich-exaggerates-his-ties-to-reagan/', 'snippet': 'Restore Our Future’s new ad asserts that Ronald Reagan, who died in 2004, did not return Newt Gingrich’s love.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new ad on behalf of Mitt Romney pokes fun at Newt Gingrich, and says he is exaggerating his relationship with Ronald Reagan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TV Ad Says Gingrich Exaggerates His Ties to Reagan', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'na