ain,” each topped Billboard charts this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/adele-racks-up-two-no-1s-this-week/', 'snippet': 'The album “21” from Adele, the neo-soul singer from Britain, and a single from that album, “Set Fire to the Rain,” each topped Billboard charts this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If anyone still doubted the commercial appeal of an old-fashioned soul singer who can channel raw emotion into song, Adele has put those doubts to rest. Not since 1993 has an album remained at No. 1 on the Billboard 200 chart for as long as  her album, “21” (XL/Columbia). That album finished its 17th week atop the sales chart since its release in the United States last February, selling 95,000 copies last week. That’s the best any album has done since “The Bodyguard” soundtrack, released in 1993, was on top for 20 weeks, Billboard reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adele Racks Up Two No.1’s This Week', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adele (Singer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarkson, Kelly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drake', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flo Rida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guetta, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Etta', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jessie J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keith, Toby', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minaj, Nicki', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Katy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rihanna', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young Jeezy', 'rank': 13, 