ving with hemophilia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/health/te_hemophilia/te_hemophilia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/25/health/te_hemophilia/te_hemophilia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/health/te_hemophilia/te_hemophilia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/25/health/te_hemophilia/te_hemophilia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/25/health/te_hemophilia/te_hemophilia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Patient Voices: Hemophilia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hemophilia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T20:19:56+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Health', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/4d07658e-2f0c-5219-b3b1-133593811c69', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/4d07658e-2f0c-5219-b3b1-133593811c69'}, {'abstract': 'Five people talk about life with bleeding disorders.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/the-voices-of-hemophilia/', 'snippet': 'Five people talk about life with bleeding disorders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hemophilia is a rare genetic condition in which the blood doesn’t clot normally. The disease primarily affects men, and patients with hemophilia take injections of a clotting factor to prevent or reduce bleeding episodes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Voices of Hemophilia', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T20:20:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Parker-Pope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker-Pope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2fb6961-224c-5c1d-a2d7-e530742b0bf5', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2fb6961-224c-5c1d-a2d7-e530742b0bf5'}, {'abstract': 'The Academy opts for electronic voting next year, a move that may have ramifications for the date of the ceremony.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/is-this-the-last-year-the-academy-votes-by-mail/', 'snippet': 'The Academy opts for electronic voting next year, a move that may have ramifications for the date of the ceremony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — It’s official: The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences is going to electronic voting for next year’s Oscars, with a system that will be developed by Everyone Counts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is This the Last Year the Academy Votes by Mail?', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T20:21:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'origina