 may wane in popularity because of the popularity of iMessage and other apps that let people send messages free. Is your phone bill showing an impact?', 'lead_paragraph': ' When Apple introduced iMessage, a service that lets people with its mobile devices send each other free text messages over data networks, many analysts predicted that it would take a substantial bite out of the profits that text messages generate for wireless carriers in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is iMessage Starting to Take a Bite Out of Standard Texting?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T21:24:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0788e3c-eeb3-591a-8d15-9dde8503133f', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0788e3c-eeb3-591a-8d15-9dde8503133f'}, {'abstract': 'Drug companies are finding lucrative foreign markets for their brand-name drugs after patents expire in the United States and unleash generic competition.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/despite-generic-rivals-branded-drugs-still-sell-well/', 'snippet': 'Drug companies are finding lucrative foreign markets for their brand-name drugs after patents expire in the United States and unleash generic competition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the loss of patent protection on a brand-n