ems. “6000 miles away,” a reference to Japan’s earthquake and tsunami last year, is being presented by the Joyce Theater Foundation. It consists of works by the choreographers Mats Ek, William Forsythe and Jiri Kylian. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sylvie Guillem to Make Rare New York Appearance', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guillem, Sylvie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater Foundation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sadler's Wells", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T22:15:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c4034ac-24cc-5bb4-8276-eab819d3f196', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c4034ac-24cc-5bb4-8276-eab819d3f196'}, {'abstract': 'A Quinnipiac poll of likely primary voters in Florida shows gains for Newt Gingrich over Mitt Romney after last Saturday’s primary in South Carolina.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/polls-before-and-after-south-carolina/', 'snippet': 'A Quinnipiac poll of likely primary voters in Florida shows gains for Newt Gingrich over Mitt Romney after last Saturday’s primary in South Carolina.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two Florida polls released on Wednesday offer a clearer snapshot of how Newt Gingrich’s upset victory in South Carolina is swaying the state’s likely primary voters, as Mr. Gingrich pulls even with Mitt Romney. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Polls: Before and After South Carolina', 'kick