: 'MURRAY, Ky. — The place to be on Monday nights in this Kentucky town is the wistfully named Big Apple Cafe. On a recent blustery evening, 71 people — a record, it was said — jammed into the back room to watch the Murray State radio play-by-play announcer Neal Bradley interview the university’s men’s basketball coach, Steve Prohm, for the weekly radio show “Hey Coach,” which can be heard across southwestern Kentucky.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/sports/y-jp-murray/y-jp-murray-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 705, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/sports/y-jp-murray/y-jp-murray-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/sports/y-jp-murray/y-jp-murray-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Murray State Is Small but Accustomed to Winning', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Kentucky Town, Winning Has Become a Habit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Murray State University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T22:21:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Weintraub', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weintraub', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None,