zine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/winter-wonders-day-break/', 'snippet': 'Alexa Chung, Elizabeth Olsen and Taylor Swift keep it casual in toggle coats and blazers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The casual end of the coat spectrum brings us woolens with hoodies and casual closures, like wooden toggles, zippers and snaps. Here, the singer Taylor Swift wears riding boots with a burgundy toggle coat in London; the television host Alexa Chung looks cozy in our favorite color combo, navy and black; and the actress Elizabeth Olsen sports a double-breasted schoolboy blazer, complete with gold buttons and crested pocket.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winter Wonders | Day Break', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T22:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7889a8f0-1080-55b9-870f-0db9e9448bab', 'word_count': 68, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7889a8f0-1080-55b9-870f-0db9e9448bab'}, {'abstract': 'Barcelona’s Dani Alves scored a stunning goal Wednesday in a Spanish Copa del Rey match.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/goal-of-the-year-so-far/', 'snippet': 'Barcelona’s Dani Alves scored a stunning goal Wednesday in a Spanish Copa del Rey match.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we write this, the match between Barcelona and Real Madrid at the Camp Nou, the second leg of their Copa del Rey series, is still in progress.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goal of the Year (So Far)?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alves, Dani', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barcelona (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Real Madrid (Basketball Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T22:32:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8edf17f-f7b3-5648-b7f5-c19f69ea75fe', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8edf17f-f7b3-5648-b7f5-c19f69ea75fe'}, {'abstract': 'Jan Kubis, the new United Nations representative to Afghanistan, urged Afghans to embrace a process in which all the elements of society would have a voice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/world/asia/new-un-envoy-to-afghanistan-urges-participation-in-peace-process.html', 'snippet': 'Jan Kubis, the new United Nations representative to Afghanistan, urged Afghans to embrace a process in which all the elements of society would have a voice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The new United Nations representative to Afghanistan urged Afghans on Wednesday to embrace an inclusive peace process in which all the elements of society would have a voice. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New U.N. Envoy Urges Afghans to Take Part in Peace Process', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New U.N. Envoy Urges Afghans to Take Part in Peace Process', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T22:33:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/835a44f8-eba8-5c7e-88da-456bad3ef46c', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/835a44f8-eba8-5c7e-88da-456bad3ef46c'}, {'abstract': 'Roger Federer and Rafael Nadal have a good rivalry going, and their match at the Australian Open should be a memorable one.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/previewing-federer-vs-nadal/', 'snippet': 'Roger Federer and Rafael Nadal have a good rivalry going, and their match at the Australian Open should be a memorable one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wednesday night’s Australian Open semifinal match from Melbourne between Roger Federer and Rafael Nadal has tennis fans across the globe giddy with anticipation. Their rivalry has elevated the level of play in men’s tennis, and it is a privilege to get to watch them play in such an important match. Federer has been playing sublime tennis, and, remarkably, has improved his game in the last year, especially his backhand and his net play. He knew that the book on how to play him involved attacking the Federer backhand until it broke down. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Previewing Federer Vs. Nadal', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T22:39:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By GEOFF MACDONALD', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MACDONALD', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cc9ad54-1098-5aae-ac9c-0a874055298b', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cc9ad54-1098-5aae-ac9c-0a874055298b'}, {'abstract': 'State University of New York trustees unanimously approved on Wednesday a resolution supporting a plan to offer state-sponsored tuition assistance, grants and scholarships to college-bound illegal immigrants who want to enroll in state schools.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/25/suny-trustees-support-tuition-aid-for-illegal-immigrants/', 'snippet': 'State University of New York trustees unanimously approved on Wednesday a resolution supporting a plan to offer state-sponsored tuition assistance, grants and scholarships to college-bound illegal immigrants who want to enroll in state schools.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'SUNY Trustees Support Tuition Aid for Illegal Immigrants', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T22:40:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By FERNANDA SANTOS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fernanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SANTOS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f11e2b78-2536-5579-8b10-866691fca935', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f11e2b78-2536-5579-8b10-866691fca935'}, {'abstract': 'Petula Clark performed the opening-night show of her engagement at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/arts/music/petula-clark-performs-at-feinsteins-at-loews-regency.html', 'snippet': 'Petula Clark performed the opening-night show of her engagement at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bright lights, big city. Youth and hope. A glittering wonderland of infinite possibility where “everything’s waiting for you.” That is a paradisiacal dream world of “Downtown,” held out like a bauble in Petula Clark’s signature hit that entered the charts in late 1964 and went to No. 1 early the next year. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/PETULA/PETULA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/PETULA/PETULA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/PETULA/PETULA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Generation’s Big Sister Pays a Visit to New York', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Generation’s Big Sister Pays a Visit to New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Petula', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T22:40:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/704d70d9-d325-5691-a923-247a601e1e00', 'word_count': 404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/704d70d9-d325-5691-a923-247a601e1e00'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Philharmonic gala at Avery Fisher Hall on Tuesday night included the pianist Lang Lang, the conductor Long Yu and a Mongolian children’s choir.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/arts/music/new-york-philharmonics-chinese-new-year-gala.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Philharmonic gala at Avery Fisher Hall on Tuesday night included the pianist Lang Lang, the conductor Long Yu and a Mongolian children’s choir.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That the New York Philharmonic would salute China with a glitzy affair like the Chinese New Year gala it hosted on Tuesday evening at Avery Fisher Hall should come as no surprise. For years now China has been cast as the next great frontier for Western classical music: a place of crowded conservatories, hungry audiences and, possibly, bulging coffers. The Philharmonic saw the effects of this bloom firsthand during its concert tour there in 2008.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/sub-new-1/sub-new-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 348, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/sub-new-1/sub-new-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/sub-new-1/sub-new-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lyricism of Chinese New Year', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Lyricism of Chinese New Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lang Lang', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yu, Long', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lunar New Year', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T22:40:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/31c53f9a-1d7c-5563-ad4b-b28f68bd0a51', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31c53f9a-1d7c-5563-ad4b-b28f68bd0a51'}, {'abstract': 'The David Dorfman Dance troupe is presenting Mr. Dorfman’s “Prophets of Funk” at the Joyce Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/arts/dance/ken-dorfmans-prophets-of-funk-at-the-joyce-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The David Dorfman Dance troupe is presenting Mr. Dorfman’s “Prophets of Funk” at the Joyce Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The oddest and possibly slyest aspect of David Dorfman’s “Prophets of Funk,” his tribute to Sly and the Family Stone, which opened at the Joyce Theater on Tuesday, is the role he plays himself. He’s the first dancer we meet: white, middle-aged, thick around the waist. Squatting and kicking to the groove in platform shoes, he’s more limber than you might expect, yet unavoidably comic. Mr. Dorfman knows this and makes the ridiculousness look intentional. The recorded applause isn’t for him, but he acts as if it were.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/dorfman/dorfman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 765, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/dorfman/dorfman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/dorfman/dorfman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tribute to an Artifact of ’60s Originality', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Tribute to an Artifact of ’60s Originality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dorfman, David, Dance Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dorfman, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T22:43:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/be1f746e-3398-52af-a69a-f27e46b16874', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be1f746e-3398-52af-a69a-f27e46b16874'}, {'abstract': 'Panama vs. U.S.: Pregame Notes and Quotes', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/panama-vs-u-s-pregame-notes-and-quotes/', 'snippet': 'Panama vs. U.S.: Pregame Notes and Quotes', 'lead_paragraph': 'PANAMA CITY — The road to the World Cup in Concacaf qualifying goes through Central America, and Wednesday night United States national team coach Jurgen Klinsmann got his first taste of what that means when the Yanks played Panama in Estadio Rommel Fernandez.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Panama vs. U.S.: Pregame Notes and Quotes', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinsmann, Jurgen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panama City (Panama)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T22:45:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Godfrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Godfrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a6f15f0-e865-57d2-a29a-e93bb9116806', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a6f15f0-e865-57d2-a29a-e93bb9116806'}, {'abstract': 'An academic who had no rhythm spent a sabbatical finding a way to learn to play the guitar.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/books/gary-marcus-professor-at-nyu-picks-up-a-guitar.html', 'snippet': 'An academic who had no rhythm spent a sabbatical finding a way to learn to play the guitar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 13, an age when most boys want to learn the guitar, Gary Marcus, decided he wanted to be a scientist. Twenty-five years later he had become one of the country’s best known cognitive psychologists, with major papers and three general-interest books on the workings of the human mind and a position running New York University’s Center for Language and Music. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption