nt': 1586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3114912f-e748-5fdc-8663-58fb00a17554'}, {'abstract': 'The silken-voiced leader of Antony and the Johnsons previews his elaborately staged show on Thursday at Radio City Music Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/antony-sees-the-light/', 'snippet': 'The silken-voiced leader of Antony and the Johnsons previews his elaborately staged show on Thursday at Radio City Music Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Critics like to describe Antony Hegarty, the silken-voiced leader of Antony and the Johnsons, as “otherworldly.” In recent years, the singer’s music has grown from pop, cabaret and soul signifiers to include characteristics of art song and sounds stranger still. Certainly, each of his acclaimed, prismatic albums seems to float in its own haunted universe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Antony Sees the Light', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T23:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan L. Fischer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Fischer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdc6979f-02c3-5544-91fa-51e4fbffe22e', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdc6979f-02c3-5544-91fa-51e4fbffe22e'}, {'abstract': 'After 18 years in business, the SoHo design emporium is shutting down its retail space on Greene Street.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/garden/moss-the-soho-design-emporium-is-closing.html', 'snippet': 'After 18 years in business, the SoHo design emporium is shutting down its retail space on Greene Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After 18 years in business, Moss, the SoHo design mecca, is shutting down its retail space on Greene Street, on Feb. 17.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moss, a Design Mecca, Is Closing', 'kicker': 'Currents | Closing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moss, a Design Mecca, Adapts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Moss (Retail Store)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T23:07:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfc14452-fd04-5902-ab6b-855201fa3eb2', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfc14452-fd04-5902-ab6b-855201fa3eb2'}, {'abstract': 'The American version of London’s annual Frieze Art Fair, which makes its debut in New York in May, it has commissioned eight artists to construct what is calls “a temporary pop-up village’’ on Randall’s Island, where the fair will take place.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/frieze-art-fair-new-york-announces-commissioned-art-projects/', 'snippet': 'The American version of London’s annual Frieze Art Fair, which makes its debut in New York in May, it has commissioned eight artists to construct what is calls “a temporary pop-up village’’ on Randall’s Island, where the fair will take place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American version of London’s annual Frieze Art Fair, which makes its debut in New York in May, wants to be more than just another place to see and buy contemporary art. Using its unusual and remote location – the 256-acre Randall’s Island, in the East River between East Harlem, the South Bronx and Astoria, Queens – it has commissioned eight artists to construct what is calls “a temporary pop-up village.’’ ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frieze Art Fair New York Announces Commissioned Art Projects', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frieze Art Fair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahearn, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moody, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rollins, Tim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Randalls Island (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T23:15:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c2de377-f228-51d0-aca3-55479d6ddd3b', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c2de377-f228-51d0-aca3-55479d6ddd3b'}, {'abstract': 'After being closed for almost a year, the South Street Seaport Museum reopens on Thursday with expanded gallery space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/arts/design/south-street-seaport-museum-reopens-after-a-makeover.html', 'snippet': 'After being closed for almost a year, the South Street Seaport Museum reopens on Thursday with expanded gallery space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Its historic ships still aren’t in any shape to hit the high seas. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge