t,” in which she accuses the Obama administration of turning a blind eye to illegal immigration because migrants will help Mr. Obama register more Democratic votes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Frosty Meeting for Obama and Arizona Governor', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brewer, Jan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T23:32:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77a25335-7335-5202-bd1e-4c5bfb6e0793', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77a25335-7335-5202-bd1e-4c5bfb6e0793'}, {'abstract': 'The most recent Oscar nominations reinforce the fact that many films that garner nominations had a near-miss path to the screen, built on serendipity, determination and, most often, leaps taken.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/movies/awardsseason/oscar-night-is-often-reached-via-unlikely-routes.html', 'snippet': 'The most recent Oscar nominations reinforce the fact that many films that garner nominations had a near-miss path to the screen, built on serendipity, determination and, most often, leaps taken.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When she got the script for “Midnight in Paris,” Letty Aronson, Woody Allen’s longtime producer, wasn’t buying it. “When I first read the script, honestly, my impression was: Who’s going to come to this movie?” Ms. Aronson said. “Nobody even knows Gertrude Stein anymore.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Ti