 Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e82c3509-c618-5815-bc3f-f1c0320ecf4c', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e82c3509-c618-5815-bc3f-f1c0320ecf4c'}, {'abstract': 'Standing three or four deep, observers in Penn State ski caps and other blue-and-white gear stood shoulder to shoulder along a route that wound past Beaver Stadium, the library bearing Joe Paterno’s name and the shops and downtown State College.', 'web_url': 'https://thequad.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/mourners-pay-tribute-to-paterno-during-funeral-procession/', 'snippet': 'Standing three or four deep, observers in Penn State ski caps and other blue-and-white gear stood shoulder to shoulder along a route that wound past Beaver Stadium, the library bearing Joe Paterno’s name and the shops and downtown State College.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STATE COLLEGE, Pa. — The blue Cadillac hearse carrying Joe Paterno made its way through streets lined with thousands of mourners who tossed flowers, took photographs or simply waved goodbye as his funeral procession rolled through the Penn State campus and downtown along College Avenue on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mourners Pay Tribute to Paterno During Funeral Procession', 'kicker': 'The Quad', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterno, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T23:53:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Viera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfd20a13-48d3-5f62-8cb2-762fd69cdc47', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfd20a13-48d3-5f62-8cb2-762fd69cdc47'}, {'abstract': 'The interior designer, who is starting the Dorothy Draper School of Decorating, on the ways people can improve the way they live.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/garden/carleton-varney-on-teaching-dorothy-drapers-design.html', 'snippet': 'The interior designer, who is starting the Dorothy Draper School of Decorating, on the ways people can improve the way they live.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The interior designer Carleton Varney is a man of many talents. He has designed furniture, lighting, dinnerware and linens; he has two lines of fabrics, as well as a CD (“Carleton Varney, Music With Style”); his client roster includes luminaries like former President Jimmy Carter and the late Joan Crawford; and he can often be seen hawking his wares on HSN, where he is never without his signature scarf-worn-as-tie (the scarf designs are his as well).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26QNA/26QNA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26QNA/26QNA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26QNA/26QNA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Attention, Class: Show-and-Tell Time With Carleton Varney', 'kicker': 'Currents | Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Attention, Class: Show-and-Tell Time With Carleton Varney', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Varney, Carleton', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T23:54:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/f79b8361-2971-57dc-b6ec-ae54af1f0b25', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f79b8361-2971-57dc-b6ec-ae54af1f0b25'}, {'abstract': 'Amazon offers companies a service that could potentially ease headaches around one of the less interesting, but critical and costly, parts of computing, data storage backup. It is probably a way to make companies comfortable with online computing, so they will do more interesting things with it later.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/amazon-aims-service-at-cloud-novices/', 'snippet': 'Amazon offers companies a service that could potentially ease headaches around one of the less interesting, but critical and costly, parts of computing, data storage backup. It is probably a way to make companies comfortable with online computing,...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Amazon just made life a little harder for old-line computer companies, by making a play for their data storage backup business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon Aims Service at Cloud Novices', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Storage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T23:55:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9ce88a7-2751-551d-aeda-393067b1c678', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9ce88a7-2751-551d-aeda-393067b1c678'}, {'abstract': 'A show at the 1stdibs gallery at the New York Design Center includes items for sale like painted furniture, a 1920s game wheel and a circa 1890 goat sculpture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/garden/folk-tales-opens-at-the-new-york-design-center.html', 'snippet': 'A show at the 1stdibs gallery at the New York Design Center includes items for sale like painted furniture, a 1920s game wheel and a circa 1890 goat sculpture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Susan Baerwald, a former Hollywood producer who now runs Just Folk, a gallery outside Santa Barbara, Calif., that she started with a fellow TV industry veteran, Marcy Carsey, said her first brush with American folk art was buying quilts. “They were a wonderful way to decorate an apartment in New York,” she said. “They took up a lot of wall space.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26SHOWS/26CURR4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 966, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name':