ashion stylist, creates upholstery fabrics with many of the same qualities as those found in haute couture, including hand-embroidery, hand-beading and “the idea of placement,” she said, where a print appears “in a very specific place” on a piece of furniture.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26CURR2/26CURR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26CURR2/26CURR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26CURR2/26CURR2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26CURR2/26CURR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26CURR2/26CURR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hand-Embroidered Flight of Fancy', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Hand-Embroidered Flight of Fancy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chairs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T23:58:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14bdc912-cbe3-50ec-9ba8-1bcb9785faff', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14bdc912-cbe3-50ec-9ba8-1bcb9785faff'}, {'abstract': 'A knife and fork that belonged to Adolf Hitler are listed among the objects in an exhibition planned by the New-York Historical Society. Some find the idea fascinating, while others see it as tasteless.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/stored-for-decades-hitlers-silver-will-go-on-display/', 'snippet': 'A knife and fork that belonged to Adolf Hitler are listed among the objects in an exhibition planned by the New-York Historical Society. Some find the idea fascinating, while others see it as tasteless.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 66 years, they lay unseen, first in a vault on the Upper West Side, more recently in a special cabinet. Now the New-York Historical Society plans to put them on public display alongside a silver cigar box, a silver ice cream dish and the silver controller handle that Mayor George B. McClellan Jr. used when he drove the first subway train, in 1904: A knife and fork with the initials A and H, for Adolf Hitler.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stored for Decades, Hitler’s Silver Is to Go on Display', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hitler, Adolf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New-York Historical Society', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-25T23:59:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'bylin