gn perfectionists live — some so fastidious that they have no furniture at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/20120126-DESIGNPERFECTION-slide-IR8J/20120126-DESIGNPERFECTION-slide-IR8J-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/20120126-DESIGNPERFECTION-slide-IR8J/20120126-DESIGNPERFECTION-slide-IR8J-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/20120126-DESIGNPERFECTION-slide-IR8J/20120126-DESIGNPERFECTION-slide-IR8J-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Design Perfectionists at Home', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T00:09:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Home & Garden', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/75e8ae92-fd79-5e6e-b8d2-ca5b7c352fa8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/75e8ae92-fd79-5e6e-b8d2-ca5b7c352fa8'}, {'abstract': 'Discounts on art and design books, furniture, glassware and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/garden/sales-at-phaidon-and-jensen-lewis.html', 'snippet': 'Discounts on art and design books, furniture, glassware and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hundreds of art, architecture, design and photography titles from Phaidon are up to 80 percent off during January, or while supplies last (the three-volume “Phaidon Design Classics,” regularly $175, is about $87); 83 Wooster Street (Spring Street), (212) 925-1900, phaidon.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26DEALS/26CURR5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 788, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26DEALS/26CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26DEALS/26CURR5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sales at Phaidon and Jensen-Lewis', 'kicker': 'Currents | Deals', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Art Books to Heart Designs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T00:09:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13ec6d98-eb3e-50dc-b0c6-81e5ffa94581', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13ec6d98-eb3e-50dc-b0c6-81e5ffa94581'}, {'abstract': 'Going to great lengths to stay in a childhood neighborhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/garden/thomas-r-pryor-one-foot-planted-firmly-in-the-nest.html', 'snippet': 'Going to great lengths to stay in a childhood neighborhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I LOVE Yorkville, the Manhattan neighborhood that my family has called home since 1896. During my childhood in the 1960s, it was my warren, and I burrowed joyously into and around it. There was Joe’s Candy Store, with the moodiest Italian bachelor in New York City, who served cold soda from his giant tub of frosty water. There was Parker’s Mom & Pop Grocery, starring sweet Murray Parker and his Elmer Fudd hat with earflaps that he wore year round on his bald head. And there was Prexy’s (“The hamburger with the college education”), Loftus Tavern (my father’s regular haunt) and the Cherokee Democratic Club (a double-wide brownstone on East 79th Street that I had the run of because my grandmother was Yorkville’s longtime district leader). ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26DOMESTIC1_SPAN/26JPDOMESTIC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26DOMESTIC1_SPAN/26JPDOMESTIC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26DOMESTIC1_SPAN/26JPDOMESTIC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26DOMESTIC1_SPAN/26JPDOMESTIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26DOMESTIC1_SPAN/26JPDOMESTIC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Foot Planted Firmly in the Nest', 'kicker': 'Domestic Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Foot Planted Firmly in the Nest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yorkville (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T00:09:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas R. Pryor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Pryor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fb5c9ee-81b8-5135-8919-19afc3adaad7', 'word_count': 1405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fb5c9ee-81b8-5135-8919-19afc3adaad7'}, {'abstract': 'The design perfectionist is a breed that outfits its habitat not according to style or fashion, but to a set of fastidious inner rules.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/garden/design-perfectionists-at-home.html', 'snippet': 'The design perfectionist is a breed that outfits its habitat not according to style or fashion, but to a set of fastidious inner rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TODD WATERBURY’S apartment is just perfect.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26PERFECT_SPAN/26PERFECT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26PERFECT_SPAN/26PERFECT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26PERFECT_SPAN/26PERFECT_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26PERFECT_SPAN/26PERFECT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/garden/26PERFECT_SPAN/26PERFECT_SPAN-thumb