ate': '2012-01-26T02:15:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Drew', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drew', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be0737de-2613-5f48-b660-f5d6709bcb28', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be0737de-2613-5f48-b660-f5d6709bcb28'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmakers explore the motivations, sorrows and dreams of the slain Ugandan gay rights activist David Kato.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/opinion/they-will-say-we-are-not-here.html', 'snippet': 'The filmmakers explore the motivations, sorrows and dreams of the slain Ugandan gay rights activist David Kato.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These are fragments of David Kato, glimpses of a Ugandan activist and friend who – one year ago today – was brutally murdered. These moments offer a perspective on the inner world that David shared with us, a world teeming with passion and relentless determination, good humor and vivid daydreams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/opinion/video-opdoc-kato/video-opdoc-kato-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/26/opinion/video-opdoc-kato/video-opdoc-kato-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/opinion/video-opdoc-kato/video-opdoc-kato-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/opinion/video-opdoc-kato/video-opdoc-kato-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/opinion/video-opdoc-kato/video-opdoc-kato-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/opinion/video-opdoc-kato/video-opdoc-kato-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/opinion/video-opdoc-kato/video-opdoc-kato-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'They Will Say We Are Not Here', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uganda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kato, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T02:15:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Fairfax Wright and Malika Zouhali-Worrall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': 'Fairfax', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Malika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zouhali-Worrall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a304c087-fc62-517b-9ae5-5352b52bf6df', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a304c087-fc62-517b-9ae5-5352b52bf6df'}, {'abstract': 'Laughter may be good for the soul, but sometimes stand-up comedy isn’t.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/funny-youre-so-sad/', 'snippet': 'Laughter may be good for the soul, but sometimes stand-up comedy isn’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The guy next to me had recently moved to Brooklyn from Cincinnati. When I asked him what he did in New York he said “comedy.” When I asked him what he did for money in New York he said “temping.” He and I both had little notebooks that we had written our jokes in. The relevant page in mine read “bidet, rats, Obama, Entourage.” I had spent months working on that page.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Funny, You’re So Sad', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T02:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Hill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f55c33b5-b95a-5c10-8001-37c86759716e', 'word_count': 1335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f55c33b5-b95a-5c10-8001-37c86759716e'}, {'abstract': 'The largest firefighters’ union told its members to ignore, as unconstitutional, an official order barring them from bringing opinionated material into their firehouses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/nyregion/union-assails-nyc-fire-dept-curb-on-posted-opinions.html', 'snippet': 'The largest firefighters’ union told its members to ignore, as unconstitutional, an official order barring them from bringing opinionated material into their firehouses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To New York City firefighters, who often put in 24-hour shifts, the firehouse can be a home away from home between emergency calls. It is where they cook meals, conduct training, lift weights and trade notes on the latest internal policy or city political imbroglio.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A City Order in Firehouses Draws Anger', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A City Order In Firehouses Draws Anger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uniformed Firefighters Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T02:40:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0eb0f974-cc66-5d64-a838-626342d8345b', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0eb0f974-cc66-5d64-a838-626342d8345b'}, {'abstract': 'A worker at the Ritz-Carlton New York said she had not been notified about the bug and was worried that she might inadvertently bring one home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/nyregion/bedbug-at-ritz-carlton-alarms-hotel-worker.html', 'snippet': 'A worker at the Ritz-Carlton New York said she had not been notified about the bug and was worried that she might inadvertently bring one home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A room for a midweek night starts at $695 and can soar up to $4,500 for a 