c0ae819-25e8-5624-9e8b-ebaee0bf432b'}, {'abstract': 'NBC News and NBC Sports have produced a series of 10 educational segments called, “Science of N.H.L. Hockey,” that will debut during NBC Sports Network’s coverage of the All-Star festivities this weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/nbc-brings-science-of-n-h-l-hockey-to-tvs-and-classrooms/', 'snippet': 'NBC News and NBC Sports have produced a series of 10 educational segments called, “Science of N.H.L. Hockey,” that will debut during NBC Sports Network’s coverage of the All-Star festivities this weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NBC News and NBC Sports have produced a series of 10 educational segments called “Science of N.H.L. Hockey” that will make their debut during the NBC Sports Network’s coverage of the All-Star festivities this weekend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC Brings ‘Science of N.H.L. Hockey’ to TVs and Classrooms', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Erik', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morrow, Brenden', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moulson, Matt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC Sports', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T02:50:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d89894f2-bdf0-5acb-87bd-3dd03a1821c6', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d89894f2-bdf0-5acb-87bd-3dd03a1821c6'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court was correct to rule that placing an electronic surveillance on a suspect’s car violates privacy rights, but it left too many questions unanswered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/opinion/gps-and-the-right-to-privacy.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court was correct to rule that placing an electronic surveillance on a suspect’s car violates privacy rights, but it left too many questions unanswered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court ruled unanimously on Monday that the police violated the Constitution when they hid a Global Positioning System tracking device on the car of Antoine Jones and monitored his movements for 28 days. It put law enforcement on notice that most GPS electronic surveillance will be suspect without a judge’s warrant.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'GPS and the Right to Privacy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'GPS and the Right to Privacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Antoine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T02:50:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/26058eee-e53a-502a-9a22-e62875a6f4e0', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26058eee-e53a-502a-9a22-e62875a6f4e0'}, {'abstract': 'A proposal to allow New York City to handle all but the most dangerous juvenile offenders is a good idea, but the city and state must make sure that the quality of service is high.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/opinion/better-care-for-troubled-youth.html', 'snippet': 'A proposal to allow New York City to handle all but the most dangerous juvenile offenders is a good idea, but the city and state must make sure that the quality of service is high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo has proposed allowing the New York City system, instead of the state system, to begin handling all but the most dangerous juvenile offenders. This is an excellent idea in principle, but the city and state must make sure that the quality of services is high and that a detailed plan is in place before they put this new policy into effect in the fall. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Better Care for Troubled Youth', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Better Care for Troubled Youth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Juvenile Delinquency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrion, Gladys', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Pri