as not his.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/nyregion/marky-ramone-says-leather-jacket-for-bid-wasnt-his.html', 'snippet': 'A black leather jacket said to be worn by the Ramones’ second drummer, Marky Ramone, has been withdrawn from an online auction because Mr. Ramone has said it was not his.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The online auction house offered a sweat-soaked gem from punk rock’s New York glory years — the black leather jacket worn by the Ramones’ second drummer, Marky Ramone, during his first stint with the band, from 1978 to 1983.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/nyregion/RAMONES1/RAMONES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ramone Says Jacket for Bid Is Just a Poser', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ramone Says Jacket for Bid Is Just a Poser', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramone, Marky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ramones', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T02:57:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aidan Gardiner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aidan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardiner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/972b1051-f8c6-54c5-9fa1-1c46ad9f3bb5', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/972b1051-f8c6-54c5-9fa1-1c46ad9f3bb5'}, {'abstract': 'Carmelo Anthony was 5 for 14 with 15 points as the Knicks committed 23 turnovers, which led to 24 Cavaliers points, and made only 42 percent of their shots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/sports/basketball/cavaliers-hand-knicks-7th-loss-in-8-games-91-81.html', 'snippet': 'Carmelo Anthony was 5 for 14 with 15 points as the Knicks committed 23 turnovers, which led to 24 Cavaliers points, and made only 42 percent of their shots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — With another humiliating loss bearing down, Carmelo Anthony worked to find a better shot, a way forward, a chance to change the Knicks’ fate. He looked to his All-Star frontcourt partner, Amar’e Stoudemire, waiting on the perimeter.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/sports/knicks/knicks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 835, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/sports/knicks/knicks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/sports/knicks/knicks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cavaliers Hand Knicks 7th Loss in 8 Games', 'kicker': 'Cavaliers 91, Knicks 81', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cavaliers Hand Knicks 7th Loss in 8 Games', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "Stoudemire, Amar'e", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "D'Antoni, Mike", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Cavaliers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T02:58:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cabc760-37ef-55b6-bce9-0940d4535e06', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cabc760-37ef-55b6-bce9-0940d4535e06'}, {'abstract': 'In a world of virtual noise, BMW fakes the roar of its engine with a digital recording in a red-hot 2013 model.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/opinion/warning-the-next-sound-you-hear-will-not-be-your-engine.html', 'snippet': 'In a world of virtual noise, BMW fakes the roar of its engine with a digital recording in a red-hot 2013 model.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you pay $100,000 for a red-hot BMW M5, you expect the twin-turbo V8 to emit a mighty song. Those who drive this superbrutal version of the midsize BMW are not generally in search of silence. And a nudge on the accelerator fills the cabin with a richly satisfying ascent from low rumble to high scream. But it’s a recording, a virtual roar.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Warning: The Next Sound You Hear Will Not Be Your Engine', 'kicker': 'Editorial Observer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Warning: The Next Sound You Hear Will Not Be Your Engine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T02:59:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Serge Schmemann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Serge', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmemann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac1d9e7b-47e3-5a5a-8ee0-3f4c7ecada3c', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac1d9e7b-47e3-5a5a-8ee0-3f4c7ecada3c'}, {'abstract': 'Russia’s only independent elections monitor, Golos, has been told to either find new office space or expect continual power failures from now until March 6, severely hampering the group’s ability to monitor the presidential election on March 4.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/world/europe/russia-election-monitor-group-golos-faces-threat-of-eviction.html', 'snippet': 'Russia’s only independent elections monitor, Golos, has been told to either find new office space or expect continual power failures from now until March 6, severely hampering the group’s ability to monitor the presidential election on March 4.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Russia’s only independent elections monitor has been told by its landlord to either find new office space or expect continual power failures from now until March 6, severely hampering the group’s ability to monitor the presidential election on March 4. The organization, Golos (whose name means “vote” in Russian), first came under attack nearly two months ago, as it prepared to send out 3,000 monitors to document any violations in parliamentary elections and created an interactive map for people to upload video and photographs of any election violations directly from their mobile phones. Lawmakers began calling for the group to be investigated, and state-controlled television broadcast a documentary suggesting that Golos, which receives most of its budget from Western governments, served American interests and aimed to incite an Arab Spring-type revolution in Russia. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Election Monitor Group Faces Threat of Eviction', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Election Monitor Group Faces Threat of Eviction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golos Associates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T03:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/21efe170-d2c6-5179-9b3e-564bcfa1a4e4', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21efe170-d2c6-5179-9b3e-564bcfa1a4e4'}, {'abstract': 'Making crossword puzzles is a start.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/25/paris/', 'snippet': 'Making crossword puzzles is a start.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — We haven’t seen Alan Arbesfeld since October, when he told us a very funny riddle about underwear (Across Lite, Solution, blog), but he’s back today with a letter addition theme that I thought was a bit easy for the “twist” I’ve come to expect from Thursday grids. Even so, I thought his theme was punny and enjoyable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stop Over in Paris', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T03:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2023b31-e1d6-57fc-a4d8-c2d96865fce2', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2023b31-e1d6-57fc-a4d8-c2d96865fce2'}, {'abstract': 'Pimps are turning to the Internet instead of street corners for the sex trafficking of minors. Just look at the case of this teenage girl in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/opinion/how-pimps-use-the-web-to-sell-girls.html', 'snippet': 'Pimps are turning to the Internet instead of street corners for the sex trafficking of minors. Just look at the case of this teenage girl in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In November, a terrified 13-year-old girl pounded on an apartment door in Brooklyn. When a surprised woman answered, the girl pleaded for a phone. She called her mother, and then dialed 911.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/nicholas-kristof/nicholas-kristof-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': No