tatistically, incidents of piracy off the East African coast have recently been in decline, a result of both an international naval counterpiracy presence in these waters and the wider use among merchant vessels of onboard armed security teams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Somali Pirate Gun Locker: An Oddball Assault Rifle, at Sea', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Eighties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Piracy at Sea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gulf of Oman', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T03:45:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5a1f4a7-4e7b-5156-b243-53a6734f0655', 'word_count': 1724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5a1f4a7-4e7b-5156-b243-53a6734f0655'}, {'abstract': 'A federal judge ordered the Oakland Police Department to consult with a court-appointed monitor before all major decisions, bringing the department one step closer to a federal takeover.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/us/oakland-police-ordered-to-consult-with-monitor-on-decisions.html', 'snippet': 'A federal judge ordered the Oakland Police Department to consult with a court-appointed monitor before all major decisions, bringing the department one step closer to a federal takeover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge on Tuesday ordered the Oakland Police Department to consult with a court-appointed monitor before all major decisions, bringing the department one step closer to a federal takeover. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Order in Oakland', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Order in Oakland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oakland (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henderson, Thelton E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T03:50:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c29e6832-90ba-50a4-82dd-942aeebf4ef0', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c29e6832-90ba-50a4-82dd-942aeebf4ef0'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers passed legislation that would bar unions from charging nonmembers for representation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/us/indiana-house-passes-right-to-work-bill.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers passed legislation that would bar unions from charging nonmembers for representation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Republican-held Indiana House of Representatives passed legislation on Wednesday barring union contracts from requiring nonunion members to pay fees for representation, ending weeks of partisan battling and all but assuring that the state will become the first in the Midwestern manufacturing belt deemed a “right to work” state. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indiana House Passes a Bill on Union Fees', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The House In Indiana Passes Curbs On Unions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', '