42f834ba83', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/035aeada-ca93-5a64-9cec-6942f834ba83'}, {'abstract': 'Brazil granted a tourist visa on Wednesday to Yoani Sánchez, a dissident Cuban author and blogger, had emerged as a test of Cuba’s restrictive travel policies and Brazil’s willingness to prod the nation on a prominent human rights issue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/world/americas/cuba-brazil-grants-visa-to-blogger.html', 'snippet': 'Brazil granted a tourist visa on Wednesday to Yoani Sánchez, a dissident Cuban author and blogger, had emerged as a test of Cuba’s restrictive travel policies and Brazil’s willingness to prod the nation on a prominent human rights issue.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Brazil granted a tourist visa on Wednesday to Yoani Sánchez, a dissident Cuban author and blogger, ahead of a trip to Cuba this month by Brazil’s president, Dilma Rousseff. The request by Ms. Sánchez to travel to Brazil for the screening of a documentary had emerged as a test of Cuba’s restrictive travel policies for its own citizens and Brazil’s willingness to prod a friendly government on a prominent human rights issue. Ms. Sánchez, 36, had appealed personally for the visa to Ms. Rousseff, a former member of an urban guerrilla cell, referring to a photograph made public in December that showed Ms. Rousseff as a young woman being questioned at a military hearing by men whose faces were covered. It remains to be seen whether Cuba will allow her to travel to Brazil. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuba: Brazil Grants Visa to Blogger', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuba: Brazil Grants Visa to Blogger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rousseff, Dilma', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value':