ades Into Issue of Raising Dropout Age', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Wades Into Issue Of Raising Dropout Age', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dropouts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduation Rates', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T04:27:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5f46fb2-74e5-5542-8ba5-93f3edd1be30', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5f46fb2-74e5-5542-8ba5-93f3edd1be30'}, {'abstract': 'The Palestinian president, Mahmoud Abbas, said he would leave open the possibility or resuming talks under certain conditions and after consultations with Arab League representatives on Feb. 4.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/world/middleeast/palestinians-and-israelis-dont-agree-on-new-talks.html', 'snippet': 'The Palestinian president, Mahmoud Abbas, said he would leave open the possibility or resuming talks under certain conditions and after consultations with Arab League representatives on Feb. 4.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RAMALLAH, West Bank — The Palestinian president, Mahmoud Abbas, said Wednesday that a round of exploratory discussions with Israel under Jordanian auspices had ended. But he left open the possibility of a resumption of contacts under certain conditions and after consultations with Arab League representatives on Feb. 4. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinians and Israelis Don’t Agree on New Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Palestinians And Israelis Don’t Agree On New Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABBAS, MAHMOUD', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T04:28:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c018ad27-60bc-58df-b91c-c5a46c4b30c5', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c018ad27-60bc-58df-b91c-c5a46c4b30c5'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Angelopoulos was a renowned director whose films explored the human condition in general and the condition of modern Greece in particular.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/movies/theo-angelopoulos-greek-film-director-dies-at-76.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Angelopoulos was a renowned director whose films explored the human condition in general and the condition of modern Greece in particular.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Theo Angelopoulos, a renowned director whose films explored the human condition in general and the condition of modern Greece in particular through haunting imagery rooted in myth and epic, died on Tuesday of injuries suffered in a traffic accident near Piraeus, Greece. He was 76.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/ANGELOPOULOS1-obit/ANGELOPOULOS1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 708, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/ANGELOPOULOS1-obit/ANGELOPOULOS1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/ANGELOPOULOS1-obit/ANGELOPOULOS1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Theo Angelopoulos, Greek Filmmaker, Dies at 76', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Theo Angelopoulos, Greek Filmmaker, 76', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANGELOPOULOS, THEO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T04:31:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/24c38329-e5cf-5237-9469-054691cf54e7', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24c38329-e5cf-5237-9469-054691cf54e7'}, {'abstract': 'The Foreign Ministry said that the move was meant to defend Venezuelan sovereignty and that the center was biased in favor of multinational corporations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/world/americas/venezuela-government-to-pull-out-of-nationalization-proceedings.html', 'snippet': 'The Foreign Ministry said that the move was meant to defend Venezuelan sovereignty and that the center was biased in favor of multinational corporations.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Venezuela said Wednesday that it had begun the process of pulling out of a World Bank arbitration forum that is considering about 20 cases involving property nationalized by President Hugo Chávez’s socialist government. The Foreign Ministry said that its participation in the forum, the International Center for Settlement of Investment Disputes, was banned by Venezuela’s Constitution, which it said required disputes to be settled in Venezuelan courts. It said that the move was meant to defend Venezuelan sovereignty and that the center was biased in favor of multinational corporations. The cases before the center include one brought by Exxon over the nationalization of its share in a heavy oil project. A World Bank spokesman could not confirm that the organization had received notice of Venezuela’s action. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela: Government to Pull Out of Nationalization Proceedings', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Government to Pull Out Of Nationalization Proceedings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nationalization of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Center for Settlement of Investment Disputes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T04:36:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2205e07f-a225-5de9-8ecf-fc55ae1e7f10', 'word_count': 128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2205e07f-a225-5de9-8ecf-fc55ae1e7f10'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Hancock was the organist and master of the choristers at St. Thomas Church in Manhattan for more than 30 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/arts/music/gerre-hancock-st-thomas-church-organist-dies-at-77.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Hancock was the organist and master of the choristers at St. Thomas Church in Manhattan for more than 30 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gerre Hancock, a renowned organist known for his skill at improvisation, a rare art among American classical organists, died on Saturday in Austin, Tex. He was 77.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/music/26hancock/26hancock-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/music/26hancock/26hancock-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/arts/music/26hancock/26hancock-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit':