of returning to the gold standard, rather than addressing the mortgage crisis, is not a serious approach, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson, the former chief economist at the International Monetary Fund, is the co-author of “13 Bankers.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newt Gingrich, Gold and Property Rights', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold Standard (Monetary)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntsman, Jon M Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/795a12a3-9327-51f9-bf43-3c6df0ce2474', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/795a12a3-9327-51f9-bf43-3c6df0ce2474'}, {'abstract': 'A washing machine and a bra — but not much else.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/magazine/marc-newson.html', 'snippet': 'A washing machine and a bra — but not much else.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first week in October, bound for two days of client meetings in northern Italy, Marc Newson chartered a single-engine Pilatus PC-12 prop plane with a paint job by the designer Philippe Starck. It took off from Le Bourget airport outside Paris at 11 a.m. Newson had been back in Europe less than a week after meetings in Singapore. He had also recently been in Australia, where, as part of an extensive fixtures-and-fittings commission from Caroma, an Australian design-and-manufacturing house of bathroom products, he participated in technical tests to determine flow rates of sewage through variously shaped pipes. The Caroma engineers simulated human waste with specially designed plastic bags of miso that conformed to an “international stool standard.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/magazine/29newson1/29newson1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 799, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/magazine/29newson1/29newson1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 799}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/magazine/29newson1/29newson1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 832, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/magazine/29newson1/29newson1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/magazine/29newson1/29newson1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is There Anything Marc Newson Hasn’t Designed?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘The Future Isn’t Futuristic Anymore’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newson, Marc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T10:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chip Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19d7869f-398c-5f81-8957-02249b2f4ce1', 'word_count': 4682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19d7869f-398c-5f81-8957-02249b2f4ce1'}, {'abstract': 'Red Bulls defender Tim Ream is now a member of Bolton Wanderers of England’s Premier League.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/ream-completes-transfer-to-bolton/', 'snippet': 'Red Bulls defender Tim Ream is now a member of Bolton Wanderers of England’s Premier League.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The day after his wedding, which was Jan. 7, Tim Ream received a phone call from Bolton Wanderers Manager Owen Coyle.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ream Completes Transfer to Bolton', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coyle, Owen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ream, Tim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bolton Wanderers (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Red Bulls (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T10:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ddab4b5-72c9-59f5-b952-39a96c8c7240', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ddab4b5-72c9-59f5-b952-39a96c8c7240'}, {'abstract': 'The brilliant weirdness of Die Antwoord, a South African rap-rave crew, pairs obscene, Afrikaans-laced lyrics with surreal imagery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/magazine/die-antwoord.html', 'snippet': 'The brilliant weirdness of Die Antwoord, a South African rap-rave crew, pairs obscene, Afrikaans-laced lyrics with surreal imagery.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We r taking 1 day / nite off 2 get really drunk wif some homies in a dodgy hood in Johannesburg called FIETAS on New Years Eve,” the e-mail read. “Dere are always fights in Fietas on New Years Eve which should be fun.” And so Ninja, the leader of the South African rap-rave crew Die Antwoord, invited me to ring in 2012 in the lair of zef, the scene the band brought to the world two years ago with a viral music video called “Zef Side.” Zef is the nasty, freaky, gleefully trashy underbelly of post-apartheid white South African culture. It is bling and bruises and weed-whacker mullets like the one sported by Yo-Landi Vi$$er, the tiny blonde who orbits Ninja like a foulmouthed muse.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype':