rary creates an animation tool that allows users to bring thousands of digitized stereographs from its collection back to flickering, 3-D life.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/3-d-it-yourself-thanks-to-new-library-site/', 'snippet': 'The New York Public Library creates an animation tool that allows users to bring thousands of digitized stereographs from its collection back to flickering, 3-D life.', 'lead_paragraph': '(Courtesy NYPL Labs) Samuel Dixon crossing Niagara.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3-D It Yourself, Thanks to New Library Site', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Public Library', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T12:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b0831e0-4544-544c-8261-f1673fd33560', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b0831e0-4544-544c-8261-f1673fd33560'}, {'abstract': 'In 2012 I’d like to see our output increase to $2.4 million, which would be a little more than 10 percent over 2011. And I’d like to do it without hiring anyone.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/running-the-numbers-why-our-productivity-improved/', 'snippet': 'In 2012 I’d like to see our output increase to $2.4 million, which would be a little more than 10 percent over 2011. And I’d like to do it without hiring anyone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My company has 14 employees. In the office we have me, two sales engineers, one design engineer, a part-time bookkeeper and a part-time administrative assistant. The other nine are out on the shop floor. They build, finish, and ship our product.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Running the Numbers: Why Our Productivity Improved', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACCOUNTING AND ACCOUNTANTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T12:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b955cfff-ea19-5c46-b685-4224afa28e94', 'word_count': 1414, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b955cfff-ea19-5c46-b685-4224afa28e94'}, {'abstract': 'With firms cutting jobs and pay, fewer bankers in the City are setting off for rivals after bonus season.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/london-bankers-stay-put-as-bonuses-wane/', 'snippet': 'With firms cutting jobs and pay, fewer bankers in the City are setting off for rivals after bonus season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The beginning of the year is usually a busy time for bankers and recruiters as many staff members wait to get their bonuses before setting off to a rival.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Bankers Stay Put as Bonuses Wane', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HBOS PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lloyds Banking Group Plc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T12:20:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be217b4f-87a9-52fd-a0d8-c3f4b0db021c', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be217b4f-87a9-52fd-a0d8-c3f4b0db021c'}, {'abstract': 'The long-anticipated management shuffle at EADS preserves the delicate balance of French and German control of the company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/business/global/trichet-likely-to-join-board-of-airbus-parent.html', 'snippet': 'The long-anticipated management shuffle at EADS preserves the delicate balance of French and German control of the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Jean-Claude Trichet, the former president of the European Central Bank, was nominated Thursday to the board of European Aeronautic Defense and Space, the parent company of Airbus, as part of a long-anticipated reshuffling of the group’s senior management. The move carefully preserves the balance of French and German representation in the executive suite.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 's