made as a promissory note intended to tide it over regular cash shortages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/health/gates-donates-750-million-to-global-fund.html', 'snippet': 'The donation to the struggling Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria was made as a promissory note intended to tide it over regular cash shortages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a show of faith in the faltering Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria, Bill Gates donated $750 million to the fund on Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Gates Donates $750 Million to Shore Up Disease-Fighting Fund', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bill Gates Donates $750 Million to Shore Up Disease-Fighting Fund', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T15:29:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ae27832-1d0c-5190-8dda-3298f8e59f2f', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ae27832-1d0c-5190-8dda-3298f8e59f2f'}, {'abstract': 'If you can answer this question, you are on your way to making $180,000 a year: build a sequence of nearest neighbor classifiers around its tuning parameter K, choosing K using prediction accuracy estimated through tenfold cross validation. In other words, how do you pick the best way to estimate whether an e-mail is spam? It’s why statistics courses are hot.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/what-are-the-odds-that-stats-would-get-this-popular/', 'snippet': 'If you can answer this question, you are on your way to making $180,000 a year: build a sequence of nearest neighbor classifiers around its tuning parameter K, choosing K using prediction accuracy estimated through tenfold cross validation. In oth...', 'lead_paragraph': '“Most of my life I went to parties and heard a little groan when people heard what I did,” says Robert Tibshirani, a statistics professor at Stanford University. “Now they’re all excited to meet me.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Are the Odds That Stats Would Be This Popular?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statistics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T15:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f5627cb-36db-55ed-8eb2-de8d60553447', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f5627cb-36db-55ed-8eb2-de8d60553447'}, {'abstract': 'The ad raises the specter that Nancy Pelosi holds a secret dossier of damaging information.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/new-romney-ad-focuses-on-gingrichs-ethics-violation/', 'snippet': 'The ad raises the specter that Nancy Pelosi holds a secret dossier of damaging information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JACKSONVILLE, Fla. — Moving on to Phase 2 of its aggressive campaign to stop Newt Gingrich’s momentum before the primary here on Tuesday, former Gov. Mitt Romney of Massachusetts is beginning to show a new, bruising advertisement focusing on the Congressional ethics finding against Mr. Gingrich in the 1990s. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Romney Ad Focuses on Gingrich’s Ethics Violation', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T15:33:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2835346b-da29-5384-b6c2-525790461ce0', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2835346b-da29-5384-b6c2-525790461ce0'}, {'abstract': 'The founder of China Labor Watch speaks about labor conditions at Foxconn, which has some of the world’s biggest factories, and at other electronics factories.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/q-and-a-with-li-qiang-of-china-labor-watch/', 'snippet': 'The founder of China Labor Watch speaks about labor conditions at Foxconn, which has some of the world’s biggest factories, and at other electronics factories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Li Qiang, 39, is the founder of China Labor Watch, a nonprofit group in New York City that seeks to improve labor conditions in China. In the late 1990s, while studying law in southwest China’s Sichuan Province, he began supporting striking workers and taxi drivers. Later, he moved south, to China’s biggest factory zones near Shenzhen. He worked at several electronics, toy and shoe factories, where he investigated labor conditions, and tried to expose what he saw as unjust and inhumane conditions. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Questions for Li Qiang of China Labor Watch', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sweatshops', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foxconn Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T15:43:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef170ce8-8922-522e-9e7c-aae6f0b9a9f6', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef170ce8-8922-522e-9e7c-aae6f0b9a9f6'}, {'abstract': 'To understand the World Economic Forum, you have to take in the first-hand accounts of the snowbound elite, as related through a barrage of Twitter messages from reporters and others involved in the conference.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/davos-potpourri-day-2-the-party-never-ends/', 'snippet': 'To understand the World Economic Forum, you have to take in the first-hand accounts of the snowbound elite, as related through a barrage of Twitter messages from reporters and others involved in the conference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, rolled on Thursday, with news-making speeches by Prime Minister David Cameron of Britain, Bill Gates and Archbishop Desmond Tutu, among others. Mr. Cameron proposed a “coalition of the willing” to open up global free trade, Mr. Gates pledged $750 million to a struggling AIDS fund, and Archbishop Tutu told the downtrodden financiers in attendance: “Each one of us is made for goodness, even bankers.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Davos Potpourri, Day 2: The Party Never Ends', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Tina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gross, Daniel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jagger, Mick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ledbetter, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lublin, Nancy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Matthew', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Sean', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prince', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T15:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'by