ed some Sikhs and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two members of Britain’s Parliament have become the latest people to condemn Jay Leno for a joke that appeared on NBC’s “Tonight Show” and suggested that a sacred shrine in India belonged to Mitt Romney.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leno Joke Draws Fire From Two Members of British Parliament', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'British Lawmakers Criticize Jay Leno', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sikhs and Sikhism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leno, Jay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDonnell, John (1951- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golden Temple (Amritsar, India)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labour Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lake Winnipesaukee (NH)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T15:58:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d7d335d-adcb-531f-9db8-750d03226ca1', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d7d335d-adcb-531f-9db8-750d03226ca1'}, {'abstract': 'Ioulex’s couture fashion week photo diary.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/photos-of-the-moment-valentino-2/', 'snippet': 'Ioulex’s couture fashion week photo diary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of the Moment | Valentino', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T16:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By ioulex', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e1a1276-9b15-53b9-b579-2b6a58bcd290', 'word_count': 34, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e1a1276-9b15-53b9-b579-2b6a58bcd290'}, {'abstract': 'In Colorado, a proposal to legalize possession of marijuana in small amounts is likely to be on the ballot this fall, backed by the Campaign to Regulate Marijuana Like Alcohol.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/us/a-ballot-push-to-legalize-marijuana-with-alcohol-as-the-role-model.html', 'snippet': 'In Colorado, a proposal to legalize possession of marijuana in small amounts is likely to be on the ballot this fall, backed by the Campaign to Regulate Marijuana Like Alcohol.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — Proponents of marijuana have argued for years that the drug is safer than alcohol, both to individuals and society. But a ballot proposal to legalize possession of marijuana in small amounts in Colorado, likely to be on the November ballot, is putting the two intoxicants back into the same sentence, urging voters to “regulate marijuana like alcohol,” as the ballot proposition’s title puts it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/us/27marijuanaspan/27marijuana-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/27/us/27marijuanaspan/27marijuana-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/us/27marijuanaspan/27marijuana-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 734, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/us/27marijuanaspan/27marijuana-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/27/us/27marijuanaspan/27marijuana-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marijuana Push in Colorado Likens It to Alcohol', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marijuana Push in Colorado Likens It to Alcohol', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T16:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f98f0c92-68b2-5632-9742-49ac232dc730', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f98f0c92-68b2-5632-9742-49ac232dc730'}, {'abstract': 'Rafael Nadal and Roger Federer faced each other at the Australian Open (Nadal won) in a rivalry that shows no signs of fading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/sports/intense-tennis-for-insomniacs.html', 'snippet': 'Rafael Nadal and Roger Federer faced each other at the Australian Open (Nadal won) in a rivalry that shows no signs of fading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first thing you noticed if you stayed awake (or woke up) to watch Rafael Nadal and Roger Federer play in their Australian Open semifinal (start time: 3:30 a.m. Eastern), is that the ever-gracious Nadal wore that eye-searing green shirt to help keep you awake. Yes, he has been wearing it the whole tournament, indicating he has a soft spot for American insomniacs, although little regard for their retinas. But the second thing you noticed is just how much these two do not want to lose to each other. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 710, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/27/sports/27leading1/27leading1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Intense Tennis for Insomniacs', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Intense Tennis for Insomniacs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T16:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf61cf49-db48-5585-ac79-dd11a56871c5', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf61cf49-db48-5585-ac79-dd11a56871c5'}, {'abstract': 'In Robert Harris’s new thriller, a hugely complex trading program runs dangerously amok.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/books/the-fear-index-by-robert-harris.html', 'snippet': 'In Robert Harris’s new thriller, a hugely complex trading program runs dangerously amok.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title of Robert Harris’s new thriller, “The Fear Index,” comes from the volatility index, or VIX — also known as the “fear index” — which measures expectations of violent swings in the market, as Wall Street watchers know from the harrowing meltdown of 2008. This fleet-footed, if sometimes hokey, novel takes place in the rarefied world of hedge funds, featuring one that has achieved huge returns by short-selling and using trading algorithm