e an assistant principal at another school. The school is slated to be phased out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/26/jane-addams-h-s-principal-resigns-amid-credit-scandal/', 'snippet': 'The principal of a troubled Bronx high school will resign at the end of this week amid accusations that she gave some students credit for classes they never took. City officials said on Thursday that Sharron Smalls, the principal of Jane Addams Hi...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jane Addams H.S. Principal Resigns Amid Credit Scandal', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T17:40:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANNA M. PHILLIPS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6cb15e3-27fa-5f5b-9511-1aa6b6ebfc77', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6cb15e3-27fa-5f5b-9511-1aa6b6ebfc77'}, {'abstract': 'Advice on washing dinner-party dishes, waiting for a restaurant table and letting shower guests run up your tab.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/dear-flofab-should-a-host-wait-to-wash-dishes/', 'snippet': 'Advice on washing dinner-party dishes, waiting for a restaurant table and letting shower guests run up your tab.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Valentine’s Day approaches, with its perilous combination of food, romance and etiquette, Florence Fabricant would love to help with advice on the fine points of entertaining at home and eating in restaurants. Have a question concerning the holiday — or any dining dilemma? Ask FloFab.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dear FloFab: Should a Host Wait to Wash Dishes?', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T17:55:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1716366c-a518-548a-9752-a8357c004548', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1716366c-a518-548a-9752-a8357c004548'}, {'abstract': 'Around our table, Phu Quoc and its signature product, “extra virgin” fish sauce, were spoken about with reverence and a deep longing.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/ravenous-the-taste-of-home/', 'snippet': 'Around our table, Phu Quoc and its signature product, “extra virgin” fish sauce, were spoken about with reverence and a deep longing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I began the Year of the Dragon with the taste of sea and salt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ravenous | The Taste of Home', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T18:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monique Truong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monique', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Truong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/235c3444-ca33-5bc5-9063-85d0b043fb08', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/235c3444-ca33-5bc5-9063-85d0b043fb08'}, {'abstract': 'There was one big problem: the business had to be sold in four months — before the seller was going to pack up and move to Chicago to take a job.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/selling-a-business-on-facebook/', 'snippet': 'There was one big problem: the business had to be sold in four months — before the seller was going to pack up and move to Chicago to take a job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An independent florist with a reputation for unusual arrangements, Bloom is a fixture in historic downtown Bentonville, Ark., an area whose rapid growth was recently accelerated by the opening of the Crystal Bridges Museum of American Art.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Selling a Business on Facebook', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Florists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Barbara', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T18:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barbara Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fd423a4-f3ec-5895-b571-b1925f26dd77', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fd423a4-f3ec-5895-b571-b1925f26dd77'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Ishioka, who won a 1992 Academy Award in costume design for “Bram Stoker’s ‘Dracula,’” came to be known as one of Japan’s, then the world’s, foremost art directors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/arts/design/eiko-ishioka-designer-dies-at-73.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Ishioka, who won a 1992 Academy Award in costume design for “Bram Stoker’s ‘Dracula,’” came to be known as one of Japan’s, then the world’s, foremost art directors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eiko Ishioka, a designer who brought an eerie, sensual surrealism to film and theater, album covers, the Olympics and Cirque du Soleil, in the process earning an Oscar, a Grammy and a string of other honors, died on Saturday in Tokyo. She was 73.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27ishioka/27ishioka-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27ishioka/27ishioka-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27ishioka/27ishioka-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eiko Ishioka, Multifaceted Designer and Oscar Winner, Dies at 73', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eiko Ishioka, Costumer Of the Surreal, Dies at 73', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Costumes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ishioka, Eiko', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T18:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c2488bc-b2cf-55a7-8969-8e02f1a5a696', 'word_count': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c2488bc-b2cf-55a7-8969-8e02f1a5a696'}, {'abstract': 'In Jacksonville, Fla., Mitt Romney criticized President Obama’s economic policies, but only alluded once to his Republican rival, Newt Gingrich.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/romney-holds-fires-on-gingrich-but-not-obama/', 'snippet': 'In Jacksonville, Fla., Mitt Romney criticized President Obama’s economic policies, but only alluded once to his Republican rival, Newt Gingrich.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:38 p.m. | Updated JACKSONVILLE, Fla. — Standing before a large “Obama Isn’t Working” sign, Mitt Romney on Thursday came to a printing plant that recently shut its doors and returned his focus squarely to President Obama, criticizing the president’s policies and his State of the Union speech Tuesday night, among other things. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Holds Fire on Gingrich as Surrogates Fire Away', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'majo