peared at Macworld. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/technology/26bits-macworld/26bits-macworld-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 789, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Macworld Conference Carries On Without Apple', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T20:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d512f5e-707d-5761-a2ee-2016dc74bb21', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d512f5e-707d-5761-a2ee-2016dc74bb21'}, {'abstract': 'Royal Bank of Scotland — 82 percent owned by British taxpayers — had come under pressure from Prime Minister David Cameron to rein in bonuses for top executives.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/r-b-s-slashes-bonus-for-chief-executive/', 'snippet': 'Royal Bank of Scotland — 82 percent owned by British taxpayers — had come under pressure from Prime Minister David Cameron to rein in bonuses for top executives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Royal Bank of Scotland announced on Thursday that it would pay its chief executive, Stephen Hester, an all-stock bonus of £963,000, or $1.5 million, less than half what he received last year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Royal Bank of Scotland Slashes C.E.O.’s Bonus', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 1, 'major':