ew survey found, but they remain surprisingly optimistic that things will improve for them.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/latinos-on-the-economy-hard-hit-but-hopeful/', 'snippet': 'Latinos are keenly aware that they have fared worse than other groups in the economic downturn, a Pew survey found, but they remain surprisingly optimistic that things will improve for them.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Latinos have been especially hard hit by the economic downturn, with nearly four in 10 — 38 percent — saying they have skipped meals because they did not have enough money for food, according to a national survey published on Thursday by the Pew Hispanic Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Latinos on the Economy: Hard Hit but Hopeful', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Hispanic Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T21:27:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5977791-38a4-5c67-a9dc-5c0373beec4c', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5977791-38a4-5c67-a9dc-5c0373beec4c'}, {'abstract': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission filed actions against the Latvian trader, who is accused of making more than $850,000 in illegal profits, and the four electronic trading firms he used.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/s-e-c-accuses-latvian-trader-and-4-firms-of-market-abuse/', 'snippet': 'The Securities and Exchange Commission filed actions against the Latvian trader, who is accused of making more than $850,000 in illegal profits, and the four electronic trading firms he used.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Latvian trader is accused of hacking into the brokerage accounts of innocent investors in the United States, making hundreds of thousands of dollars for himself while costing the unwitting victims millions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'S.E.C. Accuses Firms and Latvian Trader of Market Abuse', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Brokers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T21:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c24d4ba7-603c-505c-8922-18bb06de9104', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c24d4ba7-603c-505c-8922-18bb06de9104'}, {'abstract': 'A technology under development would instruct the Chevrolet Volt to charge only when the grid was pumping a percentage of energy from renewable resources.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/teaching-the-volt-to-charge-smarter-and-cleaner/', 'snippet': 'A technology under development would instruct the Chevrolet Volt to charge only when the grid was pumping a percentage of energy from renewable resources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, General Motors announced an alert system under development that would instruct the Chevy Volt to charge only when a relatively high percentage of renewable energy was available. Being plugged in at those times would further minimize the carbon footprint of the plug-in hybrid. Google plans to test the technology, facilitated by the subscription-based OnStar alert and navigation system, on its fleet of 17 Volts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teaching the Volt to Charge Smarter and Cleaner', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'OnStar Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T21:31:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f680d777-c538-5389-beb0-8b560b826d0f', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f680d777-c538-5389-beb0-8b560b826d0f'}, {'abstract': 'About that old new economic geography.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/chinese-clusters-and-me/', 'snippet': 'About that old new economic geography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I realized that if you wanted to know where I was coming from on the Apple-in-China story, the best reading is probably the paper I prepared for the Association of American Geographers (pdf), which offers both a nontechnical account of what the “new economic geography” was about and a discussion of how it applies to China.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Clusters and Me', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T21:31:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/433f209f-8f47-5239-be3d-fe81f238ce19', 'word_count': 56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/433f209f-8f47-5239-be3d-fe81f238ce19'}, {'abstract': 'Though the latest polls show Newt Gingrich’s momentum may have stalled, he has found strong backing in Brevard County, Fla., by proposing a bold initiative in space industry employment. Trip Gabriel reports.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/caucus-video-gingrich-and-the-space-program/', 'snippet': 'Though the latest polls show Newt Gingrich’s momentum may have stalled, he has found strong backing in Brevard County, Fla., by proposing a bold initiative in space industry employment. Trip Gabriel reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the latest polls show Newt Gingrich’s momentum may have stalled, he has found strong backing in Brevard County, Fla., by proposing a bold initiative in space industry employment. Trip Gabriel reports. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Caucus Video: Gingrich and the Space Industry', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'co