dress complaints that he had been too vague about his plans for France and its slowing economy, issuing a package of 60 measures that would increase taxes and government spending but aim to balance the budget by 2017.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/world/27france_337/27france_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sarkozy’s Main Rival Offers Proposals for Lifting France’s Economy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sarkozy’s Main Rival Offers Proposals for Lifting France’s Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sarkozy, Nicolas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T22:04:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/badccf4b-b5ee-5d58-8bcd-1bd658fab2ca', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/badccf4b-b5ee-5d58-8bcd-1bd658fab2ca'}, {'abstract': 'An automat at 611 West 181st Street, designed in 1930 by Louis Allen Abramson, was converted to a bank in 1978 and today the space houses a Sleepy’s mattress store.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/01/29/realestate/20120129-streetscapes-slider.html', 'snippet': 'An automat at 611 West 181st Street, designed in 1930 by Louis Allen Abramson, was converted to a bank in 1978 and today the space houses a Sleepy’s mattress store.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An automat at 611 West 181st Street, designed in 1930 by Louis Allen Abramson, was converted to a bank in 1978 and today the space houses a Sleepy’s mattress store.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before and After: Automat Under Wraps', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T22:05:02+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f1b454dd-1351-5bef-b5e9-8ee3493e1103', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f1b454dd-1351-5bef-b5e9-8ee3493e1103'}, {'abstract': 'Portland has a fast, balanced team this season, but Batum, Wallace, Felton and Camby could all depart.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/can-the-blazers-keep-all-the-pieces/', 'snippet': 'Portland has a fast, balanced team this season, but Batum, Wallace, Felton and Camby could all depart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Portland Trail Blazers of today are deep, versatile and effective on both ends of the court. This particular Portland team certainly isn’t without its flaws, but it plays an eminently watchable brand of basketball with more than enough substance as its foundation.'