ision.html', 'snippet': 'About a half-dozen new television shows about antiques auctions have appeared, but they have little resemblance to how the trade really works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reality television about antiques is available practically around the clock now, and half a dozen new shows have appeared in the past few months. But the transactions shown these days little resemble how the trade actually works.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27ANTIQUES2/ANTIQUES2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 522, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Antiques on Camera and Behind Every Door', 'kicker': 'Antiques', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Antiques on Camera And Behind Every Door', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Costumes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T22:52:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve M. Kahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cbddd2a-95d9-5738-bfb0-2ea1c4e45112', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cbddd2a-95d9-5738-bfb0-2ea1c4e45112'}, {'abstract': '“The Loving Story: Photographs by Grey Villet” portrays the Lovings, a Virginia couple at the center of a storm about interracial marriage, as accidental heroes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/arts/design/the-loving-story-at-international-center-of-photography.html', 'snippet': '“The Loving Story: Photographs by Grey Villet” portrays the Lovings, a Virginia couple at the center of a storm about interracial marriage, as accidental heroes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s the difference between a political activist and a political hero? It’s often a matter of intention versus accident. Within the civil rights movement Rosa Parks is seen as an activist: She trained at the Highlander Folk School for social justice in Tennessee, and her refusal to give up her seat on a crowded bus was the catalyst for the 1955 Montgomery Bus Boycott. Richard and Mildred Loving, an interracial couple from Virginia whose marriage prompted a benchmark 1967 Supreme Court ruling overturning state miscegenation laws, are portrayed in “The Loving Story: Photographs by Grey Villet” as heroes who fell into history by accident.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Life of Marital Bliss (Segregation Laws Aside)', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Life of Marital Bliss (Segregation Laws Aside)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Segregation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Villet, Grey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value'