nd the lifeblood of rock, the guitar also has a classical literature that (with some transcriptional tweaking) stretches back to the 16th century and includes a rich, complex contemporary repertory.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27GUITAR1_SPAN/27GUITAR1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27GUITAR1_SPAN/27GUITAR1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27GUITAR1_SPAN/JPGUITAR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 566, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27GUITAR1_SPAN/27GUITAR1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27GUITAR1_SPAN/27GUITAR1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'They’ll Strum From Day Into Night', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They’ll Strum From Day Into Night', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guitars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Merkin Concert Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T23:38:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/358b89ff-00c6-5938-83ea-1da811366b19', 'word_count': 1600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/358b89ff-00c6-5938-83ea-1da811366b19'}, {'abstract': 'The mayor said the Police Department will have to work harder to improve its relationship with the city’s Muslims.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/mayor-defends-kelly-but-says-anti-muslim-film-caused-damage/', 'snippet': 'The mayor said the Police Department will have to work harder to improve its relationship with the city’s Muslims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As his administration faces a firestorm over a video  shown to hundreds of police officers that depicted Muslims as extremists, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg conceded on Thursday that the episode had damaged relations between the city’s Islamic community and the Police Department.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor Defends Kelly, but Says Anti-Muslim Film Caused Damage', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Third Jihad, The (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Browne, Paul J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T23:38:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/851779e6-ac36-5841-b231-26d44a37b378', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/851779e6-ac36-5841-b231-26d44a37b378'}, {'abstract': 'Informal surveys indicate that on the Island, listing a home on a Wednesday in March results in the quickest sale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/realestate/long-island-in-the-region-best-time-to-list-a-home-midweek.html', 'snippet': 'Informal surveys indicate that on the Island, listing a home on a Wednesday in March results in the quickest sale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GLENN KELMAN, the chief executive of Redfin, an online real estate brokerage based in Seattle that has\xa0had a presence on the Island for two years, always thought that houses on the market in the dead of winter were like a “clearance rack.” He was convinced that winter was the worst time to sell. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/realestate/29LIZO_SPAN/29LIZO_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/realestate/29LIZO_SPAN/29LIZO_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/realestate/29LIZO_SPAN/LIZO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/realestate/29LIZO_SPAN/29LIZO_SPAN-thumbStandard.