body else.” That’s about as subtle as it gets.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27MAN1_SPAN/27MAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27MAN1_SPAN/27MAN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27MAN1_SPAN/JPMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27MAN1_SPAN/27MAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/27/arts/27MAN1_SPAN/27MAN1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cops and Robbers, and Vertigo', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cops and Robbers, and Vertigo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Ed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Worthington, Sam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banks, Elizabeth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leth, Asger', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T23:44:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/752cb005-bca0-5986-9163-4182bfb977b3', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/752cb005-bca0-5986-9163-4182bfb977b3'}, {'abstract': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta outlined on Thursday the first major step – he called it a “down payment” – of shrinking the Pentagon after a decade of war.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/a-quick-roundup-of-the-pentagons-proposed-budget-cuts/', 'snippet': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta outlined on Thursday the first major step – he called it a “down payment” – of shrinking the Pentagon after a decade of war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta outlined on Thursday the first major step — he called it a “down payment” — of shrinking the Pentagon after a decade of war. Included in the proposal: limit pay raises for troops, increase health insurance fees for military retirees and close bases in the United States. Of those proposals, our colleagues Elisabeth Bumiller and Thom Shanker write that pay-raise limits, though modest, “are certain to ignite a political fight in Congress, which since the Sept. 11, 2001, attacks has consistently raised military salaries beyond what the Pentagon has recommended.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Quick Roundup of the Pentagon’s Proposed Budget Cuts', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Martin E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panetta, Leon E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-26T23:48:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By At War', 'person': [{'firstname': 'At', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'War', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/753594a6-d6ed-505b-9bd5-72036ebecd08', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/753594a6-d6ed-505b-9bd5-72036ebecd08'}, {'abstract': 'A 740-acre property was divided into two parts, both of which will be preserved permanently for agriculture use.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/realestate/new-jersey-in-the-region-historic-long-branch-farm-sold.html', 'snippet': 'A 740-acre property was divided into two parts, both of which will be preserved permanently for agriculture use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONG VALLEY', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/realestate/29NJZO_SPAN/29NJZO_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/realestate/29NJZO_SPAN/29NJZO_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/realestate/29NJZO_SPAN/NJZO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/realestate/29NJZO_SPAN/29NJZO_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/realestate/29NJZO_SPAN/29NJZO_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Historic Dirt’ Preserved', 'kicker':