Port Moresby, early Thursday, detained the military chief and demanded that Prime Minister Peter O’Neill bow to a Supreme Court ruling ordering Sir Michael’s reinstatement as leader. But after a tense day, Mr. O’Neill said his military chief had been freed and the barracks had been returned to the control of his government. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Papua New Guinea: Mutiny Said to Fail', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Pacific', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Papua New Guinea: Mutiny Said to Fail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Papua New Guinea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neill, Peter", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Somare, Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T01:07:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Siegel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Siegel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/161974b9-1617-585c-aabf-408b421d7b6b', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/161974b9-1617-585c-aabf-408b421d7b6b'}, {'abstract': 'Because Newt Gingrich is perpetually late, local Republican officials and former colleagues must furiously tread verbal water as they try to keep a hold on crowds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/us/politics/a-tardy-gingrich-in-florida-strains-his-warm-up-acts.html', 'snippet': 'Because Newt Gingrich is perpetually late, local Republican officials and former colleag