rgins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first month of this abbreviated N.B.A. season has brought a number of unexpected twists and turns. One of the more surprising developments has been the stellar play of the Philadelphia 76ers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Early Indicators Point to Stellar Season for 76ers', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T01:14:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By JUSTIN KUBATKO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KUBATKO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6514de8c-87c0-5836-bfc2-6d5f6a0898eb', 'word_count': 487, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6514de8c-87c0-5836-bfc2-6d5f6a0898eb'}, {'abstract': 'Bridgewater Associates, which manages nearly $120 billion, posted returns of 23 percent in 2011 — a year when the average hedge fund portfolio lost 5 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/in-punishing-year-for-hedge-funds-biggest-one-thrived/', 'snippet': 'Bridgewater Associates, which manages nearly $120 billion, posted returns of 23 percent in 2011 — a year when the average hedge fund portfolio lost 5 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world’s biggest hedge fund is also one of the best performers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Punishing Year for Hedge Funds, Biggest One Thrived', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hedge Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalio, Ray', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value