 cut the number of allowances power companies can use to offset emissions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/nyregion/in-greenhouse-gas-initiative-many-unsold-allowances.html', 'snippet': 'The Greenhouse Gas Initiative involving Northeastern and Mid-Atlantic states has cut the number of allowances power companies can use to offset emissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adjusting to shifts in the economy, states in the cap-and-trade system known as the Regional Greenhouse Gas Initiative have slashed the number of allowances that electric power companies can buy to offset their emissions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Regional Cap-and-Trade Effort Seeks Greater Impact by Cutting Carbon Allowances', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Regional Cap-and-Trade Effort Seeks Greater Impact by Cutting Carbon Allowances', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Regional Greenhouse Gas Initiative', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northeastern States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T01:20:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87de2064-c596-5822-9033-6a08fd979deb', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87de2064-c596-5822-9033-6a08fd979deb'}, {'abstract': 'A school district that was sued for holding a prayer rally at a school assembly and prayers at official events has agreed to end its promotion of religion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/us/south-carolina-schools-agree-to-halt-prayers.html', 'snippet': 'A school district that was sued for holding a prayer rally at a school assembly and prayers at official events has agreed to end its promotion of religion.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A school district that was sued for holding a prayer rally at a school assembly and prayers at official events has agreed to end its promotion of religion. A federal judge on Thursday made final a consent decree in which the Chesterfield County schools admitted to violating the separation of church and state. Under the decree, school officials may not encourage prayers at events or allow endorsement of religion in the classroom. The suit was brought by the American Civil Liberties Union on behalf of a middle-school student who objected to the evangelical assembly and other Christian activities at school. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Carolina: Schools Agree to Halt Prayers', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Carolina: Schools Agree To Halt Prayers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prayers and Prayer Books', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T01:29:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckh