l': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/919c6a48-7552-55e4-9fd3-86b3beff09c3', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/919c6a48-7552-55e4-9fd3-86b3beff09c3'}, {'abstract': 'The debate was a crucial face-off just five days before Florida’s presidential primary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/26/us/20120127_DEBATE_337.html', 'snippet': 'The debate was a crucial face-off just five days before Florida’s presidential primary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The debate was a crucial face-off just five days before Florida’s presidential primary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/us/20120127_DEBATE_337-slide-7645/20120127_DEBATE_337-slide-7645-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/26/us/20120127_DEBATE_337-slide-7645/20120127_DEBATE_337-slide-7645-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/26/us/20120127_DEBATE_337-slide-7645/20120127_DEBATE_337-slide-7645-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Candidates Debate in Jacksonville, Fla.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T01:37:37+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/f2e44518-9380-51e5-a73a-a2a1ca5b3beb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/f2e44518-9380-51e5-a73a-a2a1ca5b3beb'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama seems sure of himself, but where’s the big agenda? It wasn’t in the State of the Union address.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/opinion/brooks-hope-but-not-much-change.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama seems sure of himself, but where’s the big agenda? It wasn’t in the State of the Union address.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Simpson-Bowles report wasn’t just a policy document. For a few months, it expanded the national debate. Everybody seemed to realize that the country was beset by large challenges that could no longer be neglected: soaring debt, lagging growth, wage stagnation, family breakdown, political dysfunction. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/david-brooks/david-brooks-thumbLarge-v2.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hope, but Not Much Change', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hope, But Not Much Change', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Commission on Fiscal Responsibility and Reform', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T01:38:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbda780f-f125-5846-84b7-d595058ac0dc', 'word_count': 808, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbda780f-f125-5846-84b7-d595058ac0dc'}, {'abstract': 'After Newt Gingrich said that he still believes Mitt Romney is the most “anti-immigrant” candidate, Mr. Romney puffed out of his chest and complained, to the audience’s delight.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/indignation-over-immigration-marks-beginning-of-debate/', 'snippet': 'After Newt Gingrich said that he still believes Mitt Romney is the most “anti-immigrant” candidate, Mr. Romney puffed out of his chest and complained, to the audience’s delight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Interesting start to the debate, with a question from the audience about illegal immigration. Though it at first seemed likely to prompt a more civil debate — especially since Wolf Blitzer, the moderator, chose to direct the question to Rick Santorum — it ultimately yielded the kind of vitriol between Newt Gingrich and Mitt Romney that some expected.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indignation Over Immigration Marks Beginning of Debate', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T01:40:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cc6255b-5882-5c9f-8d59-ff3beaad8eda', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cc6255b-5882-5c9f-8d59-ff3beaad8eda'}, {'abstract': 'Live updates, fact checking and analysis of the Republican presidential debate in Jacksonville, Fla.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/jacksonville-fla-debate-live-blog/', 'snippet': 'Live updates, fact checking and analysis of the Republican presidential debate in Jacksonville, Fla.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The candidates take the stage for the last debate before the Florida Primary on Tuesday. The two-hour debate, being broadcast on CNN, is co-sponsored by the Florida Republican Party. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jacksonville Debate Live Blog', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T01:40:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d35a20e-3b22-56f8-9760-bd27b49310a6', 'word_count': 4809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d35a20e-3b22-56f8-9760-bd27b49310a6'}, {'abstract': 'While saying Mitt Romney is “anti-immigrant” may be hyperbole, during the primary campaign, Mr. Romney has moved well to the restrictionist right on immigration.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/debate-fact-check-self-deportation/', 'snippet': 'While saying Mitt Romney is “anti-immigrant” may be hyperbole, during the primary campaign, Mr. Romney has moved well to the restrictionist right on immigration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wolf Blitzer asked Newt Gingrich whether Mitt Romney is anti-immigrant; a Gingrich campaign Spanish-language radio ad called Mr. Romney “anti-immigrant.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debate Fact Check: ‘Self-Deportation’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T01:43:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7bef7e0c-1f1d-5dfd-8b1c-f2e04d206fa6', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7bef7e0c-1f1d-5dfd-8b1c-f2e04d206fa6'}, {'abstract': 'Some still believe that all government