e': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/814e7a06-16b1-5524-85ec-b78577ae8133', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/814e7a06-16b1-5524-85ec-b78577ae8133'}, {'abstract': 'The Police Department’s explanation of its involvement with an agitprop video about Muslims shown to officers seems another case where no straight, plausible official story has been offered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/nyregion/police-accounts-in-new-york-like-of-jihad-video-often-prove-false.html', 'snippet': 'The Police Department’s explanation of its involvement with an agitprop video about Muslims shown to officers seems another case where no straight, plausible official story has been offered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One evening in November 1990, at the end of a speech in a hotel on the East Side of Manhattan, a man stuck out his arm and squeezed off shots that killed a militant Israeli politician and rabbi named Meir Kahane. The assassin ran to Lexington Avenue and jumped in a cab, but was caught a few blocks away.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/nyregion/ABOUT/ABOUT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 677, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/nyregion/ABOUT/ABOUT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/27/nyregion/ABOUT/ABOUT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Police Sa