ubject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mickelson, Phil', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'La Jolla (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T02:12:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/084a572e-bfa6-5e17-8e75-546126abd7ce', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/084a572e-bfa6-5e17-8e75-546126abd7ce'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney and Newt Gingrich have accused each other of profiting from the housing crisis. Both charges are misleading.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/fact-check-profiting-from-the-housing-crisis/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney and Newt Gingrich have accused each other of profiting from the housing crisis. Both charges are misleading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seeking to exploit questions over Mitt Romney’s investments, Newt Gingrich attacked Mr. Romney on Thursday night for profiting from the housing woes of Florida residents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fact Check: Profiting From the Housing Crisis', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T02:13:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccbaf578-ced1-58ec-9644-f9c757310534', 'word_count': 301, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccbaf578-ced1-58ec-9644-f9c757310534'}, {'abstract': 'In countries around the world, T.V. serials are being used to deliver important social messages to millions of viewers.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/steamy-plots-with-a-social-message/', 'snippet': 'In countries around the world, T.V. serials are being used to deliver important social messages to millions of viewers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every Sunday evening, seven million Kenyans sit in front of their television sets to watch “Makutano Junction,” a soap opera set in a fictional village. In one episode, audiences watch as a woman, Mama Mboga, holds her crying infant. “I need some money to take Joni to hospital,” she tells her husband, Erasmus, after he wakes up and takes a swig from a bottle. “I think he has malaria.” Erasmus insists that his son is healthy, that she is overreacting and that he has no money to give her.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soap Operas With a Social Message', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soap Operas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T02:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarika Bansal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarika', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bansal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb3e9d93-8d79-59d5-ba67-7bb75a5f3b0a', 'word_count': 1603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/