opportunities.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/26/executive-at-oprahs-cable-channel-departs-suddenly/', 'snippet': 'Lisa Erspamer, who had worked with Oprah Winfrey for nearly 20 years, is leaving OWN “to pursue other opportunities.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lisa Erspamer, a co-executive producer of “The Oprah Winfrey Show” who was sent to OWN to bring Ms. Winfrey’s personal touch to her cable channel, has unceremoniously exited the channel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Executive at Oprah’s Cable Channel Departs Suddenly', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Norman, Christina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winfrey, Oprah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Discovery Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oprah Winfrey Network', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T03:18:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d25f7a2-867b-5686-bb74-80a76ac252ef', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d25f7a2-867b-5686-bb74-80a76ac252ef'}, {'abstract': 'The Environment Ministry said the cleanup would cover about two-thirds of the 100-square-mile zone around the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant, with the goal of cutting radiation levels in half within two years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/world/asia/japan-nuclear-contamination-cleanup-near-stricken-plant-to-start-in-spring.html', 'snippet': 'The Environment Ministry said the cleanup would cover about two-thirds of the 100-square-mile zone around the Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant, with the goal of cutting radiation levels in half within two years.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Japan said Thursday that it would begin a cleanup this spring of radioactive contamination near the stricken Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant, with the goal of cutting radiation levels in half within two years. The Environment Ministry said the cleanup would cover about two-thirds of the 100-square-mile zone around the plant that was evacuated after last March’s accident. The ministry says radiation levels in these areas are low enough that the cleanup, along with the natural decay of radioactive materials, should make it possible for residents to return at an unspecified time after two years. However, the ministry said it had no plans to clean the remaining third of the evacuation zone, where it says radiation levels are too high to be brought to safe levels with current technology. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan: Nuclear Contamination Cleanup Near Stricken Plant to Start in Spring', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan: Nuclear Contamination Cleanup Near Stricken Plant to Start in Spring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T03:20:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastn