value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T06:15:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Morgan Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Morgan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5335476a-e7de-5566-8027-91d18d12bc06', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5335476a-e7de-5566-8027-91d18d12bc06'}, {'abstract': 'A group of flight attendants paid tribute to India’s Republic Day by bursting into a Bollywood dance routine.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/finnish-flight-attendants-go-bollywood-for-indias-republic-day/', 'snippet': 'A group of flight attendants paid tribute to India’s Republic Day by bursting into a Bollywood dance routine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The passengers had all boarded Finnair Flight AY201 from Helsinki to New Delhi on Jan. 17, when two dozen beaming flight attendants dressed in Indian attire came dancing through the aisles to “Deewangi Deewangi” from the Bollywood mega-blockbuster “Om Shanti Om.”The well-rehearsed and choreographed routine was in commemoration of India’s 63rd Republic Day, said Helena Kaartinen, the flight attendant who came up with the idea. “It was a good way to show respect,” she said, and to show Finnair’s Indian passengers “that we do know some things about them.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Finnish Flight Attendants Go Bollywood for India’s Republic Day', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flight Attendants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Finnair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T06:46:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vijai Singh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vijai', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62348e9d-0737-5ac2-bbf3-d63cbfaf2f81', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62348e9d-0737-5ac2-bbf3-d63cbfaf2f81'}, {'abstract': 'Twenty years after WSCR brought sports talk radio to Chicago, the format has moved beyond screamers and is demonstrating staying power.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/us/at-wscr-the-score-chicago-sports-radio-matures.html', 'snippet': 'Twenty years after WSCR brought sports talk radio to Chicago, the format has moved beyond screamers and is demonstrating staying power.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sports talk radio was a phenomenon fairly new to Chicago the first time I heard it here. I was visiting from California, taking my daughter to college on a trip that included a two-hour drive from Chicago. I came upon WSCR — “the Score” — while punching the buttons in a rental car and heard a boisterous guy later identified as Mike North lambasting the hopeless Bears in a loud, indignant voice that was both unmistakably “Chicawgo” and scalded-cat screechy. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/us/27CNCSPORTS/27CNCSPORTS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/27/us/27CNCSPORTS/27CNCSPORTS-articleLarge.jpg