mpsey-proves-that-government-cant-be-all-bad.html', 'snippet': 'There may be a widespread cynicism about the role of and the need for government, but the city’s superb, transformed 79-location library system is a shining example of what it can do.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0President Obama should have invited Mary Dempsey to the State of the Union address. Along with other guests, who were used as symbols of a skewed tax system and the need to retrain workers, she could have made another point: government can work.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With This Library System, Government Isn’t All Bad', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With This Library System, Government Isn’t All Bad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libraries and Librarians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State of the Union Message (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daley, Richard M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T06:51:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Warren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ff39fe9-b31c-564a-96e6-63ba3ab22842', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ff39fe9-b31c-564a-96e6-63ba3ab22842'}, {'abstract': 'The U.S.D.A. has proposed rules that all cattle moving across state lines must wear ear tags for identification, but