uri': 'nyt://article/6fe1e258-0113-5b2c-9949-286d8dad4235'}, {'abstract': 'With the ratings of “American Idol” on a downward trend, fans found Thursday night’s auditions gratifying as the show returned to its old form with hilariously deluded performers and arguments among the judges in favor of the everyone’s-a-winner tone in earlier episodes this season.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/american-idol-tries-old-tricks-in-the-face-of-stumbling-ratings/', 'snippet': 'With the ratings of “American Idol” on a downward trend, fans found Thursday night’s auditions gratifying as the show returned to its old form with hilariously deluded performers and arguments among the judges in favor of the everyone’s-a-winner t...', 'lead_paragraph': 'American Idol’s ratings this season have been on such on a downward trend that it has left some people wondering if the reality TV giant might finally have begun to stumble. So it was gratifying for many fans and bloggers to see the show return to its old form during the auditions program aired Thursday night, as the producers highlighted some hilariously deluded performers and zeroed in on arguments among the judges.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘American Idol’ Tries Old Tricks in the Face of Stumbling Ratings', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'American Idol (TV Program)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Randy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Jennifer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyler, Steven', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyler, Steven (1948- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T07:07:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca822f87-4ebe-518e-830b-9dd2328f8630', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca822f87-4ebe-518e-830b-9dd2328f8630'}, {'abstract': 'In less than a week, Mitt Romney went from inevitable to embattled to somewhere in between. Where is he now?', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/mitt-romney-the-jacksonville-jaguar/', 'snippet': 'In less than a week, Mitt Romney went from inevitable to embattled to somewhere in between. Where is he now?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wrote yesterday that last night was the most important night of Mitt Romney’s political life. Another underwhelming debate performance like the ones he delivered in South Carolina would open the door for a Newt Gingrich victory in the Florida primary. Losing Florida could begin the type of downward spiral for Romney that would lead to even less pleasant consequences.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitt Romney, the Jacksonville Jaguar', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blitzer, Wolf', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dole, Bob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schnur, Dan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jacksonville (Fla)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T07:16:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Schnur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schnur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50086901-b3c8-5a07-9ce7-dbb1002bf476', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50086901-b3c8-5a07-9ce7-dbb1002bf476'}, {'abstract': 'An overhaul would tie colleges’ eligibility for campus-based aid programs to the institutions’ success in improving value and affordability for students.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/education/obama-to-link-aid-for-colleges-to-affordability.html', 'snippet': 'An overhaul would tie colleges’ eligibility for campus-based aid programs to the institutions’ success in improving value and affordability for students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama is proposing a financial aid overhaul that for the first time would tie colleges’ eligibility for campus-based aid programs — Perkins loans, work-study jobs and supplemental grants for low-income students — to the institutions’ success in improving affordability and value for students, administration officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/us/27educ/27educ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/27/us/27educ/27educ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype