 '_id': 'nyt://article/03fcd233-38d1-533c-898a-c296ad9fbdf1', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03fcd233-38d1-533c-898a-c296ad9fbdf1'}, {'abstract': 'Salman Rushdie has “every right” to come to this country, Jaipur protestors were wrong, top Muslim leader says.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/a-conversation-with-maulana-w-khan/', 'snippet': 'Salman Rushdie has “every right” to come to this country, Jaipur protestors were wrong, top Muslim leader says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following the controversy over author Salman Rushdie’s appearance at the Jaipur Literature Festival, which ultimately ended with even a video conference with Mr. Rushdie being cancelled, India Ink is speaking with Muslim leaders about the situation, their feelings about his “The Satanic Verses” and whether politics played a part. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Maulana Wahiduddin Khan', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rushdie, Salman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Delhi (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T12:40:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c3dd910-d4ae-56c3-bded-adf260cba408', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c3dd910-d4ae-56c3-bded-adf260cba408'}, {'abstract': 'A special commission on nuclear waste is not bullish on the near-term prospects for reprocessing it so that the uranium and plutonium it contains can be reused..', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/is-spent-nuclear-fuel-really-waste/', 'snippet': 'A special commission on nuclear waste is not bullish on the near-term prospects for reprocessing it so that the uranium and plutonium it contains can be reused..', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Blue Ribbon Commission on America’s Nuclear Future was established two years ago, after the Obama administration killed a proposed repository for nuclear waste at Yucca Mountain in Nevada, one of the items on its agenda was to determine whether spent nuclear fuel was in fact waste. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Spent Nuclear Fuel Really Waste?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Wastes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plutonium', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uranium', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T12:55:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2335b0dc-7b11-5ab4-b4b9-bb26ce5de567', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2335b0dc-7b11-5ab4-b4b9-bb26ce5de567'}, {'abstract': 'In its first video in more than 10 years, Wilco meets up with the whole Popeye gang to the musical accompaniment of “Dawned on Me.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/wilco-gets-animated-with-popeye/', 'snippet': 'In its first video in more than 10 years, Wilco meets up with the whole Popeye gang to the musical accompaniment of “Dawned on Me.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'So it turns out that Jeff Tweedy, the frontman of the Chicago alternative-rock band Wilco, has a sense of humor after all. The group has just released its first video in more than 10 years, and the format is that of an old-fashioned cartoon, with Popeye, Olive Oyl, Bluto, Wimpy and Swee’Pea as the band’s fans and foils.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wilco Goes Animated With Popeye', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tweedy, Jeff', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wilco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T13:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47ff6a6d-62d8-52f5-837b-8eb8159e6f2f', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47ff6a6d-62d8-52f5-837b-8eb8159e6f2f'}, {'abstract': 'Spicy chicken wings, crisp and succulent, work for both the Super Bowl or the Chinese New Year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/dining/spicy-chicken-wings-for-the-super-bowl-or-chinese-new-year.html', 'snippet': 'Spicy chicken wings, crisp and succulent, work for both the Super Bowl or the Chinese New Year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I HAD the thought that chicken wings would be nice to make in honor of the Chinese New Year, so I pitched the idea to my editor. If wings are too banal or plebeian, it could always be thighs, I offered. The editor replied: wings absolutely, everyone loves wings! But, he said, why not something for the Super Bowl? Perhaps, I ventured, these wings could be multipurpose.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01kitchen-span/01kitchen-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01kitchen-span/01kitchen-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01kitchen-span/01kitchen-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01kitchen-span/01kitchen-span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01kitchen-span/01kitchen-span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sating the Fiery Dragon, or That Fired-Up Pigskin Fan', 'kicker': 'City Kitchen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sating the Fiery Dragon, or That Fired-Up Pigskin Fan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chickens', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T13:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8b0b9b5-69e0-5abf-8737-2b3481574160', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8b0b9b5-69e0-5abf-8737-2b3481574160'}, {'abstract': 'By buying the specialty chemicals maker Solutia, Eastman Chemical, which makes plastics, fibers and polymers, will gain share in fast-growing markets like China.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/eastman-chemical-to-buy-solutia-for-3-4-billion/', 'snippet': 'By buying the specialty chemicals maker Solutia, Eastman Chemical, which makes plastics, fibers and polymers, will gain share in fast-growing markets like China.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:19 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eastman Chemical to Buy Solutia for $3.4 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eastman Chemical Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Solutia Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T13:07:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6664c8bc-b7b9-5b71-be3a-cec01471d82c', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6664c8bc-b7b9-5b71-be3a-cec01471d82c'}, {'abstract': 'People seem to be assigning powers to Eli that he just doesn’t have, as with another quarterback that was in the news this past season.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/eli-and-the-tebow-effect/', 'snippet': 'People seem to be assigning powers to Eli that he just doesn’t have, as with another quarterback that was in the news this past season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'O.K., the headline might be a stretch, but there’s a point to be made.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eli and the Tebow Effect', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T13:11:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c832a8ca-2b43-5f93-bee6-fe03819c32b3', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c832a8ca-2b43-5f93-bee6-fe03819c32b3'}, {'abstract': 'Indian cricket player Sachin Tendulkar walks off the field after losing his wicket.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/image-of-the-day-january-27/', 'snippet': 'Indian cricket player Sachin Tendulkar walks off the field after losing his wicket.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: January 27', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cricket (Game)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tendulkar, Sachin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T13:13:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/228e90be-ec04-5e16-b79e-a8e1215ee06e', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/228e90be-ec04-5e16-b79e-a8e1215ee06e'}, {'abstract': 'Chicken wings for the Super Bowl or the Chinese New Year.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/dragon-wings/', 'snippet': 'Chicken wings for the Super Bowl or the Chinese New Year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I had fun playing with chicken wings for this week’s City Kitchen column. A lot of chicken wings. I set out to make Chinese-style wings, but the path from concept to realized dish can often be littered with somewhat less than stellar results. Trying to create a recipe sometimes takes several tries. Enlisting the (tasting) help of a few opinionated friends whose palates I trust, I experimented with a few versions until the balance of sweet and spicy rang true, with the right amount of five-spice, ginger and garlic. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dragon Wings', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T13:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ee9b61c-ee4f-55ef-a463-590eb02581a8', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ee9b61c-ee4f-55ef-a463-590eb02581a8'}, {'abstract': 'During his years in Congress, Newt Gingrich emerged as one of Washington’s most aggressive practitioners of slash-and-burn politics. He believed, and preached, tha