, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T14:17:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0739c056-4e9b-57b3-80e3-a82f00e95cf3', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0739c056-4e9b-57b3-80e3-a82f00e95cf3'}, {'abstract': 'The United States is likely to grow 2 percent to 3 percent this year, Treasury Secretary Timothy F. Geithner said in Davos, Switzerland, unless Europe fails to keep a lid on its chronic sovereign debt crisis or tensions flare with Iran.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/geithner-offers-upbeat-u-s-outlook-with-european-caveat/', 'snippet': 'The United States is likely to grow 2 percent to 3 percent this year, Treasury Secretary Timothy F. Geithner said in Davos, Switzerland, unless Europe fails to keep a lid on its chronic sovereign debt crisis or tensions flare with Iran.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:01 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Geithner Offers Upbeat U.S. Outlook, With European Caveat', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T14:19:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Alderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b28358d-b2be-5cef-bb0e-fc6c5b59896b', 'word_count': 1175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b28358d-b2be-5cef-bb0e-fc6c5b59896b'}, {'abstract': 'Irsay launches hissing war with Manning in Indianapolis while the Buccaneers confuse everyone by hiring Greg Schiano from Rutgers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/leading-off-the-circus-starts-early-in-indianapolis/', 'snippet': 'Irsay launches hissing war with Manning in Indianapolis while the Buccaneers confuse everyone by hiring Greg Schiano from Rutgers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s just pause for a few seconds here to contemplate the weirdness going on in Indianapolis, and no we are not talking about the potential difficulty of the Patriots’ team hotel stocking up on Tom Brady’s hair care products. No, it’s the hometown Colts rushing to the top of the bizarre-o-meter, with owner Jim Irsay deciding to wage a public hissing war with Peyton Manning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: The Circus Starts Early in Indianapolis', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Irsay, Jim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowe, Rob', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pagano, Chuck', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterno, Joe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiano, Greg', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Kyle', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NIKE Inc', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T14:24:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51f8510b-c19b-5aa0-949c-cfddec59dab8', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51f8510b-c19b-5aa0-949c-cfddec59dab8'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama seeks to tie a college-administered, federally-financed student aid program to efforts to cut college costs.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/obama-aid-speech/', 'snippet': 'President Obama seeks to tie a college-administered, federally-financed student aid program to efforts to cut college costs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In today’s Times, my colleague Tamar Lewin has a preview of an address that President Obama is expected to deliver at the University of Michigan on Friday morning in which he will call for an overhaul of crucial aspects of the federal financial aid system. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What if the U.S. Tied Colleges’ Financial Aid Resources to Affordability?', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T14:27:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53993d64-cdb7-5786-b8e1-cf9eb92d9323', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53993d64-cdb7-5786-b8e1-cf9eb92d9323'}, {'abstract': 'Shares in the bank have risen 64 percent since Jan. 9 when the firm started a $9.8 billion so-called rights offering, putting UniCredit at the forefront of a recent rally in European banking stocks.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/unicredit-shareholders-to-profit-from-rights-offering/', 'snippet': 'Shares in the bank have risen 64 percent since Jan. 9 when the firm started a $9.8 billion so-called rights offering, putting UniCredit at the forefront of a recent rally in European banking stocks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Investors in the Italian bank UniCredit have had a good month.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'UniCredit Shareholders to Profit From Rights Offering', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Unicredito Italiano SpA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T14:31:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c78f0d7d-a123-5d18-8e99-8cf3a9405c44', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c78f0d7d-a123-5d18-8e99-8cf3a9405c44'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Jackson’s children stamp a pair of his shoes – and a sequined glove – into the cement at a Los Angeles landmark.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/michael-jackson-immortalized-at-graumans-chinese-theater/', 'snippet': 'Michael Jackson’s children stamp a pair of his shoes – and a sequined glove – into the cement at a Los Angeles landmark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hollywood celebrities have been leaving their handprints and footprints in wet cement in front of Grauman’s Chinese Theater in Los Angeles for decades. On Thursday at dawn Michael Jackson’s children stamped a pair of the late singer’s shoes and one of his sequined gloves into a wet slab on Hollywood Boulevard to honor him, according to Agence France-Presse.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michael Jackson Honored at Grauman’s Chinese Theater', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bieber, Justin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Quincy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robinson, Smokey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T14:39:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'n