a': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Michigan, Obama Calls for Overhaul of Financial Aid', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T16:12:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64ca2030-9517-5b4a-bee2-f3734ad5d6e4', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64ca2030-9517-5b4a-bee2-f3734ad5d6e4'}, {'abstract': 'The parks department says that “it is simply too warm to make snow” for the Winter Jam, which was scheduled for Feb. 4 at Prospect Park.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/winter-jam-canceled-due-to-lack-of-winter/', 'snippet': 'The parks department says that “it is simply too warm to make snow” for the Winter Jam, which was scheduled for Feb. 4 at Prospect Park.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sorry, kids: The parks department has officially canceled winter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winter Jam Canceled Due to Lack of Winter', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Park (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T16:16:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d697c3ab-f4bf-5e94-99bb-2092dd725ae9', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d697c3ab-f4bf-5e94-99bb-2092dd725ae9'}, {'abstract': 'Novak Djokovic required five sets, physical reserves and the deep reservoir of self-belief acquired in the last two seasons to keep Andy Murray at bay on Friday in the Australian Open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/sports/tennis/28iht-tennis28.html', 'snippet': 'Novak Djokovic required five sets, physical reserves and the deep reservoir of self-belief acquired in the last two seasons to keep Andy Murray at bay on Friday in the Australian Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MELBOURNE, Australia — There were big hints of a power shift at this Australian Open. There were grueling, long-form semifinals bristling with uncertainty. But when Friday night had turned into Saturday morning in Melbourne and Novak Djokovic lay spread-eagled on his back with a fulfilled look on his stubbled face, the status quo had been preserved.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/sports/28tennis/28tennis-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/28/sports/28tennis/28tennis-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/sports/28tennis/28tennis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/sports/28tennis/28tennis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/28/sports/28tennis/28tennis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pushed to Limit, Djokovic Defeats Murray to Set Up a Familiar Final', 'kicker': 'Australian Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pushed to Limit, Djokovic Defeats Murray to Set Up a Familiar Final', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murray, Andy (1987- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T16:17:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e0d1098-f1db-5e33-bc67-5ee7056b8281', 'word_count': 1158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e0d1098-f1db-5e33-bc67-5ee7056b8281'}, {'abstract': 'Jaime Caruana, general manager of the Bank for International Settlements, says that he was against extending the phase-in period for new global banking regulations.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/a-top-central-banker-urges-no-delay-to-basel-iii/', 'snippet': 'Jaime Caruana, general manager of the Bank for International Settlements, says that he was against extending the phase-in period for new global banking regulations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — A top central banker on Friday damped the hopes of some in the banking industry that they might get more time to comply with new regulations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top Central Banker Urges No Delay to Basel III', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank for International Settlements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Basel Committee on Banking Supervision', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T16:24:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f5888fc-23c3-5f53-8008-a1f1216aca9a', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f5888fc-23c3-5f53-8008-a1f1216aca9a'}, {'abstract': 'The home of the Dallas Cowboys will open its gates for a free simulcast of Mozart’s “Magic Flute” on April 28, the Dallas Opera and the football team said on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/wolf-gang-wolf-gang-mozart-opera-at-cowboys-stadium/', 'snippet': 'The home of the Dallas Cowboys will open its gates for a free simulcast of Mozart’s “Magic Flute” on April 28, the Dallas Opera and the football team said on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It will be Sarastro’s host versus the Queen of the Night and her minions at Cowboys Stadium. The stadium, the home of the Dallas Cowboys, will open its gates for a free simulcast of Mozart’s “Magic Flute” on April 28, the Dallas Opera and the football team said on Thursday. In a statement, the Cowboys’ executive vice president for brand management, Charlotte Anderson, called it a “distinctive event.” Dallas Opera’s general director, Keith Cerny, called it a “game-changing” collaboration. The production comes from the Lyric Opera of Chicago. Officials said the opera would be shown on the “world’s largest high-definition video board structure,” which consists of four screens suspended over the field. The largest, according to the statement is 72 feet tall and 160 feet wide. There was no mention of cheerleaders or whether missed notes would be subject to instant-replay review.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "‘Wolf-gang! Wolf-gang!': Mozart Opera at Cowboys Stadium", 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cowboys Stadium (Arlington, Tex)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Cowboys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T16:25:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dc717f0-ea3d-5fbb-8e4b-769d004c9d4c', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dc717f0-ea3d-5fbb-8e4b-769d004c9d4c'}, {'abstract': 'Two new sandwich shops in New York are selling six-foot heroes for Super Bowl Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/for-super-bowl-joedough-and-no-7-sub-go-for-extra-yards/', 'snippet': 'Two new sandwich shops in New York are selling six-foot heroes for Super Bowl Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eli Manning stands 6-foot-4. But for that game-time party, a hero that measures in at a mere six feet will probably do.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': []