'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Morpurgo’s novel “War Horse” was published in 1982. Over the next 25 years, about 50,000 copies were sold. “It simply was not a book that anyone really knew about or cared about,” the author once noted in an interview. But since the release of Steven Spielberg’s Oscar-nominated film version in Britain two weeks ago, the book has sold more than 60,000 copies there, BBC News reported.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘War Horse’ Film Turns Book Into Best Seller in Britain', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morpurgo, Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T16:51:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/beb8f3ec-136d-54c5-8402-3874860be583', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/beb8f3ec-136d-54c5-8402-3874860be583'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/weekend-fare-78/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Small, interactive macaron-making classes will start on Saturday at Mille-Feuille Bakery, 552 LaGuardia Place (Bleecker Street), in Greenwich Village. The classes begin at 2 p.m., run for about four hours and cost $190 a person, with discounts for larger groups of up to six at $115 a person. Register online.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T16:51:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ab2cc3b-3ff1-529a-bff6-3a6ddbca90f9', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ab2cc3b-3ff1-529a-bff6-3a6ddbca90f9'}, {'abstract': 'The vice president of research at the Private Equity Growth Capital Council contends that the research on private equity is exhaustive and conclusive.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/another-view-private-equity-creates-value/', 'snippet': 'The vice president of research at the Private Equity Growth Capital Council contends that the research on private equity is exhaustive and conclusive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bronwyn Bailey, Ph.D., is the vice president of research at the Private Equity Growth Capital Council. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another View: Private Equity Creates Value', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T16:52:10+0000', 'document_type': 'artic