 of the capital, Damascus, and perhaps of several other neighborhoods, signaling an escalation of violence in this beleaguered country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/world/middleeast/20120128Syria-slide-XTWT/20120128Syria-slide-XTWT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 345, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/28/world/middleeast/20120128Syria-slide-XTWT/20120128Syria-slide-XTWT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 345}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/world/middleeast/20120128Syria-slide-XTWT/20120128Syria-slide-XTWT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/world/middleeast/20120128Syria-slide-XTWT/20120128Syria-slide-XTWT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/28/world/middleeast/20120128Syria-slide-XTWT/20120128Syria-slide-XTWT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Rebels Make Inroads With Help of Armed Fighters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Armed Fighters Help Syria Rebels Make Inroads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T16:59:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49b4e225-c77d-50e3-9eb1-c97027d3af14', 'word_count': 1415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49b4e225-c77d-50e3-9eb1-c97027d3af14'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to an article on visiting Jerusalem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/travel/lost-in-jerusalem.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to an article on visiting Jerusalem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: I read Travel to learn about appealing destinations and useful travel tips. I am completely uninterested in the psychological baggage and identity conflicts of Matt Gross (“Lost in Jerusalem,” Jan. 15). Furthermore, I found it offensive that he would rather visit any place on earth than Israel, because to him “Israel has always felt less like a country than a politically iffy burden.” I would expect a Travel article on Israel to report on experiences in the country unadulterated by biased personal opinion. I dare you to show me an article on any other country where your correspondent stated such an antagonism to, or disrespect for, the place he was visiting.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lost in Jerusalem', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lost in Jerusalem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T17:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/9614fc82-ef60-542f-a82c-0418ef2651b5', 'word_count': 232, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9614fc82-ef60-542f-a82c-0418ef2651b5'}, {'abstract': 'Happy Chinese New Year! Eat, drink and ink yourself a dragon tattoo.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/samurai-shopper-the-year-of-the-dragon/', 'snippet': 'Happy Chinese New Year! Eat, drink and ink yourself a dragon tattoo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Samurai Shopper hails from a tribe whose holidays are based on the moon’s orbit around the earth. This tribe gravitates toward other lunar-leaning people, especially when solar-centric Gregorians start putting fir trees in their living rooms in mid-December. So, Kung Hei Fat Choy! Happy 4,710, Year of the Black Water Dragon, to my firecracker-wielding kin who’ve provided such fulsome sustenance during our lunar year, 5,772. Eat, drink and ink yourself a dragon tattoo\xa0—\xa0unless you have Biblical issues or faint at the sight of needles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Samurai Shopper | The Year of the Dragon', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Domino, Fats', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Village (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T17:00:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By S.S. Fair', 'person': [{'firstname': 'S.', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Fair', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d7792b1-5cc1-5197-bae0-064139c70646', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d7792b1-5cc1-5197-bae0-064139c70646'}, {'abstract': 'The N.H.L. All-Star Game is 4 p.m. Sunday at Scotiabank Place, the home of the Ottawa Senators. The teams were selected via a draft Thursday night.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/n-h-l-all-star-game-rosters/', 'snippet': 'The N.H.L. All-Star Game is 4 p.m. Sunday at Scotiabank Place, the home of the Ottawa Senators. The teams were selected via a draft Thursday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.H.L. All-Star Game is 4 p.m. Sunday at Scotiabank Place, the home of the Ottawa Senators. The teams were selected via a draft Thursday night. Zdeno Chara of the Bruins and Daniel Alfredsson on the Senators were selected captains, with the Maple Leafs’ Joffrey Lupul serving as Chara’s assistant and the Rangers’ Henrik Lundqvist serving as Alfredsson’s. (Players are listed in the order they were drafted, with the six rookies assigned to each team at the bottom.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.H.L. All-Star Game Rosters', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALL STAR GAMES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T17:04:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0442aa57-34ed-5ba9-a412-4a8268fcdfe0', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0442aa57-34ed-5ba9-a412-4a8268fcdfe0'}, {'abstract': 'The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration has received 87 reports 