ts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ca82009-3659-5aad-894f-e4bc2e2a0dd1', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ca82009-3659-5aad-894f-e4bc2e2a0dd1'}, {'abstract': 'DURING the Armani couture show, I kept glancing across the runway at Jessica Chastain. Probably many people were, and all with the same thought: Does she see a dress here she might like to wear to the Oscars?', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/and-in-couture-is/', 'snippet': 'DURING the Armani couture show, I kept glancing across the runway at Jessica Chastain. Probably many people were, and all with the same thought: Does she see a dress here she might like to wear to the Oscars?', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURING the Armani couture show the other day, I kept glancing across the runway at Jessica Chastain. Probably many people were, and all with the same thought: Does she see a dress here she might like to wear to the Oscars? No doubt Mr. Armani will be happy to make her something. Ms. Chastain learned she had been nominated for “The Help” shortly before the show started. People around her applauded. Maybe in all the excitement everything looked blurry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'And in Couture Is …', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T18:43:33+0000', 'document_type': 'arti