performance over the last six years has been an occasion for admiration, mingled with bursts of skepticism and even disbelief. It is seldom a surprise that Scandinavian countries occupy at least four spots in the top 15, given their lauded environmental sensibilities (excepting, perhaps, Norwegian whalers and Danish fishermen).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Racing Up (and Down) the Performance Index', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yale University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latvia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T19:32:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a917ada7-4bb6-5c25-b12d-a66ec5218839', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a917ada7-4bb6-5c25-b12d-a66ec5218839'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich’s momentum from the South Carolina wanes days ahead of the Florida primary. Paul Volpe reports.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/timescast-gingrich-loses-momentum/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich’s momentum from the South Carolina wanes days ahead of the Florida primary. Paul Volpe reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newt Gingrich’s momentum from the South Carolina wanes days ahead of the Florida primary. Paul Volpe reports. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast: Gingrich Loses Momentum', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T19:32:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2948ac11-0c13-5c40-9b7a-644c7fa61162', 'word_count': 18, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2948ac11-0c13-5c40-9b7a-644c7fa61162'}, {'abstract': 'Aneesh Chopra, the White House’s first-ever chief technology officer, was charged with spearheading the modernization of the federal government’s technology.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/top-technology-official-leaving-the-white-house/', 'snippet': 'Aneesh Chopra, the White House’s first-ever chief technology officer, was charged with spearheading the modernization of the federal government’s technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aneesh Chopra, the White House’s first chief technology officer, will step down, the White House said Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top Technology Official Leaving the White House', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T19:32:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f720995c-d61c-56e0-904d-147a436179b6', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f720995c-d61c-56e0-904d-147a436179b6'}, {'abstract': 'Periodically ballet is pronounced dead. But the choreographer Alexei Ratmansky shows that’s not true.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/arts/dance/signs-of-choreographic-life-alexei-ratmansky-and-mark-morris.html', 'snippet': 'Periodically ballet is pronounced dead. But the choreographer Alexei Ratmansky shows that’s not true.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVERY so often someone declares ballet dead. The theater critic Kenneth Tynan even did so in the 1960s, a decade that many of us assume must have been a golden age. (The choreographer Frederick Ashton said, “It’s having the biggest funeral in history.”) In 2010 it was the turn of Jennifer Homans, the dance critic of The New Republic, in the epilogue of her ballet history, “Apollo’s Angels.” In 1993 — I’d better come clean — it was me. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29RATMANSKY2_SPAN/29RATMANSKY2_SPAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29RATMANSKY2_SPAN/29RATMANSKY2_SPAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29RATMANSKY2_SPAN/29RATMANSKY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29RATMANSKY2_SPAN/29RATMANSKY2_SPAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29RATMANSKY2_SPAN/29RATMANSKY2_SPAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Reasons The Patient Is Still Kicking', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Reasons The Patient Is Still Kicking', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bolshoi Ballet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratmansky, Alexei', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T19:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c7f807a-6d59-5eec-bb86-01cda5a5051d', 'word_count': 1229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c7f807a-6d59-5eec-bb86-01cda5a5051d'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers report on whether they’re keeping more money in their checking account to avoid fees or switching to banks that don’t require minimum balances.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/avoiding-monthly-balance-minimums-on-checking-accounts/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers report on whether they’re keeping more money in their checking account to avoid fees or switching to banks that don’t require minimum balances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s Your Money column, which I wrote with the Bucks stalwart Ann Carrns, we look at the question of why banks don’t let you know the average monthly balance in your bank account, even when they’re using that number to figure out what fees to charge you. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Avoiding Monthly Balance Minimums on Checking Accounts', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Checks and Checking Accounts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Capital One Financial Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Company', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T19:37:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce02a19e-b7b6-5491-9fa2-f2f6bcd34705', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce02a19e-b7b6-5491-9fa2-f2f6bcd34705'}, {'abstract': 'Twitter incited anger among its international users on Friday after it announced a new method of blocking individual posts from appearing in certain countries. But some Internet advocacy groups defended it.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/twitters-new-policy-on-blocking-posts-is-attacked-and-defended/', 'snippet': 'Twitter incited anger among its international users on Friday after it announced a new method of blocking individual posts from appearing in certain countries. But some Internet advocacy groups defended it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twitter users around the world reacted with confusion and a sense of betrayal on Friday to the company’s announcement that it had developed the capability to “reactively withhold” certain posts in certain countries. To many, the language sounded like a euphemism for censorship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twitter’s New Policy on Blocking Posts Is Attacked, and Defended', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T19:39:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2e68324-ad69-51cf-a658-e49ebf6d523a', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2e68324-ad69-51cf-a658-e49ebf6d523a'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Tippett’s “Child of Our Time,” inspired by the events leading to Kristallnacht, is coming to Carnegie Hall on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/arts/music/michael-tippetts-child-of-our-time-fits-with-winter.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Tippett’s “Child of Our Time,” inspired by the events leading to Kristallnacht, is coming to Carnegie Hall on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': '“THE world turns on its dark side — it is winter,” the chorus sings near the start of “A Child of Our Time” (1939-41), an oratorio by the English composer Michael Tippett. Unlike Handel’s “Messiah” and Bach’s great Passions, the formal and spiritual models Tippett emulated, his oratorio fills no particular slot in the ecclesiastical calendar.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29INTO1/29INTO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29INTO1/29INTO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/arts/29INTO1/29INTO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Darkly Spiritual Challenge to Injustice', 'kicker': 'Into The Music', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Darkly Spiritual Challenge to Injustice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Collegiate Chorale', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tippett, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date