5-9d7d-c01f27b39c58'}, {'abstract': 'Jeanette Winterson reviews a new book about Henry Miller’s controversial novel “Tropic of Cancer.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/book-review-podcast-the-legacy-of-henry-millers-tropic-of-cancer/', 'snippet': 'Jeanette Winterson reviews a new book about Henry Miller’s controversial novel “Tropic of Cancer.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the New York Times Book Review Jeanette Winterson reviews Frederick Turner’s “Renegade: Henry Miller and the Making of ‘Tropic of Cancer,’ ” about this controversial novel, which was published in the United States in 1961. Ms. Winterson writes that Mr. Turner “cleverly places Miller in a line of American folklore heroes, real and invented, like Daniel Boone and Davy Crockett, Tom Sawyer and Huck Finn.” But she takes issue with the book when it comes to addressing Mr. Miller’s treatment of women. Ms. Winterson writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast: The Legacy of Henry Miller’s ‘Tropic of Cancer’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galassi, Jonathan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGrath, Charles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Henry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turner, Frederick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winterson, Jeanette', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T20:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'org