': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/27/business/apple-cook/apple-cook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tim Cook: ‘We Care About Every Worker’', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T20:33:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Duhigg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Duhigg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/886520b1-d1ab-50fb-8686-cc12523f83a0', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/886520b1-d1ab-50fb-8686-cc12523f83a0'}, {'abstract': 'Tierney Sutton radiates good will, but she and and her band filled Birdland with an air of gravity, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/arts/music/the-tierney-sutton-band-plays-at-birdland.html', 'snippet': 'Tierney Sutton radiates good will, but she and and her band filled Birdland with an air of gravity, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An air of ceremonial gravity infused the music of the Tierney Sutton Band on Wednesday evening at Birdland, where Ms. Sutton, a Los Angeles-based jazz singer, and her group performed most of its recent album, “American Road,” which has been nominated for two Grammys. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/arts/SUTTON/SUTTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 690, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/arts/SUTTON/SUTTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/28/arts/SUTTON/SUTTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunny Face and Sounds Don’t Hide Dark Reality', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sunny Face And Sounds Don’t Hide Dark Reality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Birdland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sutton, Tierney', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T20:35:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d591e0a-ad96-55d1-a599-15b285fd70f6', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d591e0a-ad96-55d1-a599-15b285fd70f6'}, {'abstract': 'An updated look at PolitiFact’s report cards of the Republican presidential candidates.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/another-check-on-the-campaigns-truthiness/', 'snippet': 'An updated look at PolitiFact’s report cards of the Republican presidential candidates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When we last looked at how the Republican candidates for president were faring with the facts, there had been just a few debates. But Thursday night’s debate in Jacksonville, Fla., was the 25th time at least two of the candidates have gotten together to argue. A presidential debate, like the campaign trail in general, is often an unwelcoming environment for unadulterated truth. Indeed, our last post on PolitiFact, a venture of The St. Petersburg Times that grades political statements on their validity, came while the campaign was still just simmering. But it’s come to a full boil now, and most of the candidates’ PolitiFact report cards have deteriorated accordingly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Check on the Campaign’s Truthiness', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T20:47:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/949b548b-4347-5485-a5c9-9f1a84e37b65', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/949b548b-4347-5485-a5c9-9f1a84e37b65'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Global Group has helped bring Chinese companies public in the United States through reverse mergers, or buying the shell of defunct American companies that had been publicly listed.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/f-b-i-searches-offices-of-n-y-adviser-on-chinese-reverse-mergers/', 'snippet': 'The New York Global Group has helped bring Chinese companies public in the United States through reverse mergers, or buying the shell of defunct American companies that had been publicly listed.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:41 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.B.I. Looks Into Adviser on Chinese Reverse Mergers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T20:56:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89b2d654-5d79-5057-ae02-3bed974db90b', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89b2d654-5d79-5057-ae02-3bed974db90b'}, {'abstract': 'After making the beef broth for French onion soup, shred the meat and make a salad with it.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/salad-from-the-soup-pot/', 'snippet': 'After making the beef broth for French onion soup, shred the meat and make a salad with it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s column, I give a recipe for a cheesy onion soup made from a stock rich with oxtails. So for the frugal cook, the question is: what to do with the oxtails after you’ve strained them from the broth? Surely gnawing on them warm and glistening isn’t the only option. (Though it’s a good one.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Salad From the Soup Pot', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T20:56:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f716079b-7a7c-5237-aea1-de65f925acc1', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f716079b-7a7c-5237-aea1-de65f925acc1'}, {'abstract': 'How far will companies go to create a favorable impression online? Much farther than you might think. The cosmetic surgery chain Lifestyle Lift, which was fined $300,000 two years ago for creating fake Web sites with fake testimonials, provides the clearest case to date of aggressive deceit.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/faking-it-to-make-it-a-beautiful-try/', 'snippet': 'How far will companies go to create a favorable impression online? Much farther than you might think. The cosmetic surgery chain Lifestyle Lift, which was fined $300,000 two years ago for creating fake Web sites with fake testimonials, provides th...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fake reviews on the Internet are probably everywhere. We just don’t know exactly where. The Kindle Fire case on Amazon, which I wrote about today,\xa0 came to light only\xa0because an outraged customer contacted me, saying he felt he was being bribed for a positive notice. But if we don’t know the volume of counterfeits, one thing is clear: some companies will go to enormous efforts to throw a positive light on themselves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Faking It to Make It: A Beautiful Try', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Counterfeit Merchandise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastic Surgery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lifestyle Lift', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T20:57:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d53d6538-6808-5d66-9b28-a28833f6dd87', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d53d6538-6808-5d66-9b28-a28833f6dd87'}, {'abstract': 'A recipe for one-pot French onion soup with garlic-Gruyère croutons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/dining/french-onion-soup-with-garlic-gruyere-croutons-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'A recipe for one-pot French onion soup with garlic-Gruyère croutons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adapted from Philippe Bertineau, Benoit, Manhattan', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01APPE_SPAN/01APPE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01APPE_SPAN/01APPE_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01APPE_SPAN/01APPE_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01APPE_SPAN/01APPE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 668, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01APPE_SPAN/01APPE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01APPE_SPAN/01APPE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidt