 in 2010, with its most serious concern being that the drug might contribute to heart rhythm abnormalities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/health/bydureon-a-diabetes-drug-from-amylin-wins-fda-approval.html', 'snippet': 'The Food and Drug Administration twice declined to approve Bydureon in 2010, with its most serious concern being that the drug might contribute to heart rhythm abnormalities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amylin Pharmaceuticals won federal approval on Friday for its new, more convenient drug for Type 2 diabetes, ending years of setbacks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/business/Drug/Drug-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 970, 'width': 910, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Diabetes Drug Injected Weekly Wins F.D.A. Approval', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Diabetes Drug Injected Weekly Wins F.D.A. Approval', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMYLIN PHARMACEUTICALS INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Novo Nordisk A/S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-27T22:34:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58f81d3c-7d93-55b5-946d-15b1e957a758', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58f81d3c-7d93-55b5-946d-15b1e957a758'}, {'abstract': 'The face of the profession is becoming increasingly fresh, with some clients receiving motivational guidance from coaches young enough to be their children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/fashion/should-a-life-coach-have-a-life-first.html', 'snippet': 'The face of the profession is becoming increasingly fresh, with some clients receiving motivational guidance from coaches young enough to be their children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON a recent winter evening, Jeannine Yoder, a life coach, was at her Upper West Side apartment, hosting a monthly MasterMind, an industry term for a group session done via conference call. Ms. Yoder began her coaching business, theRSVPrev.com — which is centered on the “life-empowerment” mantra Restore, Simplify, Verify, Power — last year to help finance an acting career, only to find coaching taking center stage. She quickly built a stable of 18 clients (including Amanda Perna, a contestant on “Project Runway”) who each pay her $125 for the weekly hourlong sessions.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/fashion/29JPCOACHES1_SPAN/29JPCOACHES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/fashion/29JPCOACHES1_SPAN/29JPCOACHES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/fashion/29JPCOACHES1_SPAN/29JPCOACHES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/fashion/29JPCOACHES1_SPAN/29JPCOACHES1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg'