'nyt://article/d48e28c7-d7f5-55a4-be4f-b945a4d22b6e', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d48e28c7-d7f5-55a4-be4f-b945a4d22b6e'}, {'abstract': 'The California Air Resources Board approved a recommendation that included the requirement of 1.4 million additional zero-emission and transitional zero-emission vehicles to be on state roads by 2025.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/california-board-votes-unanimously-to-toughen-zero-emission-vehicle-mandate/', 'snippet': 'The California Air Resources Board approved a recommendation that included the requirement of 1.4 million additional zero-emission and transitional zero-emission vehicles to be on state roads by 2025.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a unanimous vote on Friday, the California Air Resources Board, known as CARB, affirmed a major expansion of its Advanced Clean Car rules. According to CARB’s projection, the program would result in an additional 1.4 million zero- and near-zero-emission vehicles on the state’s roads by 2025.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California Board Votes Unanimously to Toughen Zero-Emission Vehicle Mandate', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'California Air Resources Board', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Natural Resources Defense Council', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Union of Concerned Scientists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T00:31:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline'