)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LaGuardia Airport (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Newark Liberty International Airport (NJ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Teterboro Airport (NJ)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T00:46:42+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/15102109-aaa6-52e3-8eda-16398531aed1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/15102109-aaa6-52e3-8eda-16398531aed1'}, {'abstract': 'The Issue Project Room opened its new quarters in Brooklyn this week with the Gaudeamus Muziekweek festival, featuring the Wet Ink Ensemble.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/arts/music/wet-ink-in-gaudeamus-muziekweek-at-new-issue-project-room.html', 'snippet': 'The Issue Project Room opened its new quarters in Brooklyn this week with the Gaudeamus Muziekweek festival, featuring the Wet Ink Ensemble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been a long time coming — about four years of raising money and renovating — but on Wednesday evening the Issue Project Room settled into its new digs in the former Board of Education building at 110 Livingston Street in downtown Brooklyn. For anyone who spent time in Issue Project’s former home, a tiny space at the Old American Can Factory, also in Brooklyn, this is a new world: the room is spacious (5,000 square feet) and rich in retro grandeur, with marble floors, columns and arches, and a high, ornate ceiling. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Music Opens a New Hall', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Music Opens a New Hall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, 