 slopes by the religious faithful; wild goats scrambling across impossibly steep cliffs; and Buddhist monks meditating as they have for centuries in a place where newcomers find themselves gasping for air.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/world/zhandetan/zhandetan-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/28/world/zhandetan/zhandetan-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/world/zhandetan/zhandetan-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/world/zhandetan/zhandetan-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/28/world/zhandetan/zhandetan-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Teaching Tibetan Ways, a School in China Is an Unlikely Wonder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Teaching Tibetan Ways, a School in China Is an Unlikely Wonder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qinghai Province (China)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anymachen Tibetan Culture Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T00:55:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Levin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3800987-e983-5306-8fdb-23be3eb7c459', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3800987-e983-5306-8fdb-23be3eb7c459'}, {'abstract': 'The compact crossover market is a crowded field, and Honda, with the new CR-V, has decided to meet the competition with a carefully graduated step forward rather than a shoot-for-the-moon upgrade.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/reviewing-the-2012-honda-cr-v/', 'snippet': 'The compact crossover market is a crowded field, and Honda, with the new CR-V, has decided to meet the competition with a carefully graduated step forward rather than a shoot-for-the-moon upgrade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his first vehicle evaluation for The Times, Csaba Csere (pronounced CHUB-uh CHED-uh) reviews the 2012 Honda CR-V in Sunday’s Automobiles Section. Mr. Csere, an M.I.T.-trained automotive engineer, was on the staff of Car and Driver magazine for 28 years and served as editor in chief from 1993 to 2008. He previously wrote for the Automobiles section about the search for a fast-charger plug that would be compatible with all of the existing electric cars.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing the 2012 Honda CR-V', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN HONDA MOTOR CO', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T00:59:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8317e22-6308-54bc-9fea-40081e257d6c', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8317e22-6308-54bc-9fea-40081e257d6c'}, {'abstract': 'Ronald O. Perelman, the billionaire financier, lost a bitter legal battle as a federal jury decided that his company must pay $16 million to Donald Drapkin, a former business associate.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/perelman-loses-court-battle-over-16-million-suit/', 'snippet': 'Ronald O. Perelman, the billionaire financier, lost a bitter legal battle as a federal jury decided that his company must pay $16 million to Donald Drapkin, a former business associate.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:58 p.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Perelman Loses Court Battle Over $16 Million Suit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drapkin, Donald G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perelman, Ronald O', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MacAndrews & Forbes Holdings Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T01:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden and Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bb8fc91-d854-55c3-bed2-029ee94a3e78', 'word_count': 982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bb8fc91-d854-55c3-bed2-029ee94a3e78'}, {'abstract': 'Antony and the Johnsons’ performance with a 60-piece orchestra on Thursday night, called “Swanlights,” was commissioned by the Museum of Modern Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/arts/music/antony-and-the-johnsons-at-radio-city-music-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Antony and the Johnsons’ performance with a 60-piece orchestra on Thursday night, called “Swanlights,” was commissioned by the Museum of Modern Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wonderment and sorrow course through the songs of Antony Hegarty, who leads Antony and the Johnsons. Those are immense emotions, and on Thursday night he performed in a place to match their scale: Radio City Music Hall. A towering backdrop was often illuminated by lasers; his band members were supplemented by a 60-piece orchestra. He had chosen his most contemplative songs, with sustained melodies like lullabies grown operatic, carrying lyrics to proclaim and repeat revelations: “I need another world/This one’s nearly gone.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/antony/antony-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/antony/antony-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/antony/antony-thum