ges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tuition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T02:10:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1763a67c-2047-5a25-9d04-636dbcc0706b', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1763a67c-2047-5a25-9d04-636dbcc0706b'}, {'abstract': 'Waters Crest, a tiny winery in Cutchogue, is run by a self-taught winemaker who owns no vineyards, but it has food-friendly whites with a great texture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/nyregion/from-waters-crest-rich-textures-in-food-friendly-whites.html', 'snippet': 'Waters Crest, a tiny winery in Cutchogue, is run by a self-taught winemaker who owns no vineyards, but it has food-friendly whites with a great texture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The food-friendly whites made at Waters Crest in Cutchogue and sold in its adjacent tasting room, in the North Road Commons industrial park, are noteworthy for their texture.\xa0', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Like an Avocado in a Glass', 'kicker': 'Long Island Vines', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Like an Avocado in a Glass', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Waters Crest (Cutchogue, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T02:12:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name