y’s governor would like you to remember where their stadium is.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '#trendingnyc: The Week on Twitter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '#Trending N.Y.C.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T02:26:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/487b7620-3a72-5f6f-83c6-f638bd8eeff8', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/487b7620-3a72-5f6f-83c6-f638bd8eeff8'}, {'abstract': 'Fresh from a State of the Union speech he used to make his case for re-election, President Obama took to the road this week to build support for his economic message of fairness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/01/28/us/politics/28obama.html', 'snippet': 'Fresh from a State of the Union speech he used to make his case for re-election, President Obama took to the road this week to build support for his economic message of fairness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fresh from a State of the Union speech he used to make his case for re-election, President Obama took to the road this week to build support for his economic message of fairness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/us/politics/28o