rial is scheduled to begin on March 19.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/sports/baseball/expert-witnesses-faulted-in-suit-against-mets-owners.html', 'snippet': 'A trustee seeks hundreds of millions for victims of Bernard L. Madoff’s Ponzi scheme, and a trial is scheduled to begin on March 19.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawyers for the victims of Bernard L. Madoff have accused the Mets’ owners of enriching themselves with illegitimate profits from his Ponzi scheme. The owners, in turn, have called the lawyers shakedown artists bent on ruining their good reputations to extort money. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Expert Witnesses Faulted in Suit Against Mets’ Owners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Expert Witnesses Faulted in Suit Against Mets’ Owners', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katz, Saul B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ponzi and Pyramid Schemes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilpon, Fred', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T02:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94d1b64b-64a7-557a-9cb0-0d06f2a7e90b', 'word_count': 976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94d1b64b-64a7-557a-9cb0-0d06f2a7e90b'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Hegyes played Juan Epstein, a remedial student with a slouch and a towering Afro.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/arts/television/robert-hegyes-60-of-welcome-back-kotter-is-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Hegyes played Juan Epstein, a remedial student with a slouch and a towering Afro.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert Hegyes, who played Juan Epstein, the Sweathog voted Most Likely to Take a Life, on the 1970s sitcom “Welcome Back, Kotter,” died on Thursday in Edison, N.J. He was 60.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/arts/HEGYES/HEGYES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/28/arts/HEGYES/HEGYES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/28/arts/HEGYES/HEGYES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Robert Hegyes, a Sweathog on ‘Kotter,’ Dies at 60', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robert Hegyes, 60, a Sweathog on ‘Kotter’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T02:54:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d298e04-f8d8-54d2-9f7a-0b2a86a5c8b9', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d298e04-f8d8-54d2-9f7a-0b2a86a5c8b9'}, {'abstract': 'Steve Hindy, president of the Brooklyn Brewery, feeds the cat, might grab a tennis racket and sometimes imbibes an ale on Sundays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/nyregion/for-steve-hindy-finding-a-brew-that-is-true-for-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Hindy, president of the Brooklyn Brewery, feeds the cat, might grab a tennis racket and sometimes imbibes an ale on Sundays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As chairman and president of the Brooklyn Brewery, Steve Hindy enjoys the privilege of having one of his favorite brews, Brooklyn Brown Ale, on tap in his kitchen. Mr. Hindy, 62, became intrigued with beer-making in the 1980s while a Beirut-based Middle East correspondent for The Associated Press. He and a neighbor, Tom Potter, then a lawyer, went into the brewery business in 1988. Mr. Hindy lives in an 1840s clapboard house in Gowanus with his wife, Ellen Foote, 61, the principal of Intermediate School 89 in TriBeCa, and their cat, Pinsky. Their daughter, Lily, 28, lives nearby in Prospect-Lefferts Gardens and is a frequent Sunday visitor.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/nyregion/29ROUTINE2/29ROUTINE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/nyregion/29ROUTINE2/29ROUTINE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/nyregion/29ROUTINE2/29ROUTINE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cat Food, Sports and, Yes, Brew', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cat Food, Sports and, Yes, Brew', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Brewery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gowanus (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T02:54:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6593bb2-910c-559b-a3db-f24d7df8f5fc', 'word_count': 721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6593bb2-910c-559b-a3db-f24d7df8f5fc'}, {'abstract': 'Chevron’s fourth-quarter profit declined to $5.1 billion, or $2.58 a share, from $5.3 billion, or $2.64, a year earlier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/business/profit-slips-for-chevron-and-disappoints-analysts.html', 'snippet': 'Chevron’s fourth-quarter profit declined to $5.1 billion, or $2.58 a share, from $5.3 billion, or $2.64, a year earlier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chevron’s fourth-quarter profit declined to $5.1 billion, or $2.58 a share, from $5.3 billion, or $2.64, a year earlier. Its earnings per share were 32 cents below the average of five analysts’ estimates compiled by Bloomberg. Sales rose 11 percent to nearly $60 billion during the quarter. Chevron’s American refineries lost an average $2.2 million a day during the final three months of 2011 as crude-processing margins shrank and maintenance work at a California plant curbed fuel output, the company said in a statement. Chevron added the equivalent of 1.67 billion barrels in reserves last year, enough to replace 171 percent of the oil and gas the company pumped last year. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Profit Slips for Chevron, Disappointing Analysts', 'kicker': 'Business Briefing | Company News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Profit Slips For Chevron, Disappointing Analysts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevron Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T02:55:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bloomberg News', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bloomberg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'News', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bc08a62-c65a-515d-a118-a4c7f1b082e0', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bc08a62-c65a-515d-a118-a4c7f1b082e0'}, {'abstract': 'In which a fairly common word appears, surprisingly, for the first time.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/27/half/', 'snippet': 'In which a fairly common word appears, surprisingly, for the first time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY’S PUZZLE — If you ever want to look at your daily crossword puzzle in an entirely different way, take a gander at the “Analyze” feature on Xword Info. Just go to any puzzle on the site, scroll down and click the “Analyze this puzzle” button. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Cuts Power in Half', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 