” (St. Martin’s Press, $27.99), the book critic Dan Cryer ably captures the theologian who was the son of a United States senator and became a champion of liberal political causes in religion. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/nyregion/29BOOK_SPAN/29BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/nyregion/29BOOK_SPAN/29BOOK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/nyregion/29BOOK_SPAN/29BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/nyregion/29BOOK_SPAN/29BOOK_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/nyregion/29BOOK_SPAN/29BOOK_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tending the Soul, and Earthly Gardens', 'kicker': 'Bookshelf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tending the Soul, And Earthly Gardens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reitano, Joanne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T03:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role'