r': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peter, Paul and Mary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T05:04:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2e27085-54d2-5de1-b430-1b2610901fd4', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2e27085-54d2-5de1-b430-1b2610901fd4'}, {'abstract': 'The report from a task force examining how to compensate thousands of North Carolinians who were sterilized against their will under a state program was delivered to Gov. Bev Perdue on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/us/north-carolina-report-delivered-on-eugenics-program.html', 'snippet': 'The report from a task force examining how to compensate thousands of North Carolinians who were sterilized against their will under a state program was delivered to Gov. Bev Perdue on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The report from a task force examining how to compensate thousands of North Carolinians who were sterilized against their will under a state program was delivered to Gov. Bev Perdue on Friday. The governor has said she will review the report, which suggests $50,000 per living victim and mental health services, and will make her recommendations to the legislature. The program, which ran from 1929 to 1974, was intended to reduce welfare rolls by preventing mostly poor, uneducated and sometimes mentally handicapped people from bearing children. About 7,600 people were deemed unfit to reproduce. The task force estimates that as many as 2,000 of them are still alive. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Carolina: Report Delivered on Eugenics Program', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Carolina: Report Delivered On Eugenics Program', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sterilization (Biological)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T05:20:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/59fd4eb9-5100-5692-a97a-db30b2b51255', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59fd4eb9-5100-5692-a97a-db30b2b51255'}, {'abstract': 'The child was found unresponsive on Wednesday, and his death was ruled a homicide by the New York City medical examiner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/nyregion/bronx-man-charged-with-murder-in-death-of-girlfriends-son.html', 'snippet': 'The child was found unresponsive on Wednesday, and his death was ruled a homicide by the New York City medical examiner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Bronx man was charged with murder on Friday in the death of his girlfriend’s 1-year-old son, the police said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bronx Man Charged With Murder in Death of 1-Year-Old', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bronx Man Charged With Murder in Death of 1-Year-Old', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T05:21:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73b539f6-539b-58d5-9ee4-2c28555ac847', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73b539f6-539b-58d5-9ee4-2c28555ac847'}, {'abstract': 'Sheriff Joe Arpaio of Maricopa County said Friday that a man accused of threatening to kill him was arrested in Tennessee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/us/arizona-arrest-of-man-accused-in-death-threat-case.html', 'snippet': 'Sheriff Joe Arpaio of Maricopa County said Friday that a man accused of threatening to kill him was arrested in Tennessee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sheriff Joe Arpaio of Maricopa County said Friday that a man accused of threatening to kill him was arrested in Tennessee. Adam E. Cox, 33, was arrested on an unrelated warrant, but he is the prime suspect in the death threat inquiry, Sheriff Arpaio said in a statement. Mr. Cox is accused of threatening to kill the sheriff and his family last year, perhaps because of the sheriff’s continuing investigation into the legitimacy of President Obama’s birth certificate, the sheriff said. Sheriff Arpaio, who called Mr. Cox an “Obama fanatic,” said a “cold case posse” that includes retired detectives and lawyers working as volunteers would announce its findings within 30 days. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arizona: Arrest of Man Accused in Death Threat Case', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Southwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Arizona: Arrest of Man Accused In Death Threat Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maricopa County (Ariz)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'pe