re from her more experienced opponent and sonic soul mate Maria Sharapova.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Azarenka Powers Past Sharapova, Claims No. 1 Ranking', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T11:29:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By CHRISTOPHER CLAREY', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CLAREY', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74dd7a1e-c1b3-5570-b091-484ffd9e51fe', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74dd7a1e-c1b3-5570-b091-484ffd9e51fe'}, {'abstract': 'Chad Ochocinco has had a strangely quiet season, but on Twitter he became friends with John Boehner this week.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/the-state-of-chad-ochocinco/', 'snippet': 'Chad Ochocinco has had a strangely quiet season, but on Twitter he became friends with John Boehner this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Believe it or not, Chad Ochocinco is still a member of the Patriots.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The State of Chad Ochocinco', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ochocinco, Chad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T11:55:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'midd