t.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/sports/football/for-giants-quarterback-and-coach-together-in-excellence.html', 'snippet': 'Coaches and quarterbacks often have their fates — and histories — tied together, and the Giants’ Tom Coughlin and quarterback Eli Manning are no different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — Eli Manning rarely gets animated when taking questions from reporters, but his detachment reached a new level last week when he was asked if he ever tires of considering questions about his legacy.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/dog-giants/dog-giants-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 794, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/dog-giants/dog-giants-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/dog-giants/dog-giants-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Giants, Quarterback and Coach Together in Excellence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coach and Quarterback Are Building, Not Belaboring, a Legacy Together', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Eli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T17:36:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/678d2f9e-dff6-52eb-ad21-0922dbc3c757', 'word_count': 1012, 'uri': 'nyt://article/678d2f9e-dff6-52eb-ad21-0922dbc3c757'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich picked up the endorsement of Herman Cain, his former rival, as he barreled through a series of speeches and town-hall-style meetings Saturday on Florida’s “Treasure Coast.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/us/politics/gingrich-ignoring-attacks-plays-up-ties-to-reagan.html', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich picked up the endorsement of Herman Cain, his former rival, as he barreled through a series of speeches and town-hall-style meetings Saturday on Florida’s “Treasure Coast.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORT ST. LUCIE, Fla. — Despite signs that he could lose the important Florida primary on Tuesday, Newt Gingrich, who picked up the endorsement of a former opponent, Herman Cain, pledged Saturday to stay in the nominating race until the very end, telling reporters he would press on until the Republican convention in Tampa in August.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29campaign1/29campaign1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29campaign1/29campaign1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29campaign1/29campaign1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'w