', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T18:19:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By BENJAMIN HOFFMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'HOFFMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0a44ea9-9dbe-5b5c-ba59-d99eed75582e', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0a44ea9-9dbe-5b5c-ba59-d99eed75582e'}, {'abstract': 'The Indianapolis Colts are hosting next Sunday’s Super Bowl while the club and the owner Jim Irsay contemplate tectonic shifts in the fortunes of the franchise.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/sports/football/for-the-owner-jim-irsay-and-the-colts-the-dream-may-be-over.html', 'snippet': 'The Indianapolis Colts are hosting next Sunday’s Super Bowl while the club and the owner Jim Irsay contemplate tectonic shifts in the fortunes of the franchise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS — His office has been stripped of much memorabilia, the guitar once owned by Jerry Garcia and the original manuscript scroll of Jack Kerouac’s classic “On the Road” sent to a local museum in anticipation of the tourists and parties to come. So Jim Irsay has his televisions and his Twitter feed, and pictures of the Rolling Stones and the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. keeping him company until his team re-emerges. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/irsay/irsay-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 782, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/irsay/irsay-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/irsay/irsay-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dream May Be Over for Irsay and the Colts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Dream May Be Over For Irsay and the Colts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indianapolis (Ind)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Irsay, Jim', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manning, Peyton', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T18:26:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c72a9416-7dbd-5579-bdad-0ee7b2b4afc3', 'word_count': 1545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c72a9416-7dbd-5579-bdad-0ee7b2b4afc3'}, {'abstract': 'Indianapolis is far from flashy. But it became a Super Bowl host, in part because eighth graders hand-delivered the city’s bids for the game to N.F.L. owners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/sports/football/super-bowl-eighth-graders-helped-indianapolis-land-game.html', 'snippet': 'Indianapolis is far from flashy. But it became a Super Bowl host, in part because eighth graders hand-delivered the city’s bids for the game to N.F.L. owners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS — As drizzle shrouded the city in a damp chill last week, and the downtown steam plant churned billows of clouds into a low sky. A train rumbled past the football stadium carrying flatbeds of tractors, and a question hung as plainly as the 30-story facsimile of the Lombardi Trophy plastered on the side of a downtown hotel. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/dog-indianapolis/dog-indianapolis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eighth Graders Helped a Low-Key City Land the Super Bowl', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indianapolis Did Its Homework', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indianapolis (Ind)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T18:28:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Branch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6c2e600-1183-5fb1-9faf-94aa38fbf497', 'word_count': 1327, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6c2e600-1183-5fb1-9faf-94aa38fbf497'}, {'abstract': 'Confronting an outbreak of Tibetan protest in western Sichuan Province, Chinese authorities have cordoned off the area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/world/asia/chinese-crack-down-to-curb-spread-of-tibetan-unrest.html', 'snippet': 'Confronting an outbreak of Tibetan protest in western Sichuan Province, Chinese authorities have cordoned off the area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHENGDU, China — This regional metropolis is roughly 200 miles from the wave of protest by ethnic Tibetans that is sweeping the towering mountains of western Sichuan Province. But take a stroll through Chengdu’s Tibetan quarter, and the tensions generated by the distant unrest become palpable. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/world/29china1/29china1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/world/29china1/29china1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/world/29china1/29china1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/world/29china1/29china1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/world/29china1/29china1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Crackdown Seals Off Ethnic Unrest', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese Crack Down to Curb Unrest Among Tibetans in Western Sichuan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chengdu (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sichuan Province (China)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T18:31:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fdb6673-0029-5950-8724-49e0eecef368', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fdb6673-0029-5950-8724-49e0eecef368'}, {'abstract': 'With two natural first basemen on the roster, Manager Jim Leyland will have to put one of them at a suboptimal position. Which configuration would be the least inefficient?', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/keeping-score-for-tigers-defensive-issues-that-are-hard-to-outslug/', 'snippet': 'With two natural first basemen on the roster, Manager Jim Leyland will have to put one of them at a suboptimal position. Which configuration would be the least inefficient?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In March 2008, the Detroit Tigers signed a lumbering slugger to what was then the fifth-largest contract in baseball history. His physique and conditioning were suspect, prompting skeptics to warn that he would become a defensive liability and that his hitting might tail off. But Dave Dombrowski, the club’s general manager, brushed aside such concerns and gave him an eight-year, $152 million deal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: For Tigers, Defensive Issues That Are Hard to Outslug', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cabrera, Miguel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dombrowski, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fielder, Prince', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T18:33:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Rosenheck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenheck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c9ba830-31d5-5192-8b2c-9b4dafedcbe2', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c9ba830-31d5-5192-8b2c-9b4dafedcbe2'}, {'abstract': 'The Group of 8 and NATO summit meetings in May are expected to give Chicago new worldwide visibility, and careful plans are being made to put the city in the spotlight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/us/nato-and-g-8-summit-meetings-can-mean-trouble-or-greater-global-visibility-for-chicago.html', 'snippet': 'The Group of 8 and NATO summit meetings in May are expected to give Chicago new worldwide visibility, and careful plans are being made to put the city in the spotlight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Careful planning always precedes summit meetings like those scheduled for May in Chicago for the Group of 8 economic powers and the NATO military alliance. But events rarely unfold as planned. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None