 punts during the team’s run to the Super Bowl.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOXBOROUGH, Mass. — Julian Edelman said he never saw it coming. True, he had been a versatile performer for the New England Patriots, catching passes and returning punts and kicks. He had also set season records for total offense as a quarterback in college. But playing defense?', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/YPATRIOTS1/YPATRIOTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/YPATRIOTS1/YPATRIOTS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/YPATRIOTS1/YPATRIOTS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/YPATRIOTS1/YPATRIOTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/YPATRIOTS1/YPATRIOTS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Patriots’ Triple Threat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Patriots’ Triple Threat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T18:39:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter May', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'May', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9dc1be15-2170-5276-8a54-76605799745d', 'word_count': 1061, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9dc1be15-2170-5276-8a54-76605799745d'}, {'abstract': 'Miguel Ángel Carballo of Argentina has taken a challenging and unconventional path to the PGA Tour.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/sports/golf/pga-rookie-carballo-had-to-dodge-a-few-rocks.html', 'snippet': 'Miguel Ángel Carballo of Argentina has taken a challenging and unconventional path to the PGA Tour.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DEL MAR, Calif. — The golfer Miguel Ángel Carballo sat contentedly in the middle of the kitchen before dinner while his entourage buzzed around him. His manager kneaded dough for pizza. His caddie chopped basil and tomatoes. Shuffling between them, topping the wine glasses, was his swing coach. The fellowship in the room was like yeast, making the others’ voices rise as Carballo quietly turned his gaze from one familiar face to the next.    ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/dog-golfer-1/dog-golfer-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/dog-golfer-1/dog-golfer-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/dog-golfer-1/dog-golfer-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/dog-golfer-1/dog-golfer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/dog-golfer-1/dog-golfer-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'PGA Rookie Carballo Had to Dodge a Few Rocks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'PGA Rookie Had to Dodge a Few Rocks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PGA Tour Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T18:41:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d1810ee-b1a1-576e-a774-94f106917c70', 'word_count': 1257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d1810ee-b1a1-576e-a774-94f106917c70'}, {'abstract': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta said in a “60 Minutes” interview that a doctor who is now in prison worked with the C.I.A. to gain access to Osama bin Laden’s compound.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/world/asia/panetta-credits-pakistani-doctor-in-bin-laden-raid.html', 'snippet': 'Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta said in a “60 Minutes” interview that a doctor who is now in prison worked with the C.I.A. to gain access to Osama bin Laden’s compound.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Defense Secretary Leon E. Panetta has confirmed publicly for the first time that an imprisoned doctor in Pakistan was working with the C.I.A. to gain access to Osama bin Laden’s compound in the months before American troops killed Bin Laden last May. \xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print