r': 'In-Box', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Paterno and Penn State, Great Life and Blind Spots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paterno, Joe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thomas, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T18:49:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb5e70a6-393a-54ae-ba54-f86ff31fca0f', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb5e70a6-393a-54ae-ba54-f86ff31fca0f'}, {'abstract': 'An interview with Howard Cross, who retired in 2001 after 13 seasons with 201 receptions, 17 touchdowns and countless important blocks.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/30-seconds-with-howard-cross/', 'snippet': 'An interview with Howard Cross, who retired in 2001 after 13 seasons with 201 receptions, 17 touchdowns and countless important blocks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Howard Cross played the most games at tight end in Giants history (207) and was a member of their 1990 Super Bowl team. The position will be in the spotlight Sunday in Super Bowl XLVI, as the Giants try to stop New England’s Rob Gronkowski and Aaron Hernandez.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '30 Seconds With Howard Cross', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cross, Howard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T18:51:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Brescia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brescia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2307e1d-989c-551a-8424-1d73333db62b', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2307e1d-989c-551a-8424-1d73333db62b'}, {'abstract': 'Once in a career, timing, skill and luck converge to produce a classic image. The Times sports photographer Barton Silverman recalls “a very good day” in 1966 covering Joe Namath and the Jets.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/barton-and-the-jet/', 'snippet': 'Once in a career, timing, skill and luck converge to produce a classic image. The Times sports photographer Barton Silverman recalls “a very good day” in 1966 covering Joe Namath and the Jets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having a conversation with Barton Silverman is like following a hockey game, where words scoot by like a puck on ice — glancing off events, people and places before it glides into the goal. That can mean a lot of interesting asides, considering the countless games, big and small, he has covered as a longtime sports photographer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barton and the Jet', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T19:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f34ad041-1bc8-58b1-87d7-565a354fd225', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f34ad041-1bc8-58b1-87d7-565a354fd225'}, {'abstract': 'The Romney campaign ad used almost entirely old footage of Tom Brokaw reporting on Newt Gingrich’s legal troubles.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/nbc-news-asks-romney-campaign-to-remove-ad/', 'snippet': 'The Romney campaign ad used almost entirely old footage of Tom Brokaw reporting on Newt Gingrich’s legal troubles.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:29 p.m. | Updated TAMPA, Fla. – NBC News is asking that the Romney campaign remove from its ads any references to material from the network in response to a new commercial that consists almost entirely of old footage of its former news anchor, Tom Brokaw, reporting on Newt Gingrich’s legal troubles. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC News Asks Romney Campaign to Remove Ad', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brokaw, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NBC News', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T19:18:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8c46bd9-5161-548b-8bf1-f6722cc626c2', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8c46bd9-5161-548b-8bf1-f6722cc626c2'}, {'abstract': 'Although his career consisted of just 12 games, Greg Cook left an impression that hasn’t been forgotten, especially by his teammates and coaches. He died Friday at 65.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/greg-cook-the-story-of-an-n-f-l-shooting-star/', 'snippet': 'Although his career consisted of just 12 games, Greg Cook left an impression that hasn’t been forgotten, especially by his teammates and coaches. He died Friday at 65.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greg Cook was a talented quarterback whose promising career was cut short by injury after only one season. Cook died on Friday after being hospitalized with pneumonia. He was 65:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greg Cook, the Story of an N.F.L. Shooting Star', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Bengals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T19:53:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Barall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e06437fd-ecfa-5ae0-be37-c18f0f1edc0e', 'word_count': 813, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e06437fd-ecfa-5ae0-be37-c18f0f1edc0e'}, {'abstract': 'Victoria Azarenka broke down Maria Sharapova’s game with her superior reception of the ball, allowing her to apply enough topspin to control it while maintaining pace and length.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/how-azarenka-won-australia/', 'snippet': 'Victoria Azarenka broke down Maria Sharapova’s game with her superior reception of the ball, allowing her to apply enough topspin to control it while maintaining pace and length.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Victoria Azarenka thoroughly outplayed Maria Sharapova in Saturday’s Australian Open final. The spirited Azarkena had superior hands, better footwork and near-perfect shot selection as she withstood Sharapova’s blistering pace with astonishing ease. How did Azarenka handle Sharapova’s big game? And why did Sharapova struggle when Azarenka attacked?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Azarenka Won Australia', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Azarenka, Victoria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T19:54:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65d06106-4060-51cc-b5ff-83384c7825fb', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65d06106-4060-51cc-b5ff-83384c7825fb'}, {'abstract': 'Tensions have grown since a crackdown by Egyptian authorities on several American nonprofit organizations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/world/middleeast/us-lobbyists-drop-egypts-government-as-client.html', 'snippet': 'Tensions have grown since a crackdown by Egyptian authorities on several American nonprofit organizations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Lobbyists for the Egyptian government in Washington have ended their contracts with the country because of growing tensions after a raid by Egyptian authorities on several American nonprofit organizations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'c