k': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T20:18:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36078889-96f9-54fc-b785-4cab3c5d581c', 'word_count': 2816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36078889-96f9-54fc-b785-4cab3c5d581c'}, {'abstract': 'Sydney Leroux has been called a traitor by fans in Canada because of her decision to play internationally for the U.S., not Canada, where she was born.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/sports/soccer/for-sydney-leroux-dual-citizenship-single-minded-approach.html', 'snippet': 'Sydney Leroux has been called a traitor by fans in Canada because of her decision to play internationally for the U.S., not Canada, where she was born.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VANCOUVER, British Columbia — Sydney Leroux is a substitute forward for the United States women’s soccer team with dual citizenship, an encouraging future and a complicated past. Depending on one’s point of view, she is either a revelatory young star who scored five goals in one game last week or a turncoat in her hometown.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/KICK/KICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/KICK/KICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/KICK/KICK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/KICK/KICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/sports/KICK/KICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Sydney Leroux, Dual Citizenship, Single-Minded Approach', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dual Citizenship, Single-Minded Approach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T20:23:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4df71814-e67c-539a-9e03-1669f65e2d38', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4df71814-e67c-539a-9e03-1669f65e2d38'}, {'abstract': 'Would it be ethical to produce, or take, a drug that makes us more likely to help others?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/are-we-ready-for-a-morality-pill/', 'snippet': 'Would it be ethical to produce, or take, a drug that makes us more likely to help others?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last October, in Foshan, China, a 2-year-old girl was run over by a van. The driver did not stop. Over the next seven minutes, more than a dozen people walked or bicycled past the injured child. A second truck ran over her. Eventually, a woman pulled her to the side, and her mother arrived. The child died in a hospital. The entire scene was captured on video and caused an uproar when it was shown by a television station and posted online. A similar event occurred in London in 2004, as have others, far from the lens of a video camera.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are We Ready for a ‘Morality Pill’?', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Empathy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T20:30:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Singer and Agata Sagan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Agata', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sagan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/443431cb-dd5b-5443-8ca2-fac2edc56caf', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/443431cb-dd5b-5443-8ca2-fac2edc56caf'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama’s new task force has much to tackle in the mortgage mess — and soon, if it wants to allay suspicions that the authorities have given powerful institutions a pass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/business/mortgage-task-force-has-fancy-name-but-will-it-get-tough.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama’s new task force has much to tackle in the mortgage mess — and soon, if it wants to allay suspicions that the authorities have given powerful institutions a pass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRESIDENT OBAMA told the nation last week that he was convening a task force to investigate the abusive practices in the mortgage industry that led to our economic woes. Both lending and the practice of bundling loans into securities will come under scrutiny, he said, adding: “This new unit will hold accountable those who broke the law, speed assistance to homeowners and help turn the page on an era of recklessness that hurt so many Americans.”', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/04/19/business/morgenson/morgenson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'he