nalists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wondered a bit about the topic of my Sunday column. It’s in part about the way Ethiopia’s heightening repression has resulted in the imprisonment and abuse of journalists, including two Swedes who are now serving an 11-year prison sentence in awful conditions. My sense is that Ethiopia’s Prime Minister Meles Zenawi thinks that imprisoning those Swedes will intimidate and silence the international press corps — and I want him to realize that he’s dead wrong. That’s also why I went after him by Twitter at Davos.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Journalists Are Imprisoned', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T22:36:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31a885f8-764d-5eed-a861-cdb1cdc9eac5', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31a885f8-764d-5eed-a861-cdb1cdc9eac5'}, {'abstract': 'Religious people are more likely to donate to charity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/sunday-review/religions-inspire-charity.html', 'snippet': 'Religious people are more likely to donate to charity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MITT ROMNEY’S 2010 tax return, along with an estimated version of his 2011 filing, was released on Tuesday and attracted attention for a number of reasons — chief among them his high income and low tax rate. But the disclosure also called attention to his high level of charitable giving — much in the form of donations to the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints — in a nation where most donate far less.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sunday-review/29GIVING/29GIVING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/29/sunday-review/29GIVING/29GIVING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/sunday-review/29GIVING/29GIVING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Tithe or Not to Tithe ...', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Tithe Or Not to Tithe ...', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-28T22:38:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Paulson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paulson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8ff9a2c-afc7-5c7c-8f30-469744255c15', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8ff9a2c-afc7-5c7c-8f30-469744255c15'}, {'abst