. Scalfaro, a petite 48-year-old who works in accounting, found a seat along one of the low-lying concrete walls that surround the square patches of grass on the plaza.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29BCBENCHES1/29BCBENCHES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29BCBENCHES1/29BCBENCHES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29BCBENCHES1/29BCBENCHES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Renewed Public Push for Somewhere to Sit Outdoors', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Renewed Public Push for Somewhere to Sit Outdoors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiener, Scott (1970- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T01:36:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zusha Elinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zusha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a67deca-f73e-5a53-9aa2-bb99ea53c15e', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a67deca-f73e-5a53-9aa2-bb99ea53c15e'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Rahm Emanuel had a separate agenda last week when the news media was beckoned for an announcement about the Chicago Public Library.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/us/rahm-emanuels-premeditated-opinion-on-city-schools.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Rahm Emanuel had a separate agenda last week when the news media was beckoned for an announcement about the Chicago Public Library.', 'lead_paragraph': '\u200bJames Warren writes a column for The Chicago News Cooperative.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Premeditated Opinion on City Schools', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Premeditated Opinion on City Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T01:37:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Warren', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Warren', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0af6478-1c6e-5a67-b91c-f2df8957518a', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0af6478-1c6e-5a67-b91c-f2df8957518a'}, {'abstract': 'The City Colleges of Chicago has generated more than $7 million in sick day payments for 140 former employees in the last decade, according to records.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/us/city-colleges-pay-millions-for-unused-sick-days.html', 'snippet': 'The City Colleges of Chicago has generated more than $7 million in sick day payments for 140 former employees in the last decade, according to records.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many public and private employers have a use-it-or-lose-it policy toward sick time. But the City Colleges of Chicago has generated more than $7 million in postemployment sick day payments for about 140 former employees in the last decade, according to records obtained by the Better Government Association. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29CNCWATSON/29CNCWATSON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 614, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Workers at City Colleges Paid for Unused Sick Days', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Workers at City Colleges Paid for Unused Sick Days', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'City Colleges of Chicago', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T01:38:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Rehkamp', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rehkamp', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6ba0482-822e-544d-a72d-85cc85d43392', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6ba0482-822e-544d-a72d-85cc85d43392'}, {'abstract': 'A community meeting aimed at devising a new plan to end homelessness, points out problems with interim housing and the most frequent reason for people’s plight: joblessness and inadequate income.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/us/chicago-homeless-seek-help-from-new-plan-2-0.html', 'snippet': 'A community meeting aimed at devising a new plan to end homelessness, points out problems with interim housing and the most frequent reason for people’s plight: joblessness and inadequate income.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stories were varied. There was the formerly homeless woman who said she had become ill from shelter food; the social worker who felt that without sufficient resources, she was being set up to fail; the youth who asked for more drop-in services; the mother who lost her job and then her home; and the man who was told he was ineligible for certain services because he was neither an addict nor mentally ill.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29CNCHOMELESS/29CNCHOMELESS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 874, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29CNCHOMELESS/29CNCHOMELESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29CNCHOMELESS/29CNCHOMELESS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Homeless Seek Help From New Plan 2.0', 'kicker': 'Chicago News Cooperative', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Homeless Seek Help From New Plan 2.0', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T01:53:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Meribah Knight', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Meribah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Knight', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad3a77a6-eb90-546e-b00a-832ebabf693a', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad3a77a6-eb90-546e-b00a-832ebabf693a'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Gingrich, whose supporting super PAC has received $10 million from the casino mogul Sheldon Adelson and his wife, said the issue his benefactor cared about was Israel, dodging a question about the possible spread of casino gambling in Florida.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/gingrich-deflects-questions-about-a-big-supporters-casino-interests/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Gingrich, whose supporting super PAC has received $10 million from the casino mogul Sheldon Adelson and his wife, said the issue his benefactor cared about was Israel, dodging a question about the possible spread of casino gambling in Florida.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WINTER PARK, Fla. — The possibility of gambling exploding across Florida has worried many on the religious right, and they questioned Newt Gingrich on Saturday about his financial backing by Sheldon Adelson, a casino magnate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gingrich Deflects Questions About a Big Supporter’s Casino Interests', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adelson, Sheldon G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liberty Counsel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T01:53:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ac69248-2bd4-50b9-8e33-5a03169669db', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ac69248-2bd4-50b9-8e33-5a03169669db'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Vyarawalla was hailed as the first Indian woman to work as a photojournalist and for chronicling the country’s march toward independence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/world/asia/homai-vyarawalla-india-photojournalist-dies-at-98.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Vyarawalla was hailed as the first Indian woman to work as a photojournalist and for chronicling the country’s march toward independence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Homai Vyarawalla, a photojournalist celebrated in India for chronicling the country’s march toward independence and capturing enduring images of world figures like Mohandas K. Gandhi, Ho Chi Minh and American presidents of the mid-20th century, died on Jan. 15 in Vadodara, in west India. She was 98.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/world/dog-VYARAWALLA1-obit/dog-VYARAWALLA1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 658, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 