e procedure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Moments after Amy Hagstrom Miller heard the news earlier this month —\xa0that a panel of federal judges had directed Texas to immediately enforce the most controversial tenet of the state’s new abortion sonogram law —\xa0her phone started ringing. It was the doctors who perform abortions at the five Whole Woman’s Health clinics she founded in Texas, confirming that they had to start showing their pregnant patients the image of the fetus and playing the fetal heartbeat. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29TTSONOGRAM/29TTSONOGRAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29TTSONOGRAM/29TTSONOGRAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29TTSONOGRAM/29TTSONOGRAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Required Delay Between Sonogram and Abortion Creates Logistical Issues', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Required Delay Between Sonogram and Abortion Creates Logistical Issues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Obstetrics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T02:06:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Ramshaw', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramshaw', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40026b40-9987-5aeb-961f-5e034c4b0a1d', 'word_count': 986, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40026b40-9987-5aeb-961f-5e034c4b0a1d'}, {'abstract': 'Democrats in Texas haven’t won a statewide election since 1994, the kind of drought Republicans faced decades ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/us/politics/texas-democrats-find-solace-in-past-gop-struggles.html', 'snippet': 'Democrats in Texas haven’t won a statewide election since 1994, the kind of drought Republicans faced decades ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Ramsey, the executive editor of The Texas Tribune, writes a column for The Tribune.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29TTRAMSEY-1327603645436/29TTRAMSEY-1327603645436-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 950, 'width': 807, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Their Election Drought, Texas Democrats Find Solace in G.O.P.’s Past Struggles', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Their Election Drought, Texas Democrats Find Solace in G.O.P.’s Past Struggles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T02:13:23+