locations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T02:20:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bettina Wassener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bettina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wassener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f835261-96e5-566c-880f-8089ba932d1a', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f835261-96e5-566c-880f-8089ba932d1a'}, {'abstract': 'At 30, Ben Kweller, the singer-songwriter and former “boy wonder,” has recorded his latest album for his own label, The Noise Company, which he calls a mom-and-pop business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/us/ben-kweller-takes-charge-of-his-own-career.html', 'snippet': 'At 30, Ben Kweller, the singer-songwriter and former “boy wonder,” has recorded his latest album for his own label, The Noise Company, which he calls a mom-and-pop business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, Ben Kweller was on his hands and knees on the front lawn of his South Austin office, helping a delivery driver shrink-wrap a pallet of 1,000 CDs destined for Japan. When they had secured the goods, Mr. Kweller, the 30-year-old singer-songwriter — dressed in a black version of Michael Jackson’s “Thriller” jacket and ripped jeans — popped a leg onto the boxes and threw up a devil’s sign, posing for a picture he immediately texted to his Tokyo distributor to show that the CDs were on their way. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29TTLANGER/29TTLANGER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 660, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29TTLANGER/29TTLANGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29TTLANGER/29TTLANGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Former Boy Wonder Takes Charge of His Career', 'kicker': 'Texas Monthly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Former Boy Wonder Takes Charge of His Career', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Austin (Tex)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T02:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Langer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Langer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e9d5e2b-61c3-5624-b137-37657c9e20b4', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e9d5e2b-61c3-5624-b137-37657c9e20b4'}, {'abstract': 'Herman Cain, who ended his presidential bid in early December, endorsed Newt Gingrich on Saturday night, three days before the crucial Florida primary.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/28/cain-endorses-gingrich-for-president/', 'snippet': 'Herman Cain, who ended his presidential bid in early December, endorsed Newt Gingrich on Saturday night, three days before the crucial Florida primary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — Herman Cain, who ended his presidential bid in early December, endorsed Newt Gingrich on Saturday night, three days before the crucia