 which parks at Moffet Field in Mountain View, is a genuine German zeppelin that has done work for NASA, television sporting events and insurance companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Often seen cruising Bay Area skies about 1,000 feet off the ground, the Eureka airship is one of only two of its type in the world, and the only one in the United States that carries commercial passengers. This German-made zeppelin, owned by Airship Ventures, is not a blimp; though both types of airships are filled with helium, only a zeppelin has an internal framework.\xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23B', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29BCINTEL1/29BCINTEL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29BCINTEL1/29BCINTEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/us/29BCINTEL1/29BCINTEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eureka Airship', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen | Local Intelligence', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eureka Airship: Moffet Federal Airfield, Mountain View', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Eureka (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRSHIPS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T02:50:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Louise Rafkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Louise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rafkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d0d66b2-0424-5835-b858-198f678a8c20', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d0d66b2-0424-5835-b858-198f678a8c20'}, {'abstract': 'Silicon Valley may be booming again, but things have not really improved for the technology professionals who are looking for a new job after the age of 40.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/us/bay-area-technology-professionals-cant-get-hired-as-industry-moves-on.html', 'snippet': 'Silicon Valley may be booming again, but things have not really improved for the technology professionals who are looking for a new job after the age of 40.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Silicon Valley may be booming again, but times are still tough for the 200 out-of-work professionals who crowd into Sunnyvale’s City Hall every Thursday morning.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Old Techies Never Die; They Just Can’t Get Hired as an Industry Moves On', 'kicker': 'The Bay Citizen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Old Techies Never Die; They Just Can’t Get Hired as an Industry Moves On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engineering and Engineers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T02:55:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron Glantz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glantz