 involve division of revenues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/sports/hockey/nhl-and-players-union-look-ahead-to-new-labor-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Formal talks are not yet scheduled between the sides over the collective bargaining agreement that expires in September, but a potential sticking point could involve division of revenues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OTTAWA, Ontario — The battle lines over contract negotiations between the N.H.L. and the players union discreetly took shape Saturday, as Commissioner Gary Bettman and the union’s executive director, Donald Fehr, met with reporters during All-Star weekend. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.H.L. and Players Union Look Ahead to New Labor Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bettman, Gary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fehr, Donald', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T03:05:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0baa5d7-76b8-5a41-805b-3518a5cfc291', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0baa5d7-76b8-5a41-805b-3518a5cfc291'}, {'abstract': 'The Massachusetts senator released 170 pages of unredacted records after the Defense Department provided a heavily redacted version to The Boston Globe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/us/politics/scott-brown-releases-unredacted-national-guard-records.html', 'snippet': 'The Massachusetts senator released 170 pages of unredacted records after the Defense Department provided a heavily redacted version to The Boston Globe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Senator Scott P. Brown released 170 pages of records late Saturday from his three decades of service in the Army National Guard. Mr. Brown, a Republican who is facing a tough re-election race against Elizabeth Warren, wanted to be “open and transparent” about the records, according to his Senate office, which released them. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brown Releases Records From National Guard', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brown Releases Records From National Guard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Scott P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Guard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T03:43:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32378153-ee17-53e3