ne': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Exxon Mobil Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T15:41:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afcb7a85-dab2-5930-9777-ebda260726a1', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afcb7a85-dab2-5930-9777-ebda260726a1'}, {'abstract': 'Michel Hazanavicius wins the Directors Guild contest, a strong indicator that “The Artist” will win the best picture Oscar.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/michel-hazanavicius-wins-at-the-directors-guild/', 'snippet': 'Michel Hazanavicius wins the Directors Guild contest, a strong indicator that “The Artist” will win the best picture Oscar.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The Directors Guild of America honored a bespectacled filmmaker for his love of classic Hollywood cinema, and he was a Frenchman: Michel Hazanavicius won the prize for best feature from the organization, whose choices usually dovetail with the Oscars. (Pundits quickly called it: “The Artist” will win best picture at the Academy Awards.) On Saturday night, Mr. Hazanavicius beat out Martin Scorsese, Woody Allen, Alexander Payne and David Fincher.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michel Hazanavicius Wins at the Directors Guild', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, WOODY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dujardin, Jean', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fincher, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grammer, Kelsey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hazanavicius, Michel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenkins, Patty', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marsh, James', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Payne, Alexander', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reiner, Carl', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scorsese, Martin', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weide, Robert B', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T15:53:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c17867e4-b25a-5572-9859-66df5fb590e2', 'word_count': 363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c17867e4-b25a-5572-9859-66df5fb590e2'}, {'abstract': 'According to a study, N.F.L. coaches were as conservative on fourth downs in 2011 as they’ve ever been in 20 years.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/on-fourth-down-coaches-arent-going-for-it/', 'snippet': 'According to a study, N.F.L. coaches were as conservative on fourth downs in 2011 as they’ve ever been in 20 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What do Bill Belichick, Tom Coughlin, Sean Payton and Jim Harbaugh have in common? They ranked among the top eight N.F.L. coaches in aggressiveness on going for it on fourth down this season. That shouldn’t be a huge surprise. Those four coaches are highly respected and very successful. And if there is one thing all N.F.L. statistical analysts agree on,\xa0 coaches should go for it on fourth down more often.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Fourth Down, Coaches Aren’t Going for It', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T16:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f5236a9-d5aa-51d7-a3a4-050734f35a12', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f5236a9-d5aa-51d7-a3a4-050734f35a12'}, {'abstract': 'After a year that has included the social media-fueled protests of the Arab Spring and Occupy Wall Street, global Internet privacy legislation and billions of dollars in technology stock offerings, tech and social media have not only entered the building at Davos, they are the walls holding it up.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/disruptions-in-davos-technology-moves-center-stage/', 'snippet': 'After a year that has included the social media-fueled protests of the Arab Spring and Occupy Wall Street, global Internet privacy legislation and billions of dollars in technology stock offerings, tech and social media have not only entered the b...', 'lead_paragraph': ' DAVOS, Switzerland — When I set out to report at the World Economic Forum, I imagined it might be difficult to find technology-related stories. It turns out, I was a tad wrong. I would have had more luck finding a snowless Alpine mountain in the winter than finding people discussing a topic that did not involve technology.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/technology/29bits-disruptions/29bits-disruptions-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 745, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/29/technology/29bits-disruptions/29bits-disruptions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/29/technology/29bits-disruptions/29bits-disruptions-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disruptions: In Davos, Technology Moves Center Stage', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Economic Forum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T16:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bebc216d-b9a9-5a08-9910-6d4ea37a1695', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bebc216d-b9a9-5a08-9910-6d4ea37a1695'}, {'abstract': '“Beasts of the Southern Wild,” directed by Benh Zeitlin, wins the top prize at the Sundance Film Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/sundance-honors-beasts-of-the-southern-wild/', 'snippet': '“Beasts of the Southern Wild,” directed by Benh Zeitlin, wins the top prize at the Sundance Film Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Quvenzhané Wallis, 8, cemented her status as the It Girl of this year’s Sundance Film Festival on Saturday night, as “Beasts of the Southern Wild,” starring Ms. Wallis as a poor Louisiana girl named Hushpuppy, took the festival’s top grand jury prize.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sundance Honors ‘Beasts of the Southern Wild’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dick, Kirby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawkes, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunt, Helen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jarecki, Eugene', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewin, Ben', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Searchlight Pictures', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T16:16:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/255e7078-0b73-5e6d-820d-db4b0ced37e4', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/255e7078-0b73-5e6d-820d-db4b0ced37e4'}, {'abstract': 'An elemental wildness runs through “Wuthering Heights, Restless Souls,” Theater Artemis’s spare but impressively theatrical adaptation of Emily Brontë’s novel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/theater/reviews/wuthering-heights-restless-souls-at-new-victory.html', 'snippet': 'An elemental wildness runs through “Wuthering Heights, Restless Souls,” Theater Artemis’s spare but impressively theatrical adaptation of Emily Brontë’s novel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An elemental wildness runs through “Wuthering Heights, Restless Souls,” Theater Artemis’s spare but impressively theatrical adaptation of Emily Brontë’s novel. Though intended for young audiences (13 and up), this production never condescends. Quite the opposite: it can be ferocious, even scary, as it gives physical shape to the bond between Cathy and Heathcliff (Alejandra Theus and Joris Smit, both feral, both terrific).', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/wuthering/wuthering-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 362, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/wuthering/wuthering-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 362}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/wuthering/wuthering-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/wuthering/wuthering-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/wuthering/wuthering-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Stormy Romance on the Moors, via the Netherlands', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Stormy Romance on the Moors, via the Netherlands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Victory Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bronte, Emily', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T16:33:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/170544cf-c8e3-5fad-bd40-d7d5e1b948ce', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/170544cf-c8e3-5fad-bd40-d7d5e1b948ce'}, {'abstract': 'At a Southern Baptist church in Florida, Newt Gingrich gets the crowd fired up with outlandish un-truths.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/catchy-slogans-sloppy-ideas/', 'snippet': 'At a Southern Baptist church in Florida, Newt Gingrich gets the crowd fired up with outlandish un-truths.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA – Herman Cain’s endorsement of Newt Gingrich on Saturday night made perfect sense, as each man gravitates to catchy slogans and sloppy ideas. Mr. Cain still dreams of his 9-9-9 tax plan, while Mr. Gingrich fantasizes about a moon base that would probably require a 90-90-90 tax plan.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Catchy Slogans, Sloppy Ideas', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stem Cells (Embryonic)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cain, Herman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T17:04:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e546099e-be09-5152-ad95-092c65b78eba', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e546099e-be09-5152-ad95-092c65b78eba'}, {'abstract': 'The action movie has led the way at the North American box office over the weekend with an estimated $20 million in ticket sales.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/the-grey-starring-liam-neeson-leads-at-the-box-office/', 'snippet': 'The action movie has led the way at the North American box office over the weekend with an estimated $20 million in ticket sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Liam Neeson does it again: “The Grey,” the latest in a line of successful action thrillers featuring that 59-year-old star, was No. 1 at the North American box office over the weekend, with an estimated $20 million in ticket sales. The movie, about a group of oil drillers in Alaska who become hunted by wolves, was made outside the studio system and acquired for $5 million last summer by Open Road Films, an upstart distributor backed by the multiplex operators AMC Entertainment and Regal Cinemas.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Grey,’ Starring Liam Neeson, Leads at the Box Office', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clooney, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evanovich, Janet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heigl, Katherine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neeson, Liam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hollywood.com', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T17:10:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firs