ent in time when the world’s center of gravity is shifting from the West to the East.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/books/strategic-vision-by-zbigniew-brzezinski.html', 'snippet': 'Zbigniew Brzezinski’s book “Strategic Vision” surveys current global affairs and assesses a hinge moment in time when the world’s center of gravity is shifting from the West to the East.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 2008 crash and America and Europe’s continuing economic woes; the rise of China and worries about the decline of the West; and technology-fueled uprisings around the world from the Arab Spring protests to anti-Putin demonstrations in Russia — such developments underscore just how prescient Zbigniew Brzezinski has been in his earlier writings. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/jpp-book/jpp-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 712, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/jpp-book/jpp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/jpp-book/jpp-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Surveying a Global Power Shift', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surveying a Global Power Shift', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cold War Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brzezinski, Zbigniew', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T19:50:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cc482c2-6dbf-51ca-8c11-06f8c95a307f', 'word_count': 1189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cc482c2-6dbf-51ca-8c11-06f8c95a307f'}, {'abstract': 'Campaigns and “super PACs” are singling out potential voters with a high degree of specificity as they seek an edge in Florida.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/us/politics/republican-campaigns-get-picky-about-tv-advertising.html', 'snippet': 'Campaigns and “super PACs” are singling out potential voters with a high degree of specificity as they seek an edge in Florida.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. — Republican presidential candidates have flooded this state with commercials in all the usual places: local newscasts in the morning, talk shows during the day, “Wheel of Fortune” and “Jeopardy!” at dinnertime.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For G.O.P. Ads, ‘CSI’ but Not Letterman', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘CSI’ Is a Favorite for Republican Ad Dollars in Florida. David Letterman Is Not.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T19:53:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b607b78e-3f91-59e9-91dc-48bc5cf89319', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b607b78e-3f91-59e9-91dc-48bc5cf89319'}, {'abstract': 'Hundreds of protesters tried to take over Oakland’s vacant convention center and then briefly broke into City Hall before being rousted by the police.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/us/occupy-oakland-protest-leads-to-hundreds-of-arrests.html', 'snippet': 'Hundreds of protesters tried to take over Oakland’s vacant convention center and then briefly broke into City Hall before being rousted by the police.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 400 people were arrested and three police officers were injured after a weekend protest by members of the Occupy movement in Oakland, Calif., turned into a violent confrontation with law enforcement officers that led to an assault on City Hall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'c