 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/239afffd-b4d2-50ab-b2c3-826a9b58a79a', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/239afffd-b4d2-50ab-b2c3-826a9b58a79a'}, {'abstract': 'Sydney Leroux’s story of growing up in Canada only to play for the United States national team is a common one in the world of top-level international soccer.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/29/sydney-leroux-and-soccer-without-borders/', 'snippet': 'Sydney Leroux’s story of growing up in Canada only to play for the United States national team is a common one in the world of top-level international soccer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeré Longman has a profile in the Sunday Times of the United States national team newcomer Sydney Leroux, a striker with worlds of talent and a complicated background. Leroux scored five goals in the Americans’ 13-0 demolition of Guatemala last week, but she has nonetheless been taunted in Vancouver, her hometown, for her decision to compete internationally for the United States instead of her native Canada.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sydney Leroux and Soccer Without Borders', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T20:44:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68461cfa-bbf6-5678-b913-4791f7c60a66', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68461cfa-bbf6-5678-b913-4791f7c60a66'}, {'abstract': 'The singer-songwriter Miranda Lambert’s “On Fire” tour includes songs from her new album, “Four the Record.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/arts/music/miranda-lambert-brings-four-the-record-to-the-izod-center.html', 'snippet': 'The singer-songwriter Miranda Lambert’s “On Fire” tour includes songs from her new album, “Four the Record.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J — Before Miranda Lambert came onstage at the Izod Center here Saturday night, the audience watched a video montage set to Beyoncé’s “Run the World (Girls).” It flashed pictures of women that one assumes were selected by Ms. Lambert to serve as her archetypes, and they included Patsy Cline, Lady Gaga and Betty Boop.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/lambert/lambert-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/lambert/lambert-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/lambert/lambert-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/lambert/lambert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/lambert/lambert-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Very Clearly, a Woman You Don’t Want to Mess With', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Very Clearly, A Woman You Don’t Want To Mess With', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Country Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lambert, Miranda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T20:47:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/449adaf2-4bd3-5b4c-b735-846e26bbaa64', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/449adaf2-4bd3-5b4c-b735-846e26bbaa64'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Scalfaro was Italy’s president during seven tumultuous years marked by a corruption scandal that brought down an entire political class.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/world/europe/oscar-luigi-scalfaro-ex-president-of-italy-is-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Scalfaro was Italy’s president during seven tumultuous years marked by a corruption scandal that brought down an entire political class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Oscar Luigi Scalfaro, who was the president of Italy during a tumultuous period in the 1990s marked by a widespread corruption scandal that felled an entire political class, died here on Sunday. He was 93. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/sports/sub-scalfaro-obit/sub-scalfaro-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/sports/sub-scalfaro-obit/sub-scalfaro-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/30/sports/sub-scalfaro-obit/sub-scalfaro-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Oscar Luigi Scalfaro, Ex-President of Italy, Dies at 93', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oscar Luigi Scalfaro, 93; Led Italy at Turbulent Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalfaro, Oscar Luigi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T20:47:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a66f2ed-6aae-5c31-a678-5b5fd9e994c0', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a66f2ed-6aae-5c31-a678-5b5fd9e994c0'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Philharmonic’s management and musicians have agreed on a new contract, the players’ union said late Saturday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/arts/music/new-contract-for-philharmonic.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Philharmonic’s management and musicians have agreed on a new contract, the players’ union said late Saturday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Philharmonic’s management and musicians have agreed on a new contract, the players’ union said late Saturday. Union officials said orchestra members had been prepared to strike, jeopardizing a European tour starting Monday, without an agreement this weekend. In a statement the musicians reported reaching a two-year deal — relatively short by industry standards — in which, they said, management had dropped proposals for “drastic cuts to health insurance and a radical reduction in pension benefits.” The Philharmonic confirmed in a statement on Sunday that the defined-benefit pension plan would remain, and that pension benefits would be capped at $70,000 a year per player. The orchestra also said that both sides agreed to hire a consultant to study “the advisability of moving to a defined-contribution pension plan.” Tino Gagliardi, president of Local 802 of the American Federation of Musicians, which represents Philharmonic players, said management backed down from eliminating defined-benefit pensions and replacing them with defined contributions. The Philadelphia Orchestra, which is in bankruptcy proceedings, recently made the change. In light of that, Mr. Gagliardi said, “it was really, really important” to take a stand. But the matter was essentially put off for two years. Mr. Gagliardi said the pension issue would be studied by both sides and revisited for the next contract. On health insurance, he said, the agreement gives “small economic relief to the employer.” The pact, he added, calls for no wage increase this year and a 2 percent raise next year.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Contract for Philharmonic', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Contract For Philharmonic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T21:37:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/81f25d3b-2b8f-574d-8e2b-3c830e955023', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81f25d3b-2b8f-574d-8e2b-3c830e955023'}, {'abstract': 'As Showtime edges closer to its competitor’s subscriber numbers, HBO is ready to counter with a spate of big projects over the next six months.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/business/media/with-homeland-showtime-makes-gains-on-hbo.html', 'snippet': 'As Showtime edges closer to its competitor’s subscriber numbers, HBO is ready to counter with a spate of big projects over the next six months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Showtime has long been second to HBO among premium cable channels, but on the strength of its critically acclaimed drama “Homeland,” it has seized a coveted title from its larger rival: the channel with the most discussed, praised and award-festooned cable show of the year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/business/30Showtime/30Showtime-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/business/30Showtime/30Showtime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/30/business/30Showtime/30Showtime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With ‘Homeland,’ Showtime Makes Gains on HBO', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Showtime Is Gaining On HBO', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nevins, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Showtime', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lombardo, Michael J (1954- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T21:37:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd7ae251-ef79-5bb0-bcfd-3a336271f5b9', 'word_count': 1144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd7ae251-ef79-5bb0-bcfd-3a336271f5b9'}, {'abstract': 'The New York City Ballet honored the choreographer Christopher Wheeldon on Saturday with an evening of his works, including a premiere, “Les Carillons.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/arts/dance/new-york-city-ballet-in-new-carillons-at-koch-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The New York City Ballet honored the choreographer Christopher Wheeldon on Saturday with an evening of his works, including a premiere, “Les Carillons.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Christopher Wheeldon and New York City Ballet have a special relationship. Perhaps there were some bruised feelings when, in 2008, he resigned as resident choreographer — a position City Ballet had created for him in 2001 — to concentrate on his own company, Morphoses, which he later abandoned. And it’s true that Mr. Wheeldon maintains strong ties to the Royal Ballet, where he was trained, and that he shares his talents with many other troupes. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/wheeldon/wheeldon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/wheeldon/wheeldon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/wheeldon/wheeldon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/wheeldon/wheeldon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/wheeldon/wheeldon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a New Wheeldon Ballet, Overlapping and Piling on the Riches', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a New Wheeldon Ballet, Overlapping and Piling On the Riches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeldon, Christopher', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T21:39:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0fc2b22-0436-5b32-9e98-a30b6df79190', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0fc2b22-0436-5b32-9e98-a30b6df79190'}, {'abstract': 'Focus! 2012, the Juilliard School’s venerable new-music festival, celebrates the 100th anniversary of John Cage’s birth with a six-concert series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/arts/music/juilliard-schools-focus-festival-celebrates-john-cage.html', 'snippet': 'Focus! 2012, the Juilliard School’s venerable new-music festival, celebrates the 100th anniversary of John Cage’s birth with a six-concert series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some music now considered transporting was simply too revolutionary for its time: Beethoven’s late works often baffled his peers but inspire us. The music of some 20th-century composers, on the other hand, will probably never move the listener, which was not the goal of an artist like John Cage. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/focus/focus-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/focus/focus-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/focus/focus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/focus/focus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/focus/focus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In John Cage’s Room, Sounds of Gertrude Stein', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In John Cage’s Room, Sounds of Gertrude Stein', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Focus Festival (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Juilliard School', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sachs, Joel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cage, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T21:47:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a198052-d0b2-523f-9c01-03b0ea55cc32', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a198052-d0b2-523f-9c01-03b0ea55cc32'}, {'abstract': 'Opera Lafayette, the Washington group, lovingly resurrected and performed “Le Roi et le Fermier,” which Marie Antoinette and her courtiers performed at Versailles in 1780.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/arts/music/opera-lafayettes-le-roi-et-le-fermier-at-rose-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Opera Lafayette, the Washington group, lovingly resurrected and performed “Le Roi et le Fermier,” which Marie Antoinette and her courtiers performed at Versailles in 1780.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pierre-Alexandre Monsigny’s opera “Le Roi et le Fermier” (“The King and the Farmer”), with its exploration of class issues and caricature of aristocrats, might seem an unlikely work for Marie Antoinette and her courtiers to have performed at Versailles in 1780. It was bold material for 18th-century France; the librettist, Michel-Jean Sedaine, had to tweak a scene involving the King and a commoner to appease the censor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/opera/opera-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/opera/opera-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/opera/opera-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/opera/opera-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/opera/opera-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Following in Marie Antoinette’s Footsteps', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Following in Marie Antoinette’s Footsteps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'monsigny, Pierre-Alexandre', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Opera Lafayette', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T21:47:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6397ea5c-1401-5d28-99c8-e350c77e4332', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6397ea5c-1401-5d28-99c8-e350c77e4332'}, {'abstract': 'Camille A. Brown, whose forte is the dance skit, presented her company in six works over the weekend at the Joyce Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/arts/dance/camille-a-brown-and-dancers-at-the-joyce-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Camille A. Brown, whose forte is the dance skit, presented her company in six works over the weekend at the Joyce Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The best that can be said about an evening spent with the choreographer Camille A. Brown is that she knows how to hold an audience in the palm of her hand. (This is formulaic choreography made for an easy response.) Ms. Brown’s expertise is the dance skit: solos that tell stories through a measured combination of slow-and-sharp movements and song lyrics. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/brown/brown-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/brown/brown-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/brown/brown-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Song and Dance With a Story to Tell', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Song and Dance With a Story to Tell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Camille A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-29T21:48:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf11cfb0-79a7-59db-b14e-c42e009ac0c0', 'word_count': 403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf11cfb0-79a7-59db-b14e-c42e009ac0c0'}, {'abstract': 'A hot sauce war between Frank’s RedHot and the McIlhenny Company has broken out in time for the Super Bowl, perhaps the most snack-centric day of the year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/business/media/tabasco-and-franks-redhot-in-a-buffalo-wing-sauce-duel.html', 'snippet': 'A hot sauce war between Frank’s RedHot and the McIlhenny Company has broken out in time for the Super Bowl, perhaps the most snack-centric day of the year.', 'lead_paragraph': '“SOME like it hot,” Tony Curtis told Marilyn Monroe in the 1959 movie of the same name, referring to music. Since then, Americans have grown to like something else — food — even hotter, as evidenced by the popularization of spicy fare like Buffalo chicken wings, made with cayenne pepper hot sauce.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/business/30adco1/30adco1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/business/30adco1/30adco1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width'