 Penn, star of Paolo Sorrentino’s “This Must Be the Place,” about a rich, depressed 1980s rocker, discusses the film, his family life and his relief work in Haiti.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/movies/sean-penn-at-sundance-on-haiti-and-paolo-sorrentino-film.html', 'snippet': 'Sean Penn, star of Paolo Sorrentino’s “This Must Be the Place,” about a rich, depressed 1980s rocker, discusses the film, his family life and his relief work in Haiti.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARK CITY, Utah — It’s not subtle: in his forthcoming movie, “This Must Be the Place,” Sean Penn resembles Robert Smith, the goth frontman of the Cure. The resemblance was intentional; the Italian director Paolo Sorrentino, known for the political biopic “Il Divo,” idolized the Cure growing up and decided to make his English-language debut about a rich, depressed ’80s rocker married to a no-nonsense woman (Frances McDormand) who’s a firefighter.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/30PENN/30PENN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 951, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/30PENN/30PENN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/30/arts/30PENN/30PENN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Works Overshadow Goth Looks', 'kicker': 'A Word With: Sean Penn', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good Works Overshadow Goth Looks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}