s Embassy and consulates, as well as American personnel. Some senior Iraqi officials expressed outrage at the program, saying the unarmed aircraft are an affront to Iraqi sovereignty.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Drones Patrolling Its Skies Provoke Outrage in Iraq', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Drones Stir Outrage In Iraq; Fleet May Grow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mercenaries and Private Military Contractors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T01:41:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt and Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f546646d-8902-56ac-b3b7-2167b6a8f8c1', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f546646d-8902-56ac-b3b7-2167b6a8f8c1'}, {'abstract': 'Responding to an Op-Ed article about Liberia, an official with the Ford Foundation discusses the rights of rural people worldwide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/opinion/rural-land-grabs.html', 'snippet': 'Responding to an Op-Ed article about Liberia, an official with the Ford Foundation discusses the rights of rural people worldwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rural Land Grabs', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rural Land Grabs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rural Areas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T01:43:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ae3ac2a-c5ef-5172-b9e7-ed1551b3806b', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ae3ac2a-c5ef-5172-b9e7-ed1551b3806b'}, {'abstract': 'Rap is at the heart of political protests in Africa and the Arab world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/opinion/the-mixtape-of-the-revolution.html', 'snippet': 'Rap is at the heart of political protests in Africa and the Arab world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DEF JAM will probably never sign them, but Cheikh Oumar Cyrille Touré, from a small town about 100 miles southeast of Dakar, Senegal, and Hamada Ben Amor, a 22-year-old man from a port city 170 miles southeast of Tunis, may be two of the most influential rappers in the history of hip-hop. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/opinion/0130OPEDtodd/0130OPEDtodd-artic