6301b81b4f58', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccf4eab2-d4c1-5944-be27-6301b81b4f58'}, {'abstract': 'Tennessee is leading the way with a new rule prohibiting judges from hearing cases when campaign spending by lawyers raises a question of their impartiality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/opinion/a-reform-for-fair-courts.html', 'snippet': 'Tennessee is leading the way with a new rule prohibiting judges from hearing cases when campaign spending by lawyers raises a question of their impartiality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With rising special-interest spending in state judicial elections, there is an urgent need to protect judicial integrity from the flood of campaign cash. Tennessee is leading the way with a new rule prohibiting judges from hearing cases when campaign spending by lawyers or litigants raises a reasonable question of their impartiality. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reform for Fair Courts', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Reform for Fair Courts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Judges', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T02:04:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d319cafa-392e-56c0-8140-be0ba466ec59', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://a