tics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chandy, Oommen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kerala (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T06:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By T.P. Sreenivasan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'T.', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Sreenivasan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/721941f8-7bb5-5c0c-bea8-685adeca5fb3', 'word_count': 790, 'uri': 'nyt://article/721941f8-7bb5-5c0c-bea8-685adeca5fb3'}, {'abstract': 'Punjab is struggling with power shortages leading to a slow industrial growth.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/punjab-bread-basket-of-india-hungers-for-change/', 'snippet': 'Punjab is struggling with power shortages leading to a slow industrial growth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Punjab State goes to polls Monday to elect representatives to its legislature. Once considered the pioneer of green revolution in India, the state is now struggling with slow industrial growth, Reuters reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Punjab, Bread Basket of India, Hungers for Change', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T06:03:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7ae9cec-1604-543e-a03c-96a43d855328', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7ae9cec-1604-543e-a03c-96a43d855328'}, {'abstract': 'India’s first female photojournalist remembered for her iconic photography.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/homai-vyarawalla-pioneering-indian-photojournalist-dies-at-98/', 'snippet': 'India’s first female photojournalist remembered for her iconic photography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Homai Vyarawalla, India’s first female photojournalist who chronicled the country’s march toward independence and captured enduring images of leaders like Mohandas K. Gandhi, Ho Chi Minh and various American presidents of the mid-20th century, died on Jan. 15 in Vadodara, in west India, Haresh Pandya wrote in an obituary for The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Homai Vyarawalla, Pioneering Indian Photojournalist, Dies at 98', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T06:26:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/024c77be-8df4-54ef-8740-40d0502c9cbd', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/024c77be-8df4-54ef-8740-40d0502c9cbd'}, {'abstract': 'An Islamic scholar argues that M.F. Husain and Salman Rushdie both “hurt sentiments of a community” and should be judged on the same terms.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/a-conversation-with-akhtarul-wasey/', 'snippet': 'An Islamic scholar argues that M.F. Husain and Salman Rushdie both “hurt sentiments of a community” and should be judged on the same terms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following the controversy over author Salman Rushdie’s appearance at the Jaipur Literature Festival, which ultimately ended with even a video conference with Mr. Rushdie being cancelled, India Ink is speaking with Muslim leaders about the situation, their feelings about his book “The Satanic Verses” and what role politics played in the affair. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Akhtarul Wasey', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Husain, Maqbool Fida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rushdie, Salman', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rajasthan (India)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T07:12:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0656800c-1c11-5a04-a0e9-5cfcecbff647', 'word_count': 632, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0656800c-1c11-5a04-a0e9-5cfcecbff647'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/news-quiz-jan-30-2012/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries in today’s paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | Jan. 30, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T07:18:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Frasier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frasier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/678079d7-ab68-5084-9a67-8eaa8a2c29cb', 'word_count': 20, 'uri': 'nyt://article/678079d7-ab68-5084-9a67-8eaa8a2c29cb'}, {'abstract': 'A winding march through Lower Manhattan to show solidarity for Occupy Oakland protesters led to scuffles with the police on Sunday night.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/12-arrested-at-n-y-c-march-for-oakland-protesters/', 'snippet': 'A winding march through Lower Manhattan to show solidarity for Occupy Oakland protesters led to scuffles with the police on Sunday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twelve protesters were arrested Sunday night on a march through Lower Manhattan to show support for Occupy protesters in Oakland, where a violent confrontation erupted on Saturday night between the police and demonstrators who tried to take over an empty convention center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '12 Arrested at Manhattan March for Oakland Protesters', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Occupy Wall Street', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T07:26:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News