. Sunday Review recently profiled the most famous (former) leader of...', 'lead_paragraph': 'VALPARAÍSO, Chile —On a Valparaíso street choked solid with traffic not long ago, I looked up as Chilean students on a balcony unfurled a bedsheet banner. “Please pardon the bother,” it read, “but we’re having a revolution.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/30/blogs/chile-student-demos-rdv/chile-student-demos-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bedsheet Revolution', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Valparaiso (Chile)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T10:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mort Rosenblum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mort', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenblum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef6b8eef-db5f-58e7-8ffb-7ab51ea48c42', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef6b8eef-db5f-58e7-8ffb-7ab51ea48c42'}, {'abstract': 'Belgium was paralyzed by a national strike Monday as unions, angry at austerity measures, timed their protest to coincide with a one-day meeting of European Union leaders in the capital, Brussels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/world/europe/strike-grips-belgium-ahead-of-european-union-summit.html', 'snippet': 'Belgium was paralyzed by a national strike Monday as unions, angry at austerity measures, timed their protest to 