'nyt://article/f6d77dc9-1a0c-5735-b17b-d46472822c31', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6d77dc9-1a0c-5735-b17b-d46472822c31'}, {'abstract': 'For Rachel Yang, a senior at Minnetonka High School in Minnesota, “college-app. limbo” is the worst part of the application process.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/envelope-please-rachel-yang-2/', 'snippet': 'For Rachel Yang, a senior at Minnetonka High School in Minnesota, “college-app. limbo” is the worst part of the application process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of weeks ago, I started teaching Saturday morning tot ice skating classes at an arena near my house. These children scramble through the door and pile onto the ice. Some are barely 3 years old. Some can’t stand up in skates without being hoisted under the armpits. These are the students our program director calls “Very-Beginners.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fear and Trembling on the Post-Application Roller Coaster', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T11:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Yang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f78b1f1-73a7-5d26-bf19-933ae028652b', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f78b1f1-73a7-5d26-bf19-933ae028652b'}, {'abstract': 'Plans to improve more roads or to bring more taxis into service generally make traffic worse, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/traffic-jam-economics/', 'snippet': 'Plans to improve more roads or to bring more taxis into service generally make traffic worse, an economist writes.', 'lead_p