ity’s Center for Language and Music. And he wanted to play the guitar. He said he had no rhythm, but spent his sabbatical finding a way to learn to play the guitar and wrote a book about his effort, discussed in this New York Times article last week. Dr. Marcus agreed to answer readers’ questions about the fears and challenges of learning new skills as an adult. Here are his responses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gary Marcus, Cognitive Psychologist, Answers Readers’ Questions', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Guitars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crispell, Marilyn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marcus, Gary', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Metheny, Pat', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schoenberg, Arnold', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vai, Steve', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T12:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8719fd7-b196-5435-aba3-7a29ee5582f3', 'word_count': 1769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8719fd7-b196-5435-aba3-7a29ee5582f3'}, {'abstract': 'What should McDonald’s have done differently on Twitter — or was disaster inevitable?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/this-week-in-small-business-a-twitter-lesson/', 'snippet': 'What should McDonald