new tool to fight e-mail scams, spoofs and phishing attacks. The tool, called Domain-based Message Authentication, Reporting and Conformance, or DMARC, aims to not only keep malware out of in-boxes, but also get a better sense of the threat landscape: who’s behind e-mail scams, where they lurk, how they spoof and who they target.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/technology-companies-pair-up-to-confront-the-scourge-of-internet/', 'snippet': 'On Monday, an informal working group of engineers from PayPal, Facebook, Google, Microsoft, Yahoo and other technology firms will introduce a new tool to fight e-mail scams, spoofs and phishing attacks. The tool, called Domain-based Message Authen...', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all the engineer-poaching and trash-talking going around Silicon Valley these days, there has also been a surprising amount of behind-the-scenes collaboration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Technology Companies Confront a Scourge of the Internet', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Phishing (Computer Fraud)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spam (Electronic Mail)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T14:10:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/319c9d40-29d9-55bd-a30a-f11ef56b05bf', 'word_count': 795,