illion-Dollar Theft Case, Church Worker With a Secret Past', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Million-Dollar Theft Case, Church Worker With a Secret Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Anita', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embezzlement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T14:34:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon Otterman and Russ Buettner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Otterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Russ', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buettner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e27cb6fc-8d47-5723-a9d6-9312bac6fe08', 'word_count': 1092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e27cb6fc-8d47-5723-a9d6-9312bac6fe08'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: A magazine survey says out-of-towners don’t have the nicest things to say about New Yorkers, and New Yorkers don’t, either. But that’s not the full story.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/were-not-so-bad-really/', 'snippet': 'The Day: A magazine survey says out-of-towners don’t have the nicest things to say about New Yorkers, and New Yorkers don’t, either. But that’s not the full story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last few days City Hall has noted that more people came to New York in 2011 than it had previously thought. The mayor made the point again on Sunday in his weekly radio talk. It seems that 50.5 million masochists from foreign countries and other parts of the United States journeyed to our city last year and spent $32 billion. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We’re Not So Bad. Really.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T14:41:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/443ac0f2-e6ae-57e8-8046-f6c5eec6fdcf', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/443ac0f2-e6ae-57e8-8046-f6c5eec6fdcf'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/what-were-reading-361/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Wall Street Journal: Eric Ripert discusses his favorite airport food in New York and around the world. He doesn’t mention World Bean coffee in the Delta terminal at La Guardia, one of the best pour-overs in the city. Are they still there? — Nick Fox', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T14:46:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3035f81-2e87-5d12-93d2-8257ccca9363', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3035f81-2e87-5d12-93d2-8257ccca9363'}, {'abstract': 'Why I am blogging.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/welcome/', 'snippet': 'Why I am blogging.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whenever I bump into my friend Felix Salmon, the ridiculously prolific business blogger at Reuters, he starts pestering me about getting back to blogging again. I point out to him that blogging is what he gets paid for, whereas for someone like me, blogging is something I’m supposed to be doing “in between” the things I get paid for, like writing Op-Ed columns as well as articles for the Times Magazine. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Welcome', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T14:49:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f9d9faf-cddf-526f-952f-1c57a753b585', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f9d9faf-cddf-526f-952f-1c57a753b585'}, {'abstract': 'Also, Showtime gains on H.B.O., political advertising across the dial and who are those people buying newspapers?', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/the-breakfast-meeting-reading-ruperts-tweets-and-b-n-wears-a-white-hat/', 'snippet': 'Also, Showtime gains on H.B.O., political advertising across the dial and who are those people buying newspapers?', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 80, Rupert Murdoch has jumped into Twitter with both feet, among a rare number of moguls who share their thoughts as soon as they pop up. David Carr assesses his corpus of writing – 107 Tweets and counting. They are “devoid of nuance, partisan in the extreme and prone to crankiness,” he writes; in other words, vintage Rupert Murdoch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Reading Rupert’s Tweets, and B.&N. Wears a White Hat', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galassi, Jonathan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snider, Stacey', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spielberg, Steven', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DreamWorks Animation SKG Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Showtime', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Weather Channel', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T14:54:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1