driver had been winless for six years in stock cars, but was part of the winning team in the 24-hour endurance race at Daytona International Speedway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having signed recently with Roger Penske Racing for the 2012 Nascar Sprint Cup season, A.J. Allmendinger might have been expected to pass the weeks before the Daytona 500, on Feb. 26, by visualizing races, holding conference calls with his pit crew and familiarizing himself with his new racecar. Instead, he’s busy winning races in anything but a stock car.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Victory, Elusive in Nascar, Finds A.J. Allmendinger in Rolex 24 at Daytona', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Daytona 500 (Auto Race)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nascar Sprint Cup Series', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allmendinger, A J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franchitti, Dario', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ganassi, Chip', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMurray, Jamie', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Montoya, Juan Pablo', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Justin', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indy Racing League', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Stock Car Auto Racing', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Penske Racing', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Daytona Beach (Fla)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T15:40:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60b888f8-df4f-5e1d-8ec9-256f30ce306e', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60b888f8-df4f-5e1d-8ec9-256f30ce306e'}, {'abstract': 'A survey of 1,000 Americans reveals a nation’s private mobile habits of talking, texting, even shopping, while otherwise engaged. Among the troubling stats: every fifth male has called into a meeting with his pants down.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/the-rise-of-the-toilet-texter/', 'snippet': 'A survey of 1,000 Americans reveals a nation’s private mobile habits of talking, texting, even shopping, while otherwise engaged. Among the troubling stats: every fifth male has called into a meeting with his pants down.', 'lead_paragraph': ' We know where some of you are reading this.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rise of the Toilet Texter', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bathrooms and Toilets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T15:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78212a51-5781-55c9-9c98-87051fe5325f', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78212a51-5781-55c9-9c98-87051fe5325f'}, {'abstract': '“Summertime,” has been covered more than 25,000 times, and here are some of the most memorable versions.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/summertime-rendered-25000-ways/', 'snippet': '“Summertime,” has been covered more than 25,000 times, and here are some of the most memorable versions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two Sunday Reviews ago, I wrote about the long history of “Porgy and Bess” as a prism through which African-Americans have viewed their own history. I am a relatively recent devotee of what I like to think of as the “real” “Porgy and Bess,” the full-length opera. (So far as I can tell, there is only one performance of the opera ever recorded on DVD — a 1993 Trevor Nunn production with Simon Rattle conducting, released in 2001.) Like most people, I came to “Porgy and Bess” through some of the many popular recordings of its famous songs. Indeed, I received several e-mails questioning my sanity for writing about the opera without mentioning two of the most famous recordings: the Ella Fitzgerald-Louis Armstrong version, and the equally sublime Miles Davis recording.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Summertime,’ Rendered 25,000 Ways', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T15:45:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae4ffbc8-7375-5563-8f0d-26333c02093e', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae4ffbc8-7375-5563-8f0d-26333c02093e'}, {'abstract': 'A welcome packet in Indianapolis includes a pencil drawing of a “Super Kid.”', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/in-indianapolis-the-cute-wont-quit/', 'snippet': 'A welcome packet in Indianapolis includes a pencil drawing of a “Super Kid.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS – In a great article examining how this city landed (and then prepared to host) Super Bowl XLVI, my colleague John Branch described how local eighth-graders were involved in delivering bids to the N.F.L. owners. It was innovative, thoughtful and downright cute, and surely enhanced the city’s proposal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Indianapolis, the Cute Won’t Quit', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Branch, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indianapolis (Ind)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T15:46:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37161423-745d-5f0a-82e1-10ebe63adf0e', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37161423-745d-5f0a-82e1-10ebe63adf0e'}, {'abstract': 'Going to sleep after experiencing negative emotions appears to reinforce or “preserve” them, research suggests.', 'web_url'