10 percent of the festival’s slate, 17 movies in all, including four that were in competition.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/at-sundance-kickstarter-resembled-a-movie-studio-but-without-the-egos/', 'snippet': 'The online fund-raising site had a banner year at this year’s Sundance Film Festival. It helped finance 10 percent of the festival’s slate, 17 movies in all, including four that were in competition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One night last week there was a late-night party at Sundance — one of many — this one hosted by an outfit that had helped finance 10 percent of the festival’s slate, 17 movies in all, including four that were in competition.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Sundance, Kickstarter Resembled a Movie Studio, but Without the Egos', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kickstarter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T15:50:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/057ea14c-488d-5f83-83d7-c8b0358f15fd', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/057ea14c-488d-5f83-83d7-c8b0358f15fd'}, {'abstract': 'The detective was approached from behind by two young men, one of whom hit him with a cane while the other simulated a gun and demanded money, the police said.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/off-duty-detective-fatally-shoots-robber-police-say/', 'snippet': 'The detective was approached from behind by two young men, one of whom hit him with a cane while the other simulated a gun and demanded money, the police said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 3:00 p.m. | An off-duty police detective fatally shot a teenager who tried to rob him Sunday night in Bushwick, Brooklyn, according to the police, who offered the following account:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Off-Duty Detective Fatally Shoots Robber, Police Say', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bushwick (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T15:55:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/362d5873-521e-5022-887f-e9d99b631468', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/362d5873-521e-5022-887f-e9d99b631468'}, {'abstract': 'Shared rooms and a largely female population mean that men find it harder to find a bed in nursing homes.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/fewer-beds-for-men-entering-nursing-homes/', 'snippet': 'Shared rooms and a largely female population mean that men find it harder to find a bed in nursing homes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Searching for a nursing home for his hospitalized father in semirural Massachusetts, a friend of mine recently came up against an unexpected barrier. It’s harder to find a bed for a man than for a woman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fewer Beds for Men Entering Nursing Homes', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T15:58:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3a05a8a-e6b4-5f76-bd86-2fcf98e23564', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3a05a8a-e6b4-5f76-bd86-2fcf98e23564'}, {'abstract': 'The police say the woman left her 3-year-old and 5-year-old daughters in front of a Brooklyn housing project on Sunday afternoon.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/mother-accused-of-abandoning-children-is-arrested/', 'snippet': 'The police say the woman left her 3-year-old and 5-year-old daughters in front of a Brooklyn housing project on Sunday afternoon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A woman who abandoned her 3-year-old and 5-year-old daughters in front of a Brooklyn housing project on Sunday afternoon has been arrested, the police said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mother, Accused of Abandoning Children, Is Arrested', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canarsie (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T15:58:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abf635e3-5c0b-5332-9ac4-c25a2ba228e9', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abf635e3-5c0b-5332-9ac4-c25a2ba228e9'}, {'abstract': 'Stefano Gabbana and Domenico Dolce’s newest spring bag was created to suit all personalities.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/the-get-dolce-gabbana-bag/', 'snippet': 'Stefano Gabbana and Domenico Dolce’s newest spring bag was created to suit all personalities.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Often the attention to details makes all the difference,” says the Dolce & Gabbana co-designer Stefano Gabbana, referring to the design of his and Domenico Dolce’s newest spring bag, which hits stores this week. Structured and clean, with a handle made for elbow-hooking and a padlock made of gold metal (speaking of details), the style comes in three sizes and is available in a variety of materials, from aluminum foil to straw and python, and in a range of gorgeous colors (pastels, primaries) and finishes (metallic and matte). For the minimalist, the classic leather style suits best. For the quirky carrier, a metallic picnic purse version is perfect. And, for the vintage-inspired, a dainty woven version like this one in dusty rose does the trick. Pick your poison.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Dolce & Gabbana Bag', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T16:01:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e870ddac-af3b-5a80-98b4-2be9de86b0df', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e870ddac-af3b-5a80-98b4-2be9de86b0df'}, {'abstract': 'The Russian Foreign Ministry announced Monday that it had convinced Bashar al-Assad’s government to start informal negotiations in Moscow with representatives of the opposition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/world/europe/russia-says-syria-has-agreed-to-talks.html', 'snippet': 'The Russian Foreign Ministry announced Monday that it had convinced Bashar al-Assad’s government to start informal negotiations in Moscow with representatives of the opposition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW—Russia announced on Monday that it had convinced Bashar al-Assad’s government in Syria to start informal negotiations in Moscow with representatives of the opposition in an effort to end a bloody uprising that has left thousands dead. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Says Syria Has Agreed to Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Says Syria Has Agreed to Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T16:03:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb189662-200f-535c-afe2-8f63b7da3f1e', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb189662-200f-535c-afe2-8f63b7da3f1e'}, {'abstract': 'A young girl who was burned and tortured in northern Afghanistan, allegedly by her husband’s family, continues along the path of recovery, at least physically.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/an-update-on-sahar-gul/', 'snippet': 'A young girl who was burned and tortured in northern Afghanistan, allegedly by her husband’s family, continues along the path of recovery, at least physically.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some readers might remember the last time I visited Sahar Gul, when I managed to get past the bureaucracy of the hospital in Kabul where she was being treated and her relatives, doctors and supporters welcomed me to her bedside.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Update on Sahar Gul', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gul, Sahar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T16:09:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05775877-9a8b-5ed2-bb6c-882f26ebd667', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05775877-9a8b-5ed2-bb6c-882f26ebd667'}, {'abstract': 'If you haven’t see it already, find a replay of Novak Djokovic’s epic victory over Rafael Nadal, a match for the ages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/sports/a-certified-grand-slam-classic-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'If you haven’t see it already, find a replay of Novak Djokovic’s epic victory over Rafael Nadal, a match for the ages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Normally, the weekend before the Super Bowl is a quiet one, the landscape cleared of meaningful football — the Pro Bowl not counting as meaningful or football — aided by the N.H.L. taking its season siesta at the same time for its All-Star game, but the Australian Open had other plans this year. Usually, it’s the Grand Slam that few in this hemisphere realizes is going on because A) it’s played in the American Insomniac Time Zone and B) doesn’t tennis have an offseason and isn’t it now? (Answer: it lasted three minutes and no).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Certified Grand Slam Classic', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Certified Grand Slam Classic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boatright, Ryan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Azarenka, Victoria', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Irsay, Jim', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 