ts that prices are still at some of the highest levels seen in decades.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fresh Take on the World Food Problem', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Famine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Sophia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T16:57:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7eb4e2e-bf24-523b-a79c-250c7d171019', 'word_count': 333, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7eb4e2e-bf24-523b-a79c-250c7d171019'}, {'abstract': 'Guns N’ Roses, ahead of its induction into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame, will perform three shows in New York in February.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/guns-n-roses-plans-minitour-with-3-shows-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'Guns N’ Roses, ahead of its induction into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame, will perform three shows in New York in February.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Guns N’ Roses will play three concerts at relatively small clubs in New York City in February as part of the run-up to its induction into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame in April, a publicist announced on Monday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guns N’ Roses Plans Minitour, With Three Shows in New York', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Axl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slash', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stradlin, Izzy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Guns N' Roses", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Blues', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rock and Roll Hall of Fame and Museum', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roseland Ballroom', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Webster Hall', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlantic City (NJ)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T17:09:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/867c1915-bba0-5324-a6f3-5ff97b767784', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/867c1915-bba0-5324-a6f3-5ff97b767784'}, {'abstract': 'The move to combine the Screen Actors Guild and the American Federation of Radio and Television Artists cleared another hurdle on Saturday when the Aftra board gave its approval.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/merger-of-actors-unions-keeps-up-the-momentum/', 'snippet': 'The move to combine the Screen Actors Guild and the American Federation of Radio and Television Artists cleared another hurdle on Saturday when the Aftra board gave its approval.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — A planned merger between the Screen Actors Guild and the American Federation of Radio and Television Artists, which has been clearing hurdles of one sort or another for many months, cleared another on Saturday when the Aftra board gave its approval. The SAG board had already done so.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Merger of Actors Unions Keeps Up the Momentum', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Federation of Radio and Television Artists', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Screen Actors Guild', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hollywood (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T17:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a038756-4cfb-5959-8edc-6588eb2f0a77', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a038756-4cfb-5959-8edc-6588eb2f0a77'}, {'abstract': 'Viola Davis looks like a stronger best-actress contender after the SAG Awards, but Jean Dujardin’s win and “The Help’s” good showing may not necessarily translate into Academy Awards.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/what-the-sag-awards-may-portend-for-the-oscars/', 'snippet': 'Viola Davis looks like a stronger best-actress contender after the SAG Awards, but Jean Dujardin’s win and “The Help’s” good showing may not necessarily translate into Academy Awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — “Now it’s actually a race; now it’s actually going to be fun,” one Oscar-watcher whispered after the Screen Actors Guild awards on Sunday, which scrambled predictions by picking “The Help” as the best movie of the year. The actors guild also chose the star of “The Artist,” Jean Dujardin, over the leading hopeful George Clooney (and others) for best actor, and Viola Davis of “The Help” for best actress. Octavia Spencer and Christopher Plummer continued their lockstep toward Oscar in the supporting categories.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the S.A.G. Awards May Portend for the Oscars', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T17:20:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By MELENA RYZIK', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'RYZIK', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9649235d-2b29-58e3-ae49-c32083fb0eb5', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9649235d-2b29-58e3-ae49-c32083fb0eb5'}, {'abstract': 'The actress of the film, “The Help,” is stunning in an Alexander McQueen dress at the SAG Awards.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/look-of-the-moment-emma-stone-2/', 'snippet': 'The actress of the film, “The Help,” is stunning in an Alexander McQueen dress at the SAG Awards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Look: Black Rose. A glamorous tea-length dress with a hip-defining waistline and embroidered bustier needs only a heel with the skinniest ankle strap and a lip with the rosiest tint to make it feel finished.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look of The Moment | Emma Stone', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T17:22:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/291405ee-2a3d-5ef4-8133-a380c42a8eac', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/291405ee-2a3d-5ef4-8133-a380c42a8eac'}, {'abstract': 'A Q&A with Ronen Bergman about his cover story on the possibility of an Israeli attack on Iran in 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/behind-the-cover-story-ronen-bergman-on-israeli-plans-to-strike-iran/', 'snippet': 'A Q&A with Ronen Bergman about his cover story on the possibility of an Israeli attack on Iran in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ronen Bergman is a political and military analyst for the Israeli newspaper Yedioth Ahronoth and is currently at work on a history of the Mossad. He wrote this week’s cover story on the possibility of an Israeli attack on Iran in 2012 to prevent Iran from becoming a nuclear power.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Ronen Bergman on Whether Israel Will Attack Iran', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T17:25:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78e6d7f6-cb63-5e3a-a3ae-f0b70e04027d', 'word_count': 1520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78e6d7f6-cb63-5e3a-a3ae-f0b70e04027d'}, {'abstract': 'Tax credits from New York City are the final piece of financing needed for the construction of El Barrio’s Artspace (PS109), a development of housing and work spaces for artists planned for East Harlem.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/artists-development-in-harlem-gets-final-financing/', 'snippet': 'Tax credits from New York City are the final piece of financing needed for the construction of El Barrio’s Artspace (PS109), a development of housing and work spaces for artists planned for East Harlem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The construction of El Barrio’s Artspace (P.S. 109), a development of housing and work spaces for artists planned for East Harlem, will be aided by low-income housing tax credits from the New York City Department of Housing Preservation and Development, Artspace Projects has announced. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Artists’ Development in Harlem Gets Final Financing', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'valu