onsumer Federation of America.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/lower-income-families-may-pay-more-for-auto-insurance/', 'snippet': 'Many low-income families cannot afford car insurance, at least in part because insurers price their policies in ways that result in them paying more, according to a new report from the Consumer Federation of America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated | Jan. 31 Added information from industry trade groups.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lower-Income Families May Pay More for Auto Insurance', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Insurance and Liability', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic and Parking Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Federation of America', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T18:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1004f55d-121f-584c-bee1-728be7335f7d', 'word_count': 1324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1004f55d-121f-584c-bee1-728be7335f7d'}, {'abstract': 'The former editor of Cosmopolitan is financing an institute on media innovation on both campuses, at Columbia’s journalism school and Stanford’s school of engineering. Her total gift to the journalism school was its largest ever.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/helen-gurley-brown-gives-30-million-for-new-media-studies-at-columbia-and-stanford/', 'snippet': 'The former editor of Cosmopolitan is financing an institute on media innovation on both campuses, at Columbia’s journalism school and Stanford’s school of engineering. Her total gift to the journalism school was its largest ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the backing of a $30 million donation from Helen Gurley Brown, the former editor of Cosmopolitan, the graduate school of journalism at Columbia University and the school of engineering at Stanford University on Monday said that they would create a center for media innovation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Helen Gurley Brown Gives $30 Million for Media Innovation at Columbia and Stanford', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engineering and Engineers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Journalism Schools', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Helen Gurley', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lemann, Nicholas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T18:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14358305-7f6c-5c20-9d83-0fe40a799b65', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14358305-7f6c-5c20-9d83-0fe40a799b65'}, {'abstract': 'One advantage: it does make it easier to treat different customers differently.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/does-google-offer-businesses-an-edge/', 'snippet': 'One advantage: it does make it easier to treat different customers differently.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a lot of excitement last year when Google+ — Google’s answer to Facebook — was introduced, because, well, it’s Google. But according to everything I’ve heard and can observe, the great majority of small businesses haven’t flocked to the service.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Google+ Offer Businesses an Edge?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google+', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T18:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By David H. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12b36a87-192d-5ea1-834c-27f4e2cffb0a', 'word_count': 951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12b36a87-192d-5ea1-834c-27f4e2cffb0a'}, {'abstract': 'For Autumn Chubbs, a high school senior from Long Beach, Calif., the quest for a prom date must be balanced with seeking financial aid and other rites of the season.', 'web_ur