anization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c4cfa15-8e2d-557f-bc8b-53a1bd971563', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c4cfa15-8e2d-557f-bc8b-53a1bd971563'}, {'abstract': 'A concept that didn’t seem to need naming until quite recently.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/health/views/in-search-of-the-elusive-definition-of-heterosexuality.html', 'snippet': 'A concept that didn’t seem to need naming until quite recently.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Science generally succeeds in bringing some order to human existence — except when it does just the reverse, imposing a structure that never quite fits properly no matter how much it is tweaked. Then it just accentuates the underlying chaos.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/science/31ZUGE/31ZUGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 693, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/science/31ZUGE/31ZUGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/31/science/31ZUGE/31ZUGE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Search of the Elusive Definition of Heterosexuality', 'kicker': 'Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Search of the Elusive Definition of Heterosexuality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blank, Hanne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gender', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T18:36:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Views', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abigail Zuger, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abigail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zuger', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc114333-b6dd-5cde-a49f-178b09686cbc', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc114333-b6dd-5cde-a49f-178b09686cbc'}, {'abstract': 'Kenneth Branagh on how stardom has changed over the decades and the taxonomy of the red carpet.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/kenneth-branagh-and-the-red-carpet-bazaar/', 'snippet': 'Kenneth Branagh on how stardom has changed over the decades and the taxonomy of the red carpet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Noting that fame has changed tremendously (and, also, not at all) in the past few decades, the Bagger’s pals at New York magazine have done an exhaustive study of the celebrity economy, from freebies to the cost of appearing wrinkle-free. It’s worth a look. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenneth Branagh and the Red-Carpet Bazaar', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Branagh, Kenneth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clooney, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olivier, Laurence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T18:36:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b799d4f-02b5-55f9-b0c4-4bcd9604de51', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b799d4f-02b5-55f9-b0c4-4bcd9604de51'}, {'abstract': 'The gross-out reality show apparently found a stunt too extreme even by its standards, as NBC decides to broadcast a repeat instead of a new episode featuring the stunt.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/nbc-pulls-fear-factor-episode-featuring-drinking-of-donkey-semen/', 'snippet': 'The gross-out reality show apparently found a stunt too extreme even by its standards, as NBC decides to broadcast a repeat instead of a new episode featuring the stunt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in December, when NBC was promoting the return of “Fear Factor,” the stunt and gross-out reality competition, there was one event that the producers and the host, Joe Rogan, would not discuss. It was extreme even by the standards of “Fear Factor,” they said at the time, and they didn’t know if it would ever be broadcast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'NBC Pulls ‘Fear Factor’ Episode Featuring Drinking of Donkey Semen', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T18:40:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09cdc085-537f-5d71-b07a-359438de1faa', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09cdc085-537f-5d71-b07a-359438de1faa'}, {'abstract': 'For Feb. 1, the inaugural Digital Learning Day, we present ideas any teacher, student or parent can use to participate, as well as with links to Times articles from 1970 to 2002 on the impact of the digital revolution in education.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/celebrate-digital-learning-day-with-40-years-of-n-times-edtech-reporting/', 'snippet': 'For Feb. 1, the inaugural Digital Learning Day, we present ideas any teacher, student or parent can use to participate, as well as with links to Times articles from 1970 to 2002 on the impact of the digital revolution in education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times has been covering technology’s role in education since the paper first began publishing — from an 1872 editorial questioning whether to teach science or the classics to boys of “ordinary abilities,” (PDF) to Sputnik-era pieces demanding more technical education for American schoolchildren (PDF) to today, when you can hardly open, or click on, the paper without finding an article that references the impact of technology on schools, learning or thinking. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrate Digital Learning Day With 40 Years of Times EdTech Reporting', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T18:40:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f818725b-a0be-562a-a41c-0bd34464fb3d', 'word_count': 1716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f818725b-a0be-562a-a41c-0bd34464fb3d'},