f)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T18:53:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ffa126d-1837-51dc-a759-51685e12578e', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ffa126d-1837-51dc-a759-51685e12578e'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks’ usual home-court advantage has become a cauldron of pressure this season.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/home-court-advantage-or-burden-for-the-underachieving-knicks/', 'snippet': 'The Knicks’ usual home-court advantage has become a cauldron of pressure this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even in the leanest of years for the Knicks -– an era in which they’re still arguably mired -– they have enjoyed an impressive home-court advantage at Madison Square Garden. Whatever their on-court fortunes, the Knicks can count in their favor a fan base as knowledgeable, and as loud, as any in professional sports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Home Court Advantage or Burden for the Underachieving Knicks?', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T18:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By JIM CAVAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'CAVAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/963ba156-cef8-5360-aeb8-38f80eb9d933', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/963ba156-cef8-5360-aeb8-38f80eb9d933'}, {'abstract': 'In a book review in Science Times, Abigail Zuger takes a look at “Straight: The Surprisingly Short History of Heterosexuality,” by Hanne Blank, an expert on the history of sexuality.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/the-changing-meaning-of-heterosexuality/', 'snippet': 'In a book review in Science Times, Abigail Zuger takes a look at “Straight: The Surprisingly Short History of Heterosexuality,” by Hanne Blank, an expert on the history of sexuality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In today’s Science Times, Dr. Abigail Zuger takes a look at “Straight: The Surprisingly Short History of Heterosexuality,” a book by Hanne Blank, an expert on the history of sexuality. In “Straight,” Ms. Blank delves into the history of heterosexuality – a history that in at least one sense is surprisingly short. She notes, for example, that the word “heterosexual” didn’t come into use until a little over a century ago. As Dr. Zuger writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Changing Meaning of Heterosexuality', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blank, Hanne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T19:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/913b9d45-8a4b-5e3a-92e9-58deb42f0a2e', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/913b9d45-8a4b-5e3a-92e9-58deb42f0a2e'}, {'abstract': 'For