phonograph records contains the only known recording of Otto von Bismarck.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tucked away for decades in a cabinet in Thomas Edison’s laboratory, just behind the cot in which the great inventor napped, a trove of wax cylinder phonograph records has been brought back to life after more than a century of silence. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/science/31EDIS1/31EDIS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 869, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restored Edison Records Revive Giants of 19th-Century Germany', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Restored Edison Records Revive Giants of 19th-Century Germany', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edison, Thomas A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Archives and Records', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recording Equipment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bismarck, Otto von', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T20:07:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Cowen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60628533-180e-59db-acf6-0628532fe295', 'word_count': 949, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60628533-180e-59db-acf6-0628532fe295'}, {'abstract': 'Three people living with h