ma promoted the creation of a new unit to investigate “the abusive lending and packaging of risky mortgages that led to the housing crisis” in order to “hold accountable those who broke the law, speed assistance to homeowners, and help turn the page on an era of recklessness that hurt so many Americans.” On Friday, Eric H. Holder Jr., the attorney general, announced the formation of the Residential Mortgage-Backed Securities Working Group, which will be staffed by 55 lawyers, agents and analysts, to implement the president’s program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Renewed Focus on a Financial Crisis Crackdown', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgage-Backed Securities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T20:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c722da6-8848-5e16-bbfa-bcd8f7b07684', 'word_count': 1012, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c722da6-8848-5e16-bbfa-bcd8f7b07684'}, {'abstract': 'The drug, Erivedge, made by Genentech, was approved for adults with basal cell carcinoma that has spread elsewhere in the body or those who are not candidates for surgery or radiation.', 'web_url': 'https://prescriptions.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/f-d-a-approves-drug-for-an-advanced-skin-cancer/', 'snippet': 'The drug, Erivedge, made by Genentech, was approved for adults with basal cell carcinoma that has spread elsewhere in the body or those who are not candidates for surgery or radiation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first drug for an advanced form of the most common type of skin cancer won approval from the Food and Drug Administration on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.D.A. Approves Drug for an Advanced Skin Cancer', 'kicker': 'Prescriptions', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genentech Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T20:44:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d1d54da-e910-5f4a-bcd1-f010a6672e72', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d1d54da-e910-5f4a-bcd1-f010a6672e72'}, {'abstract': 'Kyle Williams, a receiver for the 49ers, faced criticism for mishandling two punt returns in the N.F.C. Championship game. His father Ken, the general manager of the Chicago White Sox, is not a fan favorite either.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/like-son-like-father-kyle-and-ken-williams-face-the-critics/', 'snippet': 'Kyle Williams, a receiver for the 49ers, faced criticism for mishandling two punt returns in the N.F.C. Championship game. His father Ken, the general manager of the Chicago White Sox, is not a fan favorite either.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — Ken Williams, the general manager of the Chicago White Sox, was at Candlestick Park in San Francisco for the N.F.C. championship game to watch his son, Kyle, a 49ers receiver, play in the biggest football game of his life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Like Son, Like Father: Kyle and Ken Williams Face the Critics', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buehrle, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunn, Adam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Epstein, Theo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guillen, Ozzie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'RIOS, ALEX', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Kenny', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago White Sox', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Marlins', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco 49ers', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T20:48:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/948cedfd-bac0-59bc-b009-35ec075cd782', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/948cedfd-bac0-59bc-b009-35ec075cd782'}, {'abstract': "Public Prep, a charter school network in New York City, said a senior member of the finance and operations staff used the organization's credit card to spend tens of thousands of dollars on personal items. The staff member has resigned, and the network said all but $1,000 should be recouped through insurance.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/01/30/financial-improprieties-found-at-all-girls-charter-school-network/', 'snippet': "Public Prep, a charter school network in New York City, said a senior member of the finance and operations staff used the organization's credit card to spend tens of thousands of dollars on personal items. The staff member has resigned, and the ne...", 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Financial Improprieties Alleged at All-Girls Charter School Network', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T20:50:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANNA M. PHILLIPS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ff4dde6-f070-59a1-ab6b-82268c5eb00c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ff4dde6-f070-59a1-ab6b-82268c5eb00c'}, {'abstract': 'The dancer appeared to hurt herself during a performance of Christopher Wheeldon’s “Polyphonia” at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/injured-dancer-out-for-the-rest-of-city-ballet-season/', 'snippet': 'The dancer appeared to hurt herself during a performance of Christopher Wheeldon’s “Polyphonia” at the David H. Koch Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jennie Somogyi, a principal dancer at New York City Ballet, tore the Achilles’ tendon in her right foot during a performance Saturday night and will be out for the rest of the season, the company said on Monday. It was the second major injury for Ms. Somogyi since early 2004, when she tore a tendon in her left foot during a show. She battled back then, undergoing reconstructive surgery and extensive physical therapy before returning to the stage after 18 months. Rob Daniels, a City Ballet spokesman, said Ms. Somogyi would have surgery on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Injured Dancer Out for the Rest of City Ballet Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Somogyi, Jennie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T20:55:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c1de592-d685-5509-8054-ffa3671d7b64', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c1de592-d685-5509-8054-ffa3671d7b64'}, {'abstract': 'On a tiny NPR radio station in Connecticut, two writers share their belief that something will eventually sour for the Giants because much has gone wrong in the past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/sports/football/despairing-the-giants-but-without-shouting-on-public-radio.html', 'snippet': 'On a tiny NPR radio station in Connecticut, two writers share their belief that something will eventually sour for the Giants because much has gone wrong in the past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday nights from tiny WHDD-AM and FM in Sharon, Conn., David Kamp and Peter Richmond’s love for the Giants battles their sense of inevitable doom. And love loses.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/sports/football/31radio-pic/31radio-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/31/sports/football/31radio-pic/31radio-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/sports/football/31radio-pic/31radio-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/sports/football/31radio-pic/31radio-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/31/sports/football/31radio-pic/31radio-pic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Best of Times, Despairing the Giants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Best of Times, Despairing the Giants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Public Radio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richmond, Peter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kamp, David', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-30T21:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Spo