 end.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/numberplay-ordering-in-circles/', 'snippet': 'A puzzle based on a very simple idea of summing small integers arranged in a circle to magically generate all the numbers in order, without end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Take a look at the numbers in the inner black circle above. This clockwise arrangement of 1, 2, 3, 1, 3, and 4 has an interesting property. With it you can count all the numbers from one to seven in order in the following way. You go around the circle reading each number and if it is in counting sequence starting from one, you count it and move on. If it is not in counting sequence, you are allowed to add as many consecutive numbers as needed to make it so.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: Ordering in Circles', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Numbers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T00:28:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pradeep Mutalik and David Fergemann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pradeep', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mutalik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fergemann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d60806a4-0598-5f78-b2ec-ec7c661c8054', 'word_count': 850, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d60806a4-0598-5f78-b2ec-ec7c661c8054'}, {'abstract': 'The Rangers, who play the Devils on Tuesday, have a logjam at forward, but it could come in handy at the trade deadline.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/unusual-problem-rangers-have-too-many-forwards/', 'snippet': 'The Rangers, who play the Devils on Tuesday, have a logjam at forward, but it could come in handy at the trade deadline.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Unlike the Devils, whom they visit at Prudential Center on Tuesday night for the first of five remaining games this season, the Rangers have a problem unique to N.H.L. teams as the calendar turns to February: a roster logjam.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Unusual Problem: Rangers Have Too Many Forwards', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Avery, Sean', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christensen, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeBoer, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eminger, Steve', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Josefson, Jacob', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolski, Wojtek', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T00:29:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Botta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Botta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b91b2324-212c-5a9c-8bca-d98d2c24e5c3', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b91b2324-212c-5a9c-8bca-d98d2c24e5c3'}, {'abstract': 'Jon S. Corzine, former leader of MF Global, has put his 2,400-square-foot apartment in Hoboken, N.J., up for sale, and he reportedly appears to be asking nearly a $1 million less than he paid.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/corzine-puts-hoboken-penthouse-up-for-sale-for-2-9-million/', 'snippet': 'Jon S. Corzine, former leader of MF Global, has put his 2,400-square-foot apartment in Hoboken, N.J., up for sale, and he reportedly appears to be asking nearly a $1 million less than he paid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly three months after MF Global filed for bankruptcy protection, many questions still surround the failed brokerage firm. Not among them, however, is what it will cost to live in the penthouse of its former chief executive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corzine Is Seeking $2.9 Million for Hoboken Penthouse', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corzine, Jon S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T00:41:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b7d0038-e597-5fae-a96c-9a5c16538678', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b7d0038-e597-5fae-a96c-9a5c16538678'}, {'abstract': 'An iPhone app for parents who want a trove of pediatric medical information at their fingertips.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/app-smart-extra-parenting-apps/', 'snippet': 'An iPhone app for parents who want a trove of pediatric medical information at their fingertips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week’s App Smart column highlighted a pair of apps for new parents, WebMD Baby (free on Apple) and Baby Connect ($5 on Apple and Android). Given WebMD Baby’s\xa0pedigree, it’s little surprise that the app offers a deep well of medically related information.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'App Smart Extra: Parenting Apps', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Robert Sears', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WebMD Health Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T00:57:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Tedeschi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tedeschi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17dc32ea-6e33-59dc-94b8-b4360b21c8ba', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17dc32ea-6e33-59dc-94b8-b4360b21c8ba'}, {'abstract': 'The Kennedy family transferred ownership of the main home in their compound in Hyannis Port, Mass., to the Edward M. Kennedy Institute for the United States Senate on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/us/massachusetts-kennedys-transfer-hyannis-home.html', 'snippet': 'The Kennedy family transferred ownership of the main home in their compound in Hyannis Port, Mass., to the Edward M. Kennedy Institute for the United States Senate on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Kennedy family transferred ownership of the main home in their compound in Hyannis Port, Mass., to the Edward M. Kennedy Institute for the United States Senate on Monday. The institute will use the 9,055-square-foot waterfront home for educational seminars and will create a plan to allow limited visits by the public, according to a statement. The Kennedy family, which still owns other homes in the compound, will continue to use the property on a limited basis. Senator Edward M. Kennedy, who died in 2009, arranged for the home to be donated to the institute. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Kennedys Transfer Hyannis Home ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Kennedys Transfer Hyannis Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy Family', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Edward M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hyannis (Mass)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T01:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5181db07-29be-5ab6-be3a-3edd732a4bdf', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5181db07-29be-5ab6-be3a-3edd732a4bdf'}, {'abstract': 'John Jesurun’s “Stopped Bridge of Dreams” has a voice that’s mad, poetic and unsettling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/theater/reviews/john-jesuruns-stopped-bridge-of-dreams-at-la-mama.html', 'snippet': 'John Jesurun’s “Stopped Bridge of Dreams” has a voice that’s mad, poetic and unsettling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Italo Calvino, Douglas Adams and William Gibson had gotten together, maybe become a little drunk and decided to pull a literary all-nighter, the resulting collaboration might have had something of the flavor of John Jes