become similarly recognizable in legal circles as his fight against the university’s charge of trademark infringement heads to the United States Court of Appeals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/sports/ARTIST/ARTIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 788, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/sports/ARTIST/ARTIST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/31/sports/ARTIST/ARTIST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Free Speech vs. Infringement in Suit on Alabama Artwork', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Free Speech vs. Infringement in Suit on Alabama Artwork', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trademarks and Trade Names', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Alabama', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T01:56:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Grant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92d606d8-0f8c-50bc-944e-be864bd547fb', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92d606d8-0f8c-50bc-944e-be864bd547fb'}, {'abstract': 'Asset Acceptance, which buys old debts and tries to collect on them, has settled a Federal Trade Commission case charging that it deceived consumers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/business/ftc-fines-a-collector-of-debt-2-5-million.html', 'snippet': 'Asset Acceptance, which buys old debts and tries to collect on them, has settled a Federal Trade Commission case charging that it deceived consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Federal Trade Commission signaled on Monday that it would continue to crack down on debt collectors who harass consumers for money they may not even be legally obligated to pay. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.T.C. Fines a Collector of Debt $2.5 Million', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'F.T.C. Fines A Collector Of Debt $2.5 Million', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asset Acceptance Capital Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collection Agencies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Trade Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T01:57:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1fd3826-2285-5261-84c9-b035696024f1', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1fd3826-2285-5261-84c9-b035696024f1'}, {'abstract': 'The Treasury Department is investigating whether Freddie Mac bet against refinancings by homeowners while at the same time, making refinancings difficult to obtain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/business/freddie-mac-investments-under-scrutiny-by-treasury-dept.html', 'snippet': 'The Treasury Department is investigating whether Freddie Mac bet against refinancings by homeowners while at the same time, making refinancings difficult to obtain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury Department is investigating a report that Freddie Mac, the mortgage giant, bet against homeowners’ ability to refinance their loans even as it was making it more difficult for them to do so, Jay Carney, a White House spokesman, said on Monday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treasury Investigates Freddie Mac Investment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Investigates Freddie Mac Investment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T01:57:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shaila Dewan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shaila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dewan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/167d4a8d-402b-5bef-9113-6a4533491529', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/167d4a8d-402b-5bef-9113-6a4533491529'}, {'abstract': 'At the World Economic Forum, Wall Street’s top bankers discovered that foreign governments were fighting to end the so-called Volcker Rule.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/volcker-rule-stirs-up-opposition-overseas/', 'snippet': 'At the World Economic Forum, Wall Street’s top bankers discovered that foreign governments were fighting to end the so-called Volcker Rule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAVOS, Switzerland — Usually, it is the banks that are fighting efforts to impose new regulations on the industry. Now, it is foreign governments fighting against bank regulations in the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Volcker Rule Stirs Up Opposition Overseas', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, Mark J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osborne, George', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T01:59:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Ross Sorkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Ross', 'lastname': 'Sorkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72bb69e3-1938-520b-a38f-7596b6ba9e7f', 'word_count': 1058, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72bb69e3-1938-520b-a38f-7596b6ba9e7f'}, {'abstract': 'Accountable care organizations will shift the focus of medicine away from treating sickness and toward keeping patients healthy.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/the-end-of-health-insurance-companies/', 'snippet': 'Accountable care organizations will shift the focus of medicine away from treating sickness and toward keeping patients healthy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a bold prediction for the new year. By 2020, the American health insurance industry will be extinct. Insurance companies will be replaced by accountable care organizations — groups of doctors, hospitals and other health care providers who come together to provide the full range of medical care for patients. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The End of Health Insurance Companies', 'kicker': 'Ezekiel J. Emanuel', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T02:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ezekiel J. Emanuel and Jeffrey B. Liebman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ezekiel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Emanuel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': Non