snippet': 'As Italy reins in its spending, institutions in New York City dependent on the European nation’s money are being affected.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Italy’s new government scrambles to stave off economic disaster, the budget cuts it has imposed are rippling through Italian institutions in New York City, slicing into paychecks and prompting plans to shut down a venerable state-owned television operation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/nyregion/NYCITALY2/NYCITALY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/nyregion/NYCITALY2/NYCITALY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/31/nyregion/NYCITALY2/NYCITALY2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Studios and Grand Halls, Feeling a Pinch From Italy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Studios and Grand Halls, Feeling a Pinch From Italy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Italian-Americans', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T03:07:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2636816d-4858-5ed2-9350-f065b0b11e67', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2636816d-4858-5ed2-9350-f065b0b11e67'}, {'abstract': 'An N.C.A.A. press release gives a rare, and stunning, glimpse of its moral bankruptcy in the case of a University of Connecticut freshman.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/deconstructing-the-boatright-decision/', 'snippet': 'An N.C.A.A. press release gives a rare, and stunning, glimpse of its moral bankruptcy in the case of a University of Connecticut freshman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my column, I try to make sense of the decision on Ryan Boatright, the University of Connecticut freshman, who, until last Saturday, had been suspended from the men’s basketball team. In handing down its ruling to reinstate him, the N.C.A.A. issued a press release so malicious in its intent that I could not let it pass. Longtime watchers of the N.C.A.A. tell me that they have never seen an athlete and his mother thrown under the bus the way Ryan and Tanesha Boatright were on Saturday. Below, I’ve annotated the press release. Click here to see an enlarged version. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deconstructing the Boatright Decision', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boatright, Ryan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T03:12:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Nocera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nocera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a012eb0f-a309-591b-8ef8-c2a8038161b7', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a012eb0f-a309-591b-8ef8-c2a8038161b7'}, {'abstract': 'The battle pitting the corporate parents of Deadline.com and The Hollywood Reporter has a trial date of July 9 of next year. Expect more legal fireworks leading up to it.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/30/hollywood-copyright-dispute-the-skirmishing-resumes/', 'snippet': 'The battle pitting the corporate parents of Deadline.com and The Hollywood Reporter has a trial date of July 9 of next year. Expect more legal fireworks leading up to it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Save the date: Monday, July 9, 2013.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hollywood Copyright Dispute: The Skirmishing Resumes', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hollywood Reporter', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T03:12:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab53524c-5256-53aa-8646-cee8a4bdd7d2', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab53524c-5256-53aa-8646-cee8a4bdd7d2'}, {'abstract': 'Monday’s game was an important step for the Huskies, who needed a matchup like this to gain some experience and make a statement about their place in the hierarchy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/sports/ncaabasketball/uconn-women-beat-duke-on-road-but-arent-there-yet.html', 'snippet': 'Monday’s game was an important step for the Huskies, who needed a matchup like this to gain some experience and make a statement about their place in the hierarchy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURHAM, N.C. — In the post-Maya Moore era at Connecticut, the Huskies are no longer the alpha females of women’s college basketball. Baylor and Notre Dame share that place now.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/sports/UCONN/UCONN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/sports/UCONN/UCONN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/31/sports/UCONN/UCONN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'UConn Wins on Road but Isn’t There Yet', 'kicker': 'Connecticut 61, Duke 45', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'UConn Wins on Road but Isn’t There Yet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duke University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hayes, Tiffany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '201