'abstract': 'Abductions of Chinese workers in Sudan and Egypt have tested Beijing’s policy of noninterference and increased pressure to more aggressively protect its citizens abroad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/world/africa/china-says-29-workers-still-missing-in-sudan.html', 'snippet': 'Abductions of Chinese workers in Sudan and Egypt have tested Beijing’s policy of noninterference and increased pressure to more aggressively protect its citizens abroad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — China’s government, grappling with the kidnapping of a construction crew in Sudan, is facing heightened pressure over the safety of the country’s citizens abroad after a group of cement plant employees in Egypt was briefly abducted by Bedouin tribesmen on Tuesday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/02/world/sudan-image/sudan-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kidnappings of Workers Put Pressure on China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kidnappings of Workers Put Pressure on China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Sudan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sinai Peninsula (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T10:44:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs and Jeffrey Gettleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None