th Carolina showed Mr. Gingrich with a lead of 8 and 9 points, respectively. But the news has gotten worse for him almost every day, and he trails Mitt Romney by nearly 15 points in the final FiveThirtyEight forecast of the Florida primary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida Primary Overview and Forecast', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Ron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T12:44:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca7abdc2-1397-5180-b815-cc4a88343d5f', 'word_count': 1386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca7abdc2-1397-5180-b815-cc4a88343d5f'}, {'abstract': 'A galaxy of French celebrities wrote an open letter lampooning French Elle as the controversy over its article on black fashion continued. The signatories urged the magazine’s editors to get out more.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/celebrities-weigh-into-elle-dispute/', 'snippet': 'A galaxy of French celebrities wrote an open letter lampooning French Elle as the controversy over its article on black fashion continued. The signatories urged the magazine’s editors to get out more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The controversy over an alleged racist article on black fashion in French Elle refuses to die down.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrities Weigh Into Elle Dispute', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ELLE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Monde', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T12:55:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cdbb229-880f-544a-9e40-74261817091a', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cdbb229-880f-544a-9e40-74261817091a'}, {'abstract': 'Britain’s financial regulator has levied a £2.87 million ($4.52 million) fine against Ravi Sinha, who formerly led the British operations of the private equity firm J.C. Flowers, for using a fraudulent invoicing scheme to pocket millions of dollars.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/british-regulator-fines-former-top-executive-at-j-c-flowers/', 'snippet': 'Britain’s financial regulator has levied a £2.87 million ($4.52 million) fine against Ravi Sinha, who formerly led the British operations of the private equity firm J.C. Flowers, for using a fraudulent invoicing scheme to pocket millions of dollar...', 'lead_paragraph': '9:10 a.m. | Updated ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain Fines Former Top Executive at J.C. Flowers', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Einhorn, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Flowers, J C, & Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greenlight Capital Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T12:57:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b9bc132-383b-5007-9d76-7b1ad56f4d41', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b9bc132-383b-5007-9d76-7b1ad56f4d41'}, {'abstract': 'For the harried headline writer, certain tried-and-true devices can seem almost irresistible.', 'web_url': 'https://topics.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/allusions-we-love-too-much/', 'snippet': 'For the harried headline writer, certain tried-and-true devices can seem almost irresistible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Notes from the newsroom on grammar, usage and style. (Some frequently asked questions are here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Allusions We Love Too Much', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T13:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip B. Corbett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb41abfd-fe2b-5c3e-abb6-02d8eeb8c7e1', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb41abfd-fe2b-5c3e-abb6-02d8eeb8c7e1'}, {'abstract': 'The global jukebox envisioned by Alan Lomax, the folklorist and ethnomusicologist, is finally coming to fruition. His recordings have been digitized and will appear online soon.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/daily-report-a-global-jukebox-goes-digital/', 'snippet': 'The global jukebox envisioned by Alan Lomax, the folklorist and ethnomusicologist, is finally coming to fruition. His recordings have been digitized and will appear online soon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Technology has caught up to the imagination of Alan Lomax, the folklorist and ethnomusicologist whose life’s work was collecting traditional music from cultures across the world, Larry Rohter reports in Tuesday’s New York Times. Long before the Internet existed, Lomax wanted to create a “global jukebox” for the material he had found. Now, 10 years after his death, his archive — amounting to about 5,000 hours of sound recordings, 400,000 feet of film, 3,000 videotapes, 5,000 photographs and piles of manuscripts — is being digitized so that it can be accessed online. About 17,000 music tracks will be available for free streaming by the end of February, and later some of that music may be for sale as CDs or digital downloads.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty