 consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Communities Learn the Good Life Can Be a Killer', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T15:13:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32f48793-5132-5a07-81ce-23ca79427d92', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32f48793-5132-5a07-81ce-23ca79427d92'}, {'abstract': 'In prepared testimony, the Obama administration’s top intelligence official said that Iran has become more willing to carry out attacks inside the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/world/intelligence-chief-sees-al-qaeda-likely-to-continue-fragmenting.html', 'snippet': 'In prepared testimony, the Obama administration’s top intelligence official said that Iran has become more willing to carry out attacks inside the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Some senior Iranian leaders are now more willing to carry out attacks inside the United States in response to perceived American threats against their country, the Obama administration’s top intelligence official said on Tuesday, pointing to last fall’s  suspected assassination plot against the Saudi ambassador to Washington. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_pag