is summer at Second Stage Theater, the theater’s leaders announced Tuesday. The musical, based on a 1991 indie movie starring River Phoenix and Lili Taylor, will be directed by the Tony Award winner Joe Mantello (“Other Desert Cities,” “Wicked”); cast members and performance dates will be announced later.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Musical Set in 1960s Coming to Second Stage Theater', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Dogfight (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pasek, Benj', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Justin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phoenix, River', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Lili', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Second Stage Theater', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T17:06:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdd24a05-363b-5d82-be4d-8aac8945abde', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdd24a05-363b-5d82-be4d-8aac8945abde'}, {'abstract': 'Two British artist-designers bring their haunting mash-ups of antique furniture and objects to a Geneva gallery.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/the-dark-fantastic-jamesplumbs-goodnight-day/', 'snippet': 'Two British artist-designers bring their haunting mash-ups of antique furniture and objects to a Geneva gallery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dark Fantastic | JamesPlumb’s ‘Goodnight Day’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Geneva (Switzerland)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T17:15:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb89d08b-3660-5cae-bfd4-69715bb959db', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb89d08b-3660-5cae-bfd4-69715bb959db'}, {'abstract': 'Iran’s state Cyber Police said it had arrested two men and two women responsible for maintaining a Facebook page that encouraged people to send photos for a virtual beauty contest.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/iranian-authorities-arrest-four-over-facebook-beauty-contest/', 'snippet': 'Iran’s state Cyber Police said it had arrested two men and two women responsible for maintaining a Facebook page that encouraged people to send photos for a virtual beauty contest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the question “Am I hot or not?” the Iranian authorities gave a resounding answer to thousands of young people who posted glamorous shots of themselves to Facebook in recent weeks: Don’t even ask. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iranian Authorities Arrest Four Over Facebook Beauty Contest', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T17:15:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3862044-6268-53cd-b206-3f13dc1a1a84', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3862044-6268-53cd-b206-3f13dc1a1a84'}, {'abstract': 'A leopard that survived the mass killing of exotic creatures at an Ohio animal reserve last year was euthanized after a zookeeper accidentally struck it with a heavy steel gate while closing its cage at the Columbus Zoo and Aquarium, officials said Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/leopard-from-zanesville-ohio-reserve-is-euthanized-after-accident/', 'snippet': 'A leopard that survived the mass killing of exotic creatures at an Ohio animal reserve last year was euthanized after a zookeeper accidentally struck it with a heavy steel gate while closing its cage at the Columbus Zoo and Aquarium, officials sai...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A leopard that survived the mass killing of exotic animals at an Ohio reserve last year was euthanized after a zookeeper accidentally struck it with a heavy steel gate while closing its cage at the Columbus Zoo and Aquarium, officials said Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leopard From Zanesville, Ohio, Reserve Is Euthanized After Accident', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Leopards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Columbus (Ohio)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zanesville (Ohio)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T17:23:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2dc0841-b285-5960-af25-7bbabb1de64e', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2dc0841-b285-5960-af25-7bbabb1de64e'}, {'abstract': 'A performance project conveys the stories behind the scientific process.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/story-collider-where-science-is-a-story-well-told/', 'snippet': 'A performance project conveys the stories behind the scientific process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve often argued that the world would be better off if people, from an early age, absorbed science not as a set of facts (sadly the state of science education today), but as a story — full of vexing questions, conflict, dead ends, insights and the occasional thrilling leap.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Story Collider: Where Science is a Story Well Told', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Secondary)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T17:26:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf7f2cb6-3860-5976-a37b-1d408cb1f998', 'word_count': 1277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf7f2cb6-3860-5976-a37b-1d408cb1f998'}, {'abstract': 'John Browett, the chief executive officer of Dixons Retail, a British electronics chain, will oversee Apple’s stores as its senior vice president for retail.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/for-new-store-chief-apple-looks-outside/', 'snippet': 'John Browett, the chief executive officer of Dixons Retail, a British electronics chain, will oversee Apple’s stores as its senior vice president for retail.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:11 p.m. | Updated  Apple looked outside the company for an executive to run its growing chain of Apple stores with the hiring of John Browett, the chief executive of one of Europe’s largest electronics sellers, Dixons Retail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/technology/31bits-browett/31bits-browett-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/technology/31bits-browett/31bits-browett-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/31/technology/31bits-browett/31bits-browett-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Hires an Outsider to Supervise Retail Stores', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Ronald B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T17:28:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield and Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1be7a188-a494-5144-b829-099f8edebc17', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1be7a188-a494-5144-b829-099f8edebc17'}, {'abstract': 'Seven tools for children in the kitchen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/dining/kitchen-tools-for-the-younger-chefs.html', 'snippet': 'Seven tools for children in the kitchen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When your child is ready to step out of the play kitchen and into a real one, tools scaled for diminutive chefs will make cooking tasks easier and safer. A sturdy skid-free cutting board provides a proper work surface. A step-stool should allow the budding cook to stand tall enough at a counter to wield a knife or rolling pin at the proper angle and with the correct pressure. And an array of well-made kitchenware is sold online. I’ve taught children’s cooking classes and have four children of my own; here are some of the best products I’ve found.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01TOOLS1/01TOOLS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01TOOLS1/01TOOLS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01TOOLS1/01TOOLS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 555, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01TOOLS1/01TOOLS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01TOOLS1/01TOOLS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kitchen Tools for the Younger Chefs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tools of the Trade for the Young Cook', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookware', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T17:29:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Landis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8271524c-8842-5072-acbd-597d1eab323f', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8271524c-8842-5072-acbd-597d1eab323f'}, {'abstract': 'One political strategist is pointing to new evidence that winning back the House this November is in the realm of possibility for Democrats.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/democrats-see-a-shot-at-retaking-the-house/', 'snippet': 'One political strategist is pointing to new evidence that winning back the House this November is in the realm of possibility for Democrats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facing two large hills to climb in November — maintaining control of the Senate and winning back the House – some Democrats are saying that there’s new evidence that the second is in the realm of possibility.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats See a Shot at Retaking the House', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T17:34:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14c60680-0586-5a63-a8bb-05b2327c8c13', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14c60680-0586-5a63-a8bb-05b2327c8c13'}, {'abstract': 'The Italian Civil Protection Agency said on Tuesday that deteriorating safety conditions had forced divers to suspend the underwater search for missing people aboard the Costa Concordia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/world/europe/divers-suspend-underwater-search-of-costa-concordia-in-italy.html', 'snippet': 'The Italian Civil Protection Agency said on Tuesday that deteriorating safety conditions had forced divers to suspend the underwater search for missing people aboard the Costa Concordia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORENCE, Italy — The Italian Civil Protection Agency said Tuesday that deteriorating safety conditions had forced divers to suspend the underwater search for missing people in a wrecked cruise ship off the island of Giglio. The ship, the Costa Concordia, struck a reef on Jan. 13, heeled over and foundered just offshore, with the loss of at least 17 lives.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Divers Suspend Underwater Search of Stricken Italian Liner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Search Suspended for Cruise Ship Survivors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Costa Crociere SpA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cruises', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tuscany (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T17:36:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani and Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad5c1b22-5f8d-5454-8ce1-5abdfdf10fa6', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad5c1b22-5f8d-5454-8ce1-5abdfdf10fa6'}, {'abstract': 'Despite what you may have heard about risotto, this colorful dish doesn’t require constant stirring.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/03/health/nutrition/risotto-with-red-kale-and-red-beans-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'Despite what you may have heard about risotto, this colorful dish doesn’t require constant stirring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m always on the lookout for vegetables with red pigments, a good sign of anthocyanins, those beneficial flavonoids that are known for antioxidant properties and are present in purple and red vegetables. When you cook the kale with the rice, the red in the kale dyes the rice pale pink (the kale goes to a kind of drab green). The first time I made it, without the red beans, the finished product reminded me of the way the rice looks when I make red beans with rice. So I decided to add red beans to the mix, which provide a healthy dose of protein and fiber, as well as color.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/science/03recipehealth/03recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/01/31/science/03recipehealth/03recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/science/03recipehealth/03recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/science/03recipehealth/03recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/science/03recipehealth/03recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/31/science/03recipehealth/03recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/31/science/03recipehealth/03recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Risotto With Red Kale and Red Beans', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kale (Vegetable)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T17:39:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Fitness & Nutrition', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/19d21012-6043-53e0-825a-6f2e5f1b1f27', 'word_count': 653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19d21012-6043-53e0-825a-6f2e5f1b1f27'}, {'abstract': '“A Better Life’s” star, Demian Bichir, and director, Chris Weitz, weigh in on immigrants’ rights.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/demian-bichir-on-what-it-means-to-be-american/', 'snippet': '“A Better Life’s” star, Demian Bichir, and director, Chris Weitz, weigh in on immigrants’ rights.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Help” is not the only movie this Oscar season that deals with still-relevant issues of race, class and the political landscape. There’s also “A Better Life,” which earned its star, Demian Bichir, a surprise best actor nomination (and a fun, tequila-filled morning of celebration). In the film, directed by Chris Weitz (“American Pie,” “About a Boy”), Mr. Bichir plays an undocumented Mexican immigrant struggling to make a place for himself and his son by working as a gardener around Los Angeles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Demian Bichir on What It Means to Be American', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bichir, Demian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weitz, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T17:40:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfb7421b-27f8-566d-b202-112a6b2640aa', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfb7421b-27f8-566d-b202-112a6b2640aa'}, {'abstract': 'A college student enlists in the Army and people wonder why.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/college-life-enlistment-and-the-real-world/', 'snippet': 'A college student enlists in the Army and people wonder why.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You? Take orders? You?” The speaker, an English teacher I’d had in junior high, stood and looked at me, shocked, a frozen smile of disbelief on her face. It was just one of the many responses I’ve gotten to the sentence, “I’m joining the Army.” A few others: “Have you thought about the Peace Corps?” “You should be a Marine, I hear the Army trains them really well.” “Oh, like ROTC?” “Army band?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'College Life, Enlistment and the ‘Real World’', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hampshire College', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T17:46:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Wertheim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wertheim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c0e9ad0-d57e-524f-a12a-131b86592464', 'word_count': 1185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c0e9ad0-d57e-524f-a12a-131b86592464'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Knicks have high volume shooters, not efficient ones.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/knicks-need-to-look-for-efficient-scoring/', 'snippet': 'The New York Knicks have high volume shooters, not efficient ones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years, statistics have become more valued by professional teams, although this change has been a slow process. Hall of Fame baseball executive Branch Rickey hired the first full time statistician in 1947, and made numerous statistical formulas to enhance his performance. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks N