, 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santorum, Rick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vander Plaats, Bob', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iowa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T20:22:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.G. Sulzberger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Sulzberger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97e19139-cf69-5107-9788-cd6c1ff3a8fe', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97e19139-cf69-5107-9788-cd6c1ff3a8fe'}, {'abstract': '“Luck,” starring Dustin Hoffman, gets another season just two days after its premiere.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/hbo-renews-luck-for-another-season/', 'snippet': '“Luck,” starring Dustin Hoffman, gets another season just two days after its premiere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In what looked like a sure thing given the creative pedigree involved, HBO announced on Tuesday that it had renewed its new horse racing drama “Luck,” starring Dustin Hoffman and produced by Michael Mann and David Milch, for a 10-episode second season with a premiere date set for January 2013. The first episode has drawn 3.3 million total viewers over multiple airings including the 1.1 million viewers who tuned in on Sunday. The quick turnaround has become standard operating procedure for HBO; “Game of Thrones,” “Boardwalk Empire” and “Treme” were also renewed two days after their debuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'HBO Renews ‘Luck’ for Another Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Dustin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mann, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Milch, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Showtime', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T20:23:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a408fbb-0598-595d-8aa7-688c3fa43d31', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a408fbb-0598-595d-8aa7-688c3fa43d31'}, {'abstract': 'The hedge fund manager David Einhorn settled securities fraud charges with Britain’s financial regulator, but it is unlikely the Securities and Exchange Commission would pursue similar charges against him.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/einhorn-case-highlights-britains-broader-definition-of-insider-trading/', 'snippet': 'The hedge fund manager David Einhorn settled securities fraud charges with Britain’s financial regulator, but it is unlikely the Securities and Exchange Commission would pursue similar charges against him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The settlement of charges filed by the Financial Services Authority, Britain’s financial regulator, against David Einhorn and his hedge fund, Greenlight Capital, for trading on confidential information highlights how malleable the term “insider trading” can be. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Einh