054, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdbef0d3-b962-56eb-bb1c-5e7a6403cd30'}, {'abstract': 'SaveUp, a new start-up, joins other Web companies that aim to help people manage and learn about their finances. It takes a different approach, its founders say, by turning saving and paying off debt into a game with prizes– like a $2 million jackpot. Any time users save $1 or pay off $1 in debt, they earn a credit.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/a-start-up-rewards-savers-not-spenders/', 'snippet': 'SaveUp, a new start-up, joins other Web companies that aim to help people manage and learn about their finances. It takes a different approach, its founders say, by turning saving and paying off debt into a game with prizes– like a $2 million jack...', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are accustomed to earning credit card points for spending money. A start-up called SaveUp wants to flip that idea on its head and give prizes for saving money instead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Start-Up Rewards Savers, Not Spenders', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intuit Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T20:45:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15c52854-b6b9-526d-8928-515ab2e44250', 'wor