an lead to a bit of dullness around the edges, but a number of the dishes come together in ways that make you understand how classics get to be classics. Here are five that are worth ordering if you find yourself on East 81st Street with a spare hundred or two in your pocket.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Five Dishes at Crown', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T21:22:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e70fe0ef-3e2b-5399-aff6-278f716fa40f', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e70fe0ef-3e2b-5399-aff6-278f716fa40f'}, {'abstract': 'The tween category, defined vaguely as ages 8 to 14, now has several cosmetic product lines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/02/fashion/it-starts-with-lip-gloss-grade-schoolers-and-makeup.html', 'snippet': 'The tween category, defined vaguely as ages 8 to 14, now has several cosmetic product lines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE other day at Kimara Ahnert’s makeup and skin care studio on Madison Avenue, Sloane Kratzman, 12, was sitting in a chair, having blush applied to her cheeks, her legs dangling above the floor. She had been driven in after school from Greenwich, Conn., by her mother, Teresa Kratzman, a longtime friend of Ms. Ahnert’s, for her first makeup application lesson.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/02/fashion/02zSKIN1/02zSKIN1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 