ealth department, said “the ad of me doesn’t scare me.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/model-in-anti-obesity-ad-criticizes-the-campaign/', 'snippet': 'Beth Anne Sacks, who appears in one of the anti-obesity ads from the city’s health department, said “the ad of me doesn’t scare me.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Another of the overweight models appearing in ads from New York City’s health department — one who did not have a limb edited off — criticized the campaign, saying that the ads will not have the desired effect.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Model in Anti-Obesity Ad Criticizes the Campaign', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Mental Hygiene Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T22:30:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1373a18f-eddb-5372-8e34-ed852dd26975', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1373a18f-eddb-5372-8e34-ed852dd26975'}, {'abstract': 'A crowd of more than 12,000 watched the top-ranked Wisconsin women’s hockey team defeat Bemidji State 1-0.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/for-top-ranked-wisconsin-women-a-big-victory-and-a-big-crowd/', 'snippet': 'A crowd of more than 12,000 watched the top-ranked Wisconsin women’s hockey team defeat Bemidji State 1-0.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throughout the college hockey season, Slap Shot will feature reports about some of the country’s top-ranked teams. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Top-Ranked Wisconsin Women, a Big Victory and a Big Crowd', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Mark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bemidji State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Wisconsin-Madison', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Western Collegiate Hockey Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madison (Wis)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T22:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Sage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/554ed4aa-103f-5c9a-9091-5d3db8d5a401', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/554ed4aa-103f-5c9a-9091-5d3db8d5a401'}, {'abstract': 'The imports are fried in olive oil and include a version dusted with paprika.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/dining/chips-translated-from-the-spanish.html', 'snippet': 'The imports are fried in olive oil and include a version dusted with paprika.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dare we suggest elitist chips to go with workaday beer and dips? From Spain come uncommonly flavorful but light potato chips fried in olive oil. Their producer grows its own potatoes at high altitude east of Madrid and offers the chips in organic and conventional varieties, seasoned with sea salt. After tasting a third version, dusted with Spanish paprika, you may forswear barbecue-flavor chips.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01STUFF_CHIPS/01STUFF_CHIPS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 562, 'width': 920, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01STUFF_CHIPS/01STUFF_CHIPS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01STUFF_CHIPS/01STUFF_CHIPS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chips, Translated From the Spanish', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chips, Translated From the Spanish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snack Foods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T22:40:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb87dd47-7025-5e13-b932-a8186d38fa76', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb87dd47-7025-5e13-b932-a8186d38fa76'}, {'abstract': 'The line includes Polish Kimchee and Cider Braised Onion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/dining/new-condiments-from-saucy-by-nature.html', 'snippet': 'The line includes Polish Kimchee and Cider Braised Onion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every Super Bowl spread needs a kick, and that’s where the spreads and sauces come in. Saucy by Nature, a new line of condiments, makes some that can transform the usual fare. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01STUFF_SPREAD/01STUFF_SPREAD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 814, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01STUFF_SPREAD/01STUFF_SPREAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/02/01/dining/01STUFF_SPREAD/01STUFF_SPREAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Condiments With Kick', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Condiments With Kick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condiments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sauces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snack Foods', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T22:41:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c39fed7f-3300-5c6a-9a3c-6f083d34f1f7', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c39fed7f-3300-5c6a-9a3c-6f083d34f1f7'}, {'abstract': 'At a news conference of House Republicans to promote a transportation bill, Representative Don Young of Alaska suggests that earmarks would have made the bill better.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/a-rare-public-lament-for-lost-earmarks/', 'snippet': 'At a news conference of House Republicans to promote a transportation bill, Representative Don Young of Alaska suggests that earmarks would have made the bill better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the things House Republicans are most proud of is banishing earmarks from their bills, including, notably, the current version of an infrastructure and transportation bill, which has traditionally been a veritable stew pot of pork for member’s districts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rare Public Lament for Lost Earmarks', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Don', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T22:44:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d0bfa7e-c607-5913-be4e-d19a80deb87a', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d0bfa7e-c607-5913-be4e-d19a80deb87a'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Brady’s podium at Media Day was on a very special spot, for Colts fans.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/the-ground-where-brady-sat/', 'snippet': 'Tom Brady’s podium at Media Day was on a very special spot, for Colts fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS — Tom Brady’s podium stood on hallowed ground Tuesday at Media Day — at least for Colts fans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ground Where Brady Sat', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T22:44:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Nelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46bed82e-363c-5f3c-857b-0e8a45b60433', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46bed82e-363c-5f3c-857b-0e8a45b60433'}, {'abstract': 'Students at Claremont McKenna College share their reactions to the announcement that an administrator had submitted false SAT results since 2005.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/students-reputation-rankings/', 'snippet': 'Students at Claremont McKenna College share their reactions to the announcement that an administrator had submitted false SAT results since 2005.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLAREMONT, Calif. — Students at Claremont McKenna College acknowledged on Tuesday that revelations that a senior administrator had inflated SAT scores submitted to college ranking guides was not the best way to make headlines. But they also defended their school, which has climbed to No. 9 among liberal arts colleges in the U.S. News & World Report.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Students at Claremont McKenna More Worried About Reputation Than Rankings', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T22:48:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Lovett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f6622e3-49d4-5b7f-9e2b-b344bb1ebbee', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f6622e3-49d4-5b7f-9e2b-b344bb1ebbee'}, {'abstract': 'Reports to the Federal Election Commission underscore how Newt Gingrich used strong debate performances to capitalize on grass-roots contributions.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/in-last-quarter-of-2011-gingrich-rakes-in-nearly-10-million/', 'snippet': 'Reports to the Federal Election Commission underscore how Newt Gingrich used strong debate performances to capitalize on grass-roots contributions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newt Gingrich raised nearly $10 million in the final three months of 2011, according to reports his campaign filed with the Federal Election Commission on Tuesday. That is roughly triple what he raised in the first six months of his campaign, and his spokesman, R.C. Hammond, said Mr. Gingrich had raised an additional $5 million in January.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Last Quarter of 2011, Gingrich Rakes In Nearly $10 Million', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Election Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T22:49:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09dc06f0-7821-559e-9539-140dd410b71d', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09dc06f0-7821-559e-9539-140dd410b71d'}, {'abstract': 'Scarves have become an unintended symbol of Indianapolis’s embrace of the homespun feel for its Super Bowl', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/scarves-attract-attention-at-super-bowl/', 'snippet': 'Scarves have become an unintended symbol of Indianapolis’s embrace of the homespun feel for its Super Bowl', 'lead_paragraph': 'INDIANAPOLIS – The must-have souvenir from the first few days of Super Bowl week is not a team jersey or a miniature helmet. And it is not for sale, although one person has offered $200 for one and players and team executives have clamored to get them for themselves and their wives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hottest Item at the Super Bowl Is Hand Knit', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Scarves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T22:51:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judy Battista', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Battista', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaf7eb26-da6e-5fa6-bfe1-852a679c52cd', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaf7eb26-da6e-5fa6-bfe1-852a679c52cd'}, {'abstract': 'The conductor Paul Hillier and Theater of Voices presented works by the composer David Lang at Zankel Hall on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/arts/music/david-langs-music-at-zankel-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The conductor Paul Hillier and Theater of Voices presented works by the composer David Lang at Zankel Hall on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among opportunities to hear music by the composer David Lang performed live, the best are those in which he is invited to talk about his works. Genial, droll and articulate, Mr. Lang has a knack for making the disparate impulses and methods that mingle in his music seem not just appropriate but also inevitable.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/arts/lang/lang-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/arts/lang/lang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/02/01/arts/lang/lang-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Gathering for Both Conversing and Playing', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Gathering For Both Conversing And Playing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lang, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Worden, Shara', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Theater of Voices', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T22:55:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/260e5b51-07cc-52cd-bcf4-26f5a55b8140', 'word_count': 531, 'uri': 'nyt://article/260e5b51-07cc-52cd-bcf4-26f5a55b8140'}, {'abstract': 'The East Haven, Conn. police chief thinks he’s going to retire. He deserves worse.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/a-firing-offense/', 'snippet': 'The East Haven, Conn. police chief thinks he’s going to retire. He deserves worse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Friday, we ran an editorial about East Haven, Conn., a charming New England town where the police force harasses Latinos and the mayor is an incompetent fellow who makes racist jokes. The Federal Bureau of Investigation had arrested four police officers on charges of terrorizing the town’s Hispanic neighborhoods, stopping and detaining people, searching businesses without cause, beating people in handcuffs, smashing a man’s head into a wall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Firing Offense', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gallo, Leonard', 'rank': 2, 'major':