uart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ba8974f-57f9-5662-a7b2-9f584885129e', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ba8974f-57f9-5662-a7b2-9f584885129e'}, {'abstract': 'Welcome to FiveThirtyEight’s live blog of Florida’s Republican primary.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/live-coverage-of-the-florida-primary/', 'snippet': 'Welcome to FiveThirtyEight’s live blog of Florida’s Republican primary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to FiveThirtyEight’s live blog of Florida’s Republican primary. Polls in the state are closed, and we’ll be bringing you the results, data-driven observations, exit poll information and some historical perspective.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Coverage of the Florida Primary', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T23:15:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1225857-9d8f-524e-b34d-791ebcd19de1', 'word_count': 2721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1225857-9d8f-524e-b34d-791ebcd19de1'}, {'abstract': 'A draft of the proposed United Nations Security Council resolution concerning Syria, as it was circulated among diplomats on Tuesday afternoon and provided to The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/world/middleeast/draft-of-security-council-resolution-on-syria.html', 'snippet': 'A draft of the proposed United Nations Security Council resolution concerning Syria, as it was circulated among diplomats on Tuesday afternoon and provided to The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following is a draft of the proposed United Nations Security Council resolution concerning Syria, as it was circulated among diplomats on Tuesday afternoon and provided to The New York Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Draft of Security Council Resolution on Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Draft of Security Council Resolution on Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T23:18:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b29ecf06-6650-52bc-ace0-66a73e79e147', 'word_count': 1216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b29ecf06-6650-52bc-ace0-66a73e79e147'}, {'abstract': 'In Catherine Galasso’s “Bring on the Lumière!,” pioneering French filmmakers from the 1890s meet contemporary dance, at the Joyce SoHo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/arts/dance/catherine-galassos-bring-on-the-lumiere-at-joyce-soho.html', 'snippet': 'In Catherine Galasso’s “Bring on the Lumière!,” pioneering French filmmakers from the 1890s meet contemporary dance, at the Joyce SoHo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is probably impossible to recreate in modern audiences the wonder that the very earliest films must have incited. For us the poetry and pathos of those rudimentary artifacts — brief slices of life — come mainly from their mere survival, while the people in them, and the people who made them, are long gone.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/arts/galasso/galasso-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1015, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/arts/galasso/galasso-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/02/01/arts/galasso/galasso-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Physical Flickers of Light and Motion Animate Film Pioneers', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Physical Flickers of Light and Motion Animate Film Pioneers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T23:20:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d053ba1-2024-50db-a4c1-6fc4a0842d16', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d053ba1-2024-50db-a4c1-6fc4a0842d16'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to a news article, “Student Faces Town’s Wrath in Protest Against a Prayer.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/opinion/the-atheist-who-challenged-cranston-ri.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to a news article, “Student Faces Town’s Wrath in Protest Against a Prayer.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Atheist Who Challenged Cranston', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Atheist Who Challenged Cranston', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prayers and Prayer Books', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cranston (RI)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahlquist, Jessica', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Atheism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'First Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T23:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/529d6e7c-9d9a-5e04-a487-4541b404ae4b', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/529d6e7c-9d9a-5e04-a487-4541b404ae4b'}, {'abstract': 'Some findings from the early exit polls in Florida: 1 in 7 G.O.P. primary voters are Hispanic, and there are fewer late deciders and evangelicals than in the other early nominating states.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/lessons-from-the-early-exit-polls-in-florida/', 'snippet': 'Some findings from the early exit polls in Florida: 1 in 7 G.O.P. primary voters are Hispanic, and there are fewer late deciders and evangelicals than in the other early nominating states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last polls in Florida do not close until 8 p.m. ET, but we’re learning what we can about the Republican electorate from the early exit polls.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons From the Early Exit Polls in Florida', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T23:21:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a92ead9-a796-526a-955e-69e21bb8f3b3', 'word_count': 1194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a92ead9-a796-526a-955e-69e21bb8f3b3'}, {'abstract': 'The American Gaming Association responds to an Op-Ed article.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/opinion/the-casino-effect.html', 'snippet': 'The American Gaming Association responds to an Op-Ed article.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Casino Effect', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Casino Effect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN GAMING ASSN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davies, Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T23:22:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/d80724f0-1d38-5be1-b7a9-a5e728465727', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d80724f0-1d38-5be1-b7a9-a5e728465727'}, {'abstract': 'Less photo play, more closet stay is what we’re after, and a closer look at the spring collections reveals a great number of qualifying — and equally desirable — pieces.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/spring-secrets-finding-the-seasons-staples/', 'snippet': 'Less photo play, more closet stay is what we’re after, and a closer look at the spring collections reveals a great number of qualifying — and equally desirable — pieces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The subtext for the arrival of a new season of clothes in stores and online — brace yourself, it’ll happen any day now — is one riddled with tough decisions like cost-per-wear calculations and heart-wrenching explorations of need versus want. The pieces you’ve earmarked in all of your favorite magazines — the bandeau tops and hot-shorts as suit separates, perhaps? — aren’t always the most practical investments. Sure, they’re perfect on glossy paper, but watch what happens when applied to plastic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spring Secrets | Finding the Season’s Staples', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patrick, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Noten, Dries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yamamoto, Yohji', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Balmain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PRADA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saint Laurent, Yves', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T23:22:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Miesmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miesmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f5e7ff7-d423-50d2-b64b-028c11925ff7', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f5e7ff7-d423-50d2-b64b-028c11925ff7'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to Delia Ephron’s Op-Ed article, “Banks Taketh, but Don’t Giveth.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/opinion/frustrated-with-banks.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to Delia Ephron’s Op-Ed article, “Banks Taketh, but Don’t Giveth.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Frustrated With Banks', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Frustrated With Banks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T23:23:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa5f7537-9e11-55b0-9b08-819042659b68', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa5f7537-9e11-55b0-9b08-819042659b68'}, {'abstract': 'Redistricting persuades a freshman Republican in Florida to seek re-election from a new district.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/allen-west-to-switch-districts/', 'snippet': 'Redistricting persuades a freshman Republican in Florida to seek re-election from a new district.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Representative Allen West, Republican of Florida, will switch Congressional districts to greatly increase his chances of winning re-election. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Allen West to Switch Districts', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Allen B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T23:24:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81088de5-6b69-5a8b-82d5-91325c30bd54', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81088de5-6b69-5a8b-82d5-91325c30bd54'}, {'abstract': 'At Suitsupply, a suit superstore, the fabrics are impressive, the construction is done elsewhere and alterations are done quickly in-house.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/02/fashion/suitsupply-in-soho.html', 'snippet': 'At Suitsupply, a suit superstore, the fabrics are impressive, the construction is done elsewhere and alterations are done quickly in-house.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE suit sections at most of New York’s major department stores remind me of funeral homes. The dark wood. The austerity. The hands-offness of the sales clerks, who will assist when asked, but who otherwise consider respectful distance to be an effective marketing technique. If you can afford these suits, the theory seems to go, then you must understand them. And if you understand them, then you want to be left to your wandering, your fingering, your discerning.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/02/fashion/02CRITICAL2_SUBSPAN/02CRITICAL2_SUBSPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 