nial', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Crime of Genocide Denial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Armenians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T23:28:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/756ec0e1-4d00-5d11-a2cd-b3cacd9fd4cb', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/756ec0e1-4d00-5d11-a2cd-b3cacd9fd4cb'}, {'abstract': 'A former Army officer found that women were often the best soldiers he encountered.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/01/31/fighting-for-gender-equality-on-the-battlefield/', 'snippet': 'A former Army officer found that women were often the best soldiers he encountered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Suspended from her position in December, the commandant of the United States Army’s drill sergeant school is currently under investigation for an undisclosed personnel issue. Command Sgt. Maj. Teresa L. King was the first female commandant of the school, a somewhat high-profile position that is the source for the Army‘s pool of drill sergeants. These soldiers, who are typically men, are responsible for training thousands of new recruits each year. Sergeant Major King, known for her keen attention to detail and dogmatic demand for discipline, was named commandant in 2009. Since then, she has enjoyed some well-deserved popularity, including being named to Oprah Winfrey’s O Power List, as well as an appearance in the October 2010 issue of O, The Oprah Magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting for Gender Equality on the Battlefield', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Teresa L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Army', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T23:28:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Griffin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Griffin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afa0f359-b7ed-56bd-804e-14a220d75e3b', 'word_count': 1406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afa0f359-b7ed-56bd-804e-14a220d75e3b'}, {'abstract': '“The Story of Film: An Odyssey” traces the history of cinema in 15 hours. An epic in itself, it is playing at the Museum of Modern Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/01/movies/the-story-of-film-an-odyssey-by-mark-cousins-at-moma.html', 'snippet': '“The Story of Film: An Odyssey” traces the history of cinema in 15 hours. An epic in itself, it is playing at the Museum of Modern Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A glance at the nominees for best picture at this year’s Oscars will confirm that the movies, a forward-looking medium tumbling headlong into a digital future, find themselves in a moment of retrospection. It is not just that a majority of the nominees take place in lovingly imagined and carefully costumed versions of the past — that in itself is hardly new — but also that several look back with affection at earlier phases in the history of cinema.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/arts/CINEMA-JP/CINEMA-JP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/02/01/arts/CINEMA-JP/CINEMA-JP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/arts/CINEMA-JP/CINEMA-JP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/01/arts/CINEMA-JP/CINEMA-JP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/02/01/arts/CINEMA-JP/CINEMA-JP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Film of Films: A Sweeping History of an Art', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Your Film of Films: A Sweeping History of an Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-01-31T23:32:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac613080-369e-55b4-9161-91673d3546df', 'word_count': 1054, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac613080-369e-55b4-9161-91673d3546df'}, {'abstract': 'Disney acquired the 49.6 percent stake in the company that it did not already own, valuing the deal at about $450 million; it is hoping to leapfrog into one of t